- Steamworks features (overlay, Cloud setup, achievements, on-screen keyboard, SW-7..SW-14), store page (S5); translations (S4); media resizing (SW-9, S5).
- Local multiplayer (distinct players per device, join screen, the multiplayer modes; IN-6, IN-7): milestone 16: Local multiplayer: game modes and controls.
- Porting authoring''s Python (qgen, `trivia-authoring`) to Node/TS: later, own milestone.', 'This is the overall roadmap for the first version of the trivia game that a family can install and play on a computer or a Steam Deck, without the developer''s own setup. It covers the desktop app, file saves, playing with a game controller only, a credits screen, a way to see a whole picture on small screens, and a screen of its own for choosing which sets of questions to play. It also retires the old browser version so there is only one game to maintain.', '2026-10-11T21:55:09Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (9, 9, 'masterplan', 1000, 'Milestone 9 is S4 of the Steam track (D-34, `plans/11-steam.md`): enough reviewed questions, in every launch language, that a stranger''s family plays many evenings before questions repeat, plus a measurement that proves it. It needs translated UI catalogs, translated, re-rated and reviewed questions, regional bundles (D-39; decision 110: 2000 approved each, region''s language + en, free DLC, `colombia` the pilot; then `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico` by Steam audience, developer 2026-10-15), `qgen report --simulate` passing the content target for every launch language, and UI wording the gamemaster has checked on the TV (style guides, screen gallery), joker names made again English first, one symbol per joker in every language, and English-first drafting for `base` (developer, 2026-10-15): from batch-9 on `en` is the source of every new `base` question, translated to `es`, `es-ES` and `de`, each its own pool with 5000 approved (decision 21: Content target per player and language (OQ-32)); and English slug keys for every category and subcategory in every bundle, display names only from `names.<locale>.json` (developer, 2026-10-16); question translations reviewed by the LLM translation review only, no human spot check (developer, 2026-10-16); human reviews gate no regional or translation run (`decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`). Today: 1136 approved (`base` 1034, `colombia` 102), Spanish only; milestone 1 takes `base` to 5000 (D-52).

**The tasks of this masterplan are not implementation work: each one writes the plan for one part below** (`pm plan add 9 …`, priority as suggested), and that plan''s tasks do the work.

## Preconditions (other milestones; a part''s plan task checks them first)
- OQ-31 launch languages + Spanish variety: plan 37 (milestone 7). OQ-32 content target: plan 38. Default preset → burns per game: plan 35 (OQ-30). Burn multiplier for several players: plan 41 (OQ-37). If a needed decision is still pending, the plan task makes itself pending on it (`pm task-pending-decision`) and stops.
- **If OQ-31 = Spanish only:** parts 3–7 shrink to nothing: their plan tasks drop with that reason (`pm task drop`), except what the Spanish variety needs (part 8). The rest still applies to Spanish.
- TS engine (milestone 2, plans 19, 20; screens on the engine PORT-7): the simulation runs on it. Age-group windows and bundle filter in the engine (plan 27, milestone 5): the simulation and the bundle filter (RG-3) use them.
- Catalog (milestone 3: plans 21, 22, 23, 24): `t()`, `es`, `xx`, draft `en`. Settings screen (plan 36, MD-7): the language setting goes there.
- Pool growth and QC (milestone 1: plans 12 targets, 13 gap-aimed drafting, 15 drift, 16 QC/D-56, 17 batch runs). This milestone reuses them per language; it doesn''t rebuild them. The content side of the English switch (calibration examples, concept angle, cross-language overlap, health and spot check across the switch) is `plan 147: English-first batches: calibration, overlap and QC across languages` (milestone 1); part 15 doesn''t duplicate it.
- Licence/price: answered (decision 66: Price model (OQ-33), bundles as free DLC; decision 107: Licence (OQ-35)). A part that writes files depending on them follows them.

## Rules for every part
- Questions only through `qgen batch` (D-36). New pipeline steps (translate, re-rate, neutral Spanish) become `qgen batch` modes, with RUNBOOK and D-36 amended as an implementation task (like BN-11). Workers never edit pools or pick media by hand.
- Quality bar of plan 16 / D-56 applies per language to drafted batches (`base`, regional): LLM audit + blind human spot check per batch.
- Reviews don''t gate runs (milestone 1, "Reviews don''t gate generation"; decision 414): health ✗, spot checks and QC proposals are raised as pm decisions, but no task ever waits on one (no `pm task-pending-decision`, no prerequisite); health ✗ never stops `qgen batch` (drafting, `--bundle` or `--translate`): report and decision only, `qgen health ack` = the developer''s "looked at it"; answers are acted on afterwards by whatever task runs next. The only human gate is the final release (`trivia-release-check`, release bar), the developer''s, not a pm task.
- Translations (milestone, developer 2026-10-16; tr-en-1 and tr-de-1 spot checks found every translation good): the LLM translation review is the only review, in every question locale (milestone 12''s included): no native-speaker spot check, no QC decision per `tr-*` run, no pilot go/no-go, no `qgen health ack` after a pilot. Decision 45''s health thresholds are reported, never a stop (decision 414 partly supersedes decision 45 and `decision 313: Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run`); nothing waits for the developer. The developer may still review translations in the review tool; `qgen flag` still sets `needs_work`.
- `app/` never reads `authoring/` (D-35): per-locale pools and category/bundle names are exported to `app/data/`.
- The current game keeps working after every task until the Steam build replaces it (D-59): Spanish, Colombia on, same keys (unless LUI-4 changes them by decision). The family''s `es` pool keeps its es-sourced questions as they are; English-sourced ones join it as `es` translations.
- Owning plan files get tasks `[x]` with a note (`15-i18n.md`, `15a`, `15b`, `15c`, `16-content-target.md`, `22-bundles.md`); `plans/project.md` in sync. Store page texts (LUI-6) are S5 (milestone''s out of scope); note it in 15a, don''t do it.

## Parts

1. **Simulation: games per new player (CT-2)**
   - Owner: `plans/16-content-target.md` ("Metric").
   - `qgen report --simulate [--locale L] [--bundles …] [--age-group G] [--preset P] [--players N] [--seeds K]`: a new player plays game after game on the TS engine (Node, `authoring/` imports `app/`) with the default preset''s joker use, until supply fails. Median and 10th percentile; strong-player bound (always reaches 12); bottleneck level and subcategory.
   - Pass/fail against the target of OQ-32''s D-entry, per launch language, default bundle set and every age group; exit 1 on fail. Feeds part 9 (gaps) and part 12 (exit).
   - No second referee in Python: if the engine can''t run under Node without the client, the plan decides the small adapter.
   - Suggested priority: 570 (after plans 20 and 27).

2. **Release quality bar and back-audit (CT-5)**
   - Owner: `plans/16-content-target.md` ("Quality bar"). D-56 covers new batches; the ~1100 questions approved before it never had an audit or a spot check.
   - Release bar: D-56''s numbers (pm decision 2) or stricter for release (pm decision if the plan proposes stricter); error limit and what happens to a batch above it. The release bar is the developer''s own gate at release (`trivia-release-check`), not a pm task; a batch above it is reported, it stops no run (decision 414).
   - Back-audit: `qgen audit` over the pre-D-56 approved pool in slices, through `qgen` (gamemaster asks, like `qgen rework`), findings → review tool (`audit=flagged`). Cost estimate first.
   - Suggested priority: 640 (after plan 16 at 650).

3. **Translation layout and schema (QT-1, I18N-3)**
   - Owner: `plans/15b-question-translation.md` ("Storage"; draft preference A: `authoring/data/questions.<locale>.json`, same ids, translated fields + own `difficulty`, `status`, `review`, `source_hash` for `stale`).
   - Also: `translatable: false` on source questions; translated category, subcategory and bundle names (`categories.json`, `bundles.json`, per bundle); `qgen export` writes `app/data/pool.<locale>.json` (+ names); `qgen validate` checks translations, `stale`, missing names. D-entry for the layout.
   - Suggested priority: 890 (schema; after plan 26 at 900, which also changes pool fields).

4. **Translation pipeline (QT-2, QT-3)**
   - Owner: `plans/15b-question-translation.md` ("Pipeline").
   - Steps `translate --to L` (adapt units, answer format, hints that play on Spanish words; detect non-travelling questions → propose `translatable: false`) → `rate --locale L` (difficulty for that language''s main market, D-38 scale) → `factcheck --locale L` → review (D-32/D-33) → audit (D-56) → merge into the locale file. Only `approved`, translatable sources; skips done ones; costs in `costs.log`.
   - No human control of translations (milestone, developer 2026-10-16): `qgen health` drops decision 45: Health thresholds and selection order for qgen batch --translate runs''s "the pilot tr-<locale>-1 always stops the next run" (thresholds stay); `authoring/QC.md` "Translation runs" loses the spot check, RUNBOOK and plans 15b (QT-5, QT-6) follow; `pm decision record … --supersedes 45` for that clause. Decision 414: a crossed threshold no longer stops `--translate` either (report + decision only, exit code not a stop); the code, RUNBOOK and QC.md change is shared with milestone 1''s (`plan 17: Batch runs` / plan 16 revision), not written twice.
   - Entry point `qgen batch --translate L` (size like a batch, picks untranslated approved sources, fewest translated subcategories first); RUNBOOK + D-36 amended.
   - Source locale per question (part 15): es-sourced → `en`, `de`, `es-ES`; en-sourced → `es`, `es-ES`, `de`. Plan 66 (done) built es → L; the en → L direction and the `es-ES` target are part 15''s. Prompts in `authoring/tools/prompts/` (new prompts are the gamemaster''s: drafted here, approved by pm decision).
   - Suggested priority: 700.

5. **Review tool for translations (QT-4)**
   - Owner: `plans/15b-question-translation.md` ("Review tool"); `authoring/ui`, `authoring/server`.
   - `/review?batch=…&locale=L`: source and translation side by side; same approve / needs work / reject; flag media with visible text per locale; no translation spot-check sample (milestone, developer 2026-10-16): the developer reviews translations only when they choose to. Stats pages filter by locale.
   - Suggested priority: 400.

6. **Language setting, per-locale pool and first-start language screen (I18N-2)**
   - Owner: `plans/15-i18n.md` ("Model"). Plan 68 (written): save field, per-locale pool, names, Esc menu rows (task 450, done).
   - UI language and question language in the save (`SaveData.language`); Esc menu of every mode. Engine loads `pool.<locale>.json`; seen counters by id (plan 65), so switching languages never repeats a question before unseen ones run out. Category/bundle names from the locale''s names. Supply check per locale.
   - **First start (milestone change; replaces plan 68''s "no first-start language screen"):** a fresh save opens on a language screen, the guessed language preselected; the player confirms or picks another; asked once. Guess: `navigator.language` now, Steam''s client language once milestone 10 provides it. A save without `language` (the family''s, = `es`) never sees it. Plan 68 gets the screen as a new task (revision of plan 68).
   - `es-ES` gets its own question pool (part 15; until now a UI variant only, decision 156: One language for UI and questions picks `pool.es-ES.json` once its supply passes).
   - Current game: `es` fixed unless changed; the gamemaster mode unchanged.
   - Suggested priority: 480 (plan 68).

7. **UI catalogs for the launch languages (LUI-4, LUI-5)**
   - Owner: `plans/15a-ui-translation.md`. Builds on plans 21, 23, 24 (draft `en`).
   - LUI-4: joker keys per language or neutral keys: pm decision with a recommendation (also gamepad glyphs from milestone 8, plan 45).
   - LUI-5: one catalog per launch language beyond `es`/`en` draft; playful joker names per language (pm decision per joker, like plan 24); fonts checked for each script (Latin only at launch, 15a); length check with `xx`; `/comodines` cards per language; native-speaker playtest per language (gamemaster runs it; workers write the checklist and a pm decision "playtest passed?").
   - Suggested priority: 390 (after plans 23, 24 at 400).
   - Plan 69 (written; task 459 open): its playtest fixes follow the locale style guides of part 13 once they exist.

8. **Spanish variety (only if OQ-31 picks neutral Spanish)**
   - Owner: `plans/15-i18n.md` ("Spanish varieties").
   - A `qgen batch` mode (e.g. `--neutralize`) that rewrites Colombian wording in `base` to neutral Latin American Spanish, through review; `colombia` keeps its wording. If OQ-31 keeps Colombian Spanish: the plan task drops with that reason.
   - Plan 64 (done); `neutralize-1` runs as planned (decision 214: neutralize-1: qgen validate fails after fix). `es` is now idiomatic Latin American Spanish, no compromise with Spain: dropping "understood … in Spain" from `base`''s voice and the Spain-oriented rules from `neutralize.md` is part 15''s.
   - Suggested priority: 690 (tooling; the runs go to part 11).

9. **Cost and generation plan by gap (CT-3, CT-4)**
   - Owner: `plans/16-content-target.md` ("Cost").
   - Cost per approved question (draft → approved) and per translated question (from part 11''s pilot) from `costs.log`; information only (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15): no dollar budget per language or bundle, no budget decision, no over-budget gates; full runs don''t wait for a budget.
   - Gap plan: the simulation''s bottlenecks (part 1) → release targets per language/age group in `authoring/data/targets.json` (D-53, extended per locale), read by `draft` (D-54) and `--translate`. No new mechanism if plan 13''s covers it.
   - Target 5000 approved per question locale (`en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`; decision 21). English drafting for `base` aims at the locales'' deficits; replaces decision 37''s last clause, D-84 and decision 219''s `DRIVES_DRAFTING` (the en/de source shortfall steering es drafting). The change is part 15''s; plan 70''s `--cost` projection counts en drafting + three translations per question.
   - Suggested priority: 560 (after part 1).

10. **Regional bundles (RG-3..RG-5)** (plan 98)
    - Owner: `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` (superseded by bundles, D-39) and `plans/22-bundles.md`. RG-3 is BN-6 (plan 27, milestone 5) plus part 1''s `--bundles`; RG-4 is `qgen batch --bundle` (BN-11, done): mark them so.
    - RG-5 answered (decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46); partly supersedes decision 37''s "packs have no target"):
      - every regional bundle: 2000 approved, in its region''s language + en (`colombia`: es + en), free DLC (decision 66), off by default on the configure screen; the family''s save keeps base + `colombia` (D-59)
      - bundle-scoped taxonomy: every bundle has its own categories and subcategories; names may repeat verbatim across bundles (e.g. «Historia» in `base` and in `colombia`), still separate entries; the 19 `colombia` questions on `base` subcategories move to `colombia`''s own (a `qgen` migration step, no hand edits; `validate` rule; engine, «Cambiazo», export and review tool keyed by bundle + subcategory, not by name; the key becomes an English slug in part 16)
      - `colombia`''s subcategory list: the gamemaster''s (pm decision with a proposal)
      - `qgen batch --translate <locale> --bundle <id>`: the selection takes the bundle''s approved sources; the bundle''s `languages` gains the locale once its translations are approved
      - target per regional bundle (2000, D-53''s mix or the plan''s proposal) in `targets.json`, read by `--bundle` drafting and `qgen report`
      - effort measurement for the pilot: $ per approved (`qgen report --cost`, per bundle) and the gamemaster''s review time per 100 (from the review tool''s timestamps; a `qgen report` line if none exists)
      - packs as optional installs (plan 98 task 751, done); DLC depots in S5 (plan 89)
    - More regional bundles (milestone, developer 2026-10-15; replaces decision 110''s "more bundles only after a new decision with the pilot''s numbers"): by Steam audience in the launch languages (share of Steam download bandwidth, GameDiscoverCo 2024), in this order: `usa` (en, ≈20 %), `germany` (de + en, ≈4.4 %), `uk` (en, ≈3.3 %), `spain` (es-ES + en), `mexico` (es + en); later candidates `canada`, `australia`, `argentina` (no work now).
      - same rules as `colombia`: 2000 approved each, region''s language + en (en regions: en only), free DLC, off by default; own taxonomy from the general regional list via `qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>`, after part 16 (slugs + en names; decision 250: Regional drafting in en, de, es-ES: prompts apply? → redraft after slug keys) (`plan 138: Regional taxonomy: a general list, colombia reworked`; decision 213: General category list for regional bundles), one pm decision per bundle with the proposal
      - drafted in the region''s language and variety: US English, British English, German, Spain''s Spanish, Mexican Spanish (`bundles.json` `rule`/`voice`; prompt changes the developer''s); `qgen batch --bundle <id>` drafts in the bundle''s source language, not always `es` (shares part 15''s en drafting; de and es-ES drafting new); `--translate en --bundle <id>` from de and es-ES (new directions beyond part 4''s es → L and part 15''s en → L)
      - per bundle: `qgen bundle new --kind region`, taxonomy decision, target in `targets.json`; each starts once `colombia`''s taxonomy (decision 249: colombia taxonomy: categories and subcategories) and its first `qgen batch --bundle colombia` have proven the chain, not after colombia''s 2000
      - each its DLC entry like `colombia`: `steam.json` `dlc`, DLC app and depot (`plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)`, `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`), store texts and capsules (`plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)`); part 10''s plan adds a follow-up task to each of them per bundle
      - the family''s save keeps base + `colombia` (D-59); the new bundles off by default
    - Suggested priority: 300.

11. **Release content runs**
    - The recurring `qgen batch` tasks: translation pilot (QT-5: 50 questions per language, measure reject rate and cost, no go/no-go), then full translation per language (QT-6), neutral Spanish (part 8), regional bundle batches (part 10), and `base` top-ups where the simulation fails after milestone 1''s 5000. Each drafted batch followed by D-56''s QC (plan 16 procedure, `authoring/QC.md`); translation runs (`tr-*`) get no QC task and no spot check: the LLM translation review is their only review (milestone, developer 2026-10-16).
    - Reviews don''t gate runs (decision 414): a run''s health ✗ (exit 2) is reported and raised as a decision, and the chain goes on; a QC task raises its spot-check and proposals decisions and adds the next run without waiting for the answers; the answers become change tasks later. `plan 84: Release content runs`'' exit-2 rule (pend on the health-stop decision) and its waits on QC answers follow (its "too costly" pace question too: cost is information only, milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15); taxonomy and slug decisions that a bundle''s start needs are not reviews and still block; only real failures (exit 75, other codes, exit 1 three times) still stop a run task.
    - English-first `base` (part 15): `plan 17: Batch runs`'' batches draft `en` from batch-9 on (`task 1185: run batch-9`, decision 229: Continue batch-9 after the extended batch-8 review?); here their translation runs en → `es`, `es-ES`, `de`, and the es-sourced pool''s `es-ES` runs (besides `en`, `de`). No more Spanish `base` drafts or `es` top-ups.
    - Order inside: pilot first (priority -90, above the runs; the full runs follow without waiting for the developer, its cost is information for `qgen report --cost`); full runs after milestone 1''s batch runs (plan 17) so translations don''t go stale.
    - Regional pilot (decision 110): `qgen batch --bundle colombia` run/QC pairs from 102 to 2000 approved, then `--translate en --bundle colombia` pairs to 2000 en; effort recorded ($ per approved, review time per 100) in `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` / `16-content-target.md`; it sets the pace of the other bundles, no "More regional bundles?" decision (milestone, developer 2026-10-15).
    - More regional bundles (part 10): once colombia''s first batch has proven the chain, run/QC pairs per bundle in audience order `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`, each to 2000 approved in its language, then `--translate en --bundle <id>` pairs for `germany`, `spain`, `mexico`; interleaved with colombia''s runs at the pace the pilot''s numbers allow.
    - Launch doesn''t wait for the regional chain: it ships what `colombia` has then; content updates (plan 96) bring the rest.
    - Suggested priority: -110 (after plan 17''s -100).

