- `directory.md`: rows for `age-groups.json` / `bundles.json` say the game reads them (group ranges, choice; `languages`, `kind: base`); files new in plans 27–29, 71, 125–127, 133 listed (check only).
- `about` in `app/data/age-groups.json`: no "until AG-7", no "draft". `about` in `app/data/bundles.json`: `languages` and base bundles (exactly one per session), no "always on"; "players switch on or off" only for non-base bundles.
- D-68 in `plans/decisions.md`: "superseded in part by D-<plan 71''s entry>", if missing.
- New D entry only if the developer''s answer adds something beyond "fine".

## Tasks
- `task 479: Close out AG-7 and BN-6` (pending on decision 155): the play-test handling and the docs above.

## Done when
- The developer confirmed the play-test incl. the part-6 items; a start with zero or two base bundles is refused; in en and de only their bundles are offered; Start shows no supply report.
- AG-7 and BN-6 are `[x]` in plans 21, 22 and `project.md`; `rg -n "until AG-7|until BN-6|always_on|always on|Siempre activo" plans/21-age-groups.md plans/22-bundles.md plans/project.md directory.md app/data/*.json app/client/src` finds nothing (`decisions.md` history stays); `qgen validate` passes.', '', '2026-10-12T00:29:06Z', 118);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (31, 6, 'Preload the next screen''s media (UI-7)', 500, 'The fade-in after a screen change waits until the next screen''s media has loaded, at most 2 s (04, "Transitions", step 4). Today `go()` in `app/client/src/game/Game.svelte` switches the screen behind the black and fades in at once (`PLACEHOLDER(UI-7)`, line ~117). The plan also removes the last `PLACEHOLDER` hits, so the milestone''s `grep -rn PLACEHOLDER app/client/src` comes up empty.

## Shape (decided here)
- The screen hands back a promise; no separate preload helper, so the element that shows the media is the one that loads it (no second request, no cache guessing on `/media?url=…`).
- `Question.svelte` exports `ready(): Promise<void>`: resolves when the picture is decoded (`onload` / `img.decode()`), the video or audio reached `canplaythrough`, or any of them failed (`onerror`, `mediaFailed`). No media (text question) → resolves at once.
- Only Question has media worth waiting for: other screens have no `<img>`, no backgrounds from `/media` (checked 2026-10-11). Other screens: no `ready()`, `go()` doesn''t wait.
- `go()`: after `screen = next`, `await tick()`, then `await Promise.race([questionRef?.ready() ?? Promise.resolve(), sleep(PRELOAD_MAX_MS)])`, then fade in as today.
- `timing.ts`: `PRELOAD_MAX_MS = 2000` with a one-line comment.
- Video/audio must not play behind the black: drop `autoplay` on `<video>`/`<audio>`; Question exports `start()` (or a `shown` prop) that `go()` calls when `black = false`. Same moment media starts today (start of fade-in), so the first seconds aren''t lost.
- Paths into Question that don''t go through `go()` (page reload on a running game, `{#key game.question.id}` swaps by Bájale/Cambiazo inside Question): media still starts; the card flip doesn''t wait (out of scope, note in 04).
- Overlay pause (`pausedMedia`) and `replay()` keep working with the deferred start.

## Missing media notice (no more `Placeholder.svelte`)
- `Placeholder.svelte` is used once: the «medio no disponible (¿falta `trivia-media sync`?)» chip in `Question.svelte` (`task="IMG"`), a runtime fallback, not unfinished work.
- Replace it with a plain inline notice in `Question.svelte` (same text, same chip look, no `PLACEHOLDER · …` tag); delete `Placeholder.svelte`.
- Overlap with plan 21 (LUI-1), task 95 (moves `Placeholder.svelte` labels into the catalog as `placeholder.*`): whichever runs second adapts. If 95 ran first, the notice keeps its catalog key (rename `placeholder.*` → e.g. `question.mediaMissing`); if this runs first, 95 has no `Placeholder.svelte` left and catalogs the inline notice text.
- Docs (D-25 references): AGENTS.md "Placeholders" line, 04 "Implementation notes" (Placeholders bullet), `plans/project.md` ("One placeholder left", M3 row, UI-7 follow-up line) say none are left; D-25 itself stays as history.

## Files
- `app/client/src/game/Game.svelte`, `Question.svelte`, `timing.ts`; delete `Placeholder.svelte`.
- `AGENTS.md`, `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` (UI-7 note), `plans/project.md`.

## Tasks (suggested split)
1. Preload: `ready()`/`start()` in Question, `go()` waits with `PRELOAD_MAX_MS`, no autoplay behind the black; remove `PLACEHOLDER(UI-7)`.
2. Missing-media notice inline, delete `Placeholder.svelte`, update the D-25 references and project.md; UI-7 note in 04.

## Done when
- `grep -rn PLACEHOLDER app/client/src` is empty; `npm run check` and `npm run build` pass.
- Dev browser, throttled network (DevTools "Slow 4G") and a large video/image: the fade waits for the media, never longer than 2 s; video and audio start with the fade-in, not behind the black.
- Missing file (`/media` 404): fade in after at most 2 s, the «medio no disponible» notice shows.
- Text questions and screens without media fade in as fast as today.
- No new dependencies.', '', '2026-10-12T00:33:12Z', 134);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (32, 6, 'Recorded sound effects (UI-10)', 200, 'Replaces the effects that are still synthesized with CC0 (or D-45 allowlisted) recordings, mainly from Kenney.nl, and gives Soplo''s paper rustle and the token pop-back a sound. Then (masterplan part 7, `decision 81: Recorded sound effects: approve on the TV?`) three jokers get a sound that says what the joker does. Owner plan file: `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` ("Sound assets", UI-10); joker sounds: `plans/09-jokers.md` ("Sound assets", JK-9). Music loops: `plan 33: Recorded music loops (UI-10)`, which reuses this plan''s pipeline and audition aid.

## Status
- Built (tasks 142–145): every listed effect recorded, none kept synthesized; recipes stay as the fallback.
- TV check answered (`decision 81: Recorded sound effects: approve on the TV?`): all approved except three jokers (below).

## Scope (done)
- Effects formerly synthesized (`app/client/src/game/sound.svelte.ts`, `RECIPES`):
  - whooshes: `whoosh`, «swoosh que sube», `swoosh|escoba` («escoba: fuuush»)
  - `pop|carta` (card pick), `menú abierto` / `menú cerrado`, `desbloqueado`, `listo|hola`
  - jokers: `comodín` shimmer, `comodín: preparado`, `comodín: abrir`, `silbato`, `trituradora`, `latido`, `rebobinar`, `mira: tic`, `disparo|corcho`, `rasgado` (envelope tear)
  - fireworks: `cohete`, `cañón de confeti`, `bengalas`, `estrellas`
- Formerly silent: Soplo''s note rustle (`rustle`), token pop-back (`token-back`).
- Out of scope: music (plan 33, soundtracks: masterplan part 6).

## Joker sounds that say what the joker does (developer, 2026-10-17, decision 81)
- Paso y fuera (Pass & Purge, `skip`): a broom sweeping; the sweep''s cue `swoosh` (`escoba.m4a`) doesn''t read as a broom
- Soplo (Hint, `hint`): a microwave bell «bing» when the joker plays
- Hada madrina (Fairy, `easier`): a fairy''s magic wand sprinkling fairy dust; replaces the swanee whistle (`whistle-down` → `silbato.m4a`, `Game.svelte`)
- Doña Exigente (Ms Picky), Tiro mágico (Trick Shot): unchanged
- Shared files stay for their other users: `escoba` (category splash `splash-right`, `splash-wind`; `plan 181: Category splash on the question screen`, approved), `silbato` (`splash-drain`; `whistle-down` on a wrong answer in `Timed.svelte`), `susurro-papel` (`rustle`: the note sliding in, also Timed''s automatic hints). So: new files and new cues for the joker call sites only (e.g. `barrido`, `microondas`, `varita`; ASCII), each with a tiny synth recipe as fallback and in the `/?efectos` list
- Soplo: the bing on play, the rustle stays when the note lands (drop it only if the two clash)
- No new joker sounds in `timed` (no jokers there)

## Sources and licences
- Kenney.nl CC0 first (Interface Sounds, UI Audio, Impact Sounds, Casino Audio, Sci-fi Sounds), then Freesound CC0, OpenGameArt CC0; D-45 allowlist only (CC0 preferred; CC BY ok with credit; no NC/ND/unknown); licence checked on each source page.
- Download once by hand (a downloaded pack zip is not committed); keep only the converted files.

## Pipeline (as tasks 143–145)
- `nix shell nixpkgs#ffmpeg-headless` (not a project dependency).
- Trim silence, short fade-out, loudness-normalize (`loudnorm`, ~-16 LUFS, -1.5 dBTP, as the existing files), mono AAC 80k `.m4a` unless stereo matters.
- Files: `app/client/public/audio/<spanish-name>.m4a` (flat), committed.
- `app/client/public/audio/CREDITS.md`: one row per file (source URL, pack, author, licence); the Credits screen and the release check''s credits step read it.
- Budget: ≤ 40 kB per effect file; the three new files ≤ 100 kB together; within `app/desktop/media-budget.json` (shipped WebP/Opus via `stage-media.mjs`).

## Wiring
- `SAMPLE_NAMES` + `SAMPLE_FOR` entries per file; `rate` callback where pitch should vary.
- Recipes stay as the fallback (missing file, decode failure).

## Audition aid (done, task 142)
- `/?efectos` on the Start screen: every effect with «grabado» / «sintetizado»; plan 33 added the music loops.

## Tasks
1. Done: 142 audition aid, 143 whooshes/pops/menu/desbloqueado/hola, 144 joker sounds + rustle + pop-back, 145 fireworks.
2. Joker sounds that say what the joker does: broom (Paso y fuera), microwave bing (Soplo), fairy wand (Hada madrina): source, convert, wire to the joker call sites only, credit; JK-9 note and "Sound assets" in `plans/09-jokers.md`.
3. `task 146: Gamemaster check of the recorded effects on the TV`, after 2: decision 81 is answered (the other effects approved); a new developer decision for the three swapped joker sounds (`/?efectos` and a real game on the TV: Paso, Soplo, Hada madrina; options «approve» / «changes: …»); apply the answer; update UI-10''s note in 04 (effects part). UI-10 closes in `task 150: Close UI-10 in the plans` after the soundtracks (masterplan part 6).

## Done when
- Every listed effect is a recording or deliberately kept synthesized (noted in UI-10).
- Paso y fuera sweeps like a broom, Soplo bings, Hada madrina sprinkles fairy dust; the splash and Timed keep their sounds.
- `CREDITS.md` has a row per file; within budget; `npm run check` and `npm run build` pass.
- The developer approved the three joker sounds on the TV.', 'The game''s sound effects started out as tones generated by code; this work replaced them with real, freely licensed recordings so the game sounds lively on a living-room TV. After listening, the developer asked for three of the joker power-ups to get sounds that say what they do: a broom sweeping, a microwave bell, and a fairy''s magic wand. Those three are swapped in and checked on the TV again.', '2026-10-12T00:34:28Z', 135);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (33, 6, 'Recorded music loops (UI-10)', 190, 'Replaces the three generated music loops (`normal`, `question`, `submitted`) with CC0 (or D-45 allowlisted) recordings, as one matched set: one theme at three intensities, same key and tempo family, gapless. Owner plan file: `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` ("Music", "Sound assets", UI-10). Runs after plan 32 "Recorded sound effects (UI-10)", whose pipeline, budget conventions and `/?efectos` audition aid it reuses; Part 3 of `plan 6: masterplan`.

## Outcome of the TV check (2026-10-17)
- `decision 83: Recorded music loops: approve on the TV?`: the recordings sound better, the vibe is wrong; this set stays as it is, as one soundtrack among several
- Follow-up is `plan 182: Soundtracks` (Part 6), not this plan: more recorded sets, the «Banda sonora» picker, the default (synthesized until the developer picks), the rename of this set''s files to `musica-variaciones-*.m4a`, the `audio` budget in `media-budget.json` (replaces the 3.5 MB folder note below)
- Nothing left to change in this set''s audio, loop points, level or cut
- UI-10 closes after `plan 182: Soundtracks` and the joker sounds of `plan 32: Recorded sound effects (UI-10)` (Part 7)

## Scope (as built)
- Generated loops in `app/client/src/game/sound.svelte.ts` (`startTrack`, `generate()`): A minor i–VI–III–V at 76/96/120 bpm; they stay as the fallback and, per plan 182, as the `sintetizada` soundtrack
- Replaced: `normal`, `question`, `submitted`, by OpenGameArt «Music loop variations» (obscure music, CC0), 100 bpm, 8 bars = 19.2 s, −18 LUFS
- Out of scope: `roll` (`redoble.m4a`), `victory` (`victoria.m4a`), effects (plan 32)
- Behaviour as in 04 "Music": 600/800 ms fades, ~80 ms cuts `question` ↔ `submitted` (beat continues), cut to `roll` on submit, ducking for jokers

## Sources, pipeline, wiring (done: tasks 147, 148)
- D-45 allowlist; downloaded by hand, only converted files committed
- `nix shell nixpkgs#ffmpeg-headless`; whole bars, loudness-normalized like `redoble.m4a`, AAC `.m4a`, loop points in `sound.svelte.ts`
- Files `musica-normal.m4a`, `musica-pregunta.m4a`, `musica-enviada.m4a` (renamed by plan 182), `CREDITS.md` rows; 707 kB together
- `/?efectos`: «grabado» / «sintetizado» per loop, «corte», «parar» (plan 182 makes it per soundtrack)

## Tasks
1. Source a matched set; credit rows (done, task 147)
2. Convert, loop points, wire with synth fallback, `/?efectos` (done, task 148)
3. `task 149: Gamemaster check of the music loops on the TV`: answered by decision 83; nothing to apply in this set (the changes are plan 182''s); close it with a note pointing to plan 182
4. `task 150: Close UI-10 in the plans`: after `plan 182: Soundtracks` and plan 32''s joker sounds; UI-10 `[x]` in 04 with a note (effects recorded, joker sounds per decision 81, music as soundtracks: recorded sets plus the synthesized one, default as picked), `plans/project.md` line, 04 "Sound assets": flat folder (`music/`, `sfx/` subfolders never used), `CREDITS.md`, the `audio` budget of `media-budget.json` (`stage-media.mjs --check`) instead of the 3.5 MB note

## Done when
- This set plays gapless as recorded, synth fallback with the files removed, `CREDITS.md` rows (done)
- Task 149 closed per decision 83; task 150 done after plan 182 and plan 32''s joker sounds: UI-10 `[x]` in 04, `plans/project.md` updated
- Per commit: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`', 'The game used to make its own background music with simple synthesized sounds; this work replaced it with one free recorded piece that comes in a calm, a tense and a most tense version. The family heard it on the TV and found it sounded better but had the wrong mood, so it stays as one of several music sets to choose from, built separately. What remains here is to close the check and, once the other music sets and the new joker sounds are in, mark the sound work as finished.', '2026-10-12T00:35:05Z', 136);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (34, 7, 'Desktop shell (OQ-29)', 700, 'Part 1 of the masterplan (plan 7): decide the desktop shell that turns the built client into a Steam game (OQ-29, SW-1). Decision only; no shell code (S3 is out of scope).

- Owner: `plans/18-steam-integration.md` ("Desktop shell" table: Electron + steamworks.js recommended, Tauri, browser + local server).
- Context: the shell only shows `app/client/dist/` and saves one file once the TS engine runs without Python (milestone 2, plans 19 and 20; `plans/12-client-engine.md`). Not a blocker for the decision.

## Tasks
1. **Prep: refresh facts, write the decision**
   - Facts (with sources and dates): steamworks.js maintenance status (last release, open issues, Electron versions supported, alternatives such as steamworks-ffi or the Steamworks SDK via a native module); Electron install size today; Tauri v2 state on Windows (WebView2) and Linux/Deck (WebKitGTK: media, `backdrop-filter`); Steam overlay in Electron (known workarounds) and over a system webview; Deck/Proton notes (native Linux build vs. Windows build via Proton).
   - OQ-37 (part 8) as a dependency, not a blocker: phones as buzzers would need a LAN server inside the shell (Electron: Node `http` in the main process; Tauri: Rust side; browser + local server: already has one). Say how each option handles it.
   - `pm decision add "Desktop shell (OQ-29)?"` with the recommended option first; body = facts + trade-offs, ultra-short. Then `pm task-pending-decision` on task 2.
   - Update the "For/Against" cells in plan 18''s table if the facts changed (still marked draft).
2. **Follow-up: record the answer** (waits for the decision)
   - D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` (next free D-number).
   - OQ-29 moved to "Resolved" in `plans/open-questions.md` with the D-number.
   - Plan 18: table marked decided (D-number); SW-1 `[x]` with a note; SW-2..SW-6 checked against the choice and reworded if needed (e.g. electron-builder → Tauri bundler; preload bridge → Tauri commands).
   - `plans/11-steam.md` open-questions row and `plans/project.md` kept in sync (the full S3–S6 rewrite stays with part 10, the S2 close-out).

## Done when
- Decision answered; D-entry exists; OQ-29 resolved; SW-1 `[x]`; plan 18''s table says decided; SW-2..SW-6 match the choice.', '', '2026-10-12T00:39:17Z', 162);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (35, 7, 'Game modes: record the answers (OQ-30, MD-5)', 600, 'Part 2 of the masterplan (plan 7): record the gamemaster''s answer to OQ-30 and write the spec MD-6/MD-7 (plan 36) and MD-10..MD-12 (plan 59) build on. No new decisions: decisions 19 and 20 plus milestone 7''s "Game modes" are the answer. There is no "default mode"; there are five modes. Old drafts (presets Fácil/Normal/Difícil/Experto, checkpoints, «Saltar y quemar para todos» outside gamemaster mode) are dropped. No code.

- Owner: `plans/13-game-modes.md` ("Modes", "Implementation notes").
- Answers: decision 19 (no presets, no difficulty selection, no checkpoint; standard joker set; "Customize game" button; achievements only uncustomized), decision 20 (outside gamemaster mode no skip ever; «Reportar pregunta» only logs; no undo, no joker changes mid-game; abandon and sound stay).
- Multiplayer modes: plan 41 (OQ-37) writes their specs; here only their one-line entries and ids.
- Age groups (D-38, plans 27, 28): the mode never shifts the age-group window; only the chosen age group does. No change to plan 21 or `age-groups.json`.
- Existing pieces: `settings.jokers` (MD-1..MD-4, `null` = unlimited); today''s game = gamemaster mode.

## Tasks
1. **Record the answers (OQ-30, MD-5)**
   - D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` (next free D-number): the five modes (one entry, or one per mode family), rules shared by all non-gamemaster modes, achievements only outside gamemaster mode and customized games; input: gamepads, keyboard, mouse, no phones.
   - OQ-30 → "Resolved" in `plans/open-questions.md` with the D-number.
   - `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Modes": one section per mode (gamemaster mode, «Solo o en grupo», round-robin co-op, round-robin competitive, competitive timed) as in milestone 7; "Default mode" section removed; MD-5 `[x]` with a note.
   - Plan 13 "Implementation notes", spec for MD-6/MD-7:
     - `settings.mode`: the five ids (e.g. `gamemaster`, `solo`, `rr-coop`, `rr-competitive`, `timed`); missing = `gamemaster`, old saves unchanged.
     - Standard joker set as one engine constant: 3 × Soplo, 1 × each other joker.
     - `settings.customized`: set by any change via "Customize game"; feeds achievements (S5).
     - Refusals outside gamemaster mode: undo, skip, replace, joker changes.
     - `ReportRow`: logs the question to a local report list; no burn, no replacement.
   - Sync `plans/11-steam.md` open-questions row and `plans/project.md`.

## Done when
- D-entry exists; OQ-30 resolved; MD-5 `[x]`; plan 13 has one section per mode and the implementation notes above; no preset or checkpoint left in plan 13.', '', '2026-10-12T00:39:47Z', 163);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (36, 7, 'Reportar pregunta and mode screen (MD-6, MD-7)', 490, 'Part 3 of the masterplan (plan 7): «Solo o en grupo» becomes playable next to the gamemaster mode. MD-6 «Reportar pregunta» only logs the question to a local report list; MD-7 is the mode screen between Player and Level. Owner: `plans/13-game-modes.md` (MD-6, MD-7, "Implementation notes"). The spec comes from part 2 (plan 35, decisions 19 and 20): `settings.mode`, the standard joker set, `settings.customized`, refusals, `ReportRow`. This plan doesn''t re-decide them. There is no default mode, no preset and no checkpoint.

## Depends on (tasks wait; no second implementation in `app/server/game.py`)
- Plan 35 (task 373): plan 13''s "Implementation notes" written as the spec, MD-5 `[x]`. If not, the task stops and says so in its note (leave it open).
- Plan 20 (PORT-3): `engine/game.ts`, `engine/api.ts`, `SaveData` / `GameState` in `engine/state.ts`.
- M2 part 4 (save document, stores, migration, PORT-4/5) for the `version` bump; plan 50 (PORT-7): screens call the engine. If either hasn''t landed, stop and say so in the note (no `pm task drop`).
- Plan 21 (LUI-1): new strings via `t()` (`mode.*`, `report.*` keys); mode names English first, Spanish forms from plan 37 (OQ-31). Missing catalog: Spanish literals marked `// LUI-1`.
- Plan 29 (Choice screen between Player and Level, priority 400): MD-7 builds on that screen, no second screen. Hence task 3''s priority 380 (after plans 29 and 30).
- Plan 44 (action layer, done): every new screen and dialog on `input.svelte.ts` scopes (tasks 348, 349).
- Plan 59 (gamemaster configure screen and menu, 480) builds on task 1''s `settings.mode`; this plan keeps the gamemaster overlay exactly as today.

## Decisions taken here (within plan 13''s spec)
- **Mode is a game setting**: `settings.mode` with plan 13''s ids; this plan builds `gamemaster` and `solo`. Missing = `gamemaster` (`withDefaults`), so old saves and fixtures are unchanged.
- **Jokers**: `solo` fills `settings.jokers` from the engine''s standard-set constant (3 × Soplo, 1 × each other joker); `settings.customized: false` unless the "Customize game" button changed something.
- **Rules live in the engine**, not only in the UI: outside `gamemaster` mode `undo`, skip (any kind), replace and `setJokers` return `409` with a reason; abandon and sound stay. `report` is allowed in every mode (in gamemaster mode too: it only logs).
- **«Reportar pregunta» only logs**: `ReportRow {question_id, game_id, player_id, level, reported_on, note?}` in `SaveData.reports`. No burn, no replacement, no change to the game state; the question stays on screen and the player answers or uses a joker. Reporting the same question twice in one game is a no-op. Confirm step («¿Reportar esta pregunta? Queda anotada; la pregunta sigue.»), Enter/Esc.
- **Report list is a client screen**, not a server route (decision 4): reachable from the overlay; newest first: date, question id, question text, answer, player; «Copiar» copies plain text (one block per report) via `navigator.clipboard`, selectable `<pre>` fallback. Works offline.
- **Mode screen (MD-7)** = plan 29''s Choice screen: a mode row listing the built modes (gamemaster mode, «Solo o en grupo»; multiplayer modes appear when built, plan 41/MD-8/MD-9). Launch option `?mode=gamemaster|solo` presets it (the desktop shell, S3, passes it). Preset from the player''s newest game like plan 29''s age group; new player / fresh save = `gamemaster` until S3 decides the Steam build''s default. The family: Enter straight through = today''s game.
- **«Solo o en grupo»** on that screen: age group only (no difficulty selection, no preset row), plus a small «Personalizar partida» button: a dialog with the joker counts (0–9 / ∞, same steppers as MD-4); any change sets `settings.customized`. Further customizable fields only if plan 13 lists them.
- **Overlay by mode**: gamemaster mode exactly as today plus «Reportar pregunta» / «Preguntas reportadas» (plan 59 grows it into the gamemaster menu); `solo`: sound, «Reportar pregunta», «Preguntas reportadas», «Abandonar partida», read-only joker line; no undo, no skip/burn, no budget editor.

## Tasks
1. **Engine: mode, standard set, report (MD-6 engine part)**
   - `engine/state.ts`: `settings.mode`, `settings.customized`, `ReportRow`, `SaveData.reports`; version bump + migration step in part 4''s store (`reports: []`, games untouched).
   - `engine/game.ts` / `api.ts`: `newGame` accepts `mode` (+ joker overrides → `customized`) and fills `settings.jokers`; `report` action (log only); refusals outside gamemaster mode; `view` exposes `settings.mode` / `customized`; `lib/types.ts` to match.
   - Check: `npm test` (fixture replay unchanged: gamemaster mode identical), `npm run check`; throw-away script: `solo` game gets the standard set, report adds a row and leaves the game state unchanged, undo/skip/replace/setJokers refused with `409`, old save migrates with `reports: []`.
2. **«Reportar pregunta» and the report list (MD-6 UI)**
   - `Overlay.svelte` by mode; confirm step; `Reports.svelte` (new) list + «Copiar»; `Game.svelte` routing (`Screen` gains `"reports"`, back with Backspace/Esc); `lib/api.ts`. Dialog and list on the action layer (task 348).
   - Check: browser walk in both modes (gamemaster overlay otherwise unchanged; `solo`: report → confirm → same question stays, list shows it, copy works); keyboard only and mouse only (IN-1).
   - Then plan 13 MD-6 `[x]` with a note.
3. **Mode screen (MD-7)**, priority 380 (after plan 29''s Choice screen)
   - `Choice.svelte`: mode row, «Solo o en grupo» = age group + «Personalizar partida» button/dialog, `newGame({…, mode, jokers?})`; `?mode=` launch option; mode from the newest game. Screen and dialog on the action layer (task 349).
   - Docs: plan 13 MD-7 `[x]` and "Implementation notes" (fields as built); `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` (Choice section, Reports screen, overlay by mode, keys); `directory.md` (new files); `plans/project.md` if MD-6/MD-7 are listed.
   - Check: Enter straight through on an existing family save plays today''s game; a `solo` game starts with the standard set and `customized: false`; a change in «Personalizar partida» sets `customized: true`; `?mode=solo` presets the row.

## Done when
- In «Solo o en grupo» a report is logged and listed and the question stays; skip, undo, replace and joker edits are refused.
- The mode screen starts a «Solo o en grupo» game with the standard joker set.
- A gamemaster-mode game plays exactly as today (fixture replay passes, overlay unchanged apart from the report entries, Enter straight through).', '', '2026-10-12T00:41:03Z', 164);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (37, 7, 'Launch languages and Spanish variety (OQ-31)', 500, 'Part 4 of the masterplan (plan 7): decide which languages the Steam release launches with and which Spanish the pool speaks (OQ-31, I18N-1). Decision only; no code, no translation. Owner: `plans/15-i18n.md` ("Model", "Spanish varieties"), with `15a-ui-translation.md` (LUI-*), `15b-question-translation.md` (QT-*), `15c-regional-questions.md` (RG-5).

## Context
- Today: everything Spanish, Colombian usage and references where natural (D-6). Bundles replace 15c''s `region` (D-39): `colombia` holds what needs a real connection to Colombia, `base` holds the rest (D-49 moved Colombian-subcategory `base` questions out).
- D-50: store name «Living Room Trivia», Spanish localized «Trivia en Familia» (chosen partly because «sala»/«salón» splits Spanish); other languages get a localized name when they launch.
- Status: pm decision 26 answered: Spanish, English and German at launch; Simplified Chinese, Russian, Portuguese (Brazil) later, in milestone 12 "Conquer the world" (on hold). Decision 27 (Spanish variety, store languages) pending.
- Mode names are English first (milestone 7); their Spanish forms come with i18n (this part, milestone 3''s catalog). Fixed so far: Alone or as group = «Solo o en grupo».
- Feeds part 5 (OQ-32, content target per language, plan 38) and part 10 (S4''s exit in `plans/11-steam.md`, plan 43).
- Related: plan 24 "Draft en catalog (LUI-3)" (milestone 3) drafts `en.ts`; with English at launch it becomes launch work.

## Tasks
1. **Prep: facts, options and recommendation as pm decisions** (done, task 189: decisions 26 and 27)
2. **Follow-up: record the answer** (waits for decision 27; 26 is answered)
   - D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` (next free D-number): launch languages es, en, de; later zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR (milestone 12, on hold); the Spanish variety and Steam store languages from decision 27.
   - OQ-31 moved to "Resolved" in `plans/open-questions.md` with the D-number.
   - `plans/15-i18n.md`: "Spanish varieties" bullet decided, launch languages stated, I18N-1 `[x]` with a note; status no longer "stub" if the model is settled.
   - `15a`: LUI-5 names es, en, de; `15b`: QT-6 and the intro name en and de as launch targets, zh-Hans/ru/pt-BR as later (milestone 12); `15c`: RG-5 checked against the answer.
   - Mode names: the five modes'' Spanish forms listed for the catalog in `15a` (and named in `plans/13-game-modes.md`): «Solo o en grupo» fixed; the others proposed, flagged as proposals for the gamemaster.
   - If decision 27 changes `base` wording (neutral Spanish): log the rewrite as a backlog row in `plans/backlog.md` (S4 content work, through the pipeline, D-36), no pool edits here.
   - Plan 24 "Draft en catalog (LUI-3)": English is a launch language → keep; one-line note in its body (`pm plan edit 24 --body`) that `en.ts` ships at launch and German (`de.ts`) follows the same path.
   - Content per language (en, de) is part 5''s (plan 38) and S4''s; this part only states the languages.
   - `plans/11-steam.md` open-questions row and `plans/project.md` kept in sync (S4''s exit wording stays with part 10).

## Done when
- Decisions 26 and 27 answered; D-entry exists; OQ-31 resolved; I18N-1 `[x]`; 15/15a/15b name the launch languages (es, en, de); plan 24 noted as launch work; the mode names'' Spanish forms listed for the catalog.', '', '2026-10-12T00:41:48Z', 165);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (38, 7, 'Content target per player and language (OQ-32)', 590, 'Part 5 of the masterplan (plan 7). OQ-32 asked how many games a new player gets before questions repeat, per launch language, and how good the release pool must be. The gamemaster answered (pm decision 21): no games number; D-52''s 5000 with D-53''s mix per launch language is the target, and CT-2 (`qgen report --simulate`, S4, milestone 9) reports games per player for information only. Owner: `plans/16-content-target.md` (CT-1).

## Inputs (all answered)
- Pm decision 21: target = 5000 approved per launch language, D-53''s per-level mix (`authoring/data/targets.json`); no games-per-player bar.
- Pm decision 26 (plan 37, OQ-31): launch languages Spanish, English, German; later ones (zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR) in milestone 12, on hold, no target now.
- Game modes (milestone 7, plans 35, 41): no presets, no "default mode". Burns per game only feed CT-2''s information: «Solo o en grupo» and round-robin co-op = 12 + the standard joker set''s burns (3 × Soplo, 1 × each other joker); round-robin competitive ≈ N × that; competitive (timed) ≈ 1 shared question per round, no jokers. The mode never shifts the age-group window.
- Decision 21''s body used the old Normal-preset estimate; its answer sets no games number, so no corrected decision is needed.
- Quality bar: D-56 and pm decision 2 (milestone 1), release bar plan 57 (CT-5, pm decision 15). No new numbers here.

## Tasks
1. **Prep: estimate and decision** — done (task 191, pm decision 21).
2. **Record the answer** (task 192; can start now)
   - D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` (next free number): 5000 per launch language (es, en, de) with D-53''s mix; no games number; CT-2 (S4) reports games per player per mode for information (burns as in "Inputs").
   - OQ-32 moved to "Resolved" in `plans/open-questions.md`.
   - `plans/16-content-target.md`: "Target" decided (5000 × D-53 mix per launch language; whether a translation counts as a full pool follows plan 37''s D-entry, else name it open); "Quality bar" points to D-56 and plan 57 (CT-5); presets / "default mode" wording replaced by the modes; "Where we stand" refreshed; CT-1 `[x]` with a note that CT-2 (S4) reports games per player; status no longer stub.
   - `plans/project.md` in sync; `plans/11-steam.md` S4 exit names the target if it mentions one.

## Done when
- D-entry; OQ-32 resolved; CT-1 `[x]`; 16''s target section is decided.', '', '2026-10-12T00:42:23Z', 166);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (39, 7, 'Price model and Steamworks account (OQ-33)', 300, 'Part 6 of the masterplan (plan 7). OQ-33 asks how the game is sold on Steam (paid, free, or free with paid packs) and who holds the Steamworks account (a person or a company, with its tax consequences). The answer is a decision, not code; the signup and the price setting themselves stay S5 tasks (PUB-6, PUB-11). Owner: `plans/17-publishing.md` ("Steamworks and store"). Not legal or tax advice: the decision body names where a professional must check.

## Depends on
- Nothing blocks the prep. Feeds plan "Code and content licence (OQ-35)" (part 7: a paid game with a public pool is a different trade-off) and plan "Freesound API for a commercial release (OQ-45)" (part 9: whether the release is "commercial").
- Related: D-39/D-49 bundles (`colombia` as a candidate paid DLC), D-50 (store names), plan 38 "Content target per player and language (OQ-32)" (how much content a base game vs a pack carries).

## Tasks
1. **Prep: facts, options and recommendation as a pm decision**
   - Facts (numbers in the decision body, one source line each; Valve''s Steamworks docs first):
     - Steam fees and payout: revenue share (30 % → 25 % above $10 M → 20 % above $50 M), $100 app credit per app (recouped after $1,000 gross), DLC costs no app credit; monthly payout threshold and timing; refunds (2 h / 14 days); VAT/sales tax handled by Valve.
     - Regional pricing: Valve''s recommended price matrix; what a USD price band means in COP/MXN/ARS/EUR (Spanish-speaking markets, plan 37).
     - Comparable trivia/party games on Steam: 5–8 titles with price and review count (e.g. Trivia Murder Party via Jackbox packs, Quiplash-like, smaller solo trivia titles); note which use DLC question packs.
     - Free-to-play on Steam: what "free" means for wishlists, visibility and refund-free reviews; free + paid DLC (bundles as DLC per D-39: `colombia`, later bundles) vs paid base + paid DLC.
     - Account holder: person (individual tax interview, W-8BEN for non-US, income in personal tax return, real name/address visible to Valve; store "Developer/Publisher" can still be a label) vs company (W-8BEN-E, company formation and bookkeeping cost, liability). Flag for a tax advisor: country of residence, US withholding under the treaty, VAT/Kleinunternehmer-like thresholds, whether a hobby income needs registration.
   - Options (one decision, or two if too big: "Price model (OQ-33)" and "Steamworks account holder (OQ-33)"):
     - (a) Price model: paid, low band (e.g. $4.99–$7.99) with regional pricing (recommended unless the facts say otherwise: one-time purchase, no store/IAP code, fits a living-room game); free; free base + paid DLC bundles; paid base + paid DLC bundles later.
     - (b) Account: person (recommended for a hobby launch, cheapest) vs company; name what would trigger switching later (Steamworks allows transferring an app to another partner account, check the doc).
   - Each option states its consequence for part 7 (licence: paid + public pool → anyone can copy the content; free → public pool costs nothing) and part 9 (paid or DLC → "commercial" under Freesound/CC NC terms; free still counts as distribution).
   - Recommended option first; body = context + facts + trade-offs, ultra-short. Never contact Valve or an advisor; if a question for an advisor is needed, put its text in the decision body for the gamemaster.
   - `pm task-pending-decision` on task 2 for each decision.
2. **Follow-up: record the answer** (waits for the decision(s))
   - D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` (next free D-number); note the professional checks still owed.
   - OQ-33 moved to "Resolved" in `plans/open-questions.md` with the D-number; `plans/11-steam.md` open-questions row and `plans/project.md` kept in sync (S5 wording stays with part 10).
   - `plans/17-publishing.md`: "Steamworks and store" account bullet decided; PUB-6 rewritten to the holder (person/company, which tax form, app credit, any advisor check before signup); PUB-11 rewritten to the price model (price band, regional pricing, launch discount, DLC pricing if bundles become DLC). Both stay S5 tasks, unchecked.
   - If the answer makes bundles DLC: one backlog row in `plans/backlog.md` (DLC depots/app IDs for bundles, S5, plan 18 SW tasks), no code here.

## Done when
- Decision(s) answered; D-entry exists; OQ-33 resolved; PUB-6 and PUB-11 match the answer and stay S5; parts 7 and 9 can read the consequence from the D-entry.', '', '2026-10-12T00:43:13Z', 167);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (40, 7, 'Code and content licence (OQ-35)', 290, 'Part 7 of the masterplan (plan 7). The repo is public on GitHub (D-17) but has no `LICENSE`, so today it is "all rights reserved" by default; the question pool (`authoring/data/questions.json`, `app/data/pool.json`, bundles) is public too. OQ-35 asks which licence the code and the questions get, and whether release content (new batches, translations, paid bundles) stays public. The answer is a decision, then a few files. Owner: `plans/17-publishing.md` ("Code and content license", PUB-4). Not legal advice: the decision body names where a professional must check.

## Depends on
- Plan 39 "Price model and Steamworks account (OQ-33)": its D-entry (paid / free / DLC bundles) changes the trade-off. Task 1 may gather facts before it, but writes the decision only once OQ-33 is answered; if it is still pending, `pm task-pending-decision` task 1 on OQ-33''s decision.
- Plan 26 "Licence data in the pool": media licences stay per file (CC BY, CC BY-SA, CC0, PD, Freesound CC0/CC BY); the repo licence never covers media. Bundled fonts keep their OFL (`app/client/public/fonts/OFL-*.txt`).
- Feeds plan "Freesound API for a commercial release (OQ-45)" only indirectly (commercial vs not is plan 39''s).

## Tasks
1. **Prep: options and recommendation as a pm decision**
   - Facts (one line each, with source): what "no licence" means on GitHub (ToS lets others view and fork, nothing else); MIT vs GPL-3.0 vs AGPL vs all rights reserved for a paid Steam game (GPL lets anyone rebuild and redistribute the game; MIT lets anyone ship a closed fork); CC BY-SA 4.0 vs CC BY-NC 4.0 vs reserved for the questions (SA/BY allow a competitor to resell the pool; NC blocks commercial reuse but not copying; copyright on short factual questions is thin, the curated set and hints/explanations are the protectable part); AI-generated text and copyright (drafted by Claude, reviewed by a person: protection uncertain, flag for a professional; links to PUB-10).
   - Pool size today (approved per bundle, `qgen report`), so the decision says what is at stake.
   - Options (code × questions × repo; one decision, or two if too big: "Licence (OQ-35)" and "Is release content public (OQ-35)"):
     - code: MIT (recommended if the game is paid: the value is the content, not the code; easy for contributors), GPL-3.0, all rights reserved.
     - questions: reserved (recommended if paid), CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, CC BY-SA 4.0.
     - repo: public code + current pool public, release content (new batches, translations, paid bundles) in a private repo or submodule; whole repo public; whole repo private before release.
   - Each option notes what it means for the build (`nix build .#app`, packaging step reading a private pool), for D-17''s "pool is public", and for existing forks (what is already public stays copyable under whatever was implied).
   - Recommended option first; body = context + facts + trade-offs, ultra-short. Never contact a lawyer; questions for one go in the body for the gamemaster.
   - `pm task-pending-decision` on task 2.
2. **Follow-up: record the answer** (waits for the decision)
   - D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` (next free D-number); amends D-17 if the pool or release content goes private.
   - OQ-35 moved to "Resolved" in `plans/open-questions.md`; `plans/11-steam.md` open-questions row and `plans/project.md` kept in sync.
   - `plans/17-publishing.md`: "Code and content license" section decided; PUB-4 `[x]` with a note once task 3 is done.
   - If release content goes private: one backlog row in `plans/backlog.md` (private content repo/submodule, how `qgen export` and the build find it, S4/S5); no restructuring here.
3. **Licence files and mentions** (after task 2)
   - `LICENSE` at the repo root with the code licence''s full text (or an "all rights reserved" notice).
   - A separate content licence file if the questions differ from the code (e.g. `LICENSE-content.md`: which paths it covers, i.e. `authoring/data/`, `app/data/`; that media and fonts keep their own licences per file).
   - `README.md`: short "License" section. `directory.md`: the new file(s).
   - `nix build .#app` still builds; the packaged `result/` includes the licence file(s) if the chosen licence requires it.

## Done when
- Decision answered; D-entry exists; OQ-35 resolved; PUB-4 `[x]`; `LICENSE` (and the content licence file, if any) exist and are linked from `README.md` and `directory.md`.', '', '2026-10-12T00:43:52Z', 168);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (41, 7, 'Multiplayer modes and input: record the answers (OQ-37)', 580, 'Part 8 of the masterplan (plan 7). OQ-37 is answered: pm decisions 23 and 24 plus milestone 7''s "Game modes" settle the three multiplayer modes and their input. No new decisions; this plan records and specs them. Building them stays "Later" (MD-8, MD-9, IN-6), outside S2. Owners: `plans/13-game-modes.md` (multiplayer mode sections) and `plans/14-input.md` (section 3, IN-6, IN-7).

## The answer (don''t re-decide)
- Round-robin co-op: players take turns; one team, one age group, one shared standard joker set (3 × Soplo, 1 × each other joker).
- Round-robin competitive: turns; each player their own independent game, own jokers, own age group.
- Competitive (timed): own tracks; everyone answers the same question at once, own input; 30 s; a hint every 8 s; no jokers; one age group; question difficulty = average of all players'' progress; wrong answer = out; three levels behind = out; first to level 12 wins; timeout = everyone loses; pulsing red frame in the last 3 s.
- All three: no skip, no undo, no joker changes mid-game; «Reportar pregunta» only logs (plan 36); achievements unless customized.
- Input: gamepads (one per player), keyboard, mouse; shared keyboard (one dedicated key per player takes keyboard and mouse until that turn ends); no phones.

## Depends on
- Nothing blocks it. Related: plan 35 (mode spec, `settings.mode`, standard joker set), D-28 (burning), D-38 (age-group windows).
- Feeds plan 38 (burn multiplier per mode) and plan 34 (shell needs: several gamepads via the Gamepad API and the shared keyboard; no LAN server).

## Tasks
1. **Record the answer** (task 202; decisions 23, 24 answered)
   - D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` (next free D-number): the three modes as above, input, burn multiplier per mode (round-robin co-op ≈ 1 game''s burns; round-robin competitive ≈ N ×; competitive timed ≈ 1 shared question per round, no joker burns), shell needs (none beyond several gamepads and the shared keyboard).
   - OQ-37 → "Resolved" in `plans/open-questions.md`; `plans/11-steam.md` open-questions row and `plans/project.md` in sync ("Later" wording stays with plan 43).
   - `plans/13-game-modes.md`: old "Competitive mode" and "Couch co-op" stubs → one spec section per multiplayer mode (turn order, jokers shared or per player, age groups, drop-out and win rules, timer, hint cadence, red frame, burning). MD-8 and MD-9 rewritten to build exactly them; unchecked, "Later".
   - `plans/14-input.md` section 3: per-player gamepads + shared keyboard; IN-7 `[x]` (no phones); IN-6 rewritten (join screen, player binding, shared-keyboard keys), stays "Later". No backlog row for phones.
   - `plans/16-content-target.md`: the burn multiplier line points to the D-entry.

## Done when
- D-entry exists; OQ-37 resolved; plans 13 and 14 spec the three modes and the input that MD-8, MD-9 and IN-6 build later; plans 34 and 38 can read shell needs and burn multipliers from the D-entry.', '', '2026-10-12T00:44:27Z', 169);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (42, 7, 'Freesound API for a commercial release (OQ-45)', 200, 'Part 9 of the masterplan (plan 7). Freesound''s API is free for non-commercial use; commercial apps need a licence from UPF. Our pipeline uses the API only to find sounds (MP-6, `authoring/tools/providers/freesound.py`); the game ships the picked CC0/CC BY files, never the API. Before a paid Steam release the gamemaster decides whether to ask Freesound, replace the Freesound picks, or keep Freesound for the family only. Owner: `plans/23-media-providers.md` (Freesound row, provider order, MP-6).

## Depends on
- Plan 39 "Price model and Steamworks account (OQ-33)": whether the release is "commercial" (paid, DLC). Prep doesn''t wait for it; the decision names it as a dependency.
- Plan 26 "Licence data in the pool" (`provider` per picked slot) makes the Freesound picks countable and excludable; until then count by `freesound.org` in the URLs.
- Related: SW-9 media bundle (`plans/18-steam-integration.md`), D-45 allowlist, D-36 (picks only through the review tool), D-17 (media cache keyed by URL).

## Tasks
1. **Housekeeping: give the Freesound question its own number**
   - `plans/open-questions.md` uses OQ-45 twice; the resolved one belongs to D-42. Renumber the open Freesound one to the next free number (OQ-47 as of 2026-10-11; check), keep D-42''s.
   - Update the Freesound references: `plans/open-questions.md`, `plans/23-media-providers.md` (Freesound row), `plans/project.md` (open-questions table), plan 7''s body and this plan''s subject/body (`pm plan edit`), any other hit of `grep -rn ''OQ-45'' plans`. Leave references meaning D-42''s OQ-45 as they are (e.g. D-42''s context in `decisions.md`).
   - Done when: each OQ number is used once; every Freesound reference uses the new one.
2. **Prep: facts, options and recommendation as a pm decision**
   - Facts (ultra-short, one source line each):
     - Freesound API terms of use and the commercial-licence page (what counts as "commercial use of the API"; whether using it in an internal authoring tool for a paid product counts); CC0/CC BY sound licences themselves allow commercial use with credit.
     - Count today: questions with a Freesound pick in `authoring/data/questions.json` and `app/data/pool.json`, by status (2026-10-11: 2 approved, q-0752, q-1016; the masterplan''s 9/6 needs a recount), plus how many future audio slots Freesound would fill (share of Freesound picks among audio picks in the last batches).
     - What Commons and other allowlisted sources (D-45) offer for those sounds: a quick review-tool search per question, no picks.
   - Options (recommended first; recommendation from the facts, e.g. replace if the count stays small):
     - (a) Replace the Freesound picks with allowlisted sources before release and drop Freesound from the audio order (`providers.ORDER`) or from release batches.
     - (b) Ask Freesound/UPF: the worker drafts the email (English, short: what the tool does, that only CC0/CC BY files ship, no API in the game, the expected volume, the question); the gamemaster sends it. The draft goes in the decision body.
     - (c) Keep Freesound in the current game only: tag its picks and exclude them from the Steam media bundle (SW-9); questions without their sound then don''t ship or need another pick.
   - Each option notes its consequence for plan 39''s answer (free release vs paid).
   - `pm decision add`, then `pm task-pending-decision` on task 3. Never contact Freesound/UPF.
3. **Follow-up: record the answer** (waits for the decision)
   - D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` (next free D-number); the Freesound OQ moved to "Resolved" in `plans/open-questions.md`; `plans/project.md` and `plans/11-steam.md`''s open-questions row in sync.
   - `plans/23-media-providers.md`: Freesound row and the "Which provider for which slot" table match the answer; MP-6 note updated.
   - If (a): add a task to this plan that re-picks each Freesound slot through the review tool (search modal, D-36; the gamemaster or `qgen` picks, never by hand in the pool) and then removes Freesound from the order; `qgen validate` passes.
   - If (b): add a task "send the email and record the reply" pending on the gamemaster; the provider stays until the reply.
   - If (c): add the exclusion rule to SW-9 in `plans/18-steam-integration.md`.

## Done when
- The OQ numbers are unique; D-entry exists; plan 23 and the provider order reflect the answer; a replacement, if chosen, is a task in this plan.', '', '2026-10-12T00:45:18Z', 170);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (43, 7, 'S2 close-out', 150, 'Part 10 of the masterplan (plan 7): the last step of milestone 7. Once parts 1, 2, 4–9 have their answers in `plans/decisions.md`, this plan brings the Steam master plan and the indexes in line with them, so S3–S6 (milestones 8–11) start from the decided product. Docs and pm only; no code.

