INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (50, 2, 'Screens on the engine (PORT-7)', 500, 'The game screens stop talking to the Python referee and run the TypeScript engine in the browser. `lib/api.ts` keeps its function signatures (`fetchGame`, `gameAction`, `playJoker`, `fetchPlayers`, `deletePlayer`, `fetchFlags`, `setFlag`), but each one now calls `engine/api.ts` on an in-memory save and persists it through `ServerStore` (`/api/save`). The client loads `pool.json` and the categories files as static files. The same change turns on plan 49''s `game.sqlite` → `game.json` migration at server start. Part 5 of masterplan 2 (PORT-7); part 6 (task 60, PORT-8) deletes the Python game routes afterwards. Source: `plans/12-client-engine.md`, PORT-7.

## Depends on
- Plan 19 (PORT-2): `rng.ts` (`seededRng`, `randomSeed`), `pool.ts` (`parsePool`, `loadCategories`).
- Plan 20 (PORT-3): `engine/api.ts` (`getGame`, `getPlayers`, `deletePlayer`, `gameAction` → `{status, body, save}`), `engineData`, `SaveData`.
- Plan 49 (PORT-4/5): `engine/save.ts` (`parseSave`, `setFlag`, `flaggedIds`), `lib/store.ts` (`ServerStore`), `app/server/save.py` (`migrate()`, `/api/save`), `authoring/tools/save_file.py` (authoring reads `game.json` once it exists).
- Plan 27 (age groups, 590), if it has landed first: `engineData` also takes `age-groups.json` / `bundles.json`. The loader then fetches them too; nothing else here changes.
- Plan 29 (choice screen, 400) builds on this plan: it needs the data files in the client and `lib/api.ts` on the engine.
- If a dependency''s files aren''t there yet, the task waits. No Python fallback.

## Decisions taken here
- **Data files: the server serves `app/data/` read-only at `/data/…`**, not copied by the Vite build.
  - Why: `qgen export` → reload the page is enough, with no `npm run build` after every batch. `dist/` can''t hold a stale pool, and `.#app` already ships `app/data/`.
  - `GET /data/<path>` in `app/server/main.py`: files under `paths.DATA` only (resolve + `is_relative_to`, like `send_static`), else `404 not_found`. GET only. It counts as "static files" (pm decision 4, D-59).
  - Vite dev proxy: add `"/data"` next to `"/api"` and `"/media"`.
  - URLs: `/data/pool.json`, `/data/bundles.json`, `/data/categories.json`, `/data/bundles/<id>/categories.json` (only bundles listed in `bundles.json`; a 404 means the bundle has no categories, like `categories.load()`).
- **Load once per page load.** `lib/engine.ts` (new) has `ready(): Promise<{data, save}>`, memoized: data files + `store.load()` in parallel, then `engineData(...)`, `parseSave(...)`. Python re-read `pool.json` per request; now a new export needs a page reload (F5). Note it in AGENTS.md "Pool" and README.
  - Load failure (server down, missing `pool.json`, newer save version): throw a readable `Error`, which the screens show the way they show a failed fetch today.
- **`lib/api.ts` stays the screens'' only door.** Same exports, same types, same errors, so `Game.svelte`, `Player.svelte` and `Question.svelte` don''t change (at most an import path).
  - One action at a time: a promise-chain mutex in `lib/engine.ts` (replaces the server''s `_lock`). The UI already awaits each call, so the mutex only guards double clicks.
  - Per action: `io = {rng: seededRng(randomSeed()), now: localIsoSeconds()}`. `now` must match Python''s `datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds")`: local time, no zone, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS`. Put it in `lib/engine.ts`, not the engine (no clock in the engine).
  - Status mapping, like `failure()` today: 200 → body; 400/409/404 with `error` → `GameError(code, params, message, supply)`. An exception thrown by the engine → `GameError("server_error", {}, "engine error: …", null)`, like the Python 500 body.
  - 200 → adopt the new save, then `await store.save(save)`. A failed save keeps the new in-memory save (the next action PUTs the whole document again) and throws `GameError(<server code, e.g. save_locked>)`, so the TV shows something is wrong. Non-200 → the save is unchanged and no PUT.
  - Read-only calls (`fetchGame`, `fetchPlayers`, `fetchFlags`) never PUT. `getGame` may return `withDefaults`-filled state; don''t save on read, as in Python.
  - Flags: `fetchFlags` → `flaggedIds(save)`; `setFlag` → `engine/save.ts` `setFlag(save, …, now)`, store, return `flaggedIds`. `/api/flags` is no longer called.
- **`fetchCategories` leaves `app/client/src/lib/api.ts`**: the game no longer needs `/api/categories`. Move it into `authoring/ui/src/lib/api.ts` (the authoring server keeps its own `/api/categories`). `call`, `json`, `post`, `GameError` stay exported for authoring.
- **Media unchanged:** `Question.svelte` keeps `/media?url=…`. Whether it becomes a plain static path (no download on miss, decision 4) is part 6 (task 60).
- **Switch-over in the same change** (plan 49 hand-off): `main.py` calls `save.migrate()` once before `serve_forever`. From then on the game writes only `state/game.json`; `game.sqlite` and `flags.json` stay as backups. The Python game routes stay until part 6 but nothing calls them. Rollback (plan 49): delete `game.json`, check out the commit before the switch.
- **Decision entry** (next D number in `plans/decisions.md`): the game data comes from `/data/` (read-only, served from `app/data/`, loaded once per page). The engine runs in the browser behind `lib/api.ts`. Each action is persisted by a whole-document PUT. The migration runs at server start from this change on.

## Files
- `app/server/main.py`: `/data/` route, `save.migrate()` at startup, docstring (routes, "reads app/data/ and serves it under /data/").
- `app/client/vite.config.ts`: proxy `/data`.
- `app/client/src/lib/engine.ts` (new): `ready()`, mutex, `io()`, `run(route)` (status mapping, persist).
- `app/client/src/lib/data.ts` (new): `loadEngineData()`, fetches the data files and builds `engineData`.
- `app/client/src/lib/api.ts`: game, player and flag functions on the engine; `fetchCategories` removed.
- `authoring/ui/src/lib/api.ts`: own `fetchCategories`.
- Screens (`app/client/src/game/*.svelte`): only if an import has to move; no markup, style or behaviour changes. `PLACEHOLDER(...)` (D-25) stays.
- Docs: `plans/decisions.md`, `plans/12-client-engine.md` (PORT-7), `directory.md` (new `lib/` files, `/data/`), AGENTS.md and README.md (reload after `qgen export`; `trivia` writes `state/game.json`).

## Safety (real save)
- Workers never start `trivia` on the real `state/` in this plan: the first start migrates for real. Every check sets `TRIVIA_STATE` (and `TRIVIA_MEDIA` if media is touched) to a temp dir and asserts it before starting the server.
- Rehearsals use a copy of `state/game.sqlite` (+ `flags.json`), with the original''s checksum compared before and after (as in plan 49).
- The real switch happens when the gamemaster starts `trivia` after pulling; task 3 tells them so in the decision body.

## Tasks to split into
1. **`/data/` route and data loader**: the route, Vite proxy, `lib/data.ts`, `fetchCategories` moved to authoring. Can land before the switch (screens still on Python). Check with a throw-away script against a server on a temp `TRIVIA_STATE`: `/data/pool.json` and every categories file 200, `/data/../server/main.py`, `/data/%2e%2e/…` and a missing file 404; `loadEngineData()` (run under `node` with a `fetch` shim that prefixes the server URL) gives the same category order as `categories.load()`. Then `trivia-authoring` start page and `/stats/categories` still load. `npm run check`, `npm run build`.
2. **Screens on the engine + switch-over** (needs plans 19, 20, 49 done): `lib/engine.ts`, the new `lib/api.ts`, `save.migrate()` in `main.py`, docstring, decision entry. Throw-away `node` check: a temp `TRIVIA_STATE` holding a copy of the real `game.sqlite`, the server started there (migration line printed), `lib/api.ts` imported with the `fetch` shim. Then: `fetchPlayers` matches the migrated players; `fetchGame` returns the running game, if any; a new game for a test player played through 12 levels with every joker once (hint, skip, skip+purge, easier, category, snipe), a wrong answer, `skip` for everyone, `undo`, `abandon`, `jokers` budget, flag/unflag, delete the test player. After each step, GET `/api/save` equals the in-memory save. Errors: an unavailable joker → `GameError` with its code; a forced PUT failure (stop the server) → readable error, and the next action after a restart persists. Original `state/game.sqlite` checksum unchanged. `npm test`, `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`. `nix build .#app` and `result/bin/trivia` on a temp `TRIVIA_STATE` serves `/`, `/data/pool.json`, `/api/save`.
3. **Browser check, test night, close-out** (needs task 2): if the worker has a browser tool, play a short game in it on a temp `TRIVIA_STATE` (admin overlay: undo, abandon, joker budget; every joker animation shows). Then raise a decision "Family test night on the TS engine". Body: what changed for the gamemaster (first `trivia` start migrates to `state/game.json`, `game.sqlite` kept; reload the page after `qgen export`; rollback steps) and the checklist: a full game, every joker, undo, abandon, admin overlay, flag a question and see it in `trivia-authoring`, players list and delete. Options: "test night played fine" (recommended), "problems (listed in the answer)". Make a close-out task (docs: PORT-7 `[x]` in `plans/12-client-engine.md` with date, `directory.md`, AGENTS.md, README.md) pending on it. On "problems": one fix task per problem in this plan, raise the decision again.

## Done when
- A full game, every joker, undo and the admin overlay work in the browser on the engine; no game call reaches `/api/game*`, `/api/players*` or `/api/flags` (check the server log).
- The first start migrates a copy of the family''s save, and the game continues it: same players, burns and running game.
- The gamemaster confirms a family test night on the TS engine (decision answered "fine").
- `npm test`, `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`, `nix build .#app` pass; no new dependencies; screens unchanged apart from imports.', '', '2026-10-12T03:23:36Z', 59);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (51, 2, 'Python server cleanup and docs (PORT-8)', 400, 'After the screens run on the TS engine (plan 50), the Python game server shrinks to what pm decision 4 / D-59 allows: static files plus `/api/save`. This plan deletes the Python referee (`game.py`, `selection.py`, `flags.py`, the game, player, flag and category routes), moves code only authoring still uses out of `app/server/`, makes `/media` cache-only, switches authoring to the TS engine for the supply check through Node (pm decision 5 / D-60), and updates the docs. Part 6 of masterplan 2 (PORT-8); the last part of milestone 2. Source: `plans/12-client-engine.md`, PORT-8.

## Depends on
- Plan 19 (PORT-2): `engine/selection.ts`, `engine/pool.ts`, runs under plain Node 22 (type stripping, `.ts` imports).
- Plan 49 (PORT-4/5): `app/server/save.py` (`/api/save`, `migrate()`), `authoring/tools/save_file.py` (authoring reads `game.json`, with an SQLite/`flags.json` fallback that this plan removes).
- Plan 50 (PORT-7): `/data/` route, screens on the engine, migration at server start, **family test night answered "fine"**. Nothing is deleted before that answer; until then the Python referee is the rollback.
- Plan 27 / task 124 (group windows, bundle filter): if it lands first, the Node supply entry point passes its extra options through; nothing else changes here.

## Decisions taken here
- **Final route set of `trivia`** (`app/server/main.py`): `GET /` + built client (static), `GET /data/…` (plan 50, read-only `app/data/`), `GET /media?url=…` (cache lookup, below), `GET/PUT /api/save` (plan 49). Everything else 404 `not_found`. Gone: `/api/game*`, `/api/players*`, `/api/flags`, `/api/categories`.
- **`/media` stays as a cache lookup, no download.** Still `?url=<file_url>`, still only URLs from `pool.json` (not an open proxy), file from `TRIVIA_MEDIA` or `404 {"error": "media_missing"}`; no network access in the game server.
  - Why not a plain `/media/<hash>.<ext>` path: the client would need SHA-1 (`crypto.subtle` is missing on plain-http LAN addresses) or a pool format change. A URL → file lookup in the cache is still static serving (D-59); `Question.svelte` stays untouched and already shows its media-failed state on an error.
  - `trivia` prints at start: `media: N of M pool files missing from the cache; run trivia-media sync --status approved` (nothing when complete).
  - Packaged `.#app`: the cache under `$XDG_DATA_HOME/trivia/media` starts empty, so a packaged game needs `TRIVIA_MEDIA` pointing at a synced cache. Accepted: `.#app` is a pre-Steam test build; the Steam build bundles media (plan 34).
- **Download code leaves `app/`.** `app/server/media_cache.py` keeps `cache_path`, `picked`, `pool_urls` (what the game needs). `http_get`, `cached`, `RateLimited`, `USER_AGENT`, `API_URL`, `TOKEN`, `WAIT_ON_RATE_LIMIT` move to `authoring/tools/download.py`. The Commons token code then never ships. `http_base.send_media` becomes cache-only; `authoring/server/main.py` overrides it to download on a miss (the review tool keeps today''s behaviour).
- **`categories.py` moves to `authoring/tools/categories.py`.** After `game.py` is gone only authoring imports it; the game reads categories as static files (plan 50). Imports in `qgen.py`, `media.py`, `concepts.py`, `batches.py`, `targets.py`, `authoring/server/main.py` stay `import categories` (same module name, now found via `authoring/tools/`); fix the comments.
- **Supply check via Node (D-60): `authoring/tools/supply.ts`**, run as `node authoring/tools/supply.ts`.
  - stdin: `{"questions": [...], "burned": [ids]}`; stdout: `{"per_level": 4, "ranges": {"1": [lo, hi], …}, "supply": [{level, range, candidates, missing}, …]}` = `selection.ts` `available` + `supply`, plus `LEVEL_RANGES` for qgen''s «Cambiazo» table.
  - Imports `../../app/client/src/engine/selection.ts` (authoring may import from `app/`); reads stdin with `node:process`, no other `node:` use. Not type-checked by `npm run check` (outside both workspaces); kept tiny, verified by running.
  - `authoring/tools/engine.py`: `supply(questions, burned)` → the parsed JSON via `subprocess.run(["node", …], input=…, check=True)`; Node missing or a non-zero exit → `SystemExit` with a readable message (`qgen report needs node: run inside the dev shell`).
  - `qgen report` (`burned_ids` from `save_file`, `available` + `supply`, `LEVELS`/`LEVEL_RANGES`/`in_range` for the «Cambiazo» table from `ranges`) and `authoring/server/overview.py` (`supply_for`, `PER_LEVEL`) use it. One Node call per report / start page load; the start page calls it once per player (or once with all players batched: `{"players": {name: burned}}` → `{name: supply}` if per-call startup proves slow, measure first).
  - `flake.nix`: `pkgs.nodejs_22` in the runtime inputs of `qgen` and `trivia-authoring`.
- **`selection.py` is deleted** (D-60): no Python copy. `STATE_DB`, `burned_ids`, `player_id` go with it; authoring uses `save_file.py`.
- **`flags.py` is deleted.** Flags live in `SaveData` (plan 49); `apply_flags` reads only `game.json` + `state/flags-applied.json`. `save_file.py` drops its SQLite/`flags.json` fallback: no `game.json` → no players, no burns, no flags. `state/flags.json` and `state/game.sqlite` stay on disk as backups; nothing reads them except `migrate()`.
- **`migrate()` survives `game.py`.** It used `game.init` to upgrade legacy schemas; copy that function (schema + the two `ALTER`/rename steps) into `save.py` as `_upgrade(con)`, run only on the temp copy. Reason: an old install (e.g. a packaged one under `$XDG_DATA_HOME`) may still start with only `game.sqlite`.
- **Fixture recorder is deleted** (`authoring/tools/record_fixtures.py` imports `game.py`). Fixtures in `app/client/src/engine/fixtures/` are frozen; `README.md` there says so (recorded from the Python referee up to commit `<sha of the deleting commit''s parent>`; to re-record, check out that commit). Replay tests keep running.
- **Decision entry** (next D number in `plans/decisions.md`): the final route set; `/media` as cache-only lookup and why; download code and `categories.py` moved to authoring; `selection.py`/`flags.py`/`game.py` deleted; recorder deleted, fixtures frozen; `migrate()` kept with its own schema upgrade; packaged build needs a synced `TRIVIA_MEDIA`. Related: D-17, D-25, D-35, D-47, D-59, D-60.

## Files
- Delete: `app/server/game.py`, `app/server/selection.py`, `app/server/flags.py`, `authoring/tools/record_fixtures.py`.
- Move: `app/server/categories.py` → `authoring/tools/categories.py`; download half of `app/server/media_cache.py` → `authoring/tools/download.py`.
- Change: `app/server/main.py` (routes, startup media line, docstring), `app/server/http_base.py` (cache-only `send_media`, docstring), `app/server/save.py` (`_upgrade`), `app/server/media_cache.py` (docstring).
- New: `authoring/tools/supply.ts`, `authoring/tools/engine.py`.
- Authoring: `authoring/tools/qgen.py`, `authoring/server/overview.py`, `authoring/server/main.py` (`send_media` override, `apply_flags`, imports), `authoring/server/media_stats.py`, `authoring/tools/media.py`, `authoring/tools/providers/*.py` (import `download`), `authoring/tools/save_file.py` (no fallback), `authoring/tools/layout.py` (docstring).
- `flake.nix`: Node for `qgen`, `trivia-authoring`.
- Client: only comments in `app/client/src/lib/types.ts` / `lib/api.ts` that point at `game.py` or the old routes.
- Docs: `plans/decisions.md`, `plans/01-architecture.md` (server = static + `/api/save`, engine in the browser, JSON save; strike D-4''s SQLite line with a pointer), `plans/12-client-engine.md` (PORT-8 `[x]`, every PORT task checked), `plans/19-repo-layout.md` (what `app/server/` holds), `plans/project.md` (milestone 2), `AGENTS.md` (Tech stack: state `state/game.json`, no SQLite; Commands: `qgen report` needs Node; media: sync before play is required), `directory.md`, `README.md` (game night: `trivia-media sync --status approved` is required now), `app/client/src/engine/fixtures/README.md`. Fix stale mentions in `plans/03-game-flow.md`, `05-gamemaster-controls.md`, `09-jokers.md`, `13-game-modes.md`, `23-media-providers.md`, `02-question-pool.md`, `11-steam.md` only where they describe current code (a pointer to the engine file; history stays).

## Safety (real save)
- Checks run on a temp `TRIVIA_STATE` (and temp `TRIVIA_MEDIA` where media is written), asserted before any server starts, as in plans 49/50. `state/` is never written by a worker.

## Tasks to split into
1. **Supply via Node** (needs plan 19 task 74 and plan 49 task 4): `supply.ts`, `engine.py`, `qgen report` and `overview.py` on it, `flake.nix` Node inputs. Before switching, a throw-away script compares `engine.supply` with `selection.supply(selection.available(…))` on the real `app/data/pool.json` and the source pool''s approved questions, for burned sets: none, 20 % and 60 % random, one that leaves a level short; identical `supply` lists, and `ranges` equal `LEVEL_RANGES`. Then `qgen report` and `qgen report --player <name>` (temp `TRIVIA_STATE` with a hand-written `game.json`) print the same supply as before; the start page shows supply per player; without `node` on `PATH`, the readable error. Time one start page load and note it.
