INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (67, 9, 'Review tool for translations (QT-4)', 400, 'Part 5 of the masterplan (plan 9): the authoring review tool and stats pages learn translations (QT-4, `plans/15b-question-translation.md` "Review tool"). The gamemaster and native speakers review `authoring/data/questions.<locale>.json` (D-81, plan 63) with the Spanish source side by side, with the same verdicts, a per-locale "media shows text" flag and the blind spot-check sample of plan 16 per translation run. Launch locales `en`, `de` (decision 26: Launch languages (OQ-31)). The pipeline that fills the files is plan 66 (`plan 66: Translation pipeline (QT-2, QT-3)`); its batch report already links `/review?batch=tr-<locale>-<n>&locale=<locale>&sample=1`, which this plan makes work.

## Builds on
- D-81 / plan 63 (done): `authoring/tools/translations.py` (`LOCALES`, `load`, `save`, `is_stale`, `translatable`, `plays`, `exports`, `counts`); names in `app/data/names.<locale>.json` (+ per bundle), loader `load_names(locale)`.
- Plan 66 (tasks 438–440, open, pending on decision 35): runs `tr-<locale>-<n>` = the translations'' `batch`; `record` writes `status`, `review` (D-33 shape), `media_text` into the locale file and `work/<run>/recorded.json`; audit findings in `work/<run>/audit/<id>.json`; sample via `qgen.audit_sample(run)`. Build against these shapes; verify with throw-away files if 438–440 aren''t done yet.
- D-32/D-33: a human decision replaces the LLM review and keeps it as `previous`; undo restores. Plan 16 (task 47): sample mode, blind until decided, `authoring/data/spot-checks.json`, `authoring/server/spot_checks.py`.
- D-35/D-36: the review tool is the human''s way to change a pool; it re-exports after every change (here `app/data/pool.<locale>.json` via `translations.exports`).

## Server (`authoring/server/main.py`, `spot_checks.py`)
- `GET /api/questions?locale=<l>` (`l` in `LOCALES`; `es` or absent = today): one item per translation entry: the source question (id, `subcategory`, `bundle`, `media`, `background`, `translatable`, candidates) with the translation''s text fields, `difficulty`, `status`, `batch`, `review`, `media_text`, plus `source` (the Spanish text fields, `difficulty`, `status`) and `stale` (bool).
  - Filters: `batch`, `status`, `reviewer`, `sample`, `audit` on the translation; `bundle`, `subcategory`, `media` on the source. `stale=1` only stale ones.
  - `audit`: the translation''s own (`work/<t.batch>/audit/<id>.json`), never the source''s back-audit (`qgen.audit_of` takes the batch, or a locale-aware sibling).
- POST with `"locale"` in the body: `review`, `difficulty` write the locale file through `translations` (one lock, re-read, atomic save, then the locale export), same rules and undo as the source; `difficulty_original` likewise.
  - New `POST /api/questions/<id>/media-text` `{"locale", "media_text": bool}`.
  - New `POST /api/questions/<id>/translatable` `{"translatable": bool}`: sets the source''s flag (`false` = doesn''t travel; not a text field, no staleness, plan 63). With `false`, non-rejected translations of that id are rejected with feedback "no viaja" (validate''s rule, plan 63).
  - `media`, `media/search`, `bundle` refuse a locale (400): media and bundle live on the source; the Spanish view changes them.
- Spot checks: `record(batch, q, …)` accepts a translation run (`tr-*`): batch checked against the translation''s `batch`, the item gets `"locale"`; LLM decision from the run''s `recorded.json`. Same file, keyed by run name.
- Docstring API lines for every new parameter and route.

## Review page (`authoring/ui/src/review/`)
- `?locale=en|de`: header shows the locale; a locale switch (es · en · de) keeps the other params.
- Side by side: left the Spanish source (read-only, its difficulty and status), right the translation; fields aligned row by row (question, answer, wrong answers, hints, description, fun fact). A stale translation gets a banner and no approve (its source changed; the next `--translate` run redoes it).
- Subcategory and bundle shown with the locale''s names (`names.<locale>.json`) and the Spanish key.
- Same verdicts, feedback, problem toggles, difficulty, undo, keyboard keys as the Spanish view. Media: shown, not pickable; a "media shows text" toggle (`media_text`), and the source''s media link to `/review?id=<id>` for changing it.
- "Doesn''t travel" button: sets `translatable: false` (with confirm); a source with `translatable: false` shows it and allows undoing.
- Sample mode (`&sample=1`): blind as plan 16: LLM review, feedback, audit and translator notes hidden until decided; the source stays visible (fidelity is part of the check). Reveal + agree/disagree as today.
- Keep `Review.svelte` from growing: the source column as its own component (e.g. `SourcePanel.svelte`).

## Stats and start page
- `/stats/*?locale=<l>` (with `bundle`): approved, playing translations (`translations.plays`) with their own difficulty; categories/subcategories by the source, labelled with the locale''s names; targets as for Spanish (whether a translated pool counts toward the 5000 is part 9/12, plan 63). Locale switch next to the bundle switch.
- Start page (`overview.py`, `home/Home.svelte`): per locale a row: approved, needs_work, draft, rejected, stale, not translatable, untranslated approved translatable sources (`translations.counts` + source); the `tr-*` runs in the batch table, linking `/review?batch=…&locale=…` and the sample.

## Tasks (for the split)
1. **Server: locale in the question API** (priority 400): `GET /api/questions?locale=`, the POST routes with `locale`, `media-text`, `translatable`, locale export after each change, locale-aware `audit`, refusals; docstring. Verify with a throw-away `questions.en.json` of 3 entries (fresh, stale, non-translatable source) on a git worktree via `curl`; discard.
2. **Review page side by side** (priority 400): locale switch, source column, names, stale banner, verdicts/difficulty/undo, `media_text` toggle, doesn''t travel. `npm run check`, `npm run build`; click through on the worktree file from task 1.
3. **Spot check per locale** (priority 400): `spot_checks.record` for `tr-*` runs, `locale` on items, blind sample mode in the locale view; `qgen validate`''s spot-check check accepts `tr-*` items. Verify with a fake `work/tr-en-1/` (`run.json`, `recorded.json`, an audit file) on the worktree; discard.
4. **Stats and start page per locale** (priority 390).
5. **Docs** (priority 380): `plans/15b-question-translation.md` "Review tool" (what exists) and QT-4 `[x]`; `plans/08-review-tool.md` new RV entries (locale view, spot check per locale); `directory.md` if files were added; `authoring/QC.md`: the native speaker''s spot check link and steps for `tr-*` runs, if task 441 didn''t write them already.

## Done when
- On a worktree with a throw-away locale file: `/review?locale=en` shows source and translation side by side; a decision, a difficulty change, `media_text` and doesn''t-travel write the locale file and `app/data/pool.en.json`; undo restores; `qgen validate` clean.
- `/review?batch=tr-en-1&locale=en&sample=1` is blind and records into `spot-checks.json`; `/stats/difficulty?locale=en` and the start page show the locale.
- The Spanish view and `pool.json` unchanged (D-59).

## Out of scope
- The pipeline and its runs (plan 66, part 11); finding native speakers (the gamemaster).
- Replacing media with visible text per locale (flagged only; backlog if many, plan 66).
- Flags from a game played in English/German (`apply_flags` with a locale): part 6 (task 246) decides how flags carry the locale.
- Reworking needs_work translations: the next `--translate` run picks them again (plan 66''s selection).', '', '2026-10-12T19:34:03Z', 245);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (68, 9, 'Language setting and per-locale pool (I18N-2)', 480, 'Part 6 of the masterplan (plan 9): the player picks the UI language and the question language; the game plays from that locale''s pool and shows that locale''s category and bundle names; a fresh save asks for the language once, on first start (milestone 9''s revision; replaces this plan''s earlier "no first-start language screen"). Launch languages `es`, `en`, `de` (D-78, decision 26: Launch languages (OQ-31)); `es-ES` is a UI variant only (decision 27: Spanish variety). Owner: `plans/15-i18n.md` "Model", I18N-2. The family''s game stays as today: Spanish, gamemaster mode unchanged (D-59).

## Builds on
- Plan 63 (done, D-81): `app/data/pool.<locale>.json` (no `pool.es.json`: `es` = `pool.json`), `app/data/names.<locale>.json`, `app/data/bundles/<id>/names.<locale>.json`; subcategory keys stay Spanish everywhere.
- Plan 65 (seen counters, supersedes D-28''s burns): `seen` rows by question id for the whole save. Ids are shared across locales, so switching languages never repeats a question with no extra work; the outlook and the low-supply warning (decision 31: super-tight) run on the loaded locale''s pool.
- Catalog (plan 21, D-70): `lib/i18n.ts`, `CATALOGS`, `?lang=` dev override. `en` draft: plan 24; `de`, `es-ES`: plan 69. This plan only switches between whatever catalogs exist.
- Plan 36 has no general settings screen (only the mode screen, MD-7); plan 59 grows the overlay into the gamemaster menu.
- Decision 4 (Python server: static + `/api/save`): new save fields pass through untouched; `/data/` serves the new files statically.
- Built (tasks 449, 450): `SaveData.language`, `GameRow.locale` (decision 36: written only for non-es games), `defaultLanguage()` in `engine/save.ts`, `ready()`/`language()` in `lib/engine.ts`, boot language in `main.ts`, Esc menu rows in `Overlay.svelte`, `displayName`.

## Decisions taken here
- **Save field, no version bump**: `SaveData.language?: { ui: string; questions: string }`. A stored save without it = `{ui: "es", questions: "es"}` (`parseSave`), so the family''s save and fixtures stay Spanish whatever the browser says. A fresh save (`emptySave()`: no file, 404, or a backed-up broken file) gets the default below. Profile = save (plan 65): on Steam it travels with the SteamID''s save.
- **Default for a fresh save**: best match of the guessed tag among the existing catalogs (UI) and locales with a pool (questions): exact tag, then the language part (`es-CO` → `es`, `de-AT` → `de`, `es-ES` → `es-ES` UI + `es` questions), else `en` if present, else `es`. Guessed tag: `navigator.language` now; Steam''s client language once milestone 10 provides it (one seam, `guessTag()`; not wired here).
- **A game keeps its locale**: `GameRow.locale?` (missing = `es`), set by `newGame` from `language.questions`. Continuing a game loads its own locale''s data; a language change applies to the next game. No mid-game pool swap.
- **Esc menu**: two rows «Idioma» / «Idioma de las preguntas» in every mode (next to sound), shown only with ≥2 options. Today (only `es` catalog, only `pool.json`) nothing appears.
- **First-start language screen** (milestone 9):
  - Shown when the loaded save is fresh (no `language` stored, i.e. `emptySave()`), before the start screen; asked once: confirming writes `language`, so it never shows again. A stored save without `language` (the family''s) is parsed as `es` and never sees it.
  - Skipped while there is nothing to pick (one UI option and one question locale, as today); nothing is written then, so it asks once a second language ships.
  - One list of UI languages by endonym (same data as the Esc rows), the guess preselected and focused; confirm = Enter / pad A / click. A pick sets both: `ui` = the pick, `questions` = `defaultLanguage(pick)` over the locales whose supply check passes for the default bundles (`es` always). Separate question language: Esc menu.
  - No `t()` text needed to choose: endonyms plus a heading and a confirm prompt in the guessed UI language (`language.*` keys).
  - Confirm with a different UI language than the boot one: save, then `location.reload()` (same rule as the Esc menu); same one: continue to the start screen without reload.
- **Options**: UI = catalogs in `CATALOGS` minus `xx`; questions = locales whose pool file exists (`es` always). A question locale whose pool fails the supply check for the default bundles is listed but disabled in the Esc menu, with the reason.
- **UI language change reloads the app**; `lang` stays a module constant set once at boot. No reactive catalog.
- **Names**: `displayName(kind, key)` from the loaded locale''s names files; fallback the Spanish key/`categories.json` name.

## Tasks (for the split)
1. **Engine and data** (task 449, done).
2. **UI: Esc menu rows, names, boot** (task 450, done).
3. **Docs** (task 451; runs after task 4): the D-entry and `plans/15-i18n.md` "Model" also cover the first-start screen; `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` gets the screen next to the Esc menu rows.
4. **First-start language screen** (priority 470, before the docs task)
   - `lib/engine.ts`: `ready()` remembers whether the stored save had no `language` (fresh); `language()` returns `ask: boolean` (fresh and >1 UI option or >1 question locale). `guessTag()` wraps `navigator.language` (the seam for milestone 10).
   - `Game.svelte`: a `language` screen before `start` when `ask`; a new component (e.g. `game/LanguageScreen.svelte`): the endonym list, guess preselected, action layer scope and `data-nav` (IN-2..IN-5), keys and pad; confirm → `setLanguage` → reload if `ui` changed, else `start`. Esc menu not reachable on this screen (nothing to configure yet).
   - Strings via `t()` (`language.choose`, `language.confirm` or similar) in `es` and in whatever other catalogs exist (plan 24''s `en` if present, else noted for plan 69); `npm run check:literals`.
   - Check: `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `npm test`; throw-away: browser walk with no save file and throw-away `pool.en.json` + `names.en.json` + a stub `en` catalog: `navigator.language` `de-AT` → `en` preselected; pick `Español (Latinoamérica)` → reload, Spanish start screen; reload again → no screen; a copy of the family save → no screen; only `es` present → no screen, nothing written; keyboard only, pad.

## Done when
- The family''s save plays exactly as today (fixture replay passes, no language rows or screen with only `es`; never a screen for a stored save).
- With a second pool and catalog present: a fresh save opens on the language screen with the guessed language preselected, asks once; a player switches both languages from the Esc menu; the next game draws from that locale''s pool with its names, never repeating a question seen in another language before unseen ones run out.

## Out of scope
- Catalogs `en`, `de`, `es-ES` (plans 24, 69), translated pools (plans 66, part 11), Steam client language (milestone 10 wires it into `guessTag()`), store page (LUI-6).', '', '2026-10-12T19:36:15Z', 246);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (69, 9, 'UI catalogs for the launch languages (LUI-4, LUI-5)', 370, 'Part 7 of the masterplan (plan 9): every screen of the game in the launch languages, checked by native speakers. Launch catalogs `es` (neutral Latin American, es-419), `es-ES` (override), `en`, `de` (D-78; decision 26: Launch languages (OQ-31); decision 27: Spanish variety (OQ-31)). Owner: `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` (LUI-4, LUI-5). The family''s game stays Spanish with today''s keys (D-59), unless the LUI-4 decision says otherwise; its joker names change by plan 136 (D-59 exception).

## Builds on
- Plan 21 (done, D-70): `lib/i18n.ts`, `locales/es.ts`, `Catalog`/`Key` types, `npm run check:literals -w app/client`.
- Plan 23 (LUI-2): `xx` pseudo-locale, its screen walk and backlog rows (origin `LUI-2`). Plan 24 (LUI-3): draft `en.ts`, English joker name decisions, rows (origin `LUI-3`). Both at 400, before this plan; a task here that needs `xx.ts` or `en.ts` and finds it missing stops with a note.
- Plan 68 (I18N-2): language rows in the Esc menu, boot language from the save, endonyms «Español (España)», «Deutsch»; first-start language screen (task 490, milestone 9 revision) with its `language.*` keys in `es` (and `en` if present). It switches between whatever is in `CATALOGS`; this plan fills it, so the screen first appears once a second catalog ships here.
- Plan 45 (done): `Prompt.svelte`, `Glyph.svelte`, `KEY_LABELS` in `lib/input.svelte.ts`. Pad glyphs are language-independent; only key letters and text labels vary.
- Plan 46 (SW-4, 380, before this plan): `LetterPicker.svelte` with Spanish letters (`Ñ Á É Í Ó Ú Ü`); task 3 stops with a note if it doesn''t exist yet.
- Plan 64 (neutral Spanish for questions); this plan does the UI side of D-78 (`es.ts` neutral, `es-ES` override).
- `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again` (part 14, 375, before task 7): English-first joker names, one symbol per joker, `es`/`es-ES`/`de` translated from them (`es` too: D-59 exception); supersedes the German names of task 3 (`decision 54: German name for the hint joker «Soplo»?` … `decision 58: German name for the snipe joker «Francotirador»?`) and the English ones of plan 24. Task 7 waits for it.
- Plan 100 (part 13, 380, before task 7): locale style guides `app/client/src/locales/style/<locale>.md`, TV-check fixes, screen gallery. Its fixes and gallery flags land before the playtest close-out; task 7 doesn''t redo them.

## Design
- **Shipping catalogs**: `CATALOGS` = `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`, statically imported (a few KB each; no lazy loading); `xx` stays dev-only. `en.ts`/`de.ts`: `satisfies Catalog`. `es-ES.ts`: `DeepPartial<Catalog>`, only differing leaves (`vosotros` for plural addressing, regionalisms), merged over `es` at boot; plural maps and variant arrays replaced whole, not merged per item.
- **Keys (LUI-4, pm decision)**: recommendation: keep keys in the catalog per language (`joker.<id>.key`, `flag.key`, `screen.question.replayKey`, `screen.start.newKey`), mnemonic for the name. `es` unchanged. Reasons: `toIntent` matches `e.key`, so letters work on QWERTZ/AZERTY, while position-based neutral keys (`Q W E R T`) don''t; `F1`–`F5` are awkward on laptops and the Deck; pads use focus anyway (decision 9). Rule per catalog, checked by `check:literals`: keys unique, single letter, not `A`–`D` (answers), not a digit, not a key of another scope on the same screen. Alternative options in the decision: neutral `1`–`5` row… (conflicts with `pick n`), `F1`–`F5`.
- **Joker names (like plan 24; done in task 3, superseded by plan 136)**: playful German names, not literal translations; one pm decision per joker (`hint`, `skip`, `easier`, `category`, `snipe`), 3–5 candidates each, recommended first, ≤ «Francotirador»''s length. `es-ES` keeps the Spanish names unless a candidate reads off in Spain (then a decision). Plan 136 replaces them in every catalog, keys per decision 53 included; this plan doesn''t touch joker names again.
- **First-start language screen**: its `language.*` keys (heading, confirm prompt) in every catalog; the guessed language''s catalog shows them, so each must read right on its own. Endonyms stay in plan 68''s data, not in catalogs.
- **Mode names**: English first (D-74); `de` drafted in the catalog, checked in the playtest; no separate decision.
- **`es` neutral**: scan `es.ts` for Colombian wording (copy lines, error texts). Family-visible, so changes go through one pm decision (list old → new); none applied before it.
- **Letter picker**: letters per UI language from the catalog (`picker.letters`): `es`/`es-ES` today''s set, `de` adds `Ä Ö Ü ß`, `en` `A`–`Z` + `-`.
- **Fonts**: Baloo 2 and Nunito (`app/client/public/fonts`) must have every character of every catalog (`ÄÖÜäöüß „“ ‚‘ – … ¡¿ «» ñ`). Checked once by a throw-away script (`nix shell nixpkgs#python3Packages.fonttools`); a gap → pm decision (other subset of the same family, OFL), not a new font silently. Latin only at launch (15a).
- **Length**: `xx` (40 %) bounds German (+20–35 %). Long German compounds: `hyphens: auto` on text blocks (needs `<html lang>` set by plan 68). Fixes inside the `--u` system (D-29), no per-language CSS unless unavoidable.
- **`/comodines` (JK-11, `authoring/ui/src/print/JokerCards.svelte`)**: `?lang=es|es-ES|en|de`; names, keys and the one-line rules from the app catalogs (`joker.<id>.rule`, new keys; `RULES` leaves the component), page text via the catalog too. Paper: Letter for `es`/`en`, A4 for `de`/`es-ES` (`@page size`); the 3 × 4 grid of 2.5 in cards fits both.
- **Playtest**: native speaker per catalog (`es` the family, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`), arranged by the gamemaster. Checklist in 15a ("Playtest"); one `pm decision add --once` per language "Playtest passed?" (options: passed / passed with fixes listed / failed).
- **Out of scope**: LUI-6 store page texts (S5, noted in 15a); Steam client language (S5); question/category/bundle translations (15b, plans 63, 66); `zh-Hans`, `ru`, `pt-BR` (milestone 12, on hold); the review tool stays es/en.

## Tasks (for the split)
1. **Decisions: keys and German joker names** (priority 370)
   - `pm decision add` LUI-4 as above (recommendation first; body: the current keys, the collision rule, QWERTZ note).
   - Five `pm decision add` for German joker names (body: Spanish name, English name from plan 24 if decided, what the joker does, why the candidates).
   - `pm decision add`: `es` neutral wording, old → new list from the `es.ts` scan (only if the scan finds something; else note "none").
   - Candidate lists in 15a under LUI-5; link task 3 to all these decisions (`pm task-pending-decision`).
2. **`de.ts`, `es-ES.ts`, shipping wiring** (priority 370; doesn''t wait for the decisions)
   - `de.ts` (recommended joker names for now), `es-ES.ts` override + merge in `i18n.ts`, all four in `CATALOGS` for production; `Intl` plural/number per lang.
   - `check:literals` extended: key rule per catalog, same `{param}` set per leaf as `es`, no leaf identical to `es` in `en`/`de` except an allow-list (names, `OK`…).
   - Font coverage script (throw-away); `npm run check`, `npm run build`; `language.*` keys in `de`/`es-ES`/`en`; `?lang=de` and `?lang=es-ES` walk of every screen incl. the first-start language screen (fresh save; same method as plans 21/23), overflow rows to `plans/backlog.md` (origin `LUI-5`).
   - `directory.md` (`locales/de.ts`, `locales/es-ES.ts`).
3. **Keys, names, letters in** (waits for task 1''s decisions)
   - Keys per the LUI-4 answer in all catalogs; German names; `es.ts` wording per its decision; `picker.letters` in `LetterPicker.svelte`. D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` for LUI-4 (next free number), `pm decision consequences`.
4. **Overflow fixes** (priority 360)
   - Every open backlog row with origin `LUI-2`, `LUI-3`, `LUI-5`: fix within `--u`, `hyphens: auto`; re-walk `de` and `xx` (incl. the language screen) at 1920 × 1080 and 1280 × 800 (plan 46''s sizes), `es` pixel-identical except the fixed spots. Rows → `done`.
5. **`/comodines` per language** (priority 360)
   - Rules and page text into the catalogs, `?lang=`, A4/Letter; print-preview check (one page, 12 cards) for each language.
6. **Playtest checklist and decisions** (priority 350)
   - "Playtest" section in 15a: first start on a fresh save (language screen: guess preselected, pick another, asked once), full game in each mode available, every joker, overlay/Esc menu incl. language rows, keyboard and pad prompts, victory and wrong, report dialog, `/comodines` printout; what to note (wrong tone, too long, wrong register, unclear rule).
   - Four `pm decision add --once` "Playtest passed? (<lang>)"; link task 7 to them.
7. **Playtest fixes and close-out** (priority 340; waits for task 6''s decisions and for plan 136''s joker names and review)
   - Plan 136''s new joker names are in; playtest notes on joker names go to plan 136''s fix task, not here.
   - Read the locale''s style guide first (plan 100); apply the fixes from the answers per the guide (catalogs only; anything bigger → `pm task add`); new bad patterns from the playtest go into the guide. LUI-4, LUI-5 `[x]` in 15a with notes; 15a status; `plans/project.md`; `plans/11-steam.md` 15 row if done.

## Done when
- `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de` ship in the production build, pass `npm run check` and `check:literals`, have no overflow at 1920 × 1080 and 1280 × 800, and passed a native-speaker playtest each (after plan 136''s joker names); the family''s Spanish game looks and plays as before except decided wording or key changes.', '', '2026-10-12T19:43:19Z', 247);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (70, 9, 'Cost, budget and generation plan by gap (CT-3, CT-4)', 560, 'Part 9 of the masterplan (plan 9). CT-3: what an approved question costs (draft → approved per source locale, and per translation direction), so the release runs get a budget per question locale before they start. CT-4: which difficulties, subcategories and sources each question locale (`es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`; decision 21, milestone 9 "English-first drafting for `base`") still needs, aimed by the existing gap mechanism (plans 12, 13: D-53, D-54) extended per locale. Owner: `plans/16-content-target.md` ("Cost"; CT-3, CT-4).

## Decisions this builds on
- D-75 (`decision 21: Content target per player and language (OQ-32)`): 5000 approved per question locale with D-53''s mix; no games number. Milestone 9 (2026-10-15): question locales `en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`. The simulation (plan 62, CT-2) is information only: its bottlenecks never set targets.
- D-74 (pm decision 19): no presets; one standard joker set. D-77/D-80 (pm decision 23): modes. Neither adds targets: no per-mode, per-preset or per-age-group numbers (the per-level mix covers the age-group windows, D-76).
- D-78 (pm decision 26): `es`, `en`, `de` launch languages; `es-ES` a question locale with its own pool since milestone 9''s English-first change (`decision 156: One language for UI and questions`).
- `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`: `base` from batch-9 drafted in `en`, ≤ batch-8 `es`; every source gets translations into the other three locales; regional bundles keep their region''s language (`colombia`: es → en).
- `decision 37: Per-locale content targets and gap aiming`: its last clause (en/de source shortfall drives es drafting), D-84 and `decision 219: Do the new locales (zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR) steer es drafting from the start?` are replaced by `plan 148: English-first drafting for base` (task 1, records the supersessions; task 6, the new `draft_gaps`).
- `decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)`: every regional bundle 2000 approved (region''s language + en); pilot `colombia` 102 → 2000, effort = $ per approved via `qgen report --cost` + review time per 100. Bundle targets, per-bundle `--cost` rows and the review-time line are plan 98''s; this plan''s report and budget read them.
- Milestone 9 (developer, 2026-10-15; replaces decision 110''s "more bundles only after a new decision with the pilot''s numbers"): more regional bundles by Steam audience, `usa` (en), `germany` (de + en), `uk` (en), `spain` (es-ES + en), `mexico` (es + en), 2000 approved each, drafted in the region''s language; each starts once `colombia`''s chain is proven; launch doesn''t wait for them.
- D-53/D-54: `targets.json`, `targets.deficits()`, `target_weights()`, subcategory ranking by deficit. D-55: `$ per approved ≤ 0.35` per batch already stops a costly batch. D-36: no new `qgen batch` arguments.

## Where the numbers stand
- 2026-10-12, `work/*/costs.log`: draft batches batch-4..7 $0.16 / $0.37 / $0.30 / $0.24 per approved (`authoring/reports/batches.md`); batch-7 $121 for 504 approved. Overhead outside batches: concepts $65, tighten-1/2 $38, rework-1 $6, pilot/first-120 $16, bundles $2.
- 2026-10-15: `base` 1034 approved (es-sourced), `colombia` 102; no translation run yet (`tr-en-1`, `tr-de-1` wait, `decision 204: Translation pilot done (tr-en-1, tr-de-1)?`); no English draft yet (batch-9, `task 1185: run batch-9`).
- `work/` is gitignored, local: the report reads what exists and says what it skipped.

## Design
- **Cost report (CT-3):** `qgen report --cost [--json]` (task 461, done): per run, per kind, projection per launch language, `es` sources past target.
  - English-first (milestone 9): draft $/approved per source locale (`batch-*` ≤ 8 `es`, ≥ 9 `en`), translation $/approved per direction (es → L, en → L; runs `tr-<L>-*` incl. `tr-es-*`, `tr-es-ES-*`), projection per question locale (four). The code change is `plan 148: English-first drafting for base` task 6 (`--cost` per source locale), not here.
  - Projection per question locale: `en` = English drafts `draft_gaps` asks for × en draft rate; `es`, `es-ES`, `de` = deficit × translation rate en → L; plus the es-sourced backlog (≤ batch-8 approved without an `en`, `de`, `es-ES` entry) × es → L rate; every term × (1 + overhead ratio). Before a run of a kind exists, the nearest measured rate stands in and is labelled (en draft ← last 3 `es` batches; en → L ← es → L; `es-ES` ← `es` → nearest).
  - Spent vs. budget per question locale once `targets.json` has `"budget"` (task 3); information only, no stop (D-55).
- **Per-locale targets (CT-4):** no new numbers. Every question locale''s target is `targets.json` `base` (D-75); no locale block unless the developer later decides different numbers.
  - `targets.deficits(pool, bundle, locale)` and `qgen report --locale L`, `target_check` on it (task 462, done); counting sources in L + playing translations into L for all four locales is plan 148 task 6.
- **Translation aimed at gaps:** `--translate` ranks subcategories by fewest translations, weighted by the locale''s deficit at the source''s difficulty (task 464, plan 66); unchanged by the source locale.
- **Drafting aimed at gaps:** English drafting for `base` follows the largest locale deficit (plan 148 task 6''s `draft_gaps`, replacing task 462''s es source shortfall); regional bundles their own deficit (D-101). Nothing in this plan.
- **Simulation bottlenecks:** `qgen report --simulate` prints them per locale × mode × age group; read by the developer and by task 3''s decision, not by `draft`. A bottleneck that persists with the mix met is a pm decision to change `targets.json`, not code.

## Tasks
1. **`qgen report --cost` (CT-3 tooling):** done (task 461).
2. **Per-locale deficits and es source shortfall (CT-4):** done (task 462); its source shortfall is replaced by plan 148 task 6.
3. **Release budget (pm decision, CT-3):** task 463. Runs after part 11''s translation pilot (`decision 204: Translation pilot done (tr-en-1, tr-de-1)?`; task 463 is pending on it) and after plan 148 task 6 (`--cost` per source locale, four locales); if that task is still open, make task 463 wait for it (a pm decision "`--cost` per source locale done?" if no other link exists) and stop.
   - `qgen report --cost` numbers → `pm decision add "Release budget per language"` with a table: `en` drafting for `base` (to 5000 `en` and what the other locales'' deficits need), translations en → `es`, en → `es-ES`, en → `de`, the es-sourced backlog es → `en`, `de`, `es-ES`, overhead, QC.
   - Regional rows, one per bundle in audience order, each 2000 in its language (+ 2000 en where the language isn''t en): `colombia` (es → en), `usa` (en), `germany` (de → en), `uk` (en), `spain` (es-ES → en), `mexico` (es → en); plan 98''s per-bundle `--cost` rows, else the draft/translation rates; each row''s cost counts in its languages'' totals, shown apart from `base`; launch doesn''t wait for them (decision 110, milestone 9).
   - Rates not yet measured (en drafting before batch-9, en → L before its first run, de and es-ES drafting, de → en and es-ES → en) labelled as stand-ins (nearest measured rate).
   - Options: recommended = projection + 20 % margin; a lower cap naming which levels/locales give way; draft `en` past 5000 for translation sources or not.
   - On the answer: `"budget": {"en": $, "es": $, "es-ES": $, "de": $}` in `targets.json` (+ `targets.py` loader, `"budget"` in `NOT_BUNDLES`, `qgen validate` check); `--cost` shows spent vs. budget; plan 16 "Cost" and CT-3 `[x]`; `plans/project.md`. Part 11''s full runs (QT-6) wait for this decision. Priority -95 (after the pilot at -90, before batch-9 at -100 and the full runs at -110).
- CT-4 `[x]` in plan 16 with task 2 (generation plan = deficits per locale; drafting aim now plan 148''s).

## Done when
- `qgen report --cost` prints $/approved per run kind and a projection per question locale.
- `qgen report --locale L` and `--simulate` use per-locale deficits; `draft` and `--translate` follow them.
- A release budget per question locale (en drafting + three translations per English source, the es-sourced backlog, the regional bundles'' rows) is answered and stored; plan 16 CT-3, CT-4 `[x]`.

## Out of scope
- Running batches or translations (part 11, plan 17, plan 84); the English-first schema, drafting, `--cost`/deficit code for four locales (plan 148); per-bundle cost rows, bundle targets, new bundles'' drafting directions and review time per 100 (plan 98); the regional runs (plan 84); the back-audit''s cost estimate (plan 57); later languages (milestone 12); a hard budget stop in `qgen batch`.', '', '2026-10-12T19:46:01Z', 248);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (71, 5, 'Bundle languages and base bundles', 600, 'Part 5 of masterplan 5. Today every bundle is offered in every language, and `always_on: true` forces `base` into each session. This plan gives each bundle the languages it exists in, makes `kind: base` the mark of a base bundle (exactly one per session, default the locale''s first), resolves choices against the game''s locale, and teaches `qgen validate` the new rules. For `es` the defaults stay `base` + `colombia`, so the family''s sessions and plan 18''s fixture replay don''t change. Plan 29 (start screen, 400) and plan 30 (close-out, 390) build on the API here.

## Builds on
- Plan 27 (done): `Bundle`, `parseBundles` (`pool.ts`); `defaultChoice`, `gameChoice`, `resolveChoice`, `playerChoice`, `supply`, `newGame` (`game.ts`); `choice` route (`api.ts`); `choice.test.ts`; D-68 in `plans/decisions.md`.
- Plan 68 (I18N-2): `EngineData.locale`, `GameRow.locale` (missing = `es`, decision 36: GameRow.locale written only for non-es games), `loadEngineData(base, locale)`, `LOCALES` in `lib/data.ts`. A game''s engine data is already its locale''s, so "the game''s language" = `data.locale` inside the engine.
- Launch languages es, en, de (decision 26: Launch languages); `LAUNCH_LOCALES` in `authoring/tools/qgen.py`.
- Supply and outlook (decision 31: super-tight warning) run on the loaded locale''s pool already; only the bundle sets they get change.

## Decisions taken here
- **Data**: `app/data/bundles.json`: `always_on` removed from every entry; `languages` added. `base`: `["es", "en", "de"]`. `colombia`: `["es"]`: no `pool.en.json` / `pool.de.json` exists yet (only colombia''s `names.en/de.json`), so it isn''t translated into them; extending the list is part of translating it. `kind` stays (`base`, `region`, `theme`); `kind: "base"` marks a base bundle. File order decides "the locale''s first base bundle"; `taxonomy_problems`'' "base must come first" stays.
- **Offered bundles**: `bundlesFor(data, locale = data.locale)` → the bundles whose `languages` contain `locale`, file order. Exported for plan 29.
- **`resolveChoice`** (game''s locale = `data.locale`):
  - not a list → `bundles_not_list`; unknown id → `bundle_unknown` (as today);
  - known but not offered in the locale → new `GameError("bundle_not_offered", {bundle, locale})`, es «el paquete ''{bundle}'' no está disponible en este idioma»;
  - duplicates dropped, then not exactly one `kind: base` bundle → new `GameError("base_bundle_count", {count})`, es «elige exactamente un paquete básico»;
  - order normalized to file order.
  - Nothing is added any more: `[]` and `["colombia"]` are refused (zero base bundles) instead of becoming `[base]` / `[base, colombia]`. Supersedes that part of D-68.
- **Defaults** (`defaultChoice(data)`, missing `bundles`): the locale''s first base bundle plus every non-base bundle offered in the locale. `es` → `["base", "colombia"]` = today; `en`/`de` → `["base"]`.
- **Stored settings that no longer resolve** (a bundle not offered in the game''s locale, or not exactly one base bundle, e.g. after `languages` changes or a hand-edited save): `gameChoice` resolves the stored `bundles` with `resolveChoice`; on `GameError` it returns the locale''s default bundles (the stored `age_group` kept if known, else the default). Read-only, never written back, so a running game keeps going instead of breaking. `playerChoice` (preset from the player''s newest game) gets the same fallback: a newest game from another locale whose bundles don''t fit presets the current locale''s defaults. Recorded in the decision entry.
- **Outlook** (`outlook.ts`): `bundleHint` only considers non-base bundles offered in the locale and not yet active (adding a base bundle would make two).
- **Questions without `bundle`** stay `base` (`q.bundle ?? "base"`); «Cambiazo» groups and supply keep following the active bundles (unchanged).
- **`qgen validate`** (errors unless said):
  - every bundle: `languages` a non-empty list of distinct codes from `LAUNCH_LOCALES` (milestone 12 extends that list); no `always_on` key left; `kind` one of `base`, `region`, `theme`;
  - each launch language has at least one `kind: base` bundle;
  - **warning** (not error): a bundle listed for a locale ≠ es whose exported pool `app/data/pool.<locale>.json` is missing or has no approved question of that bundle. Why a warning: `base` is listed for en/de before their pools ship (decision 26), and plan 68 already lists such a locale as unavailable.
  - **warning**: `pool.<locale>.json` has approved questions of a bundle not listed for that locale (translated but not offered).
- **Authoring readers**: `authoring/server/overview.py` (`b["always_on"]` → `b["kind"] == "base"`), `authoring/ui/src/lib/types.ts` (`always_on` → `languages: string[]`), `qgen bundle new` (writes `"languages": ["es"]`, no `always_on`). No behaviour change.
- **Decision entry**: next free D number in `plans/decisions.md`: base bundles (`kind: base`) replace `always_on`, exactly one per session, default the locale''s first base bundle plus every non-base bundle of the locale; bundles offered per `languages`; invalid stored choices read as the locale''s defaults; supersedes D-68''s "every always_on bundle is always on" and its auto-adding of `base`. Also `pm decision record` with the same content.

## Tasks to split into
1. **Bundle languages and base bundles in data and engine**
   - `app/data/bundles.json` as above (keep `about` as is apart from removing any `always_on` mention; plan 30 rewrites it).
   - `pool.ts`: `Bundle {id, kind, languages, name, description}`; `parseBundles` throws on a missing/empty `languages` or a missing `kind`; `bundlesFor`.
   - `game.ts`: `defaultChoice`, `resolveChoice`, `gameChoice` / `playerChoice` fallback; `state.ts` English messages and `locales/es.ts` strings for `bundle_not_offered`, `base_bundle_count`; `lib/types.ts` comment (line 41: "every always_on bundle included").
   - `outlook.ts` `bundleHint` as above; `outlook.test.ts` and `pool.test.ts` (line 94) use `kind`/`languages`.
   - Authoring readers above (same task, since removing `always_on` breaks `overview.py`); check `authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts` cells still resolve (non-es cells pass `["base"]`, es cells every bundle: both valid).
   - `choice.test.ts`: replace "base added" cases with: `[]` and `["colombia"]` → 409 `base_bundle_count`, save unchanged; two base bundles → 409 (temp data with a second `kind: base` bundle); a bundle not offered → 409 `bundle_not_offered` (temp `engineData(..., "en")` with colombia `["es"]`); defaults per locale (`es` → base+colombia, `en` → base); a stored game whose bundles don''t resolve plays with the defaults; `choice` route preset from an es game in an en engine → en defaults.
   - Check: `npm test` (plan 18''s fixture replay byte-identical, nothing re-recorded), `npm run check`, `npm run build`; `trivia-authoring` start page loads.
2. **`qgen validate` checks and the decision entry**
   - Checks above in `authoring/tools/qgen.py` (next to `taxonomy_problems`); throw-away script: a temp `bundles.json` without `languages`, with `always_on`, with no base bundle for `de`, with an unknown locale → each flagged; a temp `pool.en.json` with a colombia question → the "not listed" warning.
   - Decision entry in `plans/decisions.md` and `pm decision record` (see "Decisions taken here").
   - Check: `qgen validate` passes on the real data (warnings for en/de base allowed).

## Done when
- No `always_on` in code or data (docs: plan 30); every bundle has `languages`.
- The engine refuses a new game with zero or two base bundles, or with a bundle not offered in its locale; `es` defaults are `base` + `colombia`, `en`/`de` defaults `base`.
- Plan 18''s fixtures replay unchanged; `npm test`, `npm run check`, `qgen validate` pass.
- Decision entry written.

## Out of scope
- Start screen (plan 29), docs and play-test (plan 30), `chinese-base` and its `qgen bundle new --kind base` (milestone 12), translating colombia.', '', '2026-10-12T20:22:37Z', 469);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (72, 13, 'masterplan', 1000, 'Masterplan of milestone 13 (Code quality): review every tracked code file in scope once, fix what is cheap, log everything in `code-review.md` at the repo root, and finish with an executive summary for the gamemaster. **The tasks of this masterplan are not implementation work: each writes the plan for one part** (`pm plan add 13 … --priority 0`); that plan''s split task then makes the review tasks (one file or a small group of related files per task, sized for one worker run).

## Ground rules for every part
- Priority: every part plan `--priority 0` (milestone 13 "Priority"); its tasks without own priority. Parts then run in plan id order = the order below (same priority → by plan id), after all other milestones'' work.
- Scope per milestone 13: code and build/package config. Not: `*.json` pools/data, `tasks.sql`, media, prompt contents (`authoring/tools/prompts/`), `plans/`, `project-manager.toml` (pm''s config).
- Checklist per file: the milestone''s six categories (unused, practice, complexity, performance, bug, inconsistency) and their examples; also against `AGENTS.md` rules, `directory.md`, `plans/decisions.md` (D-numbers) and `pm decision list --answered --grep <file or term>`.
- Fix or ask, as in the milestone: small, local fixes (behaviour unchanged or obviously fixed) in the review task itself; cross-cutting or behaviour/format changes → `pm decision add` (options, recommended first) + a follow-up task in this milestone linked with `pm task-pending-decision`; larger work → `pm task add` in the part''s plan.
- Verify fixes with throw-away scripts; no new tests by default (AGENTS.md). Before every commit: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`. Real `state/` is never written: servers and scripts run on a temp `TRIVIA_STATE` / `TRIVIA_MEDIA`.
- Open work elsewhere: before fixing a file, `pm queue` / grep open task bodies for it. Code that an open task deletes or rewrites gets a short review only and status "superseded by task N" for findings there; no refactor that would conflict. Known case: `task 302: Delete the Python referee` (plan 51) deletes `app/server/game.py`, `selection.py`, `flags.py`, `authoring/tools/record_fixtures.py` and moves `categories.py` and is blocked on decision 25 (family test night).
- Duplication across files (`app/` ↔ `authoring/`, Python ↔ TS ports, the two `types.ts`, the two `api.ts`): each review task logs what it sees as a "duplication candidate" with both paths; part 10 consolidates.
- Report format (fixed by part 1, used by all): one `## <part>` section per part in `code-review.md`, one table row per finding: file, finding, category, severity (high / medium / low), status (`fixed in <short sha or "this task">` / `follow-up task N` / `decision N` / `superseded by task N` / `won''t fix: <why>`). Files reviewed without findings are listed too ("no findings"), so "every file listed" can be checked. pm commits the task''s changes, so "fixed" names the task: `fixed (task N)`.
- Linter evidence (milestone "Linter for TypeScript"): a TS/Svelte/`.mjs`/`.cjs` finding that a lint rule or stricter `tsconfig` flag would have caught gets the rule in its finding text, e.g. `(lint: noUnusedLocals)`, `(lint: no-floating-promises)`; part 10 counts these to decide.
- Once part 10 adopts a lint pass: it is part of the pre-commit checks above for every task changing TypeScript (`.ts`, `.svelte`, `.mjs`/`.cjs`).

## Parts
1. **Baseline scans and report skeleton** — create `code-review.md` (format above, empty part sections, severity definitions), add it to `directory.md`; the file inventory: every tracked file in scope (from `git ls-files`) mapped to the part that reviews it, so nothing is missed. Cross-cutting scans by throw-away script, logged as findings or handed to the parts: `directory.md` vs `git ls-files` (e.g. `app/server/flags.py`, `authoring/server/overview.py`, `media_stats.py`, `authoring/tools/providers/`, `sim/` missing from it), unused exports (`tsc --noUnusedLocals --noUnusedParameters` once, a grep for exported names never imported, Python `def`s never referenced), unused npm dependencies in all `package.json`s, every `PLACEHOLDER(<task>)` whose task is closed, `TODO`/`FIXME`, `any`/`as` casts, `except: pass`/bare `except`, `catch {}`, sync IO in request handlers, bundle size of both Vite builds (`npm run build` output) as the baseline. The `tsc --noUnusedLocals`/`--noUnusedParameters` run and the bad-practice counts are also the first evidence for part 10''s linter evaluation: record the exact commands and counts. No code fixes here except trivially safe ones; the rest goes to the parts'' plans.
2. **Python game server** (`app/server/`: `main.py`, `http_base.py`, `save.py`, `paths.py`, `media_cache.py`, `categories.py`; `game.py`, `selection.py`, `flags.py` short-reviewed per the task 302 rule) — swallowed errors, save atomicity and migration (`save.py`), path handling (Windows, `TRIVIA_STATE`), `/media` not an open proxy, standard library only.
3. **TS engine** (`app/client/src/engine/` incl. tests, `test/` helpers and the fixture loader; not the fixture JSON) — parity with the Python originals vs. what has since diverged on purpose, `pycompat.ts` still needed, transaction/undo correctness in `state.ts`/`game.ts` (883 lines: split candidates), RNG seeding, outlook cost per call, tests that no longer earn their keep.
4. **Client lib, locales and boot** (`app/client/src/lib/`, `locales/`, `main.ts`, `App.svelte`, `app.css`, `vite-env.d.ts`, `scripts/check-literals.mjs`) — input/focus/gamepad loops (listeners, polling cost, leaks), `store.ts` races (`ServerStore`/`FileStore`), `engine.ts` save loading errors, catalog key drift between `es.ts`/`en.ts`/`xx.ts`, `i18n.ts` fallbacks, `errors.ts` codes vs. what the engine/server emit.
5. **Game screens** (`app/client/src/game/`): one task per big file (`Game.svelte` 1190 lines, `Question.svelte` 1238, `Overlay.svelte`, `sound.svelte.ts`, `Player.svelte`, `JokerTray.svelte`), small ones grouped (`Fireworks`/`Shredder`/`JokerFlight`, `Tower`/`Hud`/`Stage`/`DifficultyDial`, `CategoryPicker`/`Reports`/`LanguageScreen`, `Prompt`/`Glyph`/`Icon`, `copy.ts`/`swap.ts`/`timing.ts`/`theme.css`) — `$effect`s that redo work every frame, timers/listeners not cleaned up, unused CSS and props, unhandled game states, stale `PLACEHOLDER`s, literals outside the catalog, media preloading.
6. **Desktop shell and packaging** (`app/desktop/`: `main.mjs`, `resolve.mjs`, `save.mjs`, `preload.cjs`, `after-pack.mjs`, `stage-media.mjs`, `electron-builder.yml`, `package.json`) — Electron security settings, `app://` path traversal and Windows paths in `resolve.mjs`, save lock/backup races (D-72), offline rules, what goes into the package.
7. **qgen** (`authoring/tools/qgen.py`, 4074 lines): split by command/section into several review tasks (e.g. batch orchestration; draft/rate/factcheck/revise/review steps; translate; validate/export; report; rework/tighten/neutralize; helpers/CLI), plus one task that judges the module structure as a whole (split into modules → decision if it changes imports widely). Error handling around LLM calls and subprocesses, cost accounting, work-file IO, duplication with `health.py`, `translations.py`, `pool_export.py`.
8. **Other authoring tools** (`authoring/tools/` minus `qgen.py` and prompts: `health.py`, `translations.py`, `targets.py`, `age_groups.py`, `media.py`, `download.py`, `providers/*.py`, `concepts.py`, `progress.py`, `batches.py`, `layout.py`, `pool_export.py`, `save_file.py`, `engine.py`, `supply.ts`, `sim/*.ts`, `package.json`; `record_fixtures.py` per the task 302 rule) — rate limits/retries in `download.py` and providers, provider duplication, Node subprocess error paths in `engine.py`.
9. **Authoring server and UI** (`authoring/server/*.py`; `authoring/ui/src/**`, its configs) — handlers'' error responses and sync IO, `spot_checks.py` writes, `Review.svelte` (971 lines) split candidates, chart components'' shared code, `lib/types.ts` vs. the server''s actual JSON.
10. **Cross-cutting: duplication, consistency, build config** (needs parts 2–9) — consolidate the "duplication candidates" (`app/` ↔ `authoring/` types and API clients, Python ↔ TS ports that outlived their purpose, chart/CSS copies), naming and error-handling consistency across files, `flake.nix`, root `package.json`/`package-lock.json`, both `tsconfig.json`, `vite.config.ts`/`svelte.config.js`, `.gitignore`, `.envrc`; `directory.md` and `AGENTS.md` match the code. Larger refactors → decisions + follow-up tasks per the rules.
   - **Linter for TypeScript** (milestone section of the same name; here because it needs the findings of parts 1–9 and touches the build config this part owns):
     - Evaluate: which logged findings (`(lint: …)` tags, part 1''s `tsc` and bad-practice counts) each candidate would have caught; trial run on `app/client/src`, `authoring/ui/src`, `app/desktop` (`.mjs`/`.cjs`). Candidates: stricter `tsconfig` flags only (no new dependency), Biome, oxlint, ESLint + typescript-eslint + eslint-plugin-svelte; weigh bugs caught, Svelte support, dependency count, offline (nix/npm cache), speed, noise. Trial installs only in a temp copy, never committed before the decision.
     - Result in `code-review.md` (`### Linter evaluation` in `## Part 10`). A new dependency → `pm decision add` (options, recommended first; minimal-dependencies rule) and the adoption task waits on it via `pm task-pending-decision`; `tsconfig` flags alone need no decision.
