INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (82, 13, 'Cross-cutting duplication, consistency and build config (code review part 10)', 0, 'Part 10 of `plan 72: masterplan` (milestone 13, Code quality): consolidate the duplication candidates found by parts 2–9, check naming and error handling across files, review the build/package config, evaluate a linter for TypeScript (milestone section "Linter for TypeScript") and adopt it if useful, and check `directory.md`/`AGENTS.md`/`README.md` against the code last; fix what is cheap, log every file and finding in `## Part 10` of `code-review.md`. Scope, checklist, fix-or-ask, the task 302 rule, duplication candidates and the report format: plan 72 "Ground rules for every part"; not restated here.

## Depends on
- Parts 1–9 (plans 73–81): runs after them (same priority 0, higher plan id). **Every task re-reads `code-review.md`** (rows "duplication candidate", rows `handed to part 10`, follow-up tasks and decisions already opened) rather than assuming the clusters below; the lists here are what plans 74–81 announced, not what they found.
