- Binding: decision 4 (game server routes), decision 5 (supply via the TS engine under Node), decision 12 (desktop shell), D-59 (save read-only for authoring), D-71/D-72 (`app://`, desktop save), D-73 (local builds; CI is local per AGENTS.md), D-70 (typed catalog), AGENTS.md "Layout" (`authoring/` may import `app/`, never the reverse; `app/` never reads `authoring/data/`). `pm decision list --answered --grep <term>` before each consolidation.

## Rules for this plan
- Consolidate only where it is local and behaviour-neutral: one source of truth inside one language and one side of the layout rule (e.g. `authoring/ui` importing a type from `$app/lib/types.ts` instead of a copy). Cross-language duplication (Python ↔ TS/Node: save envelope, cache file names, MIME/range, path roots) is not merged by code: options are a shared JSON constant file, a parity check in an existing test, or "won''t fix, documented" → `pm decision add` (recommended first) + follow-up task via `pm task-pending-decision` when it changes structure or a format.
- Formats unchanged without a decision: save envelope, pool JSON, `app/data/pool*.json` byte-identical after `qgen export`, media cache file names, API routes/JSON shapes, URLs, CLI flags.
- Build config changes: `nix flake check` is not required, but `nix develop -c true` and `nix build .#app` (update `npmDepsHash` if the lockfile changes) when `flake.nix`, `flake.lock`, `package.json` or `package-lock.json` change; `trivia-desktop-build` only when `app/desktop` packaging is affected (part 6 owns it; note why if skipped). No new dependencies (AGENTS.md) except a linter after its decision (task 8); removing unused ones is in scope.
- Real `state/`, `authoring/data/`, `work/`, media cache are never written: servers and scripts on temp `TRIVIA_STATE`/`TRIVIA_MEDIA`/`TRIVIA_WORK`.
- A cluster too big for its task: fix the cheap part, `pm task add <this plan>` per remaining piece with exact files.
