- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass (plus the lint pass if adopted).', '', '2026-10-12T23:02:07Z', 512);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (84, 9, 'Release content runs', -110, 'The game needs thousands of questions in every language it ships in, plus extra regional question packs. This is the steady stream of generation runs that produces them: new regional questions, each batch checked by a person, and machine translations of the existing questions into English, German and both kinds of Spanish. Human checks and quality warnings still reach the developer as questions, but no run waits for the answers; only real failures stop a run.

Part 11 of the masterplan (plan 9): the recurring `qgen` runs that fill the release content. Drafted runs (neutral Spanish, regional batches) are each followed by D-56''s QC; translation runs (`tr-*`) are not: the LLM translation review is their only review (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-16). Reviews don''t gate runs (`decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`). Neutral Spanish rewrite (part 8, plan 64), translation pilot per language (QT-5, measured, no go/no-go), full translation per language (QT-6), the regional pilot `colombia` and the further regional bundles `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico` (part 10, plan 98; decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46); milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15). English-first `base` (part 15, `plan 148: English-first drafting for base`): from batch-9 on, `plan 17: Batch runs` drafts `base` in English; here those questions are translated en → `es`, `es-ES`, `de`, and the es-sourced pool (≤ batch-8) gets `en`, `de` and `es-ES`. No more Spanish `base` drafts or `es` top-ups. Priority -110: below plan 17''s batch runs (-100), so implementation work and milestone 1''s batches go first. Owners: `plans/15b-question-translation.md` (QT-5, QT-6), `plans/16-content-target.md` (progress per locale), `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` (pilot effort, bundle progress).

## Builds on
- D-36: workers only run `qgen batch` (and `qgen neutralize` when the developer asks); no prompt, pool, media or `qgen.py` changes inside a run or QC task.
- `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`: `locale` per source (absent = `es`); `questions.<L>.json` = translations into L of sources whose locale ≠ L; pool for L = approved sources in L + playing translations into L. Question locales `es` (Latin American), `es-ES` (Spain), `en`, `de`, each its own pool.
- Plan 148 provides, before the runs that need it: `qgen batch --translate <L>` for `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de` from either source (run names `tr-es-<n>`, `tr-es-ES-<n>`), `es-ES` prompt and market, targets and gap aiming for four question locales. Its task subjects may change; look them up with `pm show p148`.
- Decision 27 (D-78) for `base` replaced by plan 148 (es-419 comes from translation of English sources, `es-ES` its own pool); the es-sourced questions got `qgen neutralize` once (plan 64, D-83); `colombia` keeps its voice. Launch languages `es`, `en`, `de` (decision 26), plus `es-ES` as a question locale.
- Plan 66 / D-87: `qgen batch --translate <locale>`, runs `tr-<locale>-<n>`, 300 sources, first run per locale = 50-source pilot. Decision 45: Health thresholds and selection order for qgen batch --translate runs: its thresholds are reported, never a stop (decision 414 partly supersedes decision 45 and `decision 313: Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run`); its pilot stop is gone (`plan 171: Translations without human control`). Decision 35: text in media is never a problem.
- No human control of translations (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-16; the tr-en-1 and tr-de-1 spot checks, decisions 305 and 306, found every translation good): no native-speaker spot check, no QC task or QC decision per `tr-*` run, no pilot go/no-go, no `qgen health ack` after a pilot; all question locales, milestone 12''s included. The developer may still review translations in the review tool; `qgen flag` still sets `needs_work`.
- Decision 414 (developer, 2026-10-23): health ✗, spot checks and QC proposals are raised as pm decisions, but no task here ever waits on one (no `pm task-pending-decision`, no `--requires` on them); health ✗ never stops a run (drafting, `--bundle` or `--translate`), `qgen health ack` stays the developer''s "looked at it", never run by a worker; answers are acted on afterwards by the next QC task of the chain. The only human gate is the release (`trivia-release-check`, release bar), not a task here. What still blocks: real failures (below) and the non-review decisions a bundle''s start needs (taxonomy, slug keys).
- The code, RUNBOOK and `authoring/QC.md` changes for decision 414 (qgen''s exit 2 gone, QC steps without waits) are done (`plan 190: Reviews don''t gate generation`).
- Decision 21 (D-75): target 5000 approved per question locale (`en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`) with D-53''s mix, deficits per locale. English drafting (plan 17) aims at the locales'' deficits; decision 37''s last clause, D-84 and decision 219''s `DRIVES_DRAFTING` (es drafting steered by the en/de source shortfall) no longer apply. Simulation games numbers are information only.
- Decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46) (partly supersedes decision 37''s "packs have no target"): every regional bundle 2000 approved, region''s language + en (`colombia`: es + en); pilot `colombia` 102 → 2000 with its effort measured ($ per approved, the developer''s review time per 100); launch doesn''t wait for the pilot (ships what `colombia` has; content updates, plan 96, bring the rest). Its "more bundles only after a new decision with those numbers" is replaced (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15): `usa` (en), `germany` (de + en), `uk` (en), `spain` (es-ES + en), `mexico` (es + en), in that order (Steam audience), same rules, each drafted in the region''s language and variety (US English, British English, German, Spain''s Spanish, Mexican Spanish); they start once `colombia`''s taxonomy (decision 249: colombia taxonomy: categories and subcategories) and its first `qgen batch --bundle colombia` have proven the chain, not after colombia''s 2000; no "More regional bundles?" decision. The only Spanish drafting left is regional (`colombia`, `spain`, `mexico`).
- Plan 98 and `plan 138: Regional taxonomy: a general list, colombia reworked` (decision 166) provide, before the regional chain runs: `colombia`''s own taxonomy with its questions remapped, the bundle target (2000) in `targets.json`, `qgen batch --translate <locale> --bundle <id>`, and the review-time line in `qgen report`. For the further bundles plan 98 also provides, per bundle: `qgen bundle new --kind region`, its taxonomy decision and `qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>` applied (after part 16''s slug keys, `plan 149: Slug keys for categories`), its 2000 target; `qgen batch --bundle <id>` drafting in the bundle''s source language (en, de, es-ES, es; `bundles.json` `rule`/`voice`), and `--translate en --bundle <id>` from de and es-ES. Look subjects up with `pm show p98`, `pm show p138`, `pm show p149`.
- Decision 2 / D-56 / decision 15 (D-79): 30-question blind spot check, ≥ 90 % agreement for drafted batches; a run below it only feeds QC step 4. Decision 3: `qgen rework` once after each drafting batch''s QC (here: every regional `batch-<n>`).
- `authoring/QC.md`: steps 1–4 (drafted runs), without waits (decision 414); its step 5 "Next batch waits" no longer applies. Section "Neutralize runs". Its "Translation runs" section has no spot check (plan 171).
- Plan 17 "Batch tasks under pm run" and its "Reviews don''t gate (decision 414)": `tasks.sql` alone isn''t a dirty tree; stage exactly the printed `git add` paths, don''t commit. Run tasks here follow the same exit rules:
  - Health ✗ (in the output, the report or `qgen health`): look up the run''s decision (`pm decision list --grep "<run>: health"`), else `pm decision add "<run>: health ✗, look at it?"`, no task linked; the task goes on. For a `tr-*` run, ✗ = a decision 45 threshold crossed.
  - Exit 75, other non-zero codes, or exit 1 three times at one step: real failures → `pm decision add "Continue <run> …?"` with the last 30 lines, `pm task-pending-decision`, stage nothing, stop.
- Cost is information only (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15; `task 463: Release budget per language (pm decision, CT-3)` dropped): run and QC tasks note `qgen report --cost` ($ per approved per run, per direction, per bundle); no dollar budget per language or bundle, no budget decision, no over-budget gates, no pace question about cost; full runs don''t wait for a budget.

## Task shapes
- **Drafted runs** (`neutralize-<n>`, regional `batch-<n>`): two tasks, `run <run>` (the command, RUNBOOK steps; note "Done:" line, report path, health result: ✗ reported, not a stop) and `QC <run>` (requires the run task; `authoring/QC.md` steps 1–4, without waits):
  - first: the answered review decisions of the chain''s earlier runs not yet acted on (health ack notes, spot-check results, QC proposal choices; `pm decision list --answered --grep <run>`) → change tasks in their plans at their priority, report lines; an unanswered one stays open, nothing waits
  - spot check: `pm decision add "Spot check <run> done?"` (the native speaker the region needs, review link), raised, not waited on; `qgen report --qc <run>` uses the spot checks recorded so far, the next QC task adds later ones
  - `qgen report --qc <run>` → proposals decision "QC <run>: which changes?", raised, not waited on (its recommended option names the change tasks the next QC task adds once answered); none → `qgen report --qc <run> --changes none`
  - decision 3''s `qgen rework` once; then adds the next pair of its chain in the same task, without waiting for any answer
- **Translation runs** (`tr-<locale>-<n>`, with or without `--bundle`): one task, `run <run>`. After the run it notes the "Done:" line, report path and the numbers from `authoring/reports/<run>.md` and `qgen report --cost`: selected, translated, approved, needs_work, rejected, not travelling, $ per approved translation, audit agreement, health result, per source locale (es → L, en → L, de → en, es-ES → en) where the report shows them. No spot check, no QC decision, no `qgen health ack`. Then it updates the plan file line (rules per chain) and adds the next run task of its chain.
- One open run (or run/QC pair) per chain and language.
- `needs_work`: regional drafted runs per decision 3 (`qgen rework` once after QC); translations need nothing: a non-approved translation is picked again by the next `--translate` run.
- Every task body repeats the pm-run rules above (stage, health ✗, exit codes) and names its run.

## Chains
1. **Neutral Spanish** (priority -85): `run neutralize-1`, `QC neutralize-1` (both done; decision 271: no second pass). Nothing more.
2. **Translation pilot** (QT-5, priority -90): done. `run tr-en-1`, `run tr-de-1` (spot checks done before the rule changed: decisions 305, 306), `run tr-es-ES-1`, `run tr-es-1`, and `task 1506: Translation pilot numbers (QT-5)`. Nothing more.
3. **Full translation** (QT-6, priority -110), per locale `en`, `de`, `es-ES`, `es`:
   - `run tr-<locale>-<n>` (n ≥ 2): before running, plan 17: if its exit check isn''t done, wait for what blocks plan 17''s earliest open task (the queue reaches -110 only when -100 is blocked): a pending decision → `pm task-pending-decision`; a prerequisite task → `pm task requires`; stop. Translations follow milestone 1''s batches (masterplan order), so they don''t go stale. Under decision 414 that blocker is never a review. Then `qgen batch --translate <locale>` (sources of either locale ≠ L).
   - After the run, the task itself:
     - `qgen report --locale <locale>` meets the target (every level at `targets.json` `base`) → no next run; QT-6 progress line in 15b; if all four locales are done: QT-6 `[x]`.
     - The run selected fewer than 300 sources (the approved sources not yet in L ran out) → adds the next run still; that run starts only after a plan 17 batch QC done since this run, else waits for what blocks plan 17''s earliest open task (as above). The locale''s remaining deficit is English drafting''s (plan 148''s gap aiming), never an `es` top-up.
     - Else adds `run tr-<locale>-<n+1>`.
     - Each run adds a QT-6 progress line (approved per locale) in 15b.
   - A health ✗ doesn''t stop the chain: the run raises its decision and adds the next run like any other.
4. **Regional pilot `colombia`** (priority -110; decision 110):
   - Start task done (`task 643: Regional pilot colombia: start`); first pair done (`task 1295: run colombia batch (batch-<n>)`, `task 1296: QC batch-12 (colombia)`: first effort numbers, batch-12: $0.28 per approved, 35 min per 100 verdicts; the chain is proven for chain 5).
   - es pairs: `run batch-<n>` (`qgen batch --bundle colombia`, Colombian Spanish, RUNBOOK) + `QC batch-<n>` (drafted-run QC shape above, native Colombian Spanish speaker, decision 3''s `qgen rework` once). The QC task adds the next es pair until `qgen report --bundle colombia` shows 2000 approved (es), without waiting for its spot-check or proposals answers.
   - At 2000 es, the closing QC adds two tasks:
     - **Pilot effort**: $ per approved (`qgen report --cost`, per bundle) and the developer''s review time per 100 (plan 98''s `qgen report` line) recorded in `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` and `16-content-target.md`. No "More regional bundles?" decision (chain 5 already runs them).
     - The first en run: `run tr-en-<n>` with `qgen batch --translate en --bundle colombia` (translation run shape). Needs plan 98''s `--translate --bundle` done (else `pm task requires` on that task, stop). Each run adds the next until `qgen report --bundle colombia --locale en` (or the report plan 98 names) shows 2000 approved en; then `plans/15c` notes `colombia` es + en done.
   - Run names come from `qgen` (`batch-<n>`, `tr-en-<n>` shared with chain 3 and plan 17).
   - Launch (milestone 11) doesn''t wait for this chain.
5. **More regional bundles** (priority -110; milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15), in audience order `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`:
   - One start task per bundle (`task 1268: Regional runs usa: start` … `task 1272: Regional runs mexico: start`): needs plan 98''s tasks for that bundle (bundle created, taxonomy applied after plan 149''s slug keys, target, drafting in its language) done; colombia''s first QC (`task 1296`) is done. Not done: pend on the decision blocking them (the bundle''s taxonomy decision, plan 149''s slug decision, plan 98''s earliest open decision; these are choices, not reviews, so they still block) or `pm task requires` on the unfinished task, stop. Then add the bundle''s first drafting pair.
   - Drafting pairs: `run batch-<n>` (`qgen batch --bundle <id>`, region''s language and variety, RUNBOOK) + `QC batch-<n>` (drafted-run QC shape, spot check by a native speaker of US English / British English / German / Spain''s Spanish / Mexican Spanish, raised not waited on, decision 3''s `qgen rework` once). The QC adds the next pair until `qgen report --bundle <id>` shows 2000 approved in the region''s language.
   - At 2000: `germany`, `spain`, `mexico` get en runs like colombia''s (`qgen batch --translate en --bundle <id>`, translation run shape; needs plan 98''s `--translate en` from de / es-ES done, else `pm task requires` on it); each run adds the next until 2000 en; `usa`, `uk` are en only, nothing more. Then `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` notes the bundle done.
   - Pace: interleaved with colombia''s runs, one open pair (or run) per bundle and language, all at -110 (added in audience order, so `usa` runs before `germany` and so on at equal priority). Cost numbers are information only: no QC task asks whether the pace is too costly.
   - Launch (milestone 11) doesn''t wait for this chain; DLC entries, store texts and capsules per bundle are plans 130, 89, 88''s (plan 98 adds those follow-ups), not this plan''s.

## Tasks (for the split)
- Done: 632–634, 636, 643, 1221, 1223, 1295, 1296, 1506. Dropped: 635, 637, 638, 640, 642, 1222, 1224, 1225, 1227, 1229.
- Open, bodies revised to decision 414 (no new tasks):
  - full runs `run tr-en-2` (639), `run tr-de-2` (641), `run tr-es-ES-2` (1226), `run tr-es-2` (1228): drop the pilot and `plan 171` pre-checks once they''re done (pilots done; keep 171''s only if its task is still open, as `pm task requires`); plan 17 wait as in chain 3; pm-run rules as above (health ✗ raised, not waited on; real failures stop).
  - colombia''s pair `task 1690: run colombia batch (batch-<n>)` / `task 1691: QC colombia batch (batch-<n>)`: 1691''s spot check "pending, stop until answered" and proposals wait become raise-and-go-on; it first acts on answered review decisions of earlier colombia batches; its "too costly" pace line goes; pm-run rules as above.
  - bundle starts 1268–1272: pm-run rules and the pairs they add follow the drafted-run QC shape; their taxonomy/slug blockers stay.
- Later runs, pairs, the en runs of every bundle and the pilot effort task are added by the run and QC tasks, not the split.

## Done when
- The four translation chains end at their target (or with an answered decision that stops them), QT-5 and QT-6 `[x]` in 15b, `colombia` at 2000 approved in es and en, the pilot''s effort recorded, `usa`, `uk` at 2000 en, `germany` (de + en), `spain` (es-ES + en), `mexico` (es + en) at 2000 each (may land after launch), `qgen report --locale <L>` for `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de` recorded in plan 16. The close-out check (`qgen report --simulate`) is part 12 (task 251).

## Out of scope
- Prompt or code changes (QC change tasks go to plans 64, 66, 70, 148, 171 or new ones; qgen''s exit 2 and QC.md''s waits went with `plan 190: Reviews don''t gate generation`); English `base` batches themselves (plan 17, plan 147); the back-audit (plan 57); store texts (S5); later languages (milestone 12).', 'This covers the large content runs that fill the game for release: new regional questions and translations of the questions into the launch languages. Each run is a long automated job; quality warnings and human checks are reported to the developer but never hold the runs up, and only real failures stop one. It runs only when nothing more urgent is available.', '2026-10-13T05:13:28Z', 250);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (85, 10, 'Steamworks binding in the shell (SW-8)', 690, 'SW-8 (masterplan 10 part 3): the Electron shell talks to the local Steam client through steamworks-ffi-node (decision 28: Steam binding for the Electron shell; D-63). Overlay, the on-screen keyboard for the player name, per-device glyphs, Steam''s language as the first-start guess, the valid-Steam-user check that gates saves and flags, and a dev-mode menu row «Ir a pregunta…» for testing questions by id. Steam only (decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam): init failure must not crash, but no work, checks or done-whens for running without Steam; fallbacks that also serve under Steam stay (letter picker, `Gamepad.id` glyphs, `navigator.language`). Owner: `plans/18-steam-integration.md` ("Steam features", SW-8); touches `14-input.md`, `15-i18n.md`.

## Builds on (don''t rebuild)
- Shell: `app/desktop/main.mjs`, `preload.cjs` (bridge `window.trivia`, sender-origin check), `app/client/src/lib/desktop.ts` (D-71, plan 54); `FileStore` (D-72, plan 55); builds `electron-builder.yml`, `trivia-desktop-build` (D-73, plan 56).
- Glyphs: `lib/gamepad.ts` `styleOf(Gamepad.id)`, `Glyph.svelte` (plan 45). Letter picker: `LetterPicker.svelte` (plan 46). Language: `guessTag()` + `ready()` in `lib/engine.ts`, `defaultLanguage()` in `engine/save.ts` (plan 68, D-86).
- Sibling parts of masterplan 10: App ID and `steam_appid.txt` values (parts 1–2, tasks 253/254); Cloud saves and the Steam-user gate (part 4, plan 87) and achievements (part 5, plan 86) call this bridge; builds/upload (part 7, plan 89).
- Done here (tasks 645–649, 651): binding, `steam.available` via `--trivia-steam`, `steamId()`, `language()`, `unlock()`, overlay (decision 70: Steam overlay in the Electron shell: Windows only, D-92), keyboard, glyphs, rich presence.
- Dev server of plan 99 (Vite, page shim for the save half of the bridge, `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` or a temp dir).

## Rules
- Binding in the main process only; the page sees one optional object `window.trivia.steam` (and `lib/desktop.ts` exports `steam: SteamBridge | null`). The page checks `steam?.available`; no Node, no FFI in the page.
- `init` failure (no Steam client, wrong App ID, offline, missing native lib, koffi load error) → `available: false`, one line on stderr, nothing on screen. No `restartAppIfNecessary`, no DRM, no network of our own (the `webRequest` block stays).
- Run callbacks (`runCallbacks`) on a timer in main only while Steam is up; stop on quit, `shutdown()` in `will-quit`.
- App ID: one constant in `main.mjs` (`STEAM_APP_ID`), 480 (Spacewar) until the App ID decision of part 1 is answered; dev may override with `TRIVIA_STEAM_APPID`. Under a Steam launch the client''s `SteamAppId` env wins.
- Dependency: `steamworks-ffi-node` in `app/desktop/package.json` `dependencies` (pinned) and nothing else. Steamworks SDK `redistributable_bin` (Valve licence) is not in git: gitignored `app/desktop/steamworks_sdk/redistributable_bin/` (`linux64/libsteam_api.so`, `win64/steam_api64.dll`), path via `setSdkPath`; the gamemaster downloads the SDK zip (partner account, part 1); dev on NixOS may take `libsteam_api.so` from nixpkgs `steamworks-sdk-redist` (unfree) in the flake instead.
- Strings via `t()` in every catalog (es, es-ES where it differs, en, de); `check:literals` passes.

## Bridge (shape; the first task fixes it)
`steam: { available, user, steamId(), language(), overlay: {…}, showTextInput(field rect, current) → Promise<boolean>, inputTypes() → PadStyle[] | null, setPresence(key, values) , unlock(id) }` over fixed IPC channels `steam:*`, same origin check as `save:*`. `unlock` and `steamId` are for parts 4 and 5; this plan only exposes them (plain pass-through, no logic).

## Valid Steam user and dev switch (decision 111)
- Valid user = `steam.available` and a non-zero SteamID, or the dev switch. Computed once in `main.mjs` at start (the SteamID doesn''t change in a session) and passed to the page like `available` (`additionalArguments`, e.g. `--trivia-user`): `steam.user` boolean.
- Dev switch: env `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` → `steam.user` true even without Steam (saves and flags on); one stderr line `trivia: dev Steam user (TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER)`. Honoured in packaged builds too (soft check, patchable, accepted; part 7''s smoke game uses it); never set by `trivia-desktop-build`, launch options or VDFs. Under the switch without Steam `steamId()` stays null; the save folder is plan 87''s call (`TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` or a fixed dev folder).
- Page: `lib/desktop.ts` exports one `validUser: boolean` = `steam?.user === true`, or true under plan 99''s dev server shim (its `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`/temp save counts as the dev switch). Plan 87 (save gate, notice) and the flag UI read only `validUser`, never their own Steam test.
- No DRM, no `restartAppIfNecessary`, no anti-tamper, no ownership check beyond this.
- Docs: `README.md` and AGENTS.md "Commands" (`trivia-desktop` line) name `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER`; `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Steam features".

## Language guess (milestone outcome)
- `guessTag()` becomes `async` (only `ready()` calls it): `steam?.available ? fromSteam(await steam.language()) : null` ?? `navigator.language` ?? `es`. `steam.language()` = `ISteamApps::GetCurrentGameLanguage` (the game''s language set in Steam, else the client''s).
- Mapping table (pure, in `lib/engine.ts` or a small `lib/steamlang.ts`): `latam` → `es`, `spanish` → `es-ES` (UI variant es-ES, questions `es` through `defaultLanguage`''s language-part match; decision 27: Spanish variety), `english` → `en`, `german` → `de`, `schinese` → `zh-Hans`, `russian` → `ru`, `brazilian` → `pt-BR` (the last three fall through `defaultLanguage`''s best match until their locales exist, milestone 12). Unknown name → `null` → `navigator.language`.
- Only the fresh-save preselection: `save.language` always wins; the first-start screen still asks (D-86).
- 15-i18n.md "Model" and I18N-2 note: Steam language wired.

## Overlay
- Decided (decision 70: Steam overlay in the Electron shell, D-92): Windows only (`addElectronSteamOverlay` on win32); Linux without overlay (native GL window freezes the game on XWayland); Deck via Proton. Gamemaster check on Windows in the close-out.
- Game pauses nothing on overlay open (no timer outside `timed`; `timed` pause on `GameOverlayActivated` is a follow-up only if mode `timed` exists by then).

## On-screen keyboard (player name)
- Under Steam with a pad: the name field opens `ShowFloatingGamepadTextInput` (keystrokes into the focused `<input>`) at the field''s rect; returns false outside Big Picture/Deck → the letter picker (plan 46) as today. If keystrokes don''t reach Chromium, use `ShowGamepadTextInput` + `GetEnteredGamepadTextInput` (returns the text) instead; note which in 14-input.md.
- Keyboard/mouse users keep the plain field; the picker stays the fallback outside Big Picture/Deck.

## Glyphs
- With Steam Input on, every pad is a virtual Xbox pad, so `Gamepad.id` says Xbox. `steam.inputTypes()` = `GetInputTypeForHandle` of the connected handles (Steam Input init in main); one PlayStation-type pad → `playstation` glyphs; Steam Deck / Steam Controller / others → Xbox (no Deck glyph set without a pm decision). Several pads of mixed types: Xbox (per-player glyphs come with IN-6).
- If the binding doesn''t expose Steam Input: keep `Gamepad.id`, note it in 14-input.md, no follow-up.

## Rich presence (optional, last)
- «Nivel 7 de 12»: Steam shows `steam_display` tokens from a localization file uploaded in Steamworks, not our strings. Draft the token file (`#Level` = «Nivel %level% de %levels%» per launch language, from the catalogs'' `t()` strings) as a file for the gamemaster to upload; the page calls `setPresence` on level change; cleared on quit.

## Dev mode «Ir a pregunta…» (masterplan 10 rules)
- Dev mode = the dev switch (`TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`) or plan 99''s dev server; a real Steam user is not dev mode. Shell passes it like `user` (`--trivia-dev` → `desktop.dev` / `steam.dev`); `lib/desktop.ts` exports one `devMode: boolean` (dev-server shim → true). Not `validUser` (that is also true for real users).
- Row «Ir a pregunta…» in the gamemaster menu (`Overlay.svelte`), general part, every mode (testing, not a cheat: decision 34: Gamemaster menu: which cheats? keeps cheats gamemaster-only), only in dev mode and while a question is on screen; absent otherwise.
- Input: question id (text field; pad users get the letter picker/keyboard as for names, or digits only if ids allow). Submit → engine action (e.g. `goTo(save, data, io, id)` in `engine/game.ts`, beside `replace`): that question replaces the current one at the current level like «Cambiar pregunta» (old one logged `admin_replace`, not seen), ignoring level range, age group, bundle selection and seen; undo snapshot as for `replace`.
- Unknown id or not in the loaded pool (other language, pack not installed) → short message in the dialog, game unchanged (`GameError` code, string via `t()`).
- Strings via `t()` in every catalog (es, es-ES where it differs, en, de); `check:literals` passes.

## Packaging
- `electron-builder.yml`: `asarUnpack` for `node_modules/steamworks-ffi-node/**`, `node_modules/koffi/**`, `node_modules/@koromix/koffi-*/**` and the SDK folder (`extraResources` or unpacked), as the binding''s docs say. Cross-build risk: npm installs only the host''s optional `@koromix/koffi-*` package, so the Windows zip built on Linux needs the win32-x64 one too (`npm install --os=win32 --cpu=x64 …` or the doc''s way); check the zip content lists `steam_api64.dll` and the win32 koffi binary.
- `CREDITS.md`: steamworks-ffi-node (MIT), koffi (MIT), Steamworks SDK redistributable (Valve) through `app/client/credits.ts` (plan 47).
- Dev: `trivia-desktop` with the Steam client running and `TRIVIA_STEAM_APPID=480` (or the real App ID), or `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` for checks without a Steam session; `steam_appid.txt` beside the Electron binary only in dev, never in `release/` unless part 2 says so.

## Tasks (suggested order)
1. Binding spike + bridge: dependency, SDK folder (gitignored) + flake lib for dev, init/shutdown/callbacks in `main.mjs`, `steam` object in `preload.cjs`, `SteamBridge` type in `lib/desktop.ts`; `available`, `steamId()`, `language()`, `unlock()` pass-through. Check: under Steam (480) `available` true, SteamID and language printed; without Steam a full game plays (D-72 save untouched); browser game unchanged. If the SDK isn''t there yet: gamemaster step as a pm decision ("Steamworks SDK zip downloaded to …?").
2. Language guess: async `guessTag()`, mapping table, fresh save with Steam language `german` preselects de/de, `spanish` es-ES/es, `latam` es/es, unknown → navigator; a saved language unchanged. One small `node:test` for the mapping only if it stays useful.
3. Overlay spike and wiring (Linux X11, Windows; the Deck goes into part 10''s checklist): result as a D-entry; gamemaster check via pm decision where a real Steam session is needed.
4. On-screen keyboard for the player name (Player screen, `LetterPicker` fallback).
5. Glyphs via `GetInputTypeForHandle`.
6. Packaging: `asarUnpack`, win32 koffi in the cross build, SDK libs in both artefacts, credits; packaged Linux build starts under Steam (480) and `available` is true (no start test without Steam, decision 39).
7. Rich presence (optional, lowest priority; drop if the token upload isn''t worth it).
8. Close-out: gamemaster check under Steam (overlay opens on Windows, keyboard fills the name, fresh save preselects Steam''s language, PlayStation glyphs) as one pm decision, no "without Steam" rows; `18-steam-integration.md` SW-8 `[x]` with note and "Steam features" updated, `14-input.md` (glyphs, keyboard), `15-i18n.md` (I18N-2 note), `plans/project.md`, `directory.md`.
9. Valid-user check and dev switch (new; before plan 87''s gate task): `steam.user` + `--trivia-user` in `main.mjs`/`preload.cjs`, `SteamBridge.user` and `validUser` in `lib/desktop.ts` (dev-server shim → true), `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER`, README + AGENTS.md "Commands". Check: under Spacewar (480) logged in → true; `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` without Steam → true; neither → false (stderr lines show it); dev server → true. No consumers here (plan 87 and the flag UI).
10. Dev mode «Ir a pregunta…» (after task 9): `devMode` in shell/preload/`lib/desktop.ts`, engine action, menu row and dialog, strings. Check under the dev server or `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`: a video question''s id opens it at the current level, an unknown id shows the message; under Steam without the switch the row is absent. README / AGENTS.md "Commands" `trivia-desktop` line: the switch also shows the row.

## Done when
- Under Steam: the overlay opens (Windows), the keyboard fills the name, a fresh save preselects Steam''s language.
- `steam.user` / `validUser` true with a logged-in Steam user and with the dev switch, false otherwise.
- Under the dev switch or the dev server «Ir a pregunta…» opens a video question by id; without dev mode the row is absent.', '', '2026-10-13T05:17:09Z', 255);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (86, 10, 'Achievements (SW-11)', 590, 'SW-11 (masterplan 10 part 5): a few Steam achievements, no grind, earned only in games that play by the standard rules, unlocked only for a valid Steam user (decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam). Owner: `plans/18-steam-integration.md` ("Steam features", SW-11); touches `13-game-modes.md` (MD-8 note), `17-publishing.md` (credits).

## Builds on (don''t rebuild)
- Bridge `steam.unlock(id) → Promise<boolean>` (plan 85, `lib/desktop.ts`; `main.mjs` `steam:unlock` → `achievements.unlockAchievement`). Rich presence in `Game.svelte` is the pattern for a page-side Steam call.
- Valid user: `validUser` from `lib/desktop.ts` (plan 85, task 776: `steam.user`, dev switch `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER`); never an own Steam test.
- Engine: `GameRow.result`, `settings.mode` / `gameMode()`, `settings.customized` (solo only, set by `newGame` when jokers differ from `STANDARD_JOKERS`), `state.jokers` (jokers played), `history[].correct`, `categoryOf(data.broad)` (`engine/game.ts`, `state.ts`, `pool.ts`).
- Save per Steam user: plan 87 (one save per SteamID, memory-only without a valid user); App ID: masterplan parts 1–2. Achievement tests need the real App ID (Spacewar 480 has only its own achievements).

## Rules
- Qualifying game (decision 19: Default mode: presets, checkpoints and won levels): `gameMode(state) !== "gamemaster"`, `!settings.customized`, no `settings.difficulty`, `levels` missing or 12, `cards` missing or 4, no `history[].outcome === "admin_replace"` (dev mode «Ir a pregunta…», plan 85 task 813, works in every mode and logs it). Video/audio off doesn''t disqualify (not a rule change).
- **Gamemaster mode never earns achievements** (decision 74: Gamemaster mode earns no achievements): undo, skip, replace, any joker budget (D-74, D-88).
- **Derived from the save, never stored**: one pure function `earned(save, data) → AchievementId[]` over all qualifying game rows (every player of the save: the save is the Steam account''s). No achievement field in the save; nothing in the save depends on Steam.
- **Unlock only with a valid user and a live bridge**: `validUser && steam?.available`; the dev switch without a Steam client makes no calls. Without a valid user nothing persists (plan 87), so there is nothing to unlock later from that session.
- Unlock = `earned()` minus what this session already sent, through `steam.unlock`, at two moments: when a game ends (won/lost/abandoned) and once after the save loads. The second (retroactive) is the same code, so it stays: covers a save brought in with `--import-save` (plan 99, the family''s save), games played before the achievements were published in Steamworks, and a failed call. Steam caches offline unlocks itself; `unlock` is idempotent.
- No Steam stats, no progress pop-ups (`IndicateAchievementProgress`), no hidden achievements, no on-screen achievement UI of our own (Steam''s toast only; the overlay is Windows only, D-92).
- Strings: Steam shows Steamworks'' localized names, not our catalogs; texts live in the Steamworks setup file (below), not in `t()`.

## The list (draft; the gamemaster approves it as decision 73: Achievement list (SW-11)? before icons)
| API name | Trigger (qualifying games only) |
|---|---|
| `FIRST_WIN` | any game with `result === "won"` |
| `WIN_NO_JOKERS` | a won game with `state.jokers` empty, in a mode with jokers (`solo`, `rr-coop`, `rr-competitive`) |
| `ALL_CATEGORIES` | every broad category of the `base` bundle that has questions in the loaded pool''s locale has ≥ 1 correctly answered question (`history[].correct === true`) across all qualifying games, any result; question not in the loaded pool → ignored (28 categories today: ~4–6 games, the only cumulative one) |
| `WIN_RR_COOP` | won game, mode `rr-coop` |
| `WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE` | a player''s game in `rr-competitive` won |
| `WIN_TIMED` | won game, mode `timed` |

- `solo`''s win is `FIRST_WIN` (no separate `WIN_SOLO`).
- Only modes in `BUILT_MODES` go into Steamworks now (solo: the first three); the three mode wins stay in the code list and get entered in Steamworks with MD-8 (Steam shows every defined achievement; unreachable ones look broken). `13-game-modes.md` MD-8 gets that note.
- Names/descriptions per launch language: `latam` and `spanish` (same text unless es-ES needs a word changed), `english`, `german`; tone of the game''s catalogs (joker names per decisions 43/44, 54–58 where referenced).

## Icons
- Original art: SVG sources in the house style of `Icon.svelte` / `Glyph.svelte` (`10-visual-design.md` palette), one per achievement, in `app/desktop/achievements/` (`<API>.svg`); a script renders the achieved PNG and the unachieved one (greyscale, dimmed) at Valve''s current size (the masterplan says 64×64; check Steamworks docs, render the size they ask for, 256×256 if they ask for that). Renderer: something offline already in the dev shell (Electron/Chromium headless or `rsvg-convert`/`resvg` from the flake); no npm dependency.
- PNGs are build outputs for the gamemaster''s upload: gitignored, or committed if the script can''t run in every dev shell (task decides, note in `directory.md`).
- Credits (plan 47, `app/client/credits.ts`): achievement icons under the game''s own art, like the glyphs.

## Steamworks setup (values for the gamemaster, in plan 18; masterplan part 2 enters them)
- Per achievement: API name, display name + description per language, Hidden = no, achieved/unachieved icon file, "Set by" Client, no stat.
- Localization: one file `app/desktop/steam-achievements.vdf` (like `steam-presence.vdf`) in Steamworks'' achievement-localization format if Steamworks accepts an upload; otherwise the table in plan 18 to type in.
- Publish in Steamworks after entering (the gamemaster); result via pm decision.

## Tasks (suggested order)
1. Achievement list as a pm decision (task 654): decision 73 pending, decision 74 recorded; after the answer, consequences with the final list.
2. Engine + page (task 655): `app/client/src/engine/achievements.ts` (`ACHIEVEMENTS` list with API names and mode, `qualifies(row)`, `earned(save, data)`), page wiring (game end + after load, once per id per session, only `validUser && steam?.available`). One `node:test` over a fixture save (qualifying/customized/gamemaster/`admin_replace`/categories) only if it stays useful. Check: under Steam (480 or the real App ID) with a logged-in user the calls go out (stderr log in `main.mjs` on a false return); `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` without Steam makes no calls and doesn''t break. After task 776 (`validUser`).
3. Icons (task 656): SVG sources + render script, achieved/unachieved PNGs at Valve''s size, credits entry. After task 1''s answer.
4. Steamworks setup (task 657): values + `steam-achievements.vdf` in plan 18; gamemaster enters them (pm decision "Achievements entered and published in Steamworks?"). Needs the App ID (parts 1–2).
5. Close-out (task 658): gamemaster check under Steam with the real App ID (fresh Steam account or reset stats: win a solo game → `FIRST_WIN` toast; customized game earns nothing; a save with earlier qualifying wins, e.g. via `--import-save`, unlocks on next start) as one pm decision; `18-steam-integration.md` SW-11 `[x]` with note and "Steam features" bullet rewritten (drop the presets/Experto wording), `13-game-modes.md` MD-8 note, `plans/project.md`, `directory.md`.

## Done when
- Under Steam with the real App ID and a logged-in user: a qualifying win unlocks `FIRST_WIN`; a customized or gamemaster game unlocks nothing; earlier qualifying games in the save unlock on the next start.', '', '2026-10-13T05:47:45Z', 257);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (87, 10, 'Steam Cloud saves', 680, 'Masterplan 10 part 4: one save per valid Steam user, synced by Steam Auto-Cloud (gamemaster, 2026-10-12: a save = a profile, so players, seen counters, blocked, flags and selection per profile come along, plan 65 / D-82); without a valid user the game plays memory-only and hides the flag action (decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy). No Cloud API code unless the test shows a need. Owner: `plans/18-steam-integration.md` ("Steam features", Steam Cloud bullet); save format `plans/12-client-engine.md`.

## Binding
- decision 111: Steam only: saves and flags need a valid Steam user (`steam.available` and a non-zero SteamID, or the dev switch); without one: memory-only save, short notice, flag action hidden; soft check, no DRM; no "without Steam" rows in checklists or done-whens. Supersedes this plan''s earlier `local/` folder, S3 migration and «Usar el progreso de este equipo» dialog.
- decision 39: Local builds start offline?: no start test outside Steam.
- Never phones home: Auto-Cloud is Steam''s, no code of ours talks to the network.

## Done already (tasks 660–663; partly undone below)
- Per-user folder in `app/desktop/main.mjs` (`userSaveDir()`: `B/<steamid64>/`, else `B/local/`; `migrateToLocal()` S3 `B/game.json` + `backup/` → `local/`; `startSteam()` before the save is made; `--import-save` into the chosen folder). Stays: the `<steamid64>/` folder, the order, `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`. Goes: `local/`, `migrateToLocal`.
- First-start offer: `save:local-offer`/`save:adopt-local` (`main.mjs`, `preload.cjs`, `save.mjs`), `lib/desktop.ts` type, `ready()` in `lib/engine.ts`, `game/LocalProgress.svelte`, its catalog strings. Goes entirely.
- Auto-Cloud values and the Steam Cloud test table in plan 18 (task 662, task 663); decision 75 "Steam Cloud test passed?" pending with the old checklist (its `local/`/«Usar el progreso» row is void; plan 18''s table is what counts).

## Builds on (don''t rebuild)
- `FileStore` and `app/desktop/save.mjs` (D-72, plan 55): atomic `game.json.tmp` + rename, `backup/`, stale `.tmp` dropped, `--import-save`.
- Plan 85 (`task 776: Valid Steam user check and dev switch (TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER)`): `steam.user` from `main.mjs` (`--trivia-user`), `validUser` in `lib/desktop.ts` (true under plan 99''s dev server shim). This plan reads only these, never its own Steam test. Its tasks wait for task 776.
- Plan 99 (dev server, `--import-save` for the family save, `ServerStore` removal): the family''s save reaches the desktop through `trivia-desktop --import-save`, not through a dialog.
- Achievements derive from the save (plan 86) and unlock only with a valid user (plan 86''s call).

## Paths
- Base `B` = `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` if set (used as is, no subfolder), else packaged `<userData>/save` (`%APPDATA%\trivia\save`, `~/.config/trivia/save`), dev `state/desktop`.
- Valid user with a SteamID: `B/<steamid64>/game.json` (each folder its own `.tmp` and `backup/`).
- Dev switch without a SteamID (`TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, no Steam): `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` if set, else `B/dev/game.json`; one stderr line names it. Packaged builds under the switch the same (smoke game, plan 89).
- No valid user: no save file at all; `main.mjs` makes no `saveFile`, creates no folder, `save:*` load → null, write/backup → refused (soft, the page never calls them then).
- Existing `B/local/` and S3''s `B/game.json` on disk: left alone, never read or deleted (the family imports via plan 99).

## Without a valid user (page)
- `ready()` picks the store: `validUser` → `FileStore` (desktop bridge or dev shim); else a `MemoryStore` (`lib/store.ts`: load → null, write → keeps the text in memory, nothing on disk). Fresh save → D-86 first-start language screen as usual, every start.
- Notice: one short line «Sin Steam no se guarda el progreso» (wording the task''s; es, es-ES where it differs, en, de; `check:literals` passes), shown once per start where the save notices show today (`takeSaveNotice` path or the same spot), dismissable, keyboard/mouse/pad.
- Flags: flag icon, `M` key, pad Select, «Preguntas marcadas» menu entry, `FlagDialog`/`FlagList` not reachable when `!validUser` (`Game.svelte`, `Overlay.svelte`, input maps); with a valid user as today (plan 93 builds on it in milestone 11).

## Auto-Cloud (values in plan 18, part 2 enters them)
- Unchanged: root `WinAppDataRoaming`, subdirectory `trivia/save/{64BitSteamID}`, pattern `game.json`, non-recursive, Linux override `LinuxXdgConfigHome`, quota 1 file / 20 MB, Steam''s conflict dialog, Family Sharing borrower → own slot.
- Plan 18 text drops `local/` and the migration; the cloud listing check reads "only `game.json`, never `.tmp`, `backup/`, `dev/`".

## Tasks (suggested order)
1. Shell: drop `local/` and the offer. `main.mjs`: remove `migrateToLocal`, `localFile`, `save:local-offer`/`save:adopt-local`; save folder per "Paths" from `steam.user` (task 776''s value) and the SteamID; no valid user → no `saveFile`, `save:*` refused; `--import-save` without a valid user → stderr "needs a Steam user", exit non-zero; `preload.cjs`, `save.mjs` and `lib/desktop.ts` lose the offer API. If plan 99''s `task 763` is still open and its body says `local/`, `pm task set` it (target = the user''s folder, `dev/` or `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`). Check: Spacewar (480) logged in → `<steamid64>/game.json`; `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` without Steam → `dev/game.json`; neither → nothing written under `B` (stderr line).
2. Page: `MemoryStore`, store choice in `ready()` by `validUser`, `LocalProgress.svelte` and its strings removed (every catalog), notice strings added, flag action hidden without a valid user. Check on plan 99''s dev server (valid) and with the shim forced off (not valid): notice shown, no flag icon/key/menu entry, a game plays, nothing written; valid: saves and flags as before.
3. Docs: plan 18 Steam Cloud bullet (no `local/`, no migration, "no valid user → memory-only, flags hidden", dev folder) and the Steam Cloud test table: drop the `local/`/«Usar el progreso» and "no question" rows; add "Steam not running → full game, notice shown, no flag action, nothing written under `save/`"; listing row without `local/`. D-72 in `plans/decisions.md` (path per SteamID, `dev/`, no `local/`, memory-only), `12-client-engine.md` Store bullet ("one save per Steam user; memory-only without one"), `README.md` desktop save line, `directory.md` (`state/desktop/<steamid>|dev/`). Then `pm decision consequences` on decision 111 with what changed.
4. Close-out (task 664, after decision 75 "Steam Cloud test passed?", read against plan 18''s revised table): 18 Steam Cloud row `[x]` with a note, test table filled from the answer, `12-client-engine.md`, D-72, `plans/project.md`, `directory.md`, `README.md`; failures become tasks in this plan.

## Done when
- Under Steam each account has its own save under `save/<steamid64>/`, synced by Auto-Cloud between Windows and Linux/Deck.
- Without a valid user the game plays a full game memory-only with the notice, no flag action and nothing on disk; with the dev switch saves and flags work.', '', '2026-10-13T05:51:42Z', 433);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (88, 10, 'Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)', 300, 'Part 8 of masterplan 10: everything the gamemaster pastes into Steamworks'' store page admin for the `beta` milestone: texts per store language, AI disclosure, privacy line, system requirements, supported-languages table, controller flags, capsules (and the exe icon from the same script), screenshots and the trailer; plus the store page of each free DLC (one per shipped non-base bundle, decision 66). Workers draft and render; the gamemaster approves (pm decisions) and enters them. Owners: `plans/17-publishing.md` ("Steamworks and store", "AI disclosure", PUB-8), `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` (LUI-6).

## Inputs (write against them, don''t redo them)
- Store languages (decision 26: Launch languages (OQ-31); decision 27: Spanish variety): Spanish – Latin America (`es`, es-419), Spanish – Spain (`es-ES`), English (`en`), German (`de`). Later `schinese`, `russian`, `brazilian` (milestone 12, on hold): not in this plan.
- Names (D-50): «Living Room Trivia»; Spanish «Trivia en Familia»; German «Wohnzimmer-Quiz» (decision 78: German store name; needs PUB-7''s check, part 1).
- PUB-7 name check and PUB-10 Anthropic terms finding: masterplan 10 part 1 (`task 253: write plan: Partner account, name check and AI terms`). The AI disclosure text waits for PUB-10''s line in plan 17.
- System requirements: decision 90 (Store requirements, languages and controller flags?): provisional values for the beta (storage estimate, controller "Partial" until a pad-only run passes, en/de question content once their pools ship); final values measured on the release candidate (milestone 11). Install size from part 6''s media bundle and part 7''s depots.
- Controller support: plan 45 (gamepad, glyphs), plan 46 (letter picker), SW-8 (floating keyboard, plan 85). Deck compatibility is part 10''s (plan 90), not this plan''s.
- Steam features the store names (decision 111: Steam only: the integration is the reason to buy): Steam Cloud saves per Steam user (plan 87), achievements (plan 86), controller support (above); saves and flags need a Steam user.
- Free DLC (decision 66: bundles as free DLC, own store entries, optional install): decision 110 (Regional packs at launch): `colombia` ships, es + en, off by default. DLC apps themselves: part 2 (SW-7). Each DLC gets a store name, short and long description per its languages, its own capsules.
- Capsules: decision 77 (Store capsule art): typographic template in code, «Trivia» wordmark in the game''s fonts (Baloo 2, Nunito) and colours, rendered per size and language by a script; no image generation; disclosed as AI-assisted if Claude designs it. Decision 87 (Windows exe icon): the same script renders a 1024×1024 icon (`task 683` waits for it).
- Store media timing: decision 79 (Store screenshots: which set?) and decision 80 (en/de question pools): rendered late, after milestone 9''s UI wording fixes and translations, right before the store page goes to Valve''s review; nothing rendered or approved before that. en/de: the 2 question shots and the trailer wait for `pool.en.json` / `pool.de.json`; until then their pages carry the 5 menu shots.
- Dev switch: `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` (plan 85) makes the shell a valid user, so a scripted run loads its demo save and shows no "progress needs Steam" notice.
- AI review facts: D-7, D-10 (`claude -p`), D-32/D-33 (Claude reviews, `reviewer: "llm"`), D-56 (independent LLM audit + blind human spot check per batch), D-87 (translations via `qgen batch --translate`); LUI-5 native-speaker playtests (plan 15a).

## Rules
- Never phones home: the privacy line says the game collects nothing and sends nothing; player names stay on the device and in Steam Cloud (plan 87). Steam only (decision 111): no text about running without Steam; "saves need Steam" said plainly where saves come up. No claim the game can''t keep (no "full controller support" unless the whole game, name entry included, plays pad-only).
- Honest AI disclosure: pre-generated = LLM-drafted questions (Claude drafts, fact-checks with web search, reviews, translates; a person checks, edits and approves: gamemaster review, blind spot checks, native-speaker playtests) and LLM-written code; live-generated = none ("nothing is generated while you play"); no AI-generated art, images, sound or music (people''s work from Wikimedia Commons and other free sources, credited in CREDITS.md); store art typographic (decision 77). Check Valve''s current disclosure rules (pre-generated vs live-generated; whether code assistants count) at the task, cite the page. The gamemaster approves the wording.
- Drafts live in one file, `plans/17a-store-page.md` (sub-plan of 17, like 15a): per store language a block with every field and its Steam character limit; English first, then `es`, `es-ES` (only where it differs), `de`; then one block per free DLC (its languages only). Listed in `plans/README.md`.
- Every text set goes to the gamemaster as a pm decision ("Store texts approved? (<lang>)" or one decision for all); answers recorded, fixes applied before entry. Workers never log into Steamworks.
- Capsules, screenshots and the trailer are made by scripts under `authoring/store/` (authoring tool, not shipped; `authoring/` may import from `app/`), no new npm dependency (Node''s built-in `WebSocket` + raw CDP against the shell''s `--remote-debugging-port`, as `screenshots.mjs` does; or Electron''s `capturePage` behind a dev-only flag); output to the gitignored `authoring/store/out/`. Runs use a throw-away demo save (made-up player names, no family data) and `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`.

## Tasks
1. **Store texts (LUI-6, PUB-8 texts):** in `plans/17a-store-page.md`, per store language: store name, short description (≤ 300 chars), "About this game" long description, feature bullets (12 in a row, five modes per D-74, jokers by their localized names from the catalogs, offline, gamepad/keyboard, family/TV, Steam Cloud saves per Steam account, achievements), privacy line, controller line. Use the in-game wording (catalogs `app/client/src/locales/*.ts`). The German name per decision 78 needs PUB-7''s check: follow-up in part 1''s plan. Approval: pm decision per language set, native-speaker read where LUI-5''s testers are available. Mark LUI-6 `[x]` in 15a once approved.
2. **Free DLC texts:** per shipped pack (decision 110: `colombia`, es + en): store name, short description, "About this DLC" in its languages (free, needs the base game, optional install, off by default); approved with the language sets or in its own decision.
3. **AI disclosure text** (after PUB-10''s line is in plan 17): the Steam content-survey AI section ("pre-generated content" description, "live-generated": none) and the store-page wording per language in 17a, per the rule above (questions and code LLM-written and person-approved; no AI art, images, sound or music; capsules typographic, AI-assisted if Claude designed the template). Anything unclear in Valve''s rules → decision body for the gamemaster. Part 9 (PUB-9) enters it with the survey; this task only drafts and gets it approved.
4. **System requirements, supported languages, controller flags:** values in 17a (done by `task 668`); apply decision 90 and the media bundle''s installed size once part 6/7''s depots exist (`task 688`).
5. **Capsules, logo and icon** (decision 77, decision 87): Valve''s current graphical-asset list, checked on the task''s date and cited (2024 list for reference: header 920×430, small 462×174, main 1232×706, vertical 748×896, page background 1438×810, library capsule 600×900, library hero 3840×1240, library logo 1280×720 PNG, library header 920×430, community icon 184×184; recheck sizes and text-area rules), plus Valve''s DLC asset list. Script `authoring/store/capsules.mjs`: typographic template, per store language (`es` and `es-ES` share), per free DLC (its languages), and a 1024×1024 square icon for the exe/Linux/Steam client icon (decision 87, `task 683` uses it). Credit/disclose per decision 77. Capsules are typographic, not screenshots of the UI, so they may render before the store media; the gamemaster approves via pm decision.
6. **Scripted screenshots, rendered late** (decisions 79, 80): `authoring/store/screenshots.mjs` (exists from `task 670`) at 1920×1080 renders 7 per store language: 5 on modes and configuration (mode choice, configure screen, bundle selector, joker presets, Customize game; the worker orders them) and 2 gameplay (a question with a locked-in answer; a question with a joker in use, e.g. Francotirador aiming or Soplo''s hint). Under `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` (demo save loads, no notice). Run only after milestone 9''s UI wording fixes and translations, right before Valve''s review; en/de: 5 menu shots until their pools exist, then the 2 question shots. Gamemaster approves the set via pm decision. DLC store pages: screenshots optional (Valve).
7. **Trailer, rendered late** (replaces backlog B-21 in `plans/backlog.md`: mark it moved here): one command `trivia-trailer` (dev shell only, not shipped, no npm dependency): a scripted game in the real shell under Xvfb with game audio (PulseAudio/PipeWire null sink or equivalent), recorded with ffmpeg; 20 s per store language: questions answered, jokers used, a wrong answer and the loss at the end; demo save and `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`; output `authoring/store/out/trailer/<lang>.mp4` in Valve''s current trailer format (check and cite). Re-runnable after any UI change. Build the command early, render the final videos late (same timing as the screenshots; en/de after their pools); Xvfb and ffmpeg in the dev shell (flake). The gamemaster approves before upload (pm decision).
8. **Entry checklist and close-out:** a checklist in 17a (Steamworks → Store page admin field by field: names, descriptions per language, tags suggestion, each free DLC''s store page (name, descriptions, capsules; DLC app per part 2), languages, requirements, controller, assets, screenshots, trailer; AI disclosure goes with part 9''s survey) for the gamemaster; result via pm decision "Store page entered for the beta?". Then PUB-8 `[x]` in plan 17 with a note, LUI-6 in 15a, `plans/project.md` in sync.

## Done when
- 17a holds approved texts for es, es-ES, en, de, the AI disclosure, requirements, languages, controller flags, each free DLC''s texts; capsules (DLC ones too) and the icon rendered and approved; 7 screenshots per store language (5 for en/de until their pools) and the trailer rendered late and approved; the gamemaster reports the store page entered; PUB-8 and LUI-6 marked done.', '', '2026-10-13T06:05:26Z', 258);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (89, 10, 'Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)', 620, 'Part 7 of masterplan 10 (S5): the packaged desktop builds from plan 56 become Steam depots, uploaded by hand with SteamCMD to the password-protected `beta` branch. Two commands on the author''s Linux machine: `trivia-release-check` (local CI before every upload, SW-6, decision 14: CI builds (SW-6)) and `trivia-steam upload --branch beta` (clean tagged commit → release check → depot folders → generated VDFs → `run_app_build`). Nothing runs on GitHub; no secrets in git. Steam only (decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy): checks cover the game launched by Steam, not plain archives or the browser game. Owner `plans/18-steam-integration.md` ("Builds and depots", SW-6, SW-10).

## Depends on
- Plan 56 (SW-5): `trivia-desktop-build`, `electron-builder.yml`, `after-pack.mjs`, `stage-media.mjs` → `app/desktop/build/media/`; packaged layout `resources/{app.asar,client,data,media}`, media outside the asar for the content depot.
- Task 650 (plan 85): Steam binding + SDK libs in both builds. Task 2 runs without it; task 6 (first upload) needs it.
- Part 6 (task 260, media bundle, SW-9; not written yet, waits on decision 82): writes the shipped media where the content depot reads it (`app/desktop/build/media/`, same lookup keys, D-17) and owns a budget/missing-file check. Until it lands the content depot ships the staged media as is (~2.4 GB) and the release check''s media step is `stage-media.mjs`''s missing-file check; part 6 wires its own check into `trivia-release-check` (noted in task 260).
- Part 2 (task 254, SW-7): App ID, depot IDs, launch options per OS, `beta` branch. Tasks 1–5 use placeholders (`null`); task 6 waits for part 2''s "values entered" decision.
- Plan 57 / decision 15: Release quality bar: D-56''s numbers (≥ 90 % agreement, last two batches), read from `qgen report --qc`''s "Release bar" row.
- Version and tag: `app/desktop/package.json` `version` (= flake''s); masterplan 11 part 2 (task 265, versions) may move the source of truth; this plan only reads it and requires the tag `v<version>` on HEAD.
- Plan 85 task 776 (`TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER`, valid-user check) and plan 87 (save per Steam user, memory-only without one): the smoke game needs the dev switch to save and resume (task 10).
- Plan 99 task 765 removes `nix build .#app` and the release check''s `nix` step (D-59 superseded by decision 111); nothing here re-adds it.
- Packs (decision 112: Pack layout: a pool file per bundle): `app/data/bundles/<id>/`, `build/pack-media.json`; plan 98 (which packs launch, RG-5); part 6 splits media per depot. DLC App and depot IDs from part 2.
- A task whose dependency isn''t done stops and says so (except the placeholders above).

## Decisions taken here
- **SteamCMD from nixpkgs** (`steamcmd`, unfree, FHS wrapper; pinned by `flake.lock`) in the dev shell; `allowUnfreePredicate` gains it (plus whatever it pulls in, e.g. `steam-unwrapped`/`steam-run`, if nix asks). Fallback if it doesn''t run: the SDK''s `tools/ContentBuilder/builder_linux/steamcmd.sh` from the flake''s `steamSdk` fetchzip, through `steam-run`; say so in the D-entry. SteamCMD self-updates into its own home (`~/.local/share/Steam` or `~/Steam`), outside the repo.
- **Depots (3), one install folder:** `windows` (win-unpacked minus `resources/media/`), `linux` (linux-unpacked minus `resources/media/`), `content` (`resources/media/` = `app/desktop/build/media/`, shared by both OSes). Pool and client stay in the OS depots (small, change with every content update; media rarely). Both OS layouts put media at `<install>/resources/media`, so one content depot fits both. No language depots.
- **DLC depots (decision 66: bundles as free DLC):** one depot per shipped non-base bundle (its `app/data/bundles/<id>/` files + its media from part 6), listed in `steam.json` (`dlc: {<bundle id>: {appid, depot}}`, `null` until part 2) and the app VDF, uploaded with the base build; the OS depots exclude pack files, `content` excludes pack-only media. The game offers a pack when its files are installed (decision 112), no Steam call.
- **Unpacked folders for SteamCMD:** electron-builder''s `dir` target (`release/win-unpacked/`, `release/linux-unpacked/`) via a flag of `trivia-desktop-build` (e.g. `--dir`), so the zip/tar.gz stay for hand-copied local builds. The `after-pack.mjs` launcher (`trivia` → `trivia-bin --no-sandbox`) must be in `linux-unpacked` too.
- **Files in git (no secrets):** `authoring/steam/` (never ships, like `authoring/store/`): `steam.json` (`appid`, `depots: {windows, linux, content}`, all `null` until part 2), `app_build.vdf.in` + `depot_build.vdf.in` templates, `release_check.py` or `.mjs`, `steam.py`/`.mjs` (`trivia-steam`), `smoke.mjs`. Generated VDFs, SteamCMD''s `BuildOutput`, logs, the release-check report: `work/steam/<tag>/` (gitignored by `work/`). Account name via `TRIVIA_STEAM_ACCOUNT` env or a prompt; password and Steam Guard only typed into SteamCMD, cached in its own home. `steam_appid.txt` never in a depot (part 2 may say otherwise).
- **Branches:** the app VDF''s `SetLive` is `beta` only; `trivia-steam upload --branch default` (or `SetLive default`) is refused: `default` stays empty until S6 and is only ever set in the Steamworks web UI. Beta password: set by the gamemaster in Steamworks, never in a file.
- **Build description** (`Desc`): `<tag> <short sha>` plus `skipped: <steps>` if any release-check step was skipped.
- **Release check strictness:** every automated step fails the check; `--skip <step>` (repeatable) exists for a known-broken step and is printed in the report and the build description. Manual rows are asked interactively (y/n/note) or read from `--manual <file>`; a "no" fails.
- **Clean tagged commit:** `git status --porcelain` empty (gitignored media/work don''t count), HEAD carries `v<version>`; the command never creates or pushes tags (the gamemaster tags). `--preview` (Valve''s `Preview 1`: builds manifests, uploads nothing) and `--dry-run` (no SteamCMD at all) skip the tag gate.
- D-entry (next D number): the above.

## Release check (`trivia-release-check`, SW-6)
Steps in order, each ✓/✗ with time; report `work/steam/<tag-or-sha>/release-check.md` (commit, date, steps, skips, manual rows); exit 1 on any ✗:
1. Per-commit checks (AGENTS.md): `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`.
2. `trivia-media licenses` (exit 1 = files to replace).
3. Release quality bar (decision 15): `qgen report --qc` "Release bar" ✓ for the last two batches.
4. (was `nix build .#app`; removed by plan 99 task 765, decision 111.)
5. `trivia-desktop-build --dir` (both OSes, unpacked + archives) and the media check (stage-media''s, later part 6''s budget check).
6. Smoke game: `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` on `release/linux-unpacked/` under `unshare -rn`, `env -i` + FHS runtime (`steam-run`), `xvfb-run`, temp `HOME` (task 330''s recipe, now permanent), `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` (plan 85''s dev switch: saves on without a Steam session; network off = Steam offline mode, never phones home): new player → level 3 with an image, audio and video question, no missing-media notice, quit, restart → player resumes; no «progress needs Steam» notice; exit 1 with the failed step. With DLC depots: once with a pack''s files (pack offered) and once without (not offered, game plays). Under Steam (Spacewar 480 or the real App ID) optional; no start test without Steam and without the switch (decision 39). `TRIVIA_DEVTOOLS=1` + `--remote-debugging-port` as in plan 54; CDP helpers shared with `authoring/store/screenshots.mjs` where it''s cheap.
7. Manual checklist (decision 14): start test on a clean Windows machine from the Steam `beta` branch (decision 39: not from the archives), sound, the timed-competitive red frame; later rows from parts 10/11 append here.
   - Deck row: best effort (decision 125: Steam Deck: best effort, review without a Deck at hand): until the gamemaster has a Deck it reads "no Deck (decision 125)" and doesn''t fail; with one, plan 90''s real-Deck checklist from the `beta` branch.

## Tasks to split into
1. **SteamCMD, config and VDF templates** — `steamcmd` in the dev shell (`flake.nix`, unfree predicate), `steamcmd +quit` runs on NixOS (else the SDK fallback); `authoring/steam/steam.json`, `app_build.vdf.in` (AppID, Desc, `Preview`, `SetLive`, `ContentRoot`, `BuildOutput` → `work/steam/<tag>/output`, `Depots` → the three depot VDFs), `depot_build.vdf.in` (`DepotID`, `ContentRoot`, `FileMapping` `*` → `.` recursive, `FileExclusion` for `resources/media` in the OS depots, `*.pdb`/`steam_appid.txt`); `trivia-steam vdf --out <dir>` renders them with absolute paths. Check: render with placeholder IDs (`--appid 480 --depots 481,482,483`) into a temp dir; SteamCMD-parseable (a `+run_app_build -preview` without login fails only on login, or eyeball against Valve''s ContentBuilder examples). D-entry.
2. **Unpacked builds for the depots** — `trivia-desktop-build --dir` (electron-builder `dir` target alongside or instead of the archives; `after-pack.mjs` applies), `trivia-steam stage` checks `release/{win,linux}-unpacked/` and `app/desktop/build/media/` exist and match: union of OS depot + content depot = the archive''s file list (throw-away script compares with the tar.gz/zip). Content depot root stays `app/desktop/build/media/` whatever part 6 does.
3. **Packaged smoke game** — `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` (step 6 above), runnable alone (`node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs <unpacked dir>`); passes on today''s Linux build offline; fails (exit 1, message) with a media file renamed away.
4. **`trivia-release-check`** — steps 1–7, report, `--skip`, `--manual`, flake wrapper (`fromCheckout`-style, `authoring/` may call `app/`); runs green on a clean main (manual rows answered "skipped (worker)" in the worker''s run; note it). Plan 18 "Builds and depots": SW-6 text rewritten to the command; README how-to (when to run it); AGENTS.md "Commands" line; `directory.md` (`authoring/steam/`).
5. **`trivia-steam upload`** — `--branch beta` (only), `--preview`, `--dry-run`, `--checked` (reuse a passing report of the same commit instead of re-running the check); gates (clean tree, tag `v<version>`, `steam.json` IDs not null, report ✓), then release check → stage → VDFs → `steamcmd +login $TRIVIA_STEAM_ACCOUNT +run_app_build <abs app vdf> +quit`; prints the BuildID and SteamCMD''s log path. Check: `--dry-run` on a clean main writes `work/steam/<sha>/` with VDFs pointing at the staged folders; `--branch default` refused; an unclean tree refused. Docs: plan 18 "Builds and depots" (S5 bullets rewritten from "Later" to the commands, depots, branches, what''s gitignored), README "Upload to Steam", AGENTS.md "Commands", `directory.md`.
6. **First beta upload: checklist and decision** (needs part 2''s "values entered" decision with App ID + depot IDs, and task 650) — fill `steam.json`; write the checklist into plan 18 ("Builds and depots" → "First upload"): build account in Steamworks (Users & Permissions: own account, only "Edit App Metadata" + "Publish App Changes To Steam" for this app; Valve''s recommendation), `steamcmd +login <account>` once with Steam Guard, `beta` branch + password in Steamworks (App Admin → SteamPipe → Builds), tag `v<version>`, `trivia-steam upload --branch beta`, then check the build appears on `beta` and installs on the author''s machine via the beta password. `pm decision add "First beta upload done? BuildID?"` with the checklist and options "uploaded (BuildID …)", "failed (paste the error)"; `pm task-pending-decision` task 7.
7. **Record the first upload** (waits for task 6''s decision) — pass: plan 18 SW-10 `[x]` and SW-6 `[x]` with date, BuildID, files; `plans/project.md`; decision consequences. Failure: a fix task in this plan per error, a re-try decision, this task pending on it; stage and stop without closing.
8. **Windows exe icon and metadata (B-11)** — `Trivia.exe` has Electron''s icon and metadata. Icon per decision 87: Windows exe icon (B-11): the 1024×1024 icon from plan 88''s capsule script (task 669; waits for it). Tool per decision 88: Windows exe resources: electron-builder''s resedit, no wine, unsigned (`win.signExecutable: false`, not `signAndEditExecutable: false`); no new dependency. Check: exe resources show the icon and `ProductName`/`FileVersion` (throw-away script or `wrestool`); B-11 closed in `plans/backlog.md`. Signing: not required by Steam; note it.
9. **DLC depots for packs (decision 66)** (task 748; waits on plan 98''s packs as optional installs, decision 109) — per launching pack: `steam.json` `dlc` entry, depot VDF, exclusions in the OS and `content` depots; `trivia-steam stage`: union of all depots = the full build; smoke game with and without the pack. Check: `trivia-steam upload --dry-run` renders a DLC depot per launching pack with placeholder IDs; stage check passes. Docs: plan 18 "Builds and depots", D-entry.
10. **Smoke game under the dev switch** (needs plan 85 task 776 and plan 87''s save gate) — `smoke.mjs` passes `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` in its `env -i` list; asserts no «progress needs Steam» notice and that the restart resumes the player (save under the temp `HOME`, plan 87''s dev folder); `release_check.py`''s smoke row and plan 18 say so. Check: `node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs app/desktop/release/linux-unpacked` passes; without the switch it fails at the resume step (throw-away run, not a release-check row).

11. **Deck row best effort (decision 125)** — `release_check.py`''s `deck` manual row: until the gamemaster has a Deck, "no Deck (decision 125)" passes (not a ✗); with one, the row points at plan 90''s real-Deck checklist. Check: `trivia-release-check --manual <file>` with that answer doesn''t fail on the row. Docs: plan 18 "Builds and depots" / SW-6 row text.

## Done when
- `trivia-release-check` runs steps 1–7 and fails on any ✗; `trivia-steam upload --branch beta` uploads a clean tagged commit''s three depots plus one DLC depot per shipped pack; `default` can''t be set from the repo.
- The first beta build is on Steam (task 7''s decision), SW-6 and SW-10 `[x]` in plan 18.
- No secrets in git; SteamCMD output only under `work/` or SteamCMD''s home; `trivia-desktop-build` without `--dir` behaves as before; the smoke game runs under the dev switch, no checks of the game outside Steam (decision 111).', '', '2026-10-13T06:52:57Z', 261);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (90, 10, 'Steam Deck review and Deck test (SW-12)', 370, 'Part 10 of masterplan 10 (SW-12). Deck support is best effort (decision 125: Steam Deck: best effort, review without a Deck at hand): no real Deck yet, so Valve''s Deck compatibility review is requested without a prior real-Deck test, once the 1280×800 fit, the image peek, the Gamepad template as Steam Input default and a `beta` upload are in. Workers write the criteria table and the exact request steps; the gamemaster requests in Steamworks and reports Valve''s result through a pm decision. The real-Deck checklist is written down for later, not run here. Docs and pm only; no code: Valve''s notes become fix tasks.

## Binding
- decision 125: Steam Deck: best effort, review without a Deck at hand: no real-Deck test before the review; the real-Deck test and further tuning once a Deck is at hand, not a precondition of the review or of milestone 10. Replaces plan 18''s "Test on a real Deck before applying".
- decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy: only the Steam-launched build; no "without Steam" rows. The Deck runs logged in: valid Steam user is the normal case.
- decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): bundles are free DLC with optional install; decision 112: Pack layout: a pool file per bundle (optional install).
- decision 90: Store requirements, languages and controller flags?: controller "Partial" until the pad-only run passes; a Deck test on the release candidate (milestone 11). Don''t contradict it; the review result feeds it.

## Depends on (guard at the start of each task)
- First `beta` upload recorded: `task 682: Record the first beta upload` done (decision 89 answered).
- Image peek: plan 113 "Image peek on image questions" (milestone 8) done.
- Gamepad template as Steam Input default: SW-7''s checklist in `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (masterplan 10 part 2) lists it and the gamemaster confirmed the values entered (its pm decision answered). If part 2''s plan doesn''t exist yet: stop, say so.
- 1280×800 fit: plan 46, done.
- Store page (plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure) only if Valve needs it for the review (task 1 finds out).
- Guard: if a prerequisite waits on a pending decision, `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <that decision>`; if it''s just open, stop without changes and say so.

## Facts to rely on
- Deck runs the **Linux build** (`linux` + `content` depots, decision 84: SteamCMD source and depot split) via `./trivia`; no overlay on Linux (decision 70: Steam overlay in the Electron shell, D-92); Proton with the Windows build is the overlay route.
- Text ≥ 9 px at 1280×800 checked by script (SW-4); floating keyboard and glyphs are SW-8''s (plan 85, task 652).
- No DRM: starts with Steam offline.

## Valve''s criteria (re-read before task 1)
- Source: `partner.steamgames.com/doc/steamdeck/compat` (criteria), `…/steamdeck/reviews` or the app''s "Steam Deck Compatibility" section (process). Unreachable → the decision body asks the gamemaster to confirm list and timing.
- Expected categories (verify; Valve''s wording wins):
  - Input: full controller support with the default config; Deck/Xbox glyphs, no keyboard/mouse prompts; on-screen keyboard for text entry (player name); no keyboard/mouse needed.
  - Seamlessness: no compatibility warnings; no launcher.
  - Display: 1280×800 or 1280×720 default; legible text (≥ 9 px at 800p).
  - System support: runs under SteamOS (native or Proton); no unsupported anti-cheat.
- Review timing: does Valve review unreleased apps (before release, after coming-soon, only with a build on `default`, or a named branch with password)? `default` stays empty until S6 (decision 84); if Valve only tests `default` or released apps, the request moves to S6.

## Tasks
1. **Criteria table and the review request**
   - Guard (above). Read Valve''s docs. Replace the 2-line stub "Steam Deck Verified" in `plans/18-steam-integration.md`:
     - criteria table: Valve''s criterion → what the game does (plan, decision, or file) → evidence (script, SW-8 check, plan 46 layout, plan 113 peek, SW-7 Gamepad default)
     - "Review": Valve''s documented timing and how to request; best effort per decision 125, no real-Deck test first
     - "Real-Deck test (later)": the checklist for when a Deck is at hand, rows only, no results; builds on plan 48''s S3 Deck rows, no copy: install from `beta`, no warning, straight into the game fullscreen; default controls without touching Steam Input, every menu/joker/dialog/☰ reachable, Xbox glyphs; name via floating keyboard; full game with image (peek), audio, video questions; legible at arm''s length, credits scroll; suspend/resume mid-question and during a video; no "progress needs Steam" notice, flag action present; Exit → relaunch, save intact; free DLC install/uninstall (pack offered/gone, defaults, no error); airplane mode; Cloud Deck ↔ PC (refer to plan 87''s table); optional achievements toast, Proton row; battery note
   - `plans/backlog.md`: "SW-12 real-Deck test: once a Deck is at hand, run plan 18''s ''Real-Deck test (later)'' (decision 125)".
   - If Valve reviews with our setup before release: extra guard on the store page if Valve needs it (plan 88''s paste-in decision); then `did=$(pm decision add "Deck compatibility review requested? Result?" --body - …)` with the exact steps (Steamworks app → Steam Deck Compatibility → request; branch and password if asked; what to paste from the criteria table), options `Verified`, `Playable (Valve''s notes)`, `Unsupported (notes)`, `not yet reviewed`; `pm task-pending-decision` task 2 on it.
   - If only after release or coming soon: no decision; `plans/11-steam.md` ST-4 gains "request Deck review (SW-12), Valve''s timing: …"; masterplan 11 gets a dated note via `pm plan edit 11 --body -` only if it''s written and doesn''t list it; task 2 records the deferral.
   - Done when: section written; decision pending with task 2 waiting, or the S6 note in place.
2. **Record the review result and docs**
   - Valve''s result and date in plan 18 "Review". `Playable`/`Unsupported`: one `pm task add` per Valve note in the owning plan if it still has open tasks (85 binding, 87 Cloud, 89 builds/depots, 113 peek), else in this plan; a re-request decision; this task pending on it; stage and stop without closing. `not yet reviewed`: pending on a fresh copy of the decision.
   - A finding that settles something (e.g. "Deck via Proton needed") → D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` + `pm decision record`.
   - Docs: plan 18 SW-12 `[x]` (Valve''s result, or "review in S6" with reason; real-Deck test pending a Deck, decision 125); `plans/14-input.md` Steam Deck line; `plans/project.md` in sync.
   - Done when: the result (or S6 deferral) is recorded and SW-12 is ticked.

## Out of scope
- Running the real-Deck test and Deck tuning (once a Deck is at hand, decision 125); fixing Valve''s notes (fix tasks in the owning plans); Remote Play Together (SW-13); the family beta test (part 11).', '', '2026-10-13T08:19:26Z', 262);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (91, 11, 'Version numbers and patch-safe saves', 600, 'Part 2 of masterplan 11 (S6): every public build carries one semver version and a pool version, and a patch that adds, fixes or drops questions never breaks a save. Today the version `0.1.0` sits twice (`flake.nix`, `app/desktop/package.json`), the game shows neither, and a running game whose current card was dropped by a patch throws `KeyError` on the next answer (`game.ts` `question()`). Part 3 (release checklist, task 266) and part 5 (report text, task 267) build on this. Owners: `plans/18-steam-integration.md` ("Builds and depots", version bullet), `plans/12-client-engine.md` (save format, new "Saves across patches").

## What exists (checked 2026-10-13)
- Upload gate (plan 89, D-93): `trivia-steam upload` requires tag `v<version>` on HEAD, `version` from `app/desktop/package.json` (`steam.py` `version()`), never creates tags; build Desc `<tag> <sha>`. Nothing to add there.
- electron-builder stamps `package.json` `version` into artifact names and the exe''s `FileVersion` (task 683).
- Save: `SAVE_VERSION = 4`, `parseSave` upgrades step by step (`UPGRADES`), a newer save goes to a backup (`store.ts`, notice "newer"). Unknown question ids in `seen`, `blocked`, `flags`, `history` are kept, not errors; `view()` and `askedCategories` already skip ids missing from the pool.
- Seen counts (plan 65) are rows per id, never pruned: a dropped question that comes back keeps its count, so it is not "new". Ids: `qgen draft` allocates `max(id) + 1` over `authoring/data/questions.json`; rejected questions stay in the file, so ids aren''t reused as long as nobody deletes entries.
- Gaps: (1) version not shown or available to the client; (2) no pool version; (3) a running game referencing a dropped id (`current`, `options`, `last`, `undo`, `swapped_to`) breaks actions; (4) nothing stops an id from vanishing from `questions.json` (and being reused).

## Decisions
- decision 91: Game version: single source of truth → `app/desktop/package.json` `version`; `flake.nix` reads it (`builtins.fromJSON`), the client build gets it via Vite `define`; tag `v<version>` per release.
- decision 92: Pool version: export hash in pool.json → `qgen export` writes `"hash"` (8 hex, sha256 of the exported questions); pool format stays `version: 1`.
- No save version bump in this plan: the repair below doesn''t change the shape. Rule for later patches (into `12-client-engine.md`): a shape change = `SAVE_VERSION + 1` + an `UPGRADES` entry + a `save.test.ts` case; never a silent change.
- Beta vs. default: a newer save on an older build is backed up and the game starts empty (`store.ts`); so a save version bump ships to `default` in the same release the family tested on `beta`, and testers don''t switch back to `default` before it (a line in part 3''s checklist, task 266).
- Semver meaning: patch `x.y.Z` = content-only or bug fix; minor = new feature or save version bump; `1.0.0` = launch.

## Tasks to split into
1. **One version, shown in the game** — `flake.nix` app `version` from `app/desktop/package.json`; `app/client/vite.config.ts` `define: { __APP_VERSION__ }` read from `../desktop/package.json` (typed `declare const`); `qgen export` (`authoring/tools/pool_export.py` `pool_text`) writes `"hash"` per decision 92, `app/data/pool.json` re-exported; `engine/pool.ts` keeps it (optional, absent in old pools = `null`); a small `buildInfo()` in `app/client/src/lib/` → `{ version, pool }` for the credits screen now and part 5''s report text later. Credits screen (`Credits.svelte`) shows "Versión 1.0.0 · preguntas 3fa2c1d0" (strings via `t()`, es/en/de catalogs + es-ES if it overrides). Check: `npm run build`, `nix build .#app`, credits screen shows both in the browser game; bumping the version in `package.json` changes all three (flake, client, `steam.py`). Docs: plan 18 "Builds and depots" gains a **Version** bullet (source, tag, Desc, how to bump: edit `package.json`, commit, `git tag v<version>`; semver meaning above); `README.md` one line under the Steam upload how-to.
2. **Running games survive a patch** — on load (`engine/game.ts`, wherever a running game is first read for a pool, e.g. `view`/`running`, or a `repair(save, data)` pass in `api.ts`''s load), the newest running game drops ids its pool lacks: phase `select` → missing `options` redrawn for the level (no seen row); phase `question` with a missing `current` → back to `select` for the same level (no seen row, jokers and history unchanged); `last`/`swapped_to` with missing ids → `null`; `undo` referencing missing ids → `null`. Finished games and `seen`/`blocked`/`flags` untouched. Also per locale (a translation dropped from one locale''s pool). Verify with a throw-away script (not committed; tests only if one stays useful, AGENTS.md): build a v4 save against today''s pool (players, finished games, a running game in `select` and one in `question`, flags, blocked, seen), drop 10 % of its ids incl. the running game''s cards, re-add one dropped id; load against the new pool → no throw, game playable to the next level, re-added id''s seen count kept, dropped ids never drawn, flags list shows the dropped id with `question: null`. Also a v2 save (`save.py` `migrate()` output) against the new pool. Docs: `plans/12-client-engine.md` new section "Saves across patches" (what a patch may do, what the engine guarantees, the shape-change rule and the beta/default note above).
3. **Ids never vanish** — `qgen validate` fails when an id in the newest `v*` tag''s `app/data/pool.json` (`git show <tag>:app/data/pool.json`; no tag → skip, say so) is missing from `authoring/data/questions.json` (any status): dropping = status change, never deletion, so `max(id) + 1` never reuses an id. Check: delete a tagged id in a temp copy → validate fails with the id; on today''s tree (no tag yet) it says "skipped". Docs: `authoring/RUNBOOK.md` or `QC.md` one bullet; plan 18 "Version" bullet mentions it.
4. **Close-out** — `plans/18-steam-integration.md` and `plans/12-client-engine.md` as above; `plans/11-steam.md` notes S6 part 2 done (no ST-row of its own; cite this plan); `plans/project.md` in sync; decision 91/92 consequences.

## Done when
- One edit of `app/desktop/package.json` `version` changes the flake app, the client''s shown version, the artifacts and the upload gate; the credits screen shows version + pool hash.
- A save from before a patch loads against a pool with dropped, fixed and added questions without errors; a running game continues; dropped ids never come back as new; `qgen validate` guards id continuity against the last release tag.
- D-59: `trivia` (browser) and `nix build .#app` work as before.', '', '2026-10-13T08:25:30Z', 265);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (92, 11, 'Release checklist (ST-4)', 700, 'Part 3 of masterplan 11 (S6, ST-4): every public build, the launch and every later patch, passes one release checklist: the automated `trivia-release-check` (plan 89, SW-6; extended here, no new tool) plus manual rows the gamemaster runs on the `beta` branch, recorded through one pm decision per release candidate. Today the check runs the per-commit checks, licences, release bar, `nix build .#app`, both desktop builds and a packaged smoke game, and asks four manual rows; it doesn''t gate the tag, checks credits only one way inside the Vite build, and has no offline, Cloud or family rows and no patch variant. Owner: `plans/11-steam.md` (ST-4); `plans/18-steam-integration.md` ("Builds and depots", SW-6) for the command.

## What exists (checked 2026-10-13)
- `authoring/steam/release_check.py` (`task 679: trivia-release-check (SW-6)`): steps `checks` (`npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`; validate already fails on a stale `app/data/pool.json` and on vanished ids after a `v*` tag, `task 692`), `licenses`, `quality` (decision 15), `nix`, `desktop` (`trivia-desktop-build --dir` + `trivia-steam stage`), `smoke` (`smoke.mjs` offline under `unshare -rn`, to level 3), `manual` (dict `MANUAL`: windows, deck, sound, red-frame; `--manual FILE`); `--skip STEP`; report `work/steam/<tag>/release-check.{md,json}`.
- `trivia-steam upload` (`task 680`): gates clean tree + tag `v<version>` (version from `app/desktop/package.json`, decision 91), calls the check, Desc `<tag> <sha> skipped: …`; `--preview`/`--dry-run` skip the tag gate.
- Credits (plan 47, `app/client/credits.ts`): the build fails on a pool media slot without licence/source and on an `.m4a` without a row; libraries list Svelte, Electron, Chromium. Not listed: `steamworks-ffi-node` (`app/desktop/package.json` dependency) and the Steamworks SDK redistributables (`resources/steamworks_sdk/`, decision 69). Nothing checks the other direction (credits entry without a shipped file) or what actually lands in the packaged build.
- Version + pool hash (plan 91, decisions 91, 92): `package.json` version, `"hash"` in `pool.json`, both on the credits screen.

## Depends on
- Masterplan 10 part 6 (task 260, media bundle, waiting on decision 82): owns the media budget check and wires it into the `desktop` step. Until then the report carries a skipped row "media budget" (task 1), so it shows in the build Desc.
- Plan 90 (Deck, SW-12): the `deck` row points at its checklist in plan 18; if plan 90 moved "request Deck review" to ST-4 (only-after-release case), that becomes a launch-only row.
- Plan 87 (Cloud): the `cloud` row is a short A→B run of its "Steam Cloud test" table, not a copy.
- Part 4 (launch, task 269) and part 6 (patches, task 270) create the per-candidate decision from the template here; this plan creates none.

## Decisions taken here
- All automated steps stay hard failures; `--skip` stays the only escape and shows in the report and Desc (plan 89).
- New step `tag` (first): clean tree and HEAD tagged `v<version>`; the check never creates tags. `trivia-steam upload --preview/--dry-run` pass `--skip tag`; a worker''s trial run uses `--skip tag`.
- **Patch variant, automatic, with the reason:** "content-only" = since the newest earlier `v*` tag, `git diff --name-only` touches nothing that ships except `app/data/` (shipped = `app/`, `flake.nix`, `flake.lock`, root `package*.json`). Such a patch changes no code, so platform behaviour (Windows/Deck start, Cloud, sound, red frame) can''t change; what it can break (questions, media, licences, credits, pool loading) stays covered by every automated step plus the `offline` and `signoff` rows. Full-release-only rows are then answered "skipped: content-only since <tag>" automatically. No earlier tag = full release.
- Save version note (plan 91): if `SAVE_VERSION` (`app/client/src/engine/save.ts` or wherever it lives) differs from the previous tag''s, the manual list gains the `beta-save` row: testers stay on `beta` until this build is on `default`.
- Result per release candidate: one pm decision "Release candidate v<x> passed?" (template in `plans/11-steam.md`), options `passed`, `passed with minor issues (list)`, `failed (rows)`; failures become tasks in the owning plan, minor issues `plans/backlog.md`.

## Tasks to split into
1. **Tag gate, patch detection and report header** — `release_check.py`: step `tag` (clean tree, HEAD tag = `v` + `package.json` version, else ✗ with what to do: commit, `git tag v<version>`); previous tag = newest `v*` tag reachable from HEAD other than HEAD''s; kind = `full` / `content-only patch since <tag>` (rule above); `SAVE_VERSION` change vs previous tag; skipped row "media budget" (note "masterplan 10 part 6, task 260") until part 6''s check exists; report header: version, pool hash (`app/data/pool.json` `hash`), previous tag, kind, save version change. `steam.py`: `--preview`/`--dry-run` add `--skip tag`. Check: on today''s main `--skip` of the slow steps (`--skip checks --skip nix --skip desktop --skip smoke --skip quality --skip licenses --skip manual`) shows `tag` ✗ (untagged) and kind `full`; in a throw-away clone with a local tag `v0.0.1`, a commit touching only `app/data/pool.json` → content-only, one touching `app/client/` → full. Docs: plan 18 "Builds and depots" SW-6 step list; AGENTS.md "Commands" `trivia-release-check` line (`tag`, patch variant).
2. **Credits complete both ways** — new step `credits` after `desktop`: `authoring/steam/credits_check.mjs <unpacked dir>` (Node, no new dependency; read `app.asar` with the `@electron/asar` electron-builder already installs, or `asar list` from it) compares the packaged Linux build (Windows unpacked too where cheap) with its own `resources/client/credits.json` (packaged path as built): every file in `resources/media/` ↔ exactly one media entry (`cacheName(file_url)` from `app/desktop/resolve.mjs`), and no media entry without a file; every sound file in the client''s `audio/` ↔ a sound row; every font file ↔ a font entry and its OFL text present; every runtime package in the asar''s `node_modules` and every file group in `resources/steamworks_sdk/` ↔ a library entry; `CREDITS.md` present in the build. Lists what''s missing/extra, exit 1. Expected gaps today: `steamworks-ffi-node` and the Steamworks API redistributable: add them to `app/client/credits.ts` libraries (licence text from the package; Steamworks SDK: Valve''s SDK licence, name and link) so the check passes. Check: passes on today''s `--dir` build; renaming a media file away or adding a stray file under `resources/media/` fails with its name. Docs: plan 17 "Credits in the game" (PUB-5) one bullet; plan 18 SW-6 list; `directory.md`.
3. **Manual rows, decision template and ST-4 checklist** — `MANUAL` rows (each flagged full-only or always): `offline` (always; beta install, network off, Steam not running: full game to level 12 or a won checkpoint; content-only patch: a game to level 3 that hits new questions), `windows` (full), `deck` (full; plan 90''s rows in plan 18), `cloud` (full; plan 87: play on A, quit, B shows players and seen counts), `sound` (full), `red-frame` (full), `beta-save` (only when the save version changed), `signoff` (always; launch and full releases: the family plays the candidate from `beta`; content-only patch: the gamemaster''s OK). Full-only rows auto-answered on a content-only patch (task 1''s kind). `plans/11-steam.md` new section "Release checklist (ST-4)": intro, how to run (`git tag v<x>`, `trivia-steam upload --branch beta`, then the manual rows via `--manual FILE` from the gamemaster''s answers or the prompt), the rows with exact steps, the patch variant and its reason, the decision template (subject, body: tag, BuildID, report path, rows table to fill; options above) and what a worker does with each answer. ST-4 `[x]` with date and note "first full run: part 4''s release candidate (task 269)"; `plans/project.md` in sync; README "Upload to Steam" one line (release checklist section). Check: `--manual` file with every row answered parses; a content-only run lists the auto-skipped rows with the reason.

## Done when
- `trivia-release-check` fails on an untagged or dirty tree, on any credits mismatch either way, and on any automated step; the report names version, pool hash, kind and every skip.
- `plans/11-steam.md` ST-4 holds the manual checklist, the content-only variant with its reason and the per-candidate decision template; parts 4 and 6 can use it unchanged.
- D-59: `trivia`, `nix build .#app` and `trivia-desktop-build` without `--dir` unchanged.', '', '2026-10-13T08:37:48Z', 266);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (93, 11, 'Question reports: send, copy fallback and qgen flag (ST-5)', 550, 'Part 5 of masterplan 11 (S6, ST-5, the reports half): a player who flags a question sends it to us on a click. Decision 93: Question reports: where do players send them? → our own endpoint (plan 103: Report server, `POST /reports`), authenticated by a Steam Web API ticket (decision 111: Steam only). The game already keeps flags with note, question language and the shown text (decision 60, decision 102) and lists them in «Preguntas marcadas» with «Copiar». This plan adds the send (shell + client), keeps copy as the fallback, and adds the authoring side: `qgen flag` for pasted text and `qgen flag --pull` for the server''s reports, both ending as `needs_work` reviews. Owners: `plans/11-steam.md` (ST-5, reports half; cadence is plan 96), in-game `plans/13-game-modes.md` (MD-6). The earlier Steam-thread/email channel is dropped.

## What exists (checked 2026-10-13; build on it, don''t rebuild)
- Flags: save v4 `flags: {qid: {flagged_on, player, level?, note?, locale?, shown?}}` (`engine/state.ts` `FlagEntry`, `engine/save.ts` `setFlag`); `locale` and `shown` added without a version bump (decision 102: Game flags from a translated game: whose review do they change?, task 736). So the question language and the text the player saw are already there; no save shape work left for the language.
- `game/FlagDialog.svelte` (flag icon / `M` / pad Select, optional note), `game/FlagList.svelte` «Preguntas marcadas»: newest first, «Copiar» all as plain text, selectable `<pre>` fallback; no per-flag copy, no version/pool header.
- Version: `lib/build.ts` `buildInfo()` → `{version, pool}` (decision 91: Game version: single source of truth, `app/desktop/package.json` `version`; decision 92: Pool version: export hash in pool.json). `pool` is the pool of the last engine call; a flag in another locale takes `loadEngineData(locale).poolHash` or `null` (task 722''s note).
- Shell (`app/desktop/main.mjs`): `session.defaultSession.webRequest.onBeforeRequest` cancels every http(s)/ws request of the page; IPC via `handle("steam:…")`; steamworks-ffi-node has `steam.user.getAuthTicketForWebApi(identity)` (checked in `app/desktop/node_modules`).
- Valid Steam user gate: plan 87 task 780 hides the flag action without a valid Steam user (decision 111); `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` is the dev switch.
- Server: plan 103 API v1 (`POST /reports`, `GET /reports`, `POST /reports/ack`, `GET /health`, error codes, ticket identity `trivia-reports`, dev mode `trivia-report-server dev` on `127.0.0.1:8787` with `dev-*` tickets). Contract changes only by editing plan 103.
- Local family path: `trivia-authoring` `apply_flags()` (`authoring/server/main.py`) turns `state/game.json` flags into `needs_work` (locale-aware since task 736); ledger `state/flags-applied.json`. Stays as is until plan 99 moves the family save.
- Browser game and Python game server are retired by plan 99; UI checks run on plan 99''s Node dev server (task 762), the send path on `trivia-desktop`.

## Rules
- One network request, on a click (masterplan 11): the game sends only when the player confirms a send. No fetch at start, no health check, no retry, no prefetch.
- The send goes out from the shell''s main process, not the page: the page''s request block stays as it is. Main posts only to the configured report URL with Node''s `fetch` (5 s connect + 10 s total timeout); the page passes fields, never a URL.
- Report URL: one value, `reportUrl` in `app/desktop/package.json` next to `version` (the place plan 103 and plan 104 wait for). Empty = no send button, copy only. Dev override `TRIVIA_REPORT_URL`, honoured only with `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`; then the ticket is `dev-<random>` (plan 103''s fake check).
- Ticket: fresh per send, `getAuthTicketForWebApi("trivia-reports")`, cancelled after the response; never logged, never handed to the page.
- Reports don''t change game state; the only save change is an optional `reported_on` (date of the last successful send) on the flag entry, additive like decision 102 (no version bump; `save.test.ts` case for an entry with it).
- Copy fallback always there (per flag and all), also when sending works.
- Authoring: no new storage beyond `authoring/data/questions.json`, the locale translation files and a small pulled-ids ledger `state/reports-pulled.json`. Pull token from `TRIVIA_REPORT_TOKEN` or the gitignored file `state/report-token`, never git.
- Strings via `t()` in es, en, de (+ es-ES where it differs); `check:literals` passes.

## Decisions taken here
- Report text (copy fallback, parsed by `qgen flag`; `pm decision record` in task 2 with the final shape): one block per flag, first line machine-readable, the rest for humans in the UI language:
  `¡Trivia! #q-0001 · es · v1.0.0 · pool 3fa2c1d0 · 2026-11-02`
  `Pregunta: …` / `Respuesta: …` (from `shown`; the answer as today) / `Nota: …`. Header tokens fixed and untranslated: id, question language, version, pool hash (`?` if unknown), flag date.
- Sent fields (plan 103 contract): `question`, `lang` (flag `locale` ?? `es`), `text` = the human lines of that block without header and note, `note`, `version`, `pool` (or `null`), `ticket`.
- Send UI: «Enviar» per flag and «Enviar todas» (unsent ones, one request each, stops at the first failure); a confirm step with plan 103''s 1–2 line privacy text before the first send of a session. States per flag: sending, «Enviada <date>» (from `reported_on`; sending again stays possible), failed with the reason in words (no connection, try tomorrow on 429, closed on 503, otherwise «no se pudo enviar») and the copy buttons next to it. Failed state lives in memory only.
- Intake stays a `qgen` command (paste and pull), not a review-tool form; the review tool shows the resulting `needs_work` feedback.
- Mod question ids (milestone 15) aren''t in our pool: `--pull` skips them with a count and acknowledges them.

## Tasks to split into
1. **Channel decision** — done: decision 93 (own endpoint), task 698.
2. **Shell: ticket and send** (task 699 reworked; after plan 103''s API contract, which exists) — `app/desktop/package.json` `reportUrl` (empty until plan 103 task 4''s URL); `main.mjs`: IPC `report:available` (URL non-empty and valid Steam user or dev switch) and `report:send(fields)` → validates fields per plan 103''s limits, gets the ticket, POSTs, returns `{ok, id}` or `{ok: false, status, error, retryAfter?}`; dev override per Rules; `preload.cjs` + `lib/desktop.ts` types. `pm decision record` nothing here; note the URL place in `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (SW-8 bridge list). Check against `trivia-report-server dev` (plan 103 task 1; if it isn''t there yet, a throw-away Node stub of the contract): 201, 400, 429, server down (fails fast within the timeout); no request at start (main log).
3. **Client: report text, copy per flag, send** (after task 2) — `FlagList.svelte` per "Decisions taken here": header line, «Copiar» per flag (Enter on a focused row or a small button) and «Copiar todo», «Enviar» / «Enviar todas» only when `report:available`, confirm with the privacy text (from plan 103 task 3; if not there yet: `PLACEHOLDER(<task id>)`), states per flag, `reported_on` via a `setFlag`-like helper in `engine/save.ts`. Keyboard, mouse, pad as the list has today. `pm decision record` the text format (header tokens, order, separators) for tasks 4–5. Check: dev server (plan 99 task 762): flag two questions (one with note, one in en), copy one and all, header correct; `trivia-desktop` with `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` + `TRIVIA_REPORT_URL` at `trivia-report-server dev`: send one → «Enviada», send all, server stopped → failed + copy works; devtools network silent. Per-commit checks.
4. **`qgen flag`: pasted reports become needs_work** (task 700, unchanged in substance) — stdin, one or many blocks, chat text around them ignored; header parse; per report a human `needs_work` review «Reporte de jugador (v1.0.0, preguntas 3fa2c1d0, 2026-11-02[, locale]): <note> · Vista: «…»», older feedback kept after «Antes:»; es → source, en/de → that locale''s translation the way `apply_flags` does since task 736 (share that code, move it to `authoring/tools/` if needed); unknown id → warning, skipped; the same report twice adds nothing; `--dry-run`. Check: task 3''s copy text pasted → `needs_work` in `/review`. Docs: `qgen.py` usage line, `authoring/QC.md` one bullet.
5. **`qgen flag --pull`** (new; after task 4 and plan 103 task 1) — URL from `--url`, else `reportUrl` in `app/desktop/package.json`; token per Rules (missing → clear error naming both places); `GET /reports?limit=500` until `more` is false, each report → the same review code as task 4 (fields from JSON, no text parsing), ids written to `state/reports-pulled.json` before `POST /reports/ack` (a crash between write and ack doesn''t double the feedback; ids acked on the next run); unknown/mod ids skipped with a count and acked; `--dry-run` pulls without writing or acking. Summary line: pulled, applied, skipped. Check against `trivia-report-server dev` with reports from task 3''s check: applied, second pull empty; `qgen validate`.
6. **Close-out** (task 701 reworked; thread text dropped) — `plans/11-steam.md` ST-5 reports half `[x]` with a note (send, fallback, paste, pull; URL place); `plans/13-game-modes.md` MD-6; `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` flag list section; `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (ticket identity, `report:*` IPC); `README.md` how-to "pull player reports" (`qgen flag --pull`, token setup) and "a player pasted a report" (`qgen flag`); AGENTS.md `qgen` line if it lists commands; `directory.md`; `plans/project.md`; `pm decision consequences 93 "…"`.

## Done when
- From `trivia-desktop` with a valid Steam user (or the dev switch), «Enviar» on a flag sends one request to the report URL with id, language, shown text, note, version, pool hash and a ticket; nothing else goes out; failure leaves the copy fallback.
- `qgen flag --pull` turns those reports into `needs_work` reviews and acknowledges them; pasted copy text does the same via `qgen flag`; `qgen rework` picks them up.
- The local family path (`apply_flags`) works as before.', '', '2026-10-13T08:59:50Z', 267);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (94, 11, 'Coming soon page (ST-3)', 450, 'Part 1 of masterplan 11 (ST-3): the Steam store page goes public as "Coming soon", so it collects wishlists and follows before the release. Almost everything here is the gamemaster''s in Steamworks; workers write the checklist with Valve''s current rules (cited), raise one pm decision for the result and record it. The live date sets the earliest release date for part 4 (`task 269: write plan: Launch`).

## Inputs (don''t redo them)
- Store page: plan 88 (`Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)`), drafts and entry checklist in `plans/17a-store-page.md`; its `task 672: Store page entry checklist and PUB-8 close-out` gets "Store page entered for the beta?" answered.
- App ID, names, partner account: masterplan 10 part 1 (`task 253: write plan: Partner account, name check and AI terms`, PUB-6/7/10) and part 2 (`task 254: write plan: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)`); names per D-50 («Living Room Trivia», «Trivia en Familia»), set before the page goes public (`plans/17-publishing.md` "Steamworks and store").
- Content survey and price: masterplan 10 part 9 (`task 259: write plan: Content survey, rating and price (PUB-9, PUB-11)`); OQ-33 (plan 39).
- None of these plans may be done when this plan''s tasks run: the gamemaster''s decision gates the result, not task order.

## Rules
- Gamemaster does every Steamworks step (submit for review, fix, publish "Coming soon", set the date); workers never log in, enter credentials or contact Valve.
- Wishlists: only Steam''s own wishlist and follow buttons. No mailing list, own website, social accounts or marketing (milestone 11 out of scope).
- Release date on the page: "to be announced" (or a coarse "Q<n> <year>" if Steam offers it) until part 4 fixes the date; recommended, because the date depends on the content target (milestone 9) and the beta test (milestone 10).
- Timing: Valve''s minimum between "Coming soon" live and release (two weeks per the masterplan and `17-publishing.md`; verify); aim for months. Part 4''s release date counts from the live date.

## Tasks
1. **ST-3 checklist and decision**
   - Check the current Steamworks docs (e.g. partner.steamgames.com/doc/store/coming_soon, /doc/store/review_process, /doc/store/releasing): minimum "Coming soon" time before release; store page review lead time (business days); prerequisites for "Coming soon" (app credit paid, store page and content survey complete, capsules, names, ratings); release-date formats allowed (exact, month, quarter, year, "to be announced") and how often they may change. Cite each page with the date read in a new section "Coming soon page (ST-3)" in `plans/11-steam.md` (bullets). If the docs can''t be read from the worker''s environment, mark each rule "unverified (gamemaster: check <URL>)" instead of guessing.
   - Same section: gamemaster checklist, in order: prerequisites done (store page entered, `task 672`''s decision; names; survey; app credit) → Steamworks "Mark as ready for review" for the store page → wait for Valve''s review → fix what Valve returns (each fix: which file in `17a-store-page.md`, which plan owns it) → publish "Coming soon" with "to be announced" → note the live date.
   - `plans/17-publishing.md` "Coming soon page" bullet: point to the new section, add the cited source.
