- Milestone 11''s "Done when" holds: released; the first content patch went out as a patch; a report from the released build under Steam arrived via `qgen flag --pull` as needs_work, and the copy fallback worked with the server unreachable (the three decisions cited).', 'Once the game is out on Steam and its first content update has shipped, the project''s notes and how-to guides need to catch up with what actually happened. This step ticks off what was finished, parks what is left for later in one list of future ideas, and writes down the commands for cutting a release, sending an update and reading player reports. It also confirms that the release really works end to end, including a player''s question report reaching the developer.', '2026-10-13T09:20:44Z', 271);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (98, 9, 'Regional packs (RG-3..RG-5)', 300, 'Part 10 of the masterplan (plan 9): the regional bundles (packs) of the Steam release. Decision 110 answered RG-5 with OQ-46 folded in: every regional bundle 2000 approved, in its region''s language + en, free optional DLC, off by default, with its own bundle-scoped taxonomy; `colombia` is the pilot. Tasks 1–8 built what the pilot''s runs (plan 84) need and are done. The milestone (developer, 2026-10-15) adds five more bundles by Steam audience, `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`, which start once `colombia`''s chain is proven, not after its 2000: this plan now also builds what they need (drafting in a region''s own language and variety, en translation from `de` and `es-ES`) and sets each one up (bundle, taxonomy, target, DLC follow-ups). The milestone''s slug keys (developer, 2026-10-16; masterplan part 16, its plan written by `task 1305: write plan: Slug keys for categories`) come first: every category and subcategory keyed by an English slug, display names only from `names.<locale>.json`; the new taxonomies and task 10''s taxonomy and prompt redraft build on them. Owners: `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` (superseded by bundles, D-39), `plans/22-bundles.md`.

## Builds on
- decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46), partly superseding decision 37''s "packs have no target":
  - every regional bundle 2000 approved, region''s language + en (`colombia`: es + en); free DLC (decision 66: Price model (OQ-33)); off on the configure screen (decision 33 / D-88); the family''s save keeps base + `colombia` (D-85, D-59)
  - bundle-scoped taxonomy (D-99, D-100; `decision 165: Subcategory keys in code: bundle + name; base keeps bare names`); the name-as-key part replaced by part 16''s English slugs (bundle + slug, base bare)
  - pilot `colombia` 102 → 2000, effort measured; launch doesn''t wait (ships what `colombia` has; plan 96 updates bring the rest)
  - its "more bundles only after a new decision with the pilot''s numbers" is replaced by the milestone (developer, 2026-10-15): `usa` (en, ≈20 % of Steam download bandwidth, GameDiscoverCo 2024), `germany` (de + en, ≈4.4 %), `uk` (en, ≈3.3 %), `spain` (es-ES + en), `mexico` (es + en), in that order; later candidates `canada`, `australia`, `argentina` (no work now). Same rules as `colombia`; en regions en only. Also replaces decision 226''s "No Spain bundle (would need its own decision)".
- decision 112: Pack layout: `app/data/bundles/<id>/pool[.<locale>].json`, missing file = pack not offered.
- `decision 213: General category list for regional bundles` (`authoring/data/regional-categories.json`, 14 categories); `plan 138: Regional taxonomy: a general list, colombia reworked`: `qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>` proposes and `--apply`s a region''s taxonomy; `decision 249: colombia taxonomy: categories and subcategories`; `task 1140: Remap colombia''s existing questions onto its new taxonomy` open.
- `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`; `plan 148: English-first drafting for base` (done): `translations.draft_locale(bundle)` = a regional bundle''s first `languages` entry; `prompt(locale=)` per question; `--translate <L> [--bundle]` from any source locale ≠ L; question locales `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`.
- `decision 167: Translation prompt for a regional bundle (en for colombia)` (`translate-region.md`); prompts are the developer''s (decision 35: Translation prompts and markets per locale; RUNBOOK): drafted, shown in a pm decision, applied after the answer.
- Part 16, slug keys (milestone, developer 2026-10-16; plan from `task 1305: write plan: Slug keys for categories`): slugs are the keys everywhere (questions'' `subcategory`, `targets.json`, concept files, engine, reports); `categories.json` structure only, every name (en included) from `names.<locale>.json` (`es-ES` reads `names.es.json`, `names.es-ES.json` only where Spain differs); `qgen taxonomy` proposes slugs with en names and drafts `es`/`de` names on `--apply`; `regional-categories.json` follows. That plan makes task 10 and tasks 11–15 pending on its slug decision.
- `decision 250: Regional drafting in en, de, es-ES: prompts apply?` → don''t apply; redraft after slug keys: taxonomy prompts and `regional-categories.json` propose slugs + en names (part 16''s change); the locale-prompt parts (`locale-en.md`, `locale-es.md`, `locale-es-ES.md`, `locale-de.md`, `translate-region.md`) come back mostly unchanged. Its "names stay Spanish keys in every bundle" is void.
- Gaps today (for task 10):
  - `qgen bundle new` writes `languages: ["es"]`; `--name`/`--description` "Spanish", `--voice` "its Spanish usage"; `bundles.json` `about` calls `voice` Spanish usage
  - `bundle_text()` gives the voice only to Spanish drafts; `voices_text()` (house-style `{voices}`) assumes Spanish voices
  - `locale-en.md` is US spelling for everything: `uk` needs British English; `locale-de.md`, `locale-es-ES.md` were written as translation markets, never as a regional drafting voice
  - `taxonomy.md` assumes Spanish names («… de {región}», «Ríos de Colombia») and "the Spanish-speaking world" as `base`''s audience (slugs + en names: part 16; the Spanish-world audience and the samples'' language: task 10)
  - de and es-ES drafting never ran; en translation only from es so far
- Plan 84 (`plan 84: Release content runs`) chain 5: start tasks `task 1268: Regional runs usa: start` … `task 1272: Regional runs mexico: start` wait for this plan''s tasks of their bundle and colombia''s first batch QC.
- DLC per bundle: `plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)` (DLC app, `steam.json` `dlc`), `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)` (task 748 DLC depots), `plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)` (store texts, capsules).

## RG mapping (15c)
- RG-1, RG-2: done as BN-2, BN-3 (D-39). RG-3 = BN-6 (plan 27 engine, plan 29 screen, plan 30 close-out) + plan 62''s `--simulate --bundles`. RG-4 = BN-11 (`qgen batch --bundle`). RG-5 = decision 110 (amended by the milestone''s further bundles).

## Tasks
1. **RG-5 decision (OQ-46 folded in) and 15c marking** (task 749, done).
2. **Record RG-5** (task 750, done).
3. **Packs as optional installs** (task 751, done; decision 112).
4. **Bundle-scoped taxonomy** (task 826, done).
5. **`colombia` subcategories** (task 827, dropped: replaced by plan 138).
6. **Regional bundle target** (task 828, done): `targets.json` 2000 per regional bundle; `qgen bundle new` writes it.
7. **`qgen batch --translate <locale> --bundle <id>`** (task 829, done).
8. **Pilot effort in `qgen report`** (task 830, done).
10. **Regional drafting in any launch language** (task 1275; before tasks 11–15; its taxonomy and prompt redraft after part 16''s slug keys)
    - `qgen bundle new --kind region --language <L>` (`es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`): `languages: [L]` (en joins later per task 7''s rule; en regions stay `["en"]`); help texts and `bundles.json` `about`: `name`/`description` and `voice` not Spanish-only; `voice` = the region''s language variety in English words.
    - Voice for every draft locale: `bundle_text()` passes a regional bundle''s voice to its drafts whatever the language; `voices_text()` and house-style''s `{voices}` per language. Variety inside one question locale: `uk` drafts British English (spelling, words) although `locale-en.md` says US; `mexico` Mexican Spanish next to `es`''s idiomatic Latin American; how (voice overrides the locale prompt''s spelling line for a region''s own drafts, or a `locale-<L>-<region>` file) is this task''s proposal.
    - `qgen taxonomy` for a non-Spanish region, on part 16''s slugs + en names (no Spanish keys): `taxonomy.md` without the Spanish-world assumptions (base''s audience, samples in the bundle''s language); the bundle''s voice reaches its own language''s names (British spelling in `uk`''s `names.en.json`); the general list''s `{región}` pattern for en names (and the es/de names drafted on `--apply`) as part 16 leaves it.
    - Spanish-only helpers in the chain (`norm()`, number style, Spanish lints) checked for `de` and `es-ES` drafts like plan 148 task 4 did for `en`.
    - `--translate en --bundle <id>` from `de` and `es-ES` sources: `translate-region.md`, `{source_language}`; `qgen validate`''s "regional sources in the region''s language" holds for the new languages.
    - Prompt changes: decision 250 (first draft) answered "don''t apply; redraft after slug keys". Once part 16''s slugs and its taxonomy prompt changes are applied: redraft verbatim old → new (`taxonomy.md`, `taxonomy-names.md`, `regional-categories.json` on top of part 16''s; `locale-en.md`, `locale-es.md`, `locale-es-ES.md`, `locale-de.md`, `translate-region.md` mostly as in decision 250), `pm decision add "Regional drafting in en, de, es-ES: prompts apply? (after slug keys)"`, pending, applied after the answer in this task (or a follow-up task if the answer asks for more). The code staged by its first run (`bundle new --language`, voices per locale) is kept and rebased on the slugs.
    - Throw-away check on a scratch copy: a fake `de` region and a fake `en` region (British voice): `qgen taxonomy` proposal, then `qgen batch --bundle` up to `draft` for one subcategory (decision 208 reporting): German / British text, `locale` right; one `de` source → `--translate en --bundle` selection picks it; copy removed. The game offers an en-only pack only to an en save, a de pack to de and en once `languages` lists both.
    - RUNBOOK (`--bundle` drafts in the bundle''s language), D-36, `plans/22-bundles.md`.
11.–15. **Set up `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`** (tasks 1276–1280, one each, in this order; each after task 10 and part 16''s slug keys)
    - `qgen bundle new <id> --kind region --language <L>` (`usa` en, `germany` de, `uk` en, `spain` es-ES, `mexico` es) with drafted `name`, `description` (the game''s), `rule` (needs a connection to the region; disjoint from `base` and the other regions, e.g. `spain`''s vs `base`, `mexico`''s vs `colombia`''s) and `voice` (US English, British English, German, Spain''s Spanish, Mexican Spanish); 2000 target written by `bundle new` (D-101); en/de names for the bundle.
    - `qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>`; `pm decision add "<id> taxonomy: categories and subcategories"` with the proposal (slug + en name per category and subcategory, the bundle''s language name beside it where not en; counts per category, recommended first) and the bundle''s rule/voice, `pm task-pending-decision`, stop. On the answer: `--apply` (writes slugs, `names.<locale>.json` for en, es, de), `pm decision consequences`, `qgen validate`, `qgen export`.
    - DLC follow-ups for this bundle: `pm task add` in plan 130 (DLC app + `steam.json` `dlc` entry), plan 89 (its depot, like task 748) and plan 88 (store text + capsules, in the bundle''s language and en), unless an open task there already covers it; each body names the bundle, its languages and `languages`'' en rule.
    - Concept lists: not here (the bundle''s first `qgen batch --bundle <id>`, plan 84 chain 5).
    - `plans/22-bundles.md` and `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` list the bundle.
9. **Close-out** (task 752, last; after tasks 10–15, plan 138 and part 16)
    - 15c done (superseded by 22), RG-1..RG-5 `[x]`; 22''s BN-6 per task 479; plan 84''s task 643 and tasks 1268–1272 no longer wait on plan 98; `plans/11-steam.md` S4 row notes packs (2000 per bundle, region''s language + en, free DLC, off by default, pilot `colombia`, then `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`), S5 points at the DLC tasks (748 and the follow-ups of tasks 11–15); task 749''s simulation numbers in `16-content-target.md`.
    - D-entry in `plans/decisions.md` amending decision 110''s D-entry (further bundles, no pilot decision before them); `pm decision consequences 110 "…"`, 166, 167 as task 752 already says.

## Done when
- Decision 110 recorded and amended; OQ-46 resolved; 15c RG-1..RG-5 `[x]`.
- Subcategories keyed by bundle + English slug (part 16); `colombia` on its own approved list, no question on a `base` subcategory.
- `colombia` target 2000 in `targets.json`; `qgen batch --translate en --bundle colombia` works; `qgen report` shows per-bundle cost and review time per 100.
- `qgen batch --bundle <id>` drafts in the bundle''s language and variety (en US / UK, de, es-ES, es); `--translate en --bundle` works from `de` and `es-ES`.
- `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico` exist with approved slug-keyed taxonomies (names in `names.<locale>.json`) and 2000 targets; plans 130, 89, 88 have a DLC task per bundle.
- A pack is an optional file set the game offers only when present (done).

## Out of scope
- The slug migration itself, `names.<locale>.json` layout, save mapping and mods (part 16''s plan).
- Running any regional batch or translation, and the pace across bundles (plan 84 chains 4 and 5); concept lists of the new bundles (their first batch).
- `canada`, `australia`, `argentina` (later candidates, no work now).
- Steam DLC app IDs, store entries and depots themselves (plans 130, 89, 88); Workshop and player-made bundles (own milestone, decision 66); cost per bundle is information only (`qgen report --cost`; no budget, no gates; plan 70).', '', '2026-10-13T15:01:21Z', 249);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (99, 8, 'Retire the browser game and the Python game server', 450, 'Part 9 of masterplan 8. With decision 111: Steam only, the desktop build is the only game: the family''s save moves into `trivia-desktop`, the Python game server (`app/server/main.py`, `trivia`, `/api/save`, `nix build .#app`) goes, `app/` becomes Node/TS only, and workers check UI changes in a browser on a small Vite-based Node dev server instead of "`trivia` with a temp `TRIVIA_STATE`". Authoring''s Python (qgen, `trivia-authoring`, `trivia-media`) stays Python but stops importing from `app/server/`.

## Binding
- decision 111: Steam only: no work, checks or docs for running outside Steam; saves per Steam user (plan 87); dev runs and agent checks keep working through an explicit dev switch. Here: the dev server and `--import-save` print the save location they use.
- decision 39: Local builds start offline?: start test skipped (Steam beta test), not failed; nothing here re-adds it.
- decision 104: Python ↔ Node/TS twins: won''t fix: the Python modules move, they aren''t synced or rewritten.
- decision 98: Browser game: corrupt or newer state/game.json: the backup behaviour survives in `FileStore`/`app/desktop/save.mjs`; the server endpoint goes.
- Dependencies: reuse Vite (already a dev dependency) and the desktop''s own modules; anything new needs a `pm decision`.
- Supersedes D-59''s bridge (`plans/decisions.md`).
- Every step leaves the per-commit checks green (`npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`).

## What exists (2026-10-13)
- `app/server/`: `main.py` (static + `/data/` + cache-only `/media` + `GET/PUT /api/save` + `POST /api/save/backup`, `save.migrate()` at start), `paths.py`, `save.py`, `media_cache.py`, `http_base.py`.
- Authoring imports from `app/server/` via `authoring/tools/layout.py` (puts `app/server` on `sys.path`): `paths` (layout.py, save_file.py, categories.py), `save` (save_file.py: `load()`), `media_cache` (qgen.py, download.py, media.py, authoring/server/main.py, overview.py, media_stats.py), `http_base.BaseHandler` (authoring/server/main.py).
- `app/client/src/lib/store.ts`: `TextStore` → `ServerStore` (`/api/save`, `/api/save/backup`) and `FileStore` (desktop bridge `window.trivia.loadSave/writeSave/backupSave`).
- `app/client/vite.config.ts`: dev proxies `/api`, `/data`, `/media` to the Python server on :8000.
- `app/desktop/`: `save.mjs` (`makeSaveFile`, atomic write, `backup/`), `resolve.mjs` (`makeResolver`: dist, `/data/`, `/media` for `app://`), `main.mjs` (save dir `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` | `state/desktop/<steamid|local>/` in dev | `<userData>/save/…` packaged; `--import-save <file>` already there: writes only into an empty save, no `--force`, no backup).
- `flake.nix`: `trivia-dev` (the `trivia` command, `app/server/main.py`), package `app` (`nix build .#app`, also `default`).
- `authoring/steam/release_check.py`: step `nix` = `nix build .#app --no-link` (D-59).
- Family save: `state/game.json`, version 2 (the client upgrades it on load, engine/save.ts); `game.sqlite`/`flags.json` already migrated (backups only).

## Steps (in this order)

### 1. Node dev server for browser checks
- A Vite plugin in `app/client/` (like `credits.ts`), active in `vite` (dev client) and `vite preview` (built `dist/`):
  - `/data/` from `app/data/`, `/media` from the media cache (`TRIVIA_MEDIA` | repo `media/`), cache only: reuse `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` where it fits, so the rules are the desktop''s.
  - Save: dev-only middleware over `app/desktop/save.mjs` (`makeSaveFile`) and a dev-only page shim that provides the save half of the desktop bridge (`loadSave`, `writeSave`, `backupSave`), so the browser uses `FileStore`, the same Store as the desktop (no `ServerStore` needed). Not in the production bundle.
  - Save dir: `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` if set, else a fresh temp dir (never the family''s save); printed at start (`trivia dev: save <path>`). This is the dev switch of decision 111 for agent checks; plan 87''s "no Steam user = memory-only" must not apply to it.
  - Proxy to :8000 removed from `vite.config.ts`.
- One command each: `npm run dev -w app/client` (dev client) and e.g. `npm run serve -w app/client` (built client); fixed port, printed.
- Replace "walk it on `trivia` with a temp `TRIVIA_STATE`" in AGENTS.md, plan files (`plans/*.md`) and open task bodies (`pm task set`).
- Done when: a fresh-save game plays through a few levels in a browser on the dev server, the save lands in the printed dir, media from the cache plays; `trivia` is still there.

### 2. `trivia-desktop --import-save <file>` and the family switch
- Extend the existing flag in `app/desktop/main.mjs` (+ `save.mjs`):
  - checks the envelope (JSON object, numeric `version`; the client upgrades v2 on load, no Python `save.migrate()` needed);
  - writes the desktop save atomically (`makeSaveFile`);
  - refuses a non-empty target without `--force`; with `--force` first copies the old save to `backup/game-import-<stamp>.json`;
  - prints source, target file (Steam user folder, `local/` or `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`) and backup path; the source file stays untouched.
- Then `pm decision add "Family save imported into trivia-desktop?"` (kind once), body: the exact command for the gamemaster (`trivia-desktop --import-save state/game.json`, run the way the family will play, Steam up or not, since the save folder is per Steam user), what to check (players, seen counters, a round plays), and that the family plays `trivia-desktop` from then on (later the Steam beta). Options: "imported, family plays trivia-desktop" (recommended) | "not yet".
- Step 4 waits for its answer: the step-4 tasks are `pm task-pending-decision` on it.
- Done when: the import works on a copy of the family save in a temp `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`; the decision is raised.

### 3. Authoring''s Python off `app/`
- Move into authoring (e.g. `authoring/tools/`) what authoring still imports: `paths.py`, `media_cache.py`, `http_base.py`, and of `save.py` only what `save_file.py` uses (reading the save); `layout.py` stops putting `app/server` on `sys.path`; import comments updated.
- Move, don''t sync (decision 104); `trivia-authoring`, `qgen`, `trivia-media` behave as before.
- Save path for authoring (apply_flags, seen counts, `save_file.py`): the desktop''s save, not `state/game.json`: `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR/game.json` if set, else `state/desktop/<user>/game.json` (the only one, or the newest, named on stderr); `flags-applied.json` stays under `state/`. If this choice turns out not obvious, `pm decision add`.
- `app/server/main.py` keeps working from its own copies until step 4 (no shared imports across the line).
- Done when: no file under `authoring/` imports from `app/server/`; `qgen validate`, `qgen report`, `trivia-media sync --status approved --dry-run`-style check and `trivia-authoring` pages (review, flags) run; apply_flags reads a flag from a desktop save.

### 4. Deletions (wait for step 2''s decision)
- `app/server/` entirely (`main.py`, the remaining `paths.py`, `save.py`, `media_cache.py`, `http_base.py`, `__pycache__`); `app/` has no `.py` left.
- `lib/store.ts`: `ServerStore`, `/api/save`, `/api/save/backup` (task 724''s backup endpoint); the store choice keeps only `FileStore` (desktop bridge or the dev server''s shim); `TextStore` merged into it if nothing else extends it.
- `flake.nix`: `trivia-dev` (the `trivia` command), package `app` and `default` pointing at it (and the `TRIVIA_STATE` wrapper); the dev shell list updated.
- `authoring/steam/release_check.py`: the `nix` step, its `--skip` choice and docstring row; header and manual rows that mention it.
