INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (115, 15, 'Bundles from mods: one bundle loader', 600, 'Part 5 of masterplan 102 (milestone 15: Modding and Steam Workshop). Player bundles load through the same format and the same loader as ours: a mod carries `data/bundles.json` and `data/bundles/<bundle>/` laid out like `app/data/`, the shell serves one merged `/data/bundles.json`, and `loadEngineData()` reads every bundle in one path. Mod bundle and question ids are namespaced with the mod id, so player content never mixes with our ids, seen counts, flags, reports or telemetry. Mod media sits in the mod folder; nothing is downloaded.

## Binding
- Plan 102''s ground rules: no second path, our data stays ours, page only (the shell reads mod JSON as data, never runs it), offline, path safety (`contained()` per layer), per-commit checks.
- decision 128: Bundles from mods: the shell merges bundles.json; mod ids namespaced `<mod id>:<id>` (the choice asked for by part 5: merge, not a per-bundle `bundle.json` split; other `/data/` files never overlaid by mods).
- decision 129: Credits for mod media: runtime section on the Credits screen from the mod''s own pool.
- decision 38: Base bundles and bundle languages: exactly one base bundle per game; offered per `languages`; stored choices that no longer resolve read as the defaults (covers a removed mod).
- decision 33: Configure game screen (non-base bundles off by default there; default base = the locale''s first base bundle); decision 51: «Solo o en grupo» plays the default bundles (first base + every other offered).
- decision 112: Pack layout: a pool file per bundle; a missing pack file = not offered in that locale (`withPacks`).
- decision 110 (d): bundle-scoped taxonomy, implemented by task 826: Bundle-scoped taxonomy (decision 110 d) (plan 98).
- decision 66, decision 110: our packs ship as free DLC; player bundles are the Workshop''s (milestone 15), never ours.
- decision 111: Steam only; mods (and so mod bundles) load only with a valid user (plan 112).
- Plan 112 (part 2): `mods.mjs` (`discover`, `arrange`, list states, warnings), `resolve.mjs` layers; plan 114 (part 3): Workshop items, `mods:list`. This plan changes `/data/` serving in `resolve.mjs` (plan 112 overlays all of `/data/`; here: only the merge and the namespaced bundle folders).
- Not here: achievements with mods on (part 7, decision 123), the "mods on" telemetry count (part 7), mods screen texts for this plan''s warning codes (part 6), the player bundle kit and `--check-mod` (part 9), new question locales beyond `LOCALES` (part 4 may add UI locales; a follow-up then).

## Format: a mod''s bundles (same as ours)
- `<mod>/data/bundles.json`: `{ "bundles": [ { "id", "kind", "languages", "name", "description" } ] }`, the row fields of `app/data/bundles.json` (`rule`, `voice`, `about`: allowed, ignored).
  - `id`: slug `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,63}$`, unique within the mod; runtime id `<mod id>:<id>`.
  - `kind`: `base` or any other slug (non-base, a pack like `colombia`).
  - `languages`: question locales; tags outside `LOCALES` (`lib/data.ts`) dropped with warning `bundle_language`.
  - `name`, `description`: text in the bundle''s language (no `t()`: player text).
- `<mod>/data/bundles/<id>/`: `categories.json` (as ours, bundle-scoped), `names.<locale>.json` (optional, as ours), `pool.json` (es) / `pool.<locale>.json` (as ours, `version: 1`), media files anywhere below the bundle folder.
- Every bundle''s pool sits in its folder, base bundles too (our base''s top-level `app/data/pool.json` stays: `bundleFile` already maps only `base`).
- Media: `media.file_url` / `background.file_url` a relative path inside the bundle folder (`img/owl.jpg`); the loader rewrites it to `/data/bundles/<mod id>:<id>/img/owl.jpg`; `Question.svelte`''s `src()` passes `/data/…` through, `http(s)` stays `/media?url=…` (ours only). A mod question with an absolute URL or `..`: its media is dropped; with `role: essential` the question is dropped.
- Question fields as `PoolQuestion` (`lib/types.ts`); the loader drops invalid mod questions (missing text, not exactly 3 `wrong_answers`, difficulty outside 1–15, subcategory not in that bundle''s `categories.json`, status not `approved`/missing) and counts them per bundle.

## Shell: merge and serve (`resolve.mjs`, `mods.mjs`)
- `/data/bundles.json` → ours parsed + each loaded mod''s rows in load order (top first), each row `{ …row, id: "<mod>:<id>", source: "mod", mod: "<mod id>", modName: "<mod.json name>" }`; ours keep their rows untouched and come first (default base stays ours, decision 33/38). Built once per run (the layers are fixed), served as JSON.
- Row checks in `mods.mjs` (`bundleRows(dir, modId)`, pure Node, file ≤ 256 KB): structure and slugs only; a bad row → dropped, warning `bundle_row` (+ id) on the mod''s list entry; bad JSON → warning `bundle_json`, no rows. A mod with `data/bundles.json` gets `kind` `bundle` (plan 112''s derivation rule).
- `/data/bundles/<mod id>:<bundle>/<rel>` → `<that mod''s dir>/data/bundles/<bundle>/<rel>` via `contained()`, only if that mod is loaded this run and listed that bundle; else 404. No colon reaches the file system.
- Every other `/data/` path: ours only (decision 128): this plan removes plan 112''s `/data/` layering (runs after plan 112''s `resolve.mjs` task).
- Dev browser server (`app/server/`, plan 99): no mods, unchanged (decision 111).

## Loader: one path (`lib/data.ts`, `engine/pool.ts`)
- `parseBundles` keeps optional `source`, `mod`, `modName`; `Bundle` type gains them; `isOurs(id)` / `isModId(id)` in `engine/pool.ts` = no `:` / has `:` (one helper, used by every "not ours" check below).
- `load(locale)`: unchanged flow; mod bundles are packs to `packsFor` (id ≠ `base`), so their pools load through `withPacks`; for mod packs only: questions get id `<mod>:<id>`, `bundle` = the runtime bundle id, media rewritten, invalid ones dropped (`modPool(json, bundle)` in `engine/pool.ts`).
- Load issues per mod (`{ mod, bundle, code, count }`: `bad_question`, `bad_media`, `bad_categories`, `no_pool`) exported from `lib/data.ts` (`modIssues()`) for part 6''s screen; a broken mod bundle never breaks the load: it''s left out of `bundles` like a pack without a file.
- Taxonomy: after task 826 (bundle-scoped taxonomy) names repeat freely; if this plan runs first, a mod bundle whose category slug or subcategory name clashes with an earlier bundle''s is left out (`taxonomy_clash`); then this plan''s task 2 adds a follow-up task here: remove the check once task 826 is done.
- Languages: a mod bundle is offered in its `languages` ∩ `LOCALES` with a pool file there; our base pool is still required per locale (all three exist).

## Kinds and defaults
- Non-base mod bundle: a pack; off by default on the configure screen (decision 33), on in solo (decision 51: enabling the mod is the opt-in).
- Base mod bundle: allowed; a second radio choice in the base group (decision 38: one base per game), so it replaces ours for that game; ours stays the default base (listed first). Playable through the configure screen; solo keeps decision 51 (first base = ours). Stated in part 10''s guide.
- Removing or disabling a mod: its bundles vanish from `bundles.json`; stored choices naming them read as the defaults (decision 38).

## Selector and Credits
- `BundleSelector.svelte`: mod bundles marked player-made: an icon (`Icon.svelte`; a person/puzzle glyph) + text `t("bundles.playerMade", { mod })` («Hecho por jugadores · {mod}», en «Player-made · {mod}», de «Von Spielern · {mod}»); `ChoiceOptions` bundles carry `source`/`modName` (`engine/api.ts`).
- Credits screen (`Credits.svelte`): after ours, one section per loaded mod bundle: deduped `credit` + `source_url` of its questions'' media and backgrounds (decision 129); heading `t("credits.playerMade", { mod })`.

## Save and "not ours"
- Save rows keep ids as strings: `seen`, `blocked`, games'' history, `flags` take `<mod>:<id>` as they are; no format change, no `SAVE_VERSION` bump; `parseSave` unchanged (check only).
- Removing a mod: seen/blocked rows of its ids stay, ignored (no question with that id); an open game whose card or question is a removed mod''s must still load (check; fix in the engine where `data.byId.get(id)` assumes a hit).
- Flags: the flag action hidden for mod questions (`Game.svelte` `flagTarget` null when `isModId`), so no flags, no reports (plan 93) for them.
- Telemetry: plan 106''s per-answer filter (`engine/telemetry.ts`, "milestone 15 adds the mod/player-bundle exclusion at this one spot") uses `isOurs` (its `^q-\d{4,6}$` test already excludes `<mod>:<id>`; switching keeps one rule).
- Authoring: `save_file.py` drops ids containing `:` in `_seen_blocked()` and `flags()` (one line each, docstring says why); `qgen` reads seen/blocked/flags only through it.

## Tasks

### 1. Shell: merged `bundles.json` and mod bundle folders
- `mods.mjs` `bundleRows`; `resolve.mjs` merge (built once from the run''s loaded mods) and `/data/bundles/<mod>:<bundle>/` routing; `/data/` no longer layered; plan 112''s `resolve.test.mjs` gains cases: merge order and tags, bad row dropped, colon path served from the right mod only, `..` inside a namespaced path, a mod''s `data/pool.json` not served.
- Done when: `node --test app/desktop/` passes; `trivia-desktop` (dev switch) with a temp mod: `/data/bundles.json` in devtools shows ours then the mod''s rows; per-commit checks pass.

### 2. Loader: mod packs, ids, media, issues
- `engine/pool.ts`: `Bundle` fields, `isOurs`/`isModId`, `modPool()` (namespacing, media rewrite, question checks); `lib/data.ts` `load()` and `modIssues()`; `Question.svelte` `src()` for `/data/` paths; taxonomy clash check unless task 826 is done.
- Done when: a throw-away mod (non-base pack, es + en, 30 questions over difficulties 1–15, one image in the folder, one bad question, one absolute-URL media) loads: the configure screen offers it, a gamemaster game with only it on plays a question with the mod''s image, the bad question counted in `modIssues()`; `npm test` (a `pool.test.ts` case for `modPool`), check, build pass.

### 3. Selector, Credits, flags hidden
- `BundleSelector.svelte` marker and `t()` strings (es, en, de, es-ES if different; `check:literals`), `api.ts` passthrough; `Credits.svelte` mod section; `Game.svelte` flag target null for mod questions.
- Done when: in `trivia-desktop` the mod bundle shows the marker on the configure screen, a base mod bundle sits in the base radio group and plays a game alone, the Credits screen lists the mod image''s credit, the flag action is absent on a mod question and present on ours; per-commit checks pass.

### 4. Save and "not ours" checks
- `save_file.py` filter; engine fix if an open game with a removed mod question fails; telemetry spot if plan 106''s code exists.
- Throw-away check: play with the mod (seen rows `<mod>:…`), block one mod question, then remove the mod: the save parses, the player''s stored choice falls back to defaults, the open game resumes or ends cleanly, a new game plays; `qgen report` and `qgen validate` run with that save and show no mod ids; `trivia-authoring` overview counts ignore them.
- Done when: every step above holds (one line each in the done note); temp mod and save copy deleted; per-commit checks pass.

### 5. Docs and decisions
- `plans/22-bundles.md`: section "Player bundles (mods)" (format, namespacing, merge, kinds, defaults, media, credits; decisions 128, 129); `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Modding": `/data/` rules (merge, namespaced folders, no other overlay); `directory.md` where it names `bundles.json` / mod layout; `pm decision consequences 128 "…"` and `129`.
- Done when: docs name decisions 128/129 and the paths; per-commit checks pass.

## Order
After plan 112 tasks 1–3 (and plan 114''s list for warnings, optional). 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5. Part 7 (plan from task 906) uses `isModId` for achievements and the telemetry summary; part 9 (task 908) documents this format and reuses `modPool`''s checks for `--check-mod`.', '', '2026-10-13T18:09:32Z', 902);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (116, 15, 'Split Game.svelte and Question.svelte', 520, 'Part 11 of masterplan 102 (milestone 15: Modding and Steam Workshop). `Game.svelte` (1082 lines) and `Question.svelte` (1243 lines) become a thin controller each plus small per-screen and per-piece components, before part 4 (`window.trivia` screen list, task 904) and part 10 (guide, examples, task 909) name module paths. Worth it now: with plan 111''s readable build a mod overrides one file by path (decision 124), so a theme or a screen tweak would otherwise copy ~1100 lines of markup and CSS and break on every update; paths aren''t public yet, so moving them now costs no mod anything. No behaviour change.

## Binding
- decision 124: Readable client build: output naming rule for mod overrides: new files land at `game/screens/Start.svelte.js` / `.svelte.css` etc.; class names stable per component path.
- Plan 102''s ground rules: per-commit checks (AGENTS.md, D-73) green per task; `trivia-release-check` steps (smoke game, desktop builds) keep passing.
- decision 106: no new lint tooling, no new dependencies.
- Code review precedent (`code-review.md`, `engine/game.ts` row): don''t spread one state machine over files; only markup + CSS + local logic move, shared state stays in one controller.
- `code-review.md` row (`lib/input.svelte.ts`): the Francotirador modal relies on Question''s `KEYS` for A–D aim: the snipe scope stays in `Question.svelte`.

## Rules for the split
- Controller keeps the state: `Game.svelte` keeps `screen`, `go` (transitions, veil, `busy`), `act`/`request`, overlay and flag handling, music per screen, rich presence, `listen`/`listenPads`, the top input scope. `Question.svelte` keeps `locked`/`finalReady`/`submitted`/`revealed`/`result`, joker `armed`/`mode`/`fire`, timers and its input scopes (question, armed, snipe).
- Pieces get props down, callbacks up (the existing style: `onstart`, `onback`, …); no new store, no context API.
- CSS moves with its markup; shared rules (`.corner-hud`, `.side-tray`, the black veil, transitions) stay in the controller or `theme.css`; no visual change (compare screens before/after: screen gallery of plan 100 if built, else screenshots by hand on the same states).
- Modal pieces with their own root may push their own scope (as `CategoryPicker.svelte` does), e.g. the Paso dialog.
- Paths: full screens in `game/screens/` (one folder = the modder''s screen list; part 4 exposes them by these names), pieces of the Question screen in `game/question/`. Existing full screens move there too: `Player.svelte`, `Choice.svelte`, `LanguageScreen.svelte` → `screens/Language.svelte`, `Question.svelte` → `screens/Question.svelte`. Small shared widgets (`Hud`, `Prompt`, `Icon`, `JokerTray`, `Tower`, …) stay in `game/`.
- Target size: each controller ≤ ~500 lines including style; a piece ≤ ~300. A piece that needs more than ~5 callbacks or setters to work stays in the controller (note it in the done note).
- `PLACEHOLDER(<task id>)` markers, `t()` keys, `data-focus-*` attributes and `check-literals.mjs` `SCREENS` keep working (keys are per screen name, not file).
- Comments that name `Game.svelte`/`Question.svelte` (`swap.ts`, `timing.ts`, `lib/input.svelte.ts`, `lib/gamepad.svelte.ts`) updated to the new file.

## Tasks

### 1. Game.svelte: one component per screen
- New `game/screens/`: `Start.svelte` (wordmark, resume/new/play, save notice, `SupplyReport`, fireworks/effects preview), `Level.svelte` (tower, kicker, milestone line), `Select.svelte` (envelopes), `Correct.svelte`, `Wrong.svelte` (consolation), `Victory.svelte`; markup + CSS from `Game.svelte`''s `{#if screen === …}` branches.
- Move `Player.svelte`, `Choice.svelte`, `LanguageScreen.svelte` (→ `Language.svelte`) into `game/screens/`; fix imports.
- `Game.svelte` keeps the controller (see Rules) and the `{#if}` chain that mounts one screen each.
- Done when: `Game.svelte` ≤ ~500 lines; every screen looks and behaves as before (keys, pad, mouse; transitions, music, the block drop on Level after Correct, deal of envelopes, victory fireworks); per-commit checks pass; a smoke game (`trivia-desktop-build --dir`, then `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs`, or `trivia-release-check --skip tag` limited to its smoke step) passes; a manual game in `trivia-desktop` (`TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`) through start → player → choice → level → select → question → correct/wrong → victory (Esc menu «Ir a pregunta…» to reach level 12).

### 2. Question.svelte: media, answers, final answer, joker pieces
- Move `Question.svelte` to `game/screens/Question.svelte`.
- New `game/question/`:
  - `Media.svelte`: backdrop picture/video, audio element, decorative mark, ready/settle (UI-7), `mediaFailed`, replay, media volume; exposes `ready()` and `replay()`; the credit line.
  - `Card.svelte`: question card (topic, text, long-question step, replay button), hints notes, media-missing line.
  - `Answers.svelte`: the four tiles (classes, badges, shards, pad glyphs, snipe hover); `tiles` handed back for the scope/hole.
  - `FinalAnswer.svelte`: final button, padlock, waiting/error lines.
  - `SkipDialog.svelte` (Paso: plain/purge/cancel; own modal scope), `Scope.svelte` (Francotirador hole + aim/hit hints).
- Reveal: the submit → wait → sweep → reveal sequence stays in `Question.svelte` (shared state); if a pure helper falls out (e.g. `answerClass` as a function of state), it goes to `question/reveal.ts`.
- Joker flow (`press`, `fire`, flight, shredder, snipe animation) stays in `Question.svelte` unless it moves cleanly to `question/jokers.ts` (rule: ≤ ~5 callbacks).
- Done when: `screens/Question.svelte` ≤ ~500 lines; image, audio, video and missing-media questions; lock/unlock, final answer, reveal; every joker (Soplo, Paso both options, Bájale with the dial, Cambiazo with the picker and shredder, Francotirador aim/shoot/cancel with keys, pad, mouse); overlay pause during the wait; per-commit checks, smoke game and a manual game in `trivia-desktop` as in task 1.

### 3. Docs and paths
- `directory.md`: `game/screens/`, `game/question/` rows; moved files.
- `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md`, `plans/09-jokers.md`, `plans/10-visual-design.md`, `plans/05-gamemaster-controls.md`, `plans/14-input.md`, `plans/backlog.md`: references to `Game.svelte`/`Question.svelte` pointing at what moved (historic entries in `plans/decisions.md` stay).
- `code-review.md`: rows that named these files get no rewrite; one line in part 5''s section: split done by this plan.
- Open plans whose tasks name `Question.svelte`/`Game.svelte` (e.g. plan 113: Image peek on image questions, plan 106: Telemetry recording in the game, plan 86: Achievements (SW-11), plan 100: UI wording) : update open task bodies with the new paths (`pm task set`) where they name the old file.
- Note for part 4 (task 904) and part 10 (task 909): the screen list = `game/screens/*`, Question pieces = `game/question/*`; one bullet in `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Modding: module paths" if plan 111 task 6 created it, else in this task''s done note.
- Done when: `grep -rn "Game.svelte\|Question.svelte\|LanguageScreen"` outside `plans/decisions.md`, `code-review.md` history and the controllers'' own files shows only current paths; per-commit checks pass.

## Order
After plan 111 task 1 (readable build; not strictly needed, but path names follow decision 124); 1 → 2 → 3; before plan for part 4 (task 904) writes its screen list. Conflicts: plan 113 (priority 400) edits the Question screen: it runs after this plan and targets the new files.', '', '2026-10-13T18:11:10Z', 903);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (117, 15, 'Code add-ons: mods.js and the window.trivia mod API', 500, 'Part 4 of masterplan 102 (milestone 15: Modding and Steam Workshop). Mods get code: each enabled mod may name an `entry` script (plan 112''s `mod.json`) that the page imports at start, and a page-side API on `window.trivia` to hook into data, game actions, UI strings, screens and events without replacing whole files. The preload bridge gives up the name `window.trivia` for it. Everything runs in the sandboxed page; the shell only generates a small module listing the loaded mods and serves their files as bytes.

## Binding
- decision 130: Preload bridge renamed window.trivia → window.triviaShell; window.trivia is the mod API.
- decision 131: Code add-ons: shell-generated /mods.js, entry default export setup(trivia), mods run before data and language load.
- Plan 102''s ground rules: page only (the shell never `import`s/`require`s/`eval`s a mod file; it reads `mod.json` as data and serves files as bytes), no stability promise (`window.trivia` and module paths may change; renames in patch notes), offline (the request block in `main.mjs` stays: mod code gets no network), path safety (`contained()`), strings via `t()`, per-commit checks.
- decision 124: Readable client build: output naming rule for mod overrides: mods may also `import` our modules by path (`/lib/api.js`, `/engine/game.js`); ES modules are single instances, so they see the game''s live state, but exports are read-only: patching goes through the hooks below.
- decision 111: Steam only: mods (and so entries) load only with a valid user or the dev switch (plan 112''s `arrange`); no "without Steam" work.
- decision 128: Bundles from mods: mod bundles come through plan 115''s loader, not through these hooks (no second path); data hooks see mod questions with their `<mod id>:<id>` ids.
- Plan 111: Readable client build (paths, `index.html` with one module script `/main.js`, per-component CSS). Plan 112: Mod format, local mods/ and the app:// overlay (`mods.mjs` `arrange` → `list`/`layers`, load order: index 0 = top, top wins, entries run bottom-up so the top mod patches last). Plan 114: Workshop source (adds `mods` to the bridge: under its new name). Plan 116: Split Game.svelte and Question.svelte (screen names = `game/screens/*`).
- Not here: mods screen, error texts, one-time notice, crash marker and safe start (part 6: it reads this plan''s `modErrors()` and the `ready` event), achievements with mods on (part 7: reads `loadedMods()`), guide and example mods (part 10; this plan''s checks use throw-away mods).

## Bridge rename (decision 130)
- `preload.cjs`: `exposeInMainWorld("triviaShell", …)`; header comment.
- `lib/desktop.ts`: `Window.triviaShell?: DesktopBridge`, `desktop = window.triviaShell ?? null`; the only reader. Plan 99''s dev page shim (task 762, open) sets `window.triviaShell` instead: `pm task set 762` adds the line if it''s still open, else that shim is edited here.
- Docs and open task bodies that say `window.trivia` for the bridge (plans 99, 106, 114 tasks; `plans/18-steam-integration.md`; `directory.md`) follow: `grep -rn "window.trivia\b"`.
- Mods can reach `window.triviaShell` (save, unlock): accepted; part 6''s notice says mods run with the game''s access.

## `/mods.js` and `/mods/<id>/` (shell, decision 131)
- Generated per run by `mods.mjs` `modsScript(list)` (pure), served by `resolve.mjs` at `/mods.js` ahead of all layers (a mod can''t override it; our `dist/` has no root `mods.js`: `src/lib/mods.ts` builds to `lib/mods.js`):
  ```js
  export default [
    { "id": "big-text", "name": "Big text", "version": "1.0.0",
      "entry": "/mods/big-text/main.js", "style": "/mods/big-text/style.css" }
  ];
  ```
  - only mods loaded this run (state `loaded`), in run order = bottom of the load order first; `entry` from `mod.json` `entry` (null if none), `style` if the mod has a root `style.css` (null else); JSON-encoded values, no paths of the player''s disk.
  - `--no-mods`, no valid user, no mods: `export default [];`.
- `/mods/<id>/<rel>` → `<that mod''s dir>/<rel>` only for a mod loaded this run, via `contained()`, files only, `mod.json` not served; else 404. A mod''s relative imports (`./util.js`) and `import.meta.url` resolve inside its own folder; two mods'' `main.js` never collide. Reserved: our `dist/` has no `mods/` folder.
- MIME: `.js`/`.mjs` as `text/javascript` (plan 112''s table).
- Outside the shell (Vite dev, plan 99''s dev server): `/mods.js` is missing → the page runs without mods (no dev-server mod support: decision 111).

## Page loader: `lib/mods.ts` and `main.ts` (order fixed)
1. `main.ts` first line of work: `await loadMods()` (before `language()`, which loads save and data, and before `initLang`).
2. `loadMods()`: `import("/mods.js")` (`/* @vite-ignore */`; failure → `[]`); sets `window.trivia` (global view); per mod in order: link `style` (`<link rel=stylesheet>` appended after ours, so later = stronger, top mod wins the cascade), then `import(entry)`; if the module''s `default` is a function, `await setup(view)` where `view` is the API scoped to that mod (`view.mod` = its `{ id, name, version }`; registrations tagged with the id). Import + setup race a 5 s timeout.
3. A mod that fails (`import` rejects, setup throws, timeout) → `modErrors()` gets `{ id, code: "load_failed" | "setup_failed" | "timeout", message }`, `console.error`, and its registrations are removed (also ones a timed-out setup makes later); the next mod loads; the game always starts.
4. Then as today: `language()` → `initLang` → `initDocument` → mount `App`; after mount the `ready` event fires (part 6''s crash marker clears on it).
- Hooks that throw later (data, action, event, screen render setup) → caught at the call site, reported as `hook_failed` with the mod id, that registration removed for the rest of the run; the game goes on with the unhooked value.
- Error codes stay codes (part 6 maps them to `t()`); no UI here.

## `window.trivia` (`lib/mods.ts`): exactly this
Thin: registrations + re-exports; no stability promise; the type `TriviaApi` exported from `lib/mods.ts` (source maps + public repo are the reference).
- `version`: `buildInfo().version` (decision 91); `mods`: loaded mods `{ id, name, version }[]`; `mod` (scoped view only).
- `modules`: re-exports for convenience, same instances as by path: `api` (`lib/api.ts`), `engine` (`lib/engine.ts` `read`, `run`: a mod''s own route over save + data), `game` (`engine/game.ts`), `i18n` (`t`, `lang`, `fill`), `input` (`pushScope`, `lastDevice` from `lib/input.svelte.ts`), `sound` (`sfx`, `music`), `svelte` (`mount`, `unmount`, `flushSync` from our Svelte runtime: compiled mod components must use our runtime at `/vendor/svelte/…`, not their own).
- `data(fn)`: data hook, in `lib/data.ts` `load()` after parsing and plan 115''s mod-pool step, before `engineData(...)`: `fn({ locale, questions, bundles, ageGroups }) → void | partial replacement` (arrays may be filtered, mapped, extended). Runs per locale load (cached as today), in run order. Example: drop video questions; add a difficulty offset.
- `actions.before(fn)` / `actions.after(fn)`: in `lib/api.ts` `gameAction()` and `playJoker()`: `before(action, body) → body | void` (e.g. a rules tweak: every `new` game gets 2 Soplo via `body.jokers`), `after(action, game) → void` (read-only clone). The engine still validates the body; a refused body errors as today.
- `i18n.add(locale, catalog, opts?)`: in `lib/i18n.ts`: existing locale → deep-merged over it (existing `merge()`), so a mod rewords keys; new locale (`opts.endonym`, `opts.base` default `en`) → `merge(base, catalog)` added to `CATALOGS` and `UI_LANGS` (UI language only; question locales stay `LOCALES`, plan 115) and `ENDONYMS`. Must be called in `setup` (before `initLang`); later calls apply after a reload (stated in the type doc).
- `screens.replace(name, component)` / `screens.dom(name, render)`: names = `game/screens/*` files after plan 116 (`Start`, `Language`, `Player`, `Choice`, `Level`, `Select`, `Question`, `Correct`, `Wrong`, `Victory`; exact list from plan 116''s result). `Game.svelte` mounts `screenFor("Victory", Victory)` instead of the import directly (registry `game/screens/registry.ts`, read once at mount: registrations are before mount). The replacement gets the same props as ours (the guide points at our source). `dom(name, render)`: for mods without a Svelte compiler: `render(el, props) → cleanup?`, mounted through our `game/screens/DomScreen.svelte` wrapper. Last registration (top mod) wins.
- `screens.show(render)` / extra screens: a mod''s own full-screen layer over the game (`DomScreen` in a modal layer in `Game.svelte`, its own input scope via `input.pushScope`), closed by the returned `close()`; reached from `menu.add({ label, onselect })`: extra rows in the Esc menu (`Overlay.svelte`, own column after ours; label is the mod''s text, `check:literals` doesn''t see it).
- `on(event, fn) → off`: `ready` (after mount), `screen` (`{ name }`, from `Game.svelte` `go()` after the switch), `game:start` (`{ game }` after a successful `new`), `game:end` (`{ game, result }` when an action turns `result` from null to won/lost/abandoned), `question:shown` (`{ id, level }`, after the Question screen''s `ready()`), `question:answered` (`{ id, level, index, correct }` after `answer`). Emitted from `lib/api.ts` (game diffs) and `Game.svelte`; payloads are `structuredClone`s; return values ignored.
- `css(href)`: `<link>` for a mod''s extra stylesheets (relative to the mod: `new URL("./x.css", import.meta.url)`).
- Internals for parts 6 and 7 (not on `window.trivia`): `loadedMods()`, `modErrors()`.

## Tasks

### 1. Bridge rename and decision follow-through
- `preload.cjs`, `lib/desktop.ts` as above; plan 99''s shim (task 762 body or code); docs and open task bodies naming the bridge `window.trivia` (`pm task set` for open ones).
