- `mods.mjs` `modsScript(list)`; `resolve.mjs` routes `/mods.js` (ahead of layers) and `/mods/<id>/<rel>` (loaded mods only, `contained()`, no `mod.json`); `main.mjs` passes the run''s `list`. Extend plan 112''s `resolve.test.mjs`: `/mods.js` for zero and two mods (order bottom-up, `style` only when the file exists), `/mods/<id>/` for a loaded mod, 404 for an off/invalid mod, `..` and symlink escapes, `mod.json` not served.
- Done when: the test passes in `npm test`; `trivia-desktop` with a repo `mods/` mod shows the right `/mods.js` in devtools (`TRIVIA_DEVTOOLS=1`); per-commit checks pass.

### 3. Page loader (`lib/mods.ts`, `main.ts`)
- `loadMods()`, scoped views, style links, timeout, `modErrors()`, `loadedMods()`, `window.trivia` with `version`, `mods`, `modules`, `on`/`ready`, `css`; the registration store with removal per mod; `hook_failed` reporting helper used by tasks 4–5.
- Done when: throw-away mods in a temp `TRIVIA_MODS_DIR` under `trivia-desktop`: a `style.css`-only mod recolours; an entry logging `trivia.version` and `trivia.mod.id` on `ready`; one throwing in `setup`, one importing a missing file, one hanging 10 s → each listed in `modErrors()` (console) and the game starts within ~5 s; with no mods the start is unchanged; `npm run dev -w app/client` (no `/mods.js`) starts; per-commit checks pass.

