   - update: account A changes the theme''s colour, `--publish-mod … --changenote "test"`; B restarts Steam/the game: new colour (allow Steam''s update delay).
   - unsubscribe on B: gone from the mods screen after restart, save still plays (no unknown-id error).
   - answer = date + ✓/✗ per row (+ the four item ids and the visibility chosen). `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <decision>` and stop. After the answer: ✗ → follow-ups per routing; `pm decision consequences` on decisions 127 and 132 (what Steam did in practice: install folder, update delay, visibility); the item ids go to task 3.
2. **Gamemaster: guide link on the store page** (after plan 121 task 4) — `pm decision add` (kind once) "Store page: modding bullet and guide link live?", body: the approved texts from `plans/17a-store-page.md` "Modding" per language, where they go (task 672''s rows or the plan 95 task plan 121 added), the guide URL (decision 134), the Workshop item links from task 1 if public; options "live on the store page" (recommended) | "entered, live at launch" | "not yet". Pending on it; after the answer: a note in 17a''s "Modding" (date, live or at launch), `pm decision consequences` on decision 134. "entered, live at launch" → the task closes with that note and task 3 records the milestone''s store-link line as "at launch (plan 95)".
3. **Close-out docs** (after tasks 1, 2) — check what parts 1–10 wrote, fill only gaps (no duplicated prose):
   - `plans/18-steam-integration.md`: "Modding" sections of plans 111, 112, 114, 115, 117, 118, 119, 120 present, top line "player-facing: `modding/README.md`"; bridge rename done everywhere it means the bridge (`grep -rn "window\.trivia\b" plans app directory.md README.md`: only mod-API uses left, historical log lines in `plans/project.md` get "(now `window.triviaShell`, decision 130)"); IPC list complete (`mods:list`, `mods:set`, `mods:notice`, `mods:restart`, `mods:ready`) and matches `preload.cjs`; Workshop facts from task 1 (install folder, update delay, what a subscriber sees).
   - `plans/01-architecture.md`: one overlay bullet (sources local → Workshop, `mods.json` order, layers top-wins then ours, `/mods.js`, merged `/data/bundles.json`, page-only rule) and the readable-build bullet (decision 124); add what''s missing.
   - `plans/11-steam.md`: Tracks table row "Modding and Steam Workshop" (milestone 15, guide `modding/README.md`); Principles: mods run in the page only, no network for mod code; Launch "Preconditions": milestone 15 done; ST-4 rows match task 942 (check, don''t rewrite).
   - `plans/project.md`: Steam track list gains `[x] Modding and Steam Workshop: readable build, mods from mods/ and the Workshop, code add-ons, mods screen, publish and check commands, player bundle kit, guide and examples (<date>, pm milestone 15, plans 102, 111–121 + part 7''s; decisions 124, 127–134)`.
   - `README.md`: how-tos of plans 119, 120, 121 present; add "Test mods locally" if missing (`mods/`, `TRIVIA_MODS_DIR`, `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, `TRIVIA_DEV_WORKSHOP_DIR`, `--no-mods`, devtools `TRIVIA_DEVTOOLS=1`).
   - `AGENTS.md` "Commands": `trivia-desktop` line names `TRIVIA_MODS_DIR`, `TRIVIA_DEV_WORKSHOP_DIR`, `--no-mods`, `--check-mod <folder>`, `--publish-mod <folder>` (`--dry-run` without Steam); if five plans'' additions made it unreadable, one sub-bullet "mods: …"; `trivia-release-check` line names `modkit` and `mods`.
   - `directory.md`: every path milestone 15 added (`app/desktop/{mods,workshop,publish}.mjs`, `lib/mods.ts`, the mods screen, `mods/`, `modding/`, `state/desktop/mods.json`, `mods-start.json`) — `ls` each.
   - `modding/README.md` and the examples'' `mod.json`: the four Workshop item links / `workshopId`s from task 1 (if public; private → no links).
