INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (123, 8, 'Silent game for agents: muted by default under PM_WORKER, opt-in sound', 900, 'Agents (pm workers and interactive sessions) start the game for checks; it shouldn''t make noise on the gamemaster''s machine. Workers mustn''t need to remember a switch: under `PM_WORKER` (set by `pm run` and inherited by everything a worker launches) the game is muted unless the task opts in. Sound work opts in explicitly.

## Behaviour
- Muted when `PM_WORKER` or `TRIVIA_MUTE=1` is set; `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` overrides both (for sound tasks).
- `trivia-desktop`: `webContents.setAudioMuted(true)` in `app/desktop/main.mjs`; prints `trivia desktop: muted (PM_WORKER)` or similar at start.
- Node dev server (`task 762`, plan 99 step 1) and `vite preview`: same env rule, passed to the page (or `?mute`); if task 762 isn''t done yet, a task here adds it there afterwards.
- Session only: never writes `muted` into the stored volumes (`trivia.volumes`, `sound.svelte.ts`); the family''s settings and the Esc-menu volume UI are unchanged.
- No `PM_WORKER`, no env: sound as today (the gamemaster''s runs).

## Telling agents
- AGENTS.md (Commands and Rules): game is muted under `PM_WORKER`; outside pm, launch with `TRIVIA_MUTE=1` unless the work is about sound; `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` for sound checks.
- Open plans/tasks that need audio: say `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` in their body (`pm task set`): at least plans 32: Recorded sound effects (UI-10), 33: Recorded music loops (UI-10), the smoke game / release check if it checks audio, decisions 81/83 (the gamemaster listens: no change, but check their text).
- `trivia-release-check` smoke game: decide muted or not by what it checks; not silently.
- `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (dev switches) in sync.

## Done when
- A worker-started `trivia-desktop` and dev-server page are silent; with `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` they play.
- A normal `trivia-desktop` start plays sound; stored volumes unchanged after a muted run.
- AGENTS.md says it; sound-related open tasks name the opt-in.', '', '2026-10-13T20:13:33Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (124, 15, 'Achievements, flags and telemetry with mods on', 590, 'Part 7 of masterplan 102 (`plan 102: masterplan`, milestone 15: Modding and Steam Workshop). Decision 123''s answer: achievements stay allowed with mods on, because mods may change anything anyway. So achievements, the unlock gate and the save don''t change. Plan 115 already covers flags, reports and per-question telemetry for player questions. What''s left is the telemetry summary''s `mods` flag, which is hard-coded `false` today, plus docs that state the rules.

## Binding
- `decision 123: Achievements in games with mods on: allowed or off?` → always allowed.
- `decision 19: Default mode: presets, checkpoints and won levels`, `decision 73: Achievement list (SW-11)?`, `decision 74: Gamemaster mode earns no achievements`: qualifying games as before; mods add no rule.
- `decision 128: Bundles from mods: the shell merges bundles.json; mod ids namespaced <mod id>:<id>`: `isModId` / `isOurs` (`engine/pool.ts`) is the one "not ours" test.
- `decision 119: Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file`: no save field. Plan 105''s contract already has `games[].mods` (required boolean: "mod or player bundles on"), and plan 109 already reports the mods share.
- `decision 131: Code add-ons: shell-generated /mods.js, …`: `/mods.js` lists every mod loaded in this run''s overlay.
- `decision 71: Upload the rich presence tokens in Steamworks?`: presence tokens as uploaded.

## What exists (checked 2026-10-13)
- `engine/achievements.ts` `qualifies()` / `earned(save, data)`, `lib/achievements.ts` unlock gate (valid user + live bridge). Mod questions already behave this way:
  - `BUNDLE_*`: skips mod bundles (`!isModId(b.id)`).
  - `ALL_CATEGORIES`: looks only at the categories of our `base` bundle.
  - `SPECIALIST`, `QUESTIONS_1000`, the wins and the joker achievements: count player questions like ours.
  - Questions of a removed mod: ignored (`data.byId` miss).
- Flags hidden on mod questions (`Game.svelte`, task 961). `qgen flag --pull` skips and acks mod ids (plan 93). `save_file.py` drops ids with `:` (task 962). Per-answer telemetry keeps `isOurs` ids only (`engine/telemetry.ts` `ourQuestion`).
- `engine/telemetry.ts` `telemetryGame()` sets `mods: false`. `lib/mods.ts` has the rows of `/mods.js` (`fetchList()`, state `loaded` in `mods.mjs` `modsScript`) and `loadedMods()` (only those whose setup succeeded; its comment says "achievements, plan 118").
- Plan 118''s one-time notice already says mods run with the game''s access to the save and Steam achievements.

## Choices
- **Achievements: no change** (decision 123). There''s no `modsActive` in `earned()` or the unlock gate, no `kinds`, no save field in the game row. Without a mods gate, the retroactive pass needs no record of which games were modded. Player questions count like ours except where an achievement names our content (`BUNDLE_*`: our regional bundles; `ALL_CATEGORIES`: our base). Recorded as `decision 146: Achievements, mods screen and rich presence with mods on`.
- **Mods screen: no achievements line** (plan 118''s "part 7 adds its achievements line"). With nothing switched off, there''s nothing to explain beyond the notice''s existing words.
- **Rich presence: unchanged.** A "modded" token would mean a new `steam-presence.vdf` token, a Steamworks re-upload (decision 71) and strings in 4 languages, just to tell friends something they don''t need. A full conversion can set its own presence through the bridge anyway.
- **"Mods on" for telemetry = this run''s overlay isn''t empty:** any row in `/mods.js`, including a mod whose setup failed (its CSS, overrides and bundles still serve). `--no-mods` or a safe start → empty → `false`. It''s per run, not per game: a game spanning two runs is recorded per session slice (plan 106), so each slice carries its own run''s flag. No save field.

## Tasks

### 1. Telemetry: `mods` from this run''s overlay
- `lib/mods.ts`: keep the `/mods.js` row count from `loadMods()`; export `modsOn(): boolean` (rows > 0). Fix `loadedMods()`''s comment (drop "achievements").
- `engine/telemetry.ts`: `telemetryGame(row, from, data, mods)` and `buildTelemetry(…, mods)` take the flag (the engine stays pure). `lib/telemetry.ts` `record()` passes `modsOn()`. A recorded game whose row is gone keeps its stored value, as now.
- Done when: under `trivia-desktop` with `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, `TRIVIA_TELEMETRY_DIR` in `/tmp` and consent `true` set in `install.json`:
  - one question played with a throw-away theme mod (`style.css` only) enabled → the session file''s game has `mods: true`;
  - with `--no-mods` → `mods: false`;
  - no `answers` row carries a `<mod>:` id when a mod bundle question was played.
- Also: temp mod and dir deleted; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.

### 2. Docs: achievements, flags, telemetry, presence with mods on
- `plans/18-steam-integration.md`:
  - "Achievements" bullet: allowed with mods on (decision 123); player questions count except `BUNDLE_*`/`ALL_CATEGORIES`.
  - "Modding" section: one bullet for achievements, flags (hidden on player questions), reports (ours only), telemetry (`isOurs` answers, `games[].mods` per run), presence unchanged.
- `plans/12-client-engine.md` "Telemetry recording": the `mods` flag line.
- `plans/22-bundles.md` "Player bundles (mods)": achievements line if it lists "not ours" rules.
- Plan 121''s guide (`modding/README.md`) takes this from these docs; not written here.
