INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (125, 5, 'Play-test fixes: player Enter, Choice screen, overlay line, Regional: Colombia', 400, 'Fixes from `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` (answered "problems", items 1–6; item 7 is its own plan, language). Plans 27, 29 and 71 are done, so the fixes land here. After this plan and the language plan, the play-test is raised again and `task 479: Close out AG-7 and BN-6` (plan 30) waits on it.

## Fixes (one task each)
1. **Player screen Enter** (`app/client/src/game/screens/Player.svelte`): with saved players and nothing focused, Enter does nothing. Enter picks the most recent player (`shown[0]`), as if its name button were pressed.
2. **Overlay choice line labelled** (`app/client/src/game/Overlay.svelte` `choiceLine`, `choice.line` in `locales/{es,es-ES,en,de}.ts`): today «Niños · Básico, Colombia». Two labelled parts: «Edad: Niños», «Paquetes de preguntas: Básico, Regional: Colombia»; en "Age group", "Question bundles"; de likewise (e.g. «Altersgruppe», «Fragenpakete»). A custom difficulty keeps its «Desde–Hasta» text under the age label.
   - Term: "question bundle" («paquete de preguntas»), as the Steam DLC; base bundle and the others are all question bundles; never «Temas». Grep the catalogs for «Temas» / bundle wording and align.
3. **`colombia` named «Regional: Colombia» everywhere**: `app/data/bundles.json` `name`, `app/data/names.en.json` / `names.de.json` (en "Regional: Colombia", de «Regional: Kolumbien» or as the catalog style says), so Choice screen, `BundleSelector.svelte`, overlay, credits show it; Steam DLC name in the store/Steam docs and data (grep `Colombia` in `plans/`, `app/desktop/`, steam config). Bundle letter keys (`keyOf`) still unique; `qgen validate` passes.
4. **Mode row order** (`Choice.svelte` mode list, ~line 239): «Solo o en grupo» first, then «Modo anfitrión». Default focus/selection unchanged otherwise; screen gallery and docs (`plans/13-game-modes.md`, `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md`) follow.
5. **Bundle selection in every mode**: «Solo o en grupo» has no bundle selector today (only gamemaster mode''s configure screen has `BundleSelector`). Solo gets it too. Bundle selection, like the age group, is its own step/section in every mode, not session customization: not inside «Personalizar partida» nor counted as "customized"; in gamemaster mode it stays apart from the other configure fields.
   - Overrides `decision 38: Base bundles and bundle languages` / `decision 33: Configure game screen: which fields?` where they say solo plays the locale''s defaults. Preset as gamemaster mode: the player''s last choice, else the locale''s defaults (first base bundle; non-base off per decision 33''s consequence — check `playerChoice`).
   - Record the rule: `pm decision record` and a D entry in `plans/decisions.md` (supersedes those parts); docs `plans/13-game-modes.md`, `plans/22-bundles.md`.
6. **Difficulty «Desde»/«Hasta» always visible** (`Choice.svelte` gamemaster difficulty stepper, `difficulty.ts`): with an age group selected they show the group''s window from `app/data/age-groups.json` (e.g. Niños 1–6), read-only and skipped by the arrow keys/focus ring; editable only with «A medida» (as today). Pad and mouse the same.

## Checks
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `check:literals`, `qgen validate`.
- Browser (`npm run dev -w app/client`, `TRIVIA_MUTE=1`): each fix by mouse and keyboard (IN-1); es, en, de catalogs.', '', '2026-10-14T07:41:56Z', 479);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (126, 5, 'One language setting for UI and questions', 500, 'Item 7 of `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles`: one language for UI and questions, replacing D-86''s two settings (`plans/decisions.md` D-86: `SaveData.language {ui, questions}`, Esc menu rows «Idioma» / «Idioma de las preguntas»). Bundles depend on the language, so the language can''t change once bundles are chosen. Runs before `plan 125: Play-test fixes: player Enter, Choice screen, overlay line, Regional: Colombia` (400); the play-test is raised again after both.

## Rules (from the answer)
- One setting: the game''s language = UI language = question language.
- Chosen at first start (`screens/Language.svelte`, default from Steam''s client language / `guessTag()`, as now).
- Afterwards changeable only via a language flag button top right on the very first screen (Start); clickable and on a key/pad (IN-1). Not on later screens.
- No language rows in the Esc menu (`Overlay.svelte`), in any mode.
- Never changeable once bundles are chosen or in a session: a game keeps its locale (`GameRow.locale`, as now).
- A language without its own pool (`pool.<locale>.json` missing, en/de today) plays the Spanish questions (`pool.json`, `es` bundles via `bundlesFor`) until its translation ships. All UI languages stay selectable (testing).
  - So the question locale = the language if its pool exists and passes, else `es`; define this in one helper (`lib/data.ts` / `lib/engine.ts`) and use it for `loadEngineData`, `newGame`''s locale, `bundlesFor`.

## Changes
- Save: `SaveData.language` → one value (e.g. `language: string`); `parseSave` reads old `{ui, questions}` saves as `ui`; a save-version bump only if `plans/` rules require it (check `parseSave` / D-82, D-86). Desktop `FileStore` unaffected.
- `lib/i18n.ts`, `lib/data.ts`, `lib/engine.ts`, `lib/api.ts`, `lib/types.ts`: drop the separate question language; options = `UI_LANGS`.
- `Language.svelte` (first start): picks the one language; `Start.svelte`: the flag button opening the same picker (UI change still reloads, D-86).
- `Overlay.svelte`: language rows removed; `locales/*.ts` strings for them removed, flag button strings added (`check:literals`).
- Achievements `POLYGLOT` (wins in two question languages, `GameRow.locale`): check it still works with the fallback (a de UI on Spanish questions is an `es` game).
- Docs: D entry in `plans/decisions.md` (supersedes D-86''s two rows and question-language option, in part), `pm decision record`; `plans/15-*` i18n plan, `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md`, `directory.md` if files change; README how-to if it mentions the question language.

## Checks
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`.
- Browser: fresh save → language screen; Start flag switches es/en/de (reload); en/de play the Spanish pool with `es` bundles; Esc menu has no language rows; an old save with `{ui, questions}` loads.', '', '2026-10-14T07:42:09Z', 479);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (127, 5, 'Age group and bundle names in the UI language', 400, 'Seen in `task 1022: In-game «Dificultad y paquetes»: «Desde»/«Hasta» always visible, read-only for age groups`''s browser check: en UI (no en pool, so `decision 156: One language for UI and questions` plays the es pool), Esc → «Dificultad y paquetes» shows the age groups as «Adolescentes», «Jóvenes», «Adultos», «Niños» next to English labels. Runs before `plan 30: Play-test and close-out of age groups and bundles`.

## Fix (one task)
- Cause: `app/client/src/lib/data.ts` (~line 131) loads `names.<locale>.json` for the question locale (es → `NO_NAMES`), so `app/data/names.en.json` / `names.de.json` (age_groups, bundles) go unused when the pool falls back to es.
- Age group and bundle display names follow the UI language (`names.<ui language>.json` when it exists); category/subcategory names may stay with the questions.
- Places: Choice screen, `GameSettings.svelte`, `BundleSelector.svelte`, overlay choice line, credits.

## Checks
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`.
- Browser: en and de UI show group and bundle names in that language; es unchanged.', '', '2026-10-14T08:22:43Z', 1022);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (128, 9, 'S4 close-out', -130, 'Part 12 of the masterplan (`plan 9: masterplan`): the last step of milestone 9 (S4). Once the other S4 plans are done, this plan checks the milestone''s "Done when" (target met per launch language, first-start language picker, UI wording reviewed, joker names and symbols, English-first `base` with its translations, English slug keys for every category and subcategory), records the results, and brings the plan files, indexes and later masterplans in line. The regional bundles (`colombia` pilot, then `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`, 2000 approved each in their languages) may land after launch: their record is a separate, last task; the milestone''s close-out waits for it, the launch (milestone 11) never does. Docs, checks and pm only; failures become tasks in the owning plans, never fixes here.

## Binding
- `decision 21: Content target per player and language (OQ-32)?` (D-75): pass/fail = 5000 approved per question locale (`en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`; milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15) with D-53''s mix; the simulation''s games numbers are information only. decision 26 (D-78): launch languages `es`, `en`, `de` (+ `es-ES`). Deficits per question locale (plan 148 task 6; replaces decision 37''s last clause and D-84).
- `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`: `locale` on every source (absent = `es`); `base` from batch-9 `en`, ≤ batch-8 `es`; pool for L = approved sources in L + playing translations into L; `pool.json` = `es`, `pool.es-ES.json` new.
- `decision 156: One language for UI and questions`: an `es-ES` save plays `pool.es-ES.json` once its default bundles'' supply passes, else `es`.
- decision 50 item 7 → D-96 (plan 126, tasks 1019–1021): one language for UI and questions; picker at first start (guess preselected: `navigator.language`, Steam''s language once milestone 10 wires it); afterwards only Start''s language button; no Esc menu language rows; a stored save without `language` (the family''s) = `es`, never sees the picker. This supersedes the masterplan''s "Esc menu" wording for the check.
- decision 110 (D-99): Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46): every regional bundle 2000 approved in its region''s language + en (en regions: en only); `colombia` (es + en) the pilot, effort measured ($ per approved, review time per 100); launch ships what the bundles have. Its "more bundles only after a new decision with the pilot''s numbers" is replaced (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15): `usa` (en), `germany` (de + en), `uk` (en), `spain` (es-ES + en), `mexico` (es + en), run by plan 84''s chain 5; no "More regional bundles?" decision.
- decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): packs are free DLC.
- Cost (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15): `qgen report --cost` is information only; no dollar budget per language or bundle, no budget decision, no over-budget gate (`decision 204: Translation pilot done (tr-en-1, tr-de-1)?` irrelevant for it, which dropped task 1''s first task, task 1032).
- Plan 57 (CT-5): every drafted batch/back-audit slice with approved questions in the release pool is release-ready (`qgen report --qc`); translation runs (`tr-*`) have no QC and no release-ready row. Release-ready is reported here, never waited on: the release bar is the developer''s own gate at `trivia-release-check` (decision 414).
- `decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation` (developer, 2026-10-23): health ✗, spot checks and QC proposals are raised as decisions, no task waits on them; health ✗ never stops a run (drafting, `--bundle`, `--translate`); partly supersedes decision 45 and `decision 313: Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run`. This plan never pends on a review decision; its own decisions (target shortfall, chains still running) are scope choices, not reviews. The code, RUNBOOK and `authoring/QC.md` change is the plan `task 1699: write plan: Reviews don''t gate generation` writes (milestone 1).
- Translations without human control (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-16): the LLM translation review is a translation''s only review, every question locale; no native-speaker spot check, no QC decision per `tr-*` run, no pilot go/no-go, no `qgen health ack` after a pilot; decision 45''s thresholds are reported, never a stop (decision 414). Replaces QT-5''s go/no-go, QT-6''s spot check, decision 45''s "the pilot always stops the next run" (plan 66 or its follow-up records the supersession), `authoring/QC.md` "Translation runs" spot check.
- Plan 100: decisions 161–164 "Screen gallery reviewed? (<lang>)"; task 1026 (gallery fixes). Plan 69: decisions 62–65 "Playtest passed?", task 459.
- Plan 136 (`plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`; masterplan part 14, developer 2026-10-14): one English-first name per joker, translated in `es`, `es-ES`, `de` (keys per `decision 53: Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?`), one symbol across languages, shown in its follow-up dialog; its record supersedes decisions 40–44 and 54–58; its "Joker names and symbols reviewed?" decision; task 459 runs after it. Find the decisions with `pm decision list --grep "Joker names"`.
- Slug keys (masterplan part 16, developer 2026-10-16; its plan written by `task 1305: write plan: Slug keys for categories`): every category and subcategory in every bundle keyed by an English slug, unique within its bundle; display names, `en` included, only from `names.<locale>.json` (`es-ES` reads `names.es.json` + `names.es-ES.json` overrides); old saves (Spanish names, old category slugs in `purged`, `swapped_to`, `notified_exhausted`) load; mods'' plain-string format stays valid. Supersedes the name-as-key part of `decision 165: Subcategory keys in code: bundle + name; base keeps bare names`, D-99, D-100 (that plan records it).

## Depends on
- Tasks 1–3 wait for plans 57, 62–64, 66–70, 98, 100, 126, 136, 138, 147, 148 and the slug-keys plan (part 16, from task 1305; find its id with `pm plans list`; until it exists, task 1305 counts as its open task) (all tasks done or dropped) and plan 84''s chains 1–3 (neutral Spanish, translation pilot (no go/no-go), full translation per locale `en`, `de`, `es-ES`, `es`) at their end. Not plan 84''s chains 4 (`colombia`) and 5 (`usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`) nor the pilot-effort task: those are task 4''s. `plan 17: Batch runs` (English `base` drafts, milestone 1) isn''t waited for: task 1''s numbers say whether there is enough.
- Guard at the start of each task: `pm plans list`, `pm show` of the plans above. If one has open tasks (other than plan 84''s regional chains 4–5 for tasks 1–3): if one of them is pending on a decision, `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <that decision>`; otherwise stop without changes and say so (the queue brings the task back). Never drop or edit tasks of other plans.
- Not the milestone''s post-milestone cleanup; this plan doesn''t set the milestone status.

## Tasks
1. **Content target check** (-130)
