   - Done when: the milestone''s "Done when" holds in full; task note cites decision 110 and the milestone''s 2026-10-15 change.

## Out of scope
- Running or fixing content (plans 17, 84), English-first tooling and prompts (plans 147, 148), slug-key migration and tooling (the slug-keys plan, part 16), UI fixes (plans 69, 100, 126), joker names and symbols (plan 136), store texts (S5, plan 88), Steam language detection (milestone 10), later languages (milestone 12).', 'This is the final check before the content work for the Steam release counts as finished. It confirms there are enough reviewed questions in every launch language, that new players are asked for their language once, that the on-screen wording, joker names and category names are settled, and that machine translations rely on an automatic review only. It then brings the project''s written records in line; the regional question packs may finish after launch and get their own last check.', '2026-10-14T21:33:52Z', 251);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (129, 10, 'Partner account, name check and AI terms (PUB-6, PUB-7, PUB-10)', 720, 'Part 1 of `plan 10: masterplan` (milestone 10, S5). Three paper tasks before the Steamworks app exists: the partner signup and app credit (PUB-6), the name and trademark check of the store names (PUB-7), and Anthropic''s commercial-use terms for the pipeline''s outputs (PUB-10). Owner: `plans/17-publishing.md` ("Steamworks and store", "AI disclosure"); PUB-6, PUB-7, PUB-10 rows there get `[x]` with a note.

## Binding
- `decision 67: Steamworks account holder (OQ-33): person or company?`: a person, after an advisor check; store Developer/Publisher as a label; company later via app transfer (D-98).
- `decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): how is the game sold on Steam?`: paid base app; packs as free DLC (no app credit per DLC, check Valve''s page).
- D-50 (store names «Living Room Trivia», Spanish «Trivia en Familia») and `decision 78: German store name (PUB-8, D-50): keep «Living Room Trivia» or a localized one?` («Wohnzimmer-Quiz»): all three stand only once PUB-7 passes; fail → OQ-34 reopens as a new pm decision, store names wait.
- `decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`: no rows for selling or running outside Steam (no itch.io, no own shop, no domain shop).
- Workers research and write; they never log in, enter credentials, pay, file a trademark, buy a domain, or contact Valve, a lawyer or a tax advisor. Questions for a professional go into a pm decision body the developer forwards.

## Parts

1. **PUB-10 Anthropic terms** (research, no human needed)
   - Which terms govern `claude -p` on the developer''s plan type (consumer Pro/Max → Consumer Terms; API key / Console → Commercial Terms); read the current pages (anthropic.com/legal: consumer terms, commercial terms, usage policy) and note URL + read date.
   - Questions: who owns outputs; may outputs be sold in a commercial product (questions, translations, code); any restriction that bites (e.g. using outputs to build competing models: irrelevant here, say so); attribution needed or not.
   - Result: one line + source in plan 17 "AI disclosure" (replace the "Check Anthropic''s terms…" bullet), PUB-10 `[x]`.
   - Unclear point (e.g. plan type allows commercial use only via API) → `pm decision add` with a body ready for a professional (question, quoted clause, URL, date) and the options (keep, switch the pipeline to an API key, ask a lawyer); PUB-10 waits on it.
   - Feeds `task 667: AI disclosure text (Steam survey + store wording)` (plan 88): the disclosure facts are fixed by the milestone (pre-generated = LLM-drafted questions checked, edited, approved by a person, and LLM-written code; live-generated = none; no AI-generated art, images, sound or music; capsules typographic per `decision 77: Store capsule art (PUB-8): who makes the capsules and logo?`). Only if the terms change one of them: a note in `plans/17a-store-page.md` "AI disclosure" and in task 667''s body (`pm task set`, if still open).
   - Also add PUB-10''s finding to plan 17 "Code and content license" ("Lawyer check owed" bullet: drop PUB-10 there if the finding is clear).

2. **PUB-7 name and trademark check** (research, then a decision)
   - Names: «Living Room Trivia» (en, default), «Trivia en Familia» (es, es-ES), «Wohnzimmer-Quiz» (de).
   - Per name: Steam store search (exact and close titles, also the Steam app list), EUIPO (eSearch plus / TMview), USPTO (Trademark Search), WIPO Global Brand Database, classes 9 and 41 (games software, entertainment); a web search for apps/board games of the same name (Play Store, App Store, BoardGameGeek); domains (`.com`, plus `.de` for the German, `.es`/`.com.co` for the Spanish) via RDAP/whois — for information only, the game needs no domain.
   - Findings table in plan 17 under a new "Name check (PUB-7)" section: name, source, hit (exact / similar / none), class, owner, status, date read. Not legal advice; a professional clearance search is optional and the developer''s call.
   - `pm decision add "Store names pass PUB-7?"`: body = summary per name with the riskiest hits; options: pass all three (recommended if no live identical mark in classes 9/41 and no Steam game of that name) / pass some (list) / fail → reopen OQ-34.
   - After the answer: pass → D-50 and OQ-34 marked final (`plans/decisions.md` D-50 note, `plans/open-questions.md`, `plans/11-steam.md` OQ table, `plans/17a-store-page.md` "Name … (provisional)" note dropped); fail → a new pm decision for OQ-34 (new name candidates with a quick pre-check each), store names, capsules (plan 88) and the exe''s `ProductName` (`plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Exe metadata") wait; PUB-7 `[x]` with the result.
   - Renaming builds (`productName`, artefact names) after a pass: not this plan''s; add a follow-up task to `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)` if none exists.

3. **PUB-6 signup checklist and the App ID** (checklist, then a decision)
   - Read Valve''s current pages (partner.steamgames.com/doc/gettingstarted, /onboarding, /appfee; Steamworks tax interview help) and note URL + read date.
   - Checklist in plan 17 under a new "Steamworks signup (PUB-6)" section, in order, for the developer:
     - advisor check first (decision 67): questions for the tax advisor as a ready list (registration as a sole trader in the developer''s country, US withholding and the treaty rate via W-8BEN, VAT/OSS on Steam sales (Valve collects VAT in the EU), the DSA trader address shown on the store page and whether a home address is acceptable, when to switch to a company)
     - partner signup: legal name, address, contact; the NDA/distribution agreement; identity verification
     - bank details; tax interview (W-8BEN for a non-US individual)
     - store Developer/Publisher label (the developer''s choice, e.g. a studio label; not a company)
     - pay the $100 app credit (Steam Direct fee, recouped after $1,000 adjusted gross revenue); note the payment date (21-day rule before release, `plans/11-steam.md` "Coming soon page (ST-3)")
     - create the app: name «Living Room Trivia» if PUB-7 passed, else a working name (changeable before "coming soon"); DLC apps (one per shipped pack, decision 66) need no app credit (confirm on Valve''s page); they are part 2''s (`task 254: write plan: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)`)
     - grant the build account later (part 7, plan 89), not here
   - `pm decision add "Steamworks app created? App ID?"`: body = the checklist link, what to report (App ID, app credit payment date, Developer/Publisher label); options: created (App ID …, paid on …, label …) / not yet. Make PUB-6''s closing task pending on it (`pm task-pending-decision`).
   - Answer → App ID and payment date into plan 17 (PUB-6 note) and `plans/11-steam.md` (S5 prerequisites); `decision 89: Steamworks App ID, depot IDs and beta branch entered? (for the first beta upload)` stays part 2''s/plan 89''s (depots, branch); the switch from Spacewar 480 to the real App ID (`steam_appid.txt`, `TRIVIA_STEAM_APPID`) is part 2''s, not here.

4. **Close-out**
   - Plan 17: PUB-6, PUB-7, PUB-10 `[x]` with notes; status line; `plans/project.md` and `plans/11-steam.md` (S5 prerequisites) in sync; `pm decision consequences` on each answered decision.

## Order
- Parts 1 and 2 run now (research only); part 2''s decision and part 3''s decision wait on the developer.
- Part 3''s checklist can be written before PUB-7 is answered; the app name step points to PUB-7''s result.
- Part 4 last.

## Done when
- Plan 17 holds PUB-10''s line with source, the PUB-7 findings table and result, the PUB-6 checklist with App ID and payment date; PUB-6, PUB-7, PUB-10 `[x]`.', '', '2026-10-14T21:35:41Z', 253);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (130, 10, 'Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)', 700, 'SW-7 (masterplan 10 part 2): the exact Steamworks values the developer enters for the base app and each free DLC app, as one checklist in `plans/18-steam-integration.md`, confirmed through one pm decision; then the real App ID replaces Spacewar 480 in the repo. Docs and pm, plus a one-constant code change; no Steamworks access for workers (they never log in, never enter values). Steam only (decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam): no values for running outside Steam, no DRM, no `restartAppIfNecessary`, no anti-tamper.

## Binding
- decision 67: Steamworks account holder (OQ-33): person or company?: person; the app comes from `plan 129: Partner account, name check and AI terms (PUB-6, PUB-7, PUB-10)` via decision 177 "Steamworks app created? App ID?" (pending).
- decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): bundles are free DLC, own store entries, optional install; DLC needs no app credit.
- decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46): only `colombia` ships, es + en, off by default.
- decision 84: SteamCMD source and depot split for Steam uploads: depots `windows`, `linux`, `content`, one install folder; `SetLive` beta only; `default` set only in the web UI, empty until S6.
- decision 125: Steam Deck: best effort, review without a Deck at hand: the Gamepad template as Steam Input default is a precondition of `plan 90: Steam Deck review and Deck test (SW-12)`''s review request.
- decision 90: Store requirements, languages and controller flags?: store-page languages and controller flags (Partial) live in `plans/17a-store-page.md`; not repeated here.
- decision 152: Manual safe start: --no-mods only: no second Steamworks launch option.
- decision 26: Launch languages (OQ-31) / decision 27 (Spanish variants): latam (es-419), spanish (es-ES), english, german.
- decision 78 / decision 176 "Store names pass PUB-7?" (pending): localized names; if PUB-7 fails, the names row waits for the new OQ-34 decision.

## Reuse, don''t copy (point to these sections)
- Auto-Cloud: plan 18 "Steam features" → "Auto-Cloud values for SW-7" (`plan 87: Steam Cloud saves`).
- Achievements: plan 18 "Achievements in Steamworks"; entered via decision 140 "Achievements entered and published in Steamworks?" (`plan 86: Achievements (SW-11)`).
- Rich presence: `app/desktop/steam-presence.vdf` (`plan 85: Steamworks binding in the shell (SW-8)`).
- Depots, `steam.json`, DLC depots, branches: plan 18 "Builds and depots" (`plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`); decision 89 "Steamworks App ID, depot IDs and beta branch entered?" already asks for the IDs: the new decision asks the same plus the rest, and says "answer decision 89 with ''see decision N''".
- Store fields (texts, languages table, controller flags, requirements, capsules): `plans/17a-store-page.md`, entered via `task 672: Store page entry checklist and PUB-8 close-out`; DLC store texts via decision 173.
- Workshop: decision 135 "Steamworks: enable Workshop …" (milestone 15), not here.
- Deck review request: plan 90, not here.

## Values (task 1 writes them as checklist rows; field names from memory, "recheck at entry")
- **App:** App ID from decision 177; type Game.
- **Names (D-50):** default/english «Living Room Trivia»; latam + spanish «Trivia en Familia»; german «Wohnzimmer-Quiz» (decision 78); in-game `productName` «Trivia» unchanged (plan 18 "Exe metadata").
- **Installation folder:** `LivingRoomTrivia` (Cloud paths don''t depend on it).
- **Launch options** (Installation → General), no arguments, no Proton forcing:
  - Windows, 64-bit: executable `Trivia.exe`
  - Linux + SteamOS, 64-bit: executable `trivia` (the `after-pack.mjs` launcher, adds `--no-sandbox`; binary `trivia-bin`)
  - Linux runtime: Steam Linux Runtime (current "sniper"/3.0 if Steamworks offers the choice; recheck); the beta test (`task 263: write plan: Beta test and S5 close-out`) confirms it starts
  - never `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER`, `--no-mods` or other dev args
- **Redistributables:** none (Electron ships its runtime).
- **Depots** (Installation → Depots): `windows` (OS Windows, 64-bit), `linux` (OS Linux, 64-bit), `content` (all OS), language "all" for each; plus `colombia` (all OS, tied to the colombia DLC app); IDs → `authoring/steam/steam.json` (task 2 / `task 681: First beta upload: checklist and decision`).
- **Free DLC per shipped pack:** base app → "All Associated Packages, DLC, Demos And Tools" → "Add New DLC": `colombia`, name «Regional: Colombia» (es, es-ES, en «Regional: Colombia»; de «Regional: Kolumbien» only once a de pack pool ships), price free, depot `colombia` linked to it, optional (installed when owned and ticked in Properties → DLC); the base app lists it; store texts per 17a "Free DLC". Only packs in `app/data/bundles/` at upload time.
- **Branches** (SteamPipe → Builds): `default` empty until S6; `beta` password-protected, password with the developer only, never in a file.
- **Steam Cloud:** plan 18''s Auto-Cloud values (quota 1 file / 20 MB; root `WinAppDataRoaming`, `trivia/save/{64BitSteamID}`, `game.json`, non-recursive; Linux override `LinuxXdgConfigHome`), conflict: Steam''s dialog, no code.
- **Steam Input** (Application → Steam Input): default configuration for every controller type = the **Gamepad** template (Valve''s "Gamepad" / "Generic Gamepad" template; the Deck''s controls arrive as a virtual Xbox pad); no opt-outs for PlayStation/Xbox/Switch configuration support (glyphs read `GetInputTypeForHandle`, plan 85); no custom action set (the game reads the browser Gamepad API).
- **Deck:** nothing else to set in SW-7 (fit plan 46, peek plan 113, review plan 90).
- **Rich presence:** upload `app/desktop/steam-presence.vdf` (Community → Rich Presence or Steamworks'' localization upload; recheck).
- **Achievements:** decision 140 (not repeated).
- **Publish** the Steamworks changes after each block.
- **Dev:** `TRIVIA_STEAM_APPID` / `SteamAppId` override stay; the default switches from 480 to the real App ID; no `steam_appid.txt` in the repo or in builds (`steam.py` `EXCLUDE`); a dev run that needs one writes it gitignored.

## Tasks
1. **SW-7 checklist in plan 18 and the "configured" decision**
   - New section "Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)" in `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (after "Builds and depots"): an intro paragraph, then a checklist (`- [ ]` rows, grouped by Steamworks page) with the values above; pointers instead of copies where "Reuse" lists a source. Note at the top: needs decision 177''s App ID; Valve''s field names unverified, recheck at entry.
   - `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Steam Deck Verified": the Gamepad-template bullet points to this section.
   - `did=$(pm decision add "Steamworks app configured (SW-7)? IDs?" …)`, body: after decision 177; the section to follow; report App ID, depot IDs `windows`, `linux`, `content`, `colombia` DLC app ID + its depot ID, `beta` branch created (no password), Gamepad template set as Steam Input default, Cloud values, launch options, rich presence uploaded, published; decision 89 asks the same IDs: answer it "see decision <did>"; achievements stay decision 140, Workshop decision 135, store page task 672. Options: `configured: App ID …, depots windows … linux … content …, colombia DLC … depot …` (recommended), `not yet`, `issues (rows)`.
   - `pm task-pending-decision <task 2> $did`.
   - Done when: section written; decision pending; task 2 waits on it.
2. **Real App ID in the repo and SW-7 close-out**
   - After the decision. `app/desktop/main.mjs` `STEAM_APP_ID` → the real App ID (comment gone); README `TRIVIA_STEAM_APPID` default; plan 18 "Steam features" Dev line (480 until SW-7) and SW-8 note updated; `authoring/steam/steam.json` with every ID unless task 681 already filled it (`steam.py` `--dry-run` keeps 480).
   - Fill the answered IDs into the SW-7 section, rows `[x]`; issues → follow-up tasks in the owning plan (85, 87, 89, 90) with the failing row.
   - Plan 18 SW-7 `[x]` with date and note; `plans/project.md` S5 row; `pm decision consequences` on the decision.
   - Check: `npm run check`, `trivia-steam vdf` (or `--dry-run`) writes the VDFs with the real IDs.
   - Done when: no 480 default left outside `--dry-run`; SW-7 ticked.

## Out of scope
- Entering values (the developer), store page fields (plan 88), achievements entry (decision 140), Workshop (decision 135), the first upload (plan 89), the Deck review (plan 90), price (part 9), `report-server/wrangler.toml` `STEAM_APP_ID` (decision 147''s follow-up).', '', '2026-10-14T21:50:30Z', 254);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (131, 10, 'Content survey, rating and price (PUB-9, PUB-11)', 290, 'Part 9 of `plan 10: masterplan` (milestone 10, S5): the Steamworks content survey with its age rating (PUB-9) and the price (PUB-11). Workers research Valve''s current rules, draft the answers and values from the game as it is, and get them approved through pm decisions; the developer enters them in Steamworks. Owner: `plans/17-publishing.md` (PUB-9, PUB-11 rows, "Steamworks and store"); the values to paste live next to the other store fields in `plans/17a-store-page.md`. Steam only (`decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`): no other shops, no rating work for other platforms.

## Binding
- `decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): how is the game sold on Steam?`: paid one-time purchase, base $9.99 "for now; final check at PUB-11"; Valve''s regional matrix; launch discount; every bundle ships as free DLC, never paid; no paid DLC. D-98 in `plans/decisions.md`.
- `decision 67: Steamworks account holder (OQ-33): person or company?`: the app comes from decision 177 "Steamworks app created? App ID?" (`plan 129: Partner account, name check and AI terms (PUB-6, PUB-7, PUB-10)`); nothing here is entered before it.
- `decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)`: only `colombia` ships as DLC (es + en); its DLC app comes from `plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)` (decision 179 "Steamworks app configured (SW-7)? IDs?").
- AI disclosure: drafted in `plans/17a-store-page.md` "AI disclosure" (`task 667: AI disclosure text (Steam survey + store wording)`), approval pending in decision 180 "AI disclosure approved?". This plan rechecks the open points of that draft (field localized?, length limit, own survey per DLC) and enters the approved text with the survey; it doesn''t redraft it.
- Never phones home (masterplan rules): question reports only on the player''s click (`plan 103: Report server (POST /reports)`), telemetry opt-in only; say so where the survey asks about data or online features.
- Workers research and write; they never log into Steamworks, never contact Valve or a rating body. Unclear rules → a decision body for the developer.
- Valve''s pages change: every rule cited with URL and read date; an earlier worker''s "from memory" notes (decision 66, 17a "Valve''s rules", `plans/11-steam.md` "Launch (S6)" discount line) are rechecked, not copied.

## Tasks
1. **Content survey and age rating: research and draft (PUB-9)**
   - Read Valve''s current pages: partner.steamgames.com/doc/gettingstarted/contentsurvey, the mature-content / content-descriptor rules, the IARC page in Steamworks docs (what it costs, which regions show its ratings, whether Germany (USK) or other launch markets need it). Note URL + date.
   - Scan the game for what the survey asks (content descriptors: nudity/sexual content, violence/gore, general mature content, adult-only; plus whatever the current form asks, e.g. user-generated content, online interaction):
     - pool (`app/data/pool.json`, `app/data/bundles/colombia/`): questions on war, death, crime, drugs/alcohol, religion, sex; a throw-away script with keyword lists per language, counts and example ids
     - media: pictures that may show nudity (classical paintings and sculptures) or violence (war photos), via the media licence data''s Commons categories/restriction flags and the question text; list ids, no full manual audit
     - player-entered text: player names stay on the device and in Steam Cloud, never shown to others; Workshop mods (milestone 15, decision 135: creators pick per-item descriptors) if the form asks about user content; question reports (plan 103) send text only on the player''s click
     - no gambling, no purchases in the game, no chat
   - Write section "Content survey (PUB-9)" in `plans/17a-store-page.md` (after "AI disclosure"): Valve''s rules with sources; the scan''s findings (counts, examples); every survey question with the proposed answer and, where a descriptor is borderline (e.g. classical nudes, war history), the reasoning and the alternative; IARC: recommendation (get one or not) with the reason; DLC: whether `colombia` needs its own survey.
   - Recheck decision 180''s open points (description field localized or English only, length limit, own survey per DLC app); if one changes the AI draft (e.g. too long, English only), fix it in 17a "AI disclosure" and say so in the new decision''s body (decision 180 may still be pending; don''t touch it).
   - `pm decision add "Content survey answers approved? (PUB-9)"`: body = summary of the answers, the borderline items with options, the IARC recommendation, link to the 17a section; options: approved as drafted (recommended) / approved with IARC changed / fixes (list).
   - Done when: section written with sources; decision pending.

2. **Price, regional prices and launch discount: research and draft (PUB-11)**
   - Read Valve''s current pages: partner.steamgames.com/doc/store/pricing (regional pricing, the recommended matrix), /doc/marketing/discounts (launch discount: max %, length, setup deadline, cooldown after it, any rule against discounting soon after a price change), /doc/store/application/dlc (how a free DLC is priced and packaged). Note URL + date.
   - Comparable titles: recheck decision 66''s table (price, reviews, DLC model) on the store today; add 3–5 smaller family/party trivia games on Steam; one line on where $9.99 sits.
   - Regional prices for $9.99: Valve''s published recommendation for at least USD, EUR, GBP, MXN, COP, LATAM-USD (ARS etc.), CLP, PEN, CHF; if the matrix is only visible in the Steamworks pricing tool, write the developer''s step (accept Valve''s recommendation, read off these rows) instead of guessing numbers.
   - Launch discount proposal: % and length within Valve''s rules, and what it blocks afterwards (cooldown before e.g. a seasonal sale).
   - Write section "Price (PUB-11)" in `plans/17-publishing.md` (after "Steamworks and store"): sources, comparables, the regional rows, the launch discount, free DLC setup for `colombia` (and every later pack); fix `plans/11-steam.md` "Launch (S6)" → "Valve''s rules" discount line ("unverified") with the verified facts.
   - `pm decision add "Price, regional prices and launch discount? (PUB-11)"`: body = the summary; options: $9.99, Valve''s regional matrix, launch discount <x> % for <n> days (recommended) / other base price (state) / no launch discount.
   - Done when: section written with sources; decision pending.

3. **Entry checklist and the "entered" decision**
   - Runs after tasks 1 and 2; if decision 177 (App ID) isn''t answered yet, the checklist still gets written.
   - Checklist "Content survey and pricing: entry" in `plans/17a-store-page.md` (Steamworks page by page; Valve''s field names as found in tasks 1–2, "recheck at entry"):
     - content survey: answers per task 1''s approved decision; AI section from 17a "AI disclosure" once decision 180 is answered (approved variant); IARC if approved; per DLC app if Valve needs it
     - pricing: base package price $9.99 (or the approved value), regional prices, submit for Valve''s price approval if Valve requires it; `colombia` DLC free per task 2''s setup
     - launch discount: not entered now; the launch-day row in `plans/11-steam.md` "Launch-day checklist" (plan 95) points to PUB-11''s values
     - publish the Steamworks changes
   - `did=$(pm decision add "Content survey and prices entered in Steamworks? (PUB-9, PUB-11)" …)`: body = the checklist link; needs decisions 177, 179, 180 and tasks 1–2''s decisions answered first; report: survey submitted (date), IARC rating(s) received if any, base and regional prices entered (approved by Valve or pending), DLC free; options: entered (recommended) / not yet / issues (rows).
   - `pm task-pending-decision <task 4> $did`.
   - Done when: checklist written; decision pending; task 4 waits on it.

4. **Close-out of PUB-9 and PUB-11**
   - After the "entered" decision. Record the answers: rows in the 17a checklist `[x]`, IARC ratings in "Content survey (PUB-9)"; issues → follow-up tasks (wording in 17a → plan 88; a survey answer the game contradicts → the owning plan).
   - `plans/17-publishing.md`: PUB-9 and PUB-11 `[x]` with date and note; price bullet in "Steamworks and store" final; if the price differs from $9.99, D-98 in `plans/decisions.md` gets an amendment note and decision 66 a consequence (`pm decision consequences 66 …`).
   - `plans/project.md` S5 row in sync; `pm decision consequences` on tasks 1–3''s decisions.
   - Done when: PUB-9 and PUB-11 ticked; the launch discount waits only for the launch day (plan 95).

## Out of scope
- Store texts, capsules, screenshots, trailer (`plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)`); the AI disclosure wording itself (decision 180).
- Scheduling the launch discount and pressing Release (`plan 95: Launch`); later sales and discounts.
- Ratings outside Steam (consoles, mobile); paid DLC (decision 66: none).', '', '2026-10-14T21:55:25Z', 259);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (132, 10, 'Media bundle for shipping (SW-9)', 640, 'Part 6 of masterplan 10 (S5, SW-9): the content depot ships the media cache as is (1100 files, ~2.5 GB, 854 files over 1 MB, three WebM videos 27–90 MB). This plan turns the approved cache into a shipped bundle: images fit in 3840×2160 (D-48) as WebP, audio as Opus, video re-encoded, with a size budget per depot and a check that fails over budget or on a missing file. It extends the step that already builds the depot content, `app/desktop/stage-media.mjs` → `app/desktop/build/media/` + `build/pack-media.json` (plan 89 reads both), so depots, DLC split, smoke game and credits check keep working. Owner `plans/18-steam-integration.md` ("Platforms and display" → media size, "Builds and depots", SW-9); `plans/23-media-providers.md` gets a note.

## Depends on
- Plan 56 / plan 89: `stage-media.mjs` (pool URLs via `poolUrls`, names via `cacheName`, D-17; base vs pack-only media → `build/pack-media.json`, decision 66, decision 112), `trivia-desktop-build`, `trivia-steam stage` (DLC folders from `pack-media.json`), `trivia-release-check` step `media-budget` (today always skipped, names this task).
- Resolver: `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` `/media?url=` → `contained(media, cacheName(url))`; dev runs serve the raw cache (`TRIVIA_MEDIA` or `<repo>/media`), packaged builds `resources/media/`.
- Credits (plan 26, plan 92): `app/client/credits.ts` → `credits.json` / `CREDITS.md` from base + every pack pool; `authoring/steam/credits_check.mjs` matches `cacheName(file_url)` against `resources/media/`.
- Freesound: `decision 82: Freesound API for a paid Steam release (OQ-45): replace, ask, or family only?` → (a), D-103: no exclusion rule in the bundle; the 2 re-picks are `task 1051: Freesound: re-pick its 2 audio slots from Commons, drop it from the audio order`; the release check''s `licenses` step gates the rest. The bundle needs nothing extra.

## Decisions taken here
- **Where:** `stage-media.mjs` encodes (build tooling under `app/desktop/`, no `authoring/` imports, run by `trivia-desktop-build`); not `trivia-media` (`authoring/tools/media.py`, an authoring tool). SW-9''s "checked by `media.py`" changes to `stage-media.mjs --check`.
- **Formats** (Chromium/Electron plays all natively):
  - images (`.jpg .jpeg .png .webp`): fit inside 3840×2160, never upscaled (D-48), WebP lossy (`cwebp`, alpha kept), start q 82, step down to q 60 while > 1 MB; still > 1 MB = listed, not a failure
  - GIF and SVG: copied as is
  - audio (`.mp3 .ogg .oga .wav .flac .m4a`): Opus in Ogg, `.opus`, 96 kb/s (ffmpeg `libopus`)
  - video: WebM VP9 + Opus, at most 1920×1080, CRF ~33 (exact values by measurement in task 2; a TV question clip doesn''t need 4K)
  - AVIF not used: slower encode, no encoder in the shell, WebP is enough for the < 1 MB target
- **Names (one adapter, D-17 keys unchanged):** shipped name = `cacheName(url)`''s 16-hex stem + the shipped extension (`.webp`, `.opus`, `.webm`, else unchanged): `shippedName(url)` in `resolve.mjs`, deterministic, no manifest. The resolver tries `cacheName` first (raw cache in dev runs), then `shippedName` (packaged). `pack-media.json`, `credits_check.mjs` and `smoke.mjs` use `shippedName`.
- **Encode cache:** `work/ship-media/` (gitignored), file = `<stem>-<settings hash>.<ext>`, the settings hash covers tool versions + parameters; a rebuild re-encodes only new or changed files; `build/media/` gets hard links from it (copy fallback, as today). Parallel jobs (`os.availableParallelism()`).
- **Credits: one list, not split per DLC.** `credits.json` / `CREDITS.md` already cover base + every shipped pack and live in the OS depots; a pack''s lines with the pack not installed are harmless; no runtime filtering. "Exactly the shipped files" = the union of all depots, as `credits_check.mjs` checks today.
- **Budget:** `app/desktop/media-budget.json`: `{ "content": <MB>, "dlc": { "<pack>": <MB> }, "default_dlc": <MB>, "file": <MB> }`; numbers set in task 3 from the first full encode (measured + ~50 % headroom, rounded), noted in plan 18. Over a depot budget or a file over `file` (hard limit, e.g. 5 MB; videos their own limit) = ✗.
- D-entry (next free D number) with the above, in task 4.

## Tasks to split into
1. **Shipped names and the resolver adapter** — `shippedName(url)` beside `cacheName` in `app/desktop/resolve.mjs`; `/media` tries `cacheName` then `shippedName`; `credits_check.mjs`, `smoke.mjs` (if it names files) and `stage-media.mjs`''s `pack-media.json` use `shippedName`; `lib/types.ts` comment ("Packaged file: cacheName(file_url)") updated. Until task 2 lands, `stage-media.mjs` still links raw files, under the shipped name only where the extension doesn''t change (no behaviour change otherwise). Check: `resolve.test.mjs` case for both lookups; `trivia-desktop` dev run against the raw cache shows an image, audio and video question; `npm test`.
2. **Encode in stage-media** — images, audio, video per the formats above; encode cache `work/ship-media/`; `trivia-desktop-build` gets `pkgs.ffmpeg-headless` (libopus, libvpx) and `pkgs.libwebp` in `runtimeInputs` (`flake.nix`; nothing in `package.json`); `--allow-missing` as today; summary line: files, MB before → after, files still > 1 MB. Check: a full `trivia-desktop-build --dir`; `trivia-steam stage` passes; `node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs app/desktop/release/linux-unpacked` (image, audio, video question, no missing-media notice); throw-away visual check: 10 images (photos, a map, a PNG with text or alpha) at 1920×1080 side by side with the source, video playback in the shell; second build re-encodes nothing. Note sizes before/after in the task note.
3. **Budget and missing-file check** — `node app/desktop/stage-media.mjs --check` (no encoding): every pool URL (base + packs) has its file in `build/media/` (missing = ✗), per-depot totals (`content` = all minus `pack-media.json`''s, each pack its own) against `app/desktop/media-budget.json`, files over `file` listed (✗), files over 1 MB listed (info); exit 1 on ✗. `trivia-release-check` step `media-budget` runs it instead of skipping (`authoring/steam/release_check.py`, `MEDIA_BUDGET` text gone). Check: passes on the task-2 build; a budget set below the measured size fails; a file removed from `build/media/` fails.
4. **Docs and close-out (SW-9)** — plan 18: SW-9 `[x]` with date and files, "Platforms and display" media-size bullet (formats, budgets, measured sizes), "Builds and depots" (`trivia-desktop-build` encodes; `media-budget` step text; layout line), D-entry in `plans/decisions.md`; `plans/23-media-providers.md` note (shipped formats ≠ cache formats; keys unchanged); `plans/11-steam.md` install-size line; `plans/17a-store-page.md` depot sizes and storage (decision 90''s estimate re-measured from the new depots); `directory.md` (`work/ship-media/`, `media-budget.json`); `plans/project.md` in sync.

## Done when
- `trivia-desktop-build --dir` ships WebP/Opus/re-encoded WebM under the shipped names; images fit 3840×2160; the content and each DLC depot are within budget; the smoke game and `credits_check.mjs` pass.
- `trivia-release-check`''s `media-budget` step runs and fails over budget or on a missing file.
- Dev runs against the raw cache still play every media type.', '', '2026-10-14T22:12:22Z', 260);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (133, 5, 'No supply report on the Start screen', 400, 'Part 6 of `plan 5: masterplan` (milestone 5: Age groups and bundles in the game). Start shows `SupplyReport` («No hay suficientes preguntas para una partida completa…», GF-5) for `defaultChoice`, before any player, group or bundle is chosen: it checks a choice nobody made, and it confused the developer. Start never shows a supply report; the supply check stays on the Choice screen, where the choice is made. Runs before `plan 30: Play-test and close-out of age groups and bundles` (390), whose `task 479: Close out AG-7 and BN-6` waits on the repeated play-test.

## Today
- `app/client/src/game/Game.svelte`: `supply` state from `fetchGame()` (`refresh`, line ~160) and from a refused action''s `GameError.supply` (`request`, line ~263); passed to `S.Start` (line ~617).
- `app/client/src/game/screens/Start.svelte`: `supply` prop, `{#if supply}<SupplyReport {supply} />{/if}`, header comment names GF-5.
- `app/client/src/lib/api.ts` `fetchGame()` → `engine/api.ts` `getGame()`: `{ game, supply: game.supply(save, data) }`, a full supply matching on every refresh.
- Other readers of `getGame`''s `supply` (checked 2026-10-14):
  - `engine/game.test.ts`: fixture replay compares recorded `get_game` responses (Python recordings, `fixtures/game/*.json`, ~20 files with `supply`); the plan 65 test asserts `getGame(...).body.supply.ok`.
  - No other: `lib/engine.ts` `nextLocale` calls `game.supply` directly; `authoring/tools/supply.ts` uses `selection.supply`; desktop, achievements, `modding/` docs don''t read it.
- Choice screen (`game/screens/Choice.svelte`): own supply via `fetchChoice`, its `SupplyReport`, «¡A jugar!» disabled while short, `refused` (`GameError`, carries `supply`) for a refused `new`.

## Change
- `Start.svelte`: drop the `supply` prop, the `SupplyReport` import and markup, `Supply` type import, GF-5 in the comment.
- `Game.svelte`: drop the `supply` state, its `Supply` import if unused, `{supply}` on `S.Start`; `request` no longer sets it from `GameError.supply` (a refused `new` shows on the Choice screen via `refused`; mid-game `settings` refusals stay in `GameSettings.svelte`).
- `getGame` / `fetchGame`: drop `supply` (no reader left; saves a matching per refresh): `Reply<{ game: Game | null }>`, `Promise<{ game: Game | null }>`; doc comment "view first, then supply" updated.
  - `game.test.ts` replay: strip `supply` from recorded `get_game` bodies always (as it already does when `seen` is set); fixtures stay untouched.
  - Plan 65 test: `game.supply(save, d).ok` instead of `getGame(...).body.supply.ok`.
- Stays: `GameError.supply`, `errors.ts` `supply_short`, `SupplyReport.svelte` (Choice), `SupplyNotice` unchanged (`decision 31: Low-supply warning: below how many fresh games left (K) should the game start warn?`), `nextLocale`''s supply check (`decision 156: One language for UI and questions`).

## Specs and docs
- `plans/03-game-flow.md`: "Supply check" bullet: the Choice screen (not Start) reports which levels lack questions; GF-5''s note: `GET /api/game` → `supply` on Start retired, the check lives on the Choice screen (this plan).
- `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` "Start": one bullet: no supply report; the supply check is on the Choice screen ("Choice" section already says so).
- `directory.md`: `Start.svelte` entry without `SupplyReport`; `SupplyReport.svelte` entry: Choice screen.
- `trivia-gallery`: drop the `start-supply-report` shot (`authoring/tools/gallery.py` `start()` and the shot list), keep `choice-supply-report`; `authoring/tools/gallery_saves.mjs` comment of `saves.blocked`: Choice only.

## Checks
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`.
- Browser (`TRIVIA_MUTE=1`, `npm run dev -w app/client`, `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` with every question blocked, e.g. the gallery''s `blocked` save): Start shows no report; «¡Jugar!» → player → Choice shows the report, «¡A jugar!» disabled; by mouse and keyboard (IN-1).
- `trivia-gallery --only choice-supply-report` still shoots.

## Tasks
- One task: the change, specs, docs and gallery above (small, one commit).', '', '2026-10-14T23:12:01Z', 1061);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (134, 10, 'Beta test and S5 close-out', 130, 'The last step of milestone 10 (S5), part 11 of masterplan 10. Once the first `beta` upload (with the free `colombia` DLC depot) exists, this plan gives the developer one beta-test checklist: install from Steam on a second machine, play with the network off, Cloud to another machine, and the no-Steam-user case. It records the result through a pm decision and brings the docs in line. Workers have no Steam account, second machine or Deck: they write the checklist and record results, they never tick a row themselves. Docs and pm only, no code: failures become tasks in the owning plans.

## Binding
- decision 111: Steam only: the beta test covers the Steam-launched build (Windows, Linux/SteamOS). The only "no Steam" rows are the milestone''s own check: with no valid Steam user nothing persists and flags are off.
- decision 39: Local builds start offline?: the plain-artefact start test was skipped. This beta test is the clean-machine start test: second machine, no dev setup, network off. Plan 18''s "Local build start test" tables stay as they are; their result line points here.
- decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): bundles ship as free DLC with optional install. The test installs the `colombia` DLC and uninstalls it again.
- decision 67: Steamworks account holder (OQ-33): a person, so the developer''s own Steam account owns the app. A second account (family member, beta key or Family Sharing) is optional; rows that need one are optional.
- decision 82: Freesound API for a paid Steam release (OQ-45): the beta build must not carry the 2 Freesound picks. The release check''s `licenses` step on the uploaded build covers this (`task 1051: Freesound: re-pick its 2 audio slots from Commons, drop it from the audio order`). The checklist intro states that step''s result; no row of its own.
- decision 125: Steam Deck: best effort, review without a Deck at hand: plan 90 (Steam Deck review and Deck test (SW-12)) owns the review request and its result. They count toward close-out. The real-Deck test doesn''t count and stays open for when a Deck is at hand. The second machine is a PC, not a Deck.
- decision 86: Release check fails on licences and the release bar: the family beta may be uploaded with `--skip quality`. The intro names the skipped steps from the build description.
- decision 174: Store requirements: beta test distro and real-pad run?: the checklist records the Linux distro the beta ran on and whether the pad-only run passed. The developer answers decision 174 from that; workers don''t.

## Reuse, don''t copy
- Steam Cloud: plan 87''s "Steam Cloud test" table in `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (decision 75: Steam Cloud test passed?). Not copied. If decision 75 is still pending, the beta test fills that table in the same session and the developer answers both. If it already passed, the beta row only checks Cloud A → B on the beta install.
- Real-Deck rows: plan 90''s "Real-Deck test (later)", not here.
- Release check manual rows (`offline`, `cloud`, `signoff`, `deck`, … in `authoring/steam/release_check.py`, steps in `plans/11-steam.md` "Release checklist (ST-4)"): this beta test answers them for the uploaded build. The section names the `release-check.md` it used; no new rows in the tool.
- Plan 48 (S3 close-out and platform test) rows (controller only, jokers, glyphs, media, peek, credits): the beta checklist names them as one row, "plan 48''s per-platform rows, on the Steam install", and doesn''t repeat them.

## Depends on (guard at the start of each task)
- Task 1: `task 682: Record the first beta upload` done: a `beta` build exists, including the `colombia` DLC depot. Also `decision 179: Steamworks app configured (SW-7)? IDs?` answered (Cloud values, Steam Input default, Linux runtime) and `task 650: Package the Steam binding in both builds` done.
- Task 3: every other milestone-10 plan done. Rules:
  - A remaining task that waits on a pending decision → `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <that decision>`, stop.
  - Task 673 (Store media: en and de question shots and trailers once their pools land) or another task that only waits for milestone 9 content: `pm decision add "S5 close-out: wait for <task> or carry it over?"`, options `close S5 without it (the task stays in plan 88; noted in plan 11)`, `wait`. This task waits on it.
  - Any other open task → stop without changes and say so.
- Guard: `pm show` of this plan and `pm plans list`. Never drop or edit tasks of other plans. This plan doesn''t set the milestone status: pm''s post-milestone cleanup does.

## The checklist
- New section "S5 beta test" in `plans/18-steam-integration.md`, after "Steam Cloud test". Intro lines:
  - BuildID and tag (`v<version>`) from `task 682`''s note, and the `release-check.md` path
  - release check steps skipped (decision 86)
  - result of the `licenses` step (decision 82)
  - date
  - machines: second machine OS, and Linux distro + version if Linux (decision 174)
  - Steam account used
- One table per machine: check, result (pass / fail / skipped + reason), note.
- Second machine (no dev setup, never had the game; Windows or Linux):
  - Steam → Library → Trivia → Properties → Betas → `beta` with the password; install the base and the `colombia` DLC
  - network off, Steam in offline mode, launch from the Library: no warning, no launcher, fullscreen, no console window
  - the language is preselected from Steam''s language; the player confirms it
  - telemetry consent screen: decline; with the network off, an accept doesn''t hang either
  - the family plays a full game to level 12 or a loss with a pad only; the bundle selector offers «Regional: Colombia»
  - plan 48''s per-platform rows on the Steam install: jokers, glyphs, image/audio/video questions with sound, image peek, credits
  - quit and relaunch: players and seen counts still there
  - flag a question offline: the flag action is present, sending fails cleanly, the copy fallback works (release check `offline` row)
  - overlay with Shift+Tab (Windows only, decision 70)
  - floating keyboard for a new player''s name (Big Picture)
  - an achievement toast once Steamworks has them (decision 140); optional
  - uninstall the `colombia` DLC → relaunch: no Colombia bundle offered, no error; reinstall → offered again
- Cloud: Cloud A → B on the beta install (or plan 87''s table, see "Reuse"); network back on before the sync.
- No valid Steam user (decision 111), on either machine: start the installed build with Steam not running (Linux `./trivia`, Windows `Trivia.exe` from the install folder):
  - full game
  - «Sin Steam no se guarda el progreso» notice
  - no flag action
  - nothing new under the save folder
  - the plan 87 table''s row, if decision 75 is open
- Optional: a second Steam account or Family Sharing borrower → own save. Family save via `--import-save` on the family machine (README; Steam launch option or the exe from the install folder): players and seen counts shown.

## Tasks
1. **Beta checklist and the test decision**
   - Guard (task 1 above). Write "S5 beta test" in plan 18 as above, results empty.
   - Point the "Local build start test" result line at this section.
   - Worker-side: read `task 682`''s note and the build''s `release-check.md`; fill the intro. If a prerequisite is missing or the release check failed: note it, `pm task add` in the owning plan, stop without the decision.
   - `did=$(pm decision add "S5 beta test passed?" --body - …)`. The body holds:
     - the whole checklist (tables as Markdown)
     - the BuildID, tag and branch (never the password)
     - how to switch to `beta` and install the DLC
     - how to start without Steam
     - how to report: copy the tables, fill result and note; "skipped" needs a reason; name the Linux distro
     - a reminder to answer decision 75 too if it''s still pending
   - Options: `passed`, `passed with minor issues (list them; they go to the backlog)`, `failed (list the failing rows)`.
   - `pm task-pending-decision` for tasks 2 and 3 on `did`.
   - Done when: the section exists, the decision is pending, and tasks 2 and 3 wait for it.
2. **Record the beta result**
   - Copy the reported results into the tables (date, BuildID).
   - `passed`: done. In the note, say that decision 174 and the release check''s manual rows can be answered now.
   - `passed with minor issues`: each issue goes into `plans/backlog.md` with the owning plan file''s ID prefix.
   - `failed`: per failing row, `pm task add` in the owning plan, with the row, the note and repro steps, at that plan''s priority. Owners: 85 binding/overlay/keyboard/language, 87 saves/Cloud/notice, 89 builds/depots/upload, 130 Steamworks values, 132 media, 86 achievements, 93 flags, 113 peek, 45/46 input; if the owner is done, the task goes in this plan. Then a new decision "S5 beta re-test passed?" with only the failed rows plus the full-game row, and this task and task 3 pending on it. Stage and stop without closing. Repeat until passed.
   - A finding that settles something (e.g. the Linux runtime) → D-entry in `plans/decisions.md`, `pm decision record`.
   - Done when: every non-optional row shows pass.
3. **S5 docs close-out** (after task 2; guard for task 3 above)
   - `plans/11-steam.md`: S5 row in the phases table marked done with date and a link to "S5 beta test". In the Launch (S6) gate table, the row "Beta test passed (masterplan 10 part 11)" ✓ with the date.
   - Deferred, each with a dated note:
     - SW-13 Remote Play Together: after IN-6, not in S5
     - SW-14 macOS: later; developer account, notarization
     - online co-op: later (decision 111), "eventually, not planned"
     - set in plan 18''s Tasks list and in `plans/11-steam.md`
   - `plans/18-steam-integration.md`:
     - SW-6, SW-7, SW-10 `[x]` with notes, if their plans left them open (check, don''t redo, the parts'' own ticks)
     - SW-12 as plan 90 left it: Valve''s result, or "review in S6"; real-Deck test pending a Deck (decision 125)
     - status line `stub` → `draft`, or `agreed` where S5 settled everything
   - `plans/17-publishing.md` (PUB-6..PUB-11), `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` (LUI-6), `plans/14-input.md` (Steam Input default, Deck line): ticks checked, status lines brought up to date. `plans/README.md` status column to match.
   - `plans/project.md` "Steam track": an S5 done line (date, beta BuildID, link), every S5 item ticked there too, open-question rows S5 resolved removed.
   - Masterplan 11 (`plan 11: masterplan`, milestone 11): if S5 changed S6''s scope, add a short dated note with `pm plan edit 11 --body -`. Examples: Deck review moved to S6, a task carried over (task 673), Linux distro / pad-run facts for decision 90''s final values, a DLC finding.
   - Done when: the milestone''s "Done when" holds and is cited in the task note:
     - the beta installed from Steam on a second machine and played by the family
     - without a Steam user nothing persists and flags are off
     - with one, saves sync through Steam Cloud (decision 75 or the beta Cloud row)
     - the Deck review requested and its result (or the S6 deferral) noted in plan 18
     - `qgen validate` unaffected

## Out of scope
- Running the real-Deck test (plan 90, decision 125); fixing failures (tasks in the owning plans); the release candidate and launch (milestone 11, plan 95); Workshop and mod checks (plans 114, 119, 122).', '', '2026-10-14T23:38:50Z', 263);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (135, 6, 'Playful icons and language flags before a game session', 400, 'Part 4 of `plan 6: masterplan`: every button on the screens before a game session gets a playful VD-8 icon, and the languages show national flags instead of decision 157''s globe (developer, 2026-10-14). Pure client UI: `app/client/src/game/`, no engine, save or catalog change.

