INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (150, 6, 'Start screen horizon', 300, 'Part 5 of `plan 6: masterplan`: the bottom third of Start shows a colourful horizon, a row of overlapping Commons cut-outs (landmarks, animals, objects from many topics and regions) like a skyline (developer, 2026-10-16). Shipped as app assets with their own credits, the same in every language; the developer approves the picks before anything ships, then the result in the screen gallery.

## Picks (decision first)
- Wikimedia Commons only, D-45 allowlist (CC0, PD, CC BY, CC BY-SA, as in the allowlist); GFDL-only no; prefer files already cut out (PNG/SVG with alpha); a photo without alpha only if the cut-out exists as a derivative on Commons (credited as such)
- 12–20 candidates, one fixed set for every language: spread over continents (Africa, Americas north and south, Asia, Europe, Oceania) and topics (landmark, animal, plant, object, vehicle, instrument); no flags, text, logos, people''s faces, religious or political symbols; nothing that marks one country as "ours" (no Colombia/Spain/Germany favourite; Colombia at most one item like any other country)
- Silhouette variety: tall (tower, giraffe), wide (bridge, bus), small (teapot, cactus), so the row reads as a skyline
- Pick task (`--web`): downloads candidates to `work/horizon/candidates/` (originals, kept for the build), contact sheet `work/horizon/contact-sheet.png` (imagemagick `montage`, number + short name per tile, on `--night-800`), raises `pm decision add` (once) listing per candidate: number, file page URL, author, licence, why; options "approve all", "approve with changes (list numbers to drop/replace)"; makes the build tasks pending on it (`pm task-pending-decision`)
- Nothing ships before the answer; replacements the developer asks for: the build task picks them under the same rules and lists them in its note

## Assets and credits
- `app/client/public/horizon/` (committed, like `public/audio/`): `<slug>.webp` with alpha, ASCII kebab-case names (e.g. `giraffe.webp`); height 360 px (1080p band ≈ 360 px; no upscaling: a smaller source stays its size), quality ~80, each ≤ 150 KB, the set ≤ 2 MB
- Encode: imagemagick from the dev shell (`magick … -resize x360 -quality 80 x.webp`, alpha kept, metadata stripped); a one-off, not part of `stage-media.mjs` (decision 185 covers the media depots; its WebP choice applies, its 3840×2160 fit doesn''t); the command goes into the CREDITS.md intro
- `app/client/public/horizon/CREDITS.md`: same table as `public/audio/CREDITS.md` (`File | Used for | Source | Author | Licence`; "Used for": what it shows, e.g. "Giraffe, Kenya"); note "cut-out/resized from …" for adaptations (CC BY-SA: the adaptation stays CC BY-SA)
- `app/client/credits.ts`: generalize `sounds()` into one reader for a `public/<dir>/CREDITS.md` table (import, don''t copy, decision 199); `Credits` gets `horizon: { entries, … }` like `sounds`; shipped `CREDITS.md` gets a "Start screen images" section; both ways: a file without a row or a row without a file throws
- `Credits.svelte`: a section like the sounds'' with a new key `credits.horizon` («Imágenes de la pantalla de inicio», all four catalogs, `locales/style/<locale>.md` read first)
- `authoring/steam/credits_check.mjs`: `resources/client/horizon/*.webp` against `credits.horizon.entries`, both ways; the summary line counts them
- Budget: new key `"horizon": 2` (MB, the set) and per file `file` (5 MB, existing) in `app/desktop/media-budget.json`; `stage-media.mjs --check` (release check `media-budget` step) sums `app/client/public/horizon/` against it

## Look and layout
- New `app/client/src/game/Horizon.svelte`, used only by `screens/Start.svelte`: `aria-hidden`, `pointer-events: none`, absolute along the bottom, height `min(33.3vh, …)`, behind the content (title, buttons, notice, held line, language button stay on top and clickable)
- Images in a fixed order from a list in the component (file, height share 0.55–1, horizontal overlap ~25 %), spread so no region clusters; the row spans the full width at 16:9 and 16:10 (overflow cut at the edges, never squeezed)
- Palette (`plans/10-visual-design.md`): natural colours, slightly lowered saturation (`filter: saturate(0.85)`) so amber stays the strongest colour; a soft ground glow along the bottom (amber/coral/sky tokens at low alpha), the top edge fades into `--night-800` (mask gradient); tokens only, no raw hex (VD-2)
- Motion: each item bobs gently (≤ 0.4 `--u`, 6–9 s, staggered); off under `prefers-reduced-motion` (theme.css''s rule already stops `.game` animations; check it does)
- Readability: title, subtitle, buttons, save notice, mods button and held line, language button readable at 1920 × 1080 and 1280 × 800, all four catalogs (de longest); if the buttons sit over the band, the band goes lower/shorter, never the other way round; no change to keys, focus, prompts, catalogs of Start
- Only on Start (not Language, Credits or Mods overlays above it, which cover it as they do now)

## Check and approval
- `trivia-gallery --only start,start-resume,start-save-notice,language-from-start,credits` for all four locales; the gallery has no size option: add `--size WxH` (default 1920x1080; other sizes write `work/gallery/<locale>@<W>x<H>/`) and run it at 1280x800 as well
- Developer decision (once): approve the horizon in `/gallery` (like `plan 135: Playful icons and language flags before a game session`''s review); a fix task waits on it
- Per commit: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`

## Docs
- `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` "Start": the horizon line
- `plans/10-visual-design.md`: a VD entry for the horizon (sources, look, motion)
- `directory.md`: no new top-level dir; `public/horizon/` only if the file lists `public/audio/`
- `plans/project.md` / milestone 6 Done-when line: left to the close-out

## Constraints
- D-45 licences only; nothing fetched at runtime; no new npm or Python dependencies (imagemagick and cwebp are already in the shells)', '', '2026-10-16T13:48:49Z', 1325);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (151, 8, 'Bundle selection on its own full screen', 400, 'Part 11 of `plan 8: masterplan` (developer''s gallery flags of 2026-10-16): the question bundles get a full screen of their own in both modes, the base bundle an explicit name in every UI language. Done: own screen, base names, country field and flags, region order, flow after Choice with the supply report on Bundles (tasks 1338, 1339, 1350, 1351, 1360). The developer''s second review (`decision 264: Bundle screen (two columns) reviewed in /gallery?`) set the layout; the milestone edit of 2026-10-16 (later the same day) then allowed any bundle combination: base bundle(s) are toggle tiles like the optional ones, preset on, base off or nothing selected allowed on screen, start enabled only when the selection has questions. This revision adds that work (engine, selector, start check, docs) and changes the layout''s base column; no separate fix plan.

## Binding
- `decision 158: Bundle selection in every mode, apart from customization`: "own section" → "own screen"; never part of «Personalizar partida», not counted in `customized`, preset = `playerChoice` (newest game''s bundles, else the locale''s first base bundle, non-base off): the preset keeps the base bundle on
- `decision 264: Bundle screen (two columns) reviewed in /gallery?` (supersedes `decision 260: Bundle screen: where it sits, supply report, in-game settings`): flow, layout, highlighting, counts, supply report per milestone 8''s bundle-screen line; its "base bundle info only" is replaced by toggle tiles (milestone edit)
  - from decision 260 still holds: shown in both modes, also with one offered bundle; «Ajustes de la partida» (`GameSettings.svelte`, MD-12) keeps `BundleSelector` (compact, with descriptions)
- Milestone 8''s any-combination line (developer, 2026-10-16) supersedes:
  - `decision 269: Bundle screen: a mod''s extra base bundle` (info-only single base tile, radio tiles for two or more): every base bundle is a toggle tile
  - "exactly one base bundle" of `decision 38: Base bundles and bundle languages` / D-85, BN-6 as closed under `decision 155: Play-test of age groups and bundles (again, after the decision 50 fixes)`, and the engine''s `base_bundle_count` refusal
  - still holds from decision 38: `kind: base`, bundles offered per `languages` (`bundle_not_offered`), the locale''s first base bundle as default, stored choices that no longer resolve read as defaults (never written back); `qgen validate`''s "each launch language has a base bundle"
- `decision 206: Play-test: no supply report on Start, report on the Choice screen only`: "Choice screen" → bundle screen (decision 264); Start still shows none; record with `pm decision consequences 206` if task 1360 didn''t
- `decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings`: shipped bundles fixed «5000+» (base) / «2000+» (others); mod bundles their own count from the loaded pool, rounded down, capped at their kind''s string
- `decision 268: Short-group marks after the flow change`: Choice shows no supply information; the bundle screen''s report covers the chosen group; no per-group marks
- `decision 261: Name of the base bundle per UI language (not «Basics»)`: «Paquete básico», «Base bundle», «Grundpaket» (applied)
- `decision 263: Bundle screen reviewed in /gallery?`: country flags, region order, names only (done in tasks 1350, 1351)
- `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles`: the term "question bundle" holds

## Done (tasks 1338, 1339, 1350, 1351, 1360; stays)
- `app/client/src/game/screens/Bundles.svelte`, scope `bundles`, letters via `bundleKeys` (`BundleSelector.svelte` module script, displayed order), pick kept in `Game.svelte`, `"Bundles"` in `SCREENS` (`lib/mods.ts`)
- Base names in `bundles.json`, `names.{en,de}.json`, style guides
- `country` (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, required for `kind: region` only): `bundles.json` (colombia `CO`), `qgen validate`, `qgen bundle new --country`, `mods.mjs` / `check-mod.mjs`, client loader, `modding/` docs, `ChoiceOptions["bundles"]` (`region`, `country`)
- Flags: `Flags.svelte` single-country mode, regional icon = flag wherever a bundle shows an icon (globe for undrawn countries), no pin
- Region: `app.getLocaleCountryCode()` → `preload.cjs` → `lib/desktop.ts` `playerRegion`; browser fallback `navigator.language`; `?region=XX` / `?region=`
- Order: `orderBundles` (player''s region first, non-regional, other regions; `bundles.json` order then mods); base bundles `bundles.json` order, mods after
- Flow (task 1360): Player → Choice («Seguir», no bundle line, no supply) → Bundles («¡A jugar!», through `SupplyNotice`) → Level in both modes; Back from Bundles → Choice, both picks kept; supply of the full choice on every toggle, `SupplyReport` and refusals on Bundles; walkers (gallery, smoke, screenshots, trailer) follow it
- Scroll with fade and focus follow (`data-nav-scroll` in `lib/focus.ts`); the mechanism stays for the flowing tile area

## Any combination (engine, selector, start check)
- Engine (`engine/choice.ts` `resolveBundles`, its callers in `new`, `settings`, defaults): drop the base count check and `base_bundle_count`; offered/unknown checks stay; a list without a base bundle resolves as given
  - the supply of a selection (`outlook`/supply calls the bundle screen makes) works for any list, `[]` included: 0 questions, not an error
  - `new` and in-game `settings`: a selection with no question for the choice (e.g. `[]`) is refused with a new code (e.g. `no_questions`) replacing `base_bundle_count`; the existing supply refusal stays for short-but-nonzero
  - stored choices keep loading: every list valid before (exactly one base) stays valid; `playerChoice` of an old save unchanged
  - `engine/*.test.ts`: the `base_bundle_count` cases become the new refusal / base-off acceptance (keep it few, AGENTS.md)
- `BundleSelector.svelte`: `toggled` toggles every bundle (no radio replacement); base tiles `role="switch"` like the others; compact mode in «Ajustes de la partida» the same
- Client guards on exactly one base bundle go (`Bundles.svelte` `reason`, `Game.svelte`, `lib/types.ts` / `lib/api.ts` comments)
- Start check on Bundles: count the questions of the selected bundles for Choice''s age group (or custom range) and levels, from the supply already fetched on every toggle (no second engine path, decision 199); > 0 → «¡A jugar!» enabled (unless the supply report says short, as today); 0 → disabled with a short reason under the buttons (e.g. «Ningún paquete elegido tiene preguntas para esta partida»; catalogs `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`; `locales/style/<locale>.md` first, the de guide''s `base_bundle_count` line updated); nothing selected shows the same reason
- Error catalogs: `error.base_bundle_count` out of `es.ts`, `en.ts`, `de.ts` (and `es-ES` if it has one), `state.ts`; the new code in
- Achievements and «Cambiazo» groups with the base bundle off: whatever reads "the" base bundle of a game (`rg "kind === \"base\""` in `engine/`, `lib/`) works with none; achievements tied to the base bundle simply don''t fire

## Layout (replaces task 1351''s two equal columns)
- Left: base column, narrow (as little width as its tile needs); its tile(s) toggle tiles like the optional ones (focusable, letter keys, same highlighting), preset on; no heading «Elijan uno», no pick prompt; a mod''s extra base bundles stack in the same column
- A vertical ruler between the base column and the optional area
- Right: optional bundles as fixed-width tiles flowing into rows and columns (CSS grid, `auto-fill`); the area scrolls when they don''t fit (wheel, touch); fade at a cut edge; the focused tile always in view
- 2D focus: arrows / D-pad move between tiles in rows and columns and across the ruler (`lib/focus.ts` spatial nav), down from the last row to the buttons; letters toggle and scroll into view; default focus as today
- Tiles: icon (flag for regional), name, count (decision 267); no descriptions; no column headings unless a short one is needed for the optional area (catalogs, all four locales, style guides first)
- Highlighting (base and optional alike): hover/focus a clear ring or lift; selected-for-this-game clearly different (filled tile in the accent colour plus a check mark), not only a small «activado» line; both visible at once on a focused selected tile
- Counts: shipped bundles from catalog strings («5000+», «2000+»; number formatting per locale); mod bundles counted from the pool the client loaded for the UI language (`lib/data.ts` / engine data), rounded per decision 267
- Order: `orderBundles` as done
- Fits at 1280×800, 1280×720 and 1920×1080 (`plan 46: Deck layout and controller-only text entry (SW-4)`) with 1 and ~15 optional bundles, one and two base bundles, with and without a supply report or the start reason
- «Ajustes de la partida»: compact selector with descriptions, order and flags unchanged; counts there only if cheap

## Docs
- `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md`: Bundles layout (toggle base tiles, ruler, flowing tiles), start check and its reason; drop "one-of-N tiles, exactly one selected" and "zero or two base bundles"
- `plans/22-bundles.md`: any combination (lines 11, 67, 79 today), counts (decision 267), base column; BN-6 note amended (any combination, 2026-10-16)
- `plans/13-game-modes.md` (bundles line: radio group, `base_bundle_count`), `plans/14-input.md` (scope `bundles`, 2D focus), `plans/project.md` (BN-6 "exactly one base bundle")
- `plans/decisions.md`: D-85 and D-97 amended (any combination, start check, counts); D-entry of decision 206 if it has one
- `README.md` line on bundles ("picks one base bundle"): any combination, Choice before Bundles
- `modding/README.md`, `modding/bundles.md`: a mod''s base bundle is a tile that toggles like any other, preset off (ours stays the preset); count shown for mod bundles
- Code comments: `BundleSelector.svelte`, `Bundles.svelte`, `engine/choice.ts`, `lib/types.ts`, `lib/api.ts`; `code-review.md`''s `BundleSelector` row
- `rg` "exactly one base", "base_bundle_count", "radio", "one-of-N", "Elijan uno", "one tile per row", "two columns", "Player → Bundles → Choice" over code comments, plan files and `.md` files; fix hits (decision 200)
- Decisions: `pm decision consequences 269` (superseded by the milestone''s any-combination line: toggle tiles, no radio), `pm decision consequences 155` (BN-6''s "exactly one base bundle" dropped, `base_bundle_count` gone, the new refusal), `pm decision consequences 38` likewise

## Check
- Node dev server (`npm run dev -w app/client`) at 1280×800 and 1920×1080, both modes, pad (or forced `device: "gamepad"`) and keys: Player → Choice («Seguir») → Bundles (toggle colombia) → start; Back to Choice and forward keeps both picks
- Base off + colombia on starts a game that plays colombia only; everything off → start disabled with the reason; base on alone as before; an old save (`blocked` demo or the family''s imported save) loads its stored bundles
- «Ajustes de la partida» in a running game: base off accepted when the rest has questions; an empty selection refused with the reason
- Blocked save (as the gallery''s `blocked`): report and disabled start on Bundles, none on Choice; running-out notice from Bundles
- ~15 fake mod bundles (throw-away mod folder, one a second base bundle, regional with drawn and undrawn countries, small ones for counts): tiles flow, the area scrolls, focus in view with arrows, pad and letters, both base tiles toggle; counts per decision 267
- Order with `?region=CO`, `?region=`, `?region=DE`
- Per commit: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`

## Tasks (suggested)
1–4, 5. Done: tasks 1338, 1339, 1350, 1351, 1360
6. New: Any bundle combination: engine without `base_bundle_count`, toggle base tiles in `BundleSelector`, start check with reason on Bundles, catalogs, docs and decision consequences above (priority 410, before the layout)
7. `task 1361: Bundle screen layout: narrow base column, ruler, flowing tiles, highlighting, counts` (after 6): body revised: base column with toggle tiles (no info-only tile, no radio tiles, no wait on decision 269), 2D focus across the ruler, the fit rows above
8. `task 1340: Gallery run of the flowing-tile bundle screen and developer review` (after 7): as listed, plus a shot or note for base off / nothing selected (start reason) if the gallery can set it; consequences of decisions 263 and 264; a new review decision like decision 264

## Done when
- The milestone''s bundle-screen line holds: flow Player → Choice («Seguir») → Bundles → Level in both modes; narrow base column with toggle tiles, any combination with the start check, ruler, flowing tiles with scroll and focus follow, clear focus and selected states, counts, region order, country flags, names only, supply report and notice on Bundles
- No `base_bundle_count` left; owning plan files, `modding/` docs, README and D-85 / D-97 updated; consequences on decisions 38, 155, 206, 263, 264, 269; the new review decision answered "approved"', 'Before a game starts, players pick which sets of questions to play: the general set plus optional extras, such as questions for people with ties to Colombia. These sets have a full screen of their own, after the age-group choice, so it can warn when the picked sets run short. Every set, the general one included, is now a tile that can be switched on or off, so a family can play only the extras if they like; the game only refuses to start when the picked sets hold no questions at all. The extras flow across the screen as tiles with a flag or icon, a question count and a clear look when picked, and the list stays easy to use with a game controller as player-made sets are added.', '2026-10-16T13:54:45Z', 1335);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (152, 16, 'masterplan', 1000, 'Masterplan of milestone 16: Local multiplayer: game modes and controls. Its own tasks are not implementation work: each of them writes the plan for one part below (`pm plan add 16 …` with the priority given), and that plan''s split makes the work tasks.

## Ground rules
- The milestone is the spec; it replaces milestone 7''s multiplayer sections, `decision 23: Competitive format (OQ-37)?` and `decision 24: Multiplayer input and couch co-op (OQ-37)?` where they differ, and every "Later" for MD-8, MD-9, IN-6
- Rules shared by the three modes as in `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Modes" (no skip, undo, joker changes; flag only logs, `decision 60: One mechanism for questions with problems: flag or report?`; achievements unless customized, `decision 19`, `decision 74: Gamemaster mode earns no achievements`)
- Gamemaster mode and «Solo o en grupo» unchanged, controls too (`plan 156: Prompts follow the last input` finishes milestone 8''s rule: every device drives the one player)
- Steam only (`decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`); local only, no phones, no network (D-77)
- `milestone 17: Remote Play Together` builds on this: a remote guest is one more pad; keep the player binding device-agnostic (a pad index, the keyboard-and-mouse player), no Remote Play code here

## Decisions for the developer (raised by task 1353)
- `decision 273: Keyboard-only turn-based sessions: what does a player''s own key do?`: parts 5, 6
- `decision 274: Pads plus keyboard: one keyboard player, or several key players?`: parts 5, 6
- `decision 275: Timed mode, keyboard-only: how does the claimer answer in the 6 seconds?`: parts 5, 8
- `decision 276: Timed mode: after a drop-out, how many questions does a round have?`: part 3 (and part 4''s outlook)
- The split links each part''s plan task to the decisions named here (`pm task-pending-decision`); the others don''t wait

## Parts

### 1. Session model and save format (priority 900)
- Today: one `GameRow` per game, one `player_id`, one `GameState` (`engine/state.ts`); `getGame` finds the one running game
- Design a multiplayer session: players in join order (save player rows: names picked or created on the join screen), mode, shared settings (bundles, locale; age group per mode), per-player state where the mode needs it (`rr-competitive`: own level, jokers, age group; `timed`: lives, out), turn or round pointer; how it maps onto `games[]` (one row per session with `players[]`, or one row per player plus a session id): pick the one that keeps stats, flags, achievements, telemetry and `qgen report --played` readers simplest, record it (`pm decision record`)
- `SAVE_VERSION` bump if the shape changes: `engine/save.ts` `UPGRADES`, `authoring/tools/save_file.py` (and `app/server/save.py` while it lives, `plan 99: Retire the browser game and the Python game server`); old saves and the fixture replay unchanged
- Seen events (D-82): every question shown in a session counts for the save, as solo does
- Engine API shape for multiplayer actions: every action carries the acting player; the engine refuses an action from a player whose turn or claim it isn''t (`not_your_turn`, …), so input bugs can''t cheat
- Done: types, save round-trip, `parseSave` upgrade; no mode logic yet

### 2. Round-robin modes in the engine (priority 600)
- `rr-coop`: one team game, turns in join order (one question each), one age group, one shared `STANDARD_JOKERS` set usable by whoever''s turn it is, wrong answer ends the game for all, level 12 = all win
- `rr-competitive`: per player own game, level, standard jokers, age group; turns in join order skipping players who are out; wrong answer ends only that player; first to level 12 wins (ends the session); last one standing: settle in the plan (wins or plays on) and record it
- Selection per player (`selection.draw`, ranges per age group), supply check (GF-5) and outlook for the whole session
- `view()` for the screens: whose turn, each player''s level, jokers, status
- Engine tests only where they stay useful (AGENTS.md); fixture replay unchanged

### 3. Competitive (timed) in the engine (priority 590, `--model opus` for the core)
- As the milestone specs: 12 rounds = levels, one age group, no jokers, questions per round per `decision 276`
- Time without timers in the engine: actions carry a timestamp (the `Io` clock); the engine derives hints shown (every 8 s), the 30 s expiry and the 6 s claim expiry from timestamps; the client sends `tick`/`expire` and the engine checks them, so a reload or a slow frame can''t change the outcome
- `claim {player}`, `answer {player, index}`; claim timeout = wrong; wrong = out; round end: no correct answer in it = −1 life, third lost = out; round 12 sudden death (first correct wins); one player left wins; edge cases to settle and record: everyone out in one round end, round 12 exhausted with no correct answer, the Esc menu or the Steam overlay open during a question (pause or not; D-92 says nothing pauses because no timer exists outside `timed`)
- Seen events per question shown, claimed or not

### 4. Engine consumers (priority 580)
- Achievements (`engine/achievements.ts`): `WIN_RR_COOP`, `WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE`, `WIN_TIMED` from a won session; which other achievements multiplayer sessions feed (wins, jokers, categories, seen): one Steam user per machine, so settle and record a rule (e.g. any player''s win counts); `qualifies` per mode
- Telemetry (`engine/telemetry.ts`, milestone 14''s side file): mode and player count per session, nothing personal
- Outlook (`engine/outlook.ts` `seenPerLevel`, backlog B-15) and `qgen report --simulate` (`authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts`, `qgen.py` `SIM_MODES`): replace the MD-8/MD-9 stand-ins with the engine''s modes (`plans/16-content-target.md`); the Choice screen''s supply notice per mode
- Stats and review readers of `games[]` (`qgen report --played`, the authoring pages, gallery/demo saves in `authoring/tools/*saves.mjs`) follow part 1''s shape

### 5. Per-player controls (priority 480, after plan 156)
- Investigate first (throw-away, report in the plan): how many pads `navigator.getGamepads()` lists in Electron on Linux and Windows, with and without Steam Input (Chromium may stop at 4; XInput''s limit); pad identity across disconnect/reconnect; Steam''s per-handle input type ↔ `Gamepad.index` (per-player glyph style, `lib/gamepad.ts` `padStyle`)
- Binding: device → player (each pad index; keyboard and mouse together; keyboard-only: one key per player, per `decision 273` and `decision 274`)
- Before the session starts (menus, setup, join): every device drives the shared UI, as today; joining only records the binding
- In a session: the action layer (`lib/input.svelte.ts`, `lib/gamepad.svelte.ts`) tags each action with its player; only the acting player''s actions reach the game (turn''s player in the round-robin modes; in `timed` claims from anyone, then only the claimer for 6 s); the overlay (Esc/Start): who may open it and what it does in a session (settle in the plan)
- `timed` claim: one pad button per pad player (not a face button that picks an answer), the claim key per keyboard-only player, one claim key for the keyboard-and-mouse player; claimer''s answer per `decision 275`
- Prompts: follow the last input per milestone 8 in every mode; in a session per player where it matters (a pad player''s glyphs on their turn)
- Disconnect mid-session: a pad lost → pause and «reconnect pad n» or skip that player (settle in the plan)

### 6. Mode row, session setup and join screen (priority 400)
- The three modes on the Choice screen''s mode row (gated by `BUILT_MODES`, part 10), names per `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` "Mode names"
- Join screen: «press A to join» per pad, keyboard and mouse join as one player, keyboard-only key picking (per `decision 273`/`decision 274`); each player a name (save player row or new, `LetterPicker.svelte` for pads); leave/rejoin before start; no player cap of our own (minimum 2)
- Per-mode setup: age group per player (`rr-competitive`) or one for all; bundles (`decision 158: Bundle selection in every mode, apart from customization`, `plan 151: Bundle selection on its own full screen`); «Personalizar partida» where the mode allows it (customized: no achievements); supply check for the session
- Screens added to `screens/registry.ts`; Deck sizes (1280×800) as every screen

### 7. Round-robin game screens (priority 390)
- Turn banner (whose turn, their device glyph), the shared Tower (`rr-coop`) or one track per player (`rr-competitive`), shared or per-player joker tray, a player out, the session''s Victory/Wrong screens per mode
- Reuse Level, Select, Question, Correct, Wrong (`game/screens/`) rather than new copies (decision 199)

### 8. Timed game screens, drama and sound (priority 380)
- One question for all: 30 s countdown, a hint every 8 s, claim prompt per player, the claimer''s 6 s, rounds and hearts per player
- Drama as the milestone specs: pulsing heart at a player''s last chance in a round, stronger on the last heart; last 3 s after a claim: a tick per second, louder each time, pulsing red frame; same frame when every player is at risk at once; sounds through `game/sound.svelte.ts` (synth until `plan 32: Recorded sound effects (UI-10)`), checked with `TRIVIA_SOUND=1`
- Sudden death round 12 and the winner screen
- `PLACEHOLDER(<task id>)` for unpolished visuals (AGENTS.md)

### 9. UI strings and gallery (priority 360)
- Every new string in es, es-ES, en, de (`app/client/src/locales/`), per `locales/style/<locale>.md`; key collision rule of `npm run check` (`decision 53: Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?`) for claim keys
- `trivia-gallery`: demo saves for each new screen and state (join with 5 players, each mode mid-game, timed claim, last heart, red frame, each victory) in `authoring/tools/gallery_saves.mjs`; shots for all four locales

### 10. Shipping the modes and docs (priority 340)
- Per mode: its win achievement entered in Steamworks and `steam-achievements.vdf` (plan 86) before it joins `BUILT_MODES`; the Steamworks step is the developer''s: a decision per mode (`--once`), the mode''s `BUILT_MODES` task waits for it
- Store texts name a mode once it''s built (`decision 168: Store texts name only the built game modes`; `plans/17a-store-page.md`); controller line if a pad-only run changes `decision 90`
- Docs: `plans/13-game-modes.md`, `plans/14-input.md` section 3, `plans/11-steam.md`, `plans/16-content-target.md`, `plans/17a-store-page.md`, `plans/backlog.md` (B-15) point to this milestone; `rg "MD-8|MD-9|IN-6|Later"` leaves none for these (decision 200); the earlier parts update their own doc sections as they land

### 11. Close-out: end-to-end runs and family playtest (priority 130)
- Each mode start to finish: pads only, keyboard only, 4 pads + keyboard and mouse (5 players); fake pads headless where real ones are missing, real pads by the developer
- A playtest decision for the developer: each mode played on the TV with the family; failures become follow-up tasks
- Feeds `milestone 17: Remote Play Together`''s gate C

## Order
- 1 → 2, 3 → 4; 5 after `plan 156: Prompts follow the last input` and after 1 (the acting player in the API); 6 after 1 and 5; 7 after 2; 8 after 3; 9 alongside 6–8 (strings land with their screens, the gallery after); 10 per mode once its screens pass; 11 last', 'Today the game is played by one person or one group as a team. This work adds three ways for several people in the same room to play against each other or together on one TV: taking turns as a team, taking turns each in their own game, and a race where anyone can grab a question against the clock. Each controller is one player and the keyboard with the mouse is another, so the game has to tell players apart by what they hold, which it never had to before.', '2026-10-16T16:03:30Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (153, 17, 'masterplan', 1000, 'Masterplan of `milestone 17: Remote Play Together`. Its own tasks are not implementation work: each of them writes the plan for one part below (`pm plan add 17 …` with the priority given), and that plan''s split makes the work tasks.

## Ground rules
- The milestone is the spec; SW-13 (`plans/18-steam-integration.md`) and `plans/14-input.md` "Remote Play Together" ("works for free") are replaced by it
- Steam only, no netcode, lobbies or servers of our own (`decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`); Steam''s stream and Steam''s invites, nothing else
- A remote guest is one more local player: milestone 16''s device → seat binding (`decision 277: Multiplayer sessions in the save: one games[] row per session, with seats`, task 1396''s per-player controls) is used unchanged; Remote Play code adds facts about devices (which guest, which name), never a second binding or mode logic
- Binding: `steamworks-ffi-node` 0.11.3 (`decision 28: Steam binding for the Electron shell?`), SDK 1.62 (`decision 69: Steamworks SDK libs for dev and the bridge''s SDK path`); its loader has `ISteamInput::GetRemotePlaySessionID` and the overlay''s Remote Play invite dialog, no `ISteamRemotePlay`
- Overlay Windows only (`decision 70: Steam overlay in the Electron shell`): on a Linux/Deck host the invite comes from Steam''s own UI; no in-game invite button that works on one OS only unless part 3''s plan finds it cheap
- Headless checks: a dev switch fakes guests (as `TRIVIA_DEV_WORKSHOP_DIR` fakes Workshop items), so workers can check screens without a second machine; real sessions are the developer''s
- Guests don''t need to own the game; testing needs a second Steam account on a second machine (`decision 135: Steamworks: enable Workshop for ¡Trivia! and a second Steam account?`)

## Gate and decisions
- `decision 284: Remote Play Together gate: single player, controller input and local multiplayer playtested?` (the milestone''s gate A, B, C): every split of the parts below links each implementation task it makes to it (`pm task-pending-decision <task> 284`); investigation tasks (part 1, part 6''s measurement) and plan tasks don''t wait
- `decision 283: Remote Play Together: what happens when a remote guest leaves mid-game?`: part 5''s plan task waits for it
- Timed lag: part 6 measures first, then raises its decision (accept the lag, or adjust claiming)

## Parts

### 1. Investigation: Remote Play input and session API (priority 710; plan task `--web` for Valve''s ISteamRemotePlay and ISteamInput docs)
- Not gated: throw-away probes, report in the plan, outcome recorded (`pm decision record`)
- `ISteamRemotePlay` in SDK 1.62''s `steam_api` libs (Windows, Linux): session list and callbacks (`GetSessionCount`, `GetSessionID`, `GetSessionSteamID`, `GetSessionClientName`, `GetSessionClientFormFactor`, `SteamRemotePlaySessionConnected_t`/`Disconnected_t`), per-guest input (`BEnableRemotePlayTogetherDirectInput`, `GetInput`, mouse cursor calls): which exist, from which SDK version
- Reachable from the shell: through `steamworks-ffi-node`''s loaded library (its koffi handle) or our own koffi load of the same lib in `app/desktop/main.mjs`; callbacks through the binding''s `runCallbacks` loop or polling; or an upstream contribution (no fork of our own)
- Direct input semantics: with it on, are guests'' keyboard and mouse kept out of the host''s window and delivered per session; what the guest sees as cursor; what happens with it off (merged into the host''s)
- Guests'' pads: how they reach `navigator.getGamepads()` on a Windows and a Linux/SteamOS host (Steam''s virtual pads; Linux `uinput`), together with task 1396''s investigation (Chromium''s 4-pad cap); mapping a `Gamepad.index` to its guest (`GetRemotePlaySessionID` per Steam Input handle ↔ pad index), else by connect order against session events
- Steam''s own per-guest toggles (keyboard, mouse, controller) in the Remote Play overlay: usable as the "no" branch''s way to ignore remote keyboard and mouse
- Answer: yes (a guest''s keyboard and mouse can be one distinct player) or no; probes needing a live session become a developer checklist decision (`--once`) in this part''s plan

### 2. Steamworks switch and test setup (priority 700, after `plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)`)
- The developer''s step, checklist in `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (SW-13): Remote Play Together enabled for the real App ID (Spacewar 480 is no test), the store feature flag, a `beta` build with this milestone''s code (`plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`), host and guest machines (one Windows, one Linux or the Deck), a second account
- A decision (`--once`) with the checklist; parts 6 and 9''s live runs wait for it

### 3. Remote Play sessions in the shell bridge (priority 700)
- Per part 1''s answer: `app/desktop/main.mjs` reads the guest sessions and their connect/disconnect callbacks; `preload.cjs` and `lib/desktop.ts` `SteamBridge` expose them to the client: guests `{session, steamName, formFactor}` and events; pad ↔ guest mapping where part 1 found one
- Per-guest keyboard and mouse events (only if part 1 says yes): on in a session, delivered with the guest''s session; host''s keyboard and mouse unaffected
- Dev switch faking guests and their join/leave (README, `AGENTS.md` Commands row of `trivia-desktop`)
- Nothing persists: a guest''s Steam name isn''t stored unless picked as a player name on the join screen; telemetry gets at most a remote-guest count per session (`decision 119: Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file`), settle in the plan

### 4. Remote guests as players (priority 470, after task 1396''s per-player controls plan and part 3)
- Pad: a guest''s virtual pad joins with «press A» and is one seat in all three modes, through milestone 16''s binding unchanged; glyphs by the guest''s controller type (Steam input type per handle, `lib/gamepad.ts` `padStyle`)
- Pad count: local pads + guests'' pads beyond Chromium''s cap (part 1, task 1396): what the join screen does at the cap
- Keyboard and mouse, by part 1''s answer:
  - yes: a guest''s keyboard and mouse join as one distinct player, in the action layer (`lib/input.svelte.ts`) as a device of their own; turn-based modes and `timed` claim/answer per decisions 273–275 as for the local keyboard-and-mouse player
  - no: remote guests must use a pad; remote keyboard and mouse are ignored during the game (Steam''s per-guest toggles or direct input with events dropped, per part 1); the host''s keyboard and mouse stay the one keyboard player
- Gamemaster mode and «Solo o en grupo» with guests watching: no change (guests'' input drives the shared UI as any pad''s, per milestone 8)

### 5. Guests on the join screen and guests leaving (priority 400, after part 4; plan task waits for decision 283)
- Join screen: guests present with their Steam names (part 3); a guest''s name offered as the new player''s name; the «remote guests need a controller» line in the "no" branch
- A guest leaving before the start: their seat freed; joining later: as any pad
- A guest leaving mid-game: per `decision 283: Remote Play Together: what happens when a remote guest leaves mid-game?`, per mode; engine changes only if the answer differs from milestone 16''s pad-lost rule
- Screens in `screens/registry.ts` as needed; Deck sizes

### 6. Timed mode over a stream (priority 590, after `milestone 16: Local multiplayer: game modes and controls`'' timed engine plan, task 1394)
- Measurement first (investigation, not gated; needs part 2''s setup): host-to-guest picture delay and guest-to-host input delay, Windows and Linux hosts, wired and Wi-Fi; a throw-away dev probe (flash on screen, guest presses, host logs arrival) rather than the game; numbers in the plan
- Then a decision for the developer: accept the lag, or adjust claiming (e.g. a claim grace window, the 6 s claim and the 30 s/8 s hints counted from when the slowest guest saw the question); options with the numbers; the engine change (if any) per the answer, in task 1394''s timestamp model

### 7. UI strings and gallery (priority 360)
- New strings in es, es-ES, en, de (`app/client/src/locales/`), per `locales/style/<locale>.md`
- `trivia-gallery`: demo saves with fake guests (join screen with guests, the "no" branch''s line, a guest left) in `authoring/tools/gallery_saves.mjs`; all four locales

### 8. Store and docs (priority 340)
- Store: the «Remote Play Together» feature listed once part 9 passes (`plans/17a-store-page.md`, `plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)`); the controller line names remote guests on pads only if the developer approves the text (decision `--once`)
- Docs: SW-13 in `plans/18-steam-integration.md` and `plans/11-steam.md` point to this milestone, no "Later" left; `plans/14-input.md` "Remote Play Together" rewritten (pads as players, keyboard and mouse per part 1); `plans/13-game-modes.md` as needed; `rg -i "remote play"` over `plans/`, README, `AGENTS.md` (decision 200)

### 9. Close-out: play with remote guests (priority 130)
- Headless: each mode start to finish with fake guests (part 3''s switch)
- A playtest decision for the developer: each multiplayer mode with at least one remote guest on a pad, and one on keyboard and mouse if part 1 said yes; timed mode per part 6''s answer; failures become follow-up tasks
- The milestone''s "Done when"

## Order
- 1 and 2 first (2 after plan 130); 3 after 1; 4 after 3 and task 1396''s plan; 5 after 4; 6''s measurement after 2, its engine change after task 1394''s plan; 7 alongside 4–5; 8 after 9''s runs pass (docs may land earlier); 9 last
- Everything but investigation and plan tasks waits for decision 284', 'Steam can stream a game running on one computer to friends elsewhere and send their controller presses back, so they play along without owning the game; this is how the family will play the new multiplayer modes over the internet without any server of our own. It builds on playing several people in one room: a friend far away should count as one more player with a controller. Before building, we find out whether Steam can also tell apart each friend''s keyboard and mouse, and how much the stream''s delay matters for the mode where players race to answer first.', '2026-10-16T17:05:30Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (154, 18, 'masterplan', 1000, 'Masterplan of `milestone 18: Playable demo`. Its own tasks are not implementation work: each of them writes the plan for one part below (`pm plan add 18 …` with the priority given), and that plan''s split makes the work tasks.

## Ground rules
- The milestone is the spec: all features of the base game, only the demo base bundle (≈200 questions, spread over difficulties), deterministic selection, seen counts disregarded, the start screen says it is the free demo
- One codebase, a build-time demo flag (`decision 335: Playable demo: a build variant of the same code, switched at build time`); no fork, no player toggle; the engine gets `demo` as an input, never a global
- Nothing enforced hard: the code is public (`decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`); the demo ships less data, it doesn''t lock anything
- Price model unchanged (`decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): how is the game sold on Steam?`): paid base game, free bundles as DLC; the demo ships no DLC bundle, no regional, topic (`milestone 19: topic question bundles`) or mod-provided extra bundle unless part 1''s decision says mods are on
- Launch languages es, es-ES, en, de (`decision 156: One language for UI and questions`): the demo bundle has every question in all four; a locale without its demo pool isn''t offered
- Every game mode in the demo: «Solo o en grupo», Gamemaster, rr-coop, rr-competitive, timed (only those in `BUILT_MODES` when the demo ships; `decision 293: Unbuilt multiplayer modes: on the mode row in dev mode only` holds there too)
- Headless checks first: a dev switch (`TRIVIA_DEMO=1` or the like) runs the dev server, `trivia-desktop`, `trivia-gallery` and `smoke.mjs` as the demo, so workers check without a demo build

## Parts

### 1. Demo build switch, identity and save (priority 700)
- The flag: client (Vite define, `lib/build.ts` `buildInfo()` gains `demo`), desktop shell (`main.mjs`, build argument), dev switch; read once, passed to the engine through the loaded data or `Io`
- Identity: productName, exe and artefact names of the demo next to `decision 223: Build names after PUB-7: productName «Living Room Trivia», space-free exe and artefact names`; window and in-game title; its own Steam App ID (`STEAM_APP_ID`, `steam.json`), Spacewar until the developer creates the demo app (part 6)
- Save: the plan raises a decision: demo save separate from the full game''s (recommended: own `userData`, e.g. `<appData>/trivia-demo`, so the demo''s plays never touch the family''s seen counts; no carry-over) or shared/imported on purchase
- Steam features in the demo: the plan raises a decision (one, with options per feature): Steam Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry opt-in, question reports; recommended: Cloud and reports on, telemetry on with demo games marked, mods and Workshop off, achievements as Valve allows for demo apps (part 6''s plan checks Valve''s docs)
- Docs: README, `AGENTS.md` Commands rows (`trivia-desktop`, `trivia-desktop-build`, dev server) name the switch

### 2. The demo base bundle (priority 590, `questions` work tree)
- What it is: a base bundle `demo` (`kind: base`), only in demo builds, whose questions are a fixed list of approved base question ids, not new drafts; the plan settles the format (e.g. `app/data/demo.json` ids + an export step writing `pool.demo*.json` per locale) and records it, also against "every question is in exactly one bundle" (`plans/22-bundles.md`)
- Size from supply, not a guess: the list must pass the supply check (`selection.ts` `supply`/`assign`) for every mode × age group × seat count (rr-competitive''s seats each draw a game, timed''s round size = seats per `decision 276: Timed mode: after a drop-out, how many questions does a round have?`; max seats per milestone 16), with jokers'' replacements (`replacement`, category joker candidates) still fillable; ≈200 if that suffices, more if the numbers say so
- Spread: difficulties per each group''s `level_weights` (`app/data/age-groups.json`), categories and subcategories, media share like the full pool; only questions approved in all four locales, flag-free, media in the cache and shippable licences
- Picked by a deterministic script (`qgen demo` or a step of `qgen export`), not by hand; the developer approves the list (decision `--once`, sheet or `/review` link); a later flag or retirement of a listed question → the script proposes a replacement, approved the same way
- `qgen validate` checks the list (ids exist, approved in every locale, supply passes)

### 3. Deterministic selection in the demo (priority 600)
- Every draw is a function of the game''s inputs: in demo, `lib/engine.ts` `io()` seeds `seededRng` from the game''s own state (mode, age group, seats, level, the game''s action count, never time, game id or `randomSeed()`), so equal play gives equal questions and answer order on every machine and run
- All rng sites follow (`draw`, `pick`, `replacement`, `swap_in`, timed rounds); `countOf` returns 0 in demo, so seen counts don''t steer `draw` or replacements (counts may still be written)
- Seen-based features off in demo: the running-out notice (`decision 195: Supply notice: bundles running out instead of exhausted subcategories`, `outlook.ts`)
- Telemetry: demo games marked (`decision 119: Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file`); `qgen telemetry` keeps them out of calibration curves (fixed selection isn''t a sample); report-server schema per part 1''s answer
- One lasting test: two runs of the same scripted session give identical questions, the full game''s stay random

### 4. Demo packaging, release check and upload (priority 610, after `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`)
- `trivia-desktop-build --demo`: only the demo bundle''s data (no `app/data/bundles/*`, pools cut to the demo pools, names files as needed), media staged for the demo questions only (`stage-media.mjs`, its own budget in `media-budget.json`), `CREDITS.md` for the shipped media only; Windows and Linux like the full build
- `trivia-release-check --demo`: the demo''s steps (credits both ways on the demo media, smoke game per mode in demo, determinism: the smoke run twice gives identical questions, media budget), report next to the full one
- `trivia-steam upload --demo --branch beta`: the demo app''s IDs and depots in `steam.json`, its VDFs; same gates as the full upload
- `nix build` output for the demo only if the plan finds a use; else none

### 5. Demo on screen (priority 400)
- Start screen: a line saying this is the free demo version («Versión de demostración gratuita» or the like), in es, es-ES, en, de (`app/client/src/locales/`, `locales/style/<locale>.md` first)
- Bundle screen: the demo bundle alone, info only (`decision 269: Bundle screen: a mod''s extra base bundle`); the tile''s count string the demo''s own (`decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings` gives base «5000+»: wrong for the demo)
- Screens that point to what the demo doesn''t have (mods screen, DLC, Workshop) hidden per part 1''s answer; no PLACEHOLDER left on a demo screen
- `trivia-gallery --demo` (or a demo shot set): Start, Bundles, per locale; the developer reviews the start screen in `/gallery` (decision `--once`)

### 6. Steamworks demo app and store (priority 290, after `plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)` and `plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)`; plan task `--web` for Valve''s demo docs)
- Valve''s rules for demos (own app ID under the base app, "Download demo" on the base store page, what a demo may have: Cloud, achievements, Workshop, its own store page or not, review): read, written into the plan, fed back into part 1''s decisions
- The developer''s steps as a checklist decision (`--once`): demo app created, App ID and depot IDs, demo store presence, release; part 4''s real upload waits for it
- Store texts: the demo mentioned on the store page if Valve''s layout needs it (`plans/17a-store-page.md`), approved by the developer as the other store texts

### 7. Close-out: play the demo (priority 120)
- Headless: the demo build (or dev switch) plays every mode × age group start to finish (`smoke.mjs`), twice, identical questions
- A playtest decision for the developer: the demo build from Steam''s beta branch, each mode once, the start screen; failures become follow-up tasks
- Docs: `plans/11-steam.md`, `plans/17-publishing.md`, `plans/22-bundles.md` name the demo; `rg -i demo` over `plans/`, README, `AGENTS.md` (decision 200)

## Order
- 1 first; 2 and 3 in parallel after 1 (2 in `questions`, 3 in `app`); 4 after 1–3 and plan 89; 5 after 1 and 2; 6''s reading early (its plan task), its checklist after plan 130; 7 last', 'The game gets a free demo: the full game with a small, fixed set of about two hundred questions, enough to play once in every game mode and for every age group. In the demo the questions never come out at random: every run of it shows the same questions in the same order, so what a player tries is exactly what we tested, and its start screen says it is the free demo. It lets families try the game before buying it.', '2026-10-16T17:38:48Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (155, 19, 'masterplan', 1000, 'Milestone 19: five topic bundles (`kind: theme`), STEM (natural sciences, engineering, math), sports, history, movies, geography. **This masterplan''s own tasks are not implementation work: each writes the plan for one part** (`pm plan add 19 …`), which is then split into tasks.

## Builds on (binding)
- `plans/22-bundles.md`: every question in exactly one bundle; bundles **add** questions, they don''t own a topic: base''s sports, film, history, science and geography questions stay in `base`; base batches keep drafting them. Kind `theme` exists in `bundles.json` validation and `qgen bundle new --kind theme`; icon today the generic pin (`BundleSelector.svelte`).
- `decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): how is the game sold on Steam?`: free DLC, own store entry, optional install, never paid.
- `decision 112: Pack layout: a pool file per bundle (optional install)`: `app/data/bundles/<id>/pool[.<locale>].json`, missing = not offered.
- `decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings`: every shipped non-base bundle shows «2000+» → target 2000 approved per bundle.
- `decision 158: Bundle selection in every mode, apart from customization` / decision 33: non-base bundles off by default; any combination (milestone 8).
- `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` item 2: the term is "question bundle", never «Temas».
- `decision 18: Which new base subcategories?`: fan-level detail (e.g. football clubs, legendary players) is too specific for `base`: the room topic bundles fill.
- `decision 236: English-first drafting for base: what drives drafting and which locales steer it`; `translations.draft_locale()`: theme bundles already draft in `en`; launch question locales `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de` (decision 235).
- `decision 350: Overlap rate in drafting: which changes?`: overlap probe and avoid lists; topic bundles must not re-ask `base`.
- `decision 339: Demo bundle format: an id list of base questions, exported to app/data/demo/ pools, questions stay in base`: the demo stays base-only; no topic bundle in the demo.
- D-36 / AGENTS.md "Making questions": runs only through `qgen batch --bundle <id>` (`--translate <L>`), RUNBOOK unchanged.
- Launch (milestone 11) doesn''t wait for this milestone; what''s ready ships, the rest in content patches (`plan 96: Content updates as patches (ST-5)`).

## Gaps today
- `qgen taxonomy` refuses non-regional bundles (`cmd_taxonomy`: `kind != "region"`); no general list for themes (`regional-categories.json` is regions only).
- Targets: `targets.json` and `qgen bundle new` write a target for regional bundles only; `qgen validate` requires one only there; `qgen report --cost` projects per launch language and regional bundle, not theme.
- Per-locale counting and gap aiming (decision 236) exist for `base`; a theme bundle offered in four locales needs the same (sources in `en` + translations into `es`, `es-ES`, `de`).
- Achievements: `BUNDLE_*` only for `kind: region` (`achievements.ts`).
- Icons: every theme bundle would show the same pin.
- «Cambiazo» and category names: a topic bundle''s categories next to base''s same-topic category (e.g. two sport categories) may read as duplicates.
- Movies: stills and posters are mostly non-free; media share for `movies` will be low under the existing licence rules (plan 23).

## Parts
Each part: one `--kind plan` task of this masterplan, in order; priorities for the part''s plan as given.

1. **Pipeline for topic bundles** (questions, plan priority 700)
   - `qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>` for `kind: theme`: no general list; one opus call from the bundle''s `rule` + target + `base`''s own subcategories on the same topic (to go beyond them, not repeat them); same proposal format and `--apply` (slugs, `names.{en,es,de}.json`).
   - `targets.json` entry per theme bundle (2000, base''s difficulty mix scaled), written by `qgen bundle new --kind theme`, required by `qgen validate`; counted per question locale like `base`, English drafting aimed at the largest locale gap.
   - `qgen batch --bundle <id>` and `--translate <L> --bundle <id>` work end to end for a theme bundle (en source, es/es-ES/de translations, export of all four pool files); `qgen report` and `--cost` projection per theme bundle.
   - Overlap: drafting probes and avoid lists include `base`''s questions on the topic (cross-bundle), so a topic bundle never re-asks a base question; validate/QC unchanged otherwise.
   - Media: how `movies` (and sports) handles scarce free media (accept low share vs. other kinds of media); the part''s plan proposes, a decision only if the developer''s choice is needed.
   - Docs: `plans/22-bundles.md` ("In the pipeline", layout), `plans/16-content-target.md`.
2. **The five bundles: rows and taxonomies** (questions, plan priority 600; after part 1)
   - Ids `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography`; per bundle the English `rule` (membership vs. `base`: more and deeper questions on the topic at every difficulty, still answerable by families anywhere, decision 18''s fan level allowed), `voice` (none beyond base''s), Spanish `name`/`description`, en/de names; `languages` all four launch question locales once each has a pool.
   - One `pm decision add` with the five rows (names per UI language per `locales/style/<locale>.md`), then `qgen bundle new --kind theme` per bundle.
   - Per bundle `qgen taxonomy` proposal → its own taxonomy decision (like `decision 287: usa taxonomy: categories and subcategories`) → `--apply`; ≈ 50 subcategories each at ≈ 40 approved per subcategory.
3. **Content runs** (questions, plan priority −120, after `plan 84: Release content runs`''s chains)
   - Start task per bundle in the plan 84 pattern (drafting pair `batch-<n>` + `QC batch-<n>`, translation runs `tr-<L>-<n>` with `--bundle`), until 2000 approved per question locale; pm-run rules of plan 84 repeated in every body.
   - Pace and order of the five against base and regional runs: a decision with `qgen report --cost` projections (5 × 2000 × 4 locales), raised by the part''s plan before the first start task.
4. **In the game** (app, plan priority 400)
   - Own icon per topic bundle (e.g. flask, ball, scroll, film reel, globe) instead of the pin: how a row names its icon (`bundles.json` field vs. by id) and mods'' theme bundles'' fallback.
   - Tile order (non-regional group, `orderBundles`), counts «2000+» (decision 267), overlay line, supply notice (decision 195) with topic bundles on; a session with only a topic bundle on (no base) plays and «Cambiazo» has enough categories.
   - «Cambiazo» / category display when base and a topic bundle carry similar categories.
   - Achievements: `BUNDLE_*` for theme bundles too or not (the part''s plan decides or raises a decision; Steamworks entries are part 5''s).
   - Gallery review set (`trivia-gallery --set task-<id>`) of the Bundles screen with the five tiles, per UI language.
5. **Steam DLC and store** (app, plan priority 280, after `plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)`)
   - Per bundle a free DLC app (`plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)` checklist), depot (`plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`, `build/pack-media.json`), store name, short/long description per store language and capsules (plan 88''s DLC pattern), achievements if part 4 adds them; values entered by the developer.
   - Extend those plans'' generic per-bundle steps rather than copying them; only what is specific to the five.
6. **Close-out** (plan priority 100)
   - Play-test decision: a family session with each topic bundle on (alone and with base), per launch language with a pool.
   - Docs: `plans/22-bundles.md` "The first bundles" table, `README.md`/`directory.md` where they list bundles; `rg` for "regional bundle" wording that should now say "non-base bundle".
   - What ships: bundles with a pool at the release or the next content patch (`plan 96: Content updates as patches (ST-5)`).

## Out of scope
- Moving existing `base` questions into topic bundles (bundles add, they don''t own a topic).
- More topic bundles than the five; topic bundles in the demo; milestone 12''s locales (zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR).', 'The game gets five new optional question packs, each about one subject: science and technology, sports, history, movies and geography. Families who love a subject switch its pack on and get many more, and deeper, questions about it than the general pack offers. This overview splits the work into the question-making tools, the five packs'' contents, the generation runs that fill them, how they look in the game, their Steam store entries, and a final play-test.', '2026-10-16T19:04:11Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (156, 8, 'Prompts follow the last input', 500, 'Part 12 of `plan 8: masterplan`. One player conceptually (possibly a whole group): every pad, the keyboard and the mouse drive that player and replace each other at any moment, no switching step (milestone 8, developer 2026-10-16; `decision 24: Multiplayer input and couch co-op (OQ-37)?`''s per-player pads are milestone 16: Local multiplayer: game modes and controls, out of scope). Prompts follow the last input, in every mode and on every screen.

## Rule
- mouse move, click or key press → `lastDevice` `mouse`/`keyboard` → key prompts (as today)
- any pad input → `lastDevice` `gamepad` → glyphs: a press edge of any button (mapped or not, incl. triggers via `pressed`), or either stick (axes 0–3) moved past the dead zone from rest
- a control without a pad binding shows no glyph in pad mode (`Prompt.svelte` already does; screens that print keys themselves follow)
- right stick: switches only, no action of its own (`decision 272: Right stick: what it does beyond switching prompts to the pad`); R3 stays the peek (`decision 126: Image peek: which pad button and key?`)
- no flicker: an idle pad (stick drift, analog trigger noise, a held button on focus return) never switches; a stationary mouse (synthetic `pointermove` after scroll, layout or focus change) never switches

## Today''s gaps
- `lib/input.svelte.ts`: only `pointerdown` sets `mouse`; no `pointermove`
- `lib/gamepad.svelte.ts` / `lib/gamepad.ts`: `lastDevice` and `padStyle` only change through `dispatch` of a mapped action; unmapped buttons (e.g. X outside Question, triggers off-Question, L3) and the right stick don''t switch; `step` reads axes 0–1 only

## Steps
1. **Pad: any input switches** (`lib/gamepad.ts`, `lib/gamepad.svelte.ts`)
   - `step` also reports `touched`: any button''s press edge (not release), or any stick (left: axes 0–1, right: 2–3) crossing `ON` from below `OFF` (same hysteresis as the left stick''s navigation; per-stick "held" state in `PadState`, set by `held()` on focus return so a resting deflection doesn''t fire)
   - loop: `touched` with no actions → `lastDevice.current = "gamepad"`, `padStyle` from Steam/`Gamepad.id`, `first()`; actions dispatch as now
   - left-stick navigation unchanged; right stick produces no intent
   - a switch without an action doesn''t move focus; if no control has the ring, show it on the focused control (`focus.ts` `show`) so the A glyph has a target, as a key press does today
2. **Mouse move switches** (`lib/input.svelte.ts`)
   - `pointermove` with `pointerType === "mouse"` sets `mouse` only after real movement: position (`screenX/Y`) changed since the last seen one, accumulated ≥ a few px since the last keyboard/pad input (constant next to the listener); synthetic moves (same position after scroll/layout) ignored
   - `pointerdown` unchanged (touch and pen too); listener added/removed with the others in `listen`
   - check `focusControl`: `mouse` last → focus without ring, as today
3. **Glyph-less controls and screens that print keys** (`rg lastDevice`, letter-key spans)
   - every place that renders a key outside `<Prompt>` (`JokerTray.svelte` letters, Bundles tile letters, Player, Mods, FlagDialog, GoToDialog) hides it in pad mode or shows a glyph only where a pad binding exists
   - mods'' `input.lastDevice` (`lib/mods.ts`) keeps its meaning; `modding/` docs mention the new switching if they describe it
4. **Docs and check**
   - `plans/14-input.md`: IN-2/IN-5 lines: one player, every device; what switches prompts (pad any button/stick past dead zone, mouse move/click, key); right stick (decision 272); `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` "Rule (IN-5)" names the switch rule; `rg` old wording "last-used device", "after a pad press" (decision 200)
   - check: Node dev server (`npm run dev -w app/client` or `serve` after build) at 1920×1080 and 1280×800; a real pad if at hand, else a stubbed `navigator.getGamepads()` (throw-away, like `trivia-gallery`''s fake pad, with a drifting idle stick ±0.1 and a noisy trigger) and Playwright mouse moves; walk Start → Player → Choice → Bundles → Level → Question → Results in «Solo o en grupo» and «Modo anfitrión», alternating mouse, keys and pad: prompts switch on every screen on an unmapped pad button, the right stick, a mouse move, a key; no switch from the idle drifting pad or after a scroll with a still mouse; peek (R3/V) as before
   - `trivia-gallery` pad shots unchanged (its Playwright clicks/moves must not flip them to keys: if they do, the gallery presses through the fake pad or parks the mouse first)

## Out of scope
- per-device players, join screen, per-player glyphs (IN-6, milestone 16)
- hiding the mouse cursor in pad mode, Steam Input action sets (S5)

## Order and dependencies
- Steps 1–3 independent; step 4 last. Independent of `plan 99: Retire the browser game and the Python game server` and `plan 151: Bundle selection on its own full screen` (step 3 follows whatever the bundle tiles show then). `plan 48: S3 close-out and platform test` (140) runs after and gets the platform rows.

## Done when
- the milestone''s two input lines hold (one player from every device; prompts follow the last input, every mode, every screen, no glyph without a pad shortcut)
- `plans/14-input.md` and `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` updated; per-commit checks pass', 'The game can be played with a controller, a keyboard or a mouse, and the hints on screen show either keyboard keys or controller button pictures, depending on what was used last. Today the switch only happens for some inputs: moving the mouse or pressing a controller button that does nothing on the current screen leaves the old hints up, which confuses a family passing the controller around. This work makes every touch of any device count, so the hints always match the device in hand, without flickering when a controller lies idle.', '2026-10-16T19:23:14Z', 1375);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (157, 16, 'Session model and save format', 900, 'Part 1 of `plan 152: masterplan`. The save and engine shape for a local multiplayer session: players in join order, the mode, shared settings, per-player state, the turn pointer, and an action API where every action names the acting player. No mode logic: parts 2 and 3 (`task 1393: write plan: Round-robin modes in the engine`, `task 1394: write plan: Competitive (timed) in the engine`) fill it in.

## Binding
- `decision 277: Multiplayer sessions in the save: one games[] row per session, with seats` (this plan''s choice)
- D-82 (`plans/decisions.md`), plan 65: seen = one row per event, whole save, every player and mode
- `decision 119: Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file`, `decision 139: Achievement triggers derived without a save change (SW-11)`: telemetry and achievements stay derived; this plan adds no field for them
- `decision 91: Game version: single source of truth` (`plans/11-steam.md`): a `SAVE_VERSION` change = minor app version; `plans/12-client-engine.md` "Shape change": `SAVE_VERSION + 1` + `UPGRADES` entry + `save.test.ts` case
- Device-agnostic (`milestone 17: Remote Play Together`): the save and the engine know seats, never devices; the device → seat binding lives in the client (part 5)

## What exists (2026-10-16)
- `engine/state.ts`: `SAVE_VERSION = 4`; `GameRow {id, started_on, finished_on, result, player_id, locale?, state}`; `GameState` (level, phase, table, history, jokers, settings with `mode`); `newest()`
- `engine/game.ts`: `latest()` / `running()` = the newest row; `see()` writes `{question_id, game_id, seen_on}`; `players()`, `deletePlayer()`, `newestGame()` / `playerChoice()` / `playerMode()` filter on `player_id`; `MODES` has `rr-coop`, `rr-competitive`, `timed`, `BUILT_MODES` doesn''t
- `engine/api.ts` `gameAction`: one body per action, no actor
- `engine/save.ts`: `UPGRADES` 1–3, `parseSave` envelope checks, `mapOldKeys` over `games[].state` (and `undo`)
- Readers of `games[]`: `engine/achievements.ts` `earned`, `lib/achievements.ts` (ended-game keys), `engine/telemetry.ts` (key `<id>@<started_on>`, history slice), `engine/outlook.ts`, `game.ts` `repair`/`view`, `authoring/tools/demo_saves.mjs`, `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs`; `qgen report --played` (`authoring/tools/played.py`) reads telemetry, not the save
- Python: `authoring/tools/save_file.py` reads `seen`, `blocked`, `flags` only (branches on version < 3, < 4); `app/server/save.py` `VERSION`/`LISTS` until `task 765: Delete app/server, ServerStore, the trivia command and nix build .#app`

## Shape (save v5)
- `GameRow`, additive:
  - `seats?: Seat[]`: a multiplayer session (milestone 16), join order; missing = a one-player game (`player_id`)
  - `turn?: number`: seat index on turn (round-robin modes); missing outside them
  - `player_id`: `null` on session rows (comment: "null: games before D-28 or a multiplayer session"), so solo presets (`playerChoice`, `playerMode`) never pick a session
- `Seat`:
  - `player_id: number | null`: a `players[]` row (picked or created on the join screen); `null` after `deletePlayer`
  - `state?: GameState`: `rr-competitive` only: the seat''s own game (own level, jokers, age group in its `settings`)
  - `lives?: number`, `out?: true`: `timed` lives (3 at start) and drop-out; `out` also `rr-competitive`''s wrong answer
  - `result?: "won" | "lost"`: per seat in `rr-competitive` and `timed` once decided; `rr-coop` uses the row''s
- `row.state` per mode:
  - `rr-coop`: the team''s game (level, one joker set, history); `settings` as solo''s (one age group)
  - `timed`: the shared question flow: `level` = round, history of every question shown; claim and timestamp fields are part 3''s (additive, no further bump while `timed` isn''t built)
  - `rr-competitive`: shared settings only (mode, bundles; `phase` mirrors the session''s end), empty history; play is in `seats[].state`
- `row.result`: `won` when the team or one seat won, `lost` when nobody did, `abandoned`; per-seat outcomes in `Seat.result`
- `HistoryEntry.seat?: number`: who answered (`rr-coop`, `timed`); missing = the row''s one player
- Locale: `row.locale` for the whole session (one language, `decision 156: One language for UI and questions`)
- No device, pad index or key in the save

## Helpers (`engine/state.ts`)
- `rowPlayers(row): (number | null)[]`: `seats` → their `player_id`s, else `[player_id]`
- `rowStates(row): GameState[]`: `rr-competitive` → every `seats[].state`, else `[row.state]`
- `seatResult(row, i)`: `Seat.result`, else the row''s (`rr-coop`)
- Readers move onto them where they would otherwise miss a session: `players()` (a session counts as a game for every seated player; a win per `seatResult`), `deletePlayer()` (sessions stay, the seat''s `player_id` → `null`, a running session with them is abandoned; seen rows untouched), `mapOldKeys` and `repair` (every state of `rowStates`), `achievements.ts` / `telemetry.ts` only where they''d break on the shape; what multiplayer feeds them is part 4''s

## Version 5
- `SAVE_VERSION = 5`; `UPGRADES[4]`: identity (no v4 save has sessions); the bump makes an older build back the save up as `newer` (`SaveNewerError`) instead of reading a session as a gamemaster game (Steam Cloud, `beta` vs `default`, `plans/12-client-engine.md` "Beta vs. default")
- `parseSave`: `seats`, when present, a non-empty list of objects with `player_id` number or null; `turn` an integer index into `seats`; a seat''s `state` an object
- `authoring/tools/save_file.py`: reads the same three fields; docstring names v5, no branch needed; check it parses a v5 save
- `app/server/save.py`: `VERSION = 5`, `LISTS[5]` while task 765 is open (else the browser server answers 400 `bad_save`); if task 765 is done, nothing
- `authoring/tools/demo_saves.mjs`: follows `SAVE_VERSION` already
- `release_check.py` reports the save-version change by itself; nothing to do

## Seen events (D-82)
- Unchanged `see(work, qid, gid)`, `gid` = the session row: one row per question shown, however many players saw it
- `rr-coop`, `timed`: one row per question put on screen (as solo: answered, revealed, skipped by snipe); `timed`: also an unclaimed question that ran out (part 3 writes it)
- `rr-competitive`: each seat''s question one row, same session `game_id`
- Supply counts (`countOf`) unchanged: per save, not per player

## Engine API: the acting seat
- Every game action''s body may carry `seat` (integer, join-order index); `api.ts` `gameAction` passes it on, `game.ts` actions take it
- One check in `game.ts`, before any mode logic: `actor(row, seat)`:
  - one-player row: `seat` missing or 0; else `seat_unknown`
  - session row: `seat` missing → `seat_missing`; not an index → `seat_unknown`; `Seat.out` → `seat_out`
  - round-robin: `seat !== row.turn` → `not_your_turn` (helper ready for part 2)
  - `timed`''s claim rules (`not_your_claim`, …) are part 3''s, through the same check
- Error codes in `state.ts` `ERRORS` (D-57); refused = 409 with the save unchanged, as every `GameError`
- `new` for a session: body `players: string[]` (names, join order) instead of `player`; shared part here: `cleanName` each, distinct by casefold (`player_twice`), at least 2 (`players_too_few`), known names reuse their row, new ones get one; mode-specific state init is parts 2 and 3; until then `mode_not_built` still refuses (BUILT_MODES, part 10)
- Solo and gamemaster: no `seat` sent, nothing changes; the frozen fixtures (`engine/fixtures/`, `game.test.ts`) replay unchanged

## Tasks
1. Save v5: `Seat`, `GameRow.seats`/`turn`, `HistoryEntry.seat`, the three helpers, readers on them (`players`, `deletePlayer`, `mapOldKeys`, `repair`), `SAVE_VERSION` 5 + `UPGRADES[4]` + `parseSave` checks, `save_file.py`, `app/server/save.py` (if still there); one `save.test.ts` case: a v4 save upgrades unchanged, a hand-built v5 session row round-trips through `parseSave` (and `mapOldKeys`); docs `plans/12-client-engine.md` (save v5 line), `plans/decisions.md` D-82 note (session rows)
2. Acting seat: `seat` through `api.ts` → `game.ts`, `actor()` with the error codes, the session half of `new` (players list, checks, rows) still behind `mode_not_built`; fixture replay unchanged; `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Modes": the actor rule one bullet

## Done when
- `npm run check`, `npm test` (fixture replay unchanged), `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass
- The family''s real save (a copy) loads as v5, plays a solo game, writes v5; `save_file.py` reads it
- No mode logic: no session can be started yet (`mode_not_built`)', 'Local multiplayer lets several people in one room play on the same TV, each with their own controller. Before any game rules can be built, the game''s save file has to be able to hold such a session: who joined in which order, whose turn it is, and each player''s own progress where the mode gives them one. This part also makes the game refuse an action from a player whose turn it isn''t, so a misbehaving controller can never play for someone else.', '2026-10-16T19:40:48Z', 1392);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (158, 16, 'Round-robin modes in the engine', 600, 'Part 2 of `plan 152: masterplan`. The engine rules of the two turn-based multiplayer modes, `rr-coop` and `rr-competitive`, on the session shape of `plan 157: Session model and save format` (seats, `turn`, the acting seat). Engine only: no screens, no input binding, no `BUILT_MODES` change.

## Binding
- Milestone 16 "Outcome" and `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Round-robin co-op" / "Round-robin competitive": the spec; replaces `decision 23: Competitive format (OQ-37)?` where it differs
- `decision 277: Multiplayer sessions in the save: one games[] row per session, with seats`: rr-coop plays in `row.state`, rr-competitive in `seats[].state`; `HistoryEntry.seat`; `turn`
- `decision 278: Round-robin competitive: the last player standing wins at once`
- Rules shared with solo (D-74, D-88): no skip, undo, replace, level, settings, joker budget changes (`gamemasterOnly` already refuses outside gamemaster mode); `answers` off refused (`gamemaster_only`); flag only logs (`decision 60: One mechanism for questions with problems: flag or report?`)
- `decision 158: Bundle selection in every mode, apart from customization`: one bundle list per session
- D-82 / plan 65: seen per save, one row per question shown, `game_id` = the session row (plan 157 "Seen events")
- Gate: plan 157''s `actor(row, seat)` runs first in every action (`seat_missing`, `seat_unknown`, `seat_out`, `not_your_turn`)

## Starting a session (`new` with `players`)
- Builds on plan 157''s session half of `new` (names → seat rows, `player_twice`, `players_too_few`); here the mode''s state
- Body: `players: string[]`, `mode`, `bundles`, `age_group` (shared), `jokers` (overrides, as solo''s: a difference from `STANDARD_JOKERS` sets `customized`); rr-competitive also `age_groups?: string[]` (one per player, join order; missing entries = `age_group`); other fields as solo''s `new` accepts and refuses
- `rr-coop`: `row.state` as a solo game: one age group, `STANDARD_JOKERS` (+ overrides), one table dealt; `turn: 0`; `seats[]` without `state`
- `rr-competitive`: `row.state` shared settings only (mode, bundles, `customized`), empty history; each seat a full `GameState` (own `age_group`, own joker set: same overrides for every seat, own table dealt at once); `turn: 0`
- `mode_not_built`: moves from `game.ts` `newGame` to `api.ts`''s `new`, so engine tests (and part 4''s `qgen report --simulate`) can start the unbuilt modes; the UI still can''t until part 10
- Supply check (GF-5) before the session starts, `supply_short` as today:
  - `rr-coop`: as solo (one game)
  - `rr-competitive`: one matching over all seats: virtual levels seat × level, each with its seat''s range (`selection.assign` on concatenated ranges), so N seats of one age group need N × cards per level; `supply_short` levels carry `seat`; `Supply.levels[].seat?` in `lib/types.ts`

## Turns
- `row.turn` = seat on turn; only that seat''s actions pass (`not_your_turn`)
- A turn = one question, ended by its final answer: card pick, jokers, then `answer` all by the turn''s seat
- «Paso y fuera», a «Tiro mágico» hit (level repeats): same seat keeps the turn (no final answer yet)
- After a final answer: `turn` → next seat in join order (`rr-competitive`: skipping `out` seats); wraps around
- `HistoryEntry.seat` on every entry the seat caused (answers, joker drops, skips): stats and part 4 read who did what

## rr-coop
- One team game in `row.state`: level climbs one per correct answer, whoever answered; the next seat plays the next level
- Jokers: the one shared set; any seat on turn uses what''s left (`jokersLeft` over the team history, unchanged)
- Wrong answer: `row.result = "lost"`, everyone lost (`Seat.result` unset, `seatResult` falls back to the row''s)
- Correct at the last level: `row.result = "won"`, everyone won
- Selection, draws, joker plays: solo''s code on `row.state`, unchanged

## rr-competitive
- Each seat''s game in `seats[i].state`; actions run on the acting seat''s state (a `seatState(row, seat)` helper next to `running()`), saved back into its seat
- Correct answer: that seat''s level +1, new table at its level; turn passes
- Wrong answer: that seat''s `phase = "lost"`, `out: true`, `result: "lost"`; turn passes
- Correct at the last level: seat `won`, the session ends: every other seat still in → `lost`, `row.result = "won"`
- One seat left in (decision 278): it wins at once (`won`, `row.result = "won"`), whatever its level
- `row.state.phase` mirrors the end (`won`); `row.finished_on` set as solo''s
- Selection per seat: `selection.draw` with the seat''s own ranges (`rangesFor` of its age group), own `purged`, own asked categories; `availableNow` also excludes every other seat''s `offered` (no card twice in one session); if a draw fails only because of that, retry excluding just the other seats'' current tables (seen counts still order: lowest first); then `level_empty` as today
- Jokers: per seat, `jokersLeft(seatState)`; replacements (GF-2) check the seat''s own later levels

## Ending a session
- `abandon` and a new `new`: the whole session `abandoned` (row''s `result`; seats unset)
- `repair` after a patch: every state of `rowStates(row)` (plan 157)

## `view()` for the screens
- Top-level fields (level, phase, options, question, jokers, jokers_left, settings) = the game the turn''s seat plays: `row.state` (rr-coop) or `seats[turn].state` (rr-competitive); a finished session: the winner''s, else the last answerer''s
- `last` = the session''s last final answer, with `seat` (the Correct/Wrong screens show whose answer it was even after the turn moved)
- New `session` (null outside sessions), `lib/types.ts` `Game.session`:
  - `mode`, `turn`, `seats: {player, status: "playing" | "out" | "won" | "lost", level, age_group, jokers_left}[]` (rr-coop: level and jokers the team''s, on every seat or once in the block: pick what part 7 needs least to repeat)
- `player`: the turn seat''s name in a session
- `can_undo` false (not gamemaster)

## Outlook (plan 65, decision 31)
- Session outlook at the Choice screen: `outlook.ts` takes the session''s seats: `rr-coop` = solo''s; `rr-competitive` = one outlook per distinct age group with `players` = its seats (`seenPerLevel` × that count), the lowest `k` shown
- The MD-8 stand-in constants in `seenPerLevel` and `qgen report --simulate` stay for part 4 (`task 1395: write plan: Engine consumers of multiplayer sessions`); the Choice screen''s notice is part 6''s

## Tests (AGENTS.md: few, lasting)
- One `session.test.ts`: a scripted rr-coop session (turn rotation, `not_your_turn`, shared jokers, wrong = all lost) and a rr-competitive one with two age groups (no card twice, out seat skipped, last standing wins, first to 12 wins); seeded `Io`
- Frozen fixtures (`engine/fixtures/`, `game.test.ts`) replay unchanged; no new fixture

## Tasks
1. `rr-coop`: session start (state, turn, jokers, `customized`), `mode_not_built` to `api.ts`, turn rotation and the turn''s seat in `pick`/`joker`/`answer`, `HistoryEntry.seat`, team end, `view().session` + `last.seat`, `lib/types.ts`; the rr-coop half of `session.test.ts`; `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Round-robin co-op": as-built line
2. `rr-competitive` (`--model opus`): per-seat states and `age_groups`, session supply check (seat × level matching, `Supply.levels[].seat`), per-seat draw with the cross-seat exclusion and its fallback, turns skipping out seats, out/first-to-12/last-standing ends, `view()` per seat; the rr-competitive half of `session.test.ts`; `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Round-robin competitive": as-built line, decision 278
3. Session outlook: `outlook.ts` per age group for rr-competitive, rr-coop as solo; exported for the Choice screen (part 6); `outlook.test.ts` one case only if the per-age-group split needs it

## Done when
- `npm run check`, `npm test` (fixture replay unchanged), `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass
- Engine tests play both modes start to finish, each end condition reached
- The UI still offers neither mode (`BUILT_MODES` unchanged)', 'Two of the new multiplayer modes take turns: in the team version everyone climbs one shared ladder of questions together, one question each in turn, with one shared set of helpers; in the competitive version each player climbs their own ladder with their own helpers and difficulty, and a wrong answer knocks only them out. This part writes those rules into the game''s core, so the screens built later only show what the rules decide. It also makes sure two players in one game never get the same question and that the question supply is checked for everyone before a game starts.', '2026-10-16T19:43:17Z', 1393);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (159, 16, 'Competitive (timed) in the engine', 590, 'Part 3 of `plan 152: masterplan`. The engine rules of `timed` (Competitive timed) on the session shape of `plan 157: Session model and save format` (seats, `Seat.lives`/`out`/`result`, the acting seat) and the session start of `plan 158: Round-robin modes in the engine`. Engine only: no screens, no input binding, no sound, no `BUILT_MODES` change.

## Binding
- Milestone 16 "Outcome" and `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Competitive timed" (D-80): the spec; replaces `decision 23: Competitive format (OQ-37)?`''s timed part
- `decision 276: Timed mode: after a drop-out, how many questions does a round have?`: players still in at the round''s start
- `decision 277: Multiplayer sessions in the save: one games[] row per session, with seats`: `row.state` = the shared question flow, `level` = round; `HistoryEntry.seat`; timed fields additive, no further `SAVE_VERSION` bump
- `decision 280: Timed mode: everyone out at one round end means nobody wins`
- `decision 281: Timed mode: round 12 without a correct answer repeats as another sudden-death round`
- `decision 282: Timed mode: the Esc menu and the Steam overlay pause the clock and hide the question`
- D-92 (`plans/decisions.md`): nothing pauses outside `timed`; unchanged
- Shared rules (D-74, D-88): no skip, undo, replace, level, settings; flag only logs (`decision 60: One mechanism for questions with problems: flag or report?`)
- D-82 / plan 65: seen per save, `game_id` = the session row
- Gate: plan 157''s `actor(row, seat)` first (`seat_missing`, `seat_unknown`, `seat_out`); `timed` has no `turn`

## Clock
- `Io.ms?: number`: epoch ms of the action; `lib/engine.ts` `io()` sets `Date.now()`; missing (tests, fixtures) = `Date.parse(io.now)`
- Every deadline in the save as epoch ms; the engine has no timer: the client counts down from `view()` and sends `expire`; the engine checks every claim against the stored timestamps, so a reload or a slow frame can''t change the outcome
- Constants next to `STANDARD_JOKERS` (`engine/state.ts`): `QUESTION_MS = 30000`, `HINT_MS = 8000`, `CLAIM_MS = 6000`, `LIVES = 3`
- Deadlines inclusive, no grace

## State (`row.state.timed`, additive)
- `round_size`: seats in at the round''s start (decision 276); `round_done`: questions ended in this round; `round_correct: number[]`: seats with a correct answer this round
- `shown_at`: when the question on screen appeared (shifted by pauses); `claim: {seat, at} | null`; `paused_at: number | null`
- `Seat.lives` 3 at start, `Seat.out`, `Seat.result` (plan 157)
- `row.state.level` = round; round 12 repeats keep `level` 12 (`timed.repeat` count only for the view)

## Starting (`new` with `players`, `mode: "timed"`)
- Plan 158''s session start, timed part: one `age_group` for all, `bundles`; `jokers` refused (`timed_no_jokers`), budget all 0, `customized` false; `answers` off refused as every non-gamemaster mode
- No cards: one question at a time, opened at once (`cards: 0`, solo''s `openIfNoCards`); `shown_at` = start
- Supply check (GF-5): N questions per level (N = players): plan 158''s seat × level matching with N copies of the one range; `supply_short` as today
- Draw per question: `selection.draw` n = 1 at `level`, `perLevel` = `round_size` for the later levels'' check; never a question shown earlier in the session (`offered`); categories avoided over the session''s history as solo''s
- Extra round-12 rounds (decision 281): same draw; empty → the age group''s whole range; still empty → session ends, no winner; never `level_empty` mid-session

## Actions (all through `gameAction`)
- `settle(row, ms)` first in every timed action: applies a passed deadline (claim past `at + CLAIM_MS` → wrong; unclaimed past `shown_at + QUESTION_MS` → expired) before the action itself; not while paused
- `claim {seat}`: question on screen, no claim open (`claim_taken`), not paused (`paused`); stores `{seat, at: ms}`; the question clock stops (a claim at 29 s still gets 6 s); a claim that `settle` found too late: the settled state comes back, no claim, no error
- `answer {seat, index}`: only the claimer (`claim_first`, `not_your_claim`); in time → correct or wrong; late → settled as the timeout (wrong), not an error
- `expire` (no seat; plan 157''s `actor` skips clock actions): `settle`; nothing passed → `not_expired` (409, `ms` left), so a hasty client can''t skip a question
- `pause`, `resume` (no seat): `paused_at` = ms (`already_paused`); `resume` shifts `shown_at` and `claim.at` by the paused span, clears it (`not_paused`); who may open the Esc menu is part 5''s (`task 1396: write plan: Per-player controls`), the client wiring part 8''s (`task 1399: write plan: Timed game screens, drama and sound`)
- `joker`, `pick`, `skip`, `reveal`: refused in `timed` (`timed_no_jokers`, `no_cards`, `gamemaster_only` as today)
- `abandon`: the whole session (plan 158)
- New codes in `state.ts` `ERRORS` (D-57): `claim_taken`, `claim_first`, `not_your_claim`, `paused`, `already_paused`, `not_paused`, `not_expired`, `timed_no_jokers`

## A question ends
- Correct: seat into `round_correct`; round 12: that seat `won`, every other seat in `lost`, `row.result = "won"`, session over
- Wrong or claim timeout: seat `out`, `result: "lost"`; one seat left in → it wins at once (`won`, `row.result = "won"`)
- Unclaimed 30 s: nothing else
- Each: `see()` once (D-82: shown = counted, claimed or not), one `HistoryEntry` `{level, question_id, correct, seat?, chosen, hints: shown at the end}` plus `timeout: true` / `unclaimed: true`; `last` with `seat`; `round_done + 1`; round complete → round end, else the next question (`shown_at` = ms)
- Hints shown: `min(hints, floor((at − shown_at) / HINT_MS))`, `at` = the claim''s time or the end (0 to 3 at 8, 16, 24 s); derived, stored only in the history entry

## Round end
- Every seat in without a correct answer this round: `lives − 1`; 0 → `out`, `lost`
- Nobody left → no winner (decision 280): `row.result = "lost"`, `phase` `lost`
- One left → it wins
- Round < 12 → `level + 1`; round 12 → another level-12 round (decision 281); `round_size` = seats in, `round_done` 0, `round_correct` []

## `view()`
- Plan 158''s `session` block (`seats[].status`, `player`, `last.seat`) plus per seat `lives`, `correct_this_round`, `last_chance` (round''s last question, no correct answer yet this round)
- `session.timed`: `round`, `sudden_death` (level 12), `repeat`, `round_size`, `question_in_round`, `deadline` (ms; null while claimed or paused), `claim: {seat, deadline} | null`, `paused`, `hints_shown` (from `io.ms`), `all_at_risk` (every seat in on its last life and `last_chance`); `lib/types.ts`
- While paused: `question`, `answers`, hints null (decision 282)
- `jokers` empty, `can_undo` false

## Tests (AGENTS.md: few, lasting)
- The timed part of plan 158''s `session.test.ts`, seeded `Io` with `ms`: claim and answer, claim timeout, `not_expired`, a pause shifting deadlines, round end life loss, decision 276''s round size after a drop-out, round 12 win, round 12 repeat, nobody-wins end, last one standing
- Frozen fixtures (`engine/fixtures/`, `game.test.ts`) replay unchanged

## Tasks
1. Core (`--model opus`): `Io.ms` (+ `lib/engine.ts`), constants, `row.state.timed`, timed `new` (lives, no jokers, cards 0, N-per-level supply check, per-question draw), `settle`, `claim`/`answer`/`expire`, question end, round end, round 12 sudden death and repeat, no-winner and last-one ends, seen and history entries, error codes; the timed half of `session.test.ts` (without pause)
2. Pause and view: `pause`/`resume`, the paused refusals and hidden question, `view().session.timed` and the per-seat fields, `lib/types.ts`; the pause case in `session.test.ts`; `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Competitive timed": as-built lines (clock, decisions 276, 280, 281, 282), "Open detail" line removed

## Done when
- `npm run check`, `npm test` (fixture replay unchanged), `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass
- Engine tests play `timed` to each end (round 12 win, last one standing, nobody wins)
- The UI still doesn''t offer `timed` (`BUILT_MODES` unchanged)', 'The timed competitive mode is a race: every player sees the same question, anyone can grab it, and the one who grabs it has six seconds to answer; wrong answers knock players out and rounds without a right answer cost lives, until one player is left or someone wins the final sudden-death round. This part writes those rules into the game''s core, with the clock kept as recorded times rather than running timers, so reloading or a slow screen can never change who wins. It also settles the rare endings: everyone losing their last life together, the final round passing without a right answer, and what happens when the game is paused mid-question.', '2026-10-16T21:00:14Z', 1394);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (160, 16, 'Engine consumers of multiplayer sessions', 580, 'Part 4 of `plan 152: masterplan`. What reads finished or running sessions: Steam achievements, opt-in telemetry and `qgen telemetry`/`--played`, the supply outlook and `qgen report --simulate`. Built on the session shape of `plan 157: Session model and save format` and the mode rules of `plan 158: Round-robin modes in the engine` and `plan 159: Competitive (timed) in the engine`. No screens, no `BUILT_MODES` change.

## Binding
- `decision 285: Achievements from multiplayer sessions: every seat earns for the save; tower achievements need a win at the top level` (this plan''s)
- `decision 286: Telemetry of multiplayer sessions: one game per played game, a player count, timed answers not clean` (this plan''s)
- `decision 276: Timed mode: after a drop-out, how many questions does a round have?`: players still in at the round''s start
- `decision 277: Multiplayer sessions in the save: one games[] row per session, with seats`; plan 157''s helpers `rowStates`, `rowPlayers`, `seatResult`
- `decision 73: Achievement list (SW-11)?`, `decision 139: Achievement triggers derived without a save change (SW-11)`, `decision 74: Gamemaster mode earns no achievements`, decision 19; `plan 86: Achievements (SW-11)`: derived, never stored
- `decision 119: Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file`, decision 128 (mod questions never), `decision 122: Played difficulty: calibration model for qgen report --played`
- D-77, D-80, D-82 (`plans/decisions.md`); `decision 31: Low-supply warning: below how many fresh games left (K) should the game start warn?`

## What exists (2026-10-16)
- `engine/achievements.ts`: `ACHIEVEMENTS` with the three mode wins (`mode:`), `inSteamworks` (mode win only once in `BUILT_MODES`), `qualifies(row)` on `row.state` with `cards` 4, `earned` over `row.state` only; `MODE_WIN` from `gameMode`; comments say MD-8
- `lib/achievements.ts`: unlock at load and when a row gets a `result`: works for sessions as is
- `engine/telemetry.ts`: one `TelemetryGame` per row from `row.state`, key `<id>@<started_on>`, `telemetryStart` from `row.state.history.length`; `report-server/src/validate-telemetry.ts` keeps known fields only; `authoring/tools/played.py` keys counts by mode
- `engine/outlook.ts` `seenPerLevel`: `rr-competitive` = game × players, `timed` = 1 (backlog B-15); `per` = cards (≥ 1); per-age-group split for rr-competitive is `task 1409: Session outlook per age group`
- `authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts`: rr-coop run as solo, rr-competitive as N solo games, `runTimed` a model outside the engine; `qgen.py` `SIM_MODES`, `SIM_MULTI`, help text "until MD-8/MD-9"; `plans/16-content-target.md` "Mode approximations"
- Other readers of `games[]`: `played.py` reads telemetry, not the save; the authoring pages don''t read the save''s games; `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` plays solo; `authoring/tools/demo_saves.mjs`/`gallery_saves.mjs` session saves are `task 1400: write plan: Multiplayer UI strings and gallery`''s; rich presence (`Game.svelte`) and the client''s resume (`lib/api.ts`, `lib/engine.ts` `newest`) are the screens'' (`task 1398: write plan: Round-robin game screens`, `task 1399: write plan: Timed game screens, drama and sound`)

## Achievements (decision 285)
- `qualifies(row)` per mode: not gamemaster, not `customized`, no `difficulty`, 12 levels, answers on; cards 4 (solo, rr-*) or 0 (`timed`); no `admin_replace` in any state of `rowStates(row)`; rr-competitive: shared `row.state.settings` plus every seat''s
- A won session''s "winning game": rr-coop `row.state`; rr-competitive the seat with `result: "won"`; timed `row.state` with the winner''s history entries (`seat`)
- Tower win = the winning game answered level 12 right (timed: the sudden-death answer); last-standing and timed drop-out wins aren''t
- Win-based (FIRST_WIN, WINS_10, WINS_50, WIN_ADULTS, WIN_ALL_AGES, WIN_NO_JOKERS, ALL_JOKERS_WIN, SOPLO_SAVE, NIGHT_OWL, POLYGLOT): tower wins only, one per session, age group and jokers of the winning game
- Mode wins (`MODE_WIN`): any session with `row.result === "won"`
- Joker, knowledge, habit ones: every state of `rowStates(row)` (`entries()` per state, `correct` from every seat)
- Comments MD-8 → `milestone 16: Local multiplayer: game modes and controls`; `inSteamworks` unchanged (`task 1401: write plan: Shipping the multiplayer modes and docs` adds the modes)
- `achievements.test.ts`: one case per mode (tower win counts, last-standing win only the mode''s); only lasting ones

## Telemetry (decision 286)
- `telemetryGame` per mode: rr-coop, timed one game per row; rr-competitive one per seat, key `<id>@<started_on>#<seat>`; `telemetryStart` and `sessionRows` per key (seat state''s history length)
- `players`: `rowPlayers(row).length`; timed: `reached` = round, jokers 0, answers = entries with `correct` (claimed), result the row''s
- Nothing personal: no names, no seat order beyond the per-seat key
- Contract: `players` optional int 1–64 in `report-server/src/validate-telemetry.ts` (missing = 1), fixture, `seed-telemetry.mjs`; plan 105''s contract doc wherever it lives (`rg "customized" plans`); deploy is the developer''s (`trivia-report-server deploy`), an older server drops the field
- `played.py`: `games.players` count `day|mode|players`; timed answers fold with clean = 0; `qgen report --played` shows the players count per mode

## Outlook and simulation (decision 276, B-15)
- `seenPerLevel`: timed = players (one question per player still in, worst case nobody drops) and `per` = players (the supply check''s N per level); rr-coop = solo; rr-competitive as `task 1409: Session outlook per age group` leaves it
- `/api/outlook` (`engine/api.ts` `outlook`): body with `players` and rr-competitive''s `age_groups` if task 1409 didn''t add them; the Choice screen''s call is `task 1397: write plan: Mode row, session setup and join screen`''s
- `simulate.ts` on the engine''s sessions: `new` with `players` (`Sim 1…N`), seat-tagged `pick`/`joker`/`answer`; rr-coop and rr-competitive turns as the engine rotates them; timed: `Io.ms` stepped, every question claimed by a random seat still in, right with `pCorrect` (`strong`: always right, so round 12 ends it), `expire` never needed; unit = one session; `runTimed` and the N-solo loop removed
- `qgen.py`: `SIM_MULTI` gets `rr-coop`; help text without MD-8/MD-9; `outlook` with players
- Docs: `plans/16-content-target.md` "Mode approximations" → the engine''s modes; `plans/backlog.md` B-15 done (decision 276); decision 200 `rg "MD-8|MD-9|until MD"` in code and these docs

## Tasks
1. Achievements from sessions (after `task 1408: rr-competitive in the engine: per-seat games, session supply, ends` and plan 159''s core): `qualifies` per mode, winning game and tower-win rule, `earned` over `rowStates`, comments, `achievements.test.ts` cases; `plans/18-steam-integration.md` SW-11 note (decision 285)
2. Telemetry of sessions (after the same): `telemetry.ts` per mode, `players`, keys per seat; report server validator, fixture, seed script, contract doc; `played.py` players count and timed not clean, `--played` line (decision 286)
3. Timed outlook and the engine-mode simulation (after task 1409 and plan 159''s core): `seenPerLevel`/`per` for timed, `/api/outlook` body, `simulate.ts` on sessions, `qgen.py`, `outlook.test.ts` one timed case, docs above; `qgen report --simulate --mode all` runs (time it vs. today''s 56 s default matrix, note it in plan 16 if it grows a lot)

## Done when
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass
- `qgen report --simulate --mode all` runs every mode on the engine; no MD-8/MD-9 stand-in left in code or `plans/16-content-target.md`
- A scripted session of each mode (engine tests) gives the decision 285 achievements and the decision 286 telemetry games', 'Several parts of the game read what was played after the fact: Steam achievements, the anonymous play statistics players may opt into, the warning that the question supply is running low, and the developer''s tool that estimates how many games the question pool lasts. This part teaches each of them about multiplayer games, so that a family game night earns the right trophies, is counted fairly in the statistics, and that the supply estimates match how many questions the new modes really use.', '2026-10-16T21:03:04Z', 1395);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (161, 16, 'Per-player controls', 480, 'Part 5 of `plan 152: masterplan`. The client layer between devices and the session''s seats: which device acts for which seat, the filter that lets only the acting seat''s input reach the game, the `timed` claim inputs, the Esc menu and lost pads in a session. After `plan 156: Prompts follow the last input` (its switch rule is reused) and `plan 157: Session model and save format` (the acting seat in the engine API).

## Binding
- Milestone 16 "Two kinds of control": before a session every device drives the shared UI; in a session each pad is one player, keyboard and mouse together one player
- `decision 273: Keyboard-only turn-based sessions: what does a player''s own key do?`: nothing; keyboard and mouse act for whoever''s turn it is. Keys are picked only in keyboard-only `timed` sessions (the developer''s note: the answer''s "timed sessions" means keyboard-only ones; with a pad, keyboard and mouse are one player with one claim key)
- `decision 274: Pads plus keyboard: one keyboard player, or several key players?`: keyboard and mouse exactly one player once a pad has joined
- `decision 275: Timed mode, keyboard-only: how does the claimer answer in the 6 seconds?`: mouse click or the answer keys
- `decision 288: Local multiplayer: who opens the Esc menu in a session, and who drives it` (this plan)
- `decision 289: Local multiplayer: a controller lost mid-session waits for a controller to take the seat` (this plan)
- `decision 290: Timed mode: the claim input per kind of player` (this plan)
- `decision 282: Timed mode: the Esc menu and the Steam overlay pause the clock and hide the question`
- `decision 277: Multiplayer sessions in the save: one games[] row per session, with seats`: no device in the save; the binding is client-only
- `milestone 17: Remote Play Together`: device-agnostic; a remote guest is one more pad; no Remote Play code here
- `decision 272: Right stick: what it does beyond switching prompts to the pad`, `decision 126: Image peek: which pad button and key?`: unchanged

## What exists (2026-10-16)
- `lib/input.svelte.ts`: scope stack, `dispatch(action)`, `Action = Intent & { device }`, one global `lastDevice`; mouse clicks go straight to DOM handlers, outside `dispatch`; `confirm` presses the focused control (`focus.ts` `press`) → `el.click()`
- `lib/gamepad.svelte.ts`: polls all standard pads, any pad dispatches; `padStyle` one global, from Steam''s `inputTypes()` (all pads together, `steamStyle`) or `Gamepad.id`
- Question pad map: face buttons pick, LT back, RT submit, R3 peek, LB/RB joker focus
- Plan 156 adds `touched` (any button/stick switches prompts) and mouse-move switching

## Investigation first (throw-away, findings into `plans/14-input.md` section 3)
- `navigator.getGamepads()` length and listed pads in Electron (the shipped version) on Linux and Windows, with and without Steam Input; Chromium''s cap (`kItemsLengthCap`, 4 in older builds); XInput''s 4 on Windows
- Pad identity: index after disconnect/reconnect, after a second pad connects meanwhile; `Gamepad.id` stability
- Steam: `GetInputTypeForHandle` order ↔ `Gamepad.index` (is per-pad style reliable, or only the set); the Deck''s built-in pad
- What a worker can''t measure (Windows, real pads, Steam Input) goes to the developer as a `once` decision with exact steps; nothing below waits for it: binding is by index, per-pad style falls back to `Gamepad.id`
- No player cap of our own either way: the join screen takes every pad the platform lists

## Model (`lib/seats.ts` pure core + `lib/seats.svelte.ts` state)
- `Source`: `{ pad: index }` | `"keyboard"` | `"mouse"`; every `Action` carries it (`device` stays for prompts and mods)
- `Binding` per seat, join order: `{ pad: index }` | `"kbm"` (keyboard and mouse) | `{ key: string }` (keyboard-only `timed`) | `"shared"` (keyboard-only round-robin: no device, keyboard and mouse act for the turn)
- Session binding set by the join screen (part 6) when the session starts; cleared when the session ends; stored in `sessionStorage` by game id so a reload keeps it (missing → decision 289''s rebind dialog)
- `seatOf(source, intent, view)`: pad → its seat; keyboard/mouse → the `kbm` seat, else (keyboard-only) the turn seat (round-robin) or the claimer (timed), a claim intent with a key → that key''s seat
- `may(seat, view)`: round-robin: `seat === turn`; `timed`: no claim open → any seat in may claim, claim open → only the claimer; out seats never; from `view().session` (plans 158, 159)
- No session: no filter, every device acts (as today)

## Filter
- In a session `dispatch` resolves the seat, then: `menu` always passes (decision 288); a scope marked `shared` (Esc menu, flag dialog, results/victory, the lost-pad dialog) takes every device; any other scope gets the action only if `may(seat)`; dropped actions do nothing (no sound, no focus move)
- Mouse: a capture-phase `pointerdown`/`click` listener drops clicks when the top scope isn''t shared and the keyboard-and-mouse source may not act; `[data-shared]` controls (corner menu button) always pass
- `acting.seat`: set synchronously while an accepted action or click runs; `lib/engine.ts` game actions add `seat` from it, so pad `confirm` → `click()` → handler carries the right seat; the engine''s `not_your_turn`/`not_your_claim` stay the backstop
- Prompts: in a session only accepted input (and plan 156''s `touched` of a device that may act) moves `lastDevice` and `padStyle`; per-pad style `padStyleOf(index)` (Steam per handle if the investigation allows, else `styleOf(Gamepad.id)`); `seatDevice(seat)` → kind + style for part 7''s turn banner and part 8''s claim prompts
- Shared focus ring: one, driven by whoever may act

## `timed` claim (decision 290)
- New intent `claim` (with `key` for key players): pad LB/RB in the timed question scope''s pad map; Space for the `kbm` seat; each picked key for key seats; a click on the claim control (drawn by part 8) for the `kbm` seat
- Claimer''s answer: as the Question screen today (face buttons; A–D/1–4 or click, decision 275)
- `claimKeyOk(key, taken)` for the join screen (part 6): single letter or digit, not bound by the Question screen, not Enter/Esc/Space/Backspace/arrows, distinct; the Question screen''s key list exported once (decision 199), not copied
- `claimLabel(seat)` for prompts: bumper glyph, «Espacio», or the key

## Esc menu and lost pads
- Esc menu: any seat''s `menu` opens it; shared while open (decision 288); `timed` pause/resume on open/close is part 8''s wiring (`task 1399: write plan: Timed game screens, drama and sound`)
- Pad lost (decision 289): seat unbound on `gamepaddisconnected`; `SeatLost.svelte` modal when the seat is needed (round-robin: its turn; `timed`: at once, sending `pause`, `resume` on close, through the same helper as part 8''s Esc wiring, whichever lands first adds it); A on the returning pad or any unbound pad takes the seat; a seat already out never asks
- Strings for the dialog in es, es-ES, en, de per `locales/style/<locale>.md`

## Tasks
1. Investigation (`--web`): the measurements above, findings into `plans/14-input.md` section 3; a `once` decision for what needs the developer''s hardware
2. Seats and the filter (`--model opus`): `Source` on actions (keys, pads, clicks), `lib/seats.ts`/`seats.svelte.ts` (binding, `seatOf`, `may`, sessionStorage), the `dispatch` filter and `shared` scopes, mouse capture, `acting.seat` into `lib/engine.ts`, prompts from accepted input only, `padStyleOf`/`seatDevice`, join helpers for part 6 (bind an unbound pad''s A, the `kbm` join, `claimKeyOk`); throw-away check with fake pads and a fake session view; `plans/14-input.md` section 3 and IN-6 rewritten (no "Later"), decision 24 noted as superseded by milestone 16
3. Claim inputs: `claim` intent, LB/RB, Space, picked keys, claim-control click, `claimLabel`; after `task 1412: Timed core in the engine: clock, claims, rounds, lives, ends`
4. Lost pads and the Esc menu in a session: `SeatLost.svelte`, rebind, reload rebind, `pause`/`resume` in `timed`, the overlay as shared scope and `[data-shared]` corner button; strings in four locales

## Order and dependencies
- 1 first (2 doesn''t wait for its developer decision); 2 after `task 1406: Acting seat in the engine API` and plan 156''s tasks (1380, 1381); 3 after 2 and task 1412; 4 after 2 and `task 1413: Timed pause and view in the engine`
- Part 6 (join screen) builds on task 2''s helpers; parts 7 and 8 on `seatDevice`/`claimLabel`

## Out of scope
- Join screen UI, turn banner, timed screens and sounds (parts 6–8)
- Steam Input action sets; phones; network
- Gamemaster mode and «Solo o en grupo»: unchanged, every device drives the one player

## Done when
- With fake pads and a stubbed session view: a pad not on turn does nothing on a game screen and doesn''t flip prompts; the turn''s pad and the `kbm` seat act; the menu opens from anyone; a lost pad''s seat is taken by another pad
- `plans/14-input.md` section 3 describes what''s built, no "Later" for IN-6; per-commit checks pass', 'In local multiplayer each person in the room plays with their own controller, or everyone shares the keyboard and mouse. The game has to know which controller belongs to which player, let only the right player act at each moment, and give each player an obvious way to grab a question in the timed race. This part builds that layer between the controllers and the game, and settles what happens with the pause menu and with a controller that drops out mid-game.', '2026-10-16T21:06:20Z', 1396);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (162, 16, 'Mode row, session setup and join screen', 400, 'Part 6 of `plan 152: masterplan`. The screens before a local multiplayer session: the three modes on the Choice screen''s mode row, the new Join screen, the per-mode setup and the session start through the Bundles screen. After `plan 157: Session model and save format` (`players` in `new`, seats), `plan 161: Per-player controls` (binding, join helpers) and the engine starts of `plan 158: Round-robin modes in the engine` / `plan 159: Competitive (timed) in the engine`; refers to `plan 151: Bundle selection on its own full screen` for the Bundles screen.

## Binding
- `decision 291: Local multiplayer setup: flow and where each setting lives` (this plan): Player → Choice → Join → Bundles → Level
- `decision 292: Join screen: joining, leaving, names and claim keys` (this plan)
- `decision 293: Unbuilt multiplayer modes: on the mode row in dev mode only` (this plan)
- `decision 273: Keyboard-only turn-based sessions: what does a player''s own key do?`: nothing; keys picked only in keyboard-only `timed` sessions
- `decision 274: Pads plus keyboard: one keyboard player, or several key players?`: keyboard and mouse exactly one seat once a pad has joined
- `decision 290: Timed mode: the claim input per kind of player`: allowed claim keys (`claimKeyOk`, plan 161)
- `decision 158: Bundle selection in every mode, apart from customization`, `decision 264: Bundle screen (two columns) reviewed in /gallery?`, `decision 268: Short-group marks after the flow change`: Bundles screen holds the supply report and start; Choice none
- `decision 285: Achievements from multiplayer sessions: every seat earns for the save; tower achievements need a win at the top level`: customized (jokers off standard) = no achievements, as solo
- `decision 279: Round-robin screens: the Level screen is the turn handover, no screen of its own`: seat colour + device glyph per seat (defined here, reused by parts 7, 8)
- `decision 53: Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?`: mode letters per catalog, collision check of `npm run check`
- `decision 168: Store texts name only the built game modes`; `BUILT_MODES` grows only in part 10 (`task 1401: write plan: Shipping the multiplayer modes and docs`)
- Names per `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` "Mode names" (proposals: «Por turnos en equipo», «Por turnos, todos contra todos», «Contrarreloj»); the developer reviews them in part 9''s gallery
- Deck sizes: fits 1280×800, 1280×720, 1920×1080 (`plan 46: Deck layout and controller-only text entry (SW-4)`)

## What exists (2026-10-16)
- `game/Game.svelte`: `Screen` union, Player → Choice → Bundles → Level; `startGame` sends `new` with `player`; `S.*` from `screens/registry.ts` `screenFor`, names in `lib/mods.ts` `SCREENS`
- `game/screens/Choice.svelte`: `MODE_ROW` (solo, gamemaster) filtered by `BUILT_MODES`; age group line, «Personalizar partida» (jokers); `ChoiceDraft` in `game/choiceDraft.ts` (`bodyOf`, `choiceOf`)
- `game/screens/Bundles.svelte`: supply on every toggle (`fetchOutlook`), `SupplyReport`, `SupplyNotice`, «¡A jugar!»
- `game/screens/Player.svelte`: known players (1–9), new name field, `LetterPicker.svelte` / Steam floating keyboard for pads, `cleanName` via the engine
- `lib/desktop.ts` `devMode`

## Mode row (Choice)
- `MODE_ROW` gets `rr-coop`, `rr-competitive`, `timed`: name, one-line about, key `mode.<id>Key` per catalog; icons from `Icon.svelte` (new ones only if none fits)
- Shown: `BUILT_MODES`, plus in `devMode` the unbuilt ones with `PLACEHOLDER(<shipping task>)` on the tile (decision 293); `api.ts` `new` takes a dev flag that lifts `mode_not_built`, set by `lib/engine.ts` only in `devMode`
- Order: solo, gamemaster, rr-coop, rr-competitive, timed; the row wraps or narrows to fit Deck sizes with five tiles
- Preset unchanged (`playerMode`: session rows have no `player_id`); `?mode=` accepts a shown mode
- Per mode (decision 291): rr-coop, timed: the age group line; rr-competitive: no group line (a line «each player picks on the next screen»); «Personalizar partida» for rr-coop and rr-competitive (jokers), hidden in timed; gamemaster fields never
- Title: a multiplayer mode → plural title («¿Cómo juegan?»), no name
- `ChoiceDraft`: mode union widens; `bodyOf` per mode (timed: no `jokers`)
- «Seguir»: multiplayer mode → Join, else Bundles as today

## Join screen (`game/screens/Join.svelte`, new, scope `join`)
- `"Join"` in `SCREENS` (`lib/mods.ts`) and `S.Join` through `screenFor`; `modding/` screen list gains it
- Layout: a row/grid of seat cards in join order (seat colour, device glyph or «Teclado y ratón» / the claim key, name, rr-competitive: age group, remove control); a «press A to join» card per still unbound pad (count from `navigator.getGamepads()`), a «join with keyboard» card; minimum-2 reason under «Seguir»
- Joining (decision 292, through plan 161''s helpers): unbound pad A → seat `{pad}`; bound pad B → leaves its own seat; keyboard card (Enter/click) → keyboard seat; no pad seated: more keyboard seats allowed (rr-*: binding `shared`; timed: «press your key» capture right away, `claimKeyOk`, refusal reason shown, re-pick from the card); a pad seated: one `kbm` seat only; pad A refused with a notice while 2+ keyboard seats exist; a lone keyboard seat turns `kbm` when a pad joins (key dropped)
- No cap of our own: grid scrolls (`data-nav-scroll`) past what fits; tested with 8 seats
- Names: every seat needs one, distinct by casefold (engine''s `player_twice` as backstop); the seat''s name control opens a chooser: known players not yet seated (recency, keys 1–9), a new name (field; LetterPicker for pads; Steam floating keyboard as Player); reuse Player.svelte''s parts (extract a shared `NamePicker.svelte`, decision 199); first seat preset to the Player screen''s name; new focus on a joined seat''s name control
- Age group (rr-competitive): per seat ←/→ stepper over the age groups, preset from that player''s `playerChoice`, default `DEFAULT_AGE_GROUP`
- Seat colours: one palette by join order in a shared module (`game/seats.ts` or next to plan 161''s `lib/seats.ts`), contrast checked on the night background; parts 7 and 8 import it
- Before start every device drives the shared UI (milestone 16); only the join/leave inputs above are per device
- Back (Backspace, B of an unbound pad, corner): Choice, seats and names kept in `Game.svelte`
- «Seguir»: ≥ 2 seats, all named (timed keyboard-only: all with keys) → Bundles

## Session start
- `Game.svelte`: `chosen` + a `seats` draft (names, bindings, groups) kept across Choice ↔ Join ↔ Bundles
- Bundles: title plural for sessions; supply per whole session: `fetchOutlook` / supply body with `players` (count) and rr-competitive `age_groups` (task 1409, plan 160''s `/api/outlook`); `SupplyReport` names the seat for `supply_short` levels with `seat` (`Supply.levels[].seat`); preset bundles from the Player-screen player''s `playerChoice`
- `startGame`: `new` with `players: string[]` (join order), `mode`, `bundles`, `age_group` / `age_groups`, `jokers` if customized; on success plan 161''s session binding set (seats → bindings, `sessionStorage` by game id); greeting names all players (one line, truncated at Deck size)
- Refusals (`player_twice`, `players_too_few`, `supply_short`, `timed_no_jokers`) shown on Bundles as today''s `refused`
- Then the Level screen: parts 7, 8 take over

## Tasks
1. Mode row and per-mode Choice: the three tiles (names, abouts, keys in es, es-ES, en, de per `locales/style/<locale>.md`), devMode gate and `api.ts` dev flag (decision 293), per-mode group line / «Personalizar» / title, `ChoiceDraft` and `bodyOf`; after task 1407 (rr-coop start in the engine) and task 1412 (timed start)
2. Join screen (`--model opus`): `Join.svelte`, `NamePicker.svelte` extracted from Player, seat cards, join/leave/keyboard rules (decision 292), timed key capture, rr-competitive group stepper, seat colours module, `SCREENS` + `screenFor`, strings in four locales; after plan 161''s seats-and-filter task (join helpers, `claimKeyOk`) and task 1408 (`age_groups`)
3. Session start through Bundles: seats draft in `Game.svelte`, plural titles, session supply (players, `age_groups`, `seat` in `SupplyReport`), `new` with `players`, binding handed to plan 161, greeting, refusals; after task 2, task 1409 and task 1406
4. Docs: `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` (mode row with five modes, Join screen, flow), `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Mode screen as built" (multiplayer line), `plans/14-input.md` (scope `join`, join inputs), `modding/` (screen `Join`); `rg "Player → Choice → Bundles"` and the old flow over comments and `.md` (decision 200); can go with task 3

## Check
- Node dev server (`npm run dev -w app/client`), devMode, at 1280×800 and 1920×1080; fake pads (stubbed `navigator.getGamepads()`, throw-away, like `trivia-gallery`''s): 4 pads + keyboard (5 seats), pads only, keyboard only (rr-coop: 3 shared seats; timed: 3 key seats, a refused key), 8 pads (scroll)
- Leave and rejoin, a pad refused while 2 keyboard seats exist, the lone keyboard seat turning `kbm`; names: known, new, duplicate refused; Back to Choice and forward keeps everything
- Each mode starts a session (`new` with `players`) and reaches the Level screen; rr-competitive with two age groups; a short supply names the seat
- Without devMode: the row shows only solo and gamemaster
- Per commit: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`

## Out of scope
- Game screens of a session (parts 7, 8), gallery shots (part 9: `task 1400: write plan: Multiplayer UI strings and gallery`), `BUILT_MODES` and store texts (part 10)
- Binding and input filter internals (plan 161)', 'Before a multiplayer game night starts, the family picks one of the three new multiplayer modes, everyone signs in with their own controller (or the keyboard), each person picks their name, and they choose difficulty and question sets. This part builds those screens: the new modes next to the existing ones, a join screen where each controller claims a spot, and the setup that passes everything to the game. It matters because it decides which controller plays for whom for the rest of the evening.', '2026-10-16T21:09:09Z', 1397);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (163, 16, 'Round-robin game screens', 390, 'Part 7 of `plan 152: masterplan`. The game screens of a round-robin session (`rr-coop`, `rr-competitive`) from the first Level screen to Victory/Wrong: whose turn it is, the team''s tower or one track per player, the joker tray, a player knocked out, the session''s end. On the engine of `plan 158: Round-robin modes in the engine` (`view().session`, `last.seat`), the seat device of `plan 161: Per-player controls` (`seatDevice`) and the seat colours of `plan 162: Mode row, session setup and join screen`. Reuses Level, Select, Question, Correct, Wrong, Victory (`game/screens/`); no copies (decision 199).

