INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (168, 17, 'Investigation: Remote Play input and session API', 710, 'Part 1 of `plan 153: masterplan`. Which Steam Remote Play calls the shell can use, how guests'' pads, keyboards and mice reach the game, and the answer parts 3, 4, 5, 7, 8 and 9 wait for. Not gated by `decision 284: Remote Play Together gate: single player, controller input and local multiplayer playtested?`: probes and findings only, no game code that stays.

## Answer the other parts wait for
- Recorded by task 3 below as `pm decision record "Remote Play Together: can a remote guest''s keyboard and mouse be a distinct player?"` (answer «yes» or «no», with the mechanism); parts 3, 4, 5, 7, 8 and 9 find it with `pm decision list --answered --grep "distinct player"`
- Already recorded: `decision 301: Remote Play API from the shell: own koffi load of the Steam library, v003 calls, sessions by polling` (how part 3 reaches the API; binding for part 3''s plan)

## Findings so far (task 1418, 2026-10-16)
- SDK 1.62 (`decision 69: Steamworks SDK libs for dev and the bridge''s SDK path`), `public/steam/isteamremoteplay.h`, interface `STEAMREMOTEPLAY_INTERFACE_VERSION003`; flat exports in `libsteam_api.so` and `steam_api64.dll`:
  - sessions: `GetSessionCount`, `GetSessionID`, `GetSessionSteamID`, `GetSessionClientName`, `GetSessionClientFormFactor` (`ESteamDeviceFormFactor`: phone, tablet, computer, TV, VR), `BGetSessionClientResolution`
  - invites: `ShowRemotePlayTogetherUI`, `BSendRemotePlayTogetherInvite`; callback `SteamRemotePlayTogetherGuestInvite_t`
  - direct input: `BEnableRemotePlayTogetherDirectInput` ("available via GetInput() instead of being merged with local input"), `DisableRemotePlayTogetherDirectInput`, `GetInput(RemotePlayInput_t*, max)` (64-byte events: session id, type mouse motion/button/wheel, key down/up; keys as USB scancodes + modifiers + UCS-4 char; mouse absolute normalized 0–1 or deltas)
  - guest cursor: `SetMouseVisibility`, `SetMousePosition`, `CreateMouseCursor` (BGRA), `SetMouseCursor`, per session
  - callbacks `SteamRemotePlaySessionConnected_t` (5701), `…Disconnected_t` (5702)
  - not in 1.62 (v004, newer SDK): `GetSessionGuestID`, `BSessionRemotePlayTogether`, session avatars
- Steam Input (binding): `GetRemotePlaySessionID(handle)` (0: no session), `GetInputTypeForHandle`, `GetGamepadIndexForController`, `GetConnectedControllers`
- `steamworks-ffi-node` 0.11.3 (`decision 28: Steam binding for the Electron shell?`): no `ISteamRemotePlay`; only `ISteamInput_GetRemotePlaySessionID` and the overlay''s Remote Play invite dialog (Windows only, `decision 70: Steam overlay in the Electron shell`); its koffi handle is a private field (`libraryLoader.getLibrary()`)
- Headless probe (Node, koffi 3.3.3, Steam running, App ID 480): `koffi.load` of SDK 1.62''s lib → init, `SteamAPI_SteamRemotePlay_v003`, 0 sessions, a second load of the same lib works, direct input on → true, `GetInput` → 0 events; the same with the trunk''s local `app/desktop/steamworks_sdk/` libs, which are a newer SDK (v004 exports): packaged builds ship those, so code calls only v003 functions
- Valve docs: only the host owns the game; Remote Play Together is on by default for games listed with local multiplayer/co-op (store setting); nothing on how guests'' pads reach the host OS, cursor drawing, or per-guest overlay toggles → live probe
- Community reports (unverified): on Windows guests'' pads are emulated XInput up to 4 slots, then nothing or DirectInput; some games see guests'' pads only through Steam Input → live probe step 2 on both hosts, and task 1396''s pad-count investigation (`task 1431: Pad count, identity and per-pad style: measure in Electron and Steam`)

## Open questions (live only)
- Guests'' pads in `navigator.getGamepads()` on Windows and Linux/SteamOS hosts (Steam''s virtual pads; Linux `uinput`), with our Steam Input init (`main.mjs` `steam.input.init(false)`) on
- Pad index ↔ guest: Steam Input handle''s session id + `GetGamepadIndexForController` vs `Gamepad.index`; fallback: connect order (session connected, then a new pad within seconds)
- Direct input: guests'' keyboard and mouse kept out of the Electron window (no DOM events), host''s unaffected; what the guest sees as cursor; off: merged into the host''s
- Steam''s per-guest overlay toggles (keyboard, mouse, controller): which exist, usable as the «no» branch''s off switch
- Guest leaving and rejoining: new session id or the same; pad disconnect order vs session disconnect (feeds `decision 283: Remote Play Together: what happens when a remote guest leaves mid-game?`)

## Answer rule (task 3)
- «yes»: on both hosts, direct input on keeps a guest''s keyboard and mouse out of the window and delivers them per session, the host''s input is unaffected, and the guest sees a usable cursor (Steam''s or one set by `SetMouseCursor`); then part 4 turns `rp key`/`rp mouse` events into a device of their own (scancode → our key names, normalized position → `elementFromPoint` click and hover)
- «no» otherwise; mechanism for ignoring remote keyboard and mouse: direct input on with events dropped if it keeps them out of the window, else Steam''s per-guest toggles (the join screen line tells the host)
- Probe numbers inconclusive on one host (e.g. Linux works, Windows not): «no» (one rule on every OS), the gap noted for a later look

## Tasks
1. Remote Play probe switch in the shell (`--worktree app`, not gated): `--rp-probe` flag (Steam launch option, works on Windows and Linux) in `app/desktop/main.mjs`, one block marked `PLACEHOLDER(<task 3''s id>)`, removed by task 3
   - after `startSteam`: own koffi load per decision 301 (koffi a direct dependency, binding''s version), poll on the existing 100 ms tick: sessions diffed → `session +/-` (id, Steam id, name, form factor), `GetInput` events → `rp key`/`rp mouse` (session, scancode/char, button, normalized position); every second `steam-input` (handles, type, session id, gamepad index) and, from the page via `executeJavaScript`, `pads` (index, id, pressed buttons)
   - window input: `before-input-event` → `dom key`; page `pointermove`/`pointerdown` listeners → `dom mouse` (throttled)
   - keys F9 direct input on/off, F10 a custom guest cursor (`CreateMouseCursor` + `SetMouseCursor` for every session), F11 flash a white frame and log ms until the next guest pad press
   - log to `<userData>/rp-probe.log` and stderr; the path and the last 8 lines in an on-screen corner box
   - headless check here: Spacewar 480, `trivia-desktop --rp-probe` starts, logs 0 sessions, F9 toggles; no guest needed
   - README row of `trivia-desktop` and `AGENTS.md` Commands: `--rp-probe` (removed again by task 3)
   - in a `beta` build: the developer''s checklist `decision 302: Remote Play Together live probe: guests'' pads, keyboard and mouse on a Windows and a Linux host` needs it uploaded; this task doesn''t upload (plan 89''s `trivia-steam upload`)
2. (the developer) `decision 302: Remote Play Together live probe: guests'' pads, keyboard and mouse on a Windows and a Linux host`, after part 2''s setup decision (`plan 153: masterplan` part 2, the plan "Steamworks switch and Remote Play test setup")
3. Findings and the answer (`--worktree app`; pending on decision 302 and, once it exists, part 2''s setup decision): the decision''s notes and log into `plans/14-input.md` "Remote Play Together" (replaces "works for free": guests'' pads per host OS, the pad ↔ guest mapping that works, direct input facts, overlay toggles, session ids on rejoin); `pm decision record` the answer above per the answer rule, body with the evidence; remove the probe block, the koffi dependency if nothing else uses it (part 3 re-adds it), its README/`AGENTS.md` lines (`rg rp-probe`, decision 200); if guests'' pads don''t reach `navigator.getGamepads()` on a host: a decision for the developer (read guests'' pads through Steam Input in the shell, or that host unsupported) instead of guessing

## Order
- 1 now; 2 after 1 is in a `beta` upload and part 2''s setup; 3 after 2
- Part 3''s plan (task 1421) may start from decision 301 but its keyboard/mouse part waits for task 3''s recorded answer

## Out of scope
- Bridge API, fake guests switch, join screen, game input (parts 3–5); timed lag measurement (part 6, separate probe)', 'Steam can stream a game running at home to friends elsewhere and send their controller, keyboard and mouse back, so they play as if sitting in the room. Before building on that, we need to know exactly what Steam tells the game: who joined, which controller belongs to whom, and whether a friend''s keyboard and mouse can be told apart from the host''s. This is the research that answers those questions, partly with a small test on real machines, and ends with a clear yes or no on remote keyboard players.', '2026-10-16T21:26:01Z', 1418);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (169, 17, 'Steamworks switch and Remote Play test setup', 700, 'Part 2 of `plan 153: masterplan`. The developer''s one-time Steamworks and test setup that every live Remote Play run of `milestone 17: Remote Play Together` needs: Remote Play Together on for the real App ID, a `beta` build carrying the milestone''s code, a Windows host, a Linux or Deck machine, a second Steam account. Docs and one decision; workers never log in to Steamworks.

