- Store: the public «Remote Play Together» feature listing is part 8''s (`plans/17a-store-page.md`, after part 9 passes); here only what Steamworks requires to turn it on
- Gate `decision 284: Remote Play Together gate: single player, controller input and local multiplayer playtested?`: this plan''s tasks are docs and a developer check, not gated; the code in the `beta` build comes from other plans'' tasks, gated or not by their own plans (the probe switch of `plan 168: Investigation: Remote Play input and session API` is not gated)

## The setup decision (subject, for the other parts)
- `pm decision add "Remote Play Together test setup ready? Switch on, beta build, two machines, second account" --once`
- Waiting on it: `decision 302: Remote Play Together live probe: guests'' pads, keyboard and mouse on a Windows and a Linux host` (plan 168 task 3 "Findings and the answer"), part 6''s measurement (the plan "Timed mode over a Remote Play stream"), part 9''s playtest (the plan "Remote Play close-out: play with remote guests"); their plans find it with `pm decision list --grep "test setup ready"` and link their live tasks with `pm task-pending-decision`

## Checklist (task 1 writes it; Valve''s page and field names unverified, recheck at entry)
- Preconditions: decision 179 answered (real App ID, `beta` branch); first `beta` upload done (task 681''s decision)
- Steamworks → Remote Play settings of the app (App Admin; recheck the page): Remote Play Together on; Remote Play on TV/phone/tablet left at Steam''s default
  - if Steamworks ties it to store categories (local multiplayer / co-op / PvP): set the categories milestone 16''s modes justify; report which were needed; the store page isn''t public yet, the feature line in the store texts stays part 8''s
  - Publish the Steamworks changes
  - if Steam refuses Remote Play Together for an unreleased app or a password `beta` branch: report it, don''t work around it
- `beta` build with this milestone''s code: `trivia-steam upload --branch beta` of a commit with the code the live run needs (first: plan 168''s `--rp-probe` switch); report the BuildID and the `v<version>` tag
- Machines:
  - host A Windows (overlay works there, `decision 70: Steam overlay in the Electron shell`: in-game invite through the overlay)
  - host B Linux or the Deck (invite from Steam''s friends list)
  - each the host once, the other the guest; guest on any OS; wired and Wi-Fi as available (part 6)
- Accounts: the developer''s on the host; a second account (decision 135''s, or a family member''s) on the guest, Steam friends with the first
- Pads: at least one pad on the guest machine, one on the host; a second guest pad if at hand
- Smoke: host starts ¡Trivia! from the `beta` branch, invites the guest; the guest sees the picture and hears the sound; one pad press on the guest''s side moves the focus

## Tasks
1. SW-13 checklist in plan 18 and the setup decision (`--worktree app`, not gated)
   - `plans/18-steam-integration.md`: new section "Remote Play Together setup (SW-13)" after "Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)": intro paragraph, `- [ ]` rows per the checklist above, pointers instead of copies (SW-7 section, "Builds and depots", decision 135)
   - same file: the "Steam features" bullet «Remote Play Together: enabled … once multi-controller input works (IN-6)» and the SW-13 row in "Tasks" point to milestone 17 and the new section; nothing else rewritten (part 8 owns the rest: `plans/11-steam.md`, `plans/14-input.md`, the store)
   - the decision above: intro (plain English), body = the checklist''s rows in short plus «answer decision 302''s setup line by this», options `ready (App ID, BuildID, host OSes, what Steamworks required)` (recommended), `not yet (why)`, `issues (rows)`
   - link existing waiting tasks: `pm task list --grep` for plan 168''s task 3 and for any live task of parts 6 and 9 already split → `pm task-pending-decision <task> <id>`; not-yet-split plans find it by subject
   - task 2 pending on the decision
   - done when: section written; decision pending; existing live tasks and task 2 wait on it
2. Record the Remote Play setup (`--worktree app`, after the decision; not gated)
   - answer → the section''s rows `[x]` with date, BuildID, what Steamworks required (categories, page name), host OSes; issues → follow-up tasks in the owning plan (130 Steamworks values, 89 uploads) and a retry decision, this task pending on it
   - SW-13 stays `[ ]` (closed by part 8 after part 9); `pm decision consequences`
   - done when: the section matches what was set up

## Out of scope
- The store feature line and docs beyond the two pointers (part 8), the probe and its live steps (plan 168), lag measurement (part 6), uploads (plan 89), SW-7 values (plan 130)', 'Steam can stream a game running at home to friends elsewhere, but only after the game''s owner switches the feature on in Steam''s developer settings, and testing it needs a real test version on Steam, two computers and a second Steam account. This covers that one-time setup: a checklist the developer follows and a single check-in once everything is ready. Every real test of playing together over the internet waits for it.', '2026-10-16T21:27:26Z', 1419);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (170, 17, 'Timed mode over a Remote Play stream', 590, 'Part 6 of `plan 153: masterplan`. How much later remote guests see a `timed` question and how much later their claim reaches the host, measured on real Remote Play sessions. Then the developer decides: accept the lag, or change claiming in the engine. Measurement and decision are not gated. An engine change, if any, waits for `decision 284: Remote Play Together gate: single player, controller input and local multiplayer playtested?`.

## Binding
- Timed rules: milestone 16 and `plan 159: Competitive (timed) in the engine`
  - 30 s per question (`QUESTION_MS`), a hint every 8 s (`HINT_MS`), 6 s after a claim (`CLAIM_MS`)
  - the first claim to arrive wins (`claim_taken`)
  - deadlines inclusive, no grace
  - every time is the host''s epoch ms (`Io.ms`); the engine runs no timer of its own
- `task 1447: Timed: the question clock starts on show, not at the previous question''s end`: `shown_at` is set by the host''s `show` action, i.e. when the host''s screen shows the question, not the guest''s
- `decision 282: Timed mode: the Esc menu and the Steam overlay pause the clock and hide the question`, `decision 283: Remote Play Together: what happens when a remote guest leaves mid-game?`: unchanged here
- `decision 277: Multiplayer sessions in the save: one games[] row per session, with seats`: any new seat or claim field is additive, no `SAVE_VERSION` bump
- `decision 290: Timed mode: the claim input per kind of player`: a guest''s claim is a pad bumper (LB/RB); remote keyboard claims only if `plan 168: Investigation: Remote Play input and session API` answers «yes»
- `decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`: Steam''s stream as it is; no netcode, no clock sync of our own with the guest''s machine
- Live runs wait for part 2''s setup decision (`plan 169: Steamworks switch and Remote Play test setup`). Find it with `pm decision list --grep "test setup ready"`; link it with `pm task-pending-decision` once it exists

## What the lag does (expected, to be measured)
- Picture delay `V`: from the host''s screen to the guest''s screen (encode, network, decode)
- Input delay `I`: from the guest''s press to the press reaching the host''s page
- Claim race: compared with a host-side player, a guest is behind by `V + I`. Players in a race are often within about 100 ms of each other, so this is the part that can matter
- Guest''s 6 s after a claim: the guest sees the claim `V` late and the answer arrives `I` late, so the guest gets `6 s − (V + I)`
- 30 s and hints: everything reaches the guest `V` late; the guest''s 30 s window ends at the same host time as everyone else''s

## Lag probe (task 1)
- `--lag-probe` flag in `app/desktop/main.mjs` (Steam launch option, Windows and Linux): the window loads one self-contained page `app/desktop/lag-probe.html` (inline script, packaged by `electron-builder.yml`), not the game. Mark the flag branch and the page `PLACEHOLDER(<task 3''s id>)`; task 3 removes both
- Page:
  - a large running ms counter (host `performance.now()`), always on
  - a full-screen white flash at random intervals of 2–5 s; its onset is the first `requestAnimationFrame` after it is painted
  - presses: any `navigator.getGamepads()` button (polled every frame) and any key. Per press, log the device (pad index and `Gamepad.id`, or `key`), ms since the last flash onset, and the press''s `Gamepad.timestamp` or the event timestamp. A press with no flash in the last 2 s is logged as a miss
  - the last 8 lines on screen; a running median and spread per device
- Log to `<userData>/lag-probe.log` (renderer `console-message` → main) and stderr; the path shown on screen
- No Steam calls of its own: guests'' pads arrive as the host OS gives them, as in the game. Steam init stays as in the normal start, so Steam Input and the stream behave as in a game
- README row of `trivia-desktop` and `AGENTS.md` Commands: `--lag-probe` (task 3 removes both)

## Measurement (task 2, the developer''s live session)
- Method, per host and network:
  - local reaction: 20 flashes, one person presses a pad at the host machine → median `R_local`
  - remote reaction: 20 flashes, the same person presses a pad at the guest machine, watching the guest''s screen → median `R_remote`; `V + I ≈ R_remote − R_local`
  - picture delay: guest machine next to the host machine; 5 photos (a phone is enough) showing both counters → `V` = host''s counter − guest''s counter; `I ≈ (V + I) − V`
  - Steam''s streaming performance overlay on the guest, if it has latency figures: note them too (unverified that it does; recheck at the session)
- Matrix, as available:
  - Windows host and Linux (or Deck) host
  - guest wired and on Wi-Fi
  - at least one run over the internet (guest on another network, e.g. a phone hotspot), since guests normally play from elsewhere
- Results: per row, `V`, `V + I`, spread, and anything odd (stutter, dropped presses)

## The decision (task 3 raises it with the numbers)
- Subject: «Timed mode over Remote Play: accept the lag or adjust claiming?»
- Options, with the measured numbers in the body:
  - accept: no engine change; guests are about `V + I` behind in claim races and get `6 s − (V + I)` to answer. Recommended if the internet-row `V + I` is under about 100 ms
  - claim grace window: guests'' seats carry a fixed allowance `L` (from the measurement). When the first claim arrives, the engine keeps it provisional for `L` ms. A claim arriving within that window wins if its arrival minus its seat''s allowance is earlier; at a tie, the first arrival keeps it. Without remote seats `L` = 0, so nothing changes
  - grace window plus deadlines: as above, and a remote claimer''s 6 s and the hint times stretched by `L`
  - other (the developer''s own)
- The «slowest guest''s view» variant from `plan 153: masterplan` (the 30 s and hints counted from when the slowest guest saw the question) is covered by stretching the deadlines; the 30 s window matters far less than the race

## Engine change (task 4, only if the answer adjusts claiming)
- In plan 159''s timestamp model:
  - `Seat.remote?: true` (or the measured allowance) set at session start from part 4''s binding (the plan "Remote guests as players")
  - the claim stores arrival and adjusted times; `settle` finalizes a provisional claim once `at + L` has passed
  - `view().session.timed.claim` gets `provisional` so the Timed screen (`plan 164: Timed game screens, drama and sound`) waits before the claim banner; or it shows the banner at once and swaps it, as the answer says
  - `expire`-style client nudge at the window''s end
- `session.test.ts`: a remote claim overtaking a local one within the window; one arriving too late; no remote seats behaves as today
- `plans/13-game-modes.md` "Competitive timed": the rule as built
- Waits for `decision 284: Remote Play Together gate: single player, controller input and local multiplayer playtested?`, for the decision above, and for `task 1412: Timed core in the engine: clock, claims, rounds, lives, ends`, `task 1413: Timed pause and view in the engine` and `task 1447: Timed: the question clock starts on show, not at the previous question''s end`. If part 4''s plan doesn''t mark seats as remote: a follow-up task there, not a guess here

## Tasks
1. Lag probe switch (`--worktree app`, not gated): the probe above
   - headless check: `trivia-desktop --lag-probe` with the dev Steam user starts, flashes, logs key presses with ms
   - then add the developer''s decision for task 2 (`--once`), with the method and matrix above as a checklist. Options: `measured (numbers per row)` (recommended), `partly (which rows)`, `not possible (why)`
   - make task 2''s decision pending on part 2''s setup decision if it exists (`pm decision list --grep "test setup ready"`); else note in the decision that the setup comes first
   - the developer needs the probe in a `beta` upload (`plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`); this task doesn''t upload
2. (the developer) the measurement decision from task 1, after part 2''s setup
3. Findings and the lag decision (`--worktree app`, not gated; pending on task 1''s decision)
   - the numbers into this plan (`pm plan edit`, section "Findings") and one line in `plans/14-input.md` "Remote Play Together"
   - `pm decision add` the lag decision above, with the numbers and a recommendation
   - remove the probe: flag, page, `electron-builder.yml` entry, README and `AGENTS.md` lines (`rg lag-probe`, decision 200)
   - make task 4 pending on the new decision and on decision 284
4. Remote claim compensation in the engine (`--worktree app`, `--model opus`; pending on task 3''s decision and decision 284): per the answer, as in "Engine change" above. If the answer is «accept», only the `plans/13-game-modes.md` line («remote guests: no claim compensation, measured lag …»), then done

## Out of scope
- Pad ↔ guest mapping and the remote seat fact: parts 3 and 4 (the plans "Remote Play sessions in the shell bridge" and "Remote guests as players")
- A guest leaving mid-game: decision 283, part 5
- Live clock sync with guests'' machines, or measuring each session''s lag on the fly', 'In the fast race mode, every player sees the same question and the first to grab it gets to answer. When a friend plays from far away through Steam''s streaming, they see the question a little later than the people at the TV, and their button press arrives a little later too, so they may always lose the race. This work measures that delay on real machines and networks, then lets the developer choose: accept it, or have the game give remote players a small, fair head start when claiming.', '2026-10-16T21:29:11Z', 1420);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (171, 9, 'Translations without human control', 700, 'Milestone 9, "Question translations without human control" (developer, 2026-10-16; the tr-en-1 and tr-de-1 spot checks, decision 305: Spot check tr-en-1 done? and decision 306: Spot check tr-de-1 done?, found every translation good); `plan 9: masterplan` parts 4 and 5. `plan 66: Translation pipeline (QT-2, QT-3)` and `plan 67: Review tool for translations (QT-4)` are done; this plan changes what they built. The run/QC tasks and the go/no-go tasks of `plan 84: Release content runs` are `task 1498: revise plan 84: Release content runs`''s, not this plan''s.

## Rule
- The LLM translation review (translate-review, D-32/D-33) is a translation''s only review, in every question locale (`en`, `de`, `es`, `es-ES`, milestone 12''s `zh-Hans`, `ru`, `pt-BR`).
- No native-speaker spot check per `tr-*` run, no QC decision per run, no pilot go/no-go, no `qgen health ack` after a pilot.
- Decision 45''s thresholds stay (`decision 45: Health thresholds and selection order for qgen batch --translate runs`): a `tr-*` run with a ✗ still stops the next `qgen batch --translate <L>` (exit 2) until `qgen health ack <run>`; the ack stays the developer''s.
- The developer may still open and review any `tr-*` run (`/review?batch=tr-<L>-<n>&locale=<L>`); `qgen flag` still sets `needs_work`.
- The pilot stays a 50-source first run (`TRANSLATE_PILOT`, D-87): its numbers (reject rate, cost) are information for `qgen report --cost`, not a gate.

## Choices made here (obvious, no decision)
- `spot-checks.json`: existing `tr-*` entries (tr-en-1, tr-de-1) stay valid; `spot_check_problems` keeps checking `tr-*` entries as today (a developer''s optional sample still records the same way); nothing requires a `tr-*` entry. `qc_section`/`qc_trend` keep showing a `tr-*` run''s spot check where one exists.
- `/review?…&locale=L&sample=1` keeps working by URL (existing records, the developer''s own choice) but nothing offers it: no "sample" link on the home page''s translation rows, no "Spot check by a native speaker" line in the run report.
- Runs already done whose pilot isn''t acked (`tr-en-1`, `tr-de-1`, `tr-es-ES-1`): after the code change they stop the next run only if they fail a threshold; no retroactive ack needed. `tr-es-1` (not run yet) is a plain 50-source first run.

## Order
- Priority 700 in work tree `questions`: runs before the full translation runs of part 11 (`task 639: run tr-en-2`, `task 641: run tr-de-2`, `task 1226: run tr-es-ES-2`, priority -110). Once task 1 is in, those runs no longer exit 2 on the pilot; a pilot that fails a threshold still stops them, and that task then pends on its "Continue …?" decision as plan 84''s run rules say (the ack is the developer''s).

## Tasks
1. `qgen health` and the review tool: no pilot stop, no spot-check prompt
   - `authoring/tools/health.py`: `translate_stop_reason` drops the pilot clause (only the last done run''s threshold failures stop, until `qgen health ack`); its docstring; the `translation_health_section` text ("The pilot (`-1`) and a ✗ stop …" → "A ✗ stops …").
   - `authoring/tools/qgen.py` translation run report (`tr-*` batch-report): the "Spot check by a native speaker" line → "Review (optional): `/review?batch=…&locale=…`" without `sample=1`; any CLI help / exit-2 text that names the pilot.
   - `authoring/ui/src/home/Home.svelte`: no "sample" link on translation run rows; check `authoring/ui/src/review/` and `authoring/server/spot_checks.py`, `overview.py` for a banner or count asking for a translation spot check and drop it (existing records'' banners stay).
   - `pm decision record` "Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run" `--supersedes 45` (partly: only "The pilot tr-<locale>-1 always stops the next run until qgen health ack"; thresholds and selection order stay), with an intro.
   - Done when: `qgen batch --translate en --dry-run` (or the stop check alone) no longer reports the pilot as a stop reason for `tr-en-1`; `qgen validate`, `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build` pass.
2. Docs: translations reviewed by the LLM only
   - `authoring/QC.md` "Translation runs": no spot check, no QC steps per `tr-*` run; what stays: report, thresholds, optional developer review, `qgen flag`.
   - `authoring/RUNBOOK.md`: exit-2 row (step table) and "Translation runs" bullet: no pilot stop.
   - `plans/15b-question-translation.md`: run line (no exit 2 after the pilot), QT-5 without go/no-go, QT-6 without native-speaker spot check; status line.
   - `plans/decisions.md`: D-87 "Stop" bullet (only threshold failures, decision 45 as amended), D-55 if it names the pilot, and a line citing the developer''s 2026-10-16 change; README if it says otherwise.
   - Decision 200: `rg -i "spot.?check|go/no-go|pilot|native speaker|native-speaker"` over `.md` files and code comments in `authoring/`, `plans/`, `modding/`, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`; fix every hit about translations in the same commit (drafted batches'' spot checks, D-56, stay).
   - Done when: no doc describes a translation spot check, a pilot go/no-go or a pilot stop as required; `qgen validate` passes.', 'The game''s questions are translated by an AI into English, German and two kinds of Spanish, and another AI pass reviews each translation. Until now, a native speaker also had to check a sample of every translation run, and the first run of each language waited for the developer''s go-ahead. Those checks found every translation good, so the AI review becomes the only review; the automatic quality limits still stop a run that goes wrong. This brings the tools and the written procedures in line with that.', '2026-10-16T23:13:03Z', 1501);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (172, 16, 'Keyboard seats after a restart: a resumed session asks for a pad', 480, 'Found by `task 1473: Headless: every multiplayer mode start to finish, release-check step multiplayer` (`plan 167: Local multiplayer close-out and family playtest` routing: lost pad, resume → `plan 161: Per-player controls`, done; hence this plan). Builds on `plan 161: Per-player controls` and `decision 289: Local multiplayer: a controller lost mid-session waits for a controller to take the seat`.

## Failure (packaged Linux build, 2026-10-16)
- rr-coop, keyboard only (3 `shared` seats, `decision 273: Keyboard-only turn-based sessions: what does a player''s own key do?`), one turn played, the shell quit, started again, Start → resume
- the seat-lost dialog «Mando de Luna desconectado» shows; Enter changes nothing; no key or click takes the seat: the session can''t go on (only the Esc menu ends it)
- Cause: `app/client/src/lib/seats.svelte.ts` `stored()`: no sessionStorage after a restart → every seat''s binding `null`; `lostSeat()` treats a `null` binding as a lost pad, whatever the seat''s device was; `SeatLost.svelte` binds pads only
- Same root for a `kbm` seat in a mixed session (pads + keyboard and mouse) and for keyboard-only `timed` key seats (`{ key }`): after a restart they are `null` too; a free pad could take the `kbm` seat (wrong device), and a key seat can''t be taken at all
- Pad seats rebind as `decision 289` says (checked by the release check''s `multiplayer` step)

## Do
- After a restart, non-pad seats get their binding back without a pad: e.g. keep each seat''s device kind in the stored binding''s place in the save or derive it (keyboard-only session: `shared` / the `timed` key seats need their picked keys again, so the keys must survive a restart, or the Join-like key pick reopens); a `kbm` seat back to `kbm` when keyboard and mouse aren''t bound elsewhere
- Whether the binding moves into the save (`games[]` row, plan 157''s shape) or the dialog lets the keyboard take a non-pad seat: a choice for the worker; a lasting one → `pm decision record`
- `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs --multiplayer`: the keyboard-only rr-coop session (or a timed key-seat one) also quits and restarts mid-session and plays on after the resume (the timed pads session shows how: `restart` in `RUNS`)

## Check
- `node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs --multiplayer` on a fresh `trivia-desktop-build --dir`: all sessions green
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`', 'When a family quits the game in the middle of a multiplayer session and starts it again later, every player has to be matched to their controller again. Players with a gamepad press a button and get their seat back, but players on the shared keyboard have no way to do that: the game waits for a controller that will never come, and the session is stuck. This fixes the restart so keyboard players get their seats back too.', '2026-10-17T03:58:31Z', 1473);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (173, 18, 'Demo build switch, identity and save', 700, 'Part 1 of `plan 154: masterplan`: the demo flag every other demo part builds on, the demo''s names and Steam identity, and where its save lives. Runs first; `task 1526: write plan: The demo base bundle`, `task 1527: write plan: Deterministic selection in the demo`, `task 1528: write plan: Demo on screen`, `task 1529: write plan: Demo packaging, release check and upload` read the flag defined here.

## Ground rules
- `decision 335: Playable demo: a build variant of the same code, switched at build time`; mechanics per `decision 338: Demo flag: TRIVIA_DEMO at build, dist-demo, package.json demo, EngineData.demo`
- Nothing enforced hard (`decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`): the flag decides what ships and shows, not a lock
- Names beside `decision 223: Build names after PUB-7: productName «Living Room Trivia», space-free exe and artefact names`; the full build''s names, paths and output unchanged
- Split: the Save task `pm task-pending-decision` on decision 336, the Steam features task on decision 337; Flag, Identity, Docs don''t wait
- Waits: `decision 336: Demo save: separate from the full game''s, or shared/imported on purchase?`, `decision 337: Steam features in the demo: Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry, question reports`

## Flag
- Client: `app/client/vite.config.ts` reads `TRIVIA_DEMO=1` → `define: { __DEMO__ }` (declared in `src/vite-env.d.ts` beside `__APP_VERSION__`), `build.outDir` `dist-demo` (gitignored like `dist/`); `lib/build.ts` `BuildInfo.demo`
- Engine: `EngineData.demo: boolean` (`engine/state.ts`), set by `engineData()`''s caller (`lib/data.ts` from `buildInfo().demo`); engine code reads only that; tests build both. No behaviour behind it yet (parts 2, 3, 5)
- Dev server (`devserver.ts`, `npm run dev|serve -w app/client`): `TRIVIA_DEMO=1` serves the demo client; `serve` previews `dist-demo/`; prints `trivia dev: demo`
- Shell (`app/desktop/main.mjs`): `isDemo()` read once: packaged `package.json` `"demo": true` (read like `reportUrl`), unpackaged `TRIVIA_DEMO=1`; unpackaged demo loads `app/client/dist-demo`, missing → exit with "run `TRIVIA_DEMO=1 npm run build`"
- `trivia-gallery` (`authoring/tools/gallery.py` `build_if_stale`, preview): honours `TRIVIA_DEMO=1` (builds/serves `dist-demo`, output `work/gallery-demo/…`); `--demo` shot set is part 5''s
- `smoke.mjs` runs a packaged build: its demo run needs the demo build (part 4)

## Identity
- `app/desktop/electron-builder.demo.yml` `extends: ./electron-builder.yml`: appId `io.github.rubenmoor.trivia.demo`, productName «Living Room Trivia Demo», Linux `living-room-trivia-demo`, Windows `LivingRoomTriviaDemo.exe`, artefacts `LivingRoomTriviaDemo-<v>-…`, `extraMetadata.demo: true`, output `release/demo/` (unpacked dirs don''t collide)
- `trivia-desktop-build --demo` (`flake.nix`, `app/desktop/package.json` scripts): client built with `TRIVIA_DEMO=1`, builder on the demo config; data and media cut, budgets: part 4
- Window title (`main.mjs` `BrowserWindow`, overlay) «¡Trivia! Demo» in the demo; in-game title unchanged, the start screen''s demo line is part 5''s
- Steam App ID: `main.mjs` `STEAM_APP_ID` demo constant (480 Spacewar until the demo app exists, part 6); `authoring/steam/steam.json` gains `"demo": { "appid": null, "depots": {"windows", "linux", "content"} }` for part 4''s upload

## Save (after decision 336)
- Recommended answer: packaged demo `userData` `<appData>/trivia-demo` (save, `mods.json`, telemetry); dev demo `state/desktop-demo/`, `state/telemetry-demo/`; own single-instance lock follows, so demo and full run side by side
- Import answer: the full game''s first start finds the demo save and offers `--import-save`''s path once: its own task then

## Steam features (after decision 337)
- Gates in the shell and client per the answer: mods scan, `/mods.js`, Workshop, `--publish-mod`, achievements unlocks; screens hidden is part 5''s
- Telemetry on: a `demo` mark on sessions (shell `telemetry.mjs`, `engine/telemetry.ts`), `report-server` schema accepts it; calibration exclusion is part 3''s
- Reports on: `report-server` accepts tickets of both App IDs (`STEAM_APP_ID` → a list); `wrangler.toml` comment names `steam.json`''s demo id

## Docs
- README how-tos, `AGENTS.md` Commands rows (`trivia-desktop`, `trivia-desktop-build`, dev server, `trivia-gallery`) name `TRIVIA_DEMO=1` / `--demo`; `plans/18-steam-integration.md` a "Demo" section; `rg -i demo` (decision 200)

## Done when
- `TRIVIA_DEMO=1 npm run dev -w app/client` and `TRIVIA_DEMO=1 trivia-desktop` run with `buildInfo().demo` true and the engine seeing `demo`; without it everything as before
- `trivia-desktop-build --demo --dir` gives `release/demo/` with the demo names and `demo: true` in its `package.json`
- The save and Steam features follow the two answers; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass', 'The free demo is the same program as the full game, built with a switch turned on. This work adds that switch, gives the demo its own name, program files and Steam identity so it installs next to the full game, and decides where the demo keeps its save and which Steam features it offers. Every other part of the demo work builds on this switch.', '2026-10-17T13:24:02Z', 1525);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (174, 18, 'The demo base bundle', 590, 'Part 2 of `plan 154: masterplan`: the demo''s fixed question list, picked by a script from approved `base` questions, sized by the engine''s own supply check, exported to the demo''s pools and checked by `qgen validate`. Work in the `questions` work tree, except the demo pool load in the client (`app`).

## Ground rules
- Format: `decision 339: Demo bundle format: an id list of base questions, exported to app/data/demo/ pools, questions stay in base`: list `authoring/data/demo.json` (`{version: 1, ids: [...], approved: <decision id>}`), `qgen export` → `app/data/demo/pool.json` (es), `pool.<locale>.json` (es-ES, en, de), base''s entries unchanged; no bundle id `demo`, no `bundles.json` entry, no own taxonomy; every question stays in exactly one bundle (`plans/22-bundles.md`)
- Flag: `decision 338: Demo flag: TRIVIA_DEMO at build, dist-demo, package.json demo, EngineData.demo` (`plan 173: Demo build switch, identity and save`); this plan reads `buildInfo().demo` only in the client''s pool load
- Mods: `decision 337: Steam features in the demo: Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry, question reports` pending (recommended: off); the list is sized without mod bundles either way, a mod bundle only adds
- Rules from the engine, never re-implemented (D-60, decision 199): supply check and picker in a Node script beside `authoring/tools/supply.ts`, called through `authoring/tools/engine.py`; `qgen demo` is the Python front
- Deterministic: same pool files → same list; no time, no random seed; ties by question id
- Seen counts don''t matter (part 3: `countOf` 0 in the demo): the check uses an empty save
- RUNBOOK unchanged: `qgen demo` is a developer and pm-worker command, not a question-making step; `qgen batch --translate` keeps its arguments

## Candidates
- `base` questions (`bundle` absent or `base`), source approved, `translatable` not false
- Approved in every launch locale (es, es-ES, en, de: source or translation per `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`), not `needs_work`, not flagged, not blocked by a health or spot-check mark
- Media questions: file in the cache (`media/`), licence shippable (`authoring/tools/media.py` `licence_of`, the release check''s licence rule)
- Today only 46 base questions are approved in all four locales: the picker also takes `pending` candidates = everything above but missing translations; translation runs pick listed ids first (task 3); the list is final only when every id is a full candidate

## Size from supply
Configurations, all at the defaults (12 levels, `CARDS_MAX` 4 cards, standard jokers), per age group of `app/data/age-groups.json`:
- «Solo o en grupo», Gamemaster, rr-coop: one game (`game.ts` `supply`)
- rr-competitive: 2..S seats, every multiset of age groups over the seats (`sessionSupply` → `seatsSupply`, no card twice per session)
- timed: 2..S seats, cards = seats (`decision 276: Timed mode: after a drop-out, how many questions does a round have?`), plus sudden death at level 12 (up to 3 rounds of the seats still in), as extra level-12 slots in the matching
- Media off: each configuration again with video and audio off (`mediaAllowed`)
- Jokers: per level a reserve R on top of the cards (assign with cards + R at that level, the others at cards): R = fresh questions one game''s standard jokers and the Gamemaster''s «Cambiar pregunta» once can pull at one level (skip, «Bájale», «Cambiazo», «Francotirador»''s repeated level); the worker reads R off `game.ts` and writes it in the script''s comment
- «Bájale» needs an easier question of the same subcategory: reported as a share (listed questions with one in the list), the picker favours subcategory pairs across difficulties; no hard bar
- Custom choices (fewer or more levels, own difficulty window, keyboard-only sessions beyond S seats) aren''t sized; the supply report on the bundle screen covers them (nothing enforced hard)
- S: max seats per `milestone 16: Local multiplayer: game modes and controls`: 4 pads + keyboard and mouse = 5 (no cap of our own); the list''s size grows steeply with S (rr-competitive: S × 48 cards in one group''s window), so task 1 prints the size for S = 1 (no multiplayer), 2, 3, 4, 5 and raises the decision; ≈200 only holds without multiplayer

## Spread
- Difficulty: per group the level ranges'' needs first (the matching), then towards `level_weights`
- Categories and subcategories: as many base subcategories as the size allows, at most k per subcategory (k from size / subcategories), categories in the full pool''s proportions
- Media share like the approved base pool''s (images, audio, video), within the media-off check
- Fill order: the matching''s minimum first, then reserves, then spread; full candidates before pending ones

## Tasks
1. **`qgen demo`: candidates, supply check, picker** (`questions`, priority 590): `authoring/tools/demo.ts` (Node, engine imports) + `qgen demo` (`authoring/tools/qgen.py`, `engine.py`): `qgen demo --sizes` prints per S the minimum list size, the full/pending candidate counts and which configuration binds; `qgen demo --propose [--seats S]` writes `work/demo/proposal.json` (ids, per id: subcategory, difficulty, media, full/pending) and `work/demo/proposal.md` (per configuration pass/fail, reserve, «Bájale» share, spread vs. targets, pending ids per locale); `qgen demo --check [<file>]` checks a list (default `authoring/data/demo.json`) against the configurations. Then `pm decision add "Demo: cover multiplayer sessions up to how many seats?"` with the `--sizes` table (options S = 5 recommended if its size is within reach of the translation runs, else the largest S whose list is ≤ ≈400; the answer goes into `authoring/data/demo.json`''s `seats`)
2. **Demo pools in export and validate** (`questions`, 590): `qgen export` writes `app/data/demo/pool.json` and `pool.<locale>.json` (es-ES, en, de) from `authoring/data/demo.json` (`pool_export.py`, entries as in base''s pools; no file without a list); `qgen validate`: ids exist, `bundle` base, every id a full candidate, `qgen demo --check` passes at the list''s `seats`, demo pools not stale (like `app/data/pool.json`); a pending id is an error only once `approved` is set. Docs: `plans/22-bundles.md` "Demo" section (decision 339, layout row `app/data/demo/`), `AGENTS.md` Commands rows `qgen demo`, `qgen validate`; `directory.md` if needed
3. **Translation runs take listed ids first** (`questions`, 580): `qgen batch --translate <locale>` source selection: after stale translations, the ids of `authoring/data/demo.json` (else `work/demo/proposal.json`) without an approved translation in the locale; a listed source that turns out not to travel (`translatable: false`) or is rejected → `qgen demo --check` reports it, task 5''s replacement covers it. `plans/15b-question-translation.md` names the order; RUNBOOK''s "Translation runs" line too
4. **Demo pool in the client** (`app`, 580, after plan 173''s flag task): `lib/data.ts` / `engine/pool.ts` `poolFile`: in a demo build base''s pool file of a locale is `demo/pool.json` / `demo/pool.<locale>.json`, no pack pools (`packsFor` empty); a locale without its demo pool isn''t offered (masterplan ground rules); `TRIVIA_DEMO=1 npm run dev -w app/client` plays only listed ids; the bundle tile''s name and count are part 5''s
5. **Pick and approve the list** (`questions`, 570, after the seat decision and task 2): `qgen demo --propose --seats <S>` → `authoring/data/demo.json` (`approved` empty), export, validate; `pm decision add --once "Demo question list: approve?"` with the proposal''s table, `proposal.md` and a `/review` link of the listed ids (`/review?demo=1`: a filter on the list, added here if `/review` has none), options approve / replace these ids / change the rules; pending translations listed. After the answer: `approved` set, export, validate. Replacement rule in `plans/22-bundles.md`: a listed id later flagged, retired, blocked or untranslatable → `qgen demo --check` fails `qgen validate`; `qgen demo --replace` proposes the nearest full candidate (same level ranges, subcategory, media kind; the check passes) and the developer approves it the same way (`--once` decision per replacement round)

## Done when
- `qgen demo --check` passes for the approved list at the decided seat count; `qgen validate` checks it; `app/data/demo/` holds the four demo pools
- `TRIVIA_DEMO=1` dev client plays every mode × age group from the demo pools only; without it nothing changes
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass', 'The free demo holds only a small, fixed set of questions from the main game, just enough for a family to play each game mode once in every age group. This work writes a script that picks those questions fairly from the approved ones, sizes the set from the game''s own rules for how many questions each kind of game needs, makes sure every picked question exists in all four launch languages, and lets the developer approve the list before it ships.', '2026-10-17T13:29:07Z', 1526);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (175, 18, 'Deterministic selection in the demo', 600, 'Part 3 of `plan 154: masterplan`: in a demo build the engine draws the same questions and answer orders for the same play, on every machine and run, and seen counts no longer steer anything. Work tree `app`; after `task 1534: Demo flag in the client, engine and dev server` (`EngineData.demo`).

## Ground rules
- Flag per `decision 338: Demo flag: TRIVIA_DEMO at build, dist-demo, package.json demo, EngineData.demo`: engine code reads only `data.demo`, never `__DEMO__` or a global
- Rng per `decision 340: Demo selection: every shuffle seeded from its site and the items it shuffles`: no time, game id, call counter or `randomSeed()` in the demo
- Referee randomness stays behind the injected `Rng` (D-58); the full game unchanged (`seededRng(randomSeed())`, seen counts as today); its tape fixtures (`engine/fixtures/`) untouched
- Seen rows still written in the demo (`see()`); only reading them changes
- Not deterministic by design: what players do (cards picked, answers, jokers, blocked questions, timed''s clock and claims); equal play gives equal questions
- Demo pools are part 2''s (`plan 174: The demo base bundle`); this plan works on any pool

## Rng sites
- `engine/rng.ts`: `demoRng()`: per `shuffle(xs, site)` a seed = hash (FNV-1a or the like) of a fixed salt, `site` and the items'' keys (`id` of an object with one, else `String(x)`), then mulberry32 + Fisher–Yates as `seededRng`; `actionRng(data)` = `data.demo ? demoRng() : seededRng(randomSeed())`
- `lib/engine.ts` `io()` takes the action''s `EngineData` and uses `actionRng(data)` (`exec()` and `load()`''s `repair` call)
- Sites covered by that alone, checked one by one: `selection.draw` (`"draw"`: `game.ts` `draw`, `timedDraw`), `open` (`"pick"`), `replacement` (`"replacement"`: «Bájale», «Cambiazo», `replaceCurrent`, joker availability), `putOn` (`"swap_in"`); `rg "shuffle\("` over `engine/` for any newer one
- `lib/api.ts`''s throwaway `seededRng(0)` for the view''s joker trials: harmless (trials don''t consume `demoRng`), comment kept true

## Seen counts off
- `game.ts` `countOf(save, data)`: `() => 0` when `data.demo`; every caller passes `data` (`draw`, `timedDraw`, «Bájale», «Cambiazo», `jokersView`, `replaceCurrent`, `outlook.ts`)
- Effects: `draw` and `replacement` order by the demo rng and difficulty only; a second game with the same choice gets the same questions as the first (the milestone''s "every run exactly the same")
- Running-out notice off (`decision 195: Supply notice: bundles running out instead of exhausted subcategories`): `runningOutBundles` finds nothing with every count 0 (`qs.length > fresh` never holds), so `Outlook.runningOut` stays empty and `SupplyNotice` never names a bundle; `tight`/`none` then mean the list''s own supply (`decision 31: Low-supply warning: below how many fresh games left (K) should the game start warn?`), which part 2''s check keeps clear; `k` a constant
- `rg "\.seen\b|countOf"` over `app/client/src` for any other seen-based display (stats, players screen, achievements): list it in the task note; a visible one in the demo → follow-up task

## Telemetry
- Demo games carry the mark of `task 1540: Demo telemetry mark and question reports for the demo App ID per decision 337` (if `decision 337: Steam features in the demo: Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry, question reports` keeps telemetry on; `decision 119: Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file`)
- `qgen telemetry` (`authoring/tools/played.py`): a demo game''s answers never clean (fixed selection isn''t a sample, like timed per `decision 286: Telemetry of multiplayer sessions: one game per played game, a player count, timed answers not clean`), so no calibration curve or outlier takes them; games counted in a `demo` tally beside `mods`; stats files from before default to 0
- Telemetry off in the answer: the task is dropped

## Test
- One lasting engine test (`engine/demo.test.ts` or in `game.test.ts`, fixture pool, `data.demo` true): a scripted session (solo game: picks, answers, «Bájale», «Cambiazo», «Paso»; a timed session, a few rounds) run twice on fresh saves gives identical `offered`, `current` and `answers`; a second game on the save of the first gives the first''s questions (counts ignored); with `data.demo` false, `actionRng` seeded twice differs
- No other new tests (AGENTS.md)

## Tasks
1. **Deterministic demo selection in the engine** (`app`, 600, after task 1534): `demoRng`, `actionRng`, `io(data)`, `countOf(save, data)`, the site check, the seen-display scan, the test; `plans/12-client-engine.md` and `plans/03-game-flow.md` (selection, rng: one bullet "Demo" naming decision 340 and counts off), `plans/decisions.md` if D-58''s note needs it; check by hand: `TRIVIA_DEMO=1 npm run dev -w app/client`, two games with the same choice show the same cards
2. **Demo games out of calibration in `qgen telemetry`** (`app`, 590, pending on decision 337, after task 1540): `played.py` clean rule and `demo` tally per "Telemetry"; `qgen report` played output names the demo count if it shows `mods`''s; check with a hand-made stats input (throw-away)

## Done when
- Demo build or `TRIVIA_DEMO=1`: equal play gives equal questions and answer orders across runs and machines, seen counts ignored, no running-out notice
- Full game: random as before, fixtures pass
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass', 'In the free demo every play-through should be the same: the same choices lead to the same questions, in the same order, on any computer. The full game picks questions at random and avoids ones the family has already seen; the demo switches both off, so what a player sees in the demo is exactly what the developer tested. This work makes the game''s shuffling predictable in the demo, stops it from looking at which questions were already seen, keeps demo games out of the play statistics used to tune question difficulty, and adds a test that proves two identical runs match.', '2026-10-17T13:31:31Z', 1527);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (176, 18, 'Demo on screen', 400, 'Part 5 of `plan 154: masterplan`: what the demo shows differently on screen: a free-demo line on Start, the demo''s own tile on Bundles, no screens for features the demo doesn''t ship, no PLACEHOLDER on a demo screen, a demo gallery run and the developer''s review.

## Ground rules
- Flag: `decision 338: Demo flag: TRIVIA_DEMO at build, dist-demo, package.json demo, EngineData.demo` (`plan 173: Demo build switch, identity and save`, `task 1534: Demo flag in the client, engine and dev server`); the client reads `buildInfo().demo`, UI code takes it as a prop or from `lib/build.ts`, no new global
- Demo pool: `decision 339: Demo bundle format: an id list of base questions, exported to app/data/demo/ pools, questions stay in base`; client load in `task 1546: Demo pool in the client` (no packs, locales without a demo pool not offered)
- Bundle screen as `plan 151: Bundle selection on its own full screen` left it: every tile a toggle (`decision 269: Bundle screen: a mod''s extra base bundle` superseded, no info-only tile); counts `decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings`, the demo''s per `decision 341: Demo bundle tile: its name and question count`
- Hidden features follow `decision 337: Steam features in the demo: Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry, question reports` (pending); shell gates are `task 1539: Demo Steam feature gates: mods, Workshop, publish, achievements per decision 337` and `task 1540: Demo telemetry mark and question reports for the demo App ID per decision 337`, this plan only the client''s screens and buttons
- Nothing enforced hard (`decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`): hiding, not locking; no buy button or nag (the milestone asks for a line only)
- UI strings: `locales/style/<locale>.md` first; es, es-ES (override only if it differs), en, de; `npm run check`''s on-screen literal check
- Fit: 1280×720, 1280×800, 1920×1080 (`plan 46: Deck layout and controller-only text entry (SW-4)`)

## Start screen
- `Start.svelte`: in a demo build a line under the subtitle, e.g. «Versión de demostración gratuita» (key `screen.start.demo`); visible with the new game button, the resume button and the save notice; quiet look (subtitle colour or a small glass pill), not a button, not focusable
- Window title is plan 173''s; wordmark unchanged
- `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` "Start": the demo line

## Bundle screen
- `BundleSelector.svelte` (large and compact, «Ajustes de la partida»): demo build → the base tile''s name `bundles.demoName` (e.g. «Paquete de demostración», «Demo bundle», «Demopaket»), its count from the loaded demo pool via `countShown` (rounding of decision 267''s mod rule, no cap), per decision 341; icon as base
- One tile only (no packs): layout still fits (no empty optional area with a lone ruler: hide ruler and area when there are no optional tiles, if not already so); off → plan 151''s start reason
- The supply report stays (seats or levels beyond the demo''s list show it); the running-out notice is off in demo (`plan 175: Deterministic selection in the demo`)
- `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` "Bundles", `plans/22-bundles.md` demo section (plan 174 writes it): the tile''s name and count

## Hidden in the demo (after decision 337)
- Mods off (recommended answer): Start''s Mods button, the ☰ menu''s Mods entry, `Mods.svelte` and its crashed-start opening (`Game.svelte` `modsOpen`, `safeStart`), the held-off line: hidden because the client never asks for the mod list in demo (`fetchModList` skipped, `modList` null), not per-button checks
- Telemetry off (only if the answer says so): no consent screen at first start (`Consent.svelte`), no telemetry setting; on: unchanged
- Reports off (only if the answer says so): flag dialog and flag list (`onflags`) hidden; on: unchanged
- Achievements have no in-game screen: nothing; Workshop: no screen beyond Mods
- Credits screen: unchanged here; its media list is the demo''s once part 4 cuts `CREDITS.md`
- `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md`: what the demo hides

## No PLACEHOLDER on a demo screen
- Today `PLACEHOLDER(1453)` on Level and Timed (`task 1453`, `plan 164: Timed game screens, drama and sound`); Mode row''s unbuilt modes are dev-mode only (`decision 293: Unbuilt multiplayer modes: on the mode row in dev mode only`)
- Not fixed here: the demo gallery run lists every PLACEHOLDER text it sees (manifest), the review decision names their tasks; part 4''s `trivia-release-check --demo` should fail on one (for `task 1529: write plan: Demo packaging, release check and upload`)

## Gallery and review
- `trivia-gallery --demo` (`authoring/tools/gallery.py`, after `task 1537: trivia-gallery honours TRIVIA_DEMO`): sets `TRIVIA_DEMO=1` and a demo shot set: `language` (only demo locales), `start`, `start-resume`, `start-save-notice`, `menu-start`, `bundles`, `game-settings`, `level`; scenes without pack bundles (demo saves built from demo pool ids); output `work/gallery-demo/<locale>[@WxH]/`; `--list` names the set
- `/gallery?demo` on `trivia-authoring` (`authoring/server/ui_flags.py`, `main.py`, `authoring/ui`): reads `work/gallery-demo/manifest.json`; flags work like the full gallery''s
- Run es, es-ES, en, de at 1920×1080 and 1280×800; 0 unmatched text
- Then `pm decision add --once "Demo start screen and bundle tile reviewed in /gallery?"` (options: approved / problems: …), the `/gallery?demo` link, PLACEHOLDER hits listed
- Docs: `AGENTS.md` Commands `trivia-gallery` row (`--demo`), README gallery how-to, `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md`

## Tasks
1. Demo line on the Start screen (400, after task 1534): above, catalogs, docs
2. Demo base tile: name and count (400, after tasks 1534 and 1546): both selector modes, lone-tile layout, catalogs, docs
3. Demo hides mods and per-answer features (390, pending on decision 337): above, docs
4. `trivia-gallery --demo`, `/gallery?demo` and the developer''s review (380, after 1–3 and task 1537): shot set, review page, run, the `--once` decision

## Done when
- `TRIVIA_DEMO=1 npm run dev -w app/client`: Start shows the demo line, Bundles the demo tile with its count, no Mods button or menu entry (per decision 337); without the flag nothing changes
- The review decision is answered approved (or its problems are tasks)
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass', 'The free demo must look like the full game but say plainly that it is the free demo, and not point players to things it doesn''t contain. This work adds a short ''free demo version'' line to the start screen in all four languages, gives the demo''s single question set its own name and honest question count, hides the screens for player-made question packs and any other feature the demo leaves out, and shows the result to the developer in the screenshot gallery for approval.', '2026-10-17T13:33:32Z', 1528);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (177, 18, 'Demo packaging, release check and upload', 610, 'Part 4 of `plan 154: masterplan`: the demo build ships only the demo''s data and media, gets its own release check, and uploads to the demo app''s `beta` branch. Builds on `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)` (its commands, extended with `--demo`, never forked) and parts 1–3. Work tree `app`.

## Ground rules
- Flag and names: `decision 338: Demo flag: TRIVIA_DEMO at build, dist-demo, package.json demo, EngineData.demo`; `task 1536: Demo build: electron-builder.demo.yml, trivia-desktop-build --demo, steam.json demo` gives `trivia-desktop-build --demo [--dir]` → `app/desktop/release/demo/`, `steam.json` `demo`; this plan cuts what it ships
- Demo data: `decision 339: Demo bundle format: an id list of base questions, exported to app/data/demo/ pools, questions stay in base` (`plan 174: The demo base bundle`); selection: `decision 340: Demo selection: every shuffle seeded from its site and the items it shuffles` (`plan 175: Deterministic selection in the demo`)
- Folders, depots, reports: `decision 342: Demo packaging: own staging folders, three depots, own reports, no nix output`; depots as `decision 84: SteamCMD source and depot split for Steam uploads`, no DLC depot (masterplan: the demo ships no pack)
- Media formats and credits: `decision 185: Shipped media: formats, names and where the encode runs (SW-9)`; one `CREDITS.md` per build, for its own media
- Mods kit, Workshop, telemetry and report rows follow `decision 337: Steam features in the demo: Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry, question reports` (pending): only task 6 waits on it
- Branches as plan 89: `SetLive beta` only, `default` set in the Steamworks web UI; no secrets in git
- Real upload waits for part 6''s checklist decision (`task 1530: write plan: Steamworks demo app and store` raises it) and the full game''s first upload (`task 681: First beta upload: checklist and decision`); everything up to `--dry-run` runs with placeholder IDs
- The full build, its commands without `--demo` and its reports unchanged

## Build contents (`trivia-desktop-build --demo`)
- Data: `resources/data/` without `bundles/` and without base''s full pools (`pool.json`, `pool.<locale>.json`); with `demo/` and the rest (`age-groups.json`, `bundles.json`, `categories.json`, `names.*.json`, `old-keys.json`); `electron-builder.demo.yml` lists its own `extraResources` (check how `extends` merges arrays: replace, not append)
- Media: `stage-media.mjs --demo`: media of the demo pools (all locales) into `app/desktop/build/media-demo/`, same encode cache `work/ship-media/`; no `pack-media.json`; `--check --demo` against the demo pools and `media-budget.json` `demo` (`content`: measured size + margin; `file`, `video`, `horizon` as the full build''s)
- Credits: `app/client/credits.ts` under `TRIVIA_DEMO=1` reads `app/data/demo/pool.json` only → `dist-demo/credits.json`, `dist-demo/CREDITS.md`; the demo config ships that `CREDITS.md`
- Kept: client `dist-demo`, shell files, Steam SDK libs, `LICENSE`, `LICENSE-content.md`; `modding/` per decision 337 (task 6)
- `nix build`: no demo output (decision 342)

## Staging and VDFs (`trivia-steam stage|vdf --demo`)
- `steam.py`: depots from `release/demo/{win,linux}-unpacked/` and `build/media-demo/`, archives `LivingRoomTriviaDemo-<v>-…`; union of OS depot + content = the archive (as today); no DLC staging; fails if the demo''s `resources/data/` holds `bundles/` or a full base pool
- `vdf --demo`: `steam.json` `demo.appid`, `demo.depots`; out `work/steam/<tag>/demo/vdf/`; `--dry-run` placeholders as the full (480, 481…)

## Smoke in the demo (`smoke.mjs --demo`)
- Runs `release/demo/linux-unpacked/living-room-trivia-demo` with plan 89''s recipe (offline, `env -i`, temp `HOME`, `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`)
- Every built mode once: «Solo o en grupo» (today''s solo run: levels 1–3, image, audio, video, quit, resume), Gamemaster (start, a few levels; new scene if smoke has none), and `--multiplayer`''s rr-coop, rr-competitive, timed scenes with `--demo`; modes per `BUILT_MODES`
- Demo checks on the way: Start shows the demo line (`screen.start.demo`, `plan 176: Demo on screen`), the bundle screen offers one tile and no pack, no visible text contains `PLACEHOLDER` (plan 176 asks the release check to fail on one), every question id is in `app/data/demo/pool.json`
- Determinism: `--trace <file>` writes per scene the offered and shown question ids and answer orders; the release check runs the demo smoke twice and compares the traces (identical, else ✗ naming the first difference)

## `trivia-release-check --demo`
- Steps: `tag`, `checks` (as the full; same commit), `licenses`, `desktop` (`trivia-desktop-build --demo --dir`, `trivia-steam stage --demo`), `media-budget` (`stage-media.mjs --check --demo`), `credits` (`credits_check.mjs` on the demo''s unpacked dirs: both ways on the demo media), `smoke` (`smoke.mjs --demo --trace` a), `determinism` (run again, trace b, compare), `multiplayer` (`--demo --multiplayer`); `modkit`, `mods` only if mods are on (task 6); no `quality`, `report` steps (the full check''s)
- Manual rows: `offline`, `windows`, `sound`, `signoff` («the developer plays the demo from the demo app''s beta»), demo-only `start-line` (the start screen''s demo line, the bundle tile); `report`, `telemetry`, `workshop`, `cloud` per decision 337 (task 6)
- Report `work/steam/<tag>/demo/release-check.{md,json}`, header: version, demo list''s hash (`authoring/data/demo.json`), demo pool count per locale, `demo` marked
- Exit 1 on any ✗; `--skip`, `--manual` as the full

## `trivia-steam upload --demo --branch beta`
- Gates as the full upload (clean tree, tag `v<version>`, `steam.json` `demo` IDs set, branch `beta` only) → `trivia-release-check --demo` (or `--checked`: the demo report of this commit) → `stage --demo` → `vdf --demo` → `steamcmd +run_app_build`; `--preview`, `--dry-run` as the full; `Desc` `<tag> <sha> demo` plus skips
- Same tag as the full build: the developer uploads both from one commit (decision 342)

## Tasks
1. **Demo build ships only the demo''s data and media** (`app`, 610, after task 1536 and `task 1544: Demo pools in export and validate`): data cut in `electron-builder.demo.yml`, `stage-media.mjs --demo` (+ `--check --demo`), `media-budget.json` `demo`, `credits.ts` demo pools; check: `trivia-desktop-build --demo --dir` → `release/demo/` has no `bundles/`, no full base pool, `demo/` pools; `resources/media/` = the demo pools'' media; `CREDITS.md` lists only them; the full build''s file list unchanged (throw-away compare). Docs: `directory.md` if needed, `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Builds and depots" demo line
2. **`trivia-steam stage|vdf --demo`** (`app`, 610, after 1): above; check: `trivia-steam stage --demo` ✓ on task 1''s build, ✗ with a `bundles/` folder copied in; `vdf --demo --out <tmp>` renders the demo app with three depots, no DLC
3. **Demo smoke and determinism trace** (`app`, 600, after 1, `task 1549: Deterministic demo selection in the engine`, `task 1546: Demo pool in the client`, plan 176''s tasks 1–2 for the start line and tile): `smoke.mjs --demo`, `--trace`, the Gamemaster scene, the demo checks; check: passes twice with identical traces; a shown question outside the demo list or a PLACEHOLDER text fails it (throw-away)
4. **`trivia-release-check --demo`** (`app`, 600, after 2 and 3): steps, manual rows, report; check: runs green on a clean main with the demo build (manual rows "skipped (worker)"), the full check unchanged. Docs: README release how-to (demo next to full), `AGENTS.md` Commands `trivia-release-check` (`--demo`), plan 18 SW-6 text
5. **`trivia-steam upload --demo`** (`app`, 590, after 4): above; check: `--dry-run --demo` on a clean main writes `work/steam/<sha>/demo/` with VDFs pointing at the demo''s staged folders; null demo IDs refused without `--dry-run`; `--branch default` refused. Docs: README "Upload to Steam", `AGENTS.md` Commands `trivia-steam` and `trivia-desktop-build` rows (`--demo`), plan 18 "Builds and depots" demo bullets
6. **Demo package per decision 337** (`app`, 590, `pm task-pending-decision` on decision 337): mods off → `electron-builder.demo.yml` without `modding/`, no `modkit`/`mods` steps in `--demo`; telemetry, reports, Cloud on → their manual rows in `--demo` with the demo App ID; achievements per the answer; check: `--demo` lists exactly the answer''s rows and steps
7. **First demo beta upload** (`app`, 580, after 5 and 6; waits for part 6''s checklist decision with the demo App ID and depot IDs, and task 681''s first full upload): fill `steam.json` `demo`; `trivia-steam upload --demo --branch beta`; `pm decision add --once "First demo beta upload done? BuildID?"` (options: uploaded (BuildID …) / failed (paste the error)); after the answer: plan 18 demo line with date and BuildID, or a fix task per error. If part 6''s decision doesn''t exist yet or is unanswered: `pm task-pending-decision` on it (or say so in a note) and stop

## Done when
- `trivia-desktop-build --demo --dir` ships the demo pools and their media only; `trivia-steam stage --demo` ✓
- `trivia-release-check --demo` runs the demo''s steps, two smoke runs give identical traces, no PLACEHOLDER on a demo screen
- `trivia-steam upload --demo --branch beta --dry-run` renders the demo app''s VDFs; the first demo build is on the demo app''s `beta` (task 7''s decision)
- Full build, release check and upload unchanged; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass', 'The free demo has to be packed and sent to Steam just like the full game, but with only its own small set of questions and their pictures, sounds and videos inside. This work makes the build leave out everything the demo doesn''t contain, adds an automatic check before every demo upload that plays the demo in every game mode and proves two identical plays show the same questions, and lets the developer upload the demo to its own Steam entry with the same safety gates as the full game.', '2026-10-17T13:35:36Z', 1529);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (178, 18, 'Steamworks demo app and store', 290, 'Part 6 of `plan 154: masterplan`: Valve''s rules for demos, the demo app in Steamworks (the developer''s checklist and its decision), the demo''s store presence, and the real demo App ID in the repo. Docs, store material and pm; one constant change. Workers never log into Steamworks. After `plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)` and `plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)`; `plan 177: Demo packaging, release check and upload`''s real upload waits for this plan''s checklist decision. Work tree `app`.

## Valve''s rules (read 2026-10-17)
- [Demos](https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/store/application/demos):
  - own App ID tied to the base app: base app landing page → "All associated packages, DLC, demos and tools" → "Add Demo"; own depots, own builds "just like a full app" (upload with the demo''s App ID, [uploading](https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/uploading)); own release checklist and configuration
  - no app fee named (as free DLC, `plans/17-publishing.md` "DLC"); recheck at creation
  - store: either a "Download demo" button on the base game''s page, or an own demo store page (user reviews, no community hub, link back to the full game); own page needs demo-only description, features, languages, modes, ≥ 5 demo screenshots and a trailer, capsules and library assets marked as demo, own content survey; base-only features not listed
  - after the demo''s release: re-publish the base game''s store page by hand, else no "Download demo" button
  - before launch: possible from the coming-soon page, Valve "generally recommend[s] waiting until launch"; wishlist notification once, within two weeks of the demo''s first release
  - Cloud: the demo''s saves can go to the full game''s cloud (shared cloud), only once the full game is released
  - achievements: "We recommend that you disable achievements in demos"
  - no full-game ↔ demo matchmaking (moot: local multiplayer only); `ActivateGameOverlayToStore` links the demo to the full game''s store page
  - testing before release: demo keys requested in Steamworks, activated on the developer''s account
  - Workshop, stats, rich presence, Steam Input, DLC: not mentioned
- [Steam Cloud](https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/features/cloud): "Shared cloud APP ID" in the demo''s Cloud settings, 0 = off; unreleased base app → no sync
- [Steam Next Fest](https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/marketing/upcoming_events/nextfest): base page public, demo public by the start, game unreleased until the end, registration from the base game, review ≥ 3 (≥ 5 for press preview) weeks ahead; review checks that it runs and has the promised features, later updates unreviewed
- The demo app''s store and library pages were read from a summary of the fetched page; recheck the wording at entry

## Decisions
- Raised by this plan: `decision 343: Demo store presence: own store page, or only the Download demo button on the full game''s page?`, `decision 344: Demo release: with the full game''s launch, or earlier from the coming-soon page?`
- Fed back into part 1: `decision 345: Demo save and Steam''s shared cloud: keep the demo''s save apart, or share it with the full game''s cloud?` (beside pending `decision 336: Demo save: separate from the full game''s, or shared/imported on purchase?`; `task 1538: Demo save location and single-instance lock per decision 336` waits on both), `decision 346: Achievements in the demo: off, as Valve recommends?` (beside pending `decision 337: Steam features in the demo: Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry, question reports`; `task 1539: Demo Steam feature gates: mods, Workshop, publish, achievements per decision 337` waits on both)
- Binding: `decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`, `decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): how is the game sold on Steam?` (the demo free, no DLC in it), `decision 84: SteamCMD source and depot split for Steam uploads` and `decision 342: Demo packaging: own staging folders, three depots, own reports, no nix output` (depots `windows`, `linux`, `content`), `decision 77: Store capsule art (PUB-8): who makes the capsules and logo?` (demo art from the same template)

## Tasks
1. **Valve''s demo rules in the docs** (`app`, 290; no wait): `plans/17-publishing.md` Valve-docs list gains a "Demos" bullet set (the rules above, with links); `plans/18-steam-integration.md` a short "Demo app" note under the SW-7 section pointing to it and to plan 173''s "Demo" section (task 1541); `rg -i demo plans/` for stale claims (decision 200). Done when: both files cite the pages, nothing contradicts decisions 343–346 as asked.
2. **Demo store material per decision 343** (`app`, 280; `pm task-pending-decision` on 343 and 344):
   - Either way: demo library assets (library capsule, hero, logo, header; Valve''s current sizes, cited) and the demo''s capsules from `authoring/store/capsules.mjs` with a «Demo»/«Demostración»/«Demo» mark per store language (es/es-ES share), the developer approves (decision `--once`); the full game''s store texts in `plans/17a-store-page.md` gain one line naming the free demo per language (style guides `locales/style/<locale>.md` first), approved with that decision
   - Own page only: a "Demo" block in 17a (name, short and long description of the demo''s content, features, languages es, es-ES, en, de), 5+ demo screenshots and a demo trailer from `screenshots.mjs`/`trivia-trailer` under `TRIVIA_DEMO=1` (plan 173''s flag; rendered late as decision 79), content survey as the full game''s
   - Done when: the material exists, the developer approved it
3. **Demo app checklist and the "demo app configured" decision** (`app`, 270; after `task 1045: Real App ID in the repo and SW-7 close-out` and `task 672: Store page entry checklist and PUB-8 close-out`; if either is open: stop without closing, say so):
   - `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Steamworks demo app" section after SW-7: `- [ ]` rows grouped by Steamworks page: Add Demo; names (demo names of plan 173''s Identity, per store language); installation folder `LivingRoomTriviaDemo`; launch options (`LivingRoomTriviaDemo.exe`, `living-room-trivia-demo`), Linux runtime as SW-7; depots `windows`, `linux`, `content` (no DLC); branches `default` empty, `beta` password-protected; Steam Cloud per decisions 336/345 (own Auto-Cloud root, or Shared cloud APP ID = base); achievements per 337/346; Steam Input Gamepad template; rich presence `steam-presence.vdf`; Workshop off unless 337 says on; store presence per 343 (button or own page, material of task 2); demo keys for the developer''s account; release per 344, then re-publish the base store page; pointers, not copies, to SW-7 rows
   - `did=$(pm decision add --once "Steamworks demo app configured? IDs?" …)`, body: the section; options `configured: demo App ID …, depots windows … linux … content …` (recommended), `not yet`, `issues (rows)`; `pm task-pending-decision` task 4 and plan 177''s "First demo beta upload" task (look it up in `pm show p177`) on it
   - Done when: section written, decision pending, both tasks wait
4. **Demo App ID in the repo** (`app`, 260; waits on task 3''s decision): `app/desktop/main.mjs` demo `STEAM_APP_ID` 480 → the demo App ID; `authoring/steam/steam.json` `demo` appid and depots (unless plan 177''s upload task filled them); report server accepts the demo App ID (`report-server/wrangler.toml`, plan 173''s list from `task 1540: Demo telemetry mark and question reports for the demo App ID per decision 337`, if reports are on); section rows `[x]`; issues → follow-up tasks; `pm decision consequences`. Check: `npm run check`, `trivia-steam vdf --demo --dry-run`. Done when: no demo 480 left outside `--dry-run`

## Out of scope
- An in-game "buy the full game" link (`ActivateGameOverlayToStore`): not in the milestone; demo start screen is `plan 176: Demo on screen`
- Steam Next Fest registration: only if decision 344 says before launch, then its own task
- Uploading builds (plan 177), the full game''s app (plan 130), the full store page (plan 88)', 'The free demo is its own entry on Steam, tied to the full game, with its own settings, files and release steps. This work writes down what Valve allows and recommends for demos, prepares the demo''s store art and texts, gives the developer a checklist for setting the demo up in Steam''s partner site, and puts the demo''s real Steam number into the game once it exists. It also asks the developer how the demo shows on the store and when it goes live.', '2026-10-17T13:39:05Z', 1530);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (179, 18, 'Close-out: play the demo', 120, 'Part 7 of `plan 154: masterplan`, last: proves `milestone 18: Playable demo` and closes it. A headless run plays the demo build in every mode × age group to an end, twice, with identical questions, and stays in the demo''s release check; the developer then plays the demo from Steam''s beta branch through one checklist decision; failures go back to the plan that owns them; a docs sweep makes every doc name the demo. Work tree `app`. Workers never play the Steam build or answer for the developer.

## Builds on (don''t rebuild)
- `plan 173: Demo build switch, identity and save` (flag, names, save, Steam feature gates), `plan 174: The demo base bundle` (list, demo pools), `plan 175: Deterministic selection in the demo`, `plan 176: Demo on screen` (start line, tile, hidden screens, gallery review), `plan 177: Demo packaging, release check and upload` (`smoke.mjs --demo --trace`, `trivia-release-check --demo`, first demo beta upload), `plan 178: Steamworks demo app and store`
- Decisions: `decision 335: Playable demo: a build variant of the same code, switched at build time`, `decision 338: Demo flag: TRIVIA_DEMO at build, dist-demo, package.json demo, EngineData.demo`, `decision 339: Demo bundle format: an id list of base questions, exported to app/data/demo/ pools, questions stay in base`, `decision 340: Demo selection: every shuffle seeded from its site and the items it shuffles`, `decision 341: Demo bundle tile: its name and question count`, `decision 342: Demo packaging: own staging folders, three depots, own reports, no nix output`; answers of `decision 336: Demo save: separate from the full game''s, or shared/imported on purchase?`, `decision 337: Steam features in the demo: Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry, question reports`, 343–346 (store, release, shared cloud, achievements) as they stand when the tasks run
- Modes: `BUILT_MODES` (`engine/game.ts`) at that time; unbuilt ones not in the demo (`decision 293: Unbuilt multiplayer modes: on the mode row in dev mode only`); multiplayer modes via `plan 166: Shipping the multiplayer modes and docs`
- Model: `plan 167: Local multiplayer close-out and family playtest` (headless step, one `--once` playtest decision, routing, "again" round)

## Decisions taken here
- `decision 347: Demo close-out: the mode × age group run stays in the demo release check`: `smoke.mjs --demo --matrix`, step `matrix` in `trivia-release-check --demo`
- One playtest decision (`--once`) for the whole demo, rows ✓/✗ + note
- `failed` routing: flag, names, window title, save location, Steam feature gates → plan 173; a question missing, too few for a mode or group, a translation → plan 174; questions differ between runs, seen counts showing, running-out notice → plan 175; start line, bundle tile, a hidden screen showing, PLACEHOLDER, text fit → plan 176; build contents, media, credits, release check, upload → plan 177; Steamworks app, store, Cloud, achievements in Steam → plan 178; once that plan is done: a new plan in milestone 18 (`pm plan add 18 …`) named after the failure

## Tasks to split into
1. **Headless: every mode × age group to an end, twice; release-check step `matrix`** (`app`, 120, `--model opus`)
   - Wait: tasks 1559 (`smoke.mjs --demo`, `--trace`) and 1560 (`trivia-release-check --demo`) done, and plan 174''s list approved (`authoring/data/demo.json` `approved` set); else stop without closing and say which
   - `smoke.mjs --demo --matrix`: the packaged demo build as `--demo` runs it; per `BUILT_MODES` mode × age group (`kids`, `young_teens`, `young_adults`, `adults` today; read from `app/data/age-groups.json`) one game from Choice to an end; multiplayer modes with fake pads at the demo list''s `seats` (rr-competitive seats in mixed groups once); answers from the demo pool as the solo smoke does, mixing correct and wrong so wins and losses both occur; jokers used where the mode has them (fills replacements)
   - Ends checked: a win at level 12 in each mode at least once per group (the list''s supply reaches the top), no `supply_short` / `no_questions`, every shown id in `app/data/demo/pool.json`
   - `--trace` per game as plan 177''s; `release_check.py --demo` step `matrix` after `determinism`: run twice, compare traces, ✗ names the first difference or the short game; header comments of `smoke.mjs`, `release_check.py`; `AGENTS.md` `trivia-release-check` row; `plans/11-steam.md` release checklist
   - Full build''s steps unchanged; the step lands only green; a failure → follow-up per routing
2. **The developer plays the demo from Steam''s beta** (`app`, 110, after 1 and `task 1563: First demo beta upload`; if 1563 isn''t done: stop without closing, say so) — `pm decision add --once "Demo: played from Steam''s beta branch?"`, body written against what was built (`rg` names, keys, commands):
   - setup: the demo app''s `beta` branch under Steam (BuildID of task 1563''s decision), demo keys on the developer''s account per plan 178; full game installed beside it or not (note which)
   - rows: start screen (demo line, wording in the UI language, window title); language picker (only demo locales); Bundles (one tile, demo name and count); each mode in `BUILT_MODES` once, any age group, to an end; one mode a second time with the same choices: same questions (decision 340); the Esc menu and ☰ menu without the screens decision 337 turns off; save per decision 336 (full game''s save untouched, if installed); Steam features per 337/345/346 (Cloud, achievements, reports, telemetry consent as answered); text fits on the TV; one UI language other than es
   - answer: date, BuildID, ✓/✗ per row + note; "passed" (recommended) | "failed (list: row, screen, what happened)"
   - `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <decision>` and stop; after the answer: ✗ → follow-ups per routing plus one task in this plan "Demo playtest again" raising a new decision of the same shape once they''re done (as decision 155 followed decision 50); ✓ → close
3. **Close-out: docs sweep and milestone 18 Done** (`app`, 100, after 2 passed or its "again" passed)
   - `plans/11-steam.md`: demo app, its release check and upload next to the full game''s; `plans/17-publishing.md`: the demo (Valve rules from plan 178, store presence per decision 343, release per 344); `plans/22-bundles.md`: the demo section (decision 339, tile per 341, replacement rule) complete and true
   - `rg -i demo` over `plans/`, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `directory.md` (decision 200): every hit true for the built demo; "demo save(s)" of the gallery and trailer (synthetic saves) kept apart from the demo build in wording, renamed where a reader could confuse them (e.g. «sample save»), code names they point to checked by `rg`
   - `plans/project.md`: `[x] Playable demo (<date>, pm milestone 18, plans 154, 173–178, this plan; decisions 335–347)` with the real ids at that time
   - Milestone 18 text checked against tasks 1 and 2 (all base features, only the demo list, fixed selection, seen counts disregarded, start line); a gap → follow-up task; `pm decision consequences` on decisions whose built result differs (from tasks 1 and 2''s notes); per-commit checks

## Done when
- `trivia-release-check --demo`''s `matrix` step plays every mode × age group to an end, twice, identical
- The developer''s playtest decision answered «passed» (after any "again" round)
- `rg -i demo` over plans, README, AGENTS.md finds nothing stale; `plans/project.md` marks milestone 18 done', 'The free demo is only finished once it has really been played. This last step first lets the computer play the demo in every game mode for every age group, twice, and checks both runs showed the same questions, a check that stays before every demo release. Then the developer plays the demo as players will get it, from Steam, and anything wrong goes back to the part that built it. Finally the project''s documents are brought up to date so they all describe the demo as it was built.', '2026-10-17T13:40:23Z', 1531);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (180, 1, 'Drafting fixes after batch-10: overlap and riddles', 700, 'Implements `decision 350: Overlap rate in drafting: which changes?` (answer 1) and `decision 351: First-person riddle questions: which changes?` (answer 1 + option 7). Findings in the notes of `task 1573` and `task 1574`. Successor of `plan 15: Duplicate and drift detection` (overlap, health limits) and `plan 16: Quality control after every batch` (prompt changes from batch findings), both done.
- Runs before the next `qgen batch` (base or `colombia`): priority 700 is above the batch tasks'' -100/-110 in the `questions` work tree.
- The next batch''s report shows the effect: overlap rate ≈ 10–11 %, riddle share ≈ 5 %, top clue ≈ 51–53 % under 60 %.', 'Two changes to how new questions are drafted, from the batch-10 investigations: fewer drafts thrown away because they repeat a question from another topic, and first-person riddles only where the riddle form adds something.', '2026-10-17T15:42:07Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (181, 6, 'Category splash on the question screen', 300, 'On every new question, the question screen shows the question''s category big and centred, with its subcategory in small text below it. After ≈ 1 s both leave with an exit animation and a sound effect; one of ≈ 20 pairs is picked per question.

## Look
- On top of the question, choices and media; the screen underneath is fully visible and playable (`pointer-events: none`, answering and jokers aren''t blocked)
- Category: display font, big (≈ 8–10 vw), centred; outline (`-webkit-text-stroke` / `paint-order: stroke`) + drop shadow, readable on any image, at 1920 × 1080 and 1280 × 800
- Subcategory: small text below it, same outline and shadow, thinner
- Names via `displayName("category"| "subcategory", …)` in the question''s locale (`lang={questionLocale()}`); long names wrap or shrink, never overflow
- After the splash nothing stays; Cambiazo''s topic label in `question/Card.svelte` stays as it is

## Exits (≈ 20)
- One table `{ id, category: keyframes/transition, subcategory: minor exit, sound cue }` in a new `game/question/Splash.svelte` (+ `splash.ts` if it grows); random per question, no repeat within the last 5
- Category exits (the big one):
  1. dissolve into particles
  2. explode into letters flying outwards
  3. fly off left
  4. fly off right
  5. shoot up like a rocket
  6. drop down with gravity and bounce off-screen
  7. blown away by wind (letters peel off one by one, left to right)
  8. fade to transparency
  9. roll up like a blind
  10. flushed down: spiral and shrink into a drain point
  11. shrink to a dot and pop
  12. zoom towards the viewer and past the camera
  13. spin away (rotation + shrink)
  14. shatter like glass
  15. melt / drip down
  16. sucked into a black hole in the middle
  17. letters scatter like startled birds
  18. typewriter backspace (deleted letter by letter from the end)
  19. paper fold: folds up and flies away as a paper plane
  20. jelly wobble, then squash flat into the floor
- Subcategory exits: a smaller set of light moves (fade, slide down, tiny shrink, blur out, slight drift with the category), picked to go with the category exit; slightly before or after it
- Sounds: one cue per exit, added to `sound.svelte.ts` (`Cue`, synth version + `SAMPLE_FOR` recording); reuse existing samples where one fits (whoosh, estallido, vidrio, cohete, pop, …), new recordings CC0 or allowlisted (D-45), Kenney.nl packs first (UI-10), listed in `app/client/public/audio/CREDITS.md`

## Timing and modes
- Starts when the question card has flipped in; ≈ 1 s hold, exit ≤ 0.8 s; constants in `game/timing.ts`
- `reducedMotion()`: plain fade, sound kept
- Every screen that shows a question: solo/Gamemaster question screen and the local multiplayer modes (Timed included); not on the reveal or after a Paso/Cambiazo swap (the new question gets its own splash)
- Muted under `PM_WORKER` / `TRIVIA_MUTE=1` as every cue

## Done when
- Each of the 20 exits can be played on `/?efectos` (`EffectsDemo.svelte`) with its sound
- A gallery review set of the splash at hold time (`trivia-gallery --set task-<id> --only <shots>`), for each UI language
- The developer approves the exits and sounds on the TV (pm decision, `once`)', 'When a question appears, its topic flashes up big in the middle of the screen, over the question and the answer choices, and after a moment it leaves in one of about twenty funny ways, each with its own sound. Today the family never sees which topic a question comes from, unless a joker changed it. The splash tells them at a glance and adds a bit of show to every question.', '2026-10-17T18:00:00Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (182, 6, 'Soundtracks', 180, 'Part 6 of `plan 6: masterplan`. The music becomes a choice of soundtracks: each soundtrack is one matched set of the three loops `normal` (menu), `question`, `submitted`, with tension clearly rising at each step and a calm, relaxing menu loop (the synthesized loops are the model: chill, a clear rise on submit). Runs after `plan 33: Recorded music loops (UI-10)`: reuses its pipeline, loop points, budget conventions and `/?efectos`. Owner plan file: `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` ("Music", "Sound assets", UI-10 note).

## Binding
- `decision 83: Recorded music loops: approve on the TV?`: plan 33''s set stays as one soundtrack, 3–4 more recorded ones, selectable in a menu, the developer picks the default on the TV
- Milestone 6 "Soundtracks" (developer, 2026-10-17); D-45 licences only (CC0 preferred, CC BY with credit; no NC/ND/unknown); offline; no new npm or Python dependencies
- Decision 199 (import, don''t copy): the Overlay''s row kinds, `setVolumes`'' storage pattern, `EffectsDemo.svelte`
- UI strings: `app/client/src/locales/style/<locale>.md` read first, all four catalogs (es, es-ES, en, de)

## What exists (2026-10-17)
- `app/client/src/game/sound.svelte.ts`: `music(track)`, `startTrack()`; `MUSIC_FILE` maps `normal`/`question`/`submitted` to `musica-normal`/`-pregunta`/`-enviada`; one `LOOP_END` (19.2 s) and one `MUSIC_LEVEL` (1.6); `beatGoesOn` keeps the beat on the `question` ↔ `submitted` cut; `generate()` is the synth loop (A minor, 76/96/120 bpm, `timed` 132 bpm), used for `timed` always and as the fallback; `music(track, { synth })` forces synth (`/?efectos`)
- Volumes: `localStorage` `trivia.volumes` (`loadVolumes`, `setVolumes`), validated on load
- `Overlay.svelte` «Sonido» rows (`sound: true`): volume rows (←/→ steps, slider), mute, telemetry; value rows like `level`/`replace` step with ←/→
- `/?efectos` (`EffectsDemo.svelte`): «grabado» / «sintetizado» per loop incl. `timed`, «corte», «parar»
- `app/client/public/audio/`: flat, 2.8 MB, plan 33''s loops 707 kB together; `CREDITS.md` rows read by `app/client/credits.ts` (Credits screen) and checked by `authoring/steam/credits_check.mjs` (file ↔ row, flat folder)
- `app/desktop/media-budget.json` has no audio key; plan 33''s 3.5 MB folder budget was a convention, not checked
- Timed (`plan 164: Timed game screens, drama and sound`, sound tasks done): `Game.svelte` `MUSIC.timed = "timed"`, ducked during a claim; round screen keeps `normal`

## Soundtracks
- `sintetizada`: the generated loops (`generate()`), incl. its own `timed` track
- `variaciones`: plan 33''s set (OpenGameArt «Music loop variations», obscure music, CC0), audio unchanged
- 3–4 recorded ones, ids named by the sourcing task (ASCII, lower case, Spanish like the other files, e.g. by mood)
- Display names: catalog keys `soundtrack.<id>` in the four catalogs, short and descriptive of the mood («Sintetizada», «Variaciones», …), not the source''s title

## Sourcing (as plan 33)
- Kenney.nl first, then OpenGameArt, Freesound; D-45 allowlist, CC0 preferred; download by hand, no pack zips committed, only the converted files
- A matched set: one piece at three intensities, or stems that build up; same key and tempo family (ideally one tempo and loop length, so the beat goes on at the ~80 ms cut)
- Vibe: menu calm and relaxing; `question` noticeably more tense; `submitted` clearly the most tense; no lyrics; no set that sounds like another one already in
- Fewer than 3 good sets: a developer decision with what was found (per set: source, licence, a line on the vibe, files staged under `work/soundtracks/` to listen to), options e.g. take these, take fewer, one recording varied by rate/filter like plan 33''s decision options; the task waits on it
- Pipeline (plan 33): `nix shell nixpkgs#ffmpeg-headless`, cut to whole bars at the loop point, loudness-normalized to plan 33''s target (−18 LUFS), AAC `.m4a`, 96–128 kbit/s, loops 20–40 s; check the seam, store the loop points
- `CREDITS.md`: one row per file (source URL, pack, author, licence), CC0 too

## File layout
- Flat folder, `musica-<soundtrack>-<track>.m4a` with `<track>` `normal` | `pregunta` | `enviada` (as today); plan 33''s three files renamed `musica-variaciones-*.m4a` (`git mv`, audio unchanged), their `CREDITS.md` rows follow
- `credits_check.mjs` (flat folder) and `credits.ts` need no change beyond the rows; check after the rename
- Budget: `media-budget.json` gets `"audio": 7` (MB, the whole `app/client/public/audio/` folder: today 2.8 MB + 4 sets of ≤ 1 MB + headroom for part 7''s joker sounds); one soundtrack set ≤ 1 MB; `app/desktop/stage-media.mjs --check` checks it like `horizon` (✓/✗ line, fail over budget); raise only with the size stated; this replaces plan 33''s 3.5 MB folder note

## Engine (`sound.svelte.ts`)
- `SOUNDTRACKS`: per id the three file names (or none for `sintetizada`), `loopStart`/`loopEnd`, `level` (as `MUSIC_LEVEL`), `sameBeat` (the three loops share tempo and length: the cut continues at the old position, else starts at 0); replaces `MUSIC_FILE`, `LOOP_END`, `MUSIC_LEVEL`
- `SAMPLE_NAMES` from the table, not by hand; decoding all sets at the unlock is fine within the budget (decode lazily per soundtrack only if the unlock gets slow on the Deck)
- The soundtrack in `sound` state, stored in `localStorage` (`trivia.soundtrack`, next to `trivia.volumes`); an unknown or missing id → the default
- `setSoundtrack(id)`: stores it; if a loop track (`normal`, `question`, `submitted`, `timed`) is playing, crossfade (~0.8 s, the screen fade lengths) to the same track of the new soundtrack, from 0; `roll`, `victory`, silence: nothing to do, the next `music()` picks it up
- A recorded file missing or failing to decode: that track plays the generated loop (fallback as today)
- `timed`: a recorded soundtrack plays its `question` loop; `sintetizada` keeps the generated `timed`; ducking during a claim unchanged
- Unchanged: `roll`, `victory`, effects, the 600/800 ms fades, the ~80 ms cuts, ducking (04 "Music")
- `music(track, { synth })`: the `synth` override becomes a soundtrack override for `/?efectos` (play a given soundtrack''s loop without changing the stored choice)
- Default: `sintetizada` until the developer picks (the last task)
- Header comment of `sound.svelte.ts`: what is recorded, what synthesized

## Picker (Esc menu)
- «Sonido» gets «Banda sonora» above the volume rows: label and the current soundtrack''s name; ←/→ (pad, keyboard) steps through the soundtracks, wrapping; Enter or a click steps forward; mouse: ‹ › arrows on the row like the volume slider''s place; `tick` on change
- Switches live (above), so the developer can compare on the TV with the menu open: the music under the Esc menu keeps playing (check it does; if the overlay mutes or ducks it, the picker still switches what plays after)
- Fits 1280×800 with telemetry rows shown; mod Overlay props unchanged
- Catalog keys: `overlay.soundtrack` and `soundtrack.<id>` in es, es-ES, en, de

## Audition (`/?efectos`)
- One row per soundtrack × loop (`normal`, `pregunta`, `enviada`, and `timed` for what it maps to), «corte» per soundtrack (`question` ↔ `submitted`), «parar»; loops run long enough to hear the seam
- The picker in the Esc menu is the TV comparison in a real game

## Docs
- `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md` "Music": soundtracks (sets, picker, live switch, `timed` mapping, default); "Sound assets": flat folder, file names, audio budget; the UI-10 note gets a line; Esc menu lines in "Admin overlay"
- `task 150: Close UI-10 in the plans` runs after this plan and part 7 (`plan 32: Recorded sound effects (UI-10)`); its 3.5 MB check becomes the `audio` budget

## Tasks (suggested split)
1. Soundtrack engine and layout: `SOUNDTRACKS` table, rename plan 33''s files, per-soundtrack loop points/level/`sameBeat`, stored choice, `setSoundtrack` with live crossfade, `timed` mapping, fallback, default `sintetizada`; `/?efectos` per soundtrack; `"audio"` budget in `media-budget.json` + check in `stage-media.mjs`; `CREDITS.md` rows renamed; 04 "Music"/"Sound assets" lines; checked with `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` (switch while each track plays, `timed`, files removed → synth)
2. «Banda sonora» in the Esc menu: the row (pad, keyboard, mouse), strings in four catalogs per `locales/style/<locale>.md`, 1280×800 and 1920×1080; after task 1
3. Source and convert 3–4 matched sets (`--web`): sourcing, conversion, loop points, levels by ear-proxy (loudness, as plan 33), `CREDITS.md` rows, `SOUNDTRACKS` entries and names in four catalogs, budget check passes; fewer than 3 good sets: the decision above, the task waits on it; after task 1
4. The default soundtrack (developer): `pm decision add` (kind once) asking the developer to listen on the TV (Esc menu «Banda sonora» in a real game, `/?efectos`), one option per soundtrack (synth first as today''s default), plus «changes: <soundtrack> → …» (level, seam, drop a set); task pending on it; then set the default, apply changes, update 04 "Music" (default named); after tasks 1–3

## Done when
- The Esc menu offers every soundtrack by name in all four languages; switching crossfades live; the choice survives a restart
- Each recorded soundtrack: three loops, no click at the seam, credited; `timed` plays its question loop (recorded) or the generated `timed` (synth)
- `stage-media.mjs --check` passes the `audio` budget; `credits_check.mjs` passes
- The developer picked the default on the TV; 04 updated
- Per commit: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`', 'The game plays background music that gets more tense as a question is answered. The developer liked the recorded music better than the music the game makes itself, but its mood was wrong, so instead of one set of music there will be several to choose from in the pause menu, each a calm menu tune that gets clearly more tense during a question and after an answer is locked in. The family can switch while the music plays to compare, and the developer picks which one plays by default after listening on the TV.', '2026-10-17T23:52:49Z', 1597);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (183, 18, 'Demo list translations', 600, 'Follow-up to `plan 174: The demo base bundle`: once `authoring/data/demo.json` is `approved`, a listed id missing an approved translation is a `qgen validate` error, and 79 are.

## Tasks
1. Investigate and fix the missing translations (`questions`, 600)', 'The approved demo question list still has 79 questions without a translation in every launch language, so the pool check fails until they are translated or replaced.', '2026-10-18T01:11:04Z', NULL);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (184, 19, 'Pipeline for topic bundles', 700, 'Part 1 of `plan 155: masterplan` (milestone 19: topic question bundles): make `qgen` handle `kind: theme` bundles end to end, so part 2 can create `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography` and part 3 can run batches for them. No content here; one throw-away theme bundle checks the chain.

## Builds on (binding)
- `plan 155: masterplan` "Builds on": `plans/22-bundles.md` (bundles add questions, base keeps its sports/film/history/science/geography), `decision 112: Pack layout: a pool file per bundle (optional install)`, `decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings` (2000 per non-base bundle), `decision 18: Which new base subcategories?` (fan level → topic bundles).
- `decision 236: English-first drafting for base: what drives drafting and which locales steer it`: per-locale deficits of en, es, es-ES, de; English draft gap = largest over the four of deficit / yield − untranslated sources (`targets.locale_gap`). `translations.draft_locale()` already returns `en` for a theme.
- `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`: a locale''s count = its sources + playing translations (`targets.approved_entries`).
- `decision 350: Overlap rate in drafting: which changes?`: `draw_slots` probes the whole pool (every bundle) per concept, `rate` sees ≤ 8 `overlap_candidates` from the whole pool, `duplicates()` at merge.
- `decision 262: Taxonomy prompts on slug keys: apply?`: prompt changes go to the developer as verbatim drafts with an "apply?" decision, checked on a scratch bundle.
- `decision 227: Media share below 15 %: lower the none weight, and which residual-miss fixes?` and `decision 13: Batch health thresholds and stop rule?`: media share 15–50 % per batch.
- `plans/23-media-providers.md`: licence allowlist; never NC/ND/editorial: film stills, posters, trailers, soundtracks are out.
- D-36 / AGENTS.md "Making questions": RUNBOOK unchanged; no pipeline step run by hand on real bundles.

## Code today (read for this plan)
- `cmd_taxonomy` / `apply_taxonomy` (`qgen.py`): exit unless `kind == "region"`; prompt `taxonomy.md` + general list `regional-categories.json`; schema has `region` and `origin: general|region`.
- `cmd_bundle_new`: target (`targets.REGION_TOTAL`, `targets.scaled`) only for `region`; `languages` defaults to `["es"]`, wrong for a theme drafting in en.
- `targets.problems`: requires an entry only for regional bundles.
- `targets.draft_gaps`: per-locale gap only for `bundle == "base"`; any other bundle drafts against `deficits(pool, bundle)` without a locale, i.e. all approved sources.
- `report_supply` (`qgen report`) only for base; `bundle_costs` (`--cost`) rows only for `kind: region` × es, en.
- `source_locale_problems` (`validate`): base ≥ batch-9 must be en, region its language; theme unchecked.
- Overlap: `draw_slots` and `rate` already cross bundles; gaps: `existing_answers` (drafter''s avoid list) is the own subcategory only, and `cmd_concepts` shows the concept-list call only the own subcategory''s questions, so a theme''s concept lists pick base''s famous concepts again.
- `voice_locale`, `prompt()`: theme''s es text gets base''s voice; `translate-region.md` only for regions (right for themes).

## Tasks
Work tree `questions`, one change per task, in this order.

1. **Theme taxonomy: code and prompt draft**
   - `qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>` accepts `kind: theme`: no general list; one opus call from the bundle''s `rule`, its target (`PER_SUBCATEGORY` 40 → ≈ 50 subcategories) and base''s subcategories on the same topic, shown with their approved counts, so the proposal goes deeper than base, not beside it.
   - New prompt `taxonomy-theme.md` (or a `{kind}` part of `taxonomy.md`, whichever reads simpler); same proposal format (`slug`, `en`, `name` = en), `origin` → `base_extends` / `new`; per subcategory `base_related`: the base subcategory slugs it goes beyond (feeds task 4).
   - `--apply`: as today (`categories.json`, `names.{en,es,de}.json`, es/de drafted by `taxonomy-names.md`) plus `authoring/data/bundles/<id>/base-related.json` (authoring only, never shipped).
   - Check on a scratch theme bundle (not committed); then `pm decision add "Theme taxonomy prompt: apply?"` with the prompt verbatim and the scratch proposal''s counts, task pending on it (decision 262 pattern); `qgen` refuses a theme proposal until applied.
2. **Targets for theme bundles**
   - `qgen bundle new --kind theme`: writes `targets.json` `<id>`: 2000, base''s mix scaled (`targets.scaled`; rename `REGION_TOTAL` to a name for every non-base bundle, `rg` comments/docs, decision 200); `languages` default `["en"]` for a theme (the draft locale; part 2 lists the others as pools come); message names `qgen taxonomy` as next step for themes too.
   - `targets.problems` / `qgen validate`: every non-base bundle needs targets (message names both kinds); `source_locale_problems`: a theme''s sources must be `en`.
3. **Per-locale counting and gap aiming for themes**
   - `targets.draft_gaps`: a theme bundle aims like base: largest over en, es, es-ES, de of `locale_gap` (`source_supply(pool, bundle)`), regions keep their own deficit (D-101); the base-only branch becomes by kind, not by id.
   - `qgen report --bundle <id> [--locale L]`: the supply block (`report_supply`) for a theme too, header names the bundle.
   - Translation picking (`translate_pick`, deficit per locale) already per bundle: check only.
4. **Cross-bundle overlap with base**
   - `cmd_concepts` for a theme subcategory: the call also gets base''s approved and pending questions of the subcategory''s `base_related` (as_locale en, answers + question stems, capped), as "already in the game: don''t list these concepts"; same for `--top-up`.
   - `existing_answers` (drafter''s avoid list) for a theme subcategory adds its `base_related` subcategories'' answers (en, capped like `SAT_ASKED`).
   - `draw_slots` probe and `rate`''s `overlap_candidates` already see base: confirm with a throw-away script on the scratch bundle of task 6, no code change unless they don''t.
   - Theme without `base-related.json` (hand-made, mods): works as today.
5. **`qgen report --cost` per theme bundle**
   - `bundle_costs`: rows per theme × en (drafting, its `--bundle` batches; no own run yet → base''s en draft rate) and × es, es-ES, de (its `--translate --bundle` runs; else base''s translation rate per locale); deficit per locale from task 3; projection as for regions. Text and `--json` output.
   - Part 3''s pacing decision uses these numbers (5 × 2000 × 4 locales).
6. **End-to-end check on a throw-away theme bundle** (after 1–5)
   - On a scratch copy of the repo data (no commit, no symlinked `work/`; `QGEN_WORK` or a temp checkout, whichever the code supports): `qgen bundle new <x> --kind theme`, `qgen taxonomy` + `--apply`, a small `qgen batch --bundle <x>` (few subcategories × few slots), `qgen batch --translate es|es-ES|de --bundle <x>`, `qgen export` writes `app/data/bundles/<x>/pool.json` and `pool.{es-ES,en,de}.json`, `qgen validate` clean, `qgen report --bundle <x>` and `--cost` show it.
   - Report the claude calls and totals (decision 208). Every failure found: fixed here if small, else a follow-up task in this plan.
   - Remove every trace of the scratch bundle afterwards.
7. **Media for `movies` and `sports`**
   - Proposal (no developer choice needed while within `plans/23-media-providers.md`): accept a lower but non-zero media share for `movies`, from what is free: photos of people (actors, directors at events, Commons portraits), places (filming locations, studios, cinemas), objects (awards, props in museums, cameras); never stills, posters, trailers or soundtracks.
   - Mechanism exists (`concepts.load_axes`: a bundle''s own `authoring/data/bundles/<id>/question-axes.json`, else base''s): this task writes the `movies` weights into `plans/22-bundles.md` (`stimulus`: `photo` kept, `video` and `sound` 0, `detail`/`silhouette` low) and a follow-up task in part 2''s plan to write the file with `qgen bundle new movies`; the draft''s media hint comes from the axes, no new prompt.
   - `sports`: base''s axes (athletes, stadiums, equipment are well covered on Commons); no change.
   - If the first `movies` batches fall under health''s 15 % media share: a decision then (per-bundle health minimum vs. more `photo` weight), not now.
8. **Docs**
   - `plans/22-bundles.md`: "In the pipeline" (theme bundles: taxonomy from base''s subcategories, en drafting, per-locale gap, cross-bundle overlap with `base-related.json`), Layout table (`base-related.json` row), media for movies.
   - `plans/16-content-target.md`: Target (theme bundles: 2000 per question locale, gap rule like base), Cost (`--cost` theme rows).
   - `rg` "regional bundle" in `qgen.py` help, `targets.py`, docs where the rule now covers every non-base bundle (decision 200).

## Out of scope
- The five bundles'' rows and taxonomies (part 2), content runs (part 3), game and Steam (parts 4, 5).
- RUNBOOK changes; base''s taxonomy or concept lists.', 'The game is getting five optional question packs on one topic each: science and maths, sports, history, movies and geography. The tools that write, translate and count questions today only know the main pack and packs about one country, so they need to learn this third kind: how to propose a topic pack''s categories, how many questions it needs in each language, how to avoid asking again what the main pack already asks, and what pictures a movie pack can legally show. This work makes those tools ready, so the packs themselves can be filled afterwards.', '2026-10-21T20:22:41Z', 1615);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (185, 19, 'Topic bundles in the game', 400, 'Part 4 of `plan 155: masterplan` (milestone 19): what the game needs so the five topic bundles (`stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography`, `kind: theme`) look and play right: own icons, order and counts on the Bundles screen, a session with only topic bundles, «Cambiazo» with categories of several bundles, and whether they earn achievements. App code only; the rows and pools come from parts 1–3 (`plan 155: masterplan`), Steamworks entries from part 5.

## Builds on (binding)
- `decision 367: Topic bundle icons: an optional icon field in bundles.json, pin as fallback`: optional `icon` on non-region rows (ours and mods''), names a symbol from a fixed bundle-icon list in `Icon.svelte`; region rows keep their flag and reject `icon`; missing/unknown → today''s fallback (ours `pin`, mods `puzzle`); unknown: warning in `--check-mod`, error in `qgen validate` for our rows.
- `decision 368: Achievements for the topic bundles: one per bundle like the regional ones?` (open): task 5 waits on it.
- `decision 263: Bundle screen reviewed in /gallery?` / `plan 151: Bundle selection on its own full screen`: `orderBundles` (base, own region, non-regional, other regions; file order within a group), flags for region rows, any combination incl. base off.
- `decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings`: shipped non-base bundles show «2000+» (`countShown`, fixed for ours): no change needed for ours, check only.
- `decision 195: Supply notice: bundles running out instead of exhausted subcategories`: notice names bundles (`displayName("bundle", …)`); `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` item 2: overlay line «Paquetes de preguntas: …», term "question bundle".
- `decision 158: Bundle selection in every mode, apart from customization`; decision 33: non-base bundles off by default.
- `decision 73: Achievement list (SW-11)?`, `decision 146: Achievements, mods screen and rich presence with mods on` (mods'' bundles never earn `BUNDLE_*`), `plan 86: Achievements (SW-11)` (icons in `app/desktop/achievements/`, `render.sh`, texts in `plans/18-steam-integration.md`).
- `decision 209: Joker symbols for the kept names?` / `decision 210: Spanish joker names and keys (es), translated from the English?`: «Cambiazo» is an old name; the category joker is «Doña Exigente» (es), «Ms Picky» (en), «Wunschzeit» (de); masterplan wording «Cambiazo» = this joker.
- Decision 128 (mod ids `<mod id>:<id>`), decision 133 (`--check-mod` warns on unknown keys).

## Today (code)
- `BundleSelector.svelte` icon: `b.region ? <Flags> : source === "mod" ? "puzzle" : b.base ? "book" : "pin"`; `Bundle` from `ChoiceOptions["bundles"]` (`lib/api.ts` maps `kind` to `base`/`region`, `country`).
- Row checks: `engine/pool.ts` (`countryOk`, bundles loader), `app/desktop/mods.mjs` (`countryOk`), `app/desktop/check-mod.mjs` (`bundle_row` text), `authoring/tools/qgen.py` validate (kinds `base|region|theme`), `authoring/ui/src/lib/types.ts`.
- `CategoryPicker.svelte` + `game.ts` jokers: one flat grid of every active bundle''s broad categories (`data.categories` filtered by active bundles), then subcategories; base alone has ~28 categories, each topic bundle adds ≈ 10–14 (≈ 50 subcategories, part 2), five on ≈ 90 tiles; a sport category of `sports` next to base''s sport category reads as a duplicate.
- Category names during play: `Splash.svelte` (category + subcategory), `Card.svelte` (topic after a swap), `SkipDialog.svelte`, `Shredder` (subcategory).
- `achievements.ts`: `BUNDLE_<ID>` only for `kind === "region"`, not mods, gated by `DLC_BUNDLES`.
- Name clash: mod `kind` `theme` (CSS mods, `mods.mjs`, Workshop tag) vs. bundle `kind: "theme"`; different fields, but `modding/README.md`''s "Player bundles" should name the bundle kinds plainly.

## Throw-away row
- Until part 2''s rows (`stem` …) land in `app/data/bundles.json`, tasks test with a throw-away theme row + tiny pool (a mod folder via `TRIVIA_MODS_DIR`, or a local uncommitted row with `icon`); never committed. Once the rows exist, tasks use them.

## Tasks (suggested order)
1. **`icon` field and bundle icons** (decision 367)
   - Five symbols in `Icon.svelte`, house style of the joker symbols (decision 209): flask (`stem`), ball (`sports`), scroll (`history`), film reel (`movies`, the existing `film` if it reads as one at tile size, else a new `reel`), globe (`geography`: the existing `globe` is the language fallback icon; a globe with meridians different enough, or reuse if the developer''s gallery review accepts it).
   - Fixed list of bundle icons (one exported constant, client TS; the `.mjs`/Python checks name it in a comment, decision 199): the five + `book`, `pin`, `puzzle` and a few generic ones a mod may want (e.g. `heart`, `mic`, `music` if present); `icon` validated against it.
   - Loader (`pool.ts`), `api.ts` `Bundle.icon`, `BundleSelector.svelte`: `b.region ? flag : b.icon ?? fallback`; mods: `mods.mjs`, `check-mod.mjs` (warning `bad_icon`, message lists the names), `qgen validate` (error on our rows; `icon` on a region row an error), `authoring/ui` type, `bundles.json` `about` text, `modding/README.md` + `modding/bundles.md` (field, list, fallback; bundle `kind` values vs. mod `kind`).
   - `qgen bundle new --kind theme`: `--icon <name>` optional, written to the row (part 2 passes it); coordinate: if part 1/2''s tasks already changed `bundle new`, extend, don''t fork.
   - Check: `npm run check`, `qgen validate`, `--check-mod` on a folder with an unknown icon (warning) and a known one; screen with the throw-away row.
2. **Bundles screen with topic bundles on**
   - `orderBundles`: topic bundles in the non-regional group, file order (part 2 writes the rows in the order `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography` unless its decision says otherwise); mods'' theme bundles after ours (file order already does it): check, change only if wrong.
   - Counts «2000+» for ours (decision 267), mod theme bundles own count; tile keys (`bundleKeys`) with seven or more optional tiles per UI language: no empty key for ours (es/en/de names from part 2; if two collide, the later gets the next letter: fine), overlay line (`choice.lineBundles`) and supply notice (decision 195) with five names: line length at 1280×720, wraps without clipping.
   - Session with only a topic bundle on (base off): engine plays 12 levels (enough questions per level in the age group''s window, else the start check''s refusal, plan 151), category joker offers enough categories; with the throw-away row a small pool is expected to refuse: check the refusal names the bundle; full check again when part 3 has ≥ 2000 approved for one bundle (note in the task''s done text, no follow-up wait).
3. **Category joker with several bundles'' categories**
   - Picker groups categories by bundle when more than one bundle is active: a header row per bundle (its icon + name, `displayName("bundle", …)`, base first, then the selector''s order), arrow navigation across groups unchanged (`lib/focus.ts`), scroll with focus follow like the Bundles screen when the tiles don''t fit (≈ 90 at 1280×720); one bundle active: as today, no header.
   - Splash and card (`Splash.svelte`, `Card.svelte`): a non-base question''s category line carries its bundle''s icon (flag for regions), so «Deportes» from `sports` and base''s sport category are told apart; base questions unchanged.
   - No renaming of categories: part 2''s taxonomy decisions keep topic categories distinct from base''s (its proposal sees base''s own subcategories); flag duplicates found in the gallery as a note on part 2''s plan, not here.
   - New on-screen strings (if any, e.g. a header label): every UI catalog, `locales/style/<locale>.md` first.
4. **Gallery shots** (screen gallery, plan 100)
   - Demo saves in `authoring/tools/gallery.py`: a `topics` save/selection with the five topic bundles on (+ base), shots `bundles-topics` (Bundles screen), `cambiazo-topics` (picker with headers), `splash-topic` (a topic question''s splash); with a throw-away row only until part 2''s rows land; the shots skip (listed in the manifest as skipped) when no theme bundle is in the data.
   - Review set `trivia-gallery --set task-<id> --only bundles-topics,cambiazo-topics,splash-topic` per UI language (es, es-ES, en, de) once part 2''s five rows are in `bundles.json` (task waits for that: depends on part 2''s `qgen bundle new` task; if run earlier, `pm task-pending-decision` on part 2''s rows decision); then one review decision "Topic bundles in the game reviewed in /gallery?" linking `/gallery?set=task-<id>`, options `approved` (recommended), `problems: …`.
5. **Theme bundle achievements** (only if decision 368 says yes; else drop with the decision cited)
   - `achievements.ts`: `BUNDLE_<ID>` for `kind === "theme"` too (ours only, decision 146), `DLC_BUNDLES` unchanged mechanism (part 5 adds the ids when the DLC is in Steamworks); `achievements.test.ts` fixture row for a theme bundle if the test file already covers regions.
   - Five icon SVGs `app/desktop/achievements/BUNDLE_<ID>.svg` in the style of `BUNDLE_COLOMBIA.svg`, motif from task 1''s icons; `render.sh` output checked.
   - Texts: rows in `plans/18-steam-integration.md`''s achievement table (latam, spanish, english, german; pattern of `BUNDLE_COLOMBIA`: «Acertar 50 preguntas del paquete …»), style guides first; one review decision "Topic bundle achievement texts?" with the drafted rows, options `approved as drafted` (recommended), `changes: …`. Steamworks entry: part 5.
   - `modding/README.md` "Achievements…" line: "bundle achievements (our regional and topic bundles)"; `rg "regional bundles" ` over achievement wording.
6. **Docs**: `plans/22-bundles.md` (icon field, picker grouping, theme kind in the game), `plans/09-jokers.md` (category joker grouping), `plans/10-visual-design.md` if it lists icons, `directory.md` if a new file; `rg` for old wording (decision 200).

## Out of scope
- Rows, taxonomies, pools, translations (parts 1–3); Steamworks DLC, depots, store, achievement entries (part 5); play-test (part 6).
- Moving base questions; topic bundles in the demo (decision 339); new mod `kind` names.

## Done when
- With the five rows: each topic tile shows its own icon and «2000+», in the non-regional group; a mod theme bundle without or with an unknown `icon` shows the puzzle; the category joker groups categories by bundle and fits at 1280×720; topic questions show their bundle icon on the splash; a session with only a topic bundle on starts or refuses cleanly; gallery review decision answered; achievements per decision 368.', 'Five new optional question sets are coming: science and engineering, sports, history, movies and geography. This work makes them look and play right in the game: each gets its own picture on the selection screen instead of a generic pin, the sets sit in a sensible order with their question counts, and a family can play with only one of them switched on. When several sets are on, the joker that lets players choose a new topic groups the topics by set, so two similar sports topics aren''t mistaken for duplicates; and it settles whether each new set earns its own Steam achievement.', '2026-10-21T20:23:08Z', 1618);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (186, 19, 'The five topic bundles: rows and taxonomies', 600, 'Part 2 of `plan 155: masterplan` (milestone 19: topic question bundles): the five `kind: theme` rows `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography` in `app/data/bundles.json`, their targets, and per bundle a taxonomy the developer approved, applied. No questions here (part 3''s runs). Every task needs part 1, `plan 184: Pipeline for topic bundles`, where it says so.

## Builds on (binding)
- `plan 155: masterplan` "Builds on", above all `plans/22-bundles.md`: every question in exactly one bundle; bundles add, base keeps its sports, film, history, science and geography questions and keeps drafting them.
- `decision 18: Which new base subcategories?`: fan-level detail (clubs, legendary players) is too specific for base, the room the topic bundles fill.
- `decision 350: Overlap rate in drafting: which changes?`: topic bundles never re-ask base; plan 184 task 4 feeds base''s related subcategories into concept lists and avoid lists via `base-related.json`.
- `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` item 2: "question bundle", never «Temas».
- `decision 261: Name of the base bundle per UI language (not «Basics»)`: names per UI language, from each `locales/style/<locale>.md` glossary.
- `decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings`: target 2000 each.
- `decision 236: English-first drafting for base: what drives drafting and which locales steer it`, `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`: theme sources in `en`, translated to es, es-ES, de.
- `decision 287: usa taxonomy: categories and subcategories` (and 294, 298, 300, 304): the taxonomy decision pattern (rule, voice, proposal with slugs and en names, counts, proposal file in `work/taxonomy/<id>/`); one task proposes, waits, applies, records consequences.
- `decision 367: Topic bundle icons: an optional icon field in bundles.json, pin as fallback`: the `icon` field is part 4''s (the game); rows here leave it out unless part 4''s task has landed, then they get the icons that task lists.
- Plan 184: task 1 (`qgen taxonomy` for themes, `base-related.json`, its prompt decision), task 2 (`qgen bundle new --kind theme` writes the 2000 target, `languages: ["en"]`), task 4 (cross-bundle overlap), task 7 (media axes for `movies`: adds its own follow-up task to this plan to write `authoring/data/bundles/movies/question-axes.json`; don''t duplicate it).
- D-36 / AGENTS.md "Making questions": `qgen taxonomy` and `--apply` are setup commands, not pipeline steps; no `qgen batch` here.

## Rules: off base''s ground and off each other''s
- Membership (every rule, English, one sentence plus exclusions, like the regional rows): the bundle takes more and deeper questions on its topic at every difficulty, from kids to adults, still answerable by families anywhere in the world whatever their language; fan-level detail allowed (decision 18); the famous core of the topic (what base already asks) stays in `base`.
- No voice field: base''s voice holds (theme es text gets base''s voice, plan 184).
- Boundaries between the five, one question one bundle, by what the question tests:
  - history of science, inventions, space race → `stem`; of a sport, Olympics, World Cups → `sports`; of film → `movies`; historical borders, empires, old place names → `history`; present-day places, maps, flags, capitals, landforms, climate zones → `geography`; geology, weather physics, ecology → `stem`.
  - `movies`: scope film only or film plus TV series: a sub-question of the rows decision (recommend film only; animated films included; TV stays base''s), so its rule says it.
  - Things only one country''s players know stay in that country''s regional bundle (`usa`, `spain`, …), not here.
- `languages`: `["en"]` from `qgen bundle new` (plan 184 task 2); es, es-ES, de join one by one when part 3''s translation runs export that locale''s pool (`bundle_problems` warns while a listed locale has no pool); part 3''s plan owns that step.

## Tasks
Work tree `questions`, in this order.

1. **Rows decision for the five topic bundles**
   - Read `locales/style/{es,es-ES,en,de}.md`, `app/data/bundles.json`, `names.{en,de}.json`, `plans/22-bundles.md`, base''s `categories.json` (its subcategories on the five topics, with approved counts from `qgen report`).
   - `pm decision add "Topic bundles: names, descriptions and rules"`: a table per bundle: Spanish `name` and `description` (es; es-ES override only where the glossary differs), en and de names (and descriptions where the game shows them per UI language), English `rule` with the boundaries above, `movies` scope (film only / film + TV); names in the "question bundle" term family of decision 50, no «Temas», no clash with base''s own category names on the same topic where the style guide offers an alternative (part 4 handles «Cambiazo» display); recommended option first, "your own wording" last.
   - Task pending on it; on the answer: record consequences and finish (rows are written by task 2).
2. **Create the five bundles** (after task 1''s answer and plan 184 task 2)
   - `qgen bundle new <id> --kind theme --name … --description … --rule …` per bundle in the order `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography`; check each `targets.json` entry (2000, base''s difficulty mix scaled) and `languages: ["en"]`.
   - en/de names (and descriptions) into `app/data/names.en.json`, `names.de.json` (es-ES override where task 1 has one), the way the regional rows have them.
   - `plans/22-bundles.md` "The first bundles": a row per bundle (id, `theme`, names, rule, `languages`, target; taxonomy cell filled by tasks 3–7).
   - `qgen validate` clean (missing pools are warnings), `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`.
3. **stem taxonomy** (after task 2 and plan 184 tasks 1 and 4: theme taxonomy applied, overlap wired)
   - `qgen taxonomy --bundle stem` → proposal in `work/taxonomy/stem/`; ≈ 50 subcategories at ≈ 40 approved each (2000); each subcategory''s `base_related` slugs.
   - Check before raising: no subcategory that re-asks a base subcategory at the same depth (decision 350); none on another topic bundle''s ground per the boundaries above (against the taxonomies already applied); kids-level subcategories present at every difficulty; slugs unique, en names plain. Rerun or trim by hand in the proposal, as the regional tasks did.
   - `pm decision add "stem taxonomy: categories and subcategories"` in the decision 287 pattern: rule, target, counts, the list (category slug, en name, count, origin; subcategory slug, en name, `base_related`), path of the full proposal; options apply / apply with changes / redo.
   - Pending on it; then `qgen taxonomy --bundle stem --apply` (es/de names drafted on apply), `base-related.json` written, `qgen validate`, `plans/22-bundles.md` taxonomy cell, `pm decision consequences`.
4. **sports taxonomy**: as task 3 for `sports`; football clubs, leagues, legendary players by sport (decision 18) belong here; boundaries against `stem`''s applied list.
5. **history taxonomy**: as task 3 for `history`; periods and regions of the world in balance, not Europe-only; against `stem`, `sports`.
6. **movies taxonomy**: as task 3 for `movies`, scope per task 1; genres, eras, film countries beyond Hollywood, animation, awards, people; the proposal says which subcategories have free media (people, places, objects; plan 184 task 7) and which are text-only; against the three before.
7. **geography taxonomy**: as task 3 for `geography`; continents, landforms, waters, cities, flags and maps beyond base''s capitals; against all four before.

## Hands over to
- Part 3 (content runs): bundles with an applied taxonomy are ready for `qgen batch --bundle <id>`; adding es, es-ES, de to `languages` as pools come.
- Part 4 (in the game): `icon` per row (decision 367), «Cambiazo» with base''s and a topic bundle''s similar categories.
- Part 5 (Steam): store names start from task 1''s names.

## Out of scope
- Moving base questions into topic bundles; base''s taxonomy; prompts (plan 184); content runs, game, Steam.', 'The game is getting five optional question packs, each on one topic: science and maths, sports, history, movies and geography. Before any questions are written, each pack needs its name in every language, a rule saying which questions belong to it and not to the main pack or to another of the five, and a list of about fifty subtopics, so its 2000 questions spread evenly. This work settles those with the developer, one pack at a time, and sets the packs up for writing.', '2026-10-21T20:24:24Z', 1616);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (187, 19, 'Steam DLC and store for the topic bundles', 280, 'Part 5 of `plan 155: masterplan` (milestone 19): Steam side of the five topic bundles (`stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography`, `kind: theme`): a free DLC app, depot, store page, capsules, content survey and (per decision 368) achievement each. Extends the generic per-bundle steps the regional bundles already use; only what is specific to the five. Docs, pm and `steam.json`; workers never log into Steamworks, the developer enters every value and reports through checklist decisions.

## Builds on (binding)
- `decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): how is the game sold on Steam?`: every non-base bundle a free DLC, own store entry, optional install, never paid.
- `decision 112: Pack layout: a pool file per bundle (optional install)`: `app/data/bundles/<id>/pool[.<locale>].json`, missing = not offered; one DLC depot per bundle.
- `decision 84: SteamCMD source and depot split for Steam uploads`: base depots `windows`, `linux`, `content`; DLC depots beside them, `SetLive` beta only.
- `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` item 3: a bundle''s in-game name everywhere, Steam DLC included; term "question bundle".
- `decision 77: Store capsule art`: typographic, rendered by `authoring/store/capsules.mjs`, no image generation.
- `decision 73: Achievement list (SW-11)?` / `decision 146: Achievements, mods screen and rich presence with mods on`: `BUNDLE_<ID>` entered with its DLC; `decision 368: Achievements for the topic bundles: one per bundle like the regional ones?` (pending) decides whether the five get one (`plan 185: Topic bundles in the game` task 5 makes ids, icons, texts).
- `decision 339: Demo bundle format: an id list of base questions, exported to app/data/demo/ pools, questions stay in base` / `decision 342: Demo packaging: own staging folders, three depots, own reports, no nix output`: no topic DLC for the demo app.
- Launch doesn''t wait (masterplan): a topic DLC ships when its bundle has a pool, at a beta, the release or a content patch (`plan 96: Content updates as patches (ST-5)`).

## Generic steps reused (point to them, don''t copy)
- `plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)`: `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)", blocks "Installation → Depots" and "DLC"; regional pattern `task 1415: DLC app for regional bundle usa` (row + `steam.json` `dlc` entry with `null` IDs).
- `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`: `task 748: DLC depots for packs (decision 66)` made depots generic (`trivia-steam stage` stages `build/dlc/<id>/` from `steam.json` `dlc` + `build/pack-media.json`; smoke with and without packs); no per-bundle depot task (the regional ones, e.g. `task 1416: DLC depot for regional bundle usa`, were dropped for that reason). `app/desktop/media-budget.json` `default_dlc` covers a bundle without its own row.
- `plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)`: `plans/17a-store-page.md` "Free DLC" (fields, limits, "After approval"), pattern `task 783: Free DLC store texts in 17a` / `task 1417: Store text and capsules for DLC usa`; entry via `task 672: Store page entry checklist and PUB-8 close-out`.
- `plan 131: Content survey, rating and price (PUB-9, PUB-11)`: 17a "Content survey" → "DLC (`colombia`)" and "Content survey and pricing: entry" → `colombia` DLC blocks.
- Achievements: plan 18 "Achievements in Steamworks", `app/desktop/steam-achievements.vdf`, `DLC_BUNDLES` in `app/client/src/engine/achievements.ts`.

## Specific to the five
- **Languages:** all four launch question locales (es, es-ES, en, de); en usually first (theme bundles draft in `en`, `translations.draft_locale()`). Store text per language entered only once that locale''s pool of the bundle ships (colombia''s en rule); es-ES block only where it differs from es (base''s rule in 17a).
- **Names:** from plan 186''s rows decision and `app/data/names.<locale>.json` `bundles.<id>` (no «Regional:» prefix); the DLC store name = the in-game name.
- **Stage coupling:** `trivia-steam stage` requires a `steam.json` `dlc` entry for every bundle folder in the build (`stage_dlc`), and a real upload needs every DLC depot ID: a topic bundle folder that lands in `app/data/bundles/` (plan 186''s `qgen bundle new` / taxonomy `--apply`) breaks `stage` until its entry exists; task 1 must follow part 2''s rows promptly.
- **Content survey:** `history` (wars, violence, historical atrocities) and `movies` (film plots: violence, horror, adult themes) may need different answers than base; checked on the pool at ship time.
- **Media:** `movies` and `sports` carry few free pictures (part 1''s media proposal): DLC depots small, `default_dlc` budget enough; no store screenshots for DLC (optional per Valve).

## Tasks
1. **Steamworks rows and `steam.json` entries for the five topic DLCs** (after `plan 186: The five topic bundles: rows and taxonomies` task 2 "Create the five bundles"; if the rows aren''t in `app/data/bundles.json` yet, `pm task-pending-decision` on plan 186''s rows decision "Topic bundles: names, descriptions and rules" and stop)
   - `plans/18-steam-integration.md` SW-7 checklist: "Installation → Depots" a row per topic bundle (OS all, language all, tied to its DLC app; only if `app/data/bundles/<id>/` ships at upload time), "DLC" a row each with the names per language (en, es/es-ES, de from `names.<locale>.json`), `languages` as in `bundles.json`; the "Depot … linked" row lists them; IDs reported through task 6''s decision, not decision 179 (topic DLCs may come after it).
   - `authoring/steam/steam.json` `dlc`: `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography` with `null` IDs (row order).
   - Check: `trivia-desktop-build --dir` + `trivia-steam stage` pass with the five folders; `trivia-steam upload --dry-run` renders five more DLC depots with placeholder IDs. If a bundle folder without a pool, or a shipped bundle whose DLC isn''t entered yet, blocks a real upload (null IDs), that is generic: follow-up task in `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)` (e.g. leave unentered bundles out of the build), not a fix here.
2. **Store texts for the five topic DLCs** (after task 1; style guides `locales/style/<locale>.md` first)
   - `plans/17a-store-page.md` "Free DLC": one block per bundle (`### \`stem\` (<en name>)` …): name, short description (≤ 300), "About This Content" in en, es, de, es-ES where it differs; per 17a''s fields: free, needs the base game, optional install, off by default (switched on in the question bundle step), plays alone or with the base questions, grows with updates, its achievement only if decision 368 says yes; no question count; content facts from the bundle''s `rule`, `description` and `categories.json`; never claims the bundle owns its topic (base keeps its own sport, film, history, science, geography questions, `plans/22-bundles.md`).
   - Each language block marked "enter once `pool.<locale>.json` of the bundle ships".
   - 17a intro line of "Free DLC" mentions the topic bundles; "After approval" lines for the five (capsules task 3).
   - `pm decision add "DLC store texts approved? (topic bundles)"`, pattern of `decision 173: DLC store texts approved? (colombia)`; options `Approved as drafted` (recommended), `Approved with fixes (list them)`; fixes go into a follow-up task of this plan.
3. **Capsules for the five topic DLCs** (after task 2''s names)
   - `authoring/store/capsules.mjs` `dlcs()` already renders every non-base bundle from `bundles.json` `languages` + `names.<locale>.json`: render `dlc-<id>/<lang>/` for the four languages (es and es-ES share, like base); check the long names (e.g. de) fit every size; change the script only if one doesn''t fit.
   - Optional motif: plan 185''s bundle icon (decision 367) on the DLC capsules, so five DLC tiles in the Steam library differ beyond the text; render both variants for `stem`, the developer picks.
   - `pm decision add "Topic DLC capsules approved?"` listing `authoring/store/out/capsules/dlc-<id>/`; options `Approved as rendered (text only)` (recommended), `Approved with the bundle icon`, `Fixes (say which)`.
4. **Content survey and price rows for the topic DLCs** (plan 131''s DLC pattern; before task 6)
   - 17a "Content survey": a "DLC (topic bundles)" block: answers as the base minus Workshop; per bundle a scan of its approved pool at the task''s date (`history`: war, violence, genocide; `movies`: plot violence, horror, sexual content; `sports`: injuries, doping) with the borderline items named; AI line: the base''s DLC line ("Free DLC (`colombia`)" in "AI disclosure") reused, not a new text.
   - 17a "Content survey and pricing: entry": a block per topic DLC app (its own survey if Steamworks has one; free, no price rows), like the `colombia` blocks.
   - A borderline that changes an answer (a descriptor) → `pm decision add "Topic DLC content survey: <bundle> descriptors?"`, else no decision (the answers follow decision 181''s approved base answers).
   - Re-scan is part of task 6''s checklist for a bundle that ships later than this task.
5. **Topic bundle achievements in Steamworks** (pending on decision 368; drop with the decision cited if "No")
   - Plan 18 "Achievements in Steamworks": `BUNDLE_STEM`, `BUNDLE_SPORTS`, `BUNDLE_HISTORY`, `BUNDLE_MOVIES`, `BUNDLE_GEOGRAPHY` rows "with its DLC", like `BUNDLE_COLOMBIA`; texts and icons from plan 185 task 5 (waits for it); `steam-achievements.vdf` tokens in the same order rule.
   - No code here: `DLC_BUNDLES` gets an id only in task 7, once entered.
6. **Topic DLCs entered in Steamworks? (checklist decision)** (after tasks 1–5; raised when at least one topic bundle has a pool for the next upload)
   - `did=$(pm decision add "Topic bundle DLCs entered in Steamworks? IDs?" …)`, body per bundle that ships: DLC app (plan 18 DLC row, free, optional), depot linked, store page per 17a (approved languages with a pool only), capsules (task 3''s answer), content survey (task 4''s block), achievement `BUNDLE_<ID>` + icons + VDF re-upload (if task 5 ran), published; report DLC app ID + depot ID per bundle; bundles without a pool: "not yet".
   - Options: `entered: <id> app … depot …, …` (recommended), `not yet`, `issues (rows)`.
   - `pm task-pending-decision <task 7> $did`.
7. **Record the topic DLC IDs** (pending on task 6''s decision)
   - `steam.json` IDs of the entered bundles; `DLC_BUNDLES` + the entered `BUNDLE_<ID>`s (if task 5 ran); SW-7 rows `[x]` for them; 17a entry rows ticked; `pm decision consequences`.
   - Bundles not yet entered: a new decision like task 6''s for them and a new record task pending on it (repeat until all five).
   - Check: `npm run check`, `trivia-steam upload --dry-run` with the real IDs.

## Out of scope
- Rows, taxonomies, pools, translations (parts 1–3); icons, achievement ids/texts/icons in the game (`plan 185: Topic bundles in the game`); play-test and docs close-out (part 6).
- Generic depot, stage, upload, store-page and survey mechanics (plans 89, 88, 131, 130): only follow-ups there if the five expose a gap.
- Store screenshots or trailers for the DLCs; the demo app (`plan 178: Steamworks demo app and store`).

## Done when
- Each topic bundle with a pool has a free, optional DLC app with its depot, approved store texts per shipped language, approved capsules, a content survey and (per decision 368) its achievement, entered by the developer; IDs in `steam.json`; `trivia-steam upload --dry-run` renders its depot; bundles without a pool wait in a "not yet" decision.', 'Each of the five coming question sets (science and engineering, sports, history, movies, geography) is offered on Steam as its own free add-on that families can install if they want it. This work prepares everything Steam needs for each add-on: its entry and download package, its store page texts in Spanish, English and German, its store pictures, the age-rating questionnaire and, if decided, its achievement. The developer enters these values in Steam''s back office; the prepared checklists make sure nothing is forgotten and each add-on can go live as soon as its questions are ready.', '2026-10-21T20:25:32Z', 1619);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (188, 19, 'Content runs for the topic bundles', -120, 'Part 3 of `plan 155: masterplan` (milestone 19: topic question bundles): the recurring `qgen` runs that fill `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography` to 2000 approved per question locale (`en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`). English drafting pairs (`run batch-<n>` + `QC batch-<n>`) per bundle, translation runs `tr-<L>-<n>` with `--bundle <id>` into es, es-ES, de, in the pattern of `plan 84: Release content runs` (chains 4, 5). Priority −120: below plan 84''s chains (−110) and plan 17''s base batches (−100), so base and regional runs go first unless the pace decision says otherwise. Owners: `plans/22-bundles.md` ("The first bundles": progress per bundle and locale), `plans/16-content-target.md` (cost).

## Builds on (binding)
- `plan 155: masterplan` "Builds on": bundles add, base keeps its same-topic questions (`plans/22-bundles.md`); `decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings` (2000 per non-base bundle); `decision 339: Demo bundle format: an id list of base questions, exported to app/data/demo/ pools, questions stay in base` (no topic bundle in the demo); launch (milestone 11) doesn''t wait: what''s ready ships, the rest in content patches (`plan 96: Content updates as patches (ST-5)`; what ships is part 6''s).
- D-36 / AGENTS.md "Making questions": workers run only `qgen batch --bundle <id>` and `qgen batch --translate <L> --bundle <id>` (RUNBOOK unchanged); no prompt, pool, media or `qgen.py` changes in a run or QC task. Only exception: a locale joins a bundle''s `languages` row (below), owned by this plan (`plan 186: The five topic bundles: rows and taxonomies` "Hands over to").
- `decision 236: English-first drafting for base: what drives drafting and which locales steer it` / `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`: theme sources in `en`; a locale''s count = sources + playing translations; English drafting aims at the largest locale gap (plan 184 task 3).
- `decision 350: Overlap rate in drafting: which changes?`: topic bundles never re-ask base (plan 184 task 4, `base-related.json`).
- Plan 84 rules, unchanged here: decision 2 / D-56 / decision 15 (30-question blind spot check, ≥ 90 % agreement; below it only feeds QC step 4); decision 3 (`qgen rework` once after each drafting QC); `decision 221: How does an outside native reviewer reach the review tool?` (offline sheet when the reviewer isn''t the developer); translation runs: no spot check, no QC task, no `qgen health ack` unless decision 45''s thresholds stop a run (exit 2); cost is information only (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15): notes carry `qgen report --cost`, no budget gates.
- Needs before the first start: `plan 184: Pipeline for topic bundles` (theme targets, per-locale gap aiming, cross-bundle overlap, `--cost` theme rows, end-to-end check: `task 1626`–`task 1630`); per bundle, plan 186''s taxonomy task for it applied (`stem taxonomy` … `geography taxonomy`; subjects may change, `pm show p186`).
- `movies` media: plan 184 task 7 (`task 1631: Media for movies and sports: axes template and docs`): a health stop for media share under 15 % in a `movies` batch is exit 2 → the "Continue …?" decision names that plan''s per-bundle-minimum vs. more-`photo` question.

## Task shapes
- **Drafting pair** per bundle: `run batch-<n> (<id>)`: `nix develop -c qgen batch --bundle <id>` (RUNBOOK steps 1–5; English); after the run rename both tasks to the real batch name `qgen` printed (shared counter with plans 17 and 84). `QC batch-<n> (<id>)`: `authoring/QC.md` steps 1–4: `pm decision add "Spot check batch-<n> (<id>) done?"` (native English speaker: the developer, or an outside reviewer via `qgen spotcheck export`; never an LLM), `qgen report --qc batch-<n>`, `pm decision add "QC batch-<n> (<id>): which changes?"`, change tasks (theme pipeline findings in plan 184 while it has open tasks, else a new plan in milestone 19; the rest in plan 17 at 650 like base''s QC); decision 3''s `qgen rework` once; note QC numbers and `qgen report --cost` (per bundle).
- **Translation run** per bundle and locale (es, es-ES, de): `run tr-<L>-<n> (<id>)`: `nix develop -c qgen batch --translate <L> --bundle <id>`; rename to the real run name; note the "Done:" line, report path and the numbers of `authoring/reports/<run>.md` and `qgen report --cost` (selected, translated, approved, needs_work, rejected, not travelling, $ per approved translation, audit agreement). needs_work: nothing (picked again by the next run).
- One open pair per bundle, one open translation run per bundle and locale.
- Every body repeats the pm-run rules (below) and names its bundle and run.

## Chain per bundle
1. **Start task** `Topic runs <id>: start` (−120): checks the prerequisites above and the pace decision''s answer; any missing → `pm task-pending-decision` on the decision blocking it (the bundle''s taxonomy decision, plan 184''s or 186''s earliest open decision), stop. Then adds the first drafting pair.
2. **Each drafting QC**, after its own steps, first that applies:
   - Translations: per L in es, es-ES, de with no open `run tr-<L>-<n> (<id>)` and ≥ 50 approved en sources of the bundle not yet translated into L → adds that run.
   - `qgen report --bundle <id>` supply block shows no English draft gap left (every locale''s deficit covered by sources and untranslated sources at yield) → no next pair: notes drafting done in `plans/22-bundles.md`; under a staggered pace (below), re-adds the next bundle''s start task.
   - The pace decision''s numbers look far off (the developer''s review time or $ per approved well above its projection) → `pm decision add` asking the developer instead of the next pair.
   - Else the next pair (same bodies, next batch number).
3. **Each translation run**, after the run:
   - The run''s export wrote `app/data/bundles/<id>/pool.<L>.json` and `<L>` isn''t in the bundle''s `languages` (`app/data/bundles.json`) → add it (row edit only), `qgen validate` clean (`bundle_problems`), stage the file.
   - `qgen report --bundle <id> --locale <L>` at 2000 (every level at the bundle''s `targets.json`) → no next run; `plans/22-bundles.md` progress line; if all four locales are at 2000: the bundle is done there.
   - Else, ≥ 50 approved en sources not yet in L left → adds `run tr-<L>-<n+1> (<id>)`; fewer → nothing (the next drafting QC re-adds it).
   - Each run adds a progress line (approved per locale) for the bundle in `plans/22-bundles.md`.

## Tasks (for the split)
1. **Pace and order of the topic bundles: decision** (−120)
   - Needs `task 1629: qgen report --cost: rows per theme bundle and locale` done; else pend on the decision blocking it, stop.
   - `pm decision add "Topic bundles: pace and order of the content runs"` (intro for an outsider): `qgen report --cost` projections for 5 × 2000 × 4 locales (en drafting, es/es-ES/de translation; theme rows, else base''s rates), expected drafting pairs and spot checks per bundle (2000 / approved per English base batch, batches 9–11), the developer''s review time per 100 (`plans/15c-regional-questions.md`, colombia''s QC), against what''s still open: base (`qgen report --exit-check`, plan 17) and plan 84''s regional and translation chains.
   - Options (recommended first, numbers decide the recommendation): (1) one topic bundle at a time below base and regional runs (−120), order `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `geography`, `movies` (movies last for its low media share), the next starts when the previous one''s drafting ends, its translations keep running; (2) all five at once, one pair each, −120; (3) two at a time; (4) none until base''s exit check and plan 84''s regional chains are done; your own pace or order.
   - Pending on it; on the answer: record consequences; for a staggered answer, drop the start tasks that don''t start yet (note: "re-added by the closing drafting QC of <previous bundle>"), set start-task priorities if the answer moves them (`pm task set`); finish.
2. **Topic runs `stem`: start** (−120)
3. **Topic runs `sports`: start** (−120)
4. **Topic runs `history`: start** (−120)
5. **Topic runs `movies`: start** (−120)
6. **Topic runs `geography`: start** (−120)
- Start tasks 2–6: body per "Chain per bundle" step 1, with the full pair bodies and pm-run rules to copy; each `pm task-pending-decision` on task 1''s decision once it exists (the split adds task 1 first; a start task that runs before the decision exists pends on it the moment task 1 raises it: task 1 links every start task to its decision).
- Later pairs, translation runs and re-added start tasks are added by the run and QC tasks, not the split.

## pm-run rules (repeat in every body; plan 84, plan 17 "Batch tasks under pm run")
- D-36: no prompt, pool, media or `qgen.py` changes; findings become decisions or tasks in their own plans (184 or new).
- `tasks.sql` alone isn''t a dirty tree. Stage exactly the `git add` paths the command prints (plus `app/data/bundles.json` after a `languages` edit); don''t commit (pm commits as "task N: …").
- Exit 75, exit 2 (a health stop: the decision asks the developer for `qgen health ack`), any other non-zero code, or exit 1 three times at one step → `pm decision add "Continue <run> (<id>)…?"` with the last 30 lines of output in the body, `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <id>`, stage nothing, stop.
- Note on done: the "Done:" line and report path (run tasks), or the QC numbers (approved, rejected, needs_work, agreement, $ per approved, review time per 100).

## Done when
- Each of the five at 2000 approved in `en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de` (`qgen report --bundle <id> --locale <L>`), its `languages` listing all four, progress and cost in `plans/22-bundles.md` and `plans/16-content-target.md`; may land after launch, in content patches.

## Out of scope
- Rows, taxonomies, `question-axes.json` (plan 186); pipeline and prompt changes (plan 184 or new plans); game, Steam DLC and store (parts 4, 5); what ships when, play-test (part 6); base and regional runs (plans 17, 84).', 'The five new optional question packs (science and maths, sports, history, movies, geography) each need 2000 checked questions in English, Latin American Spanish, Spain''s Spanish and German. This is the steady stream of writing runs that fills them: English questions written in batches and spot-checked by a person, then machine-translated into the other three languages. Because it competes with the main pack and the country packs for the same machine time and the developer''s review time, the developer first chooses how fast and in what order the five packs are filled.', '2026-10-21T20:27:06Z', 1617);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (189, 19, 'Topic bundles close-out', 100, 'Part 6 of `plan 155: masterplan`, last: proves `milestone 19: topic question bundles` and closes it. Settles which topic bundles ship in which language at the release or a content patch, has the developer play each shipped topic bundle with the family through one checklist decision per wave, and sweeps the docs so every one names the topic bundles and says "non-base bundle" where it means any optional bundle. Work tree `app`. Workers never play the game for the developer or answer its decisions.

## Builds on (don''t rebuild)
- `plan 184: Pipeline for topic bundles` (theme taxonomy, targets, per-locale counts, cross-bundle overlap, media for `movies`), `plan 186: The five topic bundles: rows and taxonomies` (rows `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography`, names, rules, taxonomies), `plan 188: Content runs for the topic bundles`, `plan 185: Topic bundles in the game` (icons, order, counts, base-off session, category joker grouped by bundle, splash icon, gallery review, achievements per decision 368), `plan 187: Steam DLC and store for the topic bundles` (DLC apps, depots, store texts, capsules, survey)
- `decision 112: Pack layout: a pool file per bundle (optional install)`: missing `app/data/bundles/<id>/pool[.<locale>].json` = not offered in that locale
- `decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings`: our shipped non-base bundles show «2000+»; "the release bar, not the tile, makes them true"
- `decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): how is the game sold on Steam?`: free DLC, optional install; `decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)`: launch doesn''t wait for a bundle, content patches bring the rest
- `plan 96: Content updates as patches (ST-5)`: `plans/11-steam.md` "Content updates (ST-5)" (patch path, `qgen patch-notes`, cadence `decision 96: Content patch cadence after launch?`); a topic bundle that reaches the bar after launch rides that path
- `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` / `decision 155: Play-test of age groups and bundles (again, after the decision 50 fixes)`: the play-test pattern and its "again" round; term "question bundle"
- `decision 339: Demo bundle format: an id list of base questions, exported to app/data/demo/ pools, questions stay in base`: no topic bundle in the demo
- Model: `plan 167: Local multiplayer close-out and family playtest`, `plan 179: Close-out: play the demo` (one `--once` playtest decision, routing, "again" round, docs sweep)
- Decision 200 (`rg` old wording, fix every hit in the same commit); AGENTS.md: the developer''s review and hand edits in `../trivia-review`, `qgen flag` for reported questions

## Decisions taken here
- One play-test decision (`--once`) per shipping wave (the topic bundles at the bar at that time), rows ✓/✗ + note, not one per bundle
- `failed` routing: rule, names, boundaries between the five, taxonomy (a subcategory that re-asks base or another topic bundle) → plan 186; overlap with base in drafting, translation quality per locale, media share or licences → plan 184; too few questions for an age group, a locale lagging → plan 188; a wrong or bad single question → the developer flags it (`qgen flag`, review in `../trivia-review`), no task; tile, icon, order, count, base-off session, category joker, splash, achievements, PLACEHOLDER, text fit → plan 185; DLC install, store, Steam library, depot → plan 187; once that plan is done: a new plan in milestone 19 (`pm plan add 19 …`) named after the failure

## Tasks to split into
1. **What ships: topic bundles per release and content patch**
   - Wait: plan 186''s rows in `app/data/bundles.json` and at least one topic bundle with an exported pool in one locale; else stop without closing and say which
   - Facts: per bundle × question locale (es, es-ES, en, de) approved count (`qgen report --bundle <id>`), pool file present, `languages` in its row, DLC entered (plan 187''s checklist decision answered or not), newest `v*` tag
   - `pm decision add "Topic bundles below 2000 approved: ship or hold?"` (decision 267 promises «2000+»; decision 110 shipped `colombia` with what it had, before 267): options (1, recommended) a bundle × locale ships only from 2000 approved in that locale, below it its pool stays out of the build (how: the build or `stage` leaves the file out, not `qgen export`; follow-up task in `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)` if no switch exists); (2) ship from a floor (developer names it, e.g. 500) with the tile showing the real rounded count for ours below 2000 (follow-up in plan 185, decision 267 superseded in part); (3) ship whatever exists with «2000+»; body: the facts table, what a player sees per option, that regional bundles follow the same answer unless the developer says otherwise. `pm task-pending-decision` and stop
   - On the answer: `plans/22-bundles.md` a "Shipping non-base bundles" bullet list (the rule, release vs. patch, per locale); `plans/11-steam.md` "Content updates (ST-5)": one bullet "a non-base bundle × locale reaching the bar: its pool, its `languages` entry, its DLC store language block (plan 187) in the next content patch; the patch notes count it"; `plans/16-content-target.md` topic bundles line (2000 per locale, shipping rule); `pm decision consequences`
   - Ship table in this task''s done text: per bundle × locale "release v<x>", "patch (when at bar)" or "not offered"
2. **The developer plays the shipped topic bundles with the family** (after 1; plan 185''s tasks 1–4 done, else stop without closing and say which)
   - Wave = the topic bundles at the bar of task 1''s answer at this time; none yet → stop without closing, say so
   - `pm decision add --once "Topic bundles: each played with the family?"`, body written against what was built (`rg` names, keys, commands):
     - setup: the `beta` build under Steam with the topic DLCs installed if plan 187 entered them and a build is uploaded, else `trivia-desktop` with `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`; answer says which
     - rows per bundle of the wave: alone (base off), first locale with a pool (usually en), one age group; with base, another age group (kids at least once across the wave); per further locale with a pool of any wave bundle: one session base + every wave bundle with a pool there (es, es-ES, de as they come)
     - checks in each row: tile icon, name and «2000+» (or task 1''s count rule); the category joker grouped by bundle, no category reads as a duplicate of base''s; splash shows the bundle icon; questions go beyond base''s (fan level allowed, decision 18) and never feel re-asked from base or from another topic bundle; difficulty fits the age group; `movies` and `sports` with few pictures still play well; overlay line and no running-out notice; achievements as decision 368 answered; text fits on the TV
     - answer: date, build, ✓/✗ per row + note; "passed" (recommended) | "failed (list: bundle, locale, screen or question id, what happened)"
   - `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <decision>` and stop; after the answer: ✗ → follow-ups per routing, plus one task in this plan "Topic bundles family playtest again" raising a decision of the same shape once those are done (as decision 155 followed decision 50); ✓ → `pm decision consequences`
   - Bundles not in the wave: one task in this plan per later wave, "Topic bundles family playtest: <ids>", same shape, waits for those bundles at the bar (else stops without closing)
3. **Close-out: docs sweep and milestone 19 Done** (after 2 passed, or its "again" passed; later waves don''t hold it, they keep their own tasks)
   - `plans/22-bundles.md` "The first bundles": a row per topic bundle complete and true (id, `theme`, names per UI language, rule, `languages`, target 2000, icon, taxonomy decision, ship status per task 1: "shipped v<x>: en, …" / "content patch")
   - `README.md` (line "Age groups and bundles": "base and regional" → base, regional and topic bundles; `qgen bundle new` / `qgen taxonomy` lines name themes if plan 184 didn''t), `directory.md` and `AGENTS.md` where they list bundles or kinds
   - `rg -i "regional bundle|regional pack|regional ones"` over `plans/`, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `directory.md`, `modding/`, `authoring/*.md`, code comments and `about` texts of `app/data/*.json` (decision 200): a hit meaning any optional bundle → "non-base bundle"; a hit about the region kind stays; identifiers, catalog strings and `authoring/tools/prompts/` untouched (prompt wording goes through `decision 262: Taxonomy prompts on slug keys: apply?`''s verbatim-draft pattern: one follow-up task in plan 184, work tree `questions`, listing the hits)
   - `plans/project.md`: `[x] Topic bundles: stem, sports, history, movies, geography (<date>, pm milestone 19, plans 155, 184–189; decisions …)` with the real ids at that time
   - Milestone 19 text checked against the ship table and the playtest: five bundles created; a bundle still below the bar is listed as "ships in a content patch", not a gap; another gap → follow-up task; `pm decision consequences` where the built result differs from a decision; per-commit checks

## Out of scope
- Building anything parts 1–5 own; moving base questions; topic bundles in the demo; more than five topic bundles; milestone 12''s locales

## Done when
- Task 1''s ship decision answered and written into `plans/22-bundles.md`, `plans/11-steam.md`, `plans/16-content-target.md`
- The developer''s playtest decision for the first wave answered «passed» (after any "again" round); later waves have their own tasks
- `rg` finds no "regional bundle" meaning any non-base bundle in docs or comments; `plans/22-bundles.md` lists the five; `plans/project.md` marks milestone 19 done', 'Five new optional question sets, on science, sports, history, movies and geography, are only finished once families have actually played them and everyone knows which of them are ready to ship. This last step decides when a set is ready, at the game''s release or in a later free update, so its promised question count is true in every language. Then the developer plays each ready set with the family on the TV, and anything wrong goes back to whoever built that part. Finally the project''s documents are brought up to date so they all describe the five sets as built.', '2026-10-21T20:27:45Z', 1620);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, intro, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (190, 1, 'Reviews don''t gate generation', 700, 'Implements the masterplan''s rule "Reviews don''t gate generation" (`plan 1: masterplan`, `decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`) in code and procedure docs. Partly supersedes `decision 13: Batch health thresholds and stop rule?` (D-55''s stop), decision 45''s stop (`decision 45: Health thresholds and selection order for qgen batch --translate runs`; thresholds stay) and `decision 313: Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run`. Plans 15 and 16, which built the gates, are done; this plan changes what they built.

## What gates today (2026-10-23)
- `authoring/tools/qgen.py` `cmd_batch`: `health.stop_reason()` → `sys.exit(EXIT_HEALTH)` (2) before a new run; `authoring/tools/translate.py`: `health.translate_stop_reason(locale)` → exit 2 (not with `--dry-run`). Cleared only by `qgen health ack <run> "<note>"`.
- Texts saying "a ✗ stops the next `qgen batch`": `health.py` (stop messages, report section text, `batches.md` "the stop is cleared"), `qgen.py` docstring (`health ack` line), `authoring/data/targets.json` `about`, `README.md` (`qgen health ack` line), `plans/15b-question-translation.md` (run line), `plans/decisions.md` (D-55 entry, translation stop line).
- `authoring/RUNBOOK.md`: exit-2 row, "Under `pm run`" step 3 (exit 2 → `pm task-pending-decision`, the `<run>: health stop` lookup of `task 1692: RUNBOOK: on a health stop, link to a pending ack decision instead of adding a duplicate`), subjects table row, the translation-runs line ("makes the next one exit 2").
- `authoring/QC.md`: "a pm worker stops at each decision", step 2 (spot check: `pm task-pending-decision`, stop), step 4 (proposals: "wait on it, stop"), step 5 "Next batch waits", "Translation runs" stop line.
- No tests cover the exit-2 path (none in `authoring/`).

## New behaviour
- `qgen batch` (drafting, `--bundle`, `--translate`) never exits 2 for health: a ✗ of the last done run is printed (stderr, before the run starts, same text minus "clears the stop") and stays in the report and `qgen report --batches`; the run goes on. `EXIT_HEALTH` goes.
- `qgen health ack <run> "<note>"` stays: the developer''s "looked at it" record (`authoring/data/health-acks.json`, "Acked" in `batches.md`); acked runs no longer print the warning.
- Decision name for a ✗ (lasting, this plan''s choice): "`<run>`: health ✗, look at it?", raised once per run by the run''s (or QC) task, no task linked; look it up first with `pm decision list --grep "<run>: health"` (matches the older "`<run>`: health stop, ack?" too).
- QC: spot check, QC proposals and health decisions are raised and never waited on; the next QC task acts on answered ones (plan 17 "Reviews don''t gate", plan 84 drafted-run QC already say so).
- Reports of past runs (`authoring/reports/batch-8.md` … `tr-*-1.md`) keep their old sentence as history, unless the regeneration of their health section is a plain existing command.

## Not here (refer, don''t duplicate)
- Batch task bodies and their exit-2 fallback: `plan 17: Batch runs` (revised by `task 1698: revise plan 17: Batch runs`); release and translation runs: `plan 84: Release content runs` (revised under `task 1696: revise the masterplan of milestone 9: Steam S4: content for release`). Their "exit 2 while qgen still has it" lines become dead once the first task here is done; the second task updates the open task bodies that name it.
- Pending decisions: no milestone 1 task waits on a review decision (2026-10-23). Outside milestone 1, `decision 411: Continue run batch-<n> (stem): batch-12 health stop, ack?` still blocks tasks 1676 and 1677 (milestone 19); pm has no unlink, and batch-12 is already acked (`decision 408: batch-12: health stop, ack?`), so the developer answering decision 411 frees them; no new decision.

## Tasks
1. qgen: health ✗ no longer stops `qgen batch` (code, messages, command docs).
2. RUNBOOK and QC.md without review waits (requires 1), plus open task bodies.

## Done when
- Both tasks done: no exit 2 for health in `qgen`, `rg "EXIT_HEALTH|stop_reason|health stop"` finds only history (past reports, `code-review.md`, `plans/decisions.md` entries marked superseded), RUNBOOK and QC.md have no review wait; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.', 'The tool that writes trivia questions checks each finished set against quality thresholds, and today a failed check stops the next set until the developer signs it off. The developer has decided to trust the automatic writing and translation: warnings and human checks still reach the developer, but no run waits for them any more. This work removes the stop from the tool and rewrites the written procedures so nothing waits on a human review; the only human gate left is the final release check.', '2026-10-23T01:44:52Z', 1699);

