INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (65, 18, 'Fixture recorder skeleton (PORT-1)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-11, authoring/tools/record_fixtures.py: temp state guard, shuffle tape/now/categories patches, main.py dispatch, DB snapshots, deterministic writer, --check; registries CATEGORIES/POOLS/SCENARIOS + @scenario for tasks 66–70; throw-away 3-step run deterministic, state/game.sqlite unchanged', 'New `authoring/tools/record_fixtures.py` per plan 18 ("Decisions taken here", "Safety"). Python stdlib only.

- Temp state guard: set `TRIVIA_STATE` to `tempfile.mkdtemp()` **before** importing `layout` (it imports `paths`), `game`, `selection`; assert `game.DB` and `selection.STATE_DB` lie inside it, else exit loudly.
- Fresh state per scenario: `selection.burned_ids(db=STATE_DB)` binds the path at def time, so keep one temp dir per process and delete `game.sqlite` between scenarios (not repointing constants); remove the dir at exit.
- Patches:
  - `random.shuffle` → shuffle an index list with `random.Random(seed)`, apply it in place, append `{"site", "n", "perm"}` to the current step''s tape (`perm[j]` = old index now at j; `site` = caller''s function name).
  - `game.now` → the step''s fixed `now` (`2026-01-01T00:00:00` + step index minutes).
  - `categories.load` → fixture categories (wherever `game`/`selection` reference it).
- Dispatch mirroring `main.py` `game_action` (incl. `int(...)` coercions, `event` for `joker`), `GET /api/game` (`{"game", "supply"}`), players routes, delete player. Response `{status, body}`; any 500 aborts recording.
- Step recorder: `{now, call, args, tape, response, db}`; DB snapshot as in plan 18 "Fixture layout" (state parsed, `burned` sorted by (game_id, question_id, player_id)).
- Deterministic JSON writer: `sort_keys`, `ensure_ascii=False`, one step per line.
- CLI: default writes into `app/client/src/engine/fixtures/`; `--check` re-records into a temp dir and diffs, exit 1 on difference.

Done when: a throw-away scenario of 3 steps (new, pick, answer) records with a tape and DB snapshots, and `state/game.sqlite` mtime + checksum are unchanged after the run.', '2026-10-12T00:04:11Z', '2026-10-12T01:51:28Z', 62, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (66, 18, 'Synthetic fixture categories and pools (PORT-1)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-11, authoring/tools/record_fixtures.py (CATEGORIES, make_pool, POOLS), app/client/src/engine/fixtures/{categories.json,pools/main.json,pools/tight.json}; main: 3 won games/player with jokers, 4 without; tight: exactly 48, every card needed', 'The recorder (`authoring/tools/record_fixtures.py`) generates and writes, deterministically, into `app/client/src/engine/fixtures/` (plan 18, "Fixture layout"):

- `categories.json`: 2 bundles (`base` + one more, D-43), 3 broad categories, ~6 subcategories; same shape as `categories.load()` output (with `bundle`).
- `pools/main.json`: ~90 approved questions, difficulties 1–10 across all subcategories, hints 0–3 (some with 0), all fields the referee and `game.view` read (`id`, `status`, `difficulty`, `subcategory`, `description`, `question`, `answer`, `wrong_answers`, `hints`, `media`, `background`, `fun_fact`, `bundle`).
- `pools/tight.json`: barely one game: the second game hits a supply failure; Bájale, Cambiazo, purge and snipe-hit unavailable.

Check against `selection.supply` / `assign` with a throw-away call: main supports several games per player with jokers; tight supports exactly one.

Done when: the files are written, re-running gives identical bytes, and the supply checks above hold.', '2026-10-12T00:04:11Z', '2026-10-12T01:53:00Z', 62, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (67, 18, 'Selection fixture cases (PORT-1)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-11, authoring/tools/record_fixtures.py (selection_cases), app/client/src/engine/fixtures/selection.json: 105 cases (in_range edges, assign subsets/shortages, supply main/tight/burns, draw keep/avoid/n/unfillable); --check passes', 'The recorder writes `app/client/src/engine/fixtures/selection.json` (plan 18, "Fixture layout"): direct calls into `app/server/selection.py`, each `{name, fn, args, tape, result}`.

- `in_range`: edges of each level range.
