INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (98, 22, 'Server errors as codes: server + client wiring, interim Spanish map', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-11, app/server/game.py, app/server/main.py, app/client/src/lib/{api,types,errors}.ts, Game/JokerTray/Question/Player.svelte, D-57, plans/12-client-engine.md, directory.md; 28 codes checked over HTTP, Spanish word for word; no PORT-1 fixtures yet; ErrorInfo.params is Record<string, unknown> (supply_short carries a list)', 'Part 2 of M3, task 1 of plan 22 (see the plan for the design and the full code table). Runs at 710, before PORT-1''s fixture tasks (700), so fixtures record codes.

- `app/server/game.py`:
  - `GameError(code, params=None, details=None)`; `ERRORS = {code: English template}`; `str(e)` = filled English text; assert unknown code in `__init__`.
  - Every `raise GameError` → its code from the plan''s table; re-grep and add any raise not in the table.
  - Re-raises keep their own code (`back_to_select`, `play_snipe`): `raise GameError("…") from None`.
  - `trial()` returns `{"code", "params"}` or None; `jokers_view` reasons become that object (Cambiazo literal → `category_none`, `SPENT` → `joker_spent` with `{joker}`); drop `SPENT`.
- `app/server/main.py`: `GET /api/game` (400), `game_action` (409), `/api/players/delete` (409) answer `{"error": code, "params": {...}, "message": english, "supply": details}`; 404 → `not_found`, 500 → `server_error` (English message). `/api/flags` unchanged.
- Client:
  - `lib/types.ts`: `ErrorInfo = { code: string; params: Record<string, string | number> }`, joker `reason: ErrorInfo | null`.
  - `lib/api.ts`: `GameError` with `code`, `params`, `message`; `json()`, `playJoker`, `gameAction` throw it when the body has `error`; network failures and bodies without `error` stay plain `Error`.
  - New `lib/errors.ts`: `errorText(e)`, `reasonText(info)`, interim Spanish map for player-facing codes only (texts moved verbatim; `joker_spent` per joker id; `supply_short` joins `supply_level` items with ", "). Unknown code or plain Error → its message.
  - `Game.svelte` (every `error = …`), `JokerTray.svelte` (reason), `Question.svelte` (purge reason), `Player.svelte` (delete errors, if shown).
- Docs: new D-number in `plans/decisions.md` (codes + params on the wire, English `message` for logs, client renders); `directory.md`: `lib/errors.ts`; mark the internal codes in the plan''s table if anything changed.
- PORT-1: if fixtures exist, re-run `authoring/tools/record_fixtures.py` and commit them; note in `plans/12-client-engine.md` that PORT-3 throws the same codes and parity compares `error`/`params`, not `message`.

Done when:
- Throw-away script hits every code over HTTP against a temp `TRIVIA_STATE`, prints code, params, message and the client''s Spanish text next to the old text; they match word for word. Delete the script after.
- `npm run check`, `npm run build` pass; `trivia` starts; no visible change in Spanish; no new dependencies.', '2026-10-12T00:15:00Z', '2026-10-12T01:43:42Z', 87, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (99, 22, 'Server error texts into the es catalog', 'work', 'done', 490, '2026-10-12, app/client/src/locales/es.ts (error.*), lib/errors.ts (t() via has()), lib/i18n.ts (has), plans/project.md, plans/15a-ui-translation.md, directory.md', 'Task 2 of plan 22. Priority 490: runs after plan 21''s tasks (LUI-1, 500), which create `app/client/src/lib/i18n.ts`, `locales/es.ts` and `check:literals`, and reserve the `error` namespace. If they don''t exist yet, stop and say so.

- `es.ts`: `error.<code>` keys for every player-facing code from `lib/errors.ts`, incl. `error.joker_spent.<id>` per joker and `error.supply_level`; texts verbatim.
- `lib/errors.ts`: drop the interim Spanish map; `errorText`/`reasonText` call `t()`. A code is player-facing iff its key exists in the catalog (typed lookup, no `⟦key⟧` for internal codes, which keep the English `message`).
- `check:literals` passes with `lib/errors.ts` included.
- Close-out: `plans/project.md` (M3: part 2 done); mark the plan file''s tasks done.

Done when: `npm run check`, `npm run build` and `check:literals` pass; `trivia` starts; same corner error lines and joker reasons in Spanish as before (spot-check `name_missing`, `joker_spent`, `supply_short`, a Cambiazo reason, and an internal code showing English).', '2026-10-12T00:15:00Z', '2026-10-12T06:02:37Z', 87, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (100, 23, 'pseudo-locale xx: generator and dev wiring', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, app/client/src/locales/xx.ts (new), app/client/src/lib/i18n.ts (?lang=xx via dev-only dynamic import, async initLang, html lang/numbers stay es, missing-key warn once), app/client/src/main.ts, directory.md; exempt: joker.*.key and flag.key; throw-away check: 195 leaves ok; dist has no xx/pseudo code', 'Part 1 of plan 23 (LUI-2). Precondition: `app/client/src/lib/i18n.ts`, `app/client/src/locales/es.ts` and the `?lang=` dev override from plan 21 exist. If they don''t, drop this task with a note (`pm task drop`) instead of building them here.

- `app/client/src/locales/xx.ts` (new): `pseudo(es): Catalog`, generated at runtime from `es`, no hand-written catalog.
  - Walks every leaf: plain strings, plural maps (`{ one, other, … }`), variant arrays (`copy.*`); same shape, so it satisfies `Catalog`.
  - ASCII letters → look-alikes (`a→å`, `e→é`, `o→ø`, `c→ç`, `n→ñ`, `A→Å`, …).
  - ~40 % extra length (rounded up, min. 2 chars) as `~` runs, inside `[` … `]`.
  - `{param}` placeholders stay byte-for-byte; only text outside `{…}` changes.
  - Small exempt list in `xx.ts`: single-letter joker keys (`joker.<id>.key`), left unchanged.
- `app/client/src/lib/i18n.ts`: picks `xx` only when `import.meta.env.DEV && ?lang=xx`, via dynamic `import()`. `document.documentElement.lang` stays `es` for `xx`.
- Missing keys: keep plan 21''s `⟦key⟧`; add a dev-only `console.warn` once per missing key.
- `directory.md`: add `app/client/src/locales/xx.ts`.

Verify with a throw-away script (delete it afterwards) that runs `pseudo()` over `es`: every leaf changed (except exempt), `{params}` unchanged, length ≥ 1.4× (except exempt), shape equal.

Done when: `npm run check` and `npm run build` pass; no `xx`/`pseudo` code in `app/client/dist/` (grep the build); `es` output unchanged.', '2026-10-12T00:15:27Z', '2026-10-12T21:29:54Z', 88, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (101, 23, 'pseudo-locale xx: screen walk, missed literals, overflow rows', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, app/client/src/locales/xx.ts (exempt *Key shortcuts: newKey/replayKey were pseudo''d, N did nothing under xx), plans/backlog.md (B-17, B-18), plans/15a-ui-translation.md, plans/project.md; screen walk under ?lang=xx at 1920x1080 + 1280x1024 (language, start incl. resume and save notice, player list/delete, level incl. milestones and ''again'', select incl. fresh badge, question with every joker armed/used, tray reasons, hints, final answer, correct, wrong, victory, overlay, reports, corner error): no missed literals; only content, endonyms, credits and English internal fallbacks (HTTP 500) stay plain; follow-up task 493 (missing() recursion); dev warning seen: LanguageScreen bind:this non-reactive (pre-existing)', 'Part 2 of plan 23 (LUI-2). Needs task "pseudo-locale xx: generator and dev wiring" done, and the screenshot method from plan 21 (decision 6).

- Run `npm run dev -w app/client` + `trivia`, open with `?lang=xx`, TV layout 1920 × 1080 (`theme.css`). Screens: start, player, level, select (every joker tray state incl. reasons), question (every joker armed and used, hints, final answer), result, victory, overlay, error line in the corner.
- Also one tight case: the narrowest supported window (height bound in `theme.css`).
- Screenshots: the same method plan 21 uses for its before/after comparison (decision 6); no new dependency in the flake or `package.json`.
- Expected to stay Spanish (not bugs): question/answer text, category/subcategory names, bundle names, English `message` fallbacks of internal error codes (plan 22).
- Any other plain Spanish under `xx` is a literal LUI-1 missed: move it into `es.ts` and use `t()`, list it in the task note.
- Each overflow/clipping: one row in `plans/backlog.md` (`B-n`, origin `LUI-2`, status `new`): screen, element, key, what breaks. No CSS changes, no redesign.
- Mark LUI-2 `[x]` in `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` with a note (date, backlog rows, or "no overflow found"); update M3 status in `plans/project.md`.

Done when: every screen above checked under `xx`; `npm run check` and `npm run build` pass; `es` output unchanged; screenshots and scripts not committed.', '2026-10-12T00:15:27Z', '2026-10-12T21:53:26Z', 88, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (102, 24, 'LUI-3: English joker name candidates and decisions', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, plans/15a-ui-translation.md; pm decisions 40-44, task 104 waits on them', 'Task 1 of plan 24. Needs plan 21 (LUI-1: `app/client/src/lib/i18n.ts`, `locales/es.ts`, `Catalog`/`Key` types) and plan 22 task 2 (`error.<code>` keys in `es.ts`). If they don''t exist yet, stop and say so (`pm task drop` with a note); don''t build them here.

- Per joker (`hint` «Soplo», `skip` «Paso», `easier` «Bájale», `category` «Cambiazo», `snipe` «Francotirador»): 3–5 playful English candidates, not literal translations, ≤ 13 characters (length of «Francotirador», tray width); each with a one-line reason (pun, tone, what it evokes). Recommended one first.
- One `pm decision add` per joker: subject e.g. "English name for the hint joker «Soplo»?", candidates as `--option`s (recommended first), body: Spanish name, what the joker does (from the catalog/joker code), why these candidates.
- Link the plan''s task "LUI-3: chosen joker names into en.ts" (task 3 of plan 24; id via `pm show <this task>`) to all five decisions with `pm task-pending-decision`.
- `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` under LUI-3: candidate lists as bullets (recommended first, decision id per joker).

Done when: five pending decisions exist, task 3 waits on all five, 15a lists the candidates.', '2026-10-12T00:16:05Z', '2026-10-12T21:55:14Z', 89, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (103, 24, 'LUI-3: draft en.ts catalog and ?lang=en dev override', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, app/client/src/locales/en.ts (draft, joker names = task 102''s recommended: Psst, Hard Pass, Dial Down, Switcheroo, Trick Shot; keys stay S P F T X, LUI-4), app/client/src/lib/i18n.ts (DEV_LANGS: dev-only ?lang=en via dynamic import, <html lang=en>), directory.md; prod build byte-identical to before (same asset hashes, no en strings); throw-away check: 182/182 leaves, same {param} sets, no áéíóúñ¡¿«», only screen.start.open empty on purpose (no opening mark in English); screen walk ?lang=en 1920x1080 (start, resume, player first/list/delete, hello, level incl. milestones and again, select incl. fresh, question with every joker armed and used incl. Dial Down dial and Trick Shot hit, tray reasons, hints, final answer, correct, wrong/consolation, victory, overlay with joker budget, corner save_locked error): no ⟦…⟧, no overflow, no backlog rows; reworded snipe hit lines; language screen and Esc language rows not reachable under en (en not in UI_LANGS, dev-only)', 'Task 2 of plan 24. Doesn''t wait for the joker-name decisions: joker names use the recommended candidates from task 1 (in `plans/15a-ui-translation.md`, LUI-3) for now. Needs plan 21 (LUI-1) and plan 22 task 2 done; if not, stop and say so.

- `app/client/src/locales/en.ts`: `export const en = { … } satisfies Catalog`; every key of `es`, own English wording.
  - Plural maps `one`/`other`; same `{param}` set per leaf as `es`.
  - Variant arrays (`copy.milestone.*`, `copy.consolation.*`): own English lines in the game''s tone (family, warm, a bit cheeky); count may differ.
  - `joker.<id>.key`: same letters as `es` (`S`, `P`, `F`, `T`, `X`), one-line comment: keys per language are LUI-4.
  - Errors: only player-facing codes (keys present in `es`).
- `lib/i18n.ts`: `en` when `import.meta.env.DEV && ?lang=en`, via dynamic `import()` (same mechanism as `xx` from plan 23, if it exists); `document.documentElement.lang = "en"`. Production stays `es` only: `npm run build` shows no `en` strings in the main chunk.
- Throw-away check script (not kept): every leaf non-empty, same `{param}` set as `es`, no `áéíóúñÁÉÍÓÚÑ¡¿«»`, no `⟦` in rendered output.
- Screen walk: `npm run dev -w app/client` + `trivia`, `?lang=en`, 1920 × 1080: start, player, level, select (joker reasons), question (every joker armed and used, hints, final answer), result, victory, overlay, error line. Same screenshot method as plans 21/23. Fix wording that reads off; overflow → `plans/backlog.md` rows (origin `LUI-3`), no CSS changes.
- Expected Spanish under `en` (not bugs): questions, answers, hints, category/subcategory/bundle names, `/comodines`, `authoring/`.
- `directory.md`: `locales/en.ts`.

Done when: `npm run check` and `npm run build` pass; `es` output unchanged; no new dependencies; the screen walk shows no `⟦…⟧`.', '2026-10-12T00:16:05Z', '2026-10-12T22:12:02Z', 89, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (104, 24, 'LUI-3: chosen joker names into en.ts', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, app/client/src/locales/en.ts, es.ts (joker.skip.pass), game/Question.svelte, plans/15a-ui-translation.md, plans/decisions.md (D-89), plans/project.md', 'Task 3 of plan 24. Waits for the five joker-name decisions from task 1 (`pm show` lists them with answers). If it isn''t linked to five answered decisions, or `locales/en.ts` doesn''t exist yet (task 2), stop and say so.

