- AGENTS.md "Commands": update the `qgen report` line if `--player` was mentioned.

Checks: `qgen report`, `qgen validate`, `trivia-authoring` start page with a temp `TRIVIA_STATE` holding a v2 and a v3 `game.json` (asserted before the server starts); never write `state/`.', '2026-10-12T18:27:24Z', '2026-10-12T19:07:47Z', 418, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (426, 65, 'CT-2 simulation with seen counts', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts, authoring/tools/qgen.py, plans/16-content-target.md, plans/backlog.md: simulation on one v3 save, engine draw by seen count, D-28 workarounds gone; stops at the first game whose level draw repeats, max 500 games (capped seeds reported). Headline = games until the first repeat (any card); Cambiazo into thin subcategories causes nearly all early repeats (adults strong 12 vs level draw 26), so there are extra columns: cambiazo seeds and draw median/bound, plus k. --json: games{…,cambiazo}, draw{…,capped}, k, repeat (was bottleneck), max_games. --mode all --seeds 2: 32 cells in 9 s. Strong draw vs k: adults 26/30, young_adults 36/36, rr-competitive adults 6/7 and young_adults 8.5/9; kids 9.5/24 and young_teens 17.5/24 (greedy draw, B-16); timed 9–11 vs 32–49 (outlook counts 1 question per round, B-15).', '`qgen report --simulate` (`authoring/tools/sim/simulate.ts`, plan 62) still burns. Plan 65, "Also".

- Simulate on a v3 save: games add seen rows; selection by count (the engine''s own `draw`, no copy). Remove the D-28 workarounds (rr-competitive burns for all, `player_id: null`).
- Headline per cell stays "games until the first repeat" (first game that offers a count ≥ 1 card); since games no longer run dry, cap the run (e.g. first repeat + a few games or a max) and say so in the output.
- Print the engine''s `k` (supply outlook task) for a fresh profile per cell as a cross-check next to the simulated number.
- `--json` keys updated; D-75 multipliers unchanged.

Checks: `qgen report --simulate --seeds 2` runs for all cells; the fresh-profile `k` and the simulated games until first repeat are in the same ballpark (note the numbers in the done note).', '2026-10-12T18:27:24Z', '2026-10-12T19:11:32Z', 418, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (427, 65, 'Plan 65 close-out: full check on a copy of the family save', 'work', 'done', 385, '2026-10-12, no file changes. Temp copy of state/game.json (v2: 44 burns, 4 blocked) via trivia (TRIVIA_STATE) + engine API under node: parseSave → v3 (40 seen, max count 2, counts = v2 burns), PUT /api/save 200 and re-reads as v3, 3 answers +3 seen rows (no repeats), undo drops exactly its row, Bloquear → blocked without seen row, Saltar → seen row, Borrar jugador keeps seen rows (game_id 0). trivia-desktop on temp TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR (keys/CDP): v2 loads, v3 written at game start, answer/undo/Bloquear/Borrar jugador same results. outlook(): k=15, exhausted Animales de Colombia + Platos típicos colombianos (single seen question each, correct); start screen doesn''t show it yet: task 623. grep burned: only v2 upgrade (save.ts, save_file.py), migrate() and test fixtures/history. directory.md already lists outlook.ts. npm run check, npm test (156), npm run build, qgen validate pass; state/ unchanged (sha256).', 'Last task of plan 65.

