  - «Quedan preguntas nuevas para unas {n} partidas; después se repetirán algunas, sobre todo de dificultad {lo}–{hi}.» (plural/singular for n = 1)
  - bundle hint, e.g. «Con el paquete {bundle} activado habría más.»
  - k = 0: «En esta partida pueden salir preguntas que ya vieron.»
  - exhausted: «Ya vieron todas las preguntas de: {list}» once per subcategory; mark them notified in the save when shown.
- Reachable and dismissable with keys and pad (action layer, plan 44, if it exists; else the current key handling).
- Record K in the D-entry of plan 65 (decisions.md) if it still says "pm decision 31".

Checks: `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `check:literals`; in the browser (or the desktop shell) with a temp `TRIVIA_STATE` holding a crafted save: k ≥ K shows nothing, k < K the warning with the right range, k = 0 the repeat line, an exhausted subcategory once and not on the next start. Never write `state/`.', '2026-10-12T18:27:35Z', '2026-10-13T00:44:13Z', 418, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (430, 64, 'Prompts: neutral voice per bundle + neutralize prompt (pm decision)', 'work', 'done', 700, '2026-10-12, decision 32 option 1 applied: house-style.md (voice per bundle via {voices}, RAE numbers), review.md reason 8, audit.md check 7, new prompts/neutralize.md; app/data/bundles.json voice per bundle; qgen.py voices_text/bundle_text, bundle in rate/revise/review/audit inputs, bundle new --voice; pool.test.ts', 'Plan 64 task 1. Draft the prompt changes for neutral Spanish in `base` (D-78) and get them approved by the gamemaster (new prompts are theirs, D-36). Task 2 and task 3 of plan 64 wait for this task''s decision.

## First pass: draft and ask
- `authoring/tools/prompts/house-style.md` "Language": voice by bundle. `base`: neutral Latin American Spanish (`es-419`), words understood across Latin America and Spain where one exists. `colombia`: today''s Colombian usage list.
- How the bundle''s voice reaches the prompt is a code choice (like `{players}` in `prompt()`, `authoring/tools/qgen.py:136`): e.g. a `voice` string per bundle in `app/data/bundles.json`, or a `{voice}` section filled in `prompt()`. Pick one, note it in the decision body.
- Number format for `base`: today "the Colombian way" (2.640 / 42,195). Options in the decision, e.g. keep (common across most of Latin America and Spain), or RAE-style (2640 / 42,195, space for 5+ digits).
- `review.md`, `audit.md`: one line each: a `base` question in Colombian (or other national) wording is `needs_work`.
- New `prompts/neutralize.md`: a scan prompt like `tighten.md`. Flags `base` questions whose wording (question, options, hints, description, fun_fact) uses Colombian or other national usage where a neutral word exists; `issue` names word → replacement. References anyone knows (Encanto, García Márquez) stay. Colombian content that needs a connection to Colombia is a bundle matter (D-49), not flagged.
- `es-ES` for questions: recommend no `questions.es-ES.json` at launch; neutral wording reads fine in Spain; the scan lists words with no pan-Hispanic form, so a sparse override can follow if there are many.
- Don''t change the live prompts yet (every `qgen batch` reads them). Put the full drafts as diffs in the decision body:
  `did=$(pm decision add "Neutral Spanish prompts for base (plan 64)" --body "<diffs, voice mechanism, number format options, es-ES recommendation>" --option "approve as drafted" --option "changes: …")`
- Make this task and plan 64''s tasks "`qgen neutralize`" and "Docs: RUNBOOK, D-entry, QC" pending on it (`pm task-pending-decision <id> $did`; ids via `pm show <this task>`). Delete scratch files, stage nothing else, stop.

## Second pass: after the answer
- Apply the drafts with the gamemaster''s changes and the chosen number format; implement the voice mechanism in `qgen.py`.
- Check: `prompt()` output for a `base` and a `colombia` batch shows the right voice (throw-away script); `qgen validate` passes.

Done when: the approved prompts are in `authoring/tools/prompts/`, new `base` drafts get the neutral voice and `colombia` drafts the Colombian one.', '2026-10-12T18:28:26Z', '2026-10-12T18:45:12Z', 417, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (431, 64, 'qgen neutralize', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/qgen.py (cmd_neutralize, SCANS: cmd_scan by mode, --dry-run with cost estimate, authoring/reports/neutralize-<n>.md, audit index + QC trend read neutralize runs), authoring/server/spot_checks.py (run_ids: neutralize runs, so /review?run=neutralize-<n>&sample=1 works). Review passes only_shortened=true for neutralize too (already in the game; reason 7 off). Verified on 7 ids in a temp work dir: 6 flagged (crispetas, gripa, bombillo, chocolatina, 1.000), 1 no-neutral-form (papa), all through fix, review, record, audit, export; pool restored.', 'Plan 64 task 2. A gamemaster-asked command that rewrites Colombian wording in `base` into neutral Spanish, modelled on `qgen tighten`. Waits for the prompt decision of plan 64 task 1 (`prompts/neutralize.md` must be approved and in place).

- `cmd_neutralize` in `authoring/tools/qgen.py`, modelled on `cmd_tighten` (`qgen.py:2735`): run `neutralize-<n>`, resumes an open run.
- Scan: reuse `cmd_scan` (`qgen.py:2710`) with a prompt/filter parameter, no copy. Only `bundle == "base"`, approved + needs_work, chunks of 50, `prompts/neutralize.md`.
- Then fix (with the scan''s issue) → media → sheets → review 1 → research → review 2 → record → audit (D-56, the run''s audit sample) → export → sync.
- `--dry-run`: scan only; print flagged ids, issues, and an estimated cost (rates from `costs.log`) before any fix.
- Done line + exact `git add` like `tighten`; when locale files exist, print the count of stale translations per locale (D-81, `source_hash`).
- Verify with a throw-away script on a handful of known Colombianisms (`grep -E ''bombillo|crispetas|gripa'' authoring/data/questions.json`): the scan flags them, a fix on those few ids goes through review and audit. No full-pool run (part 11, plan task 250). Delete the script; don''t keep pool changes from the check unless they passed review.

Done when: `qgen neutralize --dry-run` lists the known Colombianisms with word → replacement and a cost estimate, and a run on a few ids goes through to export.', '2026-10-12T18:28:26Z', '2026-10-12T18:50:51Z', 417, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (432, 64, 'Docs: RUNBOOK, D-entry, QC for qgen neutralize', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/RUNBOOK.md (neutralize with tighten), authoring/QC.md (section ''Neutralize runs'': run=neutralize-<n>&sample=1 / &audit=flagged, qgen report --qc neutralize-<n>; --qc reads runs, no backlog gap), plans/decisions.md (D-83, D-36 related line), AGENTS.md (Pool list), plans/15-i18n.md, plans/backlog.md (B-13 tooling done), plans/project.md', 'Plan 64 task 3. Document the neutral Spanish tooling once `qgen neutralize` (plan 64 task 2) exists and the prompts (task 1''s decision) are approved.

- `authoring/RUNBOOK.md`: `qgen neutralize` (no arguments) only when the gamemaster asks, same handling as `qgen tighten`.
- `plans/decisions.md`: new D-entry "neutral Spanish rewrite via `qgen neutralize`": amends D-36 (one more gamemaster-asked command), the bundle voices (`base` es-419, `colombia` Colombian), number format and `es-ES` choice from the decision. D-36''s "related" line points to it.
- `authoring/QC.md`: a neutralize run gets the same QC as a batch: `/review?run=neutralize-<n>&sample=1`, and `qgen report --qc neutralize-<n>` if `--qc` reads runs; if it doesn''t, log the gap in `plans/backlog.md`.
- `AGENTS.md` "Pool" command list: `qgen neutralize` (only when the gamemaster asks).
- `plans/15-i18n.md` "Spanish varieties" links plan 64; `plans/backlog.md` B-13 → tooling done, runs in part 11; `plans/project.md` in sync.

Done when: RUNBOOK, decisions, QC.md, AGENTS.md and the plan files say how to run and check a neutralize run.', '2026-10-12T18:28:26Z', '2026-10-12T18:51:56Z', 417, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (433, 10, 'write plan: Steam Cloud saves', 'plan', 'done', 230, '2026-10-13, plan 87 (tasks.sql)', 'Write the plan for part 4 of the masterplan (plan 10): `pm plan add 10 "Steam Cloud saves" --priority 680`. Replaces task 256 (written before the save-per-Steam-user answer).

