- `cmd_audit`/`audit_input` with locale: seeded `AUDIT_SAMPLE` from the locale file, `audit.md` + locale section, source alongside; findings → `work/<run>/audit/`.

Done when: the worktree run from the previous task goes through review 1, fix, review 2, record and audit; locale file has reviewed entries; `questions.json` changes only in `translatable`; worktree discarded.', '2026-10-12T19:15:58Z', '2026-10-12T22:24:24Z', 436, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (440, 66, 'qgen batch --translate <locale>', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/qgen.py (qgen batch --translate L: cmd_translate_batch, translate_selection/spread, TRANSLATE_SIZE 300, TRANSLATE_PILOT 50, next_translate_run tr-L-n, hidden --ids/--count, write_translate_report, commit lines; health ack accepts tr-* runs; qc_trend/qc_section read tr-* runs), authoring/tools/health.py (translation_runs/translation_health/thresholds/failures, translate_stop_reason with pilot stop, health section; batch_runs stays batch-*; table() without batches); /stats lists no batches, the start page''s tr-* rows are task 446; verified on a worktree: qgen batch --translate en --count 5 end to end (~$0.57, 5/5 approved), questions.en.json + pool.en.json written, validate OK, report written, pool.json hash identical; next run exits 2 (pilot), resume, ack, stale-first selection checked; worktree discarded', 'Plan 66, step 4: the entry point (D-36). Needs the prompt decision and the two step tasks before it.

- `cmd_batch` branch (or `cmd_translate_batch`): run `tr-<locale>-<n>`, resumes an open run of that locale; `run.json` `{"mode": "translate", "locale", "ids", "started"}`; steps translate → rate → factcheck → merge → review 1 → fix → factcheck → review 2 → record → audit → export → validate → batch-report (pattern: `cmd_neutralize`).
- Selection by code: approved, translatable, bundle `base`, no approved non-stale translation, not rejected in that locale; stale first (old review kept as `previous`); then subcategories with fewest approved translations, spread over difficulty, ties in `categories.json` order. `TRANSLATE_SIZE` (as decided), pilot 50 when no locale file exists. Hidden `--count`, `--ids`.
- Pilot stop: next `--translate <locale>` exits 2 until `qgen health ack tr-<locale>-1 "<note>"`. Health thresholds that apply (needs_work/reject share, audit agreement) noted in `health.py`; `health.batch_runs` stays `batch-*`.
- Report `authoring/reports/tr-<locale>-<n>.md` (counts, not travelling, `media_text`, stale re-translated, cost per approved translation from `costs.log`, audit, QC section via `qgen report --qc <run>`, spot-check link `/review?batch=<run>&locale=<locale>&sample=1`); "Commit exactly this" lines.
- `qgen report --qc` and `/stats` read `tr-*` runs where they list batches.

Done when: on a worktree, `qgen batch --translate en --count 5` runs end to end: locale file written, `pool.en.json` exported, `qgen validate` clean, report written, `app/data/pool.json` identical; worktree discarded.', '2026-10-12T19:15:58Z', '2026-10-12T22:29:46Z', 436, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (441, 66, 'Translation pipeline: docs and D-entry', 'work', 'done', 690, '2026-10-12, plans/decisions.md (D-87, D-36 amended), authoring/RUNBOOK.md, authoring/QC.md, directory.md, AGENTS.md, plans/15b-question-translation.md', 'Plan 66, step 5. After `qgen batch --translate` works.

