INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (461, 70, 'qgen report --cost: $/approved per run kind and projection per language (CT-3)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/qgen.py (report --cost [--json]), AGENTS.md, plans/16-content-target.md Cost: batch-4..7 0.16/0.37/0.30/0.24 match batches.md; draft $0.26, overhead ratio 0.70, es ~$1750 to go, en/de no pilot yet', 'Plan 70 design "Cost report (CT-3)". `qgen report --cost [--json]` in `authoring/qgen.py`, reusing `costs()` and the `health` metrics.

- Per run (`batch-*`, `tr-<L>-*`, `rework-*`, `tighten-*`, `neutralize-*`, `concepts`, others): calls, $ (incl. `work/<run>/audit/costs.log`), approved, $ per approved.
- Per kind: draft $/approved (last 3 `batch-*`, weighted by approved), translation $/approved per locale (`tr-<L>-*`), overhead ratio = non-batch $ / batch $.
- Projection per launch language (`es`, `en`, `de`, decision 26): deficit × $/approved × (1 + overhead ratio). `en`/`de`: "no pilot yet" until a `tr-<L>-*` run exists. Until task 2 lands, deficit = `targets.deficits()` for `es` and the full target for `en`/`de`; task 2 swaps in per-locale deficits and the `es` source shortfall.
- Spent vs. budget per language when `targets.json` has `"budget"` (task 3); information only, no stop (D-55).
- `work/` is local and gitignored: print which runs/logs were missing or skipped.
- AGENTS.md `qgen report` line; plan 16 "Cost": today''s numbers.

Done when: `qgen report --cost` and `--json` run on the local `work/`; batch-4..7 $/approved match `authoring/reports/batches.md` (0.16 / 0.37 / 0.30 / 0.24); `npm run check` / `qgen validate` still pass.', '2026-10-12T19:46:44Z', '2026-10-12T19:48:29Z', 460, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (462, 70, 'Per-locale deficits and es source shortfall (CT-4)', 'work', 'done', 550, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/{targets,translations,qgen,batches}.py, plans/decisions.md (D-84), plans/16-content-target.md, authoring/RUNBOOK.md; follow-up task 464', 'Plan 70 design "Per-locale targets", "Translation aimed at gaps", "Source supply". No new target numbers: every launch language uses `targets.json` `base` (decision 21: Content target per player and language).

- `targets.deficits(pool, bundle, locale=None)`: with a locale, count that locale''s approved, non-stale translations (via `translations.py`) by their own difficulty.
- `qgen report --locale L` (default `es`) progress section; `target_check` of `--simulate` uses the same function (drop the "until part 9 sets per-locale targets" note).
- `--translate` selection (plan 66, task 440: qgen batch --translate <locale>): within the fewest-translations subcategory order, weight by the locale''s deficit at the source''s difficulty. If task 440 is still open: do the rest, add this weight as a follow-up task in plan 66.
- Source shortfall per level = locale deficit / yield − untranslated translatable approved `es` sources at that level; yield = approved translations / translated sources from `tr-*` runs (1.0 before a pilot), largest over `en`/`de`.
- `target_weights()` for `base`: `es` deficit while any (D-54 unchanged); then the source shortfall; even weights (D-40) only when both are zero.
- Show per-locale deficits and the shortfall in `--cost` (task 1''s projection: `es` extra sources at the draft rate) and in `--locale` progress.
- Throw-away check: seeded `draw_slots` with a fake `es` pool at 5000 and an `en` deficit → slots follow the shortfall.
- D-entry "Per-locale targets and gaps" (`pm decision record`): D-75''s numbers per locale, deficits per locale, source shortfall drives `es` drafting past its target, no per-mode/age-group targets; D-54 "amended by" it.
- Plan 16: CT-4 `[x]` (generation plan = deficits per locale + source shortfall, read by `draft` and `--translate`).

Done when: `qgen report --locale en` and `--simulate` use per-locale deficits; the dry run passes; `qgen validate` passes.', '2026-10-12T19:46:44Z', '2026-10-12T19:51:20Z', 460, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (463, 70, 'Release budget per language (pm decision, CT-3)', 'work', 'dropped', -95, 'developer, 2026-10-15: no dollar budget (milestone 9)', 'Plan 70 task 3. Runs after part 11''s translation pilot (QT-5: `tr-en-1`, `tr-de-1` done, go/no-go decided; this task is pending on `decision 204: Translation pilot done (tr-en-1, tr-de-1)?`). `--cost` per source locale (draft $/approved per source locale, translation $/approved per direction, projection per question locale `en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`) is done: `task 1236: Targets and gap aiming for four question locales`; per-bundle `--cost` rows: `task 830: Pilot effort in qgen report (cost per bundle, review time)`. Before QT-6''s full runs, which wait for this decision.

- If the pilot runs or their reports don''t exist: make this task pending on decision 204 again (or a new "Translation pilot done (tr-en-1, tr-de-1)?", kind once), stop.
- Otherwise: `qgen report --cost` → `pm decision add "Release budget per language"` with a table per question locale:
  - `en` drafting for `base` (to 5000 `en` and what the other locales'' deficits need, `draft_gaps`)
  - translations en → `es`, en → `es-ES`, en → `de`
  - the es-sourced backlog (≤ batch-8 approved without an `en`, `de`, `es-ES` entry): es → `en`, es → `de`, es → `es-ES`
  - overhead (ratio outside batches), QC
  - regional rows, one per bundle in audience order, each 2000 in its language (+ 2000 en where the language isn''t en): `colombia` (es → en), `usa` (en), `germany` (de → en), `uk` (en), `spain` (es-ES → en), `mexico` (es → en); per-bundle `--cost` rows where they exist, else the draft/translation rates; each row''s cost counts in its languages'' totals, shown apart from `base`; launch doesn''t wait for them (`decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)`, milestone 9)
  - rates not yet measured (en drafting before batch-9, en → L before its first run, de and es-ES drafting, de → en, es-ES → en) labelled as stand-ins (nearest measured rate), as `--cost` labels them
- Options: recommended = projection + 20 % margin; a lower cap, naming which levels/locales give way; draft `en` past 5000 for translation sources or not.
- On the answer: `"budget": {"en": $, "es": $, "es-ES": $, "de": $}` in `targets.json`; loader in `targets.py`; `"budget"` in `NOT_BUNDLES` (else `targets.problems()` reports `''budget'' is not a bundle`, task 567); check in `qgen validate`; `--cost` shows spent vs. budget per question locale (information only, no stop, D-55).
- Plan 16 "Cost" and CT-3 `[x]` (CT-4 `[x]` too if not yet, plan 70: done with task 462); `plans/project.md`.

Done when: the decision is answered and stored in `targets.json`; `qgen validate` passes.', '2026-10-12T19:46:44Z', '2026-10-16T03:48:41Z', 460, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (464, 66, '--translate selection weighted by the locale''s deficit (plan 70, D-84)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-12, authoring/tools/qgen.py (translate_selection: D-84 deficit per es level, D''Hondt within subcategory, zero-deficit levels last)', 'Follow-up of `task 462: Per-locale deficits and es source shortfall (CT-4)`; needs `task 440: qgen batch --translate <locale>` done.

- In `--translate`''s source selection: keep the fewest-translations subcategory order; within it, weight each source by `targets.deficits(pool, "base", locale)` at the source''s `es` difficulty (D-84, decision 37). Sources at levels with deficit 0 come last.
- Same rule as D-54; no new argument (D-36).
- Throw-away check: fake locale file with one level filled → that level''s sources are picked last.
- Done when: `qgen batch --translate en --dry-run` (or 440''s equivalent) shows the selection follow the `en` deficits.', '2026-10-12T19:51:17Z', '2026-10-12T22:31:00Z', 462, 0, NULL, NULL);
