INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (706, 95, 'Launch section, Valve''s rules and the go decision', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, plans/11-steam.md (Launch (S6)), plans/17-publishing.md; decision 95, task 708 pending on it; Valve docs unreadable (no web access): marked unverified', 'Plan 95 task 1. Docs + one decision; can run now. Never log in to Steamworks or contact Valve.

**Valve''s rules** (read the docs, cite each URL with the date read; unreadable → "unverified (gamemaster: check <URL>)", no guessing):
- partner.steamgames.com/doc/store/releasing, /doc/store/review_process (build review), /doc/marketing/discounts (launch discount), /doc/store/release_dates, /doc/marketing/event_tools (announcements).
- Facts: build review lead time (plan 94 noted 3–5 business days, plan ≥ 7: re-verify); what the build review checks; how "set build live on default" and the Release button / scheduled release work; launch discount rules (max %, duration, setup deadline); whether discussions/Community Hub are open since "Coming soon".

**`plans/11-steam.md` new section "Launch (S6)"** (after "Coming soon page (ST-3)"; md style per AGENTS.md):
- Valve''s rules (cited).
- Preconditions, each with how it''s checked: ST-3 live + earliest release date (task 704''s record); milestone 9 target per launch language with the exact `qgen report --simulate` command (decision 21, decision 37); masterplan 10 beta test passed (`task 263`''s plan); decision 66/67 answered and PUB-11 written (`plans/17-publishing.md`, `task 194`); plan 93 tasks 699–701 done; Deck review timing (plan 90, `task 687`).
- Timeline backwards from the release date: build review submit ≥ N business days before; date lock 2 weeks before; candidate on `beta` before that.
- Release-candidate steps: version `1.0.0` (decision 91), commit, `git tag v1.0.0`, `trivia-steam upload --branch beta`, manual rows, family sign-off from `beta`, candidate decision per the ST-4 template ("Release checklist (ST-4)").
- Launch-day checklist, each row with exact Steamworks steps: build review passed; candidate build set live on `default` by hand (BuildID = the passed candidate''s; decision 84: SetLive `beta` only from the repo); price per PUB-11 / decision 66 and any launch discount scheduled; store languages = what the build ships (compare `plans/17a-store-page.md` "Supported languages" with the shipped UI catalogs and `app/data/` pool locales; list both; decision 26, decision 27); Community Hub discussions open, report thread (task 701''s text, per language) created and pinned; Deck review requested if plan 90 put it here; Release pressed (or scheduled release fired); announcement posted (subsection "Announcement texts", plan 95 task 2).
- First week: gamemaster reads discussions and reviews daily; what to send to pm (pasted reports → `qgen flag`, plan 93; bugs: steps to reproduce, version from the credits screen); hotfix path (version bump, new tag, ST-4 checklist; patch flow = `task 270`''s plan).
- `plans/17-publishing.md` "Steamworks and store": one bullet pointing to the section.

**Go decision** (kind once): `did=$(pm decision add "Start the launch release candidate v1.0.0?" --body … --option "go: all preconditions met, release date <date>" --option "not yet (which)")` with the preconditions as a checklist (current state of each) and the earliest release date. Then `pm task-pending-decision <id of "Release candidate v1.0.0" in plan 95> $did`.

Done when: the section holds the cited rules, preconditions, timeline, launch-day checklist and first-week steps; the go decision is raised and the candidate task waits for it.', '2026-10-13T09:07:02Z', '2026-10-13T09:09:06Z', 705, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (707, 95, 'Launch announcement and store "what''s new" texts', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, plans/11-steam.md (Launch (S6) → Announcement texts: en, es-419 + es-ES deltas, de; titles, BBCode bodies, what''s new 1.0.0; <n_*> and <thread> placeholders)', 'Plan 95 task 2. Docs; can run now (after task "Launch section, Valve''s rules and the go decision" has created "Launch (S6)" in `plans/11-steam.md`; if it''s missing, add the subsection at the end of ST-3''s neighbour and note it).

- Draft per launch language (decision 26: es, en, de; es neutral es-419 per decision 27, with an es-ES variant only where a word differs):
  - Steam event/announcement title + body for launch day: what the game is (family vs gamemaster on a TV, 12 questions to victory), modes, languages, questions per language as `<n>` (filled from `qgen report` at candidate time by the task "Release candidate v1.0.0"), how to report a question → the pinned report thread (plan 93, task 701).
  - One-line "what''s new" for `1.0.0`.
- No marketing claims, no links outside Steam, AI disclosure wording consistent with `plans/17a-store-page.md`.
- Into `plans/11-steam.md` "Launch (S6)" → "Announcement texts"; the gamemaster posts them (Steamworks events tool). Workers never post.

Done when: titles, bodies and "what''s new" lines exist for es (es-419, es-ES deltas), en, de with `<n>` placeholders.', '2026-10-13T09:07:02Z', '2026-10-13T09:11:10Z', 705, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (708, 95, 'Release candidate v1.0.0', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 95 task 3. Waits for decision 95 "Start the launch release candidate v1.0.0?" and `task 862: Launch section: report server, store facts, modding gate`; read them with `pm show`. Decision not answered or task 862 not done → stop. The "Preconditions" table in `plans/11-steam.md` "Launch (S6)" wins over decision 95''s older body.

- `go`: `app/desktop/package.json` `version` → `1.0.0` (the one edit, decision 91: Game version: single source of truth), staged; fill the `<n>` counts in "Announcement texts" from `qgen report` per locale. Run the per-commit checks (AGENTS.md).
- `not yet`: new decision naming the blocker (`pm decision add`, kind once, options as the go decision), this task pending on it (`pm task-pending-decision`), stop.
- Raise the ST-4 candidate decision `Release candidate v1.0.0 passed?` exactly per the template in `plans/11-steam.md` "Release checklist (ST-4)", incl. plan 104''s `report` and Steam-offline rows; the gamemaster''s steps first:
  - tag this task''s commit (`task <this id>: Release candidate v1.0.0`) as `v1.0.0`
  - `trivia-steam upload --branch beta`
  - manual rows on `beta`, incl. `report`: a flag sent from the candidate arrives via `qgen flag --pull`
  - the store facts run sheet ("Store facts on the release candidate", decision 90)
  - family sign-off from `beta`
  - after the ST-4 rows, a "Store facts" section with the run sheet''s answer slots (installed size base + each DLC, weak machine, Steam Deck, pad-only → controller flag)
  - release date in the body ≥ the earliest from ST-3
- `pm task-pending-decision 709 <did>`.
- A failed candidate never reuses its tag (plan 95 rules). Never upload, log in or tag on the gamemaster''s behalf.

Done when: version is `1.0.0` staged, counts filled, candidate decision raised and task 709 waits on it (or, not yet: blocker decision raised, this task pending).', '2026-10-13T09:07:02Z', NULL, 705, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (709, 95, 'Record the candidate and the store facts; release decision', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 95 task 4. Waits for `Release candidate v1.0.0 passed?` (raised by `task 708: Release candidate v1.0.0`); read the answer with `pm show`. Not raised/answered yet → stop.

Per ST-4''s "Worker on the answer" (`plans/11-steam.md` "Release checklist (ST-4)"):
- `passed` / `minor issues`: `trivia-release-check --manual FILE` with the answers (needs the tag on HEAD; if the tree has moved, record the answers in `work/steam/v1.0.0/` as the template says and note it). Minor issues → rows in `plans/backlog.md`.
- `failed`: one `pm task add` per failing row in its owning plan (`pm plan list`), plus a new task in plan 95 "Release candidate v1.0.<n+1>" (shape of task 708, with a version bump; never reuse a tag); stop.
- Store facts (the decision''s "Store facts" section): field values into `plans/17a-store-page.md` "System requirements, languages, controller" (final, measured on `v1.0.x`, date); `pm decision consequences 90 "…"`. A store fact that fails the store''s own rules (e.g. requirements too high for the Deck) → a task in its owning plan.
- Then raise `Released? date, build id` (kind once) with the launch-day checklist from "Launch (S6)" as the body (release date ≥ earliest from ST-3; build review submitted in time per the timeline; store facts entered); options `released on <date>, BuildID <n>` (recommended), `Valve''s build review returned issues (list)`, `not yet (blocker)`. `pm task-pending-decision 710 <did>`.
- `pm decision consequences` on the candidate decision.

Done when: the candidate result and store facts are recorded and either the "Released?" decision waits on task 710, or (failed) the fix tasks and the next candidate task exist.', '2026-10-13T09:07:02Z', NULL, 705, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (710, 95, 'Record the release and the first week', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 95 task 5. Waits for `Released? date, build id` (raised by task 709); read the answer with `pm show`. Not raised/answered yet → stop.

- Released: `plans/11-steam.md` S6 row and a "Launch (S6)" note with date, version, BuildID, price, report URL; rows the launch closes in `plans/17-publishing.md` (PUB-11 live) and `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (SW-12 review if requested) noted; `plans/project.md` and `README.md` in sync (the Steam build is the release; no browser-game note: plan 99 retires it); `pm decision consequences <did> "…"`.
- Build review issues: one `pm task add` per issue in its owning plan; then a new candidate task in plan 95 (shape of task 708, version bump) if code or content changed, else a fresh "Released? date, build id" decision and a new "Record the release and the first week" task pending on it.
- Not yet: same as above with the blocker named.
- On released: raise `First week after launch: what came in?` (kind once; body: the first-week steps from "Launch (S6)"; options `nothing to fix`, `issues (list: reports, bugs, review themes)`), and add a task in plan 95 "Triage the first week after launch" pending on it, body: each bug → a task in its owning plan or a `plans/backlog.md` row; reports are already `needs_work` via `qgen flag --pull` / `qgen flag` (plan 93) and go through `qgen batch` review; a wrong-answer or crash fix → a hotfix candidate via plan 96''s patch path and ST-4.
- Docs only; never log in to Steamworks or contact players.

Done when: the release is recorded in the plan files and the first-week decision waits on its triage task (or the issue/blocker path is set up).', '2026-10-13T09:07:02Z', NULL, 705, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (711, 96, 'create tasks for plan 96', 'split', 'done', 1000, '2026-10-13, tasks.sql: tasks 712–716; decision 96 raised (plan task 1 done here), task 713 pending on it', 'Split plan 96 into tasks and identify all decisions that need to be made. If the plan already has tasks,
bring them in line with the plan. A task that writes a plan gets `--kind plan`.', '2026-10-13T09:13:38Z', '2026-10-13T09:14:45Z', 270, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (712, 96, 'qgen patch-notes: counts-only notes between two releases', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, authoring/tools/patch_notes.py (new: qgen patch-notes), authoring/tools/qgen.py, authoring/steam/release_check.py (previous_tag/kind/save_version take a rev), README.md, directory.md; decision 97 recorded; checked in a throw-away clone (counts match by hand, from==to → no content changes, full kind + SAVE_VERSION change)', 'Plan 96 task 2. New `qgen patch-notes <from-ref> [<to-ref>]` under `authoring/` (D-35, no new dependency): drafts a content patch''s notes by diffing the shipped pool between two git refs.

- `from-ref` default: newest `v*` tag (reuse `authoring/steam/release_check.py` `previous_tag()`, or move it to a shared helper both use); `to-ref` default: the working tree (draft before tagging).
- Reads `app/data/pool.json` (es) + `pool.<locale>.json` and the categories files (`app/data/categories.json`, a bundle''s own `categories.json`) via `git show <ref>:<path>`; a file missing at a ref = empty pool for that locale.
- Per locale: "added" = id only in new; "dropped" = id only in old; "fixed" = same id, changed play field (question, answer, wrong answers, hints, fun fact, difficulty, subcategory, media).
- Output Markdown for the gamemaster: version + pool hash from → to (decision 91: Game version: single source of truth; decision 92: Pool version: export hash in pool.json), kind `full`/`content-only` and `SAVE_VERSION` change via `release_check` (`kind()`, `save_version()`), table locale × category: added / fixed / dropped, totals.
- Plus a Steam event draft per launch language (es, en, de), BBCode like the announcement texts in `plans/11-steam.md` "Launch (S6)" (task 707''s tone): title "Update v<x>: <n> new questions"; body: per-category counts, "fixed <n> questions (thanks for your reports)", "removed <n>"; on `full` a `<Changes: fill in>` placeholder and a printed warning. Strings live in the command (authoring, not `t()`).
- Counts only: never question text, answers or ids. `pm decision record "Patch notes: counts only?" --answer "counts only (added/fixed/dropped per language and category)" --body "<why: no spoilers; nothing leaks if OQ-35 makes the pool private>"`.
- `from == to` (or no differences) → "no content changes".
- Writes `work/steam/v<x>/patch-notes.md` when `to` is a tag, or `--out FILE`; `--json` for scripts.
- Check (throw-away clone, deleted after): tag `v0.0.1`, approve/drop/edit a few questions, `qgen export`, run → counts match by hand. Then `qgen validate`, `npm run check` and the other per-commit checks (AGENTS.md).
- Docs: `qgen.py` usage, `directory.md` if a new file, `README.md` one line under Commands.

Done when: the command drafts correct counts-only notes between two refs and the counts-only decision is recorded.', '2026-10-13T09:14:42Z', '2026-10-13T09:17:51Z', 711, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (713, 96, 'Content updates (ST-5) section, docs and the first-patch decision', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, plans/11-steam.md (Content updates (ST-5); Valve rules unverified: no web access), plans/16-content-target.md, plans/project.md, README.md; decision 96 consequences; decision 178 raised, task 714 pending on it', 'Plan 96 task 3. Decision 96: Content patch cadence after launch? is answered (monthly, only if ≥ 100 new approved per launch language or a player-reported fix is waiting; hotfixes any time). Runs after task 712: qgen patch-notes (it documents that command). Steam build only (decision 111: Steam only): no "without Steam" steps anywhere.

- Valve''s rules: read and cite with the date read: partner.steamgames.com/doc/store/updates (pushing an update to `default`: review needed?) and partner.steamgames.com/doc/marketing/event_tools (event type for patch notes: "Small update / patch notes" vs "Regular update"). Unreadable = "unverified (gamemaster: check <URL>)".
- `plans/11-steam.md` new section "Content updates (ST-5)" after "Launch (S6)" (intro paragraph, then bullets):
  - Cadence: decision 96''s answer.
  - Patch path step by step: batches (`qgen batch`, `--translate en|de`, per `authoring/RUNBOOK.md`); reports (`qgen flag --pull` for players'' reports from the report server, plan 103; `qgen flag` for pasted copy-fallback text; both → `needs_work`; `qgen rework` only when the gamemaster asks); `qgen export`; `qgen validate`; `qgen patch-notes`; bump `version` in `app/desktop/package.json` (patch; minor on `SAVE_VERSION` change, decision 91); commit; `git tag v<x>`; `trivia-steam upload --branch beta`; ST-4 rows as revised by plan 104: content-only variant = `offline` (Steam running in offline mode, a game to level 3 hitting new questions) + `signoff`, `beta-save` on a save change, the automated `report` step (`/health`) on every run, full patches add the manual `report` row; candidate decision per the ST-4 template; gamemaster sets the BuildID live on `default`, posts the event from the draft.
  - Hotfix path (wrong answer, crash): any time, same path, no cadence wait (decision 96).
  - What a patch may not do (plan 96 "Rules"): no silent rule or save-shape change; code change → kind `full` + hand-written "Changes"; dropped question = status change, never deletion; no new network request, update check or remote content (the clicked report stays the only request); report-server changes (plan 103) deploy apart from game patches; workers never log in to Steamworks, set builds live, post events or contact players.
  - "Patch notes" log subsection (empty; later patches append their event texts).
  - ST-5 note: content half here; reports half = plan 93 + plan 103.
- `plans/16-content-target.md` ("Quality bar" or an after-release bullet): what a patch adds, the cadence. `README.md` how-to "Send a content patch" (commands only). `plans/project.md` in sync.
- `pm decision consequences 96 "<what changed>"`.
- Raise the go decision (kind once): `did=$(pm decision add --once "Start the first content patch?" --body … --option "go: version 1.0.<n>" --option "not yet (why)")`. Body: preconditions checklist: "Released? date, build id" (plan 95) answered and recorded by task 710; cadence due per decision 96 (new approved per language since `v1.0.0` from `qgen patch-notes v1.0.0`, with the numbers at the time); reports pulled (`qgen flag --pull`) and the reported fixes done; `qgen validate` clean.
- `pm task-pending-decision 714 $did` (task 714: First content patch candidate).
- Per-commit checks (AGENTS.md).

Done when: the section, docs and consequences are in, and task 714 waits on the go decision.', '2026-10-13T09:14:42Z', '2026-10-14T21:47:44Z', 711, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (714, 96, 'First content patch candidate', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 96 task 4. Waits for the decision "Start the first content patch?" (raised by task 713: Content updates (ST-5) section, docs and the first-patch decision); read it with `pm show`. If it isn''t raised or answered yet, don''t proceed: stop.

- `go: version 1.0.<n>`: `app/desktop/package.json` `version` → `1.0.<n>` (decision 91: Game version: single source of truth), staged. `qgen patch-notes` draft (`--out work/steam/v1.0.<n>/patch-notes.md`); copy the event texts into the "Patch notes" log of `plans/11-steam.md` "Content updates (ST-5)". Run the per-commit checks (AGENTS.md).
- Raise `Release candidate v1.0.<n> passed?` exactly per the template in `plans/11-steam.md` "Release checklist (ST-4)" (rows as revised by plan 104), gamemaster steps first: tag this task''s commit (`task <this id>: First content patch candidate`) as `v1.0.<n>`; `trivia-steam upload --branch beta`; manual rows, content-only variant: `offline` (Steam running in offline mode, a game to level 3 hitting new questions), `signoff`; `beta-save` if `SAVE_VERSION` changed; `report` row only if the kind is `full`; OK. Then `pm task-pending-decision 715 <did>` (task 715: Record the patch candidate; live decision).
- `not yet`: new decision naming the blocker (`pm decision add --once`, options as the go decision), this task pending on it (`pm task-pending-decision`), stop.
- A failed candidate never reuses its tag. Never upload, log in or tag on the gamemaster''s behalf. Steam build only (decision 111): no "without Steam" rows.

Done when: version staged, notes drafted and logged, candidate decision raised and task 715 waits on it (or, not yet: blocker decision raised, this task pending).', '2026-10-13T09:14:42Z', NULL, 711, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (715, 96, 'Record the patch candidate; live decision', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 96 task 5. Waits for `Release candidate v1.0.<n> passed?` (raised by task 714: First content patch candidate); read it with `pm show`. Not raised or not answered: stop.

- Act per `plans/11-steam.md` "Release checklist (ST-4)" → "Worker on the answer" (rows as revised by plan 104): `passed` / `passed with minor issues`: `trivia-release-check --manual FILE` with the answers so `work/steam/v<x>/release-check.md` holds them; minor issues → `plans/backlog.md` bullets.
- `failed (rows)`: one task per failing row in its owning plan, plus a new candidate task in plan 96 (shape of task 714) with the next patch version (never reuse a tag); stop.
- On pass: raise `did=$(pm decision add --once "Content patch v<x> live? date, build id" --body … --option "live on <date>, BuildID <n>" --option "not yet (blocker)")`. Body: gamemaster steps: Steamworks → set the BuildID live on `default`; post the Steam event from `work/steam/v<x>/patch-notes.md` (one per language, event type per "Content updates (ST-5)").
- `pm task-pending-decision 716 $did` (task 716: Record the first content patch).

Done when: the answer is recorded in the report and the live decision blocks task 716 (or, failed: fix tasks and a new candidate task exist).', '2026-10-13T09:14:43Z', NULL, 711, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (716, 96, 'Record the first content patch', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Plan 96 task 6. Waits for `Content patch v<x> live? date, build id` (raised by task 715: Record the patch candidate; live decision); read it with `pm show`. Not raised or not answered: stop.

- `live on <date>, BuildID <n>`: `plans/11-steam.md` ST-5 `[x]` (only once plan 93 and plan 103 are done too; else note the content half done) with version, date, BuildID; S6 row status in "Phases"; "Content updates (ST-5)" "Patch notes" log entry dated; `plans/16-content-target.md` and `plans/project.md` in sync; `pm decision consequences <did> "<what changed>"`.
- `not yet (blocker)`: same pattern as plan 95''s "Record the release and the first week" (task 710): a task per blocker in its owning plan, then a new candidate (shape of task 714: First content patch candidate) if code or content changed, else a fresh live decision and a new record task pending on it.

Done when: the first content patch is recorded as live (milestone 11 "Done when": content updates go out as patches).', '2026-10-13T09:14:43Z', NULL, 711, 0, NULL, 'app');
