- A failed save write with code `bad_save` (`lib/store.ts`: desktop `writeSave` rejects, or `/api/save` 400 from `app/server/save.py`: invalid JSON, save over 10 MB) is thrown to the screen; `lib/errors.ts` `errorText` finds no `error.bad_save` key and shows the English `can''t save: …` message on a Spanish/German TV.
- The other codes without a key (`answer_invalid`, `budget_*`, `card_invalid`, `joker_unknown`, `language_unknown`, `no_cards`, `no_game`, `no_question`, `nothing_to_undo`, `skip_not_question`, `server_error`, `flag_invalid`) are internal/guarded by the UI: leave them.

## What
- `error.bad_save` in `app/client/src/locales/es.ts`, `en.ts`, `de.ts` (es-ES inherits): short, says the save could not be written and the game goes on; ask the gamemaster for the wording with `pm decision add` if unsure.
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass; update the `code-review.md` row''s status.', '2026-10-13T10:23:30Z', '2026-10-13T10:29:34Z', 541, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (726, 77, 'Split the Select screen out of Game.svelte', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/client/src/game/Envelopes.svelte (new), Game.svelte, code-review.md, directory.md; decision 6 pixel diff of Select/mid-pick/fresh: 0 px', 'Follow-up of `task 543: Review Game.svelte` (code review part 5, `code-review.md` `## Part 5`).

## Why
- `app/client/src/game/Game.svelte` (≈1310 lines) holds the screen state machine plus the markup and ≈200 lines of CSS of the Select screen (paper envelopes: `.cards`, `.card`, `.flap`, `.tear`, `.letter-slot`, `.letter`, `.seal`, `.new-badge`, keyframes `deal`, `chosen`, `seal-crack`, `flap-off`, `tear-show`, `letter-up`, `gone`) and `tilt()`.
- That block is self-contained: it reads only `game.options`, `picked`, `fresh`, `busy`, `game.id`/`game.level` (tilt) and calls `pick(i)`.

## What
