INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (730, 78, 'Smoke game: answer in the questions language picked on the first screen', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, authoring/steam/smoke.mjs, code-review.md', 'Follow-up of `task 720: Review Steam release and store tooling` (code-review.md `## Part 6`).

- `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` `pickQuestions()` reads only `resources/data/pool.json` (es); `playLevel()` clicks `st.answers.indexOf(q.answer)` with the es answer text.
- The smoke shell runs under `env -i` (no `LANG`), and the first screen clicks `.language .option.current`. Once a locale pool (`pool.en.json`, …) ships, the questions language may not be `es`: the es answer isn''t among the on-screen answers (`indexOf` −1 → `nth-child(0)` matches nothing) or the id is missing in that pool → the smoke fails although the game is fine.
- Fix: after the language step, read `save.language.questions` from the save, load that locale''s pool (`es` → `pool.json`, else `pool.<locale>.json`, as `app/client/src/lib/data.ts` `poolFile`) for both the picks and the answer text.
- Check: `node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` on `app/desktop/release/linux-unpacked` (dev shell; temp HOME is built in).', '2026-10-13T11:43:21Z', '2026-10-13T11:46:09Z', 720, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (731, 79, 'qgen claude(): log the cost of failed attempts in costs.log', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, authoring/tools/qgen.py, code-review.md: claude() logs every JSON result''s cost, failed and usage-limit attempts too', 'Follow-up of `task 557: Review qgen helpers, claude() wrapper, schemas and CLI` (code review part 7).

## Problem
- `claude()` in `authoring/tools/qgen.py` appends `<model>\t<total_cost_usd>` to `<cwd>/costs.log` only on success.
- A result with `is_error` or without `structured_output` (schema not met, max turns) is retried (`retries=2`) and its `total_cost_usd`, if any, is never logged: run costs (`qgen report --cost`, `health.py` "cost $", batch reports) undercount retried calls.
- `health.py` also counts lines as "calls" / "calls per approved": logging failed attempts changes those numbers too (more calls, now real ones).

## What
- Check what a failed `claude -p --output-format json` result carries (`total_cost_usd` on `is_error`?) from a real error JSON if one is at hand (work/*.log); no LLM calls just to find out.
- If failed attempts cost money: log them (same line format), so cost reports are complete; decide whether "calls" should count them (one line = one `claude -p` process is the simplest reading).
- Log the change in `## Part 7` of `code-review.md` (row of task 557: cost of failed attempts).

## Check
- Stubbed `subprocess.run` in a /tmp script: success, `is_error` with a cost, non-JSON stdout → expected costs.log lines.
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`.', '2026-10-13T11:49:43Z', '2026-10-13T12:31:47Z', 557, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (732, 79, 'qgen related_questions: answer matches before same-subcategory questions in the 30 cap', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, authoring/tools/qgen.py, code-review.md', 'Found by `task 562: Review qgen LLM batch steps: media, sheets, review, fix, research, record`.

## Problem
- `authoring/tools/qgen.py` `related_questions(q, pool)` (used by `cmd_review`, both the source and the translation payload) collects pool questions with the same/similar answer (`norm` equal or `difflib` ratio ≥ 0.7) **or** the same subcategory, in pool order, then cuts to `out[:30]`.
- Once a subcategory has > 30 non-rejected questions, same-answer questions of other subcategories that come later in pool order are cut: the reviewer misses the duplicates the list exists for.
- Today: max 21 per subcategory, 0 lost (checked 2026-10-13 over the last 700 questions); grows with every batch (targets per subcategory are higher).

## Fix
- Answer matches first (exact, then by ratio), then same-subcategory questions, then cut to 30; name the 0.7 and 30 (`RELATED_RATIO`, `RELATED_MAX`).
- Changes the review prompt''s `related` list (plan 79 rule: prompt change ≠ code fix), so this is its own task; behaviour otherwise unchanged.
- Check: throw-away script on a temp copy, `related_questions` for a question in a large subcategory before/after; no LLM calls.
- Log the row in `## Part 7` of `code-review.md` as `fixed (task N)`.', '2026-10-13T12:14:09Z', '2026-10-13T12:32:50Z', 562, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (733, 79, 'qgen: errors a step returns itself are never printed; standalone commands exit 0 with them', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, authoring/tools/qgen.py (failed() prints a step''s own error; main exits 1 on non-limit errors), code-review.md', 'Found by `task 563: Review qgen audit, back-audit and batch orchestration` (code-review.md `## Part 7`).

## Problem
- `parallel()` prints each failure (`FAILED <id>: …`), but errors a step returns itself are never printed:
  - `cmd_record`, `record_translations`: `[RuntimeError("N question(s) without a review")]`
  - `cmd_audit`: `[RuntimeError("<run>: no recorded LLM review to audit")]`
- `run_steps` prints only "Stopped at `<step>` with N error(s)", not the message.
- `main()` acts only on `UsageLimit`: standalone `qgen record` / `qgen audit` with such an error print nothing and exit 0.

## Fix (output text changes: plan 79 rule, so its own task)
- Print the message where it is returned (stderr), or have `run_steps`/`main` print errors that `parallel` didn''t (e.g. a marker attribute set in `parallel`).
- `main()`: exit 1 on non-limit errors.
- Check RUNBOOK''s exit code table still fits (exit 1 = stop and report).
- Verify with a stubbed run (no LLM calls): `qgen audit --batch <run without recorded review>` prints the reason and exits 1; a `parallel` failure is printed once.', '2026-10-13T12:17:11Z', '2026-10-13T12:34:03Z', 563, 0, NULL, NULL);
