  - `/data/` from `app/data/`; `/media` from the cache (`TRIVIA_MEDIA` | repo `media/`), cache only, never downloads; reuse `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` (`makeResolver`) where it fits so the rules are the desktop''s.
  - Save: dev-only middleware over `app/desktop/save.mjs` (`makeSaveFile`: load, atomic write, backup) plus a dev-only page shim providing the save half of the desktop bridge (`window.triviaShell.loadSave/writeSave/backupSave`; decision 130: Preload bridge renamed window.trivia → window.triviaShell), so the browser uses `FileStore` from `app/client/src/lib/store.ts`, the desktop''s Store. Not in the production bundle (check `dist/` after `npm run build`).
  - Save dir: `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR` if set, else a fresh temp dir (never `state/` or `state/desktop/`); printed at start: `trivia dev: save <path>`. This is the dev switch of decision 111: Steam only: plan 87''s "no Steam user = memory-only" must not apply here.
  - The shim marks itself on `window.triviaShell` (e.g. `devServer: true`) so `validUser` in `app/client/src/lib/desktop.ts` (task 776: Valid Steam user check and dev switch) is true on the dev server; set or read that marker there.
  - Remove the `/api`, `/data`, `/media` proxies to :8000 from `app/client/vite.config.ts`.
- Commands: `npm run dev -w app/client` (dev client) and `npm run serve -w app/client` (or similar: `vite preview` of the built client); fixed ports, printed.
- Replace "walk it on `trivia` with a temp `TRIVIA_STATE`" (and similar) with the dev server in AGENTS.md, `plans/*.md` and open task bodies (`pm task set`; running/closed ones left alone). Keep AGENTS.md''s `trivia` line until step 4; just add the dev server line.
- New dependencies: none (decision needed otherwise).
- Done when: a fresh-save game plays a few levels in a browser on the dev server (throw-away Playwright, decision 6), the save lands in the printed dir, a cached media file plays; per-commit checks pass; `trivia` still works.
- Readable build (`plan 111: Readable client build`, decision 124: Readable client build: output naming rule for mod overrides; found by task 947): the built-client command (`vite preview`) serves the readable `dist/` tree as built (`main.js`, `game/Game.svelte.js`, `vendor/svelte/…`, `.map` files, `.svelte.css`), no rewrite or fallback that hides a missing module; `vite` dev is unaffected.', '2026-10-13T15:19:47Z', '2026-10-14T04:08:57Z', 759, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (763, 99, 'trivia-desktop --import-save: envelope check, --force with backup; raise the family-switch decision', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/save.mjs (importText: envelope, --force copy to backup/game-import-<stamp>.json), app/desktop/main.mjs (--force, exit 1 on failure, prints paths), README.md; checked on a copy of state/game.json in a temp TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR; decision 150 raised, task 765 pending on it', 'Step 2 of plan 99. The family''s `state/game.json` (save version 2) moves into the desktop build.

- Extend the existing `--import-save <file>` in `app/desktop/main.mjs` (+ `app/desktop/save.mjs`):
  - check the envelope: JSON object with numeric `version` (the client upgrades v2 on load, `engine/save.ts`; no Python `save.migrate()`); a bad file: clear error, exit non-zero, nothing written;
  - write the desktop save atomically via `makeSaveFile`;
  - refuse a non-empty target without `--force`; with `--force` first copy the old save to `backup/game-import-<stamp>.json`;
  - print source, target file (the Steam user''s `<steamid64>/`, `dev/` or `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`, plan 87) and the backup path if any; the source file stays untouched.
  - needs a valid user (or `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`): without one task 779 already refuses (stderr, exit 1, nothing written).
- Check on a copy of `state/game.json` in a temp `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`: import, re-import refused, `--force` makes the backup, the game loads it (players, seen counters).
- Then raise the decision (kind once):
  `pm decision add "Family save imported into trivia-desktop?" --option "imported, family plays trivia-desktop" --option "not yet" --body …` (check `pm decision add -h` for the kind flag). Body: the exact command for the gamemaster (`trivia-desktop --import-save state/game.json`, run with Steam running and the family''s Steam account logged in, since the save folder is per Steam user, plan 87); what to check (players, seen counters, a round plays); from then on the family plays `trivia-desktop` (later the Steam beta).
- Make the step-4 task ("Delete app/server, ServerStore, the trivia command and nix build .#app") wait on it: `pm task-pending-decision <that task id> <decision id>` (find the id with `pm show p99`).
- Binding: decision 111: Steam only; decision 98: Browser game: corrupt or newer state/game.json (backup behaviour stays in `save.mjs`).
- Done when: the import works as above; the decision is raised and the deletion task waits on it; per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-13T15:19:47Z', '2026-10-14T04:14:20Z', 759, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (764, 99, 'Move authoring''s Python imports off app/server; authoring reads the desktop save', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, authoring/tools/{paths,media_cache,http_base}.py (moved copies), save_file.py (desktop save: TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR or newest state/desktop/<user>/game.json, named on stderr), layout.py (no app/server on sys.path), import comments in qgen/played/download/media/reviews/categories and authoring/server/{main,overview,media_stats}.py, app/desktop/resolve.mjs comment, directory.md', 'Step 3 of plan 99. Authoring stops importing from `app/server/` so step 4 can delete it.

- Today `authoring/tools/layout.py` puts `app/server` on `sys.path`; imports: `paths` (layout.py, save_file.py, categories.py), `save.load` (save_file.py), `media_cache` (qgen.py, download.py, media.py, authoring/server/main.py, overview.py, media_stats.py), `http_base.BaseHandler` (authoring/server/main.py). Check with `grep -rn "app/server\|app.server\|import paths\|import save\|media_cache\|http_base" authoring`.
- Move (copy into `authoring/tools/` or similar) `paths.py`, `media_cache.py`, `http_base.py`, and of `save.py` only what `save_file.py` needs (reading the save). Move, don''t sync: decision 104: Python ↔ Node/TS twins. `app/server/main.py` keeps working from its own copies until step 4 (no imports across the line). `layout.py` stops adding `app/server` to `sys.path`; import comments updated.
- Save path for authoring (apply_flags, seen counts, `save_file.py`): the desktop save, not `state/game.json`: `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR/game.json` if set, else `state/desktop/<user>/game.json` (the only one, or the newest; named on stderr). `flags-applied.json` stays under `state/`. If that turns out not obvious: `pm decision add`.
- Update `directory.md` for the new modules.
- Done when: nothing under `authoring/` imports from `app/server/`; `qgen validate`, `qgen report`, a `trivia-media sync --status approved` dry run (or equivalent status check) and `trivia-authoring` pages (review, flags) run; apply_flags reads a flag from a desktop save in a temp `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`; per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-13T15:19:48Z', '2026-10-14T04:17:30Z', 759, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (765, 99, 'Delete app/server, ServerStore, the trivia command and nix build .#app', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Step 4 of plan 99. Waits for the decision "Family save imported into trivia-desktop?" (raised by the step-2 task) and needs the step-3 task (authoring off `app/server/`) done.

- Delete `app/server/` entirely (`main.py`, `paths.py`, `save.py`, `media_cache.py`, `http_base.py`, `__pycache__`); `app/` has no `.py` left.
- `app/client/src/lib/store.ts`: drop `ServerStore`, `/api/save`, `/api/save/backup` (task 724''s endpoint); the store choice keeps only `FileStore` (desktop bridge or the dev server''s shim); merge `TextStore` into it if nothing else extends it. Backup/notice behaviour of decision 98 stays.
- `flake.nix`: drop `trivia-dev` (the `trivia` command, `TRIVIA_STATE` wrapper), package `app` and `default` pointing at it; update the dev shell list.
- `authoring/steam/release_check.py`: drop the `nix` step (`nix build .#app --no-link`), its `--skip` choice, docstring row, header/manual rows mentioning it.
- `knip.jsonc`: drop the `ignoreIssues` entry for `app/client/src/lib/store.ts` (task 1115 put it there for `ServerStore`); `npm run knip` still passes.
- Don''t delete `state/game.json`, `game.sqlite`, `flags.json` (family''s data, gitignored).
- AGENTS.md Commands: remove the `trivia` and `nix build .#app` lines/mentions so it doesn''t name dead commands (rest of the docs: step-5 task).
- Done when: per-commit checks pass; `trivia-release-check --skip tag …` runs without a `nix` step; `grep -rn "api/save\|ServerStore\|app/server\|\.#app" app authoring flake.nix` finds nothing live; the dev server (step 1) still plays a game.
- Guard: if decision "Family save imported into trivia-desktop?" is missing or not answered "imported…", run `pm task-pending-decision 765 <its id>` (raise it as in task 763 if missing) and stop without deleting anything.', '2026-10-13T15:19:48Z', NULL, 759, 0, NULL, 'app');
