INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (870, 104, 'Release check: report row, report step, Steam offline row', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, authoring/steam/release_check.py (offline/report rows, report step reading reportUrl from linux-unpacked app.asar, else app/desktop/package.json), plans/11-steam.md, plans/18-steam-integration.md, AGENTS.md, README.md; checked: report ✓ against trivia-report-server dev, ✗ server down with URL, ✗ empty URL, --manual file with report row, content-only auto-skip', 'Plan 104 task 1. Bring `trivia-release-check` and the ST-4 checklist in line with decision 111 (Steam only) and decision 93 (own report server). Details: plan 104 "Decisions taken here". Runs after plan 93 (550) and plan 103 (700) tasks; if plan 93''s `report:send` / `qgen flag --pull` or plan 103''s `trivia-report-server dev` aren''t there yet, stop with a follow-up note, don''t stub them into the release check.

- `authoring/steam/release_check.py`:
  - `MANUAL["offline"]`: full: "beta install, Steam running in offline mode (Steam → Go Offline while online, then network off), start from Steam: full game to level 12 or a won checkpoint; quit and restart: save is there; flag a question and send: fails cleanly (no hang, failed state), copy fallback copies the report text"; content-only: same setup, "a game to level 3 that hits new questions".
  - new `MANUAL["report"]` (full only): from the candidate on `beta` under Steam, online: flag a question with a note, send → «enviada»; `qgen flag --pull` → that question is `needs_work` with the note; second pull empty.
  - new step `report` (always, after `desktop`, before `credits`): URL = `reportUrl` in the unpacked Linux build''s `package.json` (plan 93''s place; fall back to `app/desktop/package.json` if the build ships it unchanged and isn''t there); empty → ✗ "no report URL in the build"; else `urllib.request` `GET <url>/health`, 10 s timeout, expect `{"ok": true, "api": 1}`; ✗ names the URL. `--skip report` until plan 103 task 4 (gamemaster setup), shown in the build Desc like other skips. Docstring step list updated.
- `plans/11-steam.md` "Release checklist (ST-4)": How to run (`report` step, `--skip report` until the server is set up); rows table (`offline` new text, `report` row with exact steps incl. `qgen flag --pull`); Patch variant: one bullet why `report` is full-only (content-only patch ships no client/shell code; server deployed apart via `trivia-report-server deploy`); decision template example rows; `failed` routing: `offline` save/start → plan 87/85; `offline` send/fallback or `report` client side → plan 93; `report` server side (server error, 401 on a real ticket, pull/ack wrong) → plan 103; `report` step ✗ → gamemaster setup (plan 103 task 4) or plan 93; once closed: new task in the plan of the code involved. ST-4 checklist line: "updated 2026-10-13, plan 104" (or the date of the work).
- `plans/18-steam-integration.md` SW-6 step list: `report` step. `AGENTS.md` "Commands" `trivia-release-check` line: `report` step. README "Upload to Steam" only if it lists steps.
- No "Steam off"/"Steam not running" row anywhere (decision 111).

Check (throw-away, nothing kept): `trivia-release-check --skip tag --skip checks --skip licenses --skip quality --skip nix --skip desktop --skip credits --skip smoke --skip manual` with `trivia-report-server dev` running and the URL set via a temporary `reportUrl` (restore the file after) → `report` ✓; server stopped (`kill $!`) → ✗ with the URL; empty URL → ✗ "no report URL"; a `--manual` file answering every row incl. `report` parses; a content-only run lists `report` as "skipped: content-only since <tag>". `grep -rn "Steam not running" authoring plans` finds nothing. Then the usual `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`.', '2026-10-13T17:22:33Z', '2026-10-14T03:24:32Z', 857, 0, NULL, NULL);
