- Tasks for the work, each with a done-when; gamemaster deploy belongs to part 6, not here.', '2026-10-13T17:25:05Z', '2026-10-13T17:27:32Z', 871, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (873, 101, 'write plan: Telemetry recording in the game', 'plan', 'done', 1000, '2026-10-13, plan 106 (tasks.sql only)', 'Write the plan for part 2 of masterplan 14 (plan 101): "Recording in the game". Read plan 101 (ground rules), milestone 14, plan 91 (`buildInfo()`, decision 91, decision 92), plan 87: Steam Cloud saves, decision 102 (additive save shape) and the engine/client save code (`plans/12-client-engine.md`, `app/client`). Create it with `pm plan add 14 "Telemetry recording in the game" --priority 600 < body.md`.

Cover part 2''s list:
- Where events are recorded (per answered question, per game end): engine save transaction or side buffer; additive save shape, no version bump unless needed.
- Install id: random, created on the first yes, stored per install; a "no" deletes buffer and id.
- Session buffer: memory or small local file (cap, drop oldest), so a crash or failed send neither loses nor double-sends; session id for the server''s dedup (match part 1''s contract: if part 1''s plan exists, use its field names).
- Session length, question language, pool hash per game (`loadEngineData(locale).poolHash`); mode, age group/custom range, levels, result, jokers.
- Our questions only: mod/player-bundle question ids not recorded per question.
- Nothing recorded while consent is off (consent storage is part 4''s choice: coordinate, read part 4''s plan if it exists).', '2026-10-13T17:25:05Z', '2026-10-13T17:30:49Z', 871, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (874, 101, 'write plan: Telemetry send from the shell', 'plan', 'done', 1000, '2026-10-13, plan 107 (Telemetry send from the shell), decision recorded', 'Write the plan for part 3 of masterplan 14 (plan 101): "Sending from the shell". Read plan 101 (ground rules), milestone 14, plan 93: Question reports (task 699: `report:send`, `report:available`, `reportUrl`, dev override), plan 103 (dev mode), plan 85 (Steamworks binding, tickets), and the plans for parts 1 and 2 (`pm plans list`; if either doesn''t exist yet, write against plan 101''s text and say so). Create it with `pm plan add 14 "Telemetry send from the shell" --priority 500 < body.md`. Its work waits for task 699 and part 1''s server; say so, don''t duplicate.

Cover part 3''s list:
- `main.mjs`: `telemetry:send` (or one call at close) with a fresh ticket (identity from part 1), timeout, URL from the same base config as `reportUrl`; the page''s request block stays.
- When: `before-quit` (already waits for pending saves); check reliability (Deck sleep, Steam "stop", crash) and fall back to game end or next start if needed; one request per session as the aim.
- Failure silent (dev log only, never bodies or tickets); buffer kept for one later try at most, or dropped (pick, considering server dedup by session id).
- Done-when: against `trivia-report-server dev` an opted-in session arrives; opted out: no request at all (main log).', '2026-10-13T17:25:05Z', '2026-10-13T17:33:09Z', 871, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (875, 101, 'write plan: Telemetry consent UI and privacy texts', 'plan', 'done', 1000, '2026-10-13, plan 108 (Telemetry consent UI and privacy texts), decision 121', 'Write the plan for part 4 of masterplan 14 (plan 101): "Consent UI and privacy texts". Read plan 101 (ground rules), milestone 14, plan 87: Steam Cloud saves, plan 103 task 867 (PRIVACY.md, store text), `LanguageScreen.svelte`, `Overlay.svelte`, and the answered decisions on UI wording (`pm decision list --answered --grep wording --grep style`). Create it with `pm plan add 14 "Telemetry consent UI and privacy texts" --priority 400 < body.md`.

Cover part 4''s list:
- First-start question (default off, focus on «No») after the language screen for a fresh save, once for existing saves without an answer; keyboard, mouse, pad.
- Esc menu on/off (general part of `Overlay.svelte`) with a line saying what is sent.
- Where the answer lives (save per Steam user / Steam Cloud vs. per install): pick one, state why; part 2 reads it. If it''s a real judgement call the human must make, `pm decision add` instead of guessing.
