- Privacy: extend `PRIVACY.md` and the store text from task 867 (what is sent, kept, how long, how to turn off); the opt-in screen''s short text derives from it.', '2026-10-13T17:25:06Z', '2026-10-13T17:34:50Z', 871, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (876, 101, 'write plan: Played vs. rated difficulty in qgen report', 'plan', 'done', 1000, '2026-10-13, plan 109 (tasks.sql), decision 122', 'Write the plan for part 5 of masterplan 14 (plan 101): "Played vs. rated difficulty in `qgen report`". Read plan 101 (ground rules), milestone 14, part 1''s plan (API contract; if missing, write against plan 101 and say so), plan 93 (`qgen flag --pull`, `TRIVIA_REPORT_TOKEN` / `state/report-token`), `app/data/age-groups.json`, D-81 (per-locale difficulty), the `qgen report` code and `/review`. Create it with `pm plan add 14 "Played vs. rated difficulty in qgen report" --priority 600 < body.md`.

Cover part 5''s list:
- Pull command (e.g. `qgen telemetry --pull`): fetch with the pull token, store under gitignored `state/` (public repo: no raw player data in git), ack.
- Report (e.g. `qgen report --played`): per question and age group: count, right rate, observed vs. rated difficulty, minimum sample size; per level/age group summaries; session stats.
- Outliers → review candidates: a list plus a way into `/review` (filter or `needs_work` with a «Datos de juego» note; pick one; never runs `qgen rework` unasked).
