INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (886, 106, 'Shell: telemetry store (install.json, session file, IPC)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/telemetry.mjs (new), app/desktop/main.mjs, app/desktop/preload.cjs, app/client/src/lib/desktop.ts, plans/18-steam-integration.md, directory.md', 'Plan 106, task 1. The shell side of opt-in telemetry recording: consent + install id per install and one session buffer file per app run; no network (plan 107 sends). Follow plan 106 "Install id and consent storage", "Session buffer" and "Bridge" exactly. Binding: decision 119: Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file; decision 121: Telemetry consent: stored per install, not in the save; decision 111: Steam only.

## What
- New `app/desktop/telemetry.mjs`:
  - folder `T`: `TRIVIA_TELEMETRY_DIR`, else packaged `<userData>/telemetry` (sibling of `save/`, outside Auto-Cloud), dev `state/telemetry`
  - `T/install.json`: `{"consent": true, "install": "<uuid v4>"}` / `{"consent": false}` / missing = never asked; `setConsent(true)` creates the id if missing (`crypto.randomUUID()`); `setConsent(false)` writes `{"consent": false}` and deletes `T/sessions/`
  - session per run: at start with consent yes (or on a mid-run yes) `session = crypto.randomUUID()`, writes `T/sessions/<session>.json` with `games: []`, `index: []`
  - `record({games, index})`: stamps `session`, `install`, `version` (`app.getVersion()`), `length_s` (`Math.round(process.uptime())`, cap 86400); atomic `.tmp` + rename through its own queue (pattern of `save.mjs` / `queued()`); refuses without a stored yes
  - rollover when a write would exceed 30 games, 500 answers or 60 KiB serialized: close the file, new session id, the games that didn''t fit go there; per game the first 100 answers kept
  - ≤ 5 files in `T/sessions/` (count every `*.json`, incl. plan 107''s `<session>.retry.json`); on a new session the oldest by mtime deleted
  - exports `pending()` (list + read of leftover files) for plan 107; no IPC for it
  - a final `length_s` stamp exported for `before-quit`
- `main.mjs`: `validUser` gate (without one every telemetry IPC is a no-op, `state` → `{consent: null, available: false}`, no folder created); `before-quit` waits for the telemetry queue too and does the last `length_s` stamp; IPC `telemetry:state|consent|load|record` behind `bridge()`''s origin check; arguments validated (plain objects, size).
- `preload.cjs`: `telemetry.state()`, `setConsent(yes)`, `load()` (current session''s `{games, index}` or null), `record({games, index})`.
- `app/client/src/lib/desktop.ts`: optional `telemetry` on the bridge type.
- No logging of ids or bodies.

## Check
Throw-away script or `trivia-desktop` with `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, `TRIVIA_TELEMETRY_DIR` in `/tmp`:
- no `install.json` → no `sessions/` written
- `setConsent(true)` → id created, one session file per run with `games: []`, `length_s` grows
- `setConsent(false)` → `sessions/` gone, no id
- six runs → five files
- no valid user → nothing under `T`
- per-commit checks (AGENTS.md)

## Docs
- `plans/18-steam-integration.md` IPC list
- `directory.md`: `app/desktop/telemetry.mjs`, `state/telemetry/`', '2026-10-13T17:40:48Z', '2026-10-13T19:42:58Z', 879, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (887, 106, 'Page: telemetry recording from the save', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/client/src/engine/telemetry.ts, app/client/src/lib/telemetry.ts, app/client/src/lib/engine.ts, plans/12-client-engine.md', 'Plan 106, task 2, after task 886 (shell telemetry store). The page derives this run''s telemetry games from the save after every action and hands them to the shell; the save''s shape doesn''t change. Follow plan 106 "What a game becomes" and "Bridge" exactly. Binding: decision 119: Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file; decision 121: Telemetry consent: stored per install, not in the save; plan 105''s contract (v1) field names and limits.

## What
- `app/client/src/engine/telemetry.ts` (pure): save rows + `index` + data lookup → contract games
  - session''s games: rows started this run (`from` 0) and the game running at load (`from` = its history length at load); key `<game id>@<started_on>`, first record fixes `from` in `index`
  - per game: `mode`, `locale` (`gameLocale(row)`), `pool` (`loadEngineData(locale).poolHash`), `age_group`/`difficulty` (`gameChoice()`, exactly one non-null), `levels`, `reached`, `result` (`"open"` while running), `customized`, `mods: false`, `jokers` (counts over `history[from..]` + `state.jokers`, zeros kept for the five `STANDARD_JOKERS`)
  - per answer: `history[from..]` entries with `correct`; `question` only if `^q-\d{4,6}$` and in a shipped bundle (`data.bundles`; the one spot milestone 15 extends); `level` in 1–`levels` else skipped; `jokers` counts (`{}` when none); first 100 per game
  - never: names, player/game ids, dates, flags, notes, text
- `app/client/src/lib/telemetry.ts`: consent cache (`telemetry.state()` once per page load and on a setter call, for plan 108), `loadEngineData` per game locale for the pool hash, `load()` on page start to recover `index`, `record()` calls; no bridge (browser game, dev shim) or consent not `true` → builder never runs, no IPC; errors to the dev console only
- checkpoint in `lib/engine.ts`: `exec()` after a successful `run()` adopts its save, once in `load()`; fire-and-forget, never awaited by the UI

## Check
`trivia-desktop`, `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, `TRIVIA_TELEMETRY_DIR` in `/tmp`, consent set by hand in `install.json` (or the plan 108 UI if it exists):
- a solo game won + a gamemaster game lost → session file (minus `index`) validates against plan 105''s `report-server/src/validate-telemetry.ts` if it exists, else a throw-away script against the contract (fields, caps, one non-null of `age_group`/`difficulty`, answers only `q-NNNN`)
- a jokered question carries its counts; an undone answer disappears
- quit mid-game → `result: "open"`; restart and finish → only the new answers in the new session
- consent off → file untouched, no `record` IPC call
- save file shape unchanged (no `SAVE_VERSION` bump)
- per-commit checks (AGENTS.md)

## Docs
- `plans/12-client-engine.md`: short section "Telemetry recording" (derived from the save, side file, no save change, consent gate)', '2026-10-13T17:40:48Z', '2026-10-13T19:53:17Z', 879, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (888, 107, 'Shell: telemetry send at quit and next start', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, app/desktop/{main,report,telemetry}.mjs, plans/18-steam-integration.md, directory.md. reportUrl already was the base (task 699): reportTarget got a route param; shared withTicket (2 s ticket timeout, reports too) + postJson. Checked vs trivia-report-server dev (TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1, TRIVIA_TELEMETRY_DIR in /tmp): play+quit → 201, file gone; first try hit 429 (stale dev telemetry_rate rows) → .retry.json → next start 30.6 s → 201; port closed → 0 kept, hanging server → quit 4.1 s, kept; kill -9 → next start sends result open; resend acked → 200 dropped; SIGTERM reaches before-quit by itself (sent at quit, no handler added); consent false / no install.json → ''telemetry off'', no request in the server log. Report send re-checked (201, dev-invalid 401). Per-commit checks pass.', 'Implement plan 107 ("Send" and "When" sections) in `app/desktop/telemetry.mjs` + `main.mjs`. Binding: decision 120: Telemetry send: at quit, one later try at the next start; decision 119: Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file; decision 121: Telemetry consent: stored per install, not in the save; decision 111: Steam only.

## Runs after (wait if open, don''t duplicate)
- task 699: Shell: report ticket and send (report:available, report:send)
- task 884: Telemetry server: routes, migration and validation
- task 886: Shell: telemetry store (install.json, session file, IPC)

## Do
- Gate per send: `validUser`, `install.json` consent `true`, non-empty URL; closed → no ticket, no request, no file read beyond `install.json`; one start log line `trivia: telemetry off`.
- Body: session file parsed, `index` removed, `install` from current `install.json`, `ticket` added; > 64 KiB serialized → delete unsent; unreadable JSON → delete, dev log.
- Shared ticket + fetch helper with the report send (identity and path as parameters; factor out of task 699''s code if inlined); identity constant `trivia-telemetry` next to the reports'' one; fresh ticket per request, cancelled after the response; 2 s callback timeout → status 0; dev switch without SteamID → `dev-<random>`.
- URL: `reportUrl` in `app/desktop/package.json` = base; main appends `/reports` and `/telemetry`; if task 699 stored the full `/reports` URL, turn it into the base and adjust the report send. Same dev override `TRIVIA_REPORT_URL`.
- Answers: `201`, `200 duplicate`, `400`, `413`, `415`, `503` → delete; `401`, `429`, `500`, `502`, status 0 → rename to `<session>.retry.json` (still in `pending()` and the 5-file cap); at the later try any answer → delete.
- Quit: first `before-quit` with gate open and a current session file → `preventDefault()`, hide window, wait for save queue + telemetry queue (last `length_s` stamp), send, `app.quit()` again with `flushed` flag; 4 s budget for ticket + request, timeout → status 0 → `.retry.json`. Sessions with `games: []` are sent too.
- `SIGTERM`: check whether Electron routes it through `before-quit`; if not, `process.on("SIGTERM", () => app.quit())`.
- Next start: once, 30 s after window load, gate open: every `pending()` file except the current session''s, oldest first, one at a time, 5 s connect + 10 s total; then delete whatever the answer.
- Silent: nothing to the player or the page; no new IPC, no new dependency. Dev log one `console.error` per request: `trivia: telemetry → <status>` + `kept`/`dropped`; never body, ticket, session/install id, URL query, SteamID.

## Check
`trivia-report-server dev` + `trivia-desktop`, `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, `TRIVIA_REPORT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787`, `TRIVIA_TELEMETRY_DIR` in `/tmp`:
- consent yes, play one question, quit → `GET /telemetry` (pull token) shows the session with its game, file gone, log `→ 201`
- server down at quit → `.retry.json` kept, quit ≤ 4 s; next start with server up → sent after ~30 s, file gone
- `kill -9` mid-game → next start sends it with `result: "open"`
- `kill -TERM` → sent at quit (or record Electron ignores it and the handler fixes it)
- resend of an acked session → `200 duplicate`, file gone
- consent off or no `install.json` → log `telemetry off`, no `telemetry →` line, dev server log shows no request
- Per-commit checks (AGENTS.md).

## Docs
