INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (946, 111, 'No stale files across updates: cache-control and the two-build check', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/resolve.mjs (cache-control: no-cache for client and mod-overlay files), plans/18-steam-integration.md (Builds and depots: stale client files finding). Check: fresh --user-data-dir, stamps appended to built main.js and game/Game.svelte.js, CDP read per start; A,A,B,C without the header and D,D,E,F with it: every start ran the current bytes. HTTP cache held no app:// entry (only a spellcheck .bdic: follow-up task 1003); no ses.clearCache() needed. Per-commit checks pass.', 'Plan 111 task 3. Without hashes, a cached old module could mix with new ones after an update.

- `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` `sendFile`: add `cache-control: no-cache` for `dist` (client) responses; media/data unchanged unless the check says otherwise.
- Check: build A, start `trivia-desktop`, rebuild with a visibly changed module, start again: the new code runs. Try with and without the header if needed to learn whether Chromium caches `app://` (`protocol.handle`) responses at all; also V8''s code cache (should invalidate on changed bytes). The session lives in `userData` across runs.
- Only if stale code shows despite the header: clear the session cache at start (`ses.clearCache()`) when the build id changed (`__APP_VERSION__` from `app/desktop/package.json`, decision 91/92, plus a build stamp written by `vite.config.ts`), stamp stored in `userData`. No version-keyed URLs (they break override paths).

