INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (962, 115, 'Save, authoring and telemetry ignore mod ids; removed-mod check', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, authoring/tools/save_file.py, app/client/src/engine/telemetry.ts. save_file.py drops '':'' ids in _seen_blocked() and flags(); qgen.py, overview.py and main.py read the save only through it. Telemetry ourQuestion() uses isOurs (OUR_ID regex removed). parseSave unchanged, no SAVE_VERSION bump. Throw-away engine script: base mod bundle game, seen m:y-1-4, blocked m:y-2-4, open on m:y-2-2; mod removed: save parses with ids kept; repair() (plan 91) puts the open game back to select with our cards and it plays to won; player''s stored choice falls back to [base]; a new game plays; no engine fix needed. Test v4 save with mod seen/blocked/flag + q-0001: qgen validate OK, qgen report no mod ids, authoring overview blocked 0 / seen_once 1, flags() empty. Temp script and save copy deleted, real state/game.json restored (cmp). check, test, build, qgen validate pass.', 'Plan 115, task 4 (after task 3 of this plan). Binding: decision 128 ('':'' marks "not ours"); decision 38 (stored choices that no longer resolve read as the defaults); milestone 15 constraint: player content never enters our pool, seen counts, flags, reports.

