INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (963, 115, 'Docs: player bundles (mods) and /data/ rules; decisions 128, 129', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, plans/22-bundles.md (Player bundles (mods)), plans/18-steam-integration.md (Modding: /data/ rules), directory.md (app/desktop, bundles, mods/ rows); consequences on decisions 128, 129', 'Plan 115, task 5 (last). Docs style: AGENTS.md (bullets, ultra-concise).

## What
- `plans/22-bundles.md`: section "Player bundles (mods)": format (`<mod>/data/bundles.json`, `data/bundles/<id>/`), namespacing `<mod id>:<id>`, the merge, kinds and defaults (pack off on configure, on in solo; base mod bundle as a second base choice), media (relative paths, rewritten to `/data/bundles/<mod>:<id>/…`), credits, `modIssues()` codes; cite decision 128 and decision 129.
- `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Modding": `/data/` rules (merged `bundles.json`, namespaced bundle folders, no other `/data/` overlay).
- `directory.md`: where it names `bundles.json` / the mod layout.
- `pm decision consequences 128 "…"` and `pm decision consequences 129 "…"`: what changed, with file paths.

## Done when
- Docs name decisions 128/129 and the paths; per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-13T18:31:54Z', '2026-10-13T20:13:31Z', 935, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (964, 116, 'Game.svelte: one component per screen in game/screens/', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13: app/client/src/game/screens/ (Start, Level, Select, Correct, Wrong, Victory new; Player, Choice moved, LanguageScreen → Language), new shared widgets game/AnswerPanel.svelte (answer + fun fact on Correct/Wrong/Victory), game/CornerButtons.svelte (corner error line, flag and menu buttons), game/Veil.svelte (transition veil: black/rewind), Game.svelte (controller + {#if} chain; Stage, .corner-hud and .side-tray stay in it), timing.ts comment. Game.svelte is 670 lines, not ~500: the script (~540) is exactly what plan 116 keeps in the controller (go, act/request, overlay actions, flag handling, input scopes, presence); nothing further moves without spreading the state machine. Veil moved to its own widget rather than staying in Game.svelte/theme.css (not shared with any screen, only its CSS moved). CSS order: in the readable build every component CSS loads before theme.css (only Game.svelte.css after it), so the Level/Victory ''.big'' became ''.title.big'' to keep beating ''.game .title'' on font-size. Checks: npm run check, npm test, npm run build, qgen validate pass. Visual: CDP screenshots via trivia-desktop of language, start, player (new/known), choice, greeting, level 1/2 (block drop)/12, select, question, correct, wrong, victory before vs after: identical apart from random content. Keys: Enter through start/player/choice/level/correct, 1 on select, Esc opens the overlay. Smoke: authoring/steam/smoke.mjs fails at ''mode'' on old and new builds alike (no TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER, save/local path), already covered by task 786: Smoke game under the dev switch; a temporary copy with the dev switch and save/dev played levels 1-3 (image, audio, video), quit and restart, then hit the stale resume selector known in task 786 (same on the old build). Pad not tested (no pad under Xvfb); scopes unchanged in the controller. For tasks 904/909: screen list = game/screens/*.', 'Plan 116, part 1. Split `app/client/src/game/Game.svelte` (1082 lines) into a thin controller plus one component per screen. No behaviour or visual change. Runs after task 944 (readable build; paths follow decision 124: Readable client build: output naming rule for mod overrides).

## What
- New `app/client/src/game/screens/`: `Start.svelte` (wordmark, resume/new/play, save notice, `SupplyReport`, fireworks/effects preview), `Level.svelte` (tower, kicker, milestone line), `Select.svelte` (envelopes), `Correct.svelte`, `Wrong.svelte` (consolation), `Victory.svelte`; markup + CSS taken from `Game.svelte`''s `{#if screen === …}` branches.
- `git mv` `game/Player.svelte`, `game/Choice.svelte` → `game/screens/`, `game/LanguageScreen.svelte` → `game/screens/Language.svelte`; fix imports.
- `Game.svelte` keeps the controller and the `{#if}` chain mounting one screen each.

## Rules (plan 116)
- Controller keeps the state: `screen`, `go` (transitions, veil, `busy`), `act`/`request`, overlay and flag handling, music per screen, rich presence, `listen`/`listenPads`, the top input scope. Don''t spread one state machine over files (`code-review.md`, `engine/game.ts` row).
- Props down, callbacks up (`onstart`, `onback`, …); no new store, no context API; no new dependencies (decision 106: Adopt ESLint + typescript-eslint for no-floating-promises?).
- CSS moves with its markup; shared rules (`.corner-hud`, `.side-tray`, black veil, transitions) stay in `Game.svelte` or `theme.css`.
- Small shared widgets (`Hud`, `Prompt`, `Icon`, `JokerTray`, `Tower`, …) stay in `game/`.
- Sizes: controller ≤ ~500 lines incl. style; a screen ≤ ~300. A piece needing > ~5 callbacks/setters stays in the controller: say so in the done note.
- `PLACEHOLDER(<task id>)` markers, `t()` keys, `data-focus-*` attributes and `check-literals.mjs` `SCREENS` keep working (keys per screen name, not file).
- Code comments naming `Game.svelte` for moved parts (`swap.ts`, `timing.ts`, `lib/input.svelte.ts`, `lib/gamepad.svelte.ts`) point at the new file.
- Visual check: screen gallery (`trivia-gallery`, plan 100) before/after if it exists, else screenshots by hand of the same states.

## Done when
- `Game.svelte` ≤ ~500 lines; every screen looks and behaves as before (keys, pad, mouse; transitions, music, block drop on Level after Correct, envelope deal, victory fireworks).
- Per-commit checks pass (`npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`).
- Smoke game: `trivia-desktop-build --dir`, then `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` (or `trivia-release-check --skip tag` limited to its smoke step).
- Manual game in `trivia-desktop` (`TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`): start → player → choice → level → select → question → correct/wrong → victory (Esc menu «Ir a pregunta…» to reach level 12).', '2026-10-13T18:32:39Z', '2026-10-13T23:27:41Z', 936, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (965, 116, 'Question.svelte: move to screens/, pieces in game/question/', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13: app/client/src/game/screens/Question.svelte (moved, controller: state, timers, input scopes question/armed/snipe, joker flow; 479 lines), new app/client/src/game/question/: Media.svelte (backdrop, audio, mark, credit, UI-7 ready/settle, failed bindable, ready()/replay()/pause(), media volume, music off on mount), Card.svelte (card, topic, replay, notes, media-missing), Answers.svelte (tiles, badges, shards, pad glyphs; LETTERS; bind:tiles), FinalAnswer.svelte, SkipDialog.svelte (own modal scope ''question-skip''), Scope.svelte (hole computed from the target tile, aim/hit lines, markup only), reveal.ts (answerClass, answerBadge from an AnswerView); Game.svelte import and comment. Joker flow (press, fire, fly, snipe, shredder, sweep) stays in Question.svelte: it sets ~10 state fields (armed, mode, target, jokerBusy, flight, popping, shot, hit, shattering, shredding, sweeping), over the ~5 callback rule. Media sits last in the screen''s DOM (backdrop z-index -1, credit keeps painting over the footer as before); .dark moved from the screen root to the backdrop, sweeping is a prop on Card plus the footer rule in the controller; arrive/shake/pop keyframes copied per piece (components keep their own variants, theme.css). Checks: npm run check, npm test, npm run build, qgen validate pass. Visual: CDP screenshots in trivia-desktop (dev user, --no-mods) before vs after: audio, video, long, decorative, missing media (blocked /media), image, lock shaking/ready, unlock, Soplo armed/note, Francotirador aim/arrow move/cancel/miss shatter/hit, Paso dialog/plain/purge shredder, Cambiazo picker/pick, final waiting (dark backdrop)/reveal, overlay pause (no reveal while open); identical apart from the random answer order. Bájale with the dial checked at level 6. Smoke: trivia-desktop-build --dir + smoke.mjs fails at ''mode'' as known (task 786: Smoke game under the dev switch (TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER)); a temp copy with the dev switch plays levels 1-3 (image, audio, video) and stops at the known resume step. Pad not tested (no pad under Xvfb); scopes and pad maps unchanged. Comments in swap.ts, timing.ts, lib/input.svelte.ts, lib/gamepad.svelte.ts don''t name Question.svelte; docs/directory.md left to task 966: Split of Game/Question: docs, paths and open task bodies.', 'Plan 116, part 2. After the `Game.svelte` split (previous task in plan 116). Move `app/client/src/game/Question.svelte` (1243 lines) to `game/screens/Question.svelte` and split its markup + CSS + local logic into pieces in `game/question/`. No behaviour or visual change.

## What
- `git mv game/Question.svelte game/screens/Question.svelte`; fix imports (`Game.svelte`, others).
- New `app/client/src/game/question/`:
  - `Media.svelte`: backdrop picture/video, audio element, decorative mark, ready/settle (UI-7), `mediaFailed`, replay, media volume; exposes `ready()` and `replay()`; the credit line.
  - `Card.svelte`: question card (topic, text, long-question step, replay button), hints notes, media-missing line.
  - `Answers.svelte`: the four tiles (classes, badges, shards, pad glyphs, snipe hover); hands `tiles` back for the scope/hole.
  - `FinalAnswer.svelte`: final button, padlock, waiting/error lines.
  - `SkipDialog.svelte`: Paso (plain/purge/cancel); own modal scope, as `CategoryPicker.svelte` does.
  - `Scope.svelte`: Francotirador hole + aim/hit hints (markup only; the snipe input scope stays in `Question.svelte`: it relies on Question''s `KEYS` for A–D aim, `code-review.md` row `lib/input.svelte.ts`).
- Reveal: the submit → wait → sweep → reveal sequence stays in `Question.svelte`; a pure helper that falls out (e.g. `answerClass` as a function of state) goes to `question/reveal.ts`.
- Joker flow (`press`, `fire`, flight, shredder, snipe animation) stays in `Question.svelte` unless it moves cleanly to `question/jokers.ts` (≤ ~5 callbacks).

## Rules (plan 116)
- `Question.svelte` keeps the state: `locked`/`finalReady`/`submitted`/`revealed`/`result`, joker `armed`/`mode`/`fire`, timers, its input scopes (question, armed, snipe).
- Props down, callbacks up; no new store, no context API, no new dependencies (decision 106).
- CSS moves with its markup; shared rules stay in the controller or `theme.css`.
- Sizes: `screens/Question.svelte` ≤ ~500 lines incl. style; a piece ≤ ~300. A piece needing > ~5 callbacks/setters stays in the controller: say so in the done note.
- `PLACEHOLDER(<task id>)` markers, `t()` keys, `data-focus-*` attributes, `check-literals.mjs` `SCREENS` keep working.
- Code comments naming `Question.svelte` (`swap.ts`, `timing.ts`, `lib/input.svelte.ts`, `lib/gamepad.svelte.ts`) point at the new file.
- Visual check before/after: screen gallery (plan 100) if built, else screenshots by hand.

## Done when
- `screens/Question.svelte` ≤ ~500 lines.
- Works as before: image, audio, video and missing-media questions; lock/unlock, final answer, reveal; every joker (Soplo, Paso both options, Bájale with the dial, Cambiazo with picker and shredder, Francotirador aim/shoot/cancel with keys, pad, mouse); overlay pause during the wait.
- Per-commit checks pass; smoke game (`trivia-desktop-build --dir` + `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs`); manual game in `trivia-desktop` (`TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1`, Esc menu «Ir a pregunta…»).', '2026-10-13T18:32:39Z', '2026-10-14T00:04:08Z', 936, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (966, 116, 'Split of Game/Question: docs, paths and open task bodies', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13: directory.md (game/screens/, game/question/ rows), plans/04, 05, 09, 10, backlog (moved paths), plans/18-steam-integration.md ''Modding: module paths'' (screen list bullet for task 904, task 909), code-review.md part 5 line; open task bodies 652, 742, 780, 890, 922, 970, 974, 981 updated; Game.svelte refs left where still current (controller)', 'Plan 116, part 3. After the two split tasks of plan 116 (`game/screens/`, `game/question/`). Bring docs and open pm tasks in line with the new paths.

