INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (987, 121, 'Example mods: theme, rules tweak, minimal full conversion', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, modding/examples/{theme,rules-tweak,conversion}/ (mod.json, README.md, style.css / main.js / index.html+main.js); checked: --check-mod exit 0 each; dev shell under Xvfb with temp TRIVIA_MODS_DIR + dev user: theme palette, solo hint 3→4 (gamemaster numbers +1, unlimited kept), reworded joker.hint.rule, game:end log, all four incl. template-bundle active without errors, conversion replaces the game with /fonts/ fall-through, quits on Esc and pad B, --no-mods back to our game', 'Part of plan 121 (milestone 15). Three example mods modders can copy as is; the bundle example is `modding/template-bundle/` (plan 120), referenced, not copied (decision 134: Modding guide: path, language, examples).

Runs after plan 117 (code add-ons, `window.trivia`), plan 118 task 1 (mods screen) and plan 120 task 3 (template bundle). Check every API name against the code as built (`grep` in `app/`), not against plans.

## What
All in `modding/examples/`, each with `mod.json` (`game` = current version from `app/package.json` or wherever the loader reads it, `languages` where text exists) and a 3-line `README.md` (what it shows, which guide section of `modding/README.md`). No media, no network, no build step: plain JS/CSS/HTML; MIT (decision 107).
