INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (995, 115, 'Remove the mod taxonomy_clash check', 'work', 'done', 290, '2026-10-14, app/client/src/lib/data.ts, app/desktop/check-mod.mjs, modding/bundles.md, plans/22-bundles.md: taxonomy_clash removed from loader and --check-mod (decision 110 d, D-100); throw-away mod with slug comida-bebida and subcategory «Navidad» passes --check-mod and loads in trivia-desktop: offered by fetchChoiceOptions, no modIssues, its questions under its own bundle''s category', 'After `task 826: Bundle-scoped taxonomy (decision 110 d)` (priority 290 puts it after 826''s 300; if 826 is still open, leave this task alone).

Task 960 added a stopgap: names repeated across bundles weren''t allowed before bundle-scoped taxonomy, so a mod bundle whose category slug or subcategory name clashes with an earlier bundle''s is left out with issue `taxonomy_clash`.

- Remove the check in `app/client/src/lib/data.ts` `load()`: the `// Until task 826 …` line and the `slugs`/`subs` sets that feed it (also their `.add` lines after `modPool`)
- Drop `taxonomy_clash` from `ModIssue["code"]` in the same file
- Make sure a mod bundle whose subcategory is named like one of ours («Historia») loads and its questions sit in its own category (decision 110 d)
- Done when: npm test, check, build pass; a throw-away mod with a clashing name loads (configure screen offers it)

Also (found by task 826: Bundle-scoped taxonomy (decision 110 d), which keys subcategories by bundle + name, D-100):
- `app/desktop/check-mod.mjs` has the same clash check (`slugs`/`subs` sets, `taxonomy_clash` error and its message); drop it so `--check-mod` agrees with the loader
- `modding/bundles.md`: drop "must differ from the game''s own and from other mods''" and `taxonomy_clash` from the error list; names only need to be unique within the mod''s bundle
- `plans/22-bundles.md` `modIssues()` line: drop `taxonomy_clash`', '2026-10-13T20:01:53Z', '2026-10-14T21:32:18Z', 960, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (996, 123, 'create tasks for plan 123: Silent game for agents: muted by default under PM_WORKER, opt-in sound', 'split', 'done', 1000, '2026-10-13, tasks 997-999 (no files)', 'Split plan 123 into tasks and identify all decisions that need to be made. If the plan already has tasks,
bring them in line with the plan. A task that writes a plan gets `--kind plan`.', '2026-10-13T20:13:33Z', '2026-10-13T20:14:57Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (997, 123, 'Mute rule and muted trivia-desktop under PM_WORKER; muted smoke game', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/mute.mjs (muteReason), main.mjs (setAudioMuted + stderr line), electron-builder.yml, authoring/steam/smoke.mjs (TRIVIA_MUTE=1, decision 138), AGENTS.md, directory.md, plans/18-steam-integration.md; follow-up task 1000', 'Part 1 of `plan 123: Silent game for agents: muted by default under PM_WORKER, opt-in sound`: the desktop shell, the shared env rule, the packaged smoke game and the docs that tell agents.

- Env rule, one small module both the shell and the Vite plugin can import (e.g. `app/desktop/mute.mjs`, next to `resolve.mjs`): `muteReason(env)` → `"TRIVIA_SOUND"`-override → `null`; else `"PM_WORKER"` if set, `"TRIVIA_MUTE"` if `TRIVIA_MUTE=1`, else `null`.
- `app/desktop/main.mjs`: if muted, `win.webContents.setAudioMuted(true)` on the main window (effects, music and question media all go through it); one stderr line at start, like the other dev lines: `trivia desktop: muted (PM_WORKER)` / `(TRIVIA_MUTE)`. Nothing written to `trivia.volumes` (`app/client/src/game/sound.svelte.ts`); the Esc-menu volume UI unchanged. No env: sound as today.
- `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` (release check step 6): it runs with `env -i`, so `PM_WORKER` doesn''t reach the shell. It checks media load (`readyState`), not audibility; sound is a manual row. So run it muted: add `TRIVIA_MUTE=1` to its env list, with a short comment; record it with `pm decision record` ("smoke game muted: checks load, not audio; sound is the manual row"). If you find it does check audio, keep it audible and record that instead.
- Docs:
  - AGENTS.md Rules: game is muted under `PM_WORKER`; outside pm, launch with `TRIVIA_MUTE=1` unless the work is about sound; `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` for sound checks. Commands: `trivia-desktop` line names `TRIVIA_MUTE=1` / `TRIVIA_SOUND=1`.
  - `plans/18-steam-integration.md`: dev switches (near «Valid Steam user» / «Dev mode») get the mute rule.
- Done when: `PM_WORKER=1 trivia-desktop` prints the muted line and is silent; `TRIVIA_SOUND=1 PM_WORKER=1 trivia-desktop` plays; a plain start plays; `trivia.volumes` unchanged after a muted run; per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-13T20:14:54Z', '2026-10-13T20:17:19Z', 996, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (998, 123, 'Dev server and vite preview: mute rule passed to the page (session-only mute in the client)', 'work', 'done', 440, '2026-10-13, app/client/devserver.ts (muteReason from app/desktop/mute.mjs, ''trivia dev: muted (PM_WORKER)'', shim gets triviaShell.muted), devshell.js, src/lib/desktop.ts (muted?), src/game/sound.svelte.ts (session mute: shim flag or ?mute → master gain 0, mediaVolume 0, never stored), AGENTS.md, plans/18-steam-integration.md. Checked: throw-away Playwright on vite and vite preview: PM_WORKER=1 → master 0/media 0; TRIVIA_SOUND=1 → 1/1; ?mute without env → 0/0; trivia.volumes stores user values with muted:false', 'Part 2 of `plan 123: Silent game for agents: muted by default under PM_WORKER, opt-in sound`. Runs after `task 762: Node dev server for browser checks (Vite plugin, save shim, temp save dir)` (priority 440 < 450); if 762 is still open when you start, stop and leave this task open (say so in a `pm task set` note in the body) rather than building the dev server here.

- The dev server''s Vite plugin (task 762, `app/client/`), in `vite` and `vite preview`: apply the env rule from the module of the previous task (`muteReason`, e.g. `app/desktop/mute.mjs`; `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` overrides `PM_WORKER` / `TRIVIA_MUTE=1`); print `trivia dev: muted (PM_WORKER)` or similar at start; pass it to the page via the dev shim marker on `window.triviaShell` (e.g. `muted: true`). Also honour `?mute` in the URL in any build (cheap; lets a check mute a page by hand).
- Client: a session-only mute in `app/client/src/game/sound.svelte.ts`: master gain 0 and `mediaVolume()` 0 while it''s on, without touching `sound.volumes` or `trivia.volumes` in localStorage; `setVolumes` still stores what the user sets. The Esc-menu volume UI unchanged. Not in the production bundle''s behaviour unless `?mute` is given (desktop uses `setAudioMuted`, no client flag).
- Docs: AGENTS.md dev server line says it is muted under `PM_WORKER` (`TRIVIA_SOUND=1` to hear); `plans/18-steam-integration.md` dev switches in sync.
- Done when: a `PM_WORKER=1` dev server page and `vite preview` page are silent (throw-away Playwright check: master gain 0 / media volume 0); with `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` they play; stored volumes unchanged after a muted run; per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-13T20:14:54Z', '2026-10-14T04:21:48Z', 996, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (999, 123, 'Name TRIVIA_SOUND=1 in open sound plans and tasks', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, tasks.sql only: TRIVIA_SOUND=1 line in task 146 and task 149 (re-check after feedback) and task 844 (trailer shell records game audio). Plans 32/33 not edited (task bodies suffice). Decisions 81/83: gamemaster listens, no change. Others (238 gamemaster checklist, 964/965 refactors, 745, Freesound tasks) start no game to hear audio: unchanged.', 'Part 3 of `plan 123: Silent game for agents: muted by default under PM_WORKER, opt-in sound`: under `PM_WORKER` the game is muted (previous tasks); work that must hear or measure audio has to opt in with `TRIVIA_SOUND=1`.

- Find open plans and tasks about sound/music/audio/media playback (`pm plans list`, `pm queue`, `pm show p<id>`; at least `plan 32: Recorded sound effects (UI-10)` with `task 146: Gamemaster check of the recorded effects on the TV`, `plan 33: Recorded music loops (UI-10)` with tasks 149, 150, and any release-check / smoke-game task that checks audio).
- Where a worker would start the game to check audio (e.g. applying the gamemaster''s feedback and re-checking an effect), add one line to the body with `pm task set <id> --body -`: «launch with `TRIVIA_SOUND=1` (muted under PM_WORKER otherwise)». Running or closed tasks: leave alone. Plan bodies only if they still have open tasks and the line fits; `pm plan edit` requeues a split, so prefer task bodies.
- Pending decisions 81 and 83 (`decision 81: Recorded sound effects: approve on the TV?`, `decision 83: Recorded music loops: approve on the TV?`): the gamemaster listens, no `PM_WORKER`: check their text; change nothing unless it tells an agent to listen.
- Done when: every open audio task names the opt-in; nothing else changed.', '2026-10-13T20:14:54Z', '2026-10-13T20:18:58Z', 996, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1000, 107, 'Package telemetry.mjs in the desktop builds', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, no change: telemetry.mjs already in app/desktop/electron-builder.yml files: (task 947); checked: trivia-desktop-build --dir, app.asar has telemetry.mjs, packaged main.mjs loads (smoke reaches mode; its no_user stop is task 786)', '`app/desktop/main.mjs` imports `./telemetry.mjs` (task 886: Shell: telemetry store), but `app/desktop/electron-builder.yml` `files:` lists each shell module by name and doesn''t list `telemetry.mjs`. A packaged build (`trivia-desktop-build`) then fails to load `main.mjs`.
