INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1001, 82, 'Purge ''gamemaster'' as a name for the human in docs and code', 'work', 'done', 950, '2026-10-13, AGENTS.md (rule + line 32), authoring/RUNBOOK.md, QC.md, prompts (audit, house-style, review, revise), reports/batches.md, README.md, directory.md, code-review.md, plans/*.md, qgen.py, health.py, layout.py, patch_notes.py, steam/release_check.py, Home.svelte, Question.svelte, sound.svelte.ts. Kept (in-game sense): AGENTS.md:3, README.md:3, house-style.md:3, plans'' ''against the gamemaster''/''without a gamemaster'', the Start screen/block/joker budget lines in plans 03 and project.md. Doubtful: audit.md ''embarrass the gamemaster on game night'' kept as host; plans/00-vision.md and README ''(the author)'' kept; authoring/data/questions.json has 8 review ''reason'' texts saying ''gamemaster'' for the developer: left untouched (pool data, AGENTS.md: don''t edit the pools).', '"Gamemaster" is an in-game role only (Gamemaster mode, plan 05, `05-gamemaster-controls.md`). Docs, code and pm text also use "the gamemaster" for the human developer ("the gamemaster approves / enters / checks", "for the gamemaster"). That is a leftover from early drafting: workers copy it from `AGENTS.md` and `authoring/RUNBOOK.md` and spread it.

