- Done when: no dictionary request on a fresh profile; per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-13T21:15:24Z', '2026-10-13T21:52:34Z', 946, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1004, 117, 'Overlay: a code mod''s root main.js shadows our /main.js, the game never starts', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/desktop/resolve.mjs, app/desktop/main.mjs, app/desktop/resolve.test.mjs, plans/18-steam-integration.md; decision 148', 'Found while testing `task 970: Mod hooks: data, actions, i18n.add, game events`. A code mod with `"entry": "main.js"` at its folder root (the very example in plan 117''s `/mods.js` section: `/mods/big-text/main.js`) is also served as `/main.js` by the app:// overlay (plan 112: enabled mods'' folders before our `dist/`), so `index.html` loads the mod''s entry instead of our `main.js`: blank page, `window.trivia` never set, no error anywhere. Same for any root file named like one of ours (`app.css`, `lib/…`): intended for overrides, but an entry or `style.css` should never shadow by accident.

- Pick one (record with `pm decision record`): (a) the overlay never serves a mod''s `mod.json`, its `entry` file and root `style.css` at the top level (they stay reachable under `/mods/<id>/`); or (b) `readManifest`/`trivia --check-mod` warn `entry_shadows` when `entry` or `style.css` collides with a `dist/` path, and the guide says to keep entries in a subfolder or name them `mod.js`.
- Files: `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` (layers), `app/desktop/mods.mjs` (`readManifest`), `resolve.test.mjs`; fix the plan 117 example name in `plans/18-steam-integration.md` if `task 972: Docs: code add-ons, window.trivia members, file paths` already copied it.
- Done when: a throw-away mod with `"entry": "main.js"` under `TRIVIA_MODS_DIR` + `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` either starts the game with its setup run (a) or is flagged (b); per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-14T00:43:34Z', '2026-10-14T03:51:18Z', 970, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1005, 117, 'Readable build: our modules keep their unused exports for mods'' by-path imports', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-13, app/client/vite.config.ts (every shipped src module an extra Rolldown input, preserveEntrySignatures strict: dist/lib/mods.js exports modErrors/loadedMods, engine/game.js keeps all source exports; index.html still only /main.js; locales/xx.ts dev-only excluded), plans/18-steam-integration.md ''Modding: module paths''', 'Found by `task 971: Mod screens and Esc menu rows: registry, DomScreen, screens.show, menu.add` (2026-10-13). `decision 124: Readable client build: output naming rule for mod overrides` and plan 117 say mods may `import` our modules by path (`/lib/api.js`, `/engine/game.js`). But Rolldown tree-shakes exports the game itself doesn''t use, even with `preserveModules`. Example: `lib/mods.ts` exports `modErrors()` and `loadedMods()` (internals for plan 118), and the built `dist/lib/mods.js` has neither (`import("/lib/mods.js").then(m => m.modErrors)` gives `undefined`). So the module surface a mod sees by path is "what the game happens to use", not the source.

- Task 971 fixed this for Svelte''s runtime only: `app/client/vite.config.ts` lists `svelte`, `svelte/internal/client` and `svelte/internal/disclose-version` as extra `rolldownOptions.input` entries with `preserveEntrySignatures: "strict"`, so precompiled mod components can import `/vendor/svelte/src/internal/client/index.js` with every export.
- Pick one and do it:
  - keep every export of `src/**` (e.g. every source module as an extra input, or a plugin that marks exports as used; check the output naming in `outPath` and that `dist/index.html` still has only `/main.js`, decision 124)
  - or document in the modding guide (plan 121) that by-path imports only see exports the game uses, `window.trivia.modules` is the stable route.
- Done when: either `dist/lib/mods.js` exports `modErrors` (and an unused export of e.g. `engine/game.ts` survives), or the guide/plan 117 text states the limit; per-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-14T01:30:39Z', '2026-10-14T03:52:41Z', 971, 0, NULL, NULL);
