INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1019, 126, 'One language in the save and engine, question locale with Spanish fallback', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, app/client/src/{engine/{state,save,game,api,save.test,choice.test}.ts,lib/{types,engine,api}.ts,main.ts,game/Overlay.svelte,game/screens/Language.svelte}, authoring/steam/smoke.mjs', 'Engine and lib side of `plan 126: One language setting for UI and questions` (item 7 of `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles`): one language for UI and questions, replacing D-86''s `SaveData.language {ui, questions}`. The UI (`Language.svelte`, `Start.svelte`, `Overlay.svelte`) is the next task; keep the old callers compiling here only as far as needed (or adapt their calls minimally).

## What
- `engine/state.ts`, `lib/types.ts`: `Language` → one tag (`language?: string`); `SPANISH` → `"es"`.
- `engine/save.ts`: `parseSave` reads an old `{ui, questions}` object as its `ui`; a plain string as is. Save-version bump only if the `plans/` rules require it (D-82, D-86, `plans/12-client-engine.md`); a bump also touches `authoring/tools/save_file.py` (`decision 104: Python ↔ Node/TS twins: how to keep save, media cache and serving rules in sync`). `defaultLanguage(tag, ui)`: one list (`UI_LANGS`).
- One helper for the question locale, e.g. `questionLocale(language)` in `lib/engine.ts` (or `lib/data.ts`): the language if `pool.<language>.json` exists (`availableLocales()`) and its default-bundle supply passes (`supply`, as `localeSupply` does now), else `es`. `es-ES`, en, de (no pools today) and mod UI languages (`addCatalog`) → `es`.
  - Use it for `loadEngineData` (`engineData(scope)` "next"), `bundlesFor` / the Choice screen''s offer (`lib/api.ts`), and the new game''s locale: `engine/game.ts:218` reads `save.language.questions` — take the locale from the loaded data (`data.locale`) or pass it in, the engine itself doesn''t know which pools exist.
  - A running game keeps `GameRow.locale` (`gameLocale(row)`), unchanged.
- `lib/engine.ts` `ready()` / `language()`: drop the `questions` list and `localeSupply` if nothing else needs it; `ask` = fresh save and `UI_LANGS.length > 1`. `engine/api.ts` language route (`body.ui`, `body.questions`) → one `language` value. `main.ts` `initLang(save.language)`.
- `POLYGLOT` (`engine/achievements.ts:122`, wins in two question languages by `gameLocale`): unchanged logic; confirm a de UI on Spanish questions counts as an `es` game (a line in `achievements.test.ts` only if one already covers POLYGLOT).
- Record the rule: `pm decision record "One language for UI and questions" --answer "…" --body "…"` (question locale = language if its pool exists and passes, else es; supersedes D-86''s two settings in part; cite `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles`). The `plans/decisions.md` D entry is the docs task.

## Done when
- `npm run check`, `npm test` (adapt `save.test.ts` etc.: an old `{ui, questions}` save loads as `ui`), `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.
- Throw-away node script on the engine API: language `de` → new game has locale `es`, Choice offers the `es` bundles; with a throw-away `app/data/pool.de.json` (see `decision 50`''s checklist; delete it afterwards) → locale `de`.', '2026-10-14T07:44:36Z', '2026-10-14T07:47:44Z', 1012, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1020, 126, 'Language picker at first start, flag button on Start, no language rows in the Esc menu', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, app/client/src/{game/{Game,Overlay}.svelte,game/screens/{Start,Language,Mods}.svelte,lib/{input.svelte,i18n}.ts,locales/{es,en,de}.ts}, app/client/scripts/check-literals.mjs, authoring/ui/src/print/JokerCards.svelte; decision 157 (globe + endonym, keys I/L/S, pad Y); key labels now read after initLang (were es-only at import); endonym() lost its kind; screenshot work/task-1020/start-tv.png', 'UI side of `plan 126: One language setting for UI and questions`, after the save/engine task (one `language` value, question locale helper with Spanish fallback).

## What
- `game/screens/Language.svelte` (first start, default from Steam / `guessTag()` as now): picks the one language from `UI_LANGS`; no question-language list, no supply checks (`playable`, `localeSupply`). A UI change still reloads (D-86).
- `game/screens/Start.svelte`: a language button top right, opening the same picker (reuse `Language.svelte` as a screen or dialog, back returns to Start). Only on Start, never on later screens. Clickable and on a key/pad (IN-1); pick a key free in Start''s collision set (`check:literals`, `decision 53: Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?`) and a pad button in line with the existing Start bindings.
  - Look: the developer asked for a "language flag". `es` is Latin American Spanish (no single national flag) and `es-ES` is Spain, so prefer a globe/flag-style icon plus the current language''s short tag or endonym (`ENDONYMS`); record the choice with `pm decision record`. TV-readable (`plans/04-ui-tv-display.md`).
- `game/Overlay.svelte` (Esc menu): remove both language rows («Idioma», «Idioma de las preguntas») and their code (`blocked`, `setLanguage` calls, `langs`), in every mode.
- `locales/{es,es-ES,en,de}.ts`: drop the strings only those rows used (`language.questions` etc.); add the button''s label/aria/hint strings in every catalog; `npm run check:literals` passes.

## Done when
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.
- Browser (`npm run dev -w app/client`, fresh `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`, `TRIVIA_MUTE=1`): fresh save → language screen; Start''s button switches es → en → de by mouse and by keyboard (reload, UI in that language); en/de play the Spanish pool with the `es` bundles on the Choice screen; Esc menu has no language rows (default and gamemaster mode); an old save with `language: {ui: "de", questions: "es"}` loads in German. Screenshot of Start at TV size.', '2026-10-14T07:44:36Z', '2026-10-14T07:53:22Z', 1012, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1021, 126, 'Docs: one language setting (D entry, i18n and UI plans)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, plans/{decisions,04-ui-tv-display,12-client-engine,13-game-modes,15-i18n,15a-ui-translation,18-steam-integration,project}.md, directory.md; D-96 (one language, supersedes D-86 in part); README had no question-language mention', 'Docs for `plan 126: One language setting for UI and questions`, after the engine and UI tasks.

- `plans/decisions.md`: new D entry "one language for UI and questions": chosen at first start, afterwards only via Start''s language button; no Esc menu rows; fixed once bundles are chosen / in a game (`GameRow.locale`); question locale = the language if its pool exists and passes, else `es`. Mark D-86''s two settings and question-language option superseded in part; cite `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` and the decisions the earlier tasks recorded (`pm decision list --answered --grep language`).
