INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1024, 127, 'Age group and bundle names follow the UI language', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, app/client/src/lib/data.ts (loadEngineData(locale, ui), namesOf), engine/state.ts (EngineData.uiNames), lib/engine.ts (save language as ui), lib/api.ts + lib/names.svelte.ts (age group and bundle names from uiNames); browser: en/de Choice screen, menu line, «Dificultad y paquetes» in that language, es unchanged', 'Age group and bundle display names come from `names.<UI language>.json`, not the question locale''s. Today `app/client/src/lib/data.ts` `load()` (~line 131) loads names only for the question locale; when an en/de UI falls back to the es pool (`decision 156: One language for UI and questions`), names are `NO_NAMES`, so the Esc menu «Dificultad y paquetes» shows «Adolescentes», «Niños» etc. next to English labels.

