bring them in line with the plan. A task that writes a plan gets `--kind plan`.', '2026-10-14T21:33:52Z', '2026-10-14T21:34:39Z', 251, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1032, 128, 'Content target check', 'work', 'dropped', NULL, 'decision 204 irrelevant', 'Task 1 of `plan 128: S4 close-out`: check milestone 9''s content target per question locale and record it. Checks, docs and pm only; no content fixes.

Binding: `decision 21: Content target per player and language (OQ-32)?` (D-75): pass/fail = 5000 approved per question locale (`en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`; milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15) with D-53''s mix; games numbers information only. `decision 26: Launch languages (OQ-31): which languages at Steam launch, and which comes first after?` (`es`, `en`, `de` + `es-ES`). Deficits per question locale (plan 148 task 6; replaces decision 37''s last clause and D-84). `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`: `locale` on every source (absent = `es`); `base` from batch-9 `en`, ≤ batch-8 `es`; pool for L = approved sources in L + playing translations into L; `pool.json` = `es`, `pool.es-ES.json` new. `decision 156: One language for UI and questions`. Plan 57 (CT-5, release-ready slices).

## Guard
- `pm plans list`; `pm show` of plans 57, 62, 63, 64, 66, 67, 68, 69, 70, 98, 100, 126, 136 (`plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`), 138 (`plan 138: Regional taxonomy: a general list, colombia reworked`), 147 (`plan 147: English-first batches: calibration, overlap and QC across languages`), 148 (`plan 148: English-first drafting for base`) and 84.
- Each must have all tasks done or dropped; plan 84: chains 1–3 (neutral Spanish, translation pilot, full translation per locale `en`, `de`, `es-ES`, `es`) at their end. Plan 84''s chains 4 (`colombia`) and 5 (`usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`) and its pilot-effort task don''t count (`task 1035: Regional bundles record`). `plan 17: Batch runs` isn''t waited for: this task''s numbers say whether there is enough.
- An open task (other than plan 84''s chains 4–5) pending on a decision → `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <that decision>`, stop. Other open tasks → stop without changes, say so (the queue brings it back). Never drop or edit other plans'' tasks.

## Steps
- `qgen validate`; `trivia-media sync --status approved`; `qgen export`.
- `qgen report --simulate` (default matrix: every question locale `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`, default bundles, all age groups, all modes); `qgen report --locale <L>` for `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`; `qgen report --qc` (release-ready column); `qgen report --cost` (spent vs. `targets.json` `"budget"`).
- Record in `plans/16-content-target.md` ("Where we stand" → dated close-out result): per locale approved vs. 5000 and per level, ✓/✗, games per new player (median, p10, strong bound) for adults solo, bottlenecks, release-ready state, total spent per language (en drafting + translations, plan 70), file sizes of `app/data/pool*.json` and pack pools (task 3 uses them for the install size).

## English-first `base` (plan 148)
- `qgen validate` passes its source-locale rules; every `base` question of batch-9 on has `locale: "en"`.
- Counts per direction (en → `es`, `es-ES`, `de`; es → `en`, `de`, `es-ES`) from `qgen report --locale <L>`; untranslated approved translatable sources by count (information; pass/fail is the locale''s target).
- `pool.es-ES.json` exported (decision 156: an `es-ES` save plays it once its default bundles'' supply passes, else `es`; the browser row is task 2''s).

## Shortfall
- A ✗ or a slice not release-ready: no fix. If plan 84 has no open run/QC pair for that locale: `pm decision add "S4 target not met for <locale>: more runs or lower the target?"` (body: the numbers; options "more runs: plan 84 adds pairs" (recommended), "lower the target (D-75 amended)", "ship as is"), `pm task-pending-decision` for this task and tasks 2–3 of plan 128, stop. On the answer "more runs": `pm task add 84` the next run/QC pair, stop (this task waits for it).

Done when: `qgen report --simulate` exits 0 for all four question locales (or an answered decision accepts the shortfall), the result is in `plans/16-content-target.md`.', '2026-10-14T21:34:37Z', '2026-10-16T03:52:25Z', 1031, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1033, 128, 'Language picker, UI wording, joker and slug-key check', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Task 2 of `plan 128: S4 close-out`: check milestone 9''s "language on first start", "UI wording and review", "joker names" and "slug keys" rows. Checks, docs and pm only; failures become tasks in the owning plans.

Binding: D-96 (`decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` item 7, plan 126, tasks 1019–1021): one language for UI and questions; picker at first start with the guess preselected (`navigator.language` now); afterwards only Start''s language button; no Esc menu language rows; a save without `language` (the family''s) = `es`, never sees the picker. Supersedes the milestone''s "Esc menu" wording. `decision 156: One language for UI and questions`: an `es-ES` save plays `pool.es-ES.json` once its default bundles'' supply passes, else `es`. `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`: the `es` pool gains `es` translations of English-sourced questions. `decision 110` (D-99): `colombia` on for the family''s save. `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again` (developer, 2026-10-14): one English-first name per joker, translated in `es`, `es-ES`, `de`; keys per `decision 53: Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?`; one symbol across languages, shown in its follow-up dialog; its record supersedes decisions 40–44 and 54–58 (find its decisions with `pm decision list --grep "Joker names"`). Slug keys (masterplan part 16, developer 2026-10-16; `plan 149: Slug keys for categories`): every category and subcategory in every bundle keyed by an English slug, unique within its bundle; display names, `en` included, only from `names.<locale>.json` (`es-ES` reads `names.es.json` + `names.es-ES.json` overrides); old saves load; mods'' plain-string format stays valid; supersedes the name-as-key part of `decision 165: Subcategory keys in code: bundle + name; base keeps bare names`, D-99, D-100.

## Guard
- Same as task 1 of `plan 128: S4 close-out` (`task 1711: Content target check`): plans 57, 62–64, 66–70, 98, 100, 126, 136, 138, 147, 148 and `plan 149: Slug keys for categories` done or dropped; plan 84 chains 1–3 (neutral Spanish, translation pilot (no go/no-go), full translation per locale) at their end, not the regional chains 4–5. Blocked: pend on the decision blocking them unless it''s a question review (spot check, health, QC proposal; `decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`): then `pm task requires <this task> <the blocked task>`; else stop without changes.
- Decisions 161–164 "Screen gallery reviewed? (<lang>)" answered and task 1026 done; plan 136 done and its "Joker names and symbols reviewed?" answered (its fix task done, if any); decisions 62–65 "Playtest passed?" answered and task 459 done. Else `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <open decision>`, stop.

## Static check
- `app/client/src/locales/style/{en,es,es-ES,de}.md` exist; `AGENTS.md` Rules line about the style guides present.
- Grep the catalogs: `de` «Spielleitermodus»; «Steam achievements» / «logros de Steam» / «Steam-Erfolge» wherever achievements appear; Esc «Back to main menu» / «Volver al menú principal» / «Zurück zum Hauptmenü», «Quit game» / «Salir del juego» / «Spiel beenden»; no «ihr/euch/euer» in `de.ts`.
- A miss → `pm task add 100 "<fix>"` with the string, stop.

## Joker names (static)
- Each joker''s `joker.<id>.name` in `en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de` matches plan 136''s answered decisions; keys per decision 53 (`check:literals` passes).
- No old name not chosen again (Soplo, Paso, Bájale, Cambiazo, Francotirador; Hint, Pass & Purge, Fairy, Ms Picky, Trick Shot; Zaunpfahl, Näxt, Gang runter, Wunschzeit, Finte) in user-visible text: `rg` over `app/client/src/locales`, `authoring/ui/src/print`, `modding/`, `plans/17a-store-page.md`, `app/desktop/steam-achievements.vdf`; old names in the style guides'' bad-patterns lists are fine.
- Style guide glossaries list the new names.
- A miss → `pm task add 136 "<fix>"` with the string, stop.

## Slug keys (static)
- `qgen validate` passes the slug rules (slug form, unique per bundle, every names file complete) for `base`, `colombia` and every other bundle.
- `rg` finds no Spanish name used as a key in `authoring/data/` (questions'' `subcategory`, `targets.json`, concept file names) or `app/data/`; `categories.json` holds no display names.
- `app/data/` names files for `en`, `es`, `de` (+ `es-ES` overrides).
- `modding/` kit documents slugs + names as optional; `trivia-desktop --check-mod` passes on a shipped example in today''s plain-string format.
- A miss → `pm task add 149 "<fix>"` with the finding, stop.

## Browser check (throw-away)
- `npm run build`, then `npm run serve -w app/client` (Node dev server), temp `TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR`, `TRIVIA_MUTE=1`; stop it by PID.
- No save, `navigator.language` `de-AT` → picker, `Deutsch` preselected; confirm → German Start; reload → no picker; Start''s language button → `en`, next game draws from `pool.en.json` (English question text).
- `es-CO` → `Español (Latinoamérica)` preselected; `fr-FR` → `English` (fallback per D-96); `es-ES` → `Español (España)` preselected, the game draws from `pool.es-ES.json` (decision 156; `es` if task 1294 found its supply short, noted).
- The family''s `es` game includes `es` translations of English-sourced questions (one drawn, or found in `pool.json` by id with `locale: "en"` in `questions.json`).
- A copy of the family''s save (no `language` field, e.g. copied from `state/game.json`, never the file itself) → no picker, Spanish, base + `colombia` on.
- The same family-save copy: `purged`, `swapped_to`, `notified_exhausted` with old keys (Spanish names, old category slugs) map on load; category names on Configure and in the game the same as before (D-59); `en` and `de` saves show the `names.<locale>.json` names, not slugs.
- Keyboard only; pad too if the dev server has pad emulation (else note keyboard only).
- Jokers, in `en` and `de`: the tray shows the five symbols; each follow-up dialog (skip dialog, category picker both steps, snipe scope, difficulty dial, hint note) shows its joker''s symbol (the tray''s, from `TOKENS`) and the new name; `/comodines?lang=<L>` (`trivia-authoring`) per locale: new names, same symbols.
- Failure → `pm task add 126` (language picker), `pm task add 136` (jokers), `pm task add 149` (slug keys: save mapping, names) or the owning plan, with the steps to reproduce, stop.

Done when: every row passes; the result (date, commit) is in `plans/15-i18n.md` "Model" (I18N-2) and `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` "Wording and review" and "Joker names"; slug keys in `plans/22-bundles.md` (taxonomy, keys).', '2026-10-14T21:34:37Z', NULL, 1031, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1034, 128, 'Docs close-out of S4', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Task 3 of `plan 128: S4 close-out`: bring plan files, indexes and the later masterplans in line with milestone 9''s outcome. Requires `task 1711: Content target check` and `task 1033: Language picker, UI wording, joker and slug-key check`. Docs and pm only.

Binding: `decision 21` (D-75; 5000 per question locale `en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`), `decision 26` (D-78), `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`, `decision 156: One language for UI and questions`, D-96 (`decision 50` item 7), `decision 110` (D-99, `colombia` 2000 es + en may land after launch), `decision 66` (packs are free DLC), decision 96 (content updates). Slug keys (masterplan part 16, developer 2026-10-16; `plan 149: Slug keys for categories`): supersede the name-as-key part of `decision 165: Subcategory keys in code: bundle + name; base keeps bare names`, D-99, D-100. Translations without human control (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-16; `plan 171: Translations without human control`): the LLM translation review is a translation''s only review, every question locale; no native-speaker spot check, no QC decision per `tr-*` run, no pilot go/no-go, no `qgen health ack` after a pilot; decision 45''s thresholds are reported, never a stop. `decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation` (developer, 2026-10-23): health ✗, spot checks and QC proposals are decisions no task waits on; health ✗ never stops a run (drafting, `--bundle`, `--translate`); the release bar is the developer''s own gate at `trivia-release-check`; partly supersedes decision 45 and `decision 313: Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run`.

## Steps
- `plans/11-steam.md`: S4 row done (date, task 1711''s numbers; packs: each regional bundle''s approved count per language at launch (`colombia`, `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`), the rest after launch per decision 110 and milestone 9''s 2026-10-15 change); exit criterion text matches D-75 and D-96.
- Translations without human control: `authoring/QC.md` "Translation runs", `authoring/RUNBOOK.md` and `plans/15b-question-translation.md` (QT-5, QT-6) carry no spot check, no QC decision per `tr-*` run, no pilot go/no-go; decision 45''s pilot clause recorded as superseded (`pm decision list --grep health`). A miss → `pm task add 66` with the finding (docs only; cite an open task of plan 171 instead if one covers it; the pass doesn''t wait for it).
- Reviews don''t gate runs (decision 414): `authoring/RUNBOOK.md`, `authoring/QC.md` (no step 5 "Next batch waits", no health stop for drafting, `--bundle` or `--translate`) and `plans/16-content-target.md` (release bar = the developer''s gate at `trivia-release-check`) say so. A miss → `pm task add` in the plan `task 1699: write plan: Reviews don''t gate generation` wrote (milestone 1, `pm plans list`; cite an open task there instead if one covers it), with the finding (docs only; the pass doesn''t wait for it).
- `plans/15-i18n.md`, `15a`, `15b`, `15c`, `16-content-target.md`, `22-bundles.md` (slug keys, names files), `09-jokers.md` (new names, symbols per `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`): tasks `[x]` with notes (check, don''t redo, each plan''s own ticks: I18N-2, LUI-4, LUI-5, QT-1..QT-6, RG-1..RG-5, CT-1..CT-5); `15b` source locale per question, QT-5 pilot measured only, QT-6 LLM translation review only, `15` Spanish varieties (`es` idiomatic Latin American, `es-ES` own pool), `16` four question locales (`plan 148: English-first drafting for base` task 10 wrote them: check); `plans/decisions.md` D-99, D-100 amended for slug keys (plan 149 wrote it: check); LUI-6 stays open, noted as S5 (`plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)`); status lines (`stub` → `agreed`/`done`). RG-5 open until `task 1035: Regional bundles record`.
- `plans/README.md` status column for 11, 15, 15a, 15b, 15c, 16, 22; `plans/project.md`: Steam track says S4 done (date) except the regional bundles, ticked tasks ticked, resolved open-question rows removed; `plans/open-questions.md` if an S4 question is still listed.
- Masterplans of milestones 10 and 11 (`plan 10: masterplan`, `plan 11: masterplan`): compare with S4''s outcome; if scope changed, append a short dated note via `pm plan edit <id> --body -` (whole body): store languages `es`, `en`, `de` (+ `es-ES`, UI and own question pool); one free DLC depot per pack with its languages (`colombia`, `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`); packs grow after launch via content updates (`plan 96: Content updates as patches (ST-5)`, decision 96); install size with four pools (`es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`) + pack pools (task 1711''s file sizes); Steam''s language as the picker''s guess (D-96). No note if nothing changed. Milestone bodies untouched; anything they get wrong → `pm decision add`.
- `qgen validate`, `npm run check` unaffected.

Done when: milestone 9''s "Done when" holds except the regional bundles row (slug keys included); task note cites decision ids and dates.', '2026-10-14T21:34:37Z', NULL, 1031, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1035, 128, 'Regional bundles record', 'work', 'open', -140, NULL, 'Task 4 of `plan 128: S4 close-out`: record the regional bundles (`colombia` pilot with its effort, then `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`; 2000 approved each in their languages). May land after launch; the launch (milestone 11) never waits for it. Requires `task 1034: Docs close-out of S4`. Docs, checks and pm only.

Binding: `decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)` (D-99): every regional bundle 2000 approved in its region''s language + en (en regions: en only), `colombia` (es + en) the pilot, effort measured ($ per approved, review time per 100). Its "more bundles only after a new decision with the pilot''s numbers" is replaced (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15): `usa` (en), `germany` (de + en), `uk` (en), `spain` (es-ES + en), `mexico` (es + en), run by `plan 84: Release content runs` chain 5; no "More regional bundles?" decision. `decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): how is the game sold on Steam?` (packs are free DLC). D-59: the family''s save keeps base + `colombia`.

## Guard
- Plan 84''s chain 4 ended: `qgen report --bundle colombia` and `qgen report --bundle colombia --locale en` at 2000 approved; its pilot-effort task done.
- Chain 5 ended for every bundle: `qgen report --bundle <id>` at 2000 in the region''s language (`usa`, `uk` en; `germany` de; `spain` es-ES; `mexico` es), plus `--locale en` at 2000 for `germany`, `spain`, `mexico`.
- Else pend, never stop without changes (an unclosed run counts as failed in `pm run`): `pm task-pending-decision 1035 <id>` on the pending decision that blocks the earliest open task of plan 84''s chains 4–5 (`pm decision list`, "blocks task(s)"), or of `plan 98: Regional packs (RG-3..RG-5)` / `plan 138: Regional taxonomy: a general list, colombia reworked` that the chains wait for; a taxonomy, slug-key or real-failure decision, never a review one (spot check, health, QC proposal; `decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`).
- That earliest open task waits on a task instead (e.g. a qgen fix) or on a review decision: `pm task requires 1035 <that task>`.
- No such decision but tasks still queued: `pm decision add "Regional bundles record: chains still running"` (body: where each bundle stands, approved per language; option "re-check after the chains") and pend on it.

## Steps
- Pilot numbers in `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` and `plans/16-content-target.md` ($ per approved, review time per 100); missing → record them from `qgen report --cost` and `qgen report --review-time --bundle colombia`. Per further bundle: $ per approved from `qgen report --cost` (information).
- Per bundle: `app/data/bundles.json` `languages` lists its languages (region''s + `en`); `app/data/bundles/<id>/pool.<locale>.json` exists per language; off by default; `qgen validate` clean. The family''s save keeps base + `colombia`.
- DLC entries per bundle (`steam.json` `dlc`, store texts, capsules; plans 130, 89, 88): present or an open follow-up task there; else `pm task add 98` naming the bundle and what''s missing.
- `plans/11-steam.md` S4 row: regional bundles done (date, counts per bundle and language, pilot numbers); `plans/project.md`; RG-5 ticked in `15c`.

Done when: milestone 9''s "Done when" holds in full; task note cites decision 110 and milestone 9''s 2026-10-15 change.', '2026-10-14T21:34:37Z', NULL, 1031, 0, NULL, 'questions');
