INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1053, 132, 'Shipped media names and the resolver adapter', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, app/desktop/resolve.mjs (shippedName per decision 185: Shipped media: formats, names and where the encode runs (SW-9); /media tries cacheName then shippedName), resolve.test.mjs (both lookups), stage-media.mjs (staged = cacheName until task 1054: Encode shipped media in stage-media (WebP, Opus, WebM) switches to shippedName; pack-media.json uses it, so no behaviour change), authoring/steam/credits_check.mjs + smoke.mjs (file = cacheName if present, else shippedName, as the resolver), lib/types.ts comment. Checked: npm test, npm run check, npm run build, qgen validate; makeResolver on the real dist/data/raw cache serves q-0001 image, q-0025 audio, q-0055 video (206 with range); the GUI walk via Esc «Ir a pregunta…» not done (same resolver code path).', 'Part 1 of `plan 132: Media bundle for shipping (SW-9)`: one adapter from pool URLs to the shipped file names, before encoding changes extensions.
- `shippedName(url)` beside `cacheName` in `app/desktop/resolve.mjs`: `cacheName(url)`''s 16-hex stem + shipped extension (images `.jpg .jpeg .png .webp` → `.webp`; audio `.mp3 .ogg .oga .wav .flac .m4a` → `.opus`; video → `.webm`; GIF, SVG, else unchanged); deterministic, no manifest; D-17 keys unchanged
- `/media?url=`: tries `cacheName` first (raw cache in dev runs), then `shippedName` (packaged `resources/media/`)
- `shippedName` used by: `authoring/steam/credits_check.mjs`, `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` (line ~50, `resources/media/<cacheName>`), `app/desktop/stage-media.mjs`''s `build/pack-media.json`
- `app/client/src/lib/types.ts` comment "Packaged file: cacheName(file_url)" → `shippedName(file_url)`
- Until the encode task lands, `stage-media.mjs` still links raw files; under the shipped name only where the extension doesn''t change (no behaviour change otherwise; credits/smoke must still find every file)
- Check: `resolve.test.mjs` case for both lookups; `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1 TRIVIA_MUTE=1 trivia-desktop` against the raw cache shows an image, an audio and a video question (Esc «Ir a pregunta…»); `npm test`, `npm run check`', '2026-10-14T22:13:09Z', '2026-10-14T22:15:43Z', 1052, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1054, 132, 'Encode shipped media in stage-media (WebP, Opus, WebM)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, app/desktop/stage-media.mjs, flake.nix (trivia-desktop-build: ffmpeg-headless, libwebp). Encode cache work/ship-media/ (work/ already gitignored). Sizes before → after: total 2549 → 679 MB (1100 files: 1079 WebP, 17 Opus, 3 WebM, 1 GIF); content depot 2364 → 630 MB; colombia DLC 185 → 50 MB (93 files per pack-media.json). 58 files still > 1 MB: the 3 videos (60.7, 27.4, 10.0 MB) and 55 WebP of 1.0–2.3 MB at q 60. Video: VP9 CRF 33, -b:v 0, -deadline good -cpu-used 2, row-mt, ≤ 1920×1080 never upscaled, Opus 96k; measured: Apollo 480p 29 min 90 → 61 MB, Old Faithful 1080p 80 s 27 → 10 MB, Okeanos 360p VP8 280 s 45 → 27 MB (Apollo has no clip window, so the whole 29 min ships; trimming it would be a content choice). Checks: trivia-desktop-build --dir ok, second build ''0 encoded now''; trivia-steam stage ✓ win/linux; credits_check ✓ 1100 media; all 1079 images within 3840×2160; 10-image side-by-side at 1080p (maps, PNGs with text/transparency, photos) looks the same as the source; smoke: image/audio/video questions with and without packs ok, but only with the consent step patched in a throw-away copy. The checked-in smoke.mjs times out on the telemetry consent screen, which is unrelated to media: follow-up task 1065: Smoke game: answer the telemetry consent screen. npm run check/test/build, qgen validate pass.', 'Part 2 of `plan 132: Media bundle for shipping (SW-9)`: `app/desktop/stage-media.mjs` encodes the approved cache into `app/desktop/build/media/` under `shippedName(url)` (from the shipped-names task).
- images (`.jpg .jpeg .png .webp`): fit inside 3840×2160, never upscaled (D-48); WebP lossy via `cwebp`, alpha kept; q 82, step down to q 60 while > 1 MB; still > 1 MB = listed, not a failure
- GIF, SVG: copied as is
- audio (`.mp3 .ogg .oga .wav .flac .m4a`): Opus in Ogg, `.opus`, 96 kb/s, ffmpeg `libopus`
- video: WebM VP9 + Opus, at most 1920×1080, CRF ~33; settle exact values by measurement (3 WebMs, 27–90 MB today)
- encode cache `work/ship-media/` (gitignored, check `.gitignore`): `<stem>-<settings hash>.<ext>`, hash = tool versions + parameters; rebuild re-encodes only new/changed; `build/media/` hard links from it (copy fallback, as today); parallel jobs `os.availableParallelism()`
- `trivia-desktop-build` in `flake.nix`: `pkgs.ffmpeg-headless` (libopus, libvpx) and `pkgs.libwebp` in `runtimeInputs`; nothing in `package.json`; no `authoring/` imports
- `--allow-missing` as today; summary line: files, MB before → after, files still > 1 MB
- Check: full `trivia-desktop-build --dir`; `trivia-steam stage` passes; `node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs app/desktop/release/linux-unpacked` (image, audio, video question, no missing-media notice); `credits_check.mjs` passes; throw-away visual check: 10 images (photos, a map, a PNG with text or alpha) at 1920×1080 side by side with the source, video playback in the shell; second build re-encodes nothing
- Task note: sizes before/after (total, per depot: content and each pack per `build/pack-media.json`), chosen video values', '2026-10-14T22:13:09Z', '2026-10-14T23:26:02Z', 1052, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1055, 132, 'Media budget and missing-file check (stage-media --check, release check step)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, app/desktop/media-budget.json (content 950, dlc colombia 75, default_dlc 75, file 5, video 100 MB; measured 630 / 50 MB, largest video 60.7, largest WebP 2.3 MB), app/desktop/stage-media.mjs --check (missing pool files, per-depot totals from build/pack-media.json, file/video limits ✗, > 1 MB listed; exit 1 on ✗), authoring/steam/release_check.py (media-budget step runs it after desktop; MEDIA_BUDGET gone). Checks: passes on task 1054''s build; budgets below measured (content 600, colombia 40, video 50) fail; a removed build/media file fails, restored. Plan 18 docs and code-review.md''s ''media-budget still skipped'' row left to task 1056. npm run check/test/build, qgen validate pass.', 'Part 3 of `plan 132: Media bundle for shipping (SW-9)`: a check that fails over budget or on a missing shipped file, run by the release check.
- `app/desktop/media-budget.json`: `{ "content": <MB>, "dlc": { "<pack>": <MB> }, "default_dlc": <MB>, "file": <MB> }`; numbers from the encode task''s measured sizes (its task note) + ~50 % headroom, rounded; `file` hard limit e.g. 5 MB, videos their own limit
- `node app/desktop/stage-media.mjs --check` (no encoding): every pool URL (base + packs) has `shippedName(url)` in `build/media/` (missing = ✗); per-depot totals (`content` = all minus `build/pack-media.json`''s, each pack its own, unlisted packs `default_dlc`) against the budget; files over `file` listed (✗); files over 1 MB listed (info); exit 1 on ✗
- `authoring/steam/release_check.py`: step `media-budget` runs it instead of skipping; `MEDIA_BUDGET` constant and the "always skipped" header line go
- Check: passes on the encode task''s build; a budget below the measured size fails; a file removed from `build/media/` fails (restore it after)', '2026-10-14T22:13:09Z', '2026-10-14T23:27:25Z', 1052, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1056, 132, 'Media bundle docs and SW-9 close-out', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, plans/18-steam-integration.md (SW-9 [x], media-size bullet with formats/budgets/measured sizes, Builds and depots: encode, media-budget step, layout, archive sizes), plans/decisions.md (D-104), plans/23-media-providers.md (shipped ≠ cache formats), plans/11-steam.md (install size ~1.1 GB), plans/17a-store-page.md (depots re-measured: windows 0.41, linux 0.36, content 0.63, colombia 0.05 GB → 1.09/1.04 GB installed; storage 3 → 1.5 GB), directory.md (work/ship-media/, media-budget.json, shippedName), plans/project.md (SW-9 row), AGENTS.md (trivia-desktop-build, trivia-release-check lines), code-review.md (media-budget row). Follow-up in plan 88: H.264 → VP9 in the store requirements. npm run check passes.', 'Part 4 of `plan 132: Media bundle for shipping (SW-9)`: docs after the shipped-names, encode and budget tasks.
