INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1134, 17, 'qgen reports its claude calls: per-call cost and tokens, totals at the end', 'work', 'done', 490, '2026-10-15, authoring/tools/qgen.py (claude(): every attempt → work/<run>/calls.jsonl with step, item, outcome ok/retry/failed/limit, models, usd, turns, ms, seconds, input/output/cache tokens; result line ''… ok 2m19s $0.84 31k tok''; Calls tally + atexit ''claude:'' summary on success, failed step, usage limit, Ctrl-C; calls()/costs() take a work dir, read calls.jsonl + old costs.log; costs.log no longer written), progress.py (where(), extra after duration), health.py, RUNBOOK (claude: line into notes and decision bodies), AGENTS.md rule, directory.md. Checked with a fake claude on PATH: success, failed step (incl. no-JSON crash), usage limit, Ctrl-C (process group SIGINT): calls.jsonl complete, summary each time. qgen report --cost and batch_health for batch-6/7/8 unchanged (only the ''no costs.log'' wording). check, test, build, qgen validate pass.', 'decision 208
pm: task 1131 is running; tasks.sql is committed with it: What must a script that calls claude report to its caller? `task 1129: Finish batch-8 …` ran 3h49m with qgen calling claude, and pm recorded $0.37, only the worker''s own session. Builds on `task 1131: qgen output as a plain log: resume notes and one line per Claude or media call` (per-call log lines).

