- D-87 in `plans/decisions.md`: name the new locales.
- `authoring/QC.md`: only if the translation spot check reads differently for zh (e.g. character-count length, hints by character/pinyin); else unchanged.
- `directory.md`: no change expected (no new top-level file).

Done when: those docs match the files as approved; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.', '2026-10-15T20:26:31Z', '2026-10-15T20:26:41Z', 1157, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1171, 141, 'Native reviewer brief: authoring/NATIVE-REVIEW.md', 'work', 'open', 730, NULL, 'Write `authoring/NATIVE-REVIEW.md`, the brief for outside native reviewers of `zh-Hans`, `ru`, `pt-BR` (`plan 141: Native reviewers`, "Brief"). The spot-check sheet (`qgen spotcheck export`, task in this plan) embeds it at the top, so it runs first.

- In English, short; style per AGENTS.md (intro paragraph, then bullets).
- For the reviewers:
  - the game: family trivia on a TV, the family plays against the gamemaster, 12 questions to victory
  - each job with time per job (estimates in `decision 220: Native reviewers for zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR: paid freelancers, volunteers, or mixed?`): locale prompt read (~1 h, findings go back as comments, never silent edits), per-run spot check of 30 questions (~45 min), zh only: `chinese-base` fit sample, UI gallery read + playtest via a Steam key on `beta`, store text drafts
  - what they check (`authoring/QC.md` "Translation runs" extra checks): faithful to the source (English reference beside it; "gloss" marks a machine gloss), natural, hints and wrong answers that work in the language, difficulty for the language''s players; text inside images/audio/video is never a problem (`decision 35: Translation prompts and markets per locale (plan 66)`)
  - the yardstick: the rules of `authoring/tools/prompts/locale-<locale>.md`
  - verdicts: approve / needs_work / reject / doesn''t travel, problem kinds (`qgen.py` `PROBLEMS`), feedback in English, optional corrected text; general comments at the end
  - how to return work: «Download verdicts» → `spotcheck-<run>.verdicts.json` by e-mail; progress stays in the browser; deadline ~1 week per sheet
  - no mention of planted control items (they must stay blind)
- For the developer, a short section: per job what to send (sheet, gallery zip from `trivia-gallery`, Steam key, store text draft) and what to do with the reply (`qgen spotcheck import`, `qgen report --qc`, answer the playtest or store decisions). Names, contacts, payments stay out of the repo.
- `directory.md` unchanged (file inside `authoring/`).

Done when: the file exists and reads as a one-page brief; `npm run check` passes.', '2026-10-15T20:27:37Z', NULL, 1158, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1172, 141, 'qgen spotcheck export and import: offline sheet for outside reviewers', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Build the offline spot-check sheet of `decision 221: How does an outside native reviewer reach the review tool?`, as specified in `plan 141: Native reviewers` "Spot-check sheet" (read it in full).

- `authoring/tools/spotcheck.py` (new): export and import; reuse `authoring/server/spot_checks.py` (`sample`, `record`, `size`) and `authoring/tools/reviews.py`; `qgen.py` only dispatches `qgen spotcheck export|import` (`decision 101: qgen.py stays one module (code review part 7)`: no package split).
- `qgen spotcheck export <run> [--controls N]` → `work/<run>/spotcheck-<run>.html`: self-contained (inline JS/CSS, small inline images; audio/video named only), brief from `authoring/NATIVE-REVIEW.md` on top, sample in `spot_checks.sample` order; per item English reference (approved non-stale `en` translation, else a gloss made at export, marked "gloss"), translation (question, options with the right one marked, hints, explanation), subcategory, difficulty 1–15; blind: no LLM review, audit, status, feedback. Input per item as the review tool (approve / needs_work / reject / doesn''t travel, `PROBLEMS`, feedback, optional corrected text), general comments; `localStorage` progress; «Download verdicts» → `spotcheck-<run>.verdicts.json` (run, sample ids, sheet hash, verdicts).
- Controls: `--controls N` (default 3 for `zh-Hans`, `ru`, `pt-BR`, else 0) adds planted faulty copies (wrong right answer, changed number, garbled option), ids `control-<k>`, mixed into the sample order, listed in `work/<run>/spotcheck-controls.json`, never in a pool.
- `qgen spotcheck import <file> [--dry-run]`: checks run, ids, sheet hash; each verdict → the translation''s human review (`reviewer: "human"`, `by: "native"`, no name) and `spot_checks.record` (`locale` set); corrected text into the feedback, not over the translation; controls scored apart: prints "controls caught k/N", and `qgen report --qc` shows it in the run''s QC section.
- Gloss calls claude: report calls and totals (`decision 208: What must a script that calls claude report to its caller?`).
- Check end to end: no `tr-*` run exists yet in this repo; if still none, make a throw-away one in a scratch copy (e.g. `git worktree` + `TRIVIA_WORK`), export, open the sheet in a browser, fill a verdict file by hand, `--dry-run` import plus one real import in the scratch copy, `qgen report --qc`; nothing committed under `authoring/data/` or `work/`.
- Docs: `authoring/QC.md` "Translation runs" (outside reviewer: sheet + import; pm worker still `pm decision add "Spot check tr-<locale>-<n> done?"`, body names the sheet path), README how-to, D-entry (next free, D-106 or later) in `plans/decisions.md`, QT-6 note in `plans/15b-question-translation.md`.

Done when: export/import work as above; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.', '2026-10-15T20:27:37Z', NULL, 1158, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1173, 141, 'Fit-sample sheet for chinese-base (zh only)', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Extend the offline sheet (`task 1172: qgen spotcheck export and import: offline sheet for outside reviewers`) for the `chinese-base` fit pass: the zh native reviewer checks a sample of the fit pass''s picks (`plan 141: Native reviewers`, task 3).

- Waits on `decision 217: chinese-base membership: how does a translated base question count for chinese-base?` and on the fit model from the `chinese-base` model plan (written by `task 1148: write plan: chinese-base bundle: model and setup`) and the fit pass prompt (`task 1169: Fit pass prompt: draft, approval, prompts/fit.md`). Use the command name and field that plan names; else `qgen spotcheck export --fit <run>`.
- Per item: the English reference and the zh translation as in the spot-check sheet; input fit yes / no + reason (English); blind: no LLM fit verdict shown.
- Import writes the developer-correctable fit field (per decision 217''s answer, e.g. `fit` on the `questions.zh-Hans.json` entry) with the reason, marked as native; the developer can still flip it in `/review?locale=zh-Hans`.
- Brief: add the fit job''s how-to to `authoring/NATIVE-REVIEW.md` if not yet there.
- Check on a throw-away copy as task 1172 did; nothing committed under `authoring/data/`.

Done when: a fit sheet exports, a hand-filled verdict file imports into the fit field; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.', '2026-10-15T20:27:48Z', NULL, 1158, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1174, 141, 'Native reviewer requests and the engaged decisions per locale', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'After `decision 220: Native reviewers for zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR: paid freelancers, volunteers, or mixed?` is answered (`plan 141: Native reviewers`, "Gate"):

- Per locale (`zh-Hans`, `ru`, `pt-BR`) a posting / request text in `work/native-review/<locale>.md` (not committed): the jobs and hours from decision 220 and `authoring/NATIVE-REVIEW.md`, rate (paid) or credit + free key (volunteer) per the answer, trial = the pilot''s spot-check sheet, return by e-mail, ~1 week per sheet; zh adds the `chinese-base` fit sample (and full source review if `decision 218: New China-centric questions for chinese-base: drafted in Spanish and translated, or drafted in Chinese?` went Chinese). No names, contacts or payments in the repo.
- Raise three `once` decisions `Native reviewer for <locale> engaged?` with option "engaged"; body names the request file. The pilot tasks of the ru/pt-BR pools plan (`plan 143: Russian and Portuguese pools`) and of the `chinese-base` content plan get pending on them: link any that already exist with `pm task-pending-decision`; else say so in the consequences, so those plans'' split tasks do it.
- `pm decision consequences 220 "<what changed>"`.

Done when: three request files in `work/native-review/`, three engaged decisions raised and linked where possible, consequences recorded.', '2026-10-15T20:27:49Z', NULL, 1158, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1175, 142, 'Decisions: fonts per script, keys on non-Latin layouts, picker letters', 'work', 'open', 410, NULL, 'Task 1 of `plan 142: UI in the new languages`: raise the three developer decisions the plan''s "Decisions" section lists; no game code changes.

## Fonts per script
- Throw-away renders in `work/fonts/` (not committed): Start, Question (4 answers, joker row), Victory per candidate, at 1920 × 1080, in the game''s colours.
  - ru: Nunito text with its Cyrillic subset; display candidates Nunito 800–900 (recommended), Rubik, M PLUS Rounded 1c.
  - zh-Hans: one CJK family for text and display, e.g. Noto Sans SC / Source Han Sans SC variable (recommended); alternative ZCOOL KuaiLe headings + Noto Sans SC text.
  - Sample text: `en.ts` strings translated ad hoc (throw-away), plus a few `names` / question lines.
- Sizes per option: woff2 of the Cyrillic subset; CJK subset = GB2312 level 1 (3755) ∪ catalog-like sample ∪ pool estimate; fonttools from the flake (`pyftsubset`; add to `flake.nix` if missing, then it''s part of task 2).
- All OFL, rounded, heavy weights to match Baloo 2 (`app/client/public/fonts/`, `theme.css`).
- `pm decision add "Fonts for ru and zh-Hans (display, text)?"`: body with render paths, sizes, licences; options recommended first.

## Keys on non-Latin layouts (extends `decision 53: Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?`)
- Problem: `lib/input.svelte.ts` `toIntent` matches `e.key`; on ЙЦУКЕН the A–D keys give `ф и с в`.
- Options: (recommended) key letters stay Latin in `ru` and `zh-Hans`, `toIntent` falls back to `e.code` (`KeyA` → `a`) when `e.key` is a non-Latin letter, answers A–D; alternative ru Cyrillic letters (А Б В Г, Cyrillic joker keys; breaks on a Latin layout).

## Picker letters and name length
- `LetterPicker.svelte`, `picker.letters` per catalog, `MAX_NAME`.
- Options per plan: ru Cyrillic А–Я, Ё + Latin; pt-BR Latin + `Á Â Ã À Ç É Ê Í Ó Ô Õ Ú`; zh-Hans (recommended) Latin letters (pinyin) on the pad picker, Chinese names via keyboard IME / Steam on-screen keyboard; `MAX_NAME` per script (check the Player screen width with the render fonts).
- One decision with the three locales, or one per locale if the options differ in kind.

## Links
- Every other open task of plan 142 (2–10) gets pending on all three decisions: `pm task-pending-decision <task> <decision>`, so they run in id order once answered.

Done when: three pending decisions with renders and sizes in their bodies; tasks 2–10 of plan 142 pending on them; `work/fonts/` left uncommitted (delete or note it in the decision body that it''s local).', '2026-10-15T20:28:58Z', NULL, 1159, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1176, 142, 'Fonts for ru and zh-Hans in the client and build', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Task 2 of `plan 142: UI in the new languages` (plan "Design: Fonts"); per the font decision raised by task 1 (`pm show` lists it).

- Font files in `app/client/public/fonts/` + their OFL texts; `@font-face` per family with `unicode-range` (Cyrillic, CJK), so a Latin page never loads them.
- `app/client/src/game/theme.css`: `--font-display` / `--font-text` per `:lang(ru)`, `:lang(zh-Hans)` (UI via `<html lang>`, question content via its own `lang`, task 629), fallback chain ending in system Cyrillic/CJK fonts.
- CJK subset script in `app/desktop/` next to `stage-media.mjs` (fonttools from the flake): catalog `zh-Hans.ts` ∪ `app/data/names.zh-Hans.json` ∪ `pool.zh-Hans.json` (if present) ∪ GB2312 level 1; run by `trivia-desktop-build`; the dev client gets a committed subset or the same script via an npm script (pick the simpler, say which in the note).
- `trivia-release-check`: a step that fails on a zh-Hans / Cyrillic character in a shipped catalog, names file or pool missing from the font.
- `app/desktop/media-budget.json`: a `fonts` entry (MB), checked by `stage-media.mjs --check`.
- Credits: `CREDITS.md` source / credits screen (`credits.ts`) list the new fonts with licence.
- `/comodines` (`authoring/ui/src/print/JokerCards.svelte`) loads the same fonts.

Check: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`; `?lang=xx` / es page: network tab loads no Cyrillic/CJK font file; a throw-away page with ru/zh text renders in the new fonts (zh catalog may not exist yet: `names.zh-Hans.json` text suffices).', '2026-10-15T20:28:58Z', NULL, 1159, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1177, 142, 'Wiring of zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR in client, shell and tools', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Task 3 of `plan 142: UI in the new languages`; per the key and picker decisions raised by task 1 (`pm show` lists them) and `decision 222: New UI languages (zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR): offered only once their pool ships`.

- Catalogs `app/client/src/locales/{zh-Hans,ru,pt-BR}.ts`: start as copies of `en.ts` (`satisfies Catalog`), statically imported; tasks 4–6 translate them.
- `lib/i18n.ts`: `CATALOGS`, `ENDONYMS` («简体中文», «Русский», «Português (Brasil)»); `UI_LANGS` / Start''s picker and the first-start guess gated per decision 222 (pool present and its default bundles'' supply passes; else only `?lang=` in dev and under `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER`); es/es-ES/en/de unchanged. `STEAM_LANGS` in `lib/engine.ts` already maps the three.
- Flags per `decision 186: Language flags instead of the globe`: China, Russia, Brazil drawn in `Flags.svelte`.
- `lib/input.svelte.ts` `toIntent`: per the key decision (recommended: `e.code` fallback when `e.key` is a non-Latin letter).
- `picker.letters` per catalog and `MAX_NAME` per the picker decision (`LetterPicker.svelte`, Player screen).
- `check:literals`: ru plural maps need `one`/`few`/`many` (+`other`); every catalog character covered by the locale''s font (after task 2; if task 2''s font files aren''t in yet, add a follow-up task instead).
- `app/desktop/mods.mjs` `LANGS` (`check-mod.mjs` `LOCALES` is `task 1163: New locales zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR in the locale lists and rules`''s); `publish.mjs` Workshop language tags: Steam''s tag names (`schinese`/`russian`/`brazilian` style per Steam''s Workshop tag list), not `split("-")[0]`; modding kit docs (`modding/`) list the languages.
- `authoring/tools/reviews.py` `LABELS` (`decision 142: Report text format (copy fallback, qgen flag)`): Question/Answer/Note labels as the catalogs will say them (take them from the catalog leaves at runtime if simple, else placeholders updated by tasks 4–6).
- `authoring/tools/gallery.py` `LOCALES` += the three.
- `/comodines?lang=`: zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR, all A4 (`@page size`).

Check: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`; `?lang=ru` in the dev client plays with Latin keys on a Russian layout (simulate `e.key` `ф` with `e.code` `KeyA` in a throw-away test); es/es-ES/en/de gallery shots unchanged (`trivia-gallery --only` a few).', '2026-10-15T20:28:58Z', NULL, 1159, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1178, NULL, 'answer: what was the result of the code review?', 'exec', 'done', 10000, '2026-10-15, report answer', 'The owner of this project asks:

what was the result of the code review?

Answer in one paragraph for a busy person who doesn''t read code, tasks or plans: plain, good English in full
sentences, pleasant to read, no jargon, like an executive summary. Find out what you need first: the milestones
(`pm milestone list`, `pm show m<id>`), the code, `git log`, `pm show <id>`, the reports (`pm report list`). Leave out
how the work is managed (decisions, tasks, plans, runs, pm itself) unless the question is about it; never ids or file
names. If the question asks for something to be done, don''t do it: say in the paragraph what it would take.
Change nothing in the project; stage nothing.
Store it: `pm report answer < answer.md`, delete answer.md, then close your task.', '2026-10-15T20:32:24Z', '2026-10-15T20:38:58Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
