INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1182, 17, 'Ambiguity in riddles: generic answers and one question per text (QC batch-8 A)', 'work', 'done', 650, '2026-10-15, authoring/tools/prompts/review.md (reason 2: generic riddle answers checked against every event; reason 6 + style problem: two questions, fix quotes the inner one), house-style.md (Keep it short: one question per text, inner question in «…»), audit.md (check 2: generic riddle answers; quotes rule via house-style). batch-8.md ''Changes from this QC'' line already present.', 'Plan 16 (`plan 16: Quality control after every batch`) is closed, so this change task sits in plan 17 at plan 16''s priority (650), above the -100 batch tasks.

QC batch-8 proposal A, approved in `decision 226: QC batch-8: which changes?` (answer "all"). Source: `authoring/reports/batch-8.md` "## Quality control"; spot-check disagreements q-1868 and q-1733 (`authoring/data/spot-checks.json`, the developer''s feedback on them in `authoring/data/questions.json` reviews).

## Changes
- `authoring/tools/prompts/review.md` reason 2 (second defensible option): for a "¿Quién soy?"/riddle whose answer is generic (a kind of person, not a named one), check each wrong answer against every event the question describes; if a wrong answer could also have done it (q-1868: "un arqueólogo británico" could have thrown a stone into a cave), it''s needs_work; the `fix` adds a detail only the answer has.
- `authoring/tools/prompts/house-style.md` ("Keep it short" or "Format"): the question asks exactly one thing; a rhetorical question or quoted thought inside a riddle goes in quotes («…») so the players don''t hear two questions (q-1733: «¿Con qué grano dejé de merecer mi nombre?» then «¿Qué paradoja soy?»).
- `review.md`: two questions without quotes → needs_work, `fix` adds the quotes.
- Same rule in `audit.md` if its checks list ambiguity/style separately (it reads `house-style.md`; don''t duplicate what it already gets from there).

## Rules
- Prompts only; no `qgen.py` change, no batch run, no pool change.
- Ultra-short wording, matching the prompts'' style.

## Check
- `qgen validate`, `npm run check` clean.
- Then `qgen report --qc batch-8 --changes "<this task id and the task for proposal B>"` if that line isn''t written yet (QC.md step 4).', '2026-10-15T21:45:42Z', '2026-10-15T21:55:43Z', 53, 0, NULL, NULL);
