INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1185, 17, 'run batch-9', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, stopped at rate; fix: task 1369, resume: task 1370', 'Next batch of `plan 17: Batch runs` (per-batch pattern 1), added by `task 53: QC batch-8`. batch-9 is the first English `base` batch (milestone 9, "English-first drafting for `base`"). Follow `authoring/RUNBOOK.md` steps 1–5 exactly, including "Under `pm run`" (plain `qgen batch`; `tasks.sql` alone isn''t a dirty tree; stage exactly the printed `git add` paths, don''t commit).

- Gate first (plan 17 "English-first batches"): RUNBOOK says `qgen batch` drafts `en` for `base`, and `plan 147: English-first batches: calibration, overlap and QC across languages` has no open tasks (`pm show p147`). Either missing: `pm decision add "batch-9: English drafting not in place, wait?"` (body: what is missing), `pm task-pending-decision 1185 <id>`, stop. Never a Spanish `base` draft.
- Waits on `decision 229: Continue batch-9 after the extended batch-8 review?` (the developer''s `qgen health ack batch-8`), after `task 1191: Extended review of batch-8: 120-question spot check (decision 228)`.
- Runs after the change tasks of batch-8''s QC (plan 17 at 650, plan 147 at 700); they outrank -100.
- Exit 2 (health stop), exit 75, exit 1 three times at one step: RUNBOOK "Under `pm run`" / plan 17 "Batch tasks under `pm run`"; never `qgen health ack` by the worker.
