INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1186, 17, 'QC batch-9', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-17, authoring/reports/batch-9.md, authoring/data/questions.json, app/data/pool*.json, rework-4. Decisions: 323 (spot check 30/30 approved by the developer; LLM agreement 28/30 = 93 %, false approve 0, false needs_work 2: q-2301, q-2441, both approved/kept by the developer), no QC proposals (the only disagreements are 2 false needs_work with no shared problem kind; threshold not met), so no ''QC batch-9: which changes?'' decision; report ''Changes from this QC: none''. Numbers: approved base 2890/5000, every difficulty short (deficits 1:153 2:170 3:240 4:221 5:206 6:147 7:192 8:201 9:117 10:109 11:127 12:50 13:53 14:29 15:96); batch-9: 951 merged, 874 approved, 77 needs_work (8.1 %), drop rate 21.6 % ✗ (batch-7/8 13.5/12.7), overlap rate 15.4 % ✗ (2.7/5.5; 165 dropped overlap; language change noted, decision 233), top clue 52.8 % ✗, media share 29.2 % ✓ (13.8/12.2), media: no pick review 1 134, recovered 93, none at record 44; mean fun 3.51, $0.27 per approved, cost $234.67; audit 55/60 agreement 92 %, 1 major on approved; |audit−final| 0.6; needs_work by reason: giveaway 1.6 %, media 5.3 %, style 1.4 %, fact/ambiguity/overlap 0.3 %. Cross-language overlap counts and per-difficulty target-vs-rated tables: not in the report (no tooling), listed as missing. Rework: needs_work 76 → 37 (39 fixed and approved, rework-4; fix step failed once, rerun ok). No media finding beyond the known yield. Next: task 1520: run batch-10, task 1521: QC batch-10 (plan 12 targets not met).', 'QC of batch-9, the first English `base` batch, per `authoring/QC.md` (plan 16) and `plan 17: Batch runs` "Per-batch pattern" 2 and "English-first batches". Runs after `task 1185: run batch-9`; if batch-9 isn''t finished (no `authoring/reports/batch-9.md`), stop without changes.

Phases (the task runs again after each decision is answered; check which decisions exist with `pm show`):
1. `pm decision add "Spot check batch-9 done?"` (body: `/review?batch=batch-9&sample=1` link, size, how to start `trivia-authoring`; option "done"), wait on it, stop. Size: 30 (`decision 234: Spot-check size for batch-9 and batch-10 (first English batches)?`, `quality.spot_check_size`; `qgen.spot_check_size("batch-9")`).
2. `qgen report --qc batch-9`; proposals by QC.md''s threshold rule into `pm decision add "QC batch-9: which changes?"` (options: recommended set / all / none); wait on it, stop. No proposals: skip the decision. Read agreement apart from the es batches (batch-7/8).
3. Approved proposals → change tasks: English-pipeline ones (calibration, translation, cross-language overlap, en prompts) in `plan 147: English-first batches: calibration, overlap and QC across languages` (its priority), or milestone 9''s plan for the switch itself; the rest in plan 17 with `--priority 650`. Then `qgen report --qc batch-9 --changes "<task ids>"`. Record in the note:
   - approved/target per difficulty (`qgen report`, source locale, each question once);
   - difficulty: target vs. rated vs. reviewed per difficulty, compared with batch-7/8 (calibration starts over);
   - health vs. batch-7/8 with the language change noted, not read as drift; trend rule per plan 147 part 4''s decision;
   - overlap against the es-sourced pool too (`decision 232: Overlap of English drafts against the es-sourced base pool: which keys?`); cross-language overlaps found in review, counted;
   - needs_work by reason; media funnel and share from the report (`plan 146: Media yield`).
4. needs_work per `decision 3: How are needs_work questions (33 now, more per batch) resolved?`: `qgen rework --batch batch-9`; exit codes as RUNBOOK step 3 / "Under `pm run`"; stage the printed paths. Note: needs_work count before/after.
5. A new media finding: a task in plan 146, not a new plan.
6. Next: if plan 12''s targets are met (or the next batch would overshoot every remaining gap): add the exit-check task (plan 17 "Exit check"). Else add `run batch-10` and `QC batch-10` with bodies like this pair''s (batch-10 is still a "first English batch" for QC).

Missing tooling: do what exists, list the rest in the note. No prompt or `qgen.py` changes here.

Done when: phase 6 done; note lists decisions, change tasks, numbers.', '2026-10-15T21:51:41Z', '2026-10-17T05:52:31Z', 53, 0, NULL, 'questions');
