INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1194, NULL, 'qgen: scan runs keep media unless fix changed it; review qgen for bugs, follow-up tasks', 'exec', 'done', 900, '2026-10-15, authoring/tools/qgen.py (kept_slots: scan runs keep a slot''s pool pick unless fix changed it or no usable pick; media, research, record skip kept slots; cmd_record and revise_steps docstrings), plans/decisions.md (D-83 media in scan runs). Resume check on a throw-away worktree of pm/task-632-run-1159-left with a copy of work/neutralize-1, claude/search/download stubbed: 0 Claude calls, 0 searches, 1 pick checked (q-0276, fix changed its media), 394 slots of 388 reworded unchanged; 367 approved, 21 needs_work. Follow-ups in plan 17: 1241 (review history through fix/record), 1242 (record progress lines), 1243 (record parallel downloads), 1244 (scan review shows kept pick; prompt change via decision). Task 632 body: restore step (branch file unstaged, 7 research-changed media.query back to main''s, delete branch local + origin), then qgen neutralize.', 'Developer''s intervention (2026-10-15). `task 632: run neutralize-1` was stopped in `record`: the scan modes reuse the rework chain (`revise_steps`, `authoring/tools/qgen.py`), so a wording-only rewrite searched media again and the reviewers re-picked images.

## State of neutralize-1 (don''t lose it)
- `authoring/data/questions.json` on branch `pm/task-632-run-1159-left` (commit `0b795c2`, pushed; not on main): stash merged per `decision 214: neutralize-1: qgen validate fails after fix`, `fix` applied, 377 reworded questions in `draft` with `review: null`; `record` never ran, so no pick reached the pool.
- `work/neutralize-1/reviews/<id>.json`: round 1 and 2 reviews with new picks. Of 375 reworded questions with media: 70 same URL, 213 same file but thumbnail (3840px) → original URL, 92 a different image (e.g. q-0004).
- `record` was downloading every uncached pick serially (`media.checked` → `download.cached`), ~47 per 10 min, 294 left; no output (`progress.verbose = False`).
- Don''t change that branch; don''t run `qgen neutralize` here.

## 1. Fix (this task)
- Scan modes (`neutralize`, `tighten`; `SCANS`): media is out of scope unless `fix` changed `media`/`background` (`fix.changed`) or the question had no usable pick. Then no new media search and no re-pick: `record` keeps the pool''s `media`/`background` fields as they are, no download.
- `qgen rework` keeps its new media search (QG-23).
- Resuming `neutralize-1` with the fixed code must reach `record` without new claude calls (reviews on disk stay valid) and keep the 375 questions'' current picks. Check in a throw-away worktree of `pm/task-632-run-1159-left` with the fixed `qgen.py` (temp `TRIVIA_WORK`/`TRIVIA_STATE` with a copy of `work/neutralize-1`, as in `code-review.md`''s temp-worktree checks).
- `cmd_record`''s docstring ("without downloading") is stale since task 1181: fix it.
- Update `authoring/RUNBOOK.md` / `plans/decisions.md` (D-83) if they describe the scan modes'' media step.

## 2. Review qgen generally
- Read `authoring/tools/qgen.py` and the modules it calls (`media.py`, `download.py`, `translations.py`, `targets.py`, …) for bugs of this kind: steps that do more than their mode needs, state lost on resume, silent long steps, history lost, docstrings that no longer hold.
- Known so far (each a follow-up task, not fixed here unless trivial):
  - `fix` sets `review: None` on reworded questions (scan modes, rework): the earlier review (incl. a human approval) is lost; keep it as `previous`.
  - Long steps without progress output (`record`''s downloads with `progress.verbose = False`).
  - Serial downloads in `record`.
- Every bug found: `pm task add <plan> "<subject>"` with what, where, how to reproduce, how to tell it''s fixed, in the plan that owns the area (`pm plan list`; qgen pipeline work: plan 17 `Batch runs` unless a better one fits), priority above -85 so it runs before content runs. A choice only the developer can make: `pm decision add`.
- Don''t change prompts, the pool or media (D-36).

## Done when
- Scan modes keep media as described; the throw-away resume check passes; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` (on a clean tree) pass.
- Follow-up tasks added; note lists the fix''s files and the follow-up task ids.
- `task 632: run neutralize-1`''s body (`pm task set 632 --body -`, open again once pm recorded run 1159 as failed) gets a first step: restore `authoring/data/questions.json` from `pm/task-632-run-1159-left` into the working tree, unstaged (as pm''s stash would), conflicts with main''s later changes resolved per question (main''s version wins where main changed a question), then delete the branch (local and `origin`); only then plain `qgen neutralize`. Don''t restore it in this task: pm would move a closed task''s unstaged leftovers to a branch.
- If pm queued "investigate the failure of task 632": its body can''t be known here; the 632 body step above is what it and 632 see.', '2026-10-16T00:11:43Z', '2026-10-16T00:45:10Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
