INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1241, 17, 'qgen: keep the earlier review as previous through fix and record', 'work', 'done', -80, '2026-10-16, authoring/tools/qgen.py (cmd_fix keeps the old review as top-level previous; review_before: cmd_record and record_translations chain it into review.previous, also on a re-record; review_problems accepts previous under an llm review), authoring/ui/src/review/ReviewBanners.svelte (human previous shown as developer), plans/02-question-pool.md. Checked with a stubbed tighten run: human-approved question → fix → record twice ends with review.previous = the human review.', 'Found by `task 1194: qgen: scan runs keep media unless fix changed it; review qgen for bugs, follow-up tasks`. A question''s earlier review (incl. a human approval or the developer''s needs_work feedback) is lost when a run rewords it.

## What
- `authoring/tools/qgen.py` `cmd_fix` (`work()` → `change`): in `qgen rework` and the scan modes (`neutralize`, `tighten`; `SCANS`) a revised (rework: also kept) question gets `status: draft, review: None`.
- `cmd_record` then writes `review = {…, "previous": None}`; `record_translations` (`review_of`) the same for a re-translated question.
- So `review.previous` never holds the review before the run; the review tool and QC can''t show "was approved by the developer, reworded by neutralize-1".

## Fix
- `cmd_fix`: keep the old review where record finds it, e.g. `x["review"] = {"previous": x["review"]}` or a `review_before` field; record sets `previous` to it (chain as `reviews.py` does for human reviews: check how `reviews.py` writes `previous` and reuse it, decision 199).
- Same for `record_translations` (the translation''s earlier review).
- `qgen validate`''s review checks (`review_problems`) must accept the draft-state shape you choose.
- No change to prompts, the pool''s existing entries or media (D-36).

## Reproduce / done when
- Throw-away worktree, temp `TRIVIA_WORK` with a small `qgen rework` or `qgen tighten` run (or a script calling `cmd_fix`/`cmd_record` with `claude` stubbed): an approved question with `review.reviewer: "human"` that is revised ends with `review.previous` = that human review.
- `npm run check`, `qgen validate` pass.', '2026-10-16T00:44:14Z', '2026-10-16T04:05:57Z', 1194, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1242, 17, 'qgen record: progress lines for its downloads', 'work', 'done', -80, '2026-10-15, authoring/tools/qgen.py, authoring/tools/media.py: cmd_record collects its picks first, then check_picks() downloads/checks them with a start line (N pick(s) to download), a waiting() start/result line per uncached download and a Bar summary; shared media.downloading() (item + waiting) now used by media cmd_sync, qgen cmd_sync_run and record (decision 199). Ready for task 1243: Download picks in parallel (swap check_picks'' loop for parallel()). Checked with a throw-away script (temp TRIVIA_MEDIA/WORK, local HTTP server: ok, truncated → file_problem, 404 → not checked, cached → no line); npm run check/test/build, qgen validate pass.', 'Found by `task 1194: qgen: scan runs keep media unless fix changed it; review qgen for bugs, follow-up tasks`. `record` ran ~1 h silently in `task 632: run neutralize-1` (run 1159) before the developer stopped it.

## What
- `authoring/tools/qgen.py` `cmd_record`: every pick goes through `media_tool.checked` → `download.cached` (task 1181), with no `progress.waiting` line and no `progress.Bar`; the per-question `progress.detail` is off under `qgen batch`/`rework`/`tighten`/`neutralize` (`progress.verbose = False`). A run with hundreds of uncached picks prints nothing for an hour.
- Compare `cmd_sync_run`: `progress.item` + `progress.waiting(f"download {host}")` per file and a `Bar`.

## Fix
- In `cmd_record`, wrap the check in `progress.item("record", label)` + `progress.waiting(...)` like `cmd_sync_run` (only for uncached URLs, `media.cache_path(url).is_file()`), and a `progress.Bar("record", n, "downloads")` or a `progress.resumed`-style line with the number to download.
- Reuse `cmd_sync_run`''s pattern; don''t copy it twice (decision 199): a small shared helper if it fits.

## Done when
- A record step with uncached picks prints a start/result line per download and a summary line; `npm run check` passes.
- Check with a throw-away script (temp `TRIVIA_WORK`/`TRIVIA_MEDIA`) and 2–3 picks; no test.', '2026-10-16T00:44:15Z', '2026-10-16T04:08:03Z', 1194, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1243, 17, 'qgen record: download picks in parallel', 'work', 'done', -80, '2026-10-15, authoring/tools/qgen.py: check_picks downloads in a thread pool (--jobs, default 3; standalone qgen record gets --jobs). Throw-away run, 20 uncached Commons picks, temp TRIVIA_WORK/TRIVIA_MEDIA: serial 18.4 s, 4 jobs 4.7 s, same file_problem results; npm run check passes.', 'Found by `task 1194: qgen: scan runs keep media unless fix changed it; review qgen for bugs, follow-up tasks`. In `task 632: run neutralize-1` (run 1159) `record` downloaded ~47 picks per 10 min, serially (294 left when stopped).

## What
- `authoring/tools/qgen.py` `cmd_record`: the loop over questions calls `media_tool.checked(fields)` (download + `file_problem`) one pick at a time.
- `download.cached` is already thread-safe (per-URL lock); `parallel()` in qgen.py runs work with `--jobs`.

## Fix
- First collect every pick (question, slot, fields), then check the uncached ones with `parallel(...)` (args.jobs; record''s `ns()` has `jobs`), then build reviews and the one `update_pool` as now. Mind Commons'' rate limits (`download.http_get` waits out 429s); keep the jobs modest.
- Combine with `qgen record: progress lines for its downloads` if both are open (same code).
- Keep task 1181''s behaviour: a download failure leaves the pick unchecked (`sync` checks again), a broken file → `file_problem` → licence verdict `replace` → needs_work.

## Done when
- Throw-away run (temp `TRIVIA_WORK`/`TRIVIA_MEDIA`, ~20 uncached picks, `claude` not needed): wall time well below the serial one, same `file_problem` results; `npm run check` passes.', '2026-10-16T00:44:15Z', '2026-10-16T04:09:24Z', 1194, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1244, 17, 'qgen scan runs: review shows the kept pick, not candidates', 'work', 'done', -80, '2026-10-16, authoring/tools/prompts/review.md (qgen.py kept-slot payload already in)', 'Found by `task 1194: qgen: scan runs keep media unless fix changed it; review qgen for bugs, follow-up tasks`. Since task 1194, a scan run (`neutralize`, `tighten`; `SCANS`) keeps a slot''s pool pick (`kept_slots` in `authoring/tools/qgen.py`): no search, research, re-pick or download. The review still sees the old input.

## What
- `cmd_review` still sends `slot_input` for kept slots: the cached candidates, the contact sheet and `can_search_again: true`; the reviewer picks among candidates (ignored by `record`), may answer `pick: null` + `new_query` (research then skips it) and, per `prompts/review.md` ("If no candidate is adequate … decide needs_work"), may set `needs_work` for a media problem that `record` no longer acts on. In neutralize-1''s resume check, 1 of 21 needs_work had only `["media"]` as problem.
- `cmd_sheets` still builds contact sheets (preview downloads) for kept slots.
- `revise_in_pool`: any difference in the `media` dict (e.g. only `note` or `role`) counts as changed `media`, so the candidates are deleted and the slot leaves `kept_slots` though the file stays (only a `type`/`query` change unpicks it). Decide whether `kept_slots` should look at `type`/`query` instead of `fix.changed`.

## Fix
- For kept slots: the payload shows the kept pick (type, role, query, note, title via `media_title`, like `translation_payload`), no candidates/sheet, `can_search_again: false`; `cmd_sheets` skips them.
- `prompts/review.md` needs a line for that case (like `translate-review.md`''s "Media" line): judge the kept file against the new wording (giveaway, fit), leave `pick`/`background_pick`/`new_query` null. A prompt change: show the developer the exact text first (`pm decision add`, D-36), then apply.
- `record`: a kept slot with a media problem from the reviewer → needs_work with that feedback (today the model''s decision already stands; check it stays so).

## Done when
- A scan run''s review of a kept slot gets no candidates and no sheet; record keeps the pick; `npm run check`, `qgen validate` pass. Check with `claude` stubbed in a throw-away worktree (print the payload).', '2026-10-16T00:44:15Z', '2026-10-16T16:26:50Z', 1194, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1245, 148, 'base bundle rule and voice for English-first drafting', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, decision 240: base bundle rule and voice for English-first drafting: apply? (base.rule, base.voice, qgen.py VOICE as old → new); tasks 1185 and 1239 pending on it, 1239''s body applies it; no file changed', 'Follow-up of `task 1234: qgen batch drafts en for base: the whole chain on the question''s locale`. Part of `plan 148: English-first drafting for base`.

- `app/data/bundles.json` `base.rule` says "answerable by the players anywhere in the Spanish-speaking world, including well-known facts about Colombia"; `base.voice` is "neutral Latin American Spanish (es-419) … and in Spain".
- `qgen draft` puts the rule into every draft call''s user message (`bundle_text(bundle, locale)` in `authoring/tools/qgen.py`); English drafts (`locale` en) already leave the Spanish `voice` out, but the rule still steers `base` drafts towards the Spanish-speaking world, against milestone 9''s international angle.
- `rule` is also read by `qgen bundles` (membership) and shown nowhere in the game; `voice` feeds `{voices}` in `prompts/locale-es.md`.
- Draft new wording (international rule; `es` voice idiomatic Latin American, no "and in Spain") as verbatim old → new for the developer, like `task 1238: English-first prompt drafts for the developer` (one decision there or its own: `pm decision add`), and make `task 1185: run batch-9` pending on it.', '2026-10-16T01:05:46Z', '2026-10-16T01:25:20Z', 1234, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1246, 147, 'English keys for the review''s related questions', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, authoring/tools/qgen.py: related_questions matches an en question''s answer against as_locale(pool, "en") with overlap_norm(…, "en"), returns the originals; review and audit precompute the view (pool_en); check: en "Coffee" lists q-0001, 89 sampled es questions'' related lists identical to before', '`plan 147: English-first batches: calibration, overlap and QC across languages`, part 3, follow-up of `task 1205: English keys for the overlap check against the es-sourced pool`.

- `related_questions` (`authoring/tools/qgen.py`, used by the review step) matches pool questions by `norm()` of the answer (same or ≥ 0.7 similar) or same subcategory; an en question ("Coffee") never finds an es question with «El café» in another subcategory.
- Task 1205 added `as_locale(questions, "en")` (English view: en translation''s text, else `authoring/data/english-keys.json`''s answer + concept; the original under `"of"`) and `overlap_norm(text, locale)`.
- Match an en question''s answer against `as_locale(pool, "en")` with `overlap_norm(…, "en")`; return the original''s fields (`p.get("of", p)`); es questions unchanged.
