- `qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>` for a non-Spanish region on part 16''s slugs + en names (no Spanish keys): `taxonomy.md` without the Spanish-world assumptions (base''s audience, samples in the bundle''s language); the bundle''s voice reaches its own language''s names (British spelling in `uk`''s `names.en.json`); the general list''s `{región}` pattern for en names (and es/de names drafted on `--apply`) as part 16 leaves it.
- Spanish-only helpers in the chain (`norm()`, number style, Spanish lints, dedupe) checked for `de` and `es-ES` drafts, as plan 148 task 4 did for `en`.
- `--translate en --bundle <id>` from `de` and `es-ES` sources: `translate-region.md`''s `{source_language}`; `qgen validate`''s "regional sources in the region''s language" holds for the new languages.
- Prompt changes: redraft verbatim old → new on top of part 16''s applied prompts: `taxonomy.md`, `taxonomy-names.md`, `authoring/data/regional-categories.json` (slugs + en names); `locale-en.md`, `locale-es.md`, `locale-es-ES.md`, `locale-de.md`, `translate-region.md` mostly as in decision 250 (parts 4–8). `pm decision add "Regional drafting in en, de, es-ES: prompts apply? (after slug keys)"` with the drafts, `pm task-pending-decision 1275 <id>`, stage the code done so far, stop. On the answer: apply as answered (or `pm task add` a follow-up in plan 98 if the answer asks for more), `pm decision consequences <id> "…"`; `pm decision consequences 250 "…"` (superseded by the new decision).
- Throw-away check on a scratch copy (decision 208 reporting for every claude call): a fake `de` region and a fake `en` region with a British voice: `qgen taxonomy --bundle` proposal (slugs + en names), then `qgen batch --bundle` up to `draft` for one subcategory: German / British text, `locale` right; one `de` source → `--translate en --bundle` selection picks it. The game offers an en-only pack only to an en save, a de pack to de, and to en once `languages` lists both. Remove the copy.
- Docs: `authoring/RUNBOOK.md` (`--bundle` drafts in the bundle''s language and variety), D-36 note in `plans/decisions.md` if its wording assumes Spanish, `plans/22-bundles.md`; `rg` for "Spanish usage" and similar in comments and `.md` (decision 200).

