INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1276, 98, 'Set up regional bundle usa', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, app/data/bundles/usa/{categories,names.en,names.es,names.de}.json, app/client/src/engine/{pool,choice}.test.ts', 'Plan 98 part 11 (tasks 11–15, in the order `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`). Creates the regional bundle `usa` (US English; languages: `["en"]`) with its taxonomy and 2000 target, so `task 1268: Regional runs usa: start` (plan 84 chain 5) can run its first `qgen batch --bundle usa`. Same rules as `colombia` (`decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)`, amended by milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15): 2000 approved, region''s language + en (en regions en only), free DLC, off by default, own bundle-scoped taxonomy keyed by English slugs, display names only from `names.<locale>.json` (milestone 9''s slug keys, developer 2026-10-16; masterplan part 16) (`decision 213: General category list for regional bundles`, `plan 138: Regional taxonomy: a general list, colombia reworked`).

## Before starting
- Needs `task 1275: Regional drafting in any launch language (en US/UK, de, es-ES, es)` done (`--language en`, voice in any language) and part 16''s slug keys applied (plan from `task 1305: write plan: Slug keys for categories`: slugs as keys, `names.<locale>.json`, `qgen taxonomy` proposing slugs + en names). Either open → `pm task-pending-decision <this task>` on its pending decision, or stop and say so.

## Do
- `qgen bundle new usa --kind region --language en` with drafted `name`, `description` (the game''s text, in en), `rule` and `voice` (US English). `rule`: questions need a connection to the region; disjoint from `base` and the other regional bundles (`uk` vs `usa`: US-only topics here, British-only there; topics shared across the English-speaking world belong to neither, i.e. `base`). 2000 target written by `bundle new` (D-101); en/de names for the bundle where the game needs them. Obvious wording is yours (`pm decision record` only for a lasting choice); the developer sees `rule`/`voice` in the taxonomy decision below.
- `qgen taxonomy --bundle usa`; `pm decision add "usa taxonomy: categories and subcategories"` with the proposal (slug + en name per category and subcategory, the bundle''s language name beside it where not en; counts per category, recommended option first) and the bundle''s `rule`/`voice`; `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <id>`; stage what is done, stop. On the answer: `qgen taxonomy --bundle usa --apply …` as answered (writes slugs and `names.<locale>.json` for en, es, de), `pm decision consequences <id> "…"`, `qgen validate`, `qgen export`.
- DLC follow-ups, unless an open task there already covers `usa` (`pm show p130`, `p89`, `p88`): `pm task add` in `plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)` (DLC app + `steam.json` `dlc` entry), `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)` (its depot, like task 748), `plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)` (store text + capsules, in en). Each body names the bundle, its languages and the en rule (en joins `languages` once en translations exist; en regions en only).
- `plans/22-bundles.md` and `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` list `usa` (languages, rule, target, start task).
- Not here: concept lists (the bundle''s first `qgen batch --bundle usa`), any batch run.

## Done when
- `app/data/bundles.json` has `usa` (`languages` as above, rule, voice), `targets.json` 2000, its slug-keyed taxonomy applied as answered (names in `names.<locale>.json`); `qgen validate`, `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build` pass.
- Plans 130, 89, 88 have a DLC task for `usa`; 22 and 15c list it.', '2026-10-16T03:40:04Z', '2026-10-16T21:26:08Z', 1273, 0, NULL, 'questions');
