    - More regional bundles (milestone, developer 2026-10-15; replaces decision 110''s "more bundles only after a new decision with the pilot''s numbers"): by Steam audience in the launch languages (share of Steam download bandwidth, GameDiscoverCo 2024), in this order: `usa` (en, ≈20 %), `germany` (de + en, ≈4.4 %), `uk` (en, ≈3.3 %), `spain` (es-ES + en), `mexico` (es + en); later candidates `canada`, `australia`, `argentina` (no work now).
      - same rules as `colombia`: 2000 approved each, region''s language + en (en regions: en only), free DLC, off by default; own taxonomy from the general regional list via `qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>`, after part 16 (slugs + en names; decision 250: Regional drafting in en, de, es-ES: prompts apply? → redraft after slug keys) (`plan 138: Regional taxonomy: a general list, colombia reworked`; decision 213: General category list for regional bundles), one pm decision per bundle with the proposal
      - drafted in the region''s language and variety: US English, British English, German, Spain''s Spanish, Mexican Spanish (`bundles.json` `rule`/`voice`; prompt changes the developer''s); `qgen batch --bundle <id>` drafts in the bundle''s source language, not always `es` (shares part 15''s en drafting; de and es-ES drafting new); `--translate en --bundle <id>` from de and es-ES (new directions beyond part 4''s es → L and part 15''s en → L)
      - per bundle: `qgen bundle new --kind region`, taxonomy decision, target in `targets.json`; each starts once `colombia`''s taxonomy (decision 249: colombia taxonomy: categories and subcategories) and its first `qgen batch --bundle colombia` have proven the chain, not after colombia''s 2000
      - each its DLC entry like `colombia`: `steam.json` `dlc`, DLC app and depot (`plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)`, `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`), store texts and capsules (`plan 88: Store page and AI disclosure (PUB-8, LUI-6)`); part 10''s plan adds a follow-up task to each of them per bundle
      - the family''s save keeps base + `colombia` (D-59); the new bundles off by default
    - Suggested priority: 300.

11. **Release content runs**
    - The recurring `qgen batch` tasks: translation pilot (QT-5: 50 questions per language, measure reject rate and cost, go/no-go pm decision), then full translation per language (QT-6), neutral Spanish (part 8), regional bundle batches (part 10), and `base` top-ups where the simulation fails after milestone 1''s 5000. Each batch followed by D-56''s QC (plan 16 procedure, `authoring/QC.md`), native-speaker spot checks for translations.
    - English-first `base` (part 15): `plan 17: Batch runs`'' batches draft `en` from batch-9 on (`task 1185: run batch-9`, decision 229: Continue batch-9 after the extended batch-8 review?); here their translation runs en → `es`, `es-ES`, `de`, and the es-sourced pool''s `es-ES` runs (besides `en`, `de`). No more Spanish `base` drafts or `es` top-ups.
    - Order inside: pilot first (priority -90, above the runs; its go/no-go decides the full runs, its cost is information for `qgen report --cost`); full runs after milestone 1''s batch runs (plan 17) so translations don''t go stale.
    - Regional pilot (decision 110): `qgen batch --bundle colombia` run/QC pairs from 102 to 2000 approved, then `--translate en --bundle colombia` pairs to 2000 en; effort recorded ($ per approved, review time per 100) in `plans/15c-regional-questions.md` / `16-content-target.md`; it sets the pace of the other bundles, no "More regional bundles?" decision (milestone, developer 2026-10-15).
    - More regional bundles (part 10): once colombia''s first batch has proven the chain, run/QC pairs per bundle in audience order `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico`, each to 2000 approved in its language, then `--translate en --bundle <id>` pairs for `germany`, `spain`, `mexico`; interleaved with colombia''s runs at the pace the pilot''s numbers allow.
    - Launch doesn''t wait for the regional chain: it ships what `colombia` has then; content updates (plan 96) bring the rest.
    - Suggested priority: -110 (after plan 17''s -100).

