- `pm decision consequences 264 "<text>"`: what changed because of its answer (flow Player → Choice «Seguir» → Bundles → Level, supply report and notice on Bundles, narrow base column with toggle tiles, ruler, flowing tiles, highlighting, counts; tasks 1360, 1361, 1379)
- `pm decision add "Bundle screen (flowing tiles) reviewed in /gallery?"` for the developer (a go-ahead, like decision 264): intro, body lists the shots and what changed since decision 264 (incl. any combination and the start check); options "approved" (recommended), "problems (listed in the answer)"; `pm task-pending-decision 1340 <id>`
- On the answer: approved → mark the gallery flag on `choice-gamemaster` in `authoring/data/ui-flags.json` fixed, then done. Problems → fix them in this task (no fix tasks), re-run the affected shots at both sizes, `pm decision consequences <answered decision> "…"`, a new review decision listing what changed, `pm task-pending-decision 1340 <id>`, stage, stop.

## Done when
- Shots for all four locales at both sizes, decision 264''s consequences recorded (263''s are already), the latest review decision answered "approved"', '2026-10-16T13:57:26Z', '2026-10-17T18:35:42Z', 1336, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1341, 57, 'qgen validate: spot-checks.json depends on gitignored work/<run>/run.json', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, authoring/tools/qgen.py (run_ids falls back to spot-checks.json ids; validate reads run members from the entry''s ids), authoring/server/spot_checks.py (record stores ids), authoring/data/spot-checks.json (neutralize-1 ids backfilled; backaudit-1 has no entry yet, gets ids on its first record), authoring/ui/src/lib/types.ts, authoring/QC.md; qgen validate passes in a fresh worktree without work/', '- `qgen validate` fails in `../trivia-review`: `authoring/data/spot-checks.json: no batch ''neutralize-1'' in the pool`; passes in the main checkout
- Cause: `run_ids()` (`authoring/tools/qgen.py`) reads a back-audit/neutralize run''s ids from `work/<run>/run.json`, gitignored; a fresh worktree or clone has none
- Fix: keep the run''s ids in tracked data (e.g. `ids` in its `spot-checks.json` entry, or a tracked run file), so validate needs nothing under `work/`; check `backaudit-1` the same way
- Check: `qgen validate` passes in a worktree without `work/`', '2026-10-16T14:44:07Z', '2026-10-16T14:46:18Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
