- Done note: anything the built result does differently from the decisions above (task 3 uses it).', '2026-10-16T21:21:09Z', '2026-10-17T04:16:34Z', 1469, 0, 'opus', 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1474, 167, 'The developer: each multiplayer mode on the TV with the family', 'work', 'open', 120, NULL, 'Part 2 of `plan 167: Local multiplayer close-out and family playtest`: raise one checklist decision for the developer''s family playtest of all three modes, wait for it, then route the result. Workers never play with real pads or answer for the developer.

## Wait first
- `task 1473: Headless: every multiplayer mode start to finish, release-check step multiplayer` done; else stop without closing and say so.

## First run: raise the decision
- `pm decision add "Local multiplayer: each mode played on the TV with the family?" --once --intro "…"`; intro in plain English: what the developer tries and what the answer changes.
- Body written against what was built (commands, mode ids, names, keys, menu labels checked by `rg` in `app/`, not copied from the plan):
  - setup: the `beta` build under Steam if `plan 166: Shipping the multiplayer modes and docs` put the modes in `BUILT_MODES` and the build is uploaded (Steam Input as players have it); else `trivia-desktop` with `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1` (dev mode, `decision 293: Unbuilt multiplayer modes: on the mode row in dev mode only`); answer says which
  - rows per mode (`rr-coop`, `rr-competitive`, `timed`): pads only; keyboard only (timed: claim keys picked on Join, answer per `decision 275: Timed mode, keyboard-only: how does the claimer answer in the 6 seconds?`); 4 pads + keyboard and mouse, or every pad the developer owns + keyboard and mouse (note the count; whether a 5th pad is listed, task 1431''s finding)
  - each row start to finish; plus: prompts follow the last input, each pad''s glyphs on its turn; a pad unplugged and replugged mid-session (`decision 289: Local multiplayer: a controller lost mid-session waits for a controller to take the seat`); Esc menu from any seat; timed drama: heartbeat, last-3-s ticks, red frame, sudden death, with sound (`TRIVIA_SOUND=1` off-Steam); text fits on the TV
  - answer format: date, build, ✓/✗ per row + note
- Options: "passed" (recommended) | "failed (list: mode, setup, screen, what happened)".
- `pm task-pending-decision 1474 <decision>` and stop without closing.

## After the answer
- ✗ rows → follow-up tasks per plan 167''s routing (save shape, resume → plan 157; round-robin rules → 158; timed rules → 159; achievements, telemetry → 160; wrong seat, claim inputs, lost pad, Esc menu → 161; mode row, Join, setup → 162; round-robin screens → 163; timed screens → 164; strings → 165; `BUILT_MODES`, store, Steamworks achievements → 166; a done plan: `pm plan add 16 …` named after the failure); plus one task in plan 167 "Family playtest again" (worktree `app`, priority 120) that raises a new decision of the same shape once those follow-ups are done (as decision 155 followed decision 50).
- Passed → `pm decision consequences 284 "C: passed per decision <id>"` (`decision 284: Remote Play Together gate: single player, controller input and local multiplayer playtested?` stays the developer''s to answer).

## Done when
- The decision is answered and routed as above; done note names the decision id and the result.', '2026-10-16T21:21:33Z', NULL, 1469, 0, NULL, 'app');
