INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1477, 89, 'Release check: name the shipped Steamworks SDK libs'' version', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, app/desktop/steam-libs.mjs, app/desktop/steam-sdk-versions.json, authoring/steam/release_check.py, plans/18-steam-integration.md', 'Packaged builds ship whatever `libsteam_api.so`/`steam_api64.dll` sit in the gitignored `app/desktop/steamworks_sdk/redistributable_bin/` (`electron-builder.yml` `extraResources`, `steam-libs.mjs` only checks they exist). In the trunk (2026-10-16) these are a newer SDK than `decision 69: Steamworks SDK libs for dev and the bridge''s SDK path`''s 1.62 (the flake''s dev libs): they export `SteamAPI_SteamRemotePlay_v004`, `GetSessionGuestID`, session avatars, which 1.62 lacks (found by task 1418). Dev under `TRIVIA_STEAM_SDK` and the shipped build can so differ silently.

- `steam-libs.mjs` (or the release check''s header): print the shipped libs'' identity: sha256 and the SDK version, matched against a small table of known hashes (1.62 Linux `libsteam_api.so` md5 `4b7a8cabaa354fcd25743aabfb4b1366` from the flake''s zip; add the local libs'' after identifying their SDK zip), "unknown" otherwise
- `trivia-release-check` header gets a row "Steamworks SDK libs: <version or unknown>"; no failure, information only, unless the developer wants a pin (then a decision)
- `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Builds and depots" line about SDK libs: say which SDK ships
- Done when: the release check report names the libs'' SDK version', '2026-10-16T21:26:10Z', '2026-10-16T21:45:00Z', 1418, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1478, 168, 'Remote Play probe switch in the shell', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, app/desktop/main.mjs, app/desktop/package.json, app/desktop/package-lock.json, README.md, AGENTS.md', 'Part of `plan 168: Investigation: Remote Play input and session API`: a throw-away probe switch in the Electron shell, so the developer''s live test (`decision 302: Remote Play Together live probe: guests'' pads, keyboard and mouse on a Windows and a Linux host`) can log what Steam Remote Play delivers. Not gated by `decision 284: Remote Play Together gate: single player, controller input and local multiplayer playtested?` (probe only, removed by `task 1479: Remote Play findings and the distinct-player answer`).

## What
- `--rp-probe` flag (works as a Steam launch option on Windows and Linux) in `app/desktop/main.mjs`; all probe code in one block marked `PLACEHOLDER(1479)`
- after `startSteam`: own koffi load per `decision 301: Remote Play API from the shell: own koffi load of the Steam library, v003 calls, sessions by polling` (same lib as the binding via `steamSdkDir()`, newest `SteamAPI_SteamRemotePlay_v00N` accessor, only v003 flat calls); koffi a direct dependency of `app/desktop` at the binding''s version (3.3.3)
- poll on the existing 100 ms `runCallbacks` tick:
  - sessions diffed → `session +` / `session -` (session id, Steam id, name, form factor; mark guest vs host''s own id)
  - `GetInput` events → `rp key` (session, scancode, modifiers, char, down/up) / `rp mouse` (session, motion/button/wheel, normalized position or deltas)
- every second: `steam-input` (handles, input type, `GetRemotePlaySessionID`, `GetGamepadIndexForController`) and, from the page via `executeJavaScript`, `pads` (`navigator.getGamepads()`: index, id, pressed buttons)
- window input: `before-input-event` → `dom key`; page `pointermove`/`pointerdown` listeners → `dom mouse` (throttled)
- keys: F9 direct input on/off (starts off; logs the call''s result), F10 custom guest cursor (`CreateMouseCursor` BGRA + `SetMouseCursor` for every session), F11 flash a white frame and log ms until the next guest pad press
- log to `<userData>/rp-probe.log` and stderr; path printed at start; path and last 8 lines in an on-screen corner box
- without `--rp-probe`: nothing changes (no koffi load, no listeners)

## Docs
- `--rp-probe` in the README''s `trivia-desktop` row and `AGENTS.md` Commands (`trivia-desktop` line); removed again by `task 1479: Remote Play findings and the distinct-player answer`

## Done when
- headless check (Spacewar 480, Steam running): `trivia-desktop --rp-probe` starts, logs 0 sessions, F9 toggles direct input (result logged), the corner box shows the log path; no guest needed
- usual checks (`npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`)
- no upload: the `beta` build for the developer''s live test goes through `plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`''s `trivia-steam upload`', '2026-10-16T21:26:24Z', '2026-10-16T21:39:34Z', 1476, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1479, 168, 'Remote Play findings and the distinct-player answer', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Part of `plan 168: Investigation: Remote Play input and session API`: turn the developer''s live probe notes into findings, the binding answer later parts wait for, and remove the probe. Waits for `decision 302: Remote Play Together live probe: guests'' pads, keyboard and mouse on a Windows and a Linux host` (which itself needs the Steamworks switch and test setup of `plan 153: masterplan` part 2; if that part''s setup decision exists when this runs, check it''s answered).

## Findings
- the decision''s notes and log into `plans/14-input.md` section "Remote Play Together" (replaces "works for free"): guests'' pads per host OS (Windows, Linux/SteamOS), the pad ↔ guest mapping that works (Steam Input session id + gamepad index vs `Gamepad.index`, or connect order), direct input facts (window kept clean? host unaffected? guest cursor), Steam''s per-guest overlay toggles, session ids on leave/rejoin, pad vs session disconnect order (for `decision 283: Remote Play Together: what happens when a remote guest leaves mid-game?`), rough lag from F11

## The answer
- `pm decision record "Remote Play Together: can a remote guest''s keyboard and mouse be a distinct player?"` with intro, answer «yes» or «no» plus mechanism, body with the evidence; per the plan''s answer rule:
  - «yes»: on both hosts direct input keeps a guest''s keyboard and mouse out of the window and delivers them per session, host input unaffected, guest sees a usable cursor (Steam''s or `SetMouseCursor`''s)
  - «no» otherwise; mechanism to ignore remote keyboard and mouse: direct input on with events dropped if it keeps them out of the window, else Steam''s per-guest toggles (join screen tells the host)
  - works on one host only: «no» (one rule on every OS), the gap noted for a later look
- if guests'' pads don''t reach `navigator.getGamepads()` on a host: `pm decision add` for the developer (read guests'' pads through Steam Input in the shell, or that host unsupported) instead of guessing; make the open parts pending on it

## Cleanup (decision 200)
- remove the `PLACEHOLDER(<this task>)` probe block from `app/desktop/main.mjs`, the koffi dependency if nothing else uses it (part 3 re-adds it), the `--rp-probe` lines in README and `AGENTS.md`; `rg rp-probe` comes back empty outside `plans/` history notes

## Done when
- findings in `plans/14-input.md`, the decision recorded, probe gone, usual checks pass', '2026-10-16T21:26:33Z', NULL, 1476, 0, 'opus', 'app');
