   - Steps `translate --to L` (adapt units, answer format, hints that play on Spanish words; detect non-travelling questions → propose `translatable: false`) → `rate --locale L` (difficulty for that language''s main market, D-38 scale) → `factcheck --locale L` → review (D-32/D-33) → audit (D-56) → merge into the locale file. Only `approved`, translatable sources; skips done ones; costs in `costs.log`.
   - No human control of translations (milestone, developer 2026-10-16): `qgen health` drops decision 45: Health thresholds and selection order for qgen batch --translate runs''s "the pilot tr-<locale>-1 always stops the next run" (thresholds stay); `authoring/QC.md` "Translation runs" loses the spot check, RUNBOOK and plans 15b (QT-5, QT-6) follow; `pm decision record … --supersedes 45` for that clause.
