INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1508, 171, 'qgen health and the review tool: no pilot stop, no spot-check prompt', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, authoring/tools/health.py, authoring/tools/qgen.py, authoring/ui/src/home/Home.svelte', '`plan 171: Translations without human control`, part 1. Milestone 9 (developer, 2026-10-16): the LLM translation review is a translation''s only review; no native-speaker spot check per `tr-*` run, no pilot go/no-go, no ack after a pilot. Thresholds of `decision 45: Health thresholds and selection order for qgen batch --translate runs` stay: a `tr-*` run with a ✗ still stops the next `qgen batch --translate <L>` (exit 2) until `qgen health ack <run>` (the developer''s). See also `decision 305: Spot check tr-en-1 done?`, `decision 306: Spot check tr-de-1 done?`, `decision 308: Spot check tr-es-ES-1 done?`.

## What
- `authoring/tools/health.py`:
  - `translate_stop_reason` (~l. 305): drop the pilot clause ("… was the pilot of {locale} (QT-5). The developer decides on it …"); only the last done run''s threshold failures stop, until `qgen health ack`; fix its docstring.
  - `translation_health_section` (~l. 328): "The pilot (`-1`) and a ✗ stop the next `qgen batch --translate` …" → "A ✗ stops …".
- `authoring/tools/qgen.py`:
  - `tr-*` run report (~l. 4031): "Spot check by a native speaker: …&sample=1" → "Review (optional): `{REVIEW_URL}?batch={run}&locale={locale}`" (no `sample=1`).
  - any CLI help or exit-2 text that names the pilot as a stop (`rg -n pilot authoring/tools/`); keep `TRANSLATE_PILOT` (the 50-source first run, D-87) and the drafted-batch "pilot" mentions (that''s the old `pilot` batch, unrelated).
- `authoring/ui/src/home/Home.svelte`: no "sample" link on translation run rows (drafted batches keep theirs).
- Check `authoring/ui/src/review/`, `authoring/server/spot_checks.py`, `authoring/server/overview.py` for a banner, count or prompt asking for a translation spot check; drop it. Existing `tr-*` records in `spot-checks.json` (tr-en-1, tr-de-1) stay valid and keep showing where they exist; `spot_check_problems`, `qc_section`, `qc_trend` unchanged; `/review?…&locale=L&sample=1` keeps working by URL, just isn''t offered.
- Already-run pilots without an ack (`tr-en-1`, `tr-de-1`, `tr-es-ES-1`) need no retroactive ack: they stop the next run only if they fail a threshold.
- `pm decision record "Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run" --supersedes 45` (partly: only "The pilot tr-<locale>-1 always stops the next run until qgen health ack"; thresholds and selection order stay), with an `--intro`, `--answer`, `--body` citing the milestone 9 change of 2026-10-16. Check `pm decision record -h` for the supersede flag''s exact form.
- Docs are `task` "Docs: translations reviewed by the LLM only" of this plan, not this task; but fix code comments you touch.

## Done when
- The stop check (`translate_stop_reason` for `en`, or `qgen batch --translate en --dry-run`) no longer reports `tr-en-1` as a pilot stop; a run with a ✗ threshold still stops.
- `qgen validate`, `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build` pass.', '2026-10-16T23:18:37Z', '2026-10-17T02:46:43Z', 1504, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1509, 171, 'Docs: translations reviewed by the LLM only', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, authoring/QC.md, authoring/RUNBOOK.md, plans/15b-question-translation.md, plans/decisions.md', '`plan 171: Translations without human control`, part 2; after `task 1508: qgen health and the review tool: no pilot stop, no spot-check prompt` (same plan, runs first). Milestone 9 (developer, 2026-10-16): the LLM translation review is a translation''s only review; no native-speaker spot check per `tr-*` run, no QC decision per run, no pilot go/no-go, no ack after a pilot; `decision 45: Health thresholds and selection order for qgen batch --translate runs` thresholds stay (a ✗ stops the next run until `qgen health ack`, the developer''s), as amended by the decision task 1508 records ("Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run").

## What
- `authoring/QC.md` "Translation runs": no spot check, no QC steps per `tr-*` run; what stays: the run report, the thresholds, the developer''s optional review (`/review?batch=tr-<L>-<n>&locale=<L>`), `qgen flag` → `needs_work`.
- `authoring/RUNBOOK.md`: the exit-2 row of the step table and the "Translation runs" bullet: no pilot stop, only threshold failures.
- `plans/15b-question-translation.md`: run line (no exit 2 after the pilot), QT-5 without go/no-go (pilot numbers are information for `qgen report --cost`), QT-6 without native-speaker spot check; status line.
- `plans/decisions.md`: D-87 "Stop" bullet (only threshold failures, decision 45 as amended), D-55 if it names the pilot, and a line citing the developer''s 2026-10-16 change; README if it says otherwise.
- Decision 200: `rg -i "spot.?check|go/no-go|pilot|native speaker|native-speaker"` over `.md` files and code comments in `authoring/`, `plans/`, `modding/`, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`; fix every hit about translations in the same commit. Leave drafted batches'' spot checks (D-56), the old `pilot` batch, and milestone 12''s decision 220 (native reviewers for zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR) unless the text makes them required per translation run; if decision 220''s plan text conflicts with milestone 9''s "all question locales, milestone 12''s included", add a follow-up task in the plan that owns it rather than editing plans outside docs.
- Style: `.md` files as bullets, ultra-concise (AGENTS.md).

## Done when
- No doc describes a translation spot check, a pilot go/no-go or a pilot stop as required.
- `qgen validate` passes.', '2026-10-16T23:18:37Z', '2026-10-17T02:47:14Z', 1504, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1510, 165, 'Gallery shot of the lost-pad dialog', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, authoring/tools/gallery.py (seat-lost shot, 4 locales)', '`app/client/src/game/SeatLost.svelte` (task 1434, `plan 161: Per-player controls`) shows «Mando de <name> desconectado» when a session seat''s pad is gone and the seat is needed. Add a `trivia-gallery` shot for it in every UI language, from a demo save of a running session (round-robin, the turn seat unbound: after a start the binding lives in `sessionStorage` under `trivia.seats.<game id>`; the gallery can leave it empty so every seat is unbound). Check the `seat.*` catalog keys (es, es-ES, en, de) show up in the manifest.', '2026-10-16T23:26:05Z', '2026-10-17T02:51:46Z', 1434, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1511, 85, 'Steam overlay-activated event to the page, pausing the timed clock', 'work', 'dropped', NULL, 'Not reachable cleanly: steamworks-ffi-node 0.11.3 is the newest release; it calls SteamAPI_RunCallbacks and registers no GameOverlayActivated_t handler, and overlay.* has no event. Only a hand-built CCallbackBase (C++ vtable) through koffi and SteamAPI_RegisterCallback would work: fragile, untestable here (overlay is Windows-only, decision 70, no Windows/Steam session at hand), and decision 301 chose polling over own callbacks. Timed pause stays on Esc menu and hidden window (decision 282 says ''where the shell reports it'').', '`task 1450: Timed pause: Esc menu, hidden window, Steam overlay, «Pausa» veil` pauses the timed clock on the Esc menu and a hidden window only: `steamworks-ffi-node` 0.11.3 (`overlay.*` has 7 functions, none a callback) exposes no overlay-activated event (decision 282 wants it where the shell reports it).
- Check whether a newer binding version, or the raw `GameOverlayActivated_t` callback, can be reached from `app/desktop/main.mjs`.
- If so: forward it through `preload.cjs` and add `overlay.onActive(cb)` to `SteamBridge` in `app/client/src/lib/desktop.ts`.
- In `app/client/src/game/Game.svelte` (next to the `visibilitychange` hold) call `holdPause(applyClock)` on active and release on inactive.
- If not reachable, drop this task with the reason.', '2026-10-17T00:56:38Z', '2026-10-17T00:57:07Z', 1450, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1512, 164, 'Timed: question bar after a reload mid-claim', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, engine/game.ts, lib/types.ts, Timed.svelte, session.test.ts', 'Follow-up from `task 1461: Gallery: timed demo saves and shots with a frozen page clock`.

- Bug: a reload (or a fresh page) while a claim runs shows the timed screen''s question bar full, not where the claim stopped it
- Cause: `app/client/src/game/screens/Timed.svelte` `frozen` starts at 1 and only follows `session.timed.deadline`, which the engine''s view (`timedView` in `app/client/src/engine/game.ts`) sets to null while a claim runs; nothing in the view says how much of the 30 s was left at the claim
- Fix idea: the view carries the question''s time left at the claim (`claim.at - shown_at`, or the question deadline alongside the claim), `frozen` reads it; no save change
- Check: `trivia-gallery --locale es --only timed-claimed` still right; a manual reload mid-claim (dev server, timed session) shows the bar at the claim''s point', '2026-10-17T01:41:57Z', '2026-10-17T01:44:19Z', 1461, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1513, 17, 'Fix qgen fix: revise_in_pool crashes with unbound old_bg for non-audio media', 'work', 'done', 0, '2026-10-16, authoring/tools/qgen.py', '`qgen batch` (batch-9, `task 1503: Finish batch-9 after task 1369: Fix qgen rate: the model returns no rating for inventions-16 in revised-01-19`) failed three times in a row at step `fix`: 28/28 calls fail, each with `cannot access local variable ''old_bg'' where it is not associated with a value`.

Last lines (identical in all three runs):
```
  FAILED fix q-3099, q-3101, ..., q-3137: cannot access local variable ''old_bg'' where it is not associated with a value
  fix: 28/28 calls in 9m24s, 28 failed
28 item(s) failed; rerun the same command to retry them.
Stopped at `fix` with 28 error(s). Run `qgen batch` again; ...
claude: 29 calls (0 failed, 0 retried), opus 29, 87 turns, 1.2M tokens (1.0M cache), $7.05, 28m03s in calls
```

Diagnosis (read-only): `revise_in_pool` in `authoring/tools/qgen.py` (~line 1702) assigns `old_bg = q.get("background")` only inside `if new_media["type"] == "audio":`, but line ~1714 reads it unconditionally (`bool(old_bg) and new_bg is not old_bg`). Any fix of a non-audio question raises UnboundLocalError. Suggested fix: set `old_bg = q.get("background")` before the `if`.

Check: `qgen batch` resumes at `fix` and the step passes (each failed call costs ~$0.25 in Claude calls, so a pre-check with a throw-away call of `revise_in_pool` on a copy of an image question and an audio question is cheaper).', '2026-10-17T02:45:36Z', '2026-10-17T02:47:28Z', 1503, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1514, 17, 'Finish batch-9 after task 1513: Fix qgen fix: revise_in_pool crashes with unbound old_bg for non-audio media', 'work', 'done', -99, '2026-10-16, Done: batch-9: 951 merged, 874 approved, 77 needs work (took 42m04s). claude: 61 calls (0 failed, 0 retried), opus 61, 122 turns, 767k tokens, $2.72 (final run; first run timed out at 1h and resumed), report authoring/reports/batch-9.md. Next: task 1186 QC batch-9', 'Follow `authoring/RUNBOOK.md` (including "Under `pm run`"); plain `qgen batch` resumes batch-9 at step `fix`. Same Done-when as `task 1185: run batch-9`: `authoring/reports/batch-9.md` exists, the printed `git add` paths staged; note the "Done:" line and report path. Then QC: `task 1186: QC batch-9`.

Earlier runs (`task 1503: Finish batch-9 after task 1369: Fix qgen rate: the model returns no rating for inventions-16 in revised-01-19`) got through rate to fix; their partial output is already committed.', '2026-10-17T02:45:36Z', '2026-10-17T04:30:30Z', 1503, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1515, 166, 'investigate the failure of task 1467: Ship timed (Competitive timed)', 'investigate', 'done', 342, '2026-10-17, no files: 1467 ran because its gate task 1453 waits on pending decision 297 (so the queue skipped 1453), and 1467''s gate rule told the worker to stop without closing or blocking, which pm counts as a failure. Linked 1467 to decision 297 (pm task-pending-decision), so it waits until 1453 can run (1453 runs first: same priority, lower id); 1467''s gate line now says to block on the gate''s pending decision instead of stopping unblocked.', '`task 1467: Ship timed (Competitive timed)` failed in `pm run`; its summary is below. Find out why, don''t redo its work:
* read its log, `pm show 1467`, and the stashes it left (`git stash show -p --include-untracked <sha>`); don''t apply or drop them, task 1467''s next run gets them
* rerun the failing command or script to see the error yourself; find the cause in the code, not only the symptom
Then, by what you find:
* a bug in a script, test, tool or config of the project: add a task that fixes it, `pm task add 166 "<subject>" --priority 341`, with the cause, where it is and how to check the fix; it runs before task 1467 does again
* task 1467 itself is wrong or out of date: change it (`pm task set 1467 --body …`) or drop it (`pm task drop 1467 "<reason>"`)
* it needs the human: `pm decision add` with what you found and the options, then `pm task-pending-decision 1467 <decision>`
* nothing to fix (a passing outage): say so; task 1467 runs again as it is
If earlier investigations of this task are listed below, don''t repeat their fix: raise a decision instead.
Your note on `pm task done`: the cause and what you queued.

# The failure

    exit 0, but the task is still open and not blocked, after 0m16s, 4 turns
    last tool call: Bash: for t in 1445 1449 1450 1451 1452 1453 1432 1434 1458 1433; do echo "$t: $(pm show $t | grep -m1 -E ''^# Task'')"; done
    likely cause: the worker ended without `pm task done|drop 1467` or a pending decision; its last message: `task 1453: Timed visuals polish: hearts, red frame, claim banner` is still open and has the same priority (340) in this work tree. Once it''s done, `pm run` can take 1467 again. If you want the hook s
    log: /home/ruben/code/trivia/.git/pm-logs/task-1467-run-1535.log
    last output:
      Task 1453 is still open, so the gate isn''t met. The instructions say to change nothing in pm and stop without closing.
      
      Task 1467 (Ship timed) is blocked, and I changed nothing.
      
      - **Gate:** `task 1453: Timed visuals polish: hearts, red frame, claim banner` is still open. Its priority is 340, the same as this task.
      - **Done:** the other gate tasks are done: 1445, 1449 to 1452, 1432, 1433, 1434 and 1458.
      - **Next step:** this task should run again once `task 1453` is done. I didn''t touch pm, the code or the plans, and I didn''t close the task.
      I''m leaving task 1467 open on purpose. Its own instructions say that if a gate task isn''t done, I should change nothing in pm and stop without closing, so the task stays queued behind the gate.
      
      - **Why not `pm task done`:** nothing was shipped, so that would be false.
      - **Why not `pm task drop`:** the gate task isn''t dropped, only unfinished, and dropping would remove the ship work for good.
      - **Why not make it pending on a decision:** there is no question only the developer can answer yet. A decision created just to satisfy the hook would put noise in their queue.
      
      `task 1453: Timed visuals polish: hearts, red frame, claim banner` is still open and has the same priority (340) in this work tree. Once it''s done, `pm run` can take 1467 again. If you want the hook satisfied now, tell me which of the three outcomes you prefer.
      [success: 4 turns, $0.15]', '2026-10-17T03:11:26Z', '2026-10-17T03:11:48Z', NULL, 0, NULL, 'app');
