INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1517, 172, 'Non-pad seats keep their binding across a restart', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, app/client/src/lib/{types,api,seats,seats.svelte}.ts, engine/{state,save,game,api}.ts, game/Game.svelte, plans/14-input.md; decision 321', 'Fix the stuck resume of `plan 172: Keyboard seats after a restart: a resumed session asks for a pad`: after a shell restart, a session''s keyboard seats (`"shared"`, `"kbm"`, `{ key }`) must get their binding back without a pad; pad seats keep rebinding through the seat-lost dialog (`decision 289: Local multiplayer: a controller lost mid-session waits for a controller to take the seat`).

## Cause
- `app/client/src/lib/seats.svelte.ts` `stored()`: the binding lives only in sessionStorage (`trivia.seats.<id>`); after a restart every seat is `null`
- `lostSeat()` treats every `null` as a lost pad; `SeatLost.svelte` binds pads only → a keyboard-only rr-coop session (3 `shared` seats, `decision 273: Keyboard-only turn-based sessions: what does a player''s own key do?`) can''t go on; a `kbm` seat in a mixed session could be taken by a free pad; a timed key seat (`{ key }`, claim key picked on Join, `decision 292: Join screen: joining, leaving, names and claim keys`) can''t be taken at all

## Do
- Make each seat''s device kind, and a key seat''s claim key, survive a restart. Recommended: store it in the save''s session row (`games[]` row `seats[]`, `Seat` in `app/client/src/engine/state.ts`, shape of `plan 157: Session model and save format`), e.g. `device?: "pad" | "kbm" | "shared" | { key: string }` (no pad index: pad numbering changes across restarts); validate it in `app/client/src/engine/save.ts` (old rows without it: as today); bump `SAVE_VERSION` with an upgrade only if the validator requires it. The alternative (the dialog lets keyboard/mouse take a non-pad seat, key seats re-pick their key Join-style) is acceptable if it turns out simpler; either way record the lasting choice with `pm decision record`
- On resume (`watchGame` → `stored()` fallback): non-pad seats bound at once from the stored kind; a `kbm` seat back to `"kbm"` only when keyboard and mouse aren''t bound elsewhere; pad seats `null` → the existing dialog
- `lostSeat()` / `SeatLost.svelte`: only a pad seat can be lost; a lost-pad dialog never offers a keyboard seat to a pad
- Check the Join screen and `bindSession()` hand the device kinds to the engine/save (rr-coop, rr-competitive, timed)
- `rg` comments and `.md` mentioning the sessionStorage-only binding (`plans/14-input.md` section 3, `seats.svelte.ts` header) and fix them (decision 200)

## Check
- Dev client: keyboard-only rr-coop, one turn, reload with sessionStorage cleared (or a fresh tab) → plays on without a dialog; same for a timed keyboard-only session (claim keys still work) and a mixed session''s `kbm` seat
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`
- The smoke coverage is the next task in this plan', '2026-10-17T03:59:28Z', '2026-10-17T04:24:44Z', 1516, 0, 'opus', 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1518, 172, 'smoke --multiplayer: keyboard-only sessions restart mid-session', 'work', 'done', 470, '2026-10-17, authoring/steam/{smoke.mjs,release_check.py}, plans/11-steam.md, app/client/src/lib/seats.ts', 'Extend `authoring/steam/smoke.mjs --multiplayer` (`RUNS`, the timed pads session''s `restart` step shows how) so that the keyboard-only rr-coop session and a keyboard-only timed session (claim-key seats) quit mid-session, start again, resume and play on to the end without the seat-lost dialog; the mixed session (4 pads + keyboard and mouse), if cheap, also restarts and its `kbm` seat acts without a pad while the pads rebind (`decision 289: Local multiplayer: a controller lost mid-session waits for a controller to take the seat`).

Needs `task 1517: Non-pad seats keep their binding across a restart` (runs before this one in the same work tree).

- Update the header comment of `smoke.mjs` and the release-check `multiplayer` step''s description (`authoring/steam/release_check.py`, README/plan text if it lists the sessions) to name the new restarts

## Check
- `trivia-desktop-build --dir`, then `node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs --multiplayer`: all sessions green
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`', '2026-10-17T03:59:28Z', '2026-10-17T07:08:30Z', 1516, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1519, 89, 'Packs without a pool: smoke''s without-packs stage and trivia-steam stage miss them in pack-media.json', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16, app/desktop/stage-media.mjs: every bundle folder gets a pack-media.json entry ([] without a pool), so smoke withoutPacks and steam.py stage_dlc agree with steam.json dlc. Not run: trivia-desktop-build --dir stops here on the missing Steamworks SDK lib, so smoke and trivia-steam stage weren''t re-run', 'Found by `task 1473: Headless: every multiplayer mode start to finish, release-check step multiplayer` (2026-10-16), on a fresh `trivia-desktop-build --dir`.

## Failure
- `node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` (release check step `smoke`): the with-packs game passes, then `smoke: without packs: packs left: germany, mexico, spain, uk, usa`
- Cause: `app/desktop/stage-media.mjs` writes `build/pack-media.json` only for bundles with an es `bundles/<id>/pool.json` (colombia); `app/data/bundles/{germany,mexico,spain,uk,usa}/` have categories and names files but no pool yet, and still ship as `resources/data/bundles/<id>/`
- `smoke.mjs` `withoutPacks()` removes only `pack-media.json`''s packs → the others stay
- Same mismatch in `authoring/steam/steam.py` `stage_dlc()`: `shipped != set(media)` → `trivia-steam stage` (release check step `desktop`) exits
- Not caused by task 1473 (it didn''t touch these paths)

## Do
- One rule for "a pack" across `stage-media.mjs` (every shipped bundle folder gets a `pack-media.json` entry, `[]` when it has no media of its own, or pool-less folders aren''t shipped), `smoke.mjs` `withoutPacks()` and `steam.py` `stage_dlc()`; check what `steam.json` `dlc` and the DLC store tasks expect for packs without questions (decision 66)
- Import, don''t copy (decision 199)

## Check
- `trivia-desktop-build --dir`, `node authoring/steam/smoke.mjs` green (both stages), `trivia-steam stage` (or its `--dry-run`/stage part) passes
- `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`', '2026-10-17T04:05:45Z', '2026-10-17T04:17:34Z', 1473, 0, NULL, 'app');
