INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1522, 17, 'Fix qgen sheets: Wikimedia preview of q-3185 fails (HTTP 500, then thumb rate limit)', 'work', 'done', 0, '2026-10-17, authoring/tools/media.py: make_sheet skips a preview that fails (HTTP error or rate limit) and raises only when no picture could be shown; check: qgen batch passed sheets (q-3185 ok) and went on to record, stopped by my 1 h timeout, not finished (task 1523 resumes); partial batch-10 data staged. npm run check: only knip''s electron-builder warnings (unrelated, not from this change).', '`qgen batch` (batch-10, task 1520) stopped at step `sheets` three times in a row (earlier stops at revise/fix/fix factcheck/sheets were different transient failures and passed on rerun).

Failing step: `sheets`, one sheet: `q-3185.jpg` (Wikimedia Commons preview, sheet 5 of q-3185, a research pick).
Last lines (third run):
```
  rate limited by thumb.wikimedia.org, waiting 45 s
  rate limited by thumb.wikimedia.org, waiting 60 s
06:31:53 Wikimedia Commons preview 5 sheets q-3185 failed: rate-limited by thumb.wikimedia.org; try again in about 75 s 2m31s
  FAILED sheet q-3185.jpg: rate-limited by thumb.wikimedia.org; try again in about 75 s
  sheets: 5/5 sheets in 2m31s, 1 failed
Stopped at `sheets` with 1 error(s).
```
Earlier runs: `HTTP Error 500: Internal Server Error` for the same file (sheets 1-4 of q-3185 downloaded fine; preview 5 fails).

Diagnosis (read-only, shallow): the rate-limit exception is in `authoring/tools/download.py:26`; the thumbnail for preview 5 of q-3185 either 500s persistently on Commons or the retry/backoff gives up before the limit lifts. Not diagnosed further. Suggested fix: find the source file of preview 5, check whether its thumb URL works by hand; if it persistently 500s, make `sheets` skip or substitute that candidate (drop it from the sheet) instead of failing the whole step; if only rate-limiting, wait longer than `retry_after` before giving up.

