INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1538, 173, 'Demo save location and single-instance lock per decision 336', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-17, app/desktop/main.mjs (comment only)', 'Where the demo keeps its save, per `decision 336: Demo save: separate from the full game''s, or shared/imported on purchase?` (`plan 173: Demo build switch, identity and save`, part "Save"). Read the answer in `pm show` first.

- Separate (option 1 or 2): `app/desktop/main.mjs` packaged demo `userData` `<appData>/trivia-demo` (today `app.setPath("userData", …/trivia)` ~line 164), so save, `mods.json`, telemetry and probe logs move with it; dev demo `state/desktop-demo/` (save, `mods.json`) and `state/telemetry-demo/`; the single-instance lock follows `userData`, so demo and full game run side by side — check it does
- Option 2 (import): add a follow-up task in this plan for the full game''s first-start import of `<appData>/trivia-demo/save` via the `--import-save` path (detection, a dialog in four locales, save version check); not done here
- Option 3 (shared): demo keeps `<appData>/trivia` and `state/desktop/`; only the lock question remains (one instance across both)
- Full game paths unchanged

Done when: `TRIVIA_DEMO=1 trivia-desktop` saves where the answer says, a full `trivia-desktop` beside it (separate answers) runs with its own save; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.', '2026-10-17T13:25:08Z', '2026-10-17T15:02:37Z', 1532, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1539, 173, 'Demo Steam feature gates: mods, Workshop, publish, achievements per decision 337', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-17, app/desktop/main.mjs', 'Switch off in the demo the Steam features `decision 337: Steam features in the demo: Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry, question reports` turns off (`plan 173: Demo build switch, identity and save`, part "Steam features"). Read the answer in `pm show` first. Gates read `isDemo()` (shell) and `buildInfo().demo` / `EngineData.demo` (client); nothing enforced hard (`decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`).

- Mods/Workshop off: `app/desktop/main.mjs` skips the mod scan, `mods.json` load, Workshop source and `/mods.js` (~line 815, as `--no-mods` does); `--publish-mod` and `--check-mod` refuse in the demo with a one-line message
- Achievements off: the `steam:unlock` handler (~line 1141) skips unlocks in the demo (client may still compute them)
- Steam Cloud: no code (Steamworks config, part 6)
- Hiding screens/buttons is part 5''s (`task 1528: write plan: Demo on screen`); here only the code paths
- Whatever the answer keeps on stays as in the full game

Done when: `TRIVIA_DEMO=1 TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1 trivia-desktop` loads no mods (with mods in `mods/`) and logs no unlocks; the full shell unchanged; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.', '2026-10-17T13:25:08Z', '2026-10-17T15:04:03Z', 1532, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1540, 173, 'Demo telemetry mark and question reports for the demo App ID per decision 337', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-17, app/desktop/main.mjs (decision 337 off: demo gates telemetry and question reports)', 'Telemetry and question reports from the demo, if `decision 337: Steam features in the demo: Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry, question reports` keeps them on (`plan 173: Demo build switch, identity and save`, part "Steam features"). Read the answer first; an "off" part becomes a gate (shell and client skip it) instead.

