INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1573, NULL, 'Investigate: options to reduce the overlap rate when drafting new questions', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-17, no files (analysis of work/batch-8..10, throw-away scripts deleted); decision 350: Overlap rate in drafting: which changes?
Detection: drafter sees only its own subcategory''s pool questions (existing_answers, source language) + same-concept already_asked; rate (opus) scores no_overlap vs <= 8 lexical overlap_candidates over the whole pool (English keys, decision 232) + earlier run drafts; merge drops no_overlap < 4 (since task 274, first in batch-8) + lexical duplicates(). 3 % threshold (decision 13) was set on batch-4..7, before rater drops existed.
batch-9 / batch-10 overlap+duplicate drops 184 / 168: 92 % cross-subcategory; same concept 4 % / 2 %; partner earlier pool 67 % / 83 %, same run 33 % / 17 %; partner es-sourced 67 % / 52 %; levels 1-4 drop 15-25 %, 11-15 3-7 %; spread over 80 / 75 of 99 subcategories (<= 9 each); rater score 3 = 46 % / 35 % of drops; sample of 50: ~55 % same fact, ~45 % shared answer/topic only.
Jump at batch-9: drafts with a same-answer pool candidate 7 % -> 13 % -> 14 % (pool 1168 -> 2159 -> 3110), no candidate 32 % -> 12 % -> 6 %; candidate->drop conversion 29 % -> 54 % -> 40 % (English fame-first international concepts, decisions 239/242, aim at facts the es pool had; 61 same-run collisions in batch-9).
Cost: ~$0.065 per dropped draft = $10-12 per batch (~5 %); main cost ~160 fewer merged per batch and the global stop blocking task 1295.
Simulation: a concept-name probe finds the partner of 40 % / 37 % of pool-overlap drops, flags 14-15 % of slots.', 'Batch health: overlap rate 5.5 % (batch-8), 15.4 % (batch-9), 14.9 % (batch-10), threshold 3 %; 165 / 154 drafts dropped for overlap in batch-9 / batch-10 (`authoring/reports/batches.md`). Acked each time "for now" (`authoring/data/health-acks.json`); the stop is global, so each failed base batch also blocks `task 1295: run colombia batch (batch-<n>)`. Approved quality is fine (needs_work overlap 0.7 %, batch-9 spot check 30/30), so the cost is wasted drafts, not bad questions.

## Investigate
- Where overlap is detected and dropped in `qgen` (step, method, threshold), and what the drafter sees of existing questions beforehand.
