INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1574, NULL, 'Investigate: fewer first-person ''What am I?'' riddle questions', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-17, no files (investigation; findings and options in decision 351: First-person riddle questions: which changes?). Riddle share of approved base: ≤2 % to batch-5, 19/22/24/20/20 % batch-6..10, 719 in pool. Cause: rules force direct for media and number/time moves → direct over its share → usage feedback boosts riddle in free slots (riddle 42 %, direct 17 % there); drafter neutral (53 % chosen when offered); prompts never limit it, rate gives it top fun (3.79). Of 582 approved riddles batch-8..10: 60 % answer is the speaker, 34 % names itself and asks another fact, 6 % not first person; hand sample 31/60 add something, 29/60 plain question in disguise; flat across difficulty and en/es. Simulated: rule riddle→identify/who/name_concept + three_facts 2 → riddle ≈5 %, top clue ≈51–53 %; weight 0 + three_facts 2 → 0 %, ≈55 %; weight 0.5 → ≈8 %, ≈56 %; top clue ≤50 % is structural (direct forced ≈50 %).', 'The developer sees many "What am I?" / "¿Qué soy?" questions that would work as well as a straight question ("What is …?"). Approved with a first-person riddle stem (rough regex count): batch-7 86/576, batch-8 194/978, batch-9 105/914, batch-10 97/866; ≈ 0–1 % before batch-6.

Likely source: `authoring/data/question-axes.json`, axis `clue`, value `riddle` ("a riddle in the first person: «Tengo…, vivo en…, ¿qué soy?»"), default weight 1 of 5 drawable clue values → ≈ 20 % of slots. Also `top clue` fails batch health (52.8 % / 51.4 %, ≤ 50 %).

## Investigate
