Done when: `qgen validate` and the pre-commit checks pass (the demo-list failure tracked by `task 1607: Demo list: the 79 ids missing translations fail qgen validate` excepted).', '2026-10-18T01:18:27Z', '2026-10-18T01:18:36Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1609, NULL, 'write an executive summary', 'exec', 'done', 10000, '2026-10-17, executive summary stored', 'Write an executive summary for the owner of this project: a busy person who doesn''t read code, tasks or plans. Write
it for an interested outsider who knows nothing about the project: plain, good English in full sentences, no jargon.
Change nothing in the project; stage nothing.

Read first: the previous summary (`pm summary show`), the milestones (`pm milestone list`, `pm show m<id>`), and what
was done since the previous summary (`git log --stat <its commit>..HEAD`, `pm show <id>` where you need more).

Write, in this order:
1. **What the project is**, in one or two sentences: what it makes, for whom, and why. Every summary starts this way.
2. **Where it stands**, in one sentence: how far along it is toward the current goal (the open milestone), and
   whether that is on track, in terms of what the product can do.
3. **What''s new** since the previous summary (for the first one: everything so far): what the product can do now
   that it couldn''t before, and why that matters. Explain it to the outsider; don''t go into detail.
4. **What comes next**, plus a risk only if it could change the outcome or the timing.

Leave out everything about how the work is managed: decisions, sign-offs, tasks, plans, runs, failures, cost, tests
and pm itself; never ids, file names or counts of these. One screen at most, about 250 words, few headings.
Store it: `pm summary add < summary.md`, delete summary.md, then close your task.', '2026-10-18T01:24:14Z', '2026-10-18T01:24:28Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1610, NULL, 'Bundle tiles: «5000+ questions», not a bare number', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-18, app/client/src/locales/{es,en,de}.ts (es-ES inherits es; xx.ts has no bundle strings); gallery sets task-1610 (full + demo); decision 365 for the look', 'The developer: every bundle tile names the unit: «5000+ questions», «2000+ questions», «100+ questions» (demo), not a bare «5000+». Today `bundles.count` is "{n}" and `bundles.countPlus` "{n}+" in every catalog (`app/client/src/game/BundleSelector.svelte:176`).

- `app/client/src/locales/{es,es-ES,en,de}.ts` (+ `xx.ts`): `bundles.countPlus` → "{n}+ questions" in each language; `bundles.count` (a mod bundle''s exact small count) → plural forms ("1 question" / "{n} questions"); read `locales/style/<locale>.md` first
- Rules of `decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings` unchanged (which number, rounding); add a consequence line: the strings carry the noun
