Done when: every bundle tile, demo included, reads «N+ questions» in all four UI languages, the gallery sets are linked in a decision, the pre-commit checks pass.', '2026-10-18T01:47:19Z', '2026-10-18T01:50:31Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1611, 179, 'Demo matrix: multiplayer modes once one is built', 'work', 'dropped', 90, 'Can''t run as a queued task: pm has no wait-for-task, so it ran with no multiplayer mode in BUILT_MODES and couldn''t close. Its work now sits in the second run of each of tasks 1465, 1466 and 1467 (plan 166 ship tasks), where adding a mode to BUILT_MODES would otherwise turn trivia-release-check --demo step matrix ✗.', 'Part of `plan 179: Close-out: play the demo`; follows `task 1570: Headless: every demo mode × age group to an end, twice; release-check step matrix`.

## Why
- `smoke.mjs --demo --matrix` (`authoring/steam/smoke.mjs`, `matrix()`) covers only the single-player `BUILT_MODES` (`gamemaster`, `solo` today); a multiplayer mode in `BUILT_MODES` makes it throw `no matrix games for multiplayer modes yet: …`, so `trivia-release-check --demo` step `matrix` goes ✗ the day `plan 166: Shipping the multiplayer modes and docs` builds one
- `decision 348: Demo: cover multiplayer sessions up to how many seats?` (S = 1): the demo list (`authoring/data/demo.json` `seats` 1) guarantees no multiplayer session; a 2+ seat session may get the not-enough-questions notice

## Wait
- A multiplayer mode in `BUILT_MODES` (`app/client/src/engine/game.ts`); until then nothing to do (don''t close; stays open)

## What
- Per built multiplayer mode × age group in the matrix: fake pads as `--multiplayer` injects them (`launchPads`, `setup`, `turn`, `forward`, `claims`, `ended` in `smoke.mjs`, reuse), `MIN_SEATS` seats; rr-competitive mixed seat groups once
- What a short supply means under decision 348: if a session''s start is refused for supply, either the matrix expects and records that refusal (traced, not ✗) or the developer raises the demo''s seats (`qgen demo --propose --seats S`); ask with `pm decision add` if not obvious
- Docs: `smoke.mjs` header, `release_check.py` docstring, `plans/11-steam.md` "Demo `matrix` step"
- Done when `trivia-release-check --demo` step `matrix` ✓ with the mode in', '2026-10-18T03:00:25Z', '2026-10-18T03:03:27Z', 1570, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1612, 179, 'investigate the failure of task 1572: Demo close-out: docs sweep and milestone 18 Done', 'investigate', 'done', 102, '2026-10-17, no files. Cause: task 1572''s wait said ''stop without closing'', but task 1571 and task 1563 are blocked on decision 89 (Steamworks IDs), so 1572 stayed open and unblocked and pm counted that as a failure; no bug in code, no stash. Fix: 1572 is now pending on decision 89, and its body says to block on the playtest decision (or whatever 1571 waits on) instead of just stopping', '`task 1572: Demo close-out: docs sweep and milestone 18 Done` failed in `pm run`; its summary is below. Find out why, don''t redo its work:
* read its log, `pm show 1572`, and the stashes it left (`git stash show -p --include-untracked <sha>`); don''t apply or drop them, task 1572''s next run gets them
* rerun the failing command or script to see the error yourself; find the cause in the code, not only the symptom
Then, by what you find:
* a bug in a script, test, tool or config of the project: add a task that fixes it, `pm task add 179 "<subject>" --priority 101`, with the cause, where it is and how to check the fix; it runs before task 1572 does again
* task 1572 itself is wrong or out of date: change it (`pm task set 1572 --body …`) or drop it (`pm task drop 1572 "<reason>"`)
* it needs the human: `pm decision add` with what you found and the options, then `pm task-pending-decision 1572 <decision>`
* nothing to fix (a passing outage): say so; task 1572 runs again as it is
If earlier investigations of this task are listed below, don''t repeat their fix: raise a decision instead.
Your note on `pm task done`: the cause and what you queued.

# The failure

    exit 0, but the task is still open and not blocked, after 0m18s, 5 turns
    last tool call: Bash: pm show 1571 2>&1 | grep -n -i -E "^# Task 1571" ; pm decision list --answered --grep "Steam''s beta" 2>&1 | head -5
    likely cause: the worker ended without `pm task done|drop 1572` or a pending decision; its last message: Task 1572 should stay in the queue until task 1571 is closed and its decision is answered «passed». I changed and staged nothing. If you want it dropped or parked another way, tell me and I''ll do that
    log: /home/ruben/code/trivia/.git/pm-logs/task-1572-run-1690.log
    last output:
      Task 1571 is still open (the earlier listing shows it as `[open]`), and no playtest decision exists yet.
        → Bash: pm show 1571 2>&1 | grep -n -i -E "^# Task 1571" ; pm decision list --answered --grep "Steam''s beta" 2>&1 | head -5
      I stopped without doing task 1572 and without closing it. Its wait condition isn''t met: `task 1571: The developer plays the demo from Steam''s beta` is still open.
      
      No playtest decision exists yet. `pm decision list --answered --grep "Steam''s beta"` finds nothing, and the pending list has no match for "played from Steam" either. There is also no "Demo playtest again" task to wait on.
      
      Task 1572 can run once the developer''s demo playtest decision is answered «passed», or once an "again" round has passed. I changed no files and staged nothing.
      I''m leaving task 1572 open on purpose. Its instructions say to stop without closing if task 1571 isn''t finished, and it isn''t.
      
      - **Marking it done:** that would be false, because the docs sweep and the milestone 18 close-out haven''t been done.
      - **Dropping it:** that would throw away a task that is only waiting. It can''t be redone once closed.
      - **Making it pending on a decision:** the playtest decision doesn''t exist yet. Task 1571 creates it. Raising a stand-in decision myself would be a pm change nobody asked for.
      
      Task 1572 should stay in the queue until task 1571 is closed and its decision is answered «passed». I changed and staged nothing. If you want it dropped or parked another way, tell me and I''ll do that.
      [success: 5 turns, $0.16]', '2026-10-18T03:01:53Z', '2026-10-18T03:02:25Z', NULL, 0, NULL, 'app');
