INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1659, 188, 'Pace and order of the topic bundles: decision', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-21, no files: decision 371 answered (option 1); consequences recorded; kept task 1660 (stem), dropped 1661, 1662, 1664, 1663 for re-adding in order sports, history, geography, movies', '`plan 188: Content runs for the topic bundles` task 1: ask the developer how fast and in what order the five topic bundles `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography` are filled to 2000 approved per question locale (`en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`). The five start tasks (`Topic runs <id>: start`) wait for this answer. No file writes.

## Before starting
- Needs `task 1629: qgen report --cost: rows per theme bundle and locale` done (`pm show 1629`). If open: `pm task-pending-decision <this task>` on the decision blocking it (plan 184''s earliest open decision, `pm show p184`); none pending → note why and stop without closing (the queue reaches −120 again later).
- Binding: `decision 236: English-first drafting for base: what drives drafting and which locales steer it` (theme sources in `en`), `decision 267: Bundle tiles: question count strings` (2000 per non-base bundle), `decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)` (regional chains, plan 84), cost is information only (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15: no budget gates).

## Decision
`pm decision add "Topic bundles: pace and order of the content runs" --intro … --body … --option …` (`--intro`: plain English, for an outsider: five optional packs need English writing runs a person spot-checks plus machine translation; they compete with the main pack and the country packs for machine cost and the developer''s review time; the answer sets how many run at once and in what order).

Body, numbers from the repo (`nix develop -c …`):
- `qgen report --cost`: projection for 5 × 2000 × 4 locales: en drafting, es/es-ES/de translation (theme rows; none yet → base''s rates, say so).
- Drafting pairs and spot checks per bundle: 2000 / approved per English base batch (batches 9–11, `qgen report --qc batch-<n>` or `authoring/reports/`).
- The developer''s review time per 100 (`plans/15c-regional-questions.md`, colombia''s QC) → hours per bundle.
- What''s still open ahead of it: base (`qgen report --exit-check`, `plan 17: Batch runs`) and plan 84''s regional and translation chains (`pm show p84`: open runs, start tasks pending).

Options (recommended first; let the numbers decide the recommendation, say why):
1. One topic bundle at a time below base and regional runs (−120), order `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `geography`, `movies` (movies last for its low media share, `task 1631: Media for movies and sports: axes template and docs`); the next starts when the previous one''s drafting ends; its translations keep running.
2. All five at once, one pair each, −120.
3. Two at a time.
4. None until base''s exit check and plan 84''s regional chains are done.
5. Your own pace or order.

Then: `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <decision>` and the same for every open start task of plan 188 (`Topic runs stem: start`, `… sports …`, `… history …`, `… movies …`, `… geography …`; `pm show p188`); stop.

## On the answer (next run)
- `pm decision consequences <decision> "…"`.
- Staggered answer (1, 3, or a custom one): drop the start tasks that don''t start yet: `pm task drop <id> "re-added by the closing drafting QC of <previous bundle>"`; keep the first one(s).
- Priorities: if the answer moves a start task (order, or above −120), `pm task set <id> --priority N` (−120 ± multiples of 10).
- Option 4: the start tasks stay; their bodies already pend on what blocks base or plan 84 — add that to the consequences.
- Done when: the decision is answered, consequences recorded, start tasks match the answer; note names what was dropped or moved.

## pm-run rules (plan 84, plan 17 "Batch tasks under pm run")
- D-36: no prompt, pool, media or `qgen.py` changes; findings become decisions or tasks in their own plans (184 or new).
- `tasks.sql` alone isn''t a dirty tree; this task stages nothing.', '2026-10-21T20:29:08Z', '2026-10-21T23:04:39Z', 1650, 0, 'opus', 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1660, 188, 'Topic runs stem: start', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-21, no files; added pair task 1676: run batch-<n> (stem), task 1677: QC batch-<n> (stem)', '`plan 188: Content runs for the topic bundles` "Chain per bundle" step 1: start the topic bundle `stem` (milestone 19): 2000 approved per question locale `en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`, drafted in English (`decision 236: English-first drafting for base: what drives drafting and which locales steer it`), translated into es, es-ES, de. Never re-asks base (`decision 350: Overlap rate in drafting: which changes?`). Launch (milestone 11) doesn''t wait. Owners: `plans/22-bundles.md` ("The first bundles": progress per bundle and locale), `plans/16-content-target.md` (cost).

## Before starting
- The pace decision (`Topic bundles: pace and order of the content runs`, raised by `task 1659: Pace and order of the topic bundles: decision`) answered, and its answer lets `stem` start now (staggered: this task was kept or re-added by the previous bundle''s closing QC). Not yet raised → pend on the decision blocking task 1659; pending → pend on it.
- `plan 184: Pipeline for topic bundles` done for runs (`pm show p184`; subjects may change): theme targets (`task 1626: Targets for theme bundles: bundle new --kind theme, validate rules`), per-locale gap aiming (`task 1627: Per-locale gap aiming and supply report for theme bundles`), cross-bundle overlap (`task 1628: Cross-bundle overlap: theme concepts and avoid lists see base''s related subcategories`), `--cost` theme rows (`task 1629: qgen report --cost: rows per theme bundle and locale`), end-to-end check (`task 1630: End-to-end check on a throw-away theme bundle`).
- `plan 186: The five topic bundles: rows and taxonomies`: `task 1644: Create the five topic bundles` and `task 1645: stem taxonomy` done (taxonomy applied; `pm show p186`, subjects may change); `qgen report --bundle stem` shows the 2000 target.
- Any missing → `pm task-pending-decision <this task>` on the decision blocking it (the bundle''s taxonomy decision, else plan 184''s or 186''s earliest open decision), stop.

## Then: add the first drafting pair (no `--priority`: the plan''s −120, or the start task''s own if the pace answer moved it)
- `run batch-<n> (stem)`: `nix develop -c qgen batch --bundle stem` (RUNBOOK steps 1–5; English). After the run rename both tasks to the batch name `qgen` printed (`pm task set`; counter shared with plans 17 and 84). Done when its report exists, printed paths staged, note with "Done:" line and report path.
- `QC batch-<n> (stem)`: `authoring/QC.md` steps 1–4: `pm decision add "Spot check batch-<n> (stem) done?"` (native English speaker: the developer, or an outside reviewer via `qgen spotcheck export`, `decision 221: How does an outside native reviewer reach the review tool?`; never an LLM; 30-question blind check, ≥ 90 % agreement, below it only feeds step 4), `qgen report --qc batch-<n>`, `pm decision add "QC batch-<n> (stem): which changes?"`, change tasks (theme pipeline findings in plan 184 while it has open tasks, else a new plan in milestone 19; the rest in `plan 17: Batch runs` at 650); decision 3''s `qgen rework` once; note QC numbers and `qgen report --cost` (per bundle). Then, first that applies:
  1. Translations: per L in es, es-ES, de with no open `run tr-<L>-<n> (stem)` and ≥ 50 approved en sources of `stem` not yet translated into L → add that run (body below).
  2. `qgen report --bundle stem` supply block shows no English draft gap left (every locale''s deficit covered by sources and untranslated sources at yield) → no next pair; note drafting done in `plans/22-bundles.md`; under a staggered pace, re-add the next bundle''s start task (same body as this one, its own bundle).
  3. The pace decision''s numbers look far off (the developer''s review time or $ per approved well above its projection) → `pm decision add` asking the developer instead of the next pair.
  4. Else the next pair (same bodies, next batch number).
- Translation run `run tr-<L>-<n> (stem)`: `nix develop -c qgen batch --translate <L> --bundle stem`; rename to the real run name; note the "Done:" line, report path and from `authoring/reports/<run>.md` and `qgen report --cost`: selected, translated, approved, needs_work, rejected, not travelling, $ per approved translation, audit agreement. No spot check, no QC task, no `qgen health ack` unless decision 45''s thresholds stop the run (exit 2). needs_work: nothing (picked again by the next run). After the run:
  - Its export wrote `app/data/bundles/stem/pool.<L>.json` and `<L>` isn''t in `stem`''s `languages` (`app/data/bundles.json`) → add it (row edit only), `qgen validate` clean (`bundle_problems`), stage the file.
  - `qgen report --bundle stem --locale <L>` at 2000 (every level at the bundle''s `targets.json`) → no next run; progress line; all four locales at 2000 → `stem` done in `plans/22-bundles.md`.
  - Else ≥ 50 approved en sources not yet in L → add `run tr-<L>-<n+1> (stem)`; fewer → nothing (the next drafting QC re-adds it).
  - Each run adds a progress line (approved per locale) for `stem` in `plans/22-bundles.md`.
- One open pair for `stem`, one open translation run per locale. Every added body repeats the pm-run rules below and names its bundle and run.

Done when: the first drafting pair is added (or this task pends on the blocking decision); note names the pair.

## pm-run rules (plan 84, plan 17 "Batch tasks under pm run")
- D-36: no prompt, pool, media or `qgen.py` changes; findings become decisions or tasks in their own plans (184 or new). Only exception: a locale joining `stem`''s `languages` row (above).
- `tasks.sql` alone isn''t a dirty tree. Stage exactly the `git add` paths the command prints (plus `app/data/bundles.json` after a `languages` edit); don''t commit (pm commits as "task N: …").
- Exit 75, exit 2 (a health stop: the decision asks the developer for `qgen health ack`), any other non-zero code, or exit 1 three times at one step → `pm decision add "Continue <run> (stem)…?"` with the last 30 lines of output in the body, `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <id>`, stage nothing, stop.
- Note on done: the "Done:" line and report path (run tasks), or the QC numbers (approved, rejected, needs_work, agreement, $ per approved, review time per 100).', '2026-10-21T20:29:30Z', '2026-10-21T23:31:53Z', 1650, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1661, 188, 'Topic runs sports: start', 'work', 'dropped', NULL, 're-added by the closing drafting QC of stem (decision 371: one at a time, order stem, sports, history, geography, movies; copy this body)', '`plan 188: Content runs for the topic bundles` "Chain per bundle" step 1: start the topic bundle `sports` (milestone 19): 2000 approved per question locale `en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`, drafted in English (`decision 236: English-first drafting for base: what drives drafting and which locales steer it`), translated into es, es-ES, de. Never re-asks base (`decision 350: Overlap rate in drafting: which changes?`). Launch (milestone 11) doesn''t wait. Owners: `plans/22-bundles.md` ("The first bundles": progress per bundle and locale), `plans/16-content-target.md` (cost).

