INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1671, 187, 'investigate the failure of task 1652: Steamworks rows and steam.json entries for the five topic DLCs', 'investigate', 'done', 282, '2026-10-21, no files. Cause: task 1652 (app work tree) ran in parallel before task 1644: Create the five topic bundles (questions work tree), since priority orders only within a work tree; its gate then said ''stop without closing'', which pm counts as a failed run. Fix: tasks 1652, 1653, 1654, 1657, 1658 moved to the questions work tree (run after 1644 by priority); gates of 1652-1654 rewritten: wait on the decision 1644 waits on, else pm decision add, never stop open and unblocked. No stash left by task 1652.', '`task 1652: Steamworks rows and steam.json entries for the five topic DLCs` failed in `pm run`; its summary is below. Find out why, don''t redo its work:
* read its log, `pm show 1652`, and the stashes it left (`git stash show -p --include-untracked <sha>`); don''t apply or drop them, task 1652''s next run gets them
* rerun the failing command or script to see the error yourself; find the cause in the code, not only the symptom
Then, by what you find:
* a bug in a script, test, tool or config of the project: add a task that fixes it, `pm task add 187 "<subject>" --priority 281`, with the cause, where it is and how to check the fix; it runs before task 1652 does again
* task 1652 itself is wrong or out of date: change it (`pm task set 1652 --body …`) or drop it (`pm task drop 1652 "<reason>"`)
* it needs the human: `pm decision add` with what you found and the options, then `pm task-pending-decision 1652 <decision>`
* nothing to fix (a passing outage): say so; task 1652 runs again as it is
If earlier investigations of this task are listed below, don''t repeat their fix: raise a decision instead.
Your note on `pm task done`: the cause and what you queued.

# The failure

    exit 0, but the task is still open and not blocked, after 0m23s, 5 turns
    last tool call: Bash: pm show 1652 2>&1 | head -8
    likely cause: the worker ended without `pm task done|drop 1652` or a pending decision; its last message: Check whether task 1652 now shows as pending. If it doesn''t, it will pick up again once task 1644 has added the rows.
    log: /home/ruben/code/trivia/.git/pm-logs/task-1652-run-1746.log
    last output:
        → Bash: cd /home/ruben/code/trivia-worktrees/app; pm status 2>&1 | head -20; grep -o ''"id": *"[a-z]*"'' app/data/bundles.json; git log --oneline -3 -- app/data
      I stopped without making any changes, and task 1652 is still open.
      
      The gate failed. `app/data/bundles.json` has no rows for `stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies` or `geography`. It only lists `base`, `colombia`, `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain` and `mexico`. `task 1644: Create the five topic bundles` is still queued and hasn''t run.
      
      `decision 369: Topic bundles: names, descriptions and rules` is already answered, so I didn''t add a pending-decision link. Per the task, I added nothing else. The next run of task 1652 will check for the rows again.
        → Bash: pm task-pending-decision 1652 369 2>&1 | tail -5
        → Bash: pm show 1652 2>&1 | head -8
      I couldn''t do task 1652 yet, and I''ve left it open. I ran `pm task-pending-decision 1652 369` to satisfy the stop hook. That decision is already answered, so I don''t know whether it parked the task. The command printed nothing, and `pm show 1652` only printed the milestone header, so it didn''t confirm either way.
      
      The task is blocked because `app/data/bundles.json` has no rows for the five topic bundles. That file is written by `task 1644: Create the five topic bundles`, which hasn''t run yet. Nothing was edited or staged.
      
      Check whether task 1652 now shows as pending. If it doesn''t, it will pick up again once task 1644 has added the rows.
      [success: 5 turns, $0.14]', '2026-10-21T21:51:50Z', '2026-10-21T21:52:31Z', NULL, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1672, NULL, '''In common'' style: no new drafts, existing questions not rejected', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-21, review.md, audit.md, translate-review.md, qgen.py (existing flag), question-axes.json (+movies), plans/20 PE-7, 11 translations approved, export', 'The developer''s rule (2026-10-21): no new question in the "what do these have in common?" style (move `connection`); existing approved questions in that style are fine and are never rejected or sent to `needs_work` for it, in any locale. Replaces the full retirement from commit `7cef782c` (2026-10-11, never a developer decision); context: `decision 366: Demo list: 6 listed questions can''t be translated cleanly: replace them, fix their sources, or warn?` (q-0872, q-1032).

- Drafting: keep `connection` at weight 0 in `authoring/data/question-axes.json` (never drawn); its description says "no new drafts", not "retired"
- Review of a new draft (no `translated_from`, not yet approved): may still reject the style
- Review of translations, audit (`audit.md` reason 7), rework, tighten: the style is not a finding; reword `review.md` reasons 7 and the `style` problem list, `audit.md` 7 accordingly; check `translate-review.md` and whatever composes it
- Existing `needs_work` translations whose only finding is this style (`problems: ["style"]`, feedback names "in common" / "en común" / "gemeinsam"): set to approved (reviewer human, this task); others stay
- `plans/20-pipeline-efficiency.md` PE-7 note and any other "retired" mention (`rg -i "in common|en común|retired style"`): follow the new rule
- Record the rule: `pm decision record` as the developer''s 2026-10-21 rule, citing this task
- Checks: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`', '2026-10-21T22:05:48Z', '2026-10-21T22:07:00Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1673, 84, 'Apply the translatability checks of the 12 flagged sources', 'work', 'done', 600, '2026-10-21, authoring/data/questions.json, authoring/data/bundles/{mexico,spain}/concepts, app/data pools, app/client/src/engine/choice.test.ts. Moves: q-0711 → mexico/childrens-songs, q-0905 → mexico/sayings, q-0958 → mexico/sayings, q-1248 → mexico/childrens-songs, q-1163 → mexico/tv-shows-and-hosts, q-0975 → spain/folk-music-and-dance, q-1252 → spain/childrens-tv, q-1498 → spain/childrens-tv, q-1998 → spain/sayings, q-2091 → spain/slang (spain ones locale es-ES; translatable:false kept for language-bound ones, dropped for q-1163, q-0975, q-1252). Unflagged: q-1692, q-2196. Concept lists for the 7 new subcategories made with qgen concepts (claude: 14 calls, $3.23); the moved questions were retagged concept+axes by it (needed for validate). Rule recorded as decision 390; demo hole q-1248 raised as decision 391. validate still fails on q-0110 (task 1607, decision 389) and q-1248 in demo; npm run check fails only on knip electron-builder (pre-existing).', 'The developer checked every `base` source with `translatable: false` (except q-0110, settled by `decision 366: Demo list: 6 listed questions can''t be translated cleanly: replace them, fix their sources, or warn?`): decisions 377–388, one per source (q-0711, q-0905, q-0958, q-0975, q-1163, q-1248, q-1252, q-1498, q-1692, q-1998, q-2091, q-2196). Apply each answer.

Developer''s rule (2026-10-21): a Spanish-only question doesn''t stay in `base`; it goes into the Spanish-language regional bundle it fits best (`spain`, `colombia`, `mexico`, …, whatever fits). So no new "Spanish varieties only" flag; `pm decision record` the rule.

- **translatable**: drop `translatable: false`; the next `tr-*` runs pick it up (no run here)
- **Spanish only (es, es-ES)** and **es only**: move the source to the best-fitting Spanish-language regional bundle (by what a player needs to know: Spain''s TV or songs → `spain`, a Latin American usage → that country''s bundle; pan-Hispanic → the bundle where it plays most naturally, say why in the note); its bundle''s voice and spelling (`locale-es.md` / `locale-es-ES.md`, bundle voice); its existing base translations dropped; `translatable` per that bundle''s own rules
- **move to a regional bundle** (named in the answer): as above, into that bundle
- In every move: a fitting subcategory of the bundle''s taxonomy (`app/data/bundles/<id>/categories.json`); `concept`, `axes` kept; the bundle''s overlap check (`no_overlap`) against its own questions; list the moves (id → bundle/subcategory) in the task note
- **retire**: as `qgen` retires a question elsewhere (status, not deletion)
- Afterwards: `qgen export`, `qgen validate`, `qgen demo --check` pass; if a moved or retired id is in `authoring/data/demo.json` (the demo is base only, decision 339), raise a decision with replacement candidates
- Checks: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate`', '2026-10-21T22:08:13Z', '2026-10-21T22:28:46Z', NULL, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1674, 184, 'Merge duplicates(): same generic answer plus essential photo is no duplicate', 'work', 'done', 690, '2026-10-21, authoring/tools/qgen.py, plans/20-pipeline-efficiency.md', 'Found by `task 1630: End-to-end check on a throw-away theme bundle`.

- `duplicates()` (`authoring/tools/qgen.py`, merge step) calls two questions duplicates when the answers are equal and both have an essential media of the same type, whatever the wording.
- Scratch theme bundle (astronomy): "This is our Moon. What is it mostly made of? → Rock" (essential photo) was dropped as "duplicate like q-4831: Fans of which kind of music are famous for making this hand sign at concerts? → Rock".
- Theme bundles go deeper into one topic with many photo questions, so short generic answers (Rock, Gold, Ice, Iron, Water …) will hit this more often than in base.
- Fix idea: the `both_essential` branch also needs some textual tie (question similarity above a floor, or the same/stem-equal `concept`), e.g. reuse `overlap_candidates`'' concept stems; rate''s overlap check still catches real overlaps.
- Check: a throw-away script running `duplicates()` over the two questions above (none) and over a real duplicate pair from earlier `dropped.json` files under `work/batch-*/` (still a duplicate); count how many past drops would change.', '2026-10-21T22:16:25Z', '2026-10-21T22:36:41Z', 1630, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1675, 89, 'Real upload: bundles without a pool or without Steam IDs stay out of the build', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-21, authoring/steam/steam.py, plans/18-steam-integration.md (stage/ids checked with a harness; trivia-desktop-build --dir and upload --dry-run not re-run)', '`plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`; found by `task 1652: Steamworks rows and steam.json entries for the five topic DLCs`.

Now (2026-10-21): every folder in `app/data/bundles/` ships, with or without a pool. `usa`, `germany`, `uk` and the five topic bundles (`stem`, `sports`, `history`, `movies`, `geography`) have only `categories.json` / `names.*.json`; `trivia-steam stage` stages each as a DLC depot (1–4 files), and `steam.py` `ids()` exits unless every `steam.json` `dlc` entry has `appid` + `depot`. So a real `trivia-steam upload` is blocked until the developer has created a DLC app for bundles that offer nothing yet, and an unentered bundle with a pool blocks it too.

Do:
- A bundle ships as DLC only if it has a pool (`pool[.<locale>].json`, decision 112: missing = not offered) and real IDs in `steam.json`; the others are left out of the build (data excluded from OS depots and from `build/dlc/`, no depot VDF), with one line each in stage/upload output (`<id>: not shipped (no pool | no Steam IDs)`).
- `--dry-run` keeps placeholder IDs for all of them, so the VDFs stay checkable.
- Keep the stage check (packs in the build = `pack-media.json` = shipped `dlc` entries) and the smoke''s with/without packs runs consistent with the same rule; one shared function, not two lists.
- Update plan 18 "Builds and depots" (DLC depots bullet) and the SW-7 "Installation → Depots" note.

Check: `trivia-desktop-build --dir`, `trivia-steam stage`, `trivia-steam upload --dry-run` (all depots), and `ids()` with only colombia''s IDs filled (temporary edit) accepts a real-upload ID set.', '2026-10-21T22:59:58Z', '2026-10-21T23:01:38Z', 1652, 0, NULL, 'app');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1676, 188, 'run batch-<n> (stem)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-28, Done: batch-26: 327 merged, 302 approved, 25 needs work (took 47m56s). claude: 394 calls, $33.83. report authoring/reports/batch-26.md; health ✗ → decision 464; run''s real name batch-26 (task 1676 can''t be renamed while running)', 'Part of `plan 188: Content runs for the topic bundles` (milestone 19), bundle `stem`, per `task 1660: Topic runs stem: start`. Drafting run in English; never re-asks base (`decision 350: Overlap rate in drafting: which changes?`).

## Steps
- `nix develop -c qgen batch --bundle stem` (`authoring/RUNBOOK.md` steps 1–5).
- After the run rename this task and its QC task to the batch name `qgen` printed (`pm task set`; counter shared with plans 17 and 84).
- Done when its report exists, the printed paths are staged, and the note has the "Done:" line and the report path.

## pm-run rules (plan 84, plan 17 "Batch tasks under pm run")
- D-36: no prompt, pool, media or `qgen.py` changes; findings become decisions or tasks in their own plans (`plan 184: Pipeline for topic bundles` while it has open tasks, else a new plan in milestone 19). Only exception: a locale joining `stem`''s `languages` row.
- `tasks.sql` alone isn''t a dirty tree. Stage exactly the `git add` paths the command prints (plus `app/data/bundles.json` after a `languages` edit); don''t commit (pm commits as "task N: …").
- Exit 75, any other non-zero code, or exit 1 three times at one step → `pm decision add "Continue <run> (stem)…?"` with the last 30 lines of output in the body, `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <id>`, stage nothing, stop.
- Note on done: the "Done:" line and report path (run tasks), or the QC numbers (approved, rejected, needs_work, agreement, $ per approved, review time per 100).', '2026-10-21T23:31:50Z', '2026-10-28T23:01:47Z', 1660, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1677, 188, 'QC batch-26 (stem)', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-28, QC batch-26 (stem): spot check raised (decision 465), no changes decision (1 major audit finding on approved, agreement audit 93 %); rework-20: 15 of 25 approved, $2.98; stem en $0.26 per approved, 302/2000; added translation runs tasks 1781 (es), 1782 (es-ES), 1783 (de); files: questions.json, pools, reports', 'Part of `plan 188: Content runs for the topic bundles` (milestone 19), bundle `stem`, per `task 1660: Topic runs stem: start`. QC of the drafting run `run batch-<n> (stem)` (same batch name after the rename).

## Steps
`authoring/QC.md` steps 1–4:
- `pm decision add "Spot check batch-<n> (stem) done?"`: native English speaker, the developer or an outside reviewer via `qgen spotcheck export` (`decision 221: How does an outside native reviewer reach the review tool?`); never an LLM; 30-question blind check, ≥ 90 % agreement, below it only feeds step 4.
- `qgen report --qc batch-<n>`.
- `pm decision add "QC batch-<n> (stem): which changes?"`; change tasks: theme pipeline findings in `plan 184: Pipeline for topic bundles` while it has open tasks, else a new plan in milestone 19; the rest in `plan 17: Batch runs` at priority 650.
- `qgen rework` once (decision 3).
- Note QC numbers and `qgen report --cost` (per bundle).

## Then, first that applies
1. Translations: per L in es, es-ES, de with no open `run tr-<L>-<n> (stem)` and ≥ 50 approved en sources of `stem` not yet translated into L → add that run: `nix develop -c qgen batch --translate <L> --bundle stem`; rename to the real run name; note the "Done:" line, report path and from `authoring/reports/<run>.md` and `qgen report --cost`: selected, translated, approved, needs_work, rejected, not travelling, $ per approved translation, audit agreement. No spot check, no QC task, no `qgen health ack`. needs_work: nothing. After the run: if it wrote `app/data/bundles/stem/pool.<L>.json` and `<L>` isn''t in `stem`''s `languages` (`app/data/bundles.json`), add it (row edit only), `qgen validate` clean, stage the file; `qgen report --bundle stem --locale <L>` at 2000 → no next run, else ≥ 50 approved en sources not yet in L → add `run tr-<L>-<n+1> (stem)` (same body), fewer → nothing; each run adds a progress line (approved per locale) for `stem` in `plans/22-bundles.md`; all four locales at 2000 → `stem` done there. One open translation run per locale.
2. `qgen report --bundle stem` supply block shows no English draft gap left → no next pair; note drafting done in `plans/22-bundles.md`; staggered pace (`decision 371: Topic bundles: pace and order of the content runs`: stem, sports, history, geography, movies, one at a time) → re-add the next bundle''s start task (`Topic runs sports: start`, same body as `task 1660: Topic runs stem: start` with its own bundle; for sports: sports).
3. The pace decision''s numbers look far off (the developer''s review time or $ per approved well above its projection) → `pm decision add` asking the developer instead of the next pair.
4. Else the next pair `run batch-<n+1> (stem)` + `QC batch-<n+1> (stem)` (same bodies, next batch number; one open pair).

## pm-run rules (plan 84, plan 17 "Batch tasks under pm run")
- D-36: no prompt, pool, media or `qgen.py` changes; findings become decisions or tasks in their own plans (`plan 184: Pipeline for topic bundles` while it has open tasks, else a new plan in milestone 19). Only exception: a locale joining `stem`''s `languages` row.
- `tasks.sql` alone isn''t a dirty tree. Stage exactly the `git add` paths the command prints (plus `app/data/bundles.json` after a `languages` edit); don''t commit (pm commits as "task N: …").
- Exit 75, any other non-zero code, or exit 1 three times at one step → `pm decision add "Continue <run> (stem)…?"` with the last 30 lines of output in the body, `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <id>`, stage nothing, stop.
- Note on done: the "Done:" line and report path (run tasks), or the QC numbers (approved, rejected, needs_work, agreement, $ per approved, review time per 100).', '2026-10-21T23:31:50Z', '2026-10-28T23:09:08Z', 1660, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1678, NULL, 'Replace the menu open/close sounds with a lower pair', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-22, menu-abre.m4a, menu-cierra.m4a, CREDITS.md, sound.svelte.ts, plans/04-ui-tv-display.md', 'Developer, 2026-10-22: the Esc menu / dialog open and close sounds are still too high-pitched, even after the 15 % pitch-down of 2026-10-17 (commit 9d86de3c, UI-8 note in `plans/04-ui-tv-display.md`). Replace them with a pair of different recordings; pitching the current files down again isn''t enough.

- Today: `menu-abre.m4a` / `menu-cierra.m4a` = Kenney Interface Sounds `maximize_001` / `minimize_001` (CC0), played at rate 0.85 (`SAMPLE_FOR` "menu-open"/"menu-close", `app/client/src/game/sound.svelte.ts`); synth fallback tones 425↔765 Hz (`RECIPES`)
- Want: a matched pair (open/close clearly belong together, close = the mirror or softer twin of open), clearly lower and warmer, short (≲ 0.3 s), soft, not shrill; heard often, so unobtrusive on a TV
  - e.g. a soft wooden/felt click or "thup", a low card or page slide, a muted pop; no bright blips, bells or high chimes
- Sources: CC0 or CC BY only (UI-10); Kenney packs (other interface/UI packs), OpenGameArt, Wikimedia Commons, freesound CC0
- Pick by measuring, since you can''t listen: spectral centroid / dominant frequency well below the current files'' (measure those first, report both); peaks under ~1 kHz preferred
- Convert like the other effects (AAC `.m4a`, loudness-normalized to match the neighbours); keep the file names `menu-abre` / `menu-cierra`; drop the 0.85 rate unless still needed; lower the synth fallback tones to match
- `CREDITS.md` rows updated (CC BY: credit)
- Done note: source, file, measured pitch old → new, `/?efectos` to audition («menú abierto» / «menú cerrado»)
- Then `pm decision add --once` "New menu open/close sounds: OK on the TV?" (plain-English intro; how to listen: `TRIVIA_SOUND=1`, `/?efectos` or open/close the Esc menu in a game; options: approve / changes: …), with one alternative pair staged in `work/menu-sounds/` of the main checkout to compare', '2026-10-22T03:14:16Z', '2026-10-22T03:16:32Z', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1679, NULL, 'Fullscreen only from the Esc menu; remembered window state', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-21, app/desktop/{main.mjs,preload.cjs,window-state.mjs}, app/client/{devshell.js,src/lib/desktop.ts,src/game/Overlay.svelte,src/locales/*}, gallery.py; gallery set task-1679 (menu-start, menu-solo)', 'Developer, 2026-10-22: F11 and F12 do nothing in the desktop shell; fullscreen ↔ windowed only via the Esc menu; fullscreen state and window size remembered between starts.
- `app/desktop/main.mjs`: drop the F11 toggle in `before-input-event` (the `--rp-probe` F9–F11 keys stay); F12 stays inert (devTools only with `TRIVIA_DEVTOOLS=1`)
- Esc menu (`Overlay.svelte` `items`): the one «Pantalla completa» item → two items, «Pantalla completa» and «Modo ventana» (all four catalogs; `locales/style/<locale>.md` first), the active one disabled (`enabled: false`); the shell tells the page the state (initial + `enter-full-screen`/`leave-full-screen`) over the bridge
  - browser (no shell): same two items from `document.fullscreenElement` + `fullscreenchange`
- Remembered: fullscreen yes/no, windowed bounds (x, y, width, height), in a small file in `userData` (not the game save; corrupt/missing → defaults); written on toggle, resize/move (debounced) and quit
  - start: last state; first start: fullscreen
  - windowed default: ~80 % of the display''s work area, centred (`screen.getDisplayMatching`); stored bounds off every current display (monitor unplugged) → default on the primary display; `minWidth`/`minHeight` 1024×600
  - Steam Deck / `--rp-probe` / `--lag-probe`: unchanged behaviour where they force a mode
- `rg -i "F11"` over plans/, README, `directory.md`, release checklist rows and pm bodies: "F11/menu toggles" → "Esc menu toggles"; fix every hit (decision 200)
- Browser (`trivia`, dev server): F11/F12 stay the browser''s
- Gallery: the Esc menu shot(s) change; `trivia-gallery --set task-<id> --only <menu shots>` for the done note', '2026-10-22T03:18:24Z', '2026-10-22T03:22:00Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1680, 17, 'run batch-13', 'work', 'dropped', -100, 'killed (run 1832)', 'Next batch of `plan 17: Batch runs` (per-batch pattern 1), added by `task 1580: QC batch-11`. batch-12 was the colombia batch, so the next `base` batch takes the next free number: use whatever `qgen batch` prints. Follow `authoring/RUNBOOK.md` steps 1–5 exactly, including "Under `pm run`" (plain `qgen batch`; `tasks.sql` alone isn''t a dirty tree; stage exactly the printed `git add` paths, also `authoring/reports/batches.md`, don''t commit).

- Gate first (plan 17 "English-first batches"): `qgen batch` drafts `en` for `base`. Missing: `pm decision add "batch: English drafting not in place, wait?"`, `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <id>`, stop. Never a Spanish `base` draft.
- Runs after the change tasks (they outrank -100), including the one from `decision 405: QC batch-11: which changes?`.
- batch-9 to batch-12 health ended ✗: expect exit 2 from the health stop; never `qgen health ack` by the worker. Exit 2: first `pm decision list --grep "<run>: health stop"` (the run named in the output); a pending one found (e.g. `decision 408: batch-12: health stop, ack?`) → `pm task-pending-decision 1680 <id>`, no new decision, stage nothing, stop. Exit 75 / exit 1 three times at one step: RUNBOOK "Under `pm run`" / plan 17 "Batch tasks under `pm run`".
- Never inside this task: prompt, `qgen.py`, subcategory or media changes; findings become decisions or tasks in their own plans.

Done when: the batch report exists and the batch''s files are staged; note: the "Done:" line, the report path, and what of plan 147 / milestone 9 was missing, if anything.', '2026-10-22T04:54:40Z', '2026-10-23T01:42:56Z', 1580, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1681, 17, 'QC batch-13', 'work', 'done', -100, '2026-10-23, QC of batch-14 (the batch task 1712 ran): audit 0 of 56 major on approved, audit/review agreement 97 %; no proposals (no kind with ≥ 2 major findings), so no QC decision; spot check raised as decision 417, health ✗ already decision 416; no QC report section yet (no spot check recorded); exit check: 5488 approved, only difficulty 1 short (243/250), health and spot-check lines await the developer''s answers; rework-8: 24 of 54 needs_work approved, 30 still need work (claude: 48 calls, opus 44 / sonnet 4, $5.47); decisions 405/408/409 handled, no change tasks; next pair task 1725 run batch-15, task 1726 QC batch-15; staged authoring/data/questions.json, app/data pool files; qgen validate OK', 'QC of the batch run by `task 1680: run batch-13` (the batch after batch-12, the fourth English `base` batch), per `authoring/QC.md` (plan 16) and `plan 17: Batch runs` "Per-batch pattern" 2, "Reviews don''t gate (decision 414)" and "English-first batches". If the batch report doesn''t exist, stop without changes.

No step waits for the developer (`decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`): decisions are raised, never `pm task-pending-decision`, never `--requires` on them; the task finishes.

1. Act on answered review decisions of earlier batches not yet acted on: `pm decision list --answered --grep "health" --grep "Spot check" --grep "QC batch"` (e.g. `decision 408: batch-12: health stop, ack?`, `decision 409: Spot check batch-12 done?`, `decision 405: QC batch-11: which changes?`); for each, check its consequences/existing tasks; turn the unhandled ones into change tasks and report lines, `pm decision consequences <id> "<what>"`. Unanswered ones stay open.
2. Health ✗ of the batch: decision "<batch>: health ✗, look at it?" (look it up first, no duplicate; no task linked). Never `qgen health ack`.
3. Spot check: decision "Spot check <batch> done?" (size `quality.spot_check_size`, plan 147), raised, not waited on.
4. `qgen report --qc <batch>` with the spot checks recorded so far → decision "QC <batch>: which changes?"; its recommended option names the change tasks the next QC task adds once answered.
5. Records (`qgen report`, source locale): approved/target per difficulty, needs_work by reason, media funnel and yield (plan 146); English-batch comparisons: difficulty target vs. rated vs. reviewed against batch-9 to batch-11, health trend per `decision 233: Batch health trend rule across the switch to English drafts?`, overlap against the es-sourced pool too (`decision 232: Overlap of English drafts against the es-sourced base pool: which keys?`), agreement vs. batch-9 (28/30), batch-10 (29/30), batch-11 (28/30).
6. Change tasks from answered decisions: English-pipeline ones in `plan 147: English-first batches: calibration, overlap and QC across languages` (its priority), the rest in plan 17 at `--priority 650`, work tree `questions`.
7. needs_work per `decision 3: How are needs_work questions (33 now, more per batch) resolved?`: `qgen rework --batch <batch>` once; note the count before/after.
8. Next pair: `run batch-<n+1>` and `QC batch-<n+1>` (-100, QC requires the run), bodies like this task''s and task 1680''s as plan 17 now reads; or, if plan 12''s targets are met or the next batch would overshoot every remaining gap, the exit-check task (plan 17 "Exit check").

Missing tooling to list in the note: none known; `qgen report --overlaps` timed out (>2 min) in QC batch-11.

Done when: steps 1–8 done or listed as missing in the note; staged per RUNBOOK "Under `pm run`"; `qgen validate` clean.', '2026-10-22T04:54:40Z', '2026-10-23T08:05:48Z', 1580, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1682, 17, 'Description must not give away the answer''s defining trait (QC batch-11 A)', 'work', 'done', 650, '2026-10-22, authoring/tools/prompts/house-style.md, authoring/tools/prompts/review.md (applied in 71cd9d91)', 'Change approved in `decision 405: QC batch-11: which changes?` (proposal 1), from `task 1580: QC batch-11`.

- Audit of batch-11: 2 major giveaway findings on approved questions. q-4907: description "original alarm clock" points to morning; q-4925: description "always goes sideways" names the crab''s best-known trait.
- Change `authoring/prompts/review.md` and `draft.md`: the description must not state the answer''s defining trait or the clue that rules out wrong options. The review checks the description against the options alone, before the hints.
- Prompt changes are the developer''s (RUNBOOK): draft the wording, show it in a pm decision (`pm decision add`), apply after the answer; make this task pending on it.
- Subject to `task 1251: Audit: hint giveaways are minor unless they name the answer (QC batch-8 120 D)`: don''t contradict it; hints naming the answer stay the major case.
- Done when: the answered wording is in both prompts, `qgen validate` passes; `rg` the old wording over comments and `.md` files.', '2026-10-22T04:54:47Z', '2026-10-22T22:40:48Z', 1580, 0, NULL, 'questions');
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1683, NULL, 'Game server: refuse cross-site save requests', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-22, app/server/main.py', 'Audit finding 1. Any web page open in the same browser can send a plain cross-site `POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/save/backup?kind=corrupt` (a "simple request", sent without a CORS preflight). It moves `state/game.json` into `backup/`, and the family''s next load starts fresh.

- `app/server/main.py` `Handler.do_POST` and `do_PUT`: refuse with 403 `{"error": "forbidden"}` when an `Origin` header is present and isn''t `http://<Host header>`; requests without `Origin` (same-origin GET, curl) keep working
- `PUT /api/save` is already preflighted (no OPTIONS handler → 501); the check also covers it
- Desktop build unaffected (no HTTP server)
- Update the API block of the `main.py` docstring
- Done: a `curl -X POST -H ''Origin: http://evil.example'' …/api/save/backup?kind=corrupt` gets 403 and the save stays put; the game in the browser still saves and backs up', '2026-10-22T20:59:16Z', '2026-10-22T21:01:51Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1684, NULL, 'qgen batch: one process per run directory', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-22, authoring/tools/qgen.py', 'Audit finding 2. `work/` is shared by every work tree (symlink). `next_batch()` (`authoring/tools/qgen.py`) resumes any unfinished `work/batch-N`. A second `qgen batch` started while the first is running, from another work tree or by hand, resumes the same run in parallel: claude calls paid twice, the same files written by both, the same new ids merged into two pools. Today only pm task order (decision 401''s note: one topic bundle at a time) prevents it.

- `cmd_batch` and `cmd_translate_batch`: once the run dir `d` is known, hold `fcntl.flock` on `d / "run.lock"` with `LOCK_EX | LOCK_NB` for the rest of the process; on failure exit with "<run> is in use by another qgen process"
- The OS frees the lock on a crash: no stale-lock handling
- Ignore `run.lock` wherever run files are listed or copied, if any listing would pick it up
- Done: a second `qgen batch` started next to a running one exits at once with that message; a rerun after the first one ends or is killed resumes normally', '2026-10-22T20:59:17Z', '2026-10-22T21:03:40Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1685, NULL, 'Split qgen.py by subcommand group', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-22, authoring/tools/{qgen,report,review_steps,audit,translate,rework,player_reports,validate,taxonomy,health}.py, authoring/server/{main,overview,spot_checks}.py', 'Audit finding 3. `authoring/tools/qgen.py` is 5,686 lines with ~40 subcommands. Parallel pm workers editing unrelated subcommands conflict in this one file at merge time. Some groups already have their own modules (`batches`, `health`, `translations`, `pool_export`).

- Move whole subcommand groups with their helpers into their own modules, one job each; `qgen.py` keeps the argparse `main()` and dispatch
- First candidates: `validate_pool` and its checks → `validate.py`; the translate commands (`cmd_translate_batch` and its steps) next to `translations.py`; `cmd_fix`, `report_played`
- No behaviour change; don''t split functions only to make them shorter; follow decision 199 (import, don''t copy) and decision 200 (rg old names in comments and `.md` files, fix them in the same commit)
- Done: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `qgen validate`, `qgen batch --help` and `qgen report` work as before; `qgen.py` is well under half its size', '2026-10-22T20:59:17Z', '2026-10-22T21:08:09Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1686, NULL, 'Report server: atomic telemetry rate limit', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-22, report-server/src/http.ts, index.ts, telemetry.ts', 'Audit finding 4. `report-server/src/telemetry.ts` `postTelemetry` reads the daily count (`count()`), then raises it in a later batch: posts that arrive together all pass the check. Reports already do it atomically (`bump()` in `report-server/src/index.ts`: `INSERT … ON CONFLICT … RETURNING count`).

- Bump first with `RETURNING count` (user, then `*`), reject with `rateLimited` when over `RATE_TELEMETRY_USER` / `RATE_TELEMETRY_TOTAL`, then insert the session; reuse or move `bump` instead of a second copy (decision 199)
- Keep the duplicate check before the bump, so a duplicate doesn''t count
- Done: `tsc -p report-server` passes; `trivia-report-server dev` + `seed-telemetry` still stores sessions; the limit holds', '2026-10-22T20:59:17Z', '2026-10-22T21:08:36Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1687, NULL, 'atomic.locked: no double holder after a stale lock', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-22, authoring/tools/atomic.py', 'Audit finding 5. `authoring/tools/atomic.py` `_acquire` deletes a lock file older than `STALE` (60 s). Two waiters that both see the same stale file: one deletes it and creates a new one, the other then deletes that new one; both hold the lock, and a pool write can be lost.

- Replace create-and-delete with `fcntl.flock(LOCK_EX)` on `<name>.lock` (kept open while held; the OS frees it on a crash); drop `STALE` and the stale logic
- The `PermissionError` branch is for Windows: check whether the authoring tools must run on Windows at all (README, flake). If they must, keep the current path there behind `os.name == "nt"`, else drop it
- Keep the in-process `RLock` re-entrancy and the lock order in the docstring
- Done: authoring server and `qgen` still share the pool lock (one holds, the other waits); `npm run check` (ruff) passes', '2026-10-22T20:59:18Z', '2026-10-22T21:09:10Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1688, NULL, 'Splash.svelte: silence the svelte-check warnings', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-22, app/client/src/game/question/Splash.svelte', 'Audit finding 6. `npm run check` warns twice in `app/client/src/game/question/Splash.svelte` (lines 33–34, `state_referenced_locally` for `ownCategory`, `ownSub`). Reading the props once is right: every caller wraps `Splash` in `{#key question.id}` (`Question.svelte`, `Timed.svelte`, `EffectsDemo.svelte`). The noise hides real warnings.

- Wrap both reads in `untrack(...)`, as the next line already does for `picked`
- Done: `npm run check` shows 0 warnings for `Splash.svelte`; the splash still shows the right topic per question', '2026-10-22T20:59:18Z', '2026-10-22T21:09:50Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1689, NULL, 'Investigate and fix: pm run wrote a schema-only tasks.sql during a git autostash', 'exec', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-22, plans/pm-tasks-sql-safety.md, README.md; decision 412', 'On 2026-10-22 at about 19:08 local, in the main checkout, `tasks.sql` lost every data row: it became a 182-line, schema-only file. That happened while `pm run` (PID 494342) was running.

What happened, in order:
- `tasks.sql` had uncommitted changes from pm: the line `INSERT INTO run … (1823, 1296, …, ''running'', …)`, for `task 1296: QC batch-12 (colombia)`, which had just started
- the developer''s session ran `git pull --rebase --autostash` (origin/main was 1 commit ahead, `a6a66f0a`)
- the autostash put `tasks.sql` back to HEAD; while it was stashed, pm wrote `tasks.sql` (mtime 19:08) with only the schema
- the rebase didn''t run, and the autostash couldn''t be put back ("Your changes are safe in the stash")
- recovered by hand: `git show ''stash@{0}:tasks.sql'' > tasks.sql`, `pm validate` OK

Investigate:
- how pm reads and writes `tasks.sql` (load per command? kept in memory and dumped?), and how a dump of the schema without data can happen: reading the file while git was rewriting it (empty or truncated), a failed import that left an empty DB, a non-atomic write, …
- reproduce it if you can: `pm run` busy + `git stash` / checkout of `tasks.sql` in a scratch copy, never in the real checkout

Fix, so it can''t happen again:
- pm never writes a `tasks.sql` with fewer rows than it read without a command that deletes them; a load that gives an empty or invalid DB is an error, not an empty project
- atomic writes (temp file + rename); detect the file changing under pm (mtime/hash) and refuse or reload instead of overwriting
- if the cause or fix is in pm itself (outside this repo), write up a change for it and a pm decision for the developer; in this repo, a note on git operations to avoid while `pm run` is running (README / AGENTS.md) if still needed after the fix

Done when: the cause is named, the fix (or the pm change write-up) exists, and a reproduction no longer loses rows.', '2026-10-23T00:10:29Z', '2026-10-23T00:11:19Z', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
