# Plan 9: masterplan

Milestone 9 is S4 of the Steam track (D-34, `plans/11-steam.md`): enough reviewed questions, in every launch language, that a stranger''s family plays many evenings before questions repeat, plus a measurement that proves it. It needs translated UI catalogs, translated, re-rated and reviewed questions, regional bundles (D-39; decision 110: 2000 approved each, region''s language + en, free DLC, `colombia` the pilot; then `usa`, `germany`, `uk`, `spain`, `mexico` by Steam audience, developer 2026-10-15), `qgen report --simulate` passing the content target for every launch language, and UI wording the gamemaster has checked on the TV (style guides, screen gallery), joker names made again English first, one symbol per joker in every language, and English-first drafting for `base` (developer, 2026-10-15): from batch-9 on `en` is the source of every new `base` question, translated to `es`, `es-ES` and `de`, each its own pool with 5000 approved (decision 21: Content target per player and language (OQ-32)); and English slug keys for every category and subcategory in every bundle, display names only from `names.<locale>.json` (developer, 2026-10-16); question translations reviewed by the LLM translation review only, no human spot check (developer, 2026-10-16); human reviews gate no regional or translation run (`decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`). Today: 1136 approved (`base` 1034, `colombia` 102), Spanish only; milestone 1 takes `base` to 5000 (D-52).

**The tasks of this masterplan are not implementation work: each one writes the plan for one part below** (`pm plan add 9 …`, priority as suggested), and that plan''s tasks do the work.

## Preconditions (other milestones; a part''s plan task checks them first)
- OQ-31 launch languages + Spanish variety: plan 37 (milestone 7). OQ-32 content target: plan 38. Default preset → burns per game: plan 35 (OQ-30). Burn multiplier for several players: plan 41 (OQ-37). If a needed decision is still pending, the plan task makes itself pending on it (`pm task-pending-decision`) and stops.
- **If OQ-31 = Spanish only:** parts 3–7 shrink to nothing: their plan tasks drop with that reason (`pm task drop`), except what the Spanish variety needs (part 8). The rest still applies to Spanish.
- TS engine (milestone 2, plans 19, 20; screens on the engine PORT-7): the simulation runs on it. Age-group windows and bundle filter in the engine (plan 27, milestone 5): the simulation and the bundle filter (RG-3) use them.
- Catalog (milestone 3: plans 21, 22, 23, 24): `t()`, `es`, `xx`, draft `en`. Settings screen (plan 36, MD-7): the language setting goes there.
- Pool growth and QC (milestone 1: plans 12 targets, 13 gap-aimed drafting, 15 drift, 16 QC/D-56, 17 batch runs). This milestone reuses them per language; it doesn''t rebuild them. The content side of the English switch (calibration examples, concept angle, cross-language overlap, health and spot check across the switch) is `plan 147: English-first batches: calibration, overlap and QC across languages` (milestone 1); part 15 doesn''t duplicate it.
- Licence/price: answered (decision 66: Price model (OQ-33), bundles as free DLC; decision 107: Licence (OQ-35)). A part that writes files depending on them follows them.

## Rules for every part
- Questions only through `qgen batch` (D-36). New pipeline steps (translate, re-rate, neutral Spanish) become `qgen batch` modes, with RUNBOOK and D-36 amended as an implementation task (like BN-11). Workers never edit pools or pick media by hand.
- Quality bar of plan 16 / D-56 applies per language to drafted batches (`base`, regional): LLM audit + blind human spot check per batch.
- Reviews don''t gate runs (milestone 1, "Reviews don''t gate generation"; decision 414): health ✗, spot checks and QC proposals are raised as pm decisions, but no task ever waits on one (no `pm task-pending-decision`, no prerequisite); health ✗ never stops `qgen batch` (drafting, `--bundle` or `--translate`): report and decision only, `qgen health ack` = the developer''s "looked at it"; answers are acted on afterwards by whatever task runs next. The only human gate is the final release (`trivia-release-check`, release bar), the developer''s, not a pm task.
- Translations (milestone, developer 2026-10-16; tr-en-1 and tr-de-1 spot checks found every translation good): the LLM translation review is the only review, in every question locale (milestone 12''s included): no native-speaker spot check, no QC decision per `tr-*` run, no pilot go/no-go, no `qgen health ack` after a pilot. Decision 45''s health thresholds are reported, never a stop (decision 414 partly supersedes decision 45 and `decision 313: Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run`); nothing waits for the developer. The developer may still review translations in the review tool; `qgen flag` still sets `needs_work`.
- `app/` never reads `authoring/` (D-35): per-locale pools and category/bundle names are exported to `app/data/`.
- The current game keeps working after every task until the Steam build replaces it (D-59): Spanish, Colombia on, same keys (unless LUI-4 changes them by decision). The family''s `es` pool keeps its es-sourced questions as they are; English-sourced ones join it as `es` translations.
- Owning plan files get tasks `[x]` with a note (`15-i18n.md`, `15a`, `15b`, `15c`, `16-content-target.md`, `22-bundles.md`); `plans/project.md` in sync. Store page texts (LUI-6) are S5 (milestone''s out of scope); note it in 15a, don''t do it.

## Parts

1. **Simulation: games per new player (CT-2)**
   - Owner: `plans/16-content-target.md` ("Metric").
