INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1711, 128, 'Content target check', 'work', 'open', -130, NULL, 'Task 1 of `plan 128: S4 close-out`: check milestone 9''s content target per question locale and English-first `base`, record the result. Replaces `task 1294: Content target check` (dropped to shed its link to a review decision, `decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`). Checks, docs and pm only; a shortfall becomes runs in `plan 84: Release content runs`, never a fix here.

Binding: `decision 21: Content target per player and language (OQ-32)?` (D-75): pass/fail = 5000 approved per question locale (`en`, `es`, `es-ES`, `de`; milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15) with D-53''s mix; games numbers information only. `decision 26` (D-78): launch languages `es`, `en`, `de` (+ `es-ES`). `decision 235: Source locale per question and translations from either source (English-first base)`. `decision 156: One language for UI and questions`. Plan 57 (CT-5): every drafted batch/back-audit slice with approved questions in the release pool is release-ready; translation runs (`tr-*`) have no QC and no release-ready row; release-ready is reported here, never waited on: the release bar is the developer''s own gate at `trivia-release-check` (decision 414). Decision 414 (developer, 2026-10-23): health ✗, spot checks and QC proposals are decisions no task waits on; this task never pends on one. Translations without human control (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-16; `plan 171: Translations without human control`): the LLM translation review is a translation''s only review; no spot check, QC decision or go/no-go per `tr-*` run; decision 45''s thresholds are reported, never a stop (decision 414). Cost (milestone 9, developer 2026-10-15): `qgen report --cost` is information only; no budget, no gate (`decision 204: Translation pilot done (tr-en-1, tr-de-1)?` irrelevant).

## Guard
- `pm plans list`, `pm show` of plans 57, 62–64, 66–70, 98, 100, 126, 136, 138, 147, 148 and `plan 149: Slug keys for categories` (all tasks done or dropped) and plan 84''s chains 1–3 (neutral Spanish, translation pilot (no go/no-go), full translation per locale `en`, `de`, `es-ES`, `es`) at their end. Not plan 84''s chains 4–5 (regional) nor the pilot-effort task (task 4''s). `plan 17: Batch runs` isn''t waited for.
- One has open tasks: if one is pending on a decision that isn''t a review (spot check, health, QC proposal; decision 414), `pm task-pending-decision <this task> <that decision>`; if it waits on a review decision or on another task, `pm task requires <this task> <that task>`; otherwise stop without changes. Never drop or edit other plans'' tasks.

## Steps
- `qgen validate`; `trivia-media sync --status approved`; `qgen export`.
- `qgen report --simulate` (default matrix: every question locale `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`, default bundles, all age groups, all modes); `qgen report --locale <L>` for `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`; `qgen report --qc` (release-ready column; drafted batches and back-audit slices only); `qgen report --cost` (information: spent, $ per approved).
- Record in `plans/16-content-target.md` ("Where we stand" → dated close-out result): per locale approved vs. 5000 and per level, ✓/✗, games per new player (median, p10, strong bound) for adults solo, bottlenecks, release-ready state, total spent per language (en drafting + translations, plan 70), file sizes of `app/data/pool*.json` and pack pools (task 3 uses them for the install size).

## English-first `base` (plan 148)
- `qgen validate` passes its source-locale rules; every `base` question of batch-9 on has `locale: "en"`.
- Counts per direction (en → `es`, `es-ES`, `de`; es → `en`, `de`, `es-ES`) from `qgen report --locale <L>`; untranslated approved translatable sources by count (information; pass/fail is the locale''s target).
- `pool.es-ES.json` exported (decision 156: an `es-ES` save plays it once its default bundles'' supply passes, else `es`; the browser row is task 2''s).

## Not release-ready
- A drafted batch/slice not release-ready or with its spot check unanswered (e.g. `decision 203: Spot check backaudit-1 done?`): recorded in `plans/16-content-target.md` as the developer''s item for `trivia-release-check` (decision 414); no decision, no wait.

## Shortfall
- A ✗: no fix. If plan 84 has no open pair for that locale: `pm decision add "S4 target not met for <locale>: more runs or lower the target?"` (body: the numbers; options "more runs: plan 84 adds pairs" (recommended), "lower the target (D-75 amended)", "ship as is"), `pm task-pending-decision` for this task and tasks 2–3 of plan 128 (`task 1033: Language picker, UI wording, joker and slug-key check`, `task 1034: Docs close-out of S4`), stop. On the answer "more runs": `pm task add 84` the next run/QC pair (a drafted batch) or `--translate` run (no QC task), `pm task requires <this task> <it>`, stop.
- Plan 84 has an open pair for that locale: `pm task requires <this task> <that run task>`, stop.

Done when: `qgen report --simulate` exits 0 for all four question locales (or an answered decision accepts the shortfall), the result is in `plans/16-content-target.md`.', '2026-10-23T01:28:46Z', NULL, 1710, 0, NULL, 'questions');
