INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1714, 190, 'qgen: health ✗ no longer stops qgen batch', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-22, authoring/tools/{qgen,translate,health}.py, targets.json, README.md, plans/{decisions,15b-question-translation}.md, reports/batches.md', 'Part 1 of `plan 190: Reviews don''t gate generation` (`decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`; partly supersedes `decision 13: Batch health thresholds and stop rule?`, decision 45''s stop, `decision 313: Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run`).

- `authoring/tools/qgen.py` `cmd_batch` and `authoring/tools/translate.py`: a ✗ of the last done, unacked run (`health.stop_reason()`, `health.translate_stop_reason(locale)`) no longer exits; print it to stderr as a warning and go on with the run. `EXIT_HEALTH` and its import go; rename the two functions to what they now return (e.g. `unacked_failure`), `rg` their old names.
- Warning text: names the run and the failed thresholds, points to `qgen report --batches` / the run''s report, and says the developer may record a look with `qgen health ack <run> "<note>"`; no "stop" wording.
- `authoring/tools/health.py`: report section texts ("a ✗ stops the next `qgen batch` until `qgen health ack` (D-55)") → "a ✗ is reported, never a stop (decision 414); `qgen health ack` records the developer''s look"; `batches.md` line "the stop is cleared" → "looked at".
- Command docs: `qgen.py` docstring (`health ack` line), `authoring/data/targets.json` `about`, `README.md` `qgen health ack` line, `plans/15b-question-translation.md` run line, `plans/decisions.md` (D-55 entry and the translation-stop line: mark "superseded by decision 414: no stop"; keep the entries).
- Regenerate `authoring/reports/batches.md` if `qgen report --batches` (or the command that writes it) does so without LLM calls; past per-run reports stay as written.
- Tests: none cover this path today; ponytail decides whether to add one (e.g. a Python check that `cmd_batch` with a failing unacked last run doesn''t exit before drafting, stubbed). Manual check at least: `qgen batch --translate <locale> --dry-run` with a failing unacked run prints the warning and goes on.
- `rg "health stop|EXIT_HEALTH|stop_reason|exit 2|clears the stop"` over code, comments and `.md` (decision 200); RUNBOOK and QC.md are the next task''s (`plan 190` part 2), leave them; `code-review.md` rows and past reports are history.

