INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1715, 190, 'RUNBOOK and QC.md without review waits', 'work', 'dropped', NULL, 'duplicate of task 1716 (plan task and split both added part 2)', 'Part 2 of `plan 190: Reviews don''t gate generation` (`decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`). Needs `task 1714: qgen: health ✗ no longer stops qgen batch` (no exit 2 for health).

`authoring/RUNBOOK.md`:
- Exit code table: drop the 2 row (2 now falls under "other"); add after it: the output shows a health ✗ warning → go on; outside pm, tell the user the warning in step 5.
- "Under `pm run`" step 3: drop the "exit 2 first" bullet (from `task 1692: RUNBOOK: on a health stop, link to a pending ack decision instead of adding a duplicate`) and the exit-2 subjects row. New bullet: a health ✗ warning (output or report) → `pm decision list --grep "<run>: health"` (also finds the older "`<run>`: health stop, ack?"); none open or answered → `pm decision add "<run>: health ✗, look at it?"` (body: the warning verbatim; option "looked at it (qgen health ack <run> \"<note>\")"), **no** `pm task-pending-decision`; the task goes on to step 4. Never run `qgen health ack` as a worker.
- Translation-runs line ("Only a run failing a health threshold makes the next one exit 2 …") → a ✗ is reported and raised as above, never a stop.
- Step 5: "Quality control … `authoring/QC.md`" unchanged; add that review decisions never block the next run.

`authoring/QC.md`:
- Steps intro: "a pm worker stops at each decision and continues when it is answered" → raises each decision and goes on; nothing waits (decision 414).
- Step 2 pm worker: `pm decision add "Spot check <batch> done?"` (body: link, size, `trivia-authoring`; option "done"), no `pm task-pending-decision`, go on to step 3.
- Step 3: `qgen report --qc <batch>` uses the spot checks recorded so far; later ones go into the next QC task''s run.
- Step 4: proposals decision raised, not waited on; its recommended option names the change tasks. "Answered:" → done by the next QC task (step 0 below), then `qgen report --qc <batch> --changes …`.
- New step 0 (or first line of step 1): act on answered review decisions of earlier runs not yet acted on (health look notes, spot-check results, proposal choices; `pm decision list --answered --grep "health" --grep "Spot check" --grep "QC "`) → change tasks, report lines, `pm decision consequences`; unanswered ones stay open.
- Step 5 "Next batch waits" → "Nothing waits": the next batch runs whatever is answered; change tasks outrank it by priority, no link.
- Health ✗ of the batch: same decision as RUNBOOK''s, raised not waited on.
- "Translation runs" stop line → a ✗ is reported and raised as RUNBOOK''s decision, never a stop; the first run is no exception.

Open pm task bodies (decision 200): `rg`-like search with `pm show` over open tasks of `plan 17: Batch runs`, `plan 84: Release content runs`, `plan 188: Content runs for the topic bundles` (e.g. 1681, 1712, 639, 641, 1226, 1228, 1690, 1691, 1676, 1677) for "health stop", "exit 2", "task 1699", "until the plan of task 1699": replace the exit-2 fallback with "health ✗: decision per RUNBOOK, no task linked, go on" via `pm task set <id> --body -` (only tasks not running; keep the rest of each body). Plans 17 and 84''s own text: leave a pm note on them if they can''t be edited, else `pm plan edit`.

Done when: RUNBOOK and QC.md have no review wait and no exit 2 for health; `rg "health stop|exit 2|task-pending-decision" authoring/RUNBOOK.md authoring/QC.md` shows only real-failure cases; open task bodies updated; `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `qgen validate` pass.', '2026-10-23T01:45:18Z', '2026-10-23T01:46:38Z', 1699, 0, NULL, 'questions');
