INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1726, 17, 'QC batch-15', 'work', 'done', -100, '2026-10-24, QC batch-15: audit 0/54 major on approved, audit/review agreement 93 % (56/60); no proposals so no QC decision (report --qc needs a spot check); health ✗ already decision 418, spot check raised as decision 459; no answered review decisions to act on; exit check: approved base 6169, all difficulties at target, health/spot-check ✗ await developer; rework-19: 64 needs_work → 25 left (39 approved), claude 13 calls $2.57 + 56 calls $5.52; exit-check task added; staged authoring/data/questions.json, app/data/pool.en.json; qgen validate OK', 'QC of the batch run by the preceding `run batch-<n>` task, per `authoring/QC.md` (plan 16) and `plan 17: Batch runs` "Per-batch pattern" 2, "Reviews don''t gate (decision 414)", "English-first batches" and "5000 reached: batch-15 is the last". If the batch report doesn''t exist, stop without changes. Model it on `task 1681: QC batch-13`.

No step waits for the developer (`decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`): decisions are raised, never `pm task-pending-decision`, never `--requires` on them.

1. Act on answered review decisions of earlier batches not yet acted on (`pm decision list --answered --grep "health" --grep "Spot check" --grep "QC batch"`; e.g. `decision 416: batch-14: health ✗, look at it?`, `decision 417: Spot check batch-14 done?`, and a QC proposals decision if one exists); turn unhandled ones into change tasks and report lines; `pm decision consequences <id> "<what>"`.
2. Health ✗: decision "<batch>: health ✗, look at it?" (look up first, no duplicate). Never `qgen health ack`.
3. Spot check: decision "Spot check <batch> done?" (size `quality.spot_check_size`).
4. `qgen report --qc <batch>` with the spot checks recorded so far → decision "QC <batch>: which changes?" if proposals exist (≥ 2 disagreements or major audit findings of one kind, or a `fact` false approve).
5. Records: `qgen report` (source locale) approved/target per difficulty, needs_work by reason, media funnel and yield (plan 146); English comparisons against earlier English batches, health trend per `decision 233: Batch health trend rule across the switch to English drafts?`, overlap per `decision 232: Overlap of English drafts against the es-sourced base pool: which keys?`, agreement vs. batch-9 28/30, batch-10 29/30, batch-11 28/30.
6. Change tasks from answered decisions: English-pipeline ones in `plan 147: English-first batches: calibration, overlap and QC across languages`, the rest in plan 17 at `--priority 650`, work tree `questions`.
7. needs_work per `decision 3: How are needs_work questions (33 now, more per batch) resolved?`: `qgen rework --batch <batch>` once; note count before/after.
8. No next pair (batch-15 is the last). Add the exit-check task in plan 17, work tree `questions`, priority -100, `--requires` this task: subject "Exit check: milestone 1 (5000 approved base)", body from plan 17 "Exit check (last task)" (`qgen report --exit-check`; count and `qgen validate` decide; difficulty gaps listed as accepted or left to a later batch, never a new batch; health and spot-check lines read the developer''s answers, open ones don''t block; `trivia-media sync --status approved`; on a failing count or validate: drop with the failing lines and add the task the failure calls for). Note this run''s `qgen report --exit-check` lines.

Missing tooling to list in the note: none known; `qgen report --overlaps` timed out in QC batch-11.

Done when: steps 1–8 done or listed as missing in the note; the exit-check task exists; staged per RUNBOOK "Under `pm run`"; `qgen validate` clean.', '2026-10-23T08:05:43Z', '2026-10-24T13:14:30Z', 1681, 0, NULL, 'questions');
