INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web, model, worktree) VALUES (1757, 17, 'Exit check: milestone 1 (5000 approved base)', 'work', 'done', -100, '2026-10-24, exit check passed on count and validate: approved base 6169 (≥5000), every difficulty at target (no gaps), qgen validate OK, trivia-media sync 0 missing; ✗ health batch-14/15 (drop rate, overlap, max final−target gap 11–15, mean fun) and ✗ no spot checks of batch-14/15 are the developer''s open decisions 416, 418, 417, 459, not blocking (decision 414); no files staged', 'Last task of `plan 17: Batch runs` ("Exit check (last task)"): batch-15 was the last batch; 5000 approved `base` is reached.

No step waits for the developer (`decision 414: Human reviews don''t gate question generation or translation`).

1. `qgen report --exit-check`: ≥ 5000 approved `base` (source locale, each once) must pass. Count and `qgen validate` decide.
2. Difficulty: every difficulty at target, or a small gap listed in the note as accepted or left to a later batch (a release content run, plan 84, or milestone 9''s); never a new batch for it.
3. Health of the last two batches and the spot checks: read the developer''s answers (`pm decision list --answered --grep "health" --grep "Spot check"`) against `decision 2: When is batch quality "fine": human spot-check size and agreement rate with the LLM review?`. Open decisions (`decision 418: batch-15: health ✗, look at it?`, `decision 416`, `decision 417`, `decision 459: Spot check batch-15 done?`) don''t block; put the ✗ lines into the note, a new decision for the developer only if one is new. Never `qgen health ack`.
4. `qgen validate` clean; `trivia-media sync --status approved` (fills the cache; nothing to stage).
5. Fails only on the count or a broken `qgen validate`: `pm task drop` this task with the failing lines as the reason and add the task the failure calls for (a fix task, or a batch/QC pair if the count fell below 5000).

State at QC batch-15 (2026-10-24, `qgen report --exit-check`): ✓ approved base 6169 · ✓ every difficulty at target · ✗ health batch-14/15 (drop rate, overlap, max final−target gap 11–15, mean fun) · ✗ no spot checks of batch-14/15 · ✓ `qgen validate`.

The release gate after that (`trivia-release-check`, release bar) is the developer''s, not a task.', '2026-10-24T13:14:28Z', '2026-10-24T13:14:49Z', 1726, 0, NULL, 'questions');
