 }
--- /dev/null
+++ b/authoring/tools/prompts/neutralize.md
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Task: find wording that isn''t neutral Spanish
+
+You get questions from the `base` bundle of the trivia game described above, with their id: description, question, answer, wrong answers, hints and fun fact. `base` is played anywhere in the Spanish-speaking world, so its voice is neutral Latin American Spanish (house style "Language"). Find every question whose wording, in any of these fields, uses Colombian or other national usage where a neutral word exists:
+- regional words: "bombillo" → "bombilla", "crispetas" → "palomitas", "gripa" → "gripe", "arquero" → "portero", "tinto" → "café", "computador" → "computadora";
+- regional diminutives and slang: "pelotica" → "pelota", "parcero";
+- "vos" or "vosotros" forms → "tú"/"ustedes";
+- numbers with a dot as thousands separator: "2.640" → "2640", "42.195" → "42 195".
+
+Don''t flag:
+- names, titles and references anyone knows (Encanto, García Márquez, "Cien años de soledad"), and a regional word that is itself the answer or the clue (a question about what "tinto" means in Colombia);
+- Colombian content: a question that needs a connection to Colombia belongs in the `colombia` bundle (D-49), which is not this task;
+- words with no shared form ("carro"/"coche"/"auto", "celular"/"móvil") when no natural rewording exists; list them in `no_neutral_form` instead.
+
+For each question you flag, give `issue`: an English instruction for the reviser naming every field, word and replacement ("description: ''bombillo'' → ''bombilla''; hint 2: ''crispetas'' → ''palomitas''"), keeping everything else as it is. Leave every other question out.
```', '', 'approve as drafted, numbers RAE style (2640, 42 195, 42,195)', NULL, '2026-10-12T18:30:32Z', '2026-10-12T18:41:30Z', 430, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (33, 'Configure game screen: which fields?', 'answered', '["as proposed in plan 13 (age group, bundles, joker set, media on/off, start level)", "shorter: age group, bundles, joker set only"]', 'Gamemaster mode (MD-11) gets a configure screen before every game: plan 29''s Choice screen, opening on the last choice, so Enter straight through = today''s game. Proposal in plans/13-game-modes.md "Proposal A": age group, bundles, joker set (Sin límite / Como las cartas / Estándar / A medida), media questions on/off, start level. Trade-off: media on/off and start level are new engine settings (selection filter, start state) and shrink supply or shorten games; the shorter list needs nothing beyond plan 29 + today''s budget.', '', 'Configure screen fields (opens on the last choice):
- Difficulty: pick an age group, or «Custom»: start and end difficulty (1–15), end >= start; levels ramp evenly from start to end.
- Bundles: a reusable bundle selector (used elsewhere too): every bundle available in the current language, base bundles shown apart from the others. Exactly one base bundle per game (D38). Default: the locale''s first base bundle; non-base bundles off.
- Jokers: one row per joker, a number or ∞; default = the standard set (STANDARD_JOKERS). No presets (no Sin límite / Como las cartas / Estándar picker).
- Allow video questions on/off, allow audio questions on/off; both default on. No general media on/off.
- Number of levels: 1–20, default 12; the Tower adapts. Replaces start level.
- Cards to choose from per level (by description): 0–4, default 4; 0 skips the choice and shows a question directly.', NULL, '2026-10-12T19:12:49Z', '2026-10-12T22:05:48Z', 389, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 390: 2026-10-12, task 390: D-88; plan 13 ''Configure game screen'' spec: new optional settings difficulty {start,end}, video/audio (false only), levels (missing 12), cards (missing 4); fresh defaults (standard set, first base bundle only) apply on the configure screen only; games without the fields and new without jokers play as before (fixtures unchanged); LEVELS/PER_LEVEL become per game.

2026-10-12, task 497: 2026-10-12, task 497: engine: Choice = every configure field (age_group | difficulty, bundles, levels, cards, video, audio, jokers); rangesFor (decision 46), cards 0 opens at once, media filter, choice/new/outlook take CHOICE_KEYS; fresh player''s choice: first base bundle + STANDARD_JOKERS

2026-10-13, task 391: Task 391 (2026-10-12): Choice.svelte in gamemaster mode is the configure game screen: Difficulty (age groups, then «A medida» with Desde/Hasta 1–15), Niveles 1–20, Cartas por nivel 0–4, video/audio switches, one stepper per joker 0–99 or ∞ (wrapping), and the new shared game/BundleSelector.svelte (base radio group apart from the toggles). Preset = playerChoice (every field of the newest game), fresh player = young_teens, first base bundle only, STANDARD_JOKERS, video/audio on, 12 levels, 4 cards; new always gets every field. The old per-tile age-group and bundle rows remain only in «Solo o en grupo» (age group). Strings configure.* (es, en, de). Backspace/B goes back, Esc stays the overlay. Outlook display left to task 623.');
