2026-10-13, task 392: 2026-10-13, task 392: Overlay.svelte is the gamemaster menu: general column (continue, «Preguntas marcadas», fullscreen, credits, restart = abandon + the player''s configure screen, quit; sound, languages) and a dashed panel «Trucos del anfitrión» (gamemaster mode, shown while a game runs or can be undone): skip, block (confirm), undo, «Cambiar pregunta» (‹ no vista / vista ›), «Saltar a nivel» (‹ n ›), «Dificultad y paquetes» (new GameSettings.svelte, nested modal scope, BundleSelector; refusals stay in the dialog), choice line; jokers column edits uses left (limit = used + left; lib/api fetchJokersUsed, engine jokersUsed). Strings overlay.cheats/replace/seen/unseen/level/settings/settingsNote/apply/used; overlay.left gone; overlay.restart now «Terminar partida (configurar otra)». No more ''Volver al inicio'' after restart; «Reportar pregunta» item was already gone (decision 60).

2026-10-14, task 800: 2026-10-14, task 800: the Esc row overlay.restart is now «Volver al menú principal» / «Back to main menu» / «Zurück zum Hauptmenü»: abandon (confirm as before), then the start screen, not the player''s configure screen (milestone 9 replaces this part of D-88); overlay.quit «Salir del juego» in its own colour (--quit/--quit-line in theme.css). Specs: plans/04-ui-tv-display.md Esc menu, plans/13-game-modes.md MD-12 note.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (35, 'Translation prompts and markets per locale (plan 66)', 'answered', '["approve as drafted", "changes (say which)"]', 'Plan 66 (`plan 66: Translation pipeline (QT-2, QT-3)`) needs new prompt texts; prompts are the gamemaster''s (D-36). Task 437 drafted them; they are staged but unused until tasks 438–440 wire them in. Approve, or answer with changes.

## What is proposed
- **Markets:**
  - `en`: US + UK families; US spelling and dates; metric first, imperial in brackets where natural; "a"/"an" must fit all options.
  - `de`: Germany, Austria, Switzerland; standard German spelled as in Germany (`ß`); words of Germany where they differ; "du"/"ihr"; metric; numbers like Spanish (space from 10 000, decimal comma); articles/case endings must fit all options.
- **Run sizes:** `TRANSLATE_SIZE` = 300 sources per run; the first run of a locale (pilot, QT-5) = 50, then the stop until `qgen health ack tr-<locale>-1`.
- **Review/audit answers** for translation runs in English (`feedback`, `fix`, `notes`); a `fix` changes only the translation, never the Spanish source.
- **No new problem kinds:** translation problems map to the existing ones (fidelity → `fact`/`ambiguity`/`giveaway`, unnatural wording → `style`, Spanish text in media naming the answer → `media`).
- **`travels: no` reasons:** `wordplay`, `about_spanish`, `needs_local_knowledge`, `other`.

## House style and `prompt()` (applied by task 438 after approval, not now)
The "Language" block moves verbatim into `prompts/locale-es.md`; house style keeps `{locale}`, filled per locale. Output for Spanish runs stays byte-identical.

```diff
--- a/authoring/tools/prompts/house-style.md
+++ b/authoring/tools/prompts/house-style.md
 ## Language
-- All content is in Spanish. The voice depends on the question''s bundle:
-{voices}
-- Neutral means: … (unchanged)
-- Use Colombian references where they fit naturally … (unchanged)
-- Numbers (all bundles): … (unchanged)
+{locale}
--- /dev/null
+++ b/authoring/tools/prompts/locale-es.md
+(the five removed lines above, verbatim)
--- a/authoring/tools/qgen.py
+++ b/authoring/tools/qgen.py
-def prompt(*names):
+def prompt(*names, locale="es"):
     """Prompt files joined; {age_groups} and {players} are filled from app/data/age-groups.json,
-    {voices} from app/data/bundles.json."""
+    {locale} from prompts/locale-<locale>.md, {voices} from app/data/bundles.json."""
 …
     text = "\n\n".join((PROMPTS / f"{n}.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8") for n in names)
+    text = text.replace("{locale}", (PROMPTS / f"locale-{locale}.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8").rstrip())
     return (text.replace("{age_groups}", …)
```
Use in locale runs: `prompt("house-style", "translate", locale=L)`; `prompt("house-style", "rate", locale=L)`; `prompt("house-style", "review", "translate-review", locale=L)`; `prompt("house-style", "audit", "translate-review", locale=L)`.

## Drafts (staged)
```diff
diff --git a/authoring/tools/prompts/locale-de.md b/authoring/tools/prompts/locale-de.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..37432c2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/authoring/tools/prompts/locale-de.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+- All content is in German, for families in Germany, Austria and Switzerland: standard German, spelled as in Germany (with "ß").
+- Words all three understand; where they differ ("Tomate"/"Paradeiser", "Fahrrad"/"Velo", "Januar"/"Jänner"), reword around it if that stays natural, else the word used in Germany.
+- Address the players with "du" (one player) or "ihr" (the team), never "Sie".
+- Units: metric only. Numbers: no thousands separator up to 9999 ("2640 Meter"), a space from 10 000 ("42 195 Menschen"), a decimal comma ("42,195 km"); large round numbers in words ("3 Millionen"). Dates: "20. Juli 1969".
+- Names and titles as these families know them: "Christoph Kolumbus", "Jeanne d''Arc", the German title of a film or book ("Alles steht Kopf", "Hundert Jahre Einsamkeit"). A name without a German form stays as it is.
+- Articles and case endings (der/die/das, ein/eine) must fit all four options: phrase the question so none of them stands out ("Welches Tier…?", options without articles).
+- House style "Keep it short" holds; German may run a little longer than Spanish, but stays under 160 characters.
+- The players are not in Colombia: a Latin American reference that every Colombian knows is harder for them. Difficulty and distractors are judged for these players, on the same scale 1–15 (the calibration examples are about Spanish speakers, the scale isn''t).
+- Where this house style says Spanish (the description, the fun fact), read German. Its examples stay in Spanish: they show the style, not the language.
diff --git a/authoring/tools/prompts/locale-en.md b/authoring/tools/prompts/locale-en.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e0df521
--- /dev/null
+++ b/authoring/tools/prompts/locale-en.md
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+- All content is in English, for families in the United States and the United Kingdom.
+- US spelling ("color", "center"). Words both sides understand; where they differ ("soccer"/"football", "fries"/"chips", "cookie"/"biscuit"), reword around it if that stays natural, else the US word.
+- Units: metric first; add imperial in brackets in the question text and fun fact where these families think in it ("8849 m (29,032 ft)", "30 °C (86 °F)"). The four options use one unit, all in the same form.
+- Numbers: comma as thousands separator from 1,000 ("42,195 people"), decimal point ("42.195 km"), years without separator; large round numbers in words ("3 million"). Dates: "July 20, 1969".
+- Names and titles as these families know them: "Christopher Columbus", "Joan of Arc", the English title of a film or book ("Inside Out", "One Hundred Years of Solitude"). A name without an English form stays as it is.
+- Watch "a"/"an": an article in the question must fit all four options.
+- The players are not in Colombia: a Latin American reference that every Colombian knows is harder for them. Difficulty and distractors are judged for these players, on the same scale 1–15 (the calibration examples are about Spanish speakers, the scale isn''t).
+- Where this house style says Spanish (the description, the fun fact), read English. Its examples stay in Spanish: they show the style, not the language.
diff --git a/authoring/tools/prompts/translate-review.md b/authoring/tools/prompts/translate-review.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4be8533
--- /dev/null
+++ b/authoring/tools/prompts/translate-review.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Translation runs
+
+The question above is a translation of an approved Spanish question. You see the Spanish one as `source`, and the translator''s `notes`. The source was reviewed already: judge the translation, as the players will meet it. Everything above applies to the translation, with these changes.
+
+## Changes
+- **Voice:** "Language" means the section above for this locale, not Spanish. Report wording that isn''t natural for its players (a literal idiom, translationese, the wrong spelling or unit convention) as `style`.
+- **Media:** the media is the source''s picked file; there are no candidates and no new search. Leave `pick`, `background_pick` and `new_query` null. Judge the file only for its text (below).
+- **Language of your answer:** `feedback`, `fix` and `notes` in English.
+- **The source stays as it is.** A `fix` changes only the translation. If the source itself is wrong, report `fact` and say "source:" in your feedback or notes; leave `fix` empty.
+
+## Check on top
+- **Fidelity:** the translation asks the same fact with the same answer as the source. A changed fact, number or answer is `fact`; a lost detail that made the clue unique, or an added one that gives it away, is `ambiguity` or `giveaway`.
+- **Options:** a wrong answer that became correct or a synonym of the answer is `ambiguity`; one that stands out by grammar (an article, a gender, a case ending) or is absurd enough to rule itself out is `giveaway`.
+- **Hints:** a hint that still plays on the Spanish word, or names the answer in the target language before hint 3, is `giveaway`.
+- **Description:** a literal joke that makes no sense is `style`; one that gives the answer away is `giveaway`.
+- **Media text:** give `media_text`: true when the file likely shows Spanish text the players would read, else false. Not a problem on its own (it is only flagged), except when the text names the answer, or essential media can''t be played without reading it: then `media`.
+
+## Not travelling
+An item without a translation comes with the translator''s `reason` (`wordplay`, `about_spanish`, `needs_local_knowledge`, `other`). Decide in one line:
+- `approved`: right, it doesn''t travel; it stays in Spanish only.
+- `needs_work`: it can be translated; `feedback` says how in one line. It is translated in the next run.
diff --git a/authoring/tools/prompts/translate.md b/authoring/tools/prompts/translate.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..381cb7f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/authoring/tools/prompts/translate.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Task: translate questions
+
+You translate approved Spanish questions of the trivia game described above into the language of the "Language" section, for its players. The Spanish questions were written, rated, fact-checked and reviewed already. Your translation is rated, fact-checked and reviewed again. Adapt, don''t translate literally: the players must meet the same question as a Spanish family does, in natural words of their own language.
+
+## Input
+A list of questions from one subcategory, each with its `id`, `subcategory`, `difficulty`, the text fields (`description`, `question`, `answer`, `wrong_answers`, `hints`, `fun_fact`) and its `media` (type, role, and the title and description of the file the players see).
+
+## Keep
+- **The same question:** the same fact, the same correct answer, the same clue. Don''t add facts, don''t drop a detail that makes the question unambiguous, don''t make it easier or harder on purpose.
+- **The same answer**, in the form the players know it: "Cristóbal Colón" → "Christopher Columbus"; a film or book by its release title in the market ("Intensa-Mente" → "Inside Out"). A name without a form of its own stays as it is ("Gabriel García Márquez", "arepa").
+- **Don''t fix the source.** If a Spanish fact looks wrong to you, translate it anyway and say so in `notes` ("source fact doubtful: …").
+
+## Adapt
+- **Units, numbers, dates, spelling:** as the "Language" section says.
+- **Idioms:** an idiom becomes the target language''s idiom, or plain words; never a literal copy.
+- **Wrong answers:** each one stays plausible, the same form and similar length as the answer, and clearly wrong. After translating, check the four options again in the target language:
+  - none became correct or a synonym of the answer (two Spanish words can share one translation);
+  - none stands out by grammar: an article ("a"/"an", "der"/"die"/"das"), a gender or case ending that fits only one option;
+  - none became absurd.
+  Replace a wrong answer that fails with another of the same kind, and say so in `notes`.
+- **Hints:** keep the order from vague to strong. A hint that plays on the Spanish word (first letter, rhyme, syllables, gender, a Spanish saying) is rewritten to do the same job in the target language. Hint 3 must not contain the answer in the target language.
+- **Description:** rewrite the joke so it is funny in the target language: the same idea where it works, a new joke about the same content where it doesn''t. It must not give the answer away or rule out options; watch articles and genders here too.
+- **Fun fact:** translated, units adapted.
+- **Length:** house style "Keep it short" holds in the target language; don''t pad.
+- **Media mentioned in the text** ("Escucha:…", "En la foto…") is translated naturally. The file stays as it is.
+
+## Doesn''t travel
+Some questions can''t be asked fairly in the target language. Then answer `travels: "no"`, give the reason and leave the text fields empty:
+- `wordplay`: the question or its clue lives on a Spanish pun or sound that can''t be rebuilt;
+- `about_spanish`: it asks about the Spanish language itself (a spelling, a Spanish plural, what a Spanish word means);
+- `needs_local_knowledge`: the answer only makes sense to someone who lives in the Spanish-speaking world;
+- `other`: say what in `notes`.
+Don''t give up early: a language question with a clean equivalent travels (the word for opposites → "antonym"), and a question that is only harder for these players travels too (the rater re-rates it). Don''t force one that doesn''t: a strained translation costs more than a missing question.
+
+## Media text
+`media_text`: true when the title or description suggests the file shows Spanish text the players would read (a sign, a poster, a book cover, a caption), or essential audio has spoken Spanish; else false. Answer it for every question; it doesn''t change your translation.
+
+## Answer
+For every input `id`, one item:
+- `id`; `travels`: `"yes"` or `"no"`; `reason`: empty for yes, else one of the reasons above.
+- `description`, `question`, `answer`, `wrong_answers` (3), `hints` (3), `fun_fact`: in the target language; empty when `travels` is no.
+- `media_text`: as above.
+- `notes`: in English, one short line per adaptation that a reviewer should know about (a unit changed, a wrong answer replaced, a hint rewritten, a doubtful source fact); empty if you only translated.
```', '', 'Approve as drafted, except: text in media (Spanish or any language) is never a problem. Drop media_text from translate.md and translate-review.md (no flag, no ''media'' problem for text in media; the ''Media text'' sections go).', NULL, '2026-10-12T19:18:26Z', '2026-10-12T22:11:11Z', 437, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 438: 2026-10-12, task 438: media_text dropped from translate.md, translate-review.md and TRANSLATE_SCHEMA (no media_text in the locale file or the tr-* report); house-style.md Language block → prompts/locale-es.md, prompt(..., locale=) fills {locale}; qgen translate (TRANSLATE_SCHEMA, chunks of 15 per subcategory), rate/factcheck/merge read run.json locale; a re-translated stale entry keeps its old review as top-level previous.

2026-10-12, task 441: 2026-10-12, task 441: docs follow the answer: D-87 (plans/decisions.md) says text in media is never a problem (no media_text flag, no media problem); 15b''s ''Media'' bullet no longer says the review flags visible text per locale; QC.md''s translation-run checks say the same. RUNBOOK, QC.md, directory.md, AGENTS.md, 15b (QT-2, QT-3 [x]) describe qgen batch --translate.

2026-10-13, task 443: 2026-10-12, task 443: no media-text route and no media_text in GET /api/questions?locale=; task 444''s media_text toggle removed from its body');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (36, 'GameRow.locale: written only for non-es games?', 'answered', '[]', 'Keeps the family''s saves and the Python fixture replay byte-identical (plan 68: the family''s game stays as today). The lib layer runs ''new'' on the language''s pool (scope next), every other route on the newest game''s locale; newGame throws if the pool''s locale differs from language.questions.', '', 'Yes: newGame writes locale only when it isn''t es; missing = es', NULL, '2026-10-12T19:41:19Z', '2026-10-12T19:41:19Z', 449, NULL, 'rule', 449, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (37, 'Per-locale content targets and gap aiming', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 70 (CT-4). D-75 fixes one mix for every language; the simulation is information only (pm decision 21); per-level mix already covers age-group windows (D-76). Translations can only fill a locale from es sources, so the source shortfall is the one new input to D-54''s weights.', '', 'Every launch language uses targets.json base''s numbers (D-75), deficits counted per locale; no per-mode, per-age-group or per-preset targets; simulation bottlenecks are information; once es meets its target, the en/de source shortfall drives es drafting', NULL, '2026-10-12T19:46:07Z', '2026-10-12T19:46:07Z', 248, NULL, 'rule', 248, '2026-10-12, task 462: 2026-10-12, task 462: targets.deficits(..., locale), source_supply/source_shortfall/draft_gaps in targets.py; target_weights and batches.subcategories use draft_gaps; qgen report --locale, --simulate target check, --cost (es sources past target) per locale; D-84 in plans/decisions.md; --translate weight is task 464.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (38, 'Base bundles and bundle languages', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 71, D-85 in plans/decisions.md. Supersedes D-68''s ''every always_on bundle is always on'' and its auto-adding of base: [] and [colombia] are refused (base_bundle_count). A bundle not listed for the game''s locale is refused (bundle_not_offered). qgen validate: errors for missing/invalid languages, leftover always_on, unknown kind, a launch language without a base bundle; warnings for listed bundles without approved questions in pool.<locale>.json and approved questions of unlisted bundles.', '', 'kind: base replaces always_on; exactly one base bundle per session; bundles offered per languages; default = the locale''s first base bundle plus every non-base bundle offered in the locale; stored choices that no longer resolve read as the locale''s defaults (never written back)', NULL, '2026-10-12T20:39:19Z', '2026-10-12T20:39:19Z', 481, NULL, 'rule', 481, '2026-10-16, task 1379: ''exactly one base bundle'' (D-85) dropped, base_bundle_count gone: any combination, a base bundle may be off, refusal no_questions when nothing playable is chosen. Still holds: kind base, bundles per languages (bundle_not_offered), the locale''s first base bundle as preset, a mod''s base bundle off by default.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (39, 'Local builds start offline?', 'answered', '["both pass", "issues (fill the tables)"]', 'Start test of the local desktop builds (SW-5, plan 56), build commit 06c39dc (version 0.1.0).
Artefacts: `trivia-desktop-build` → app/desktop/release/Trivia-0.1.0-win-x64.zip and Trivia-0.1.0-linux-x64.tar.gz (or copy those over).
Checklist and tables to fill: plans/18-steam-integration.md, section "Local build start test".

Windows x64 without Node/Python, and Linux x64 without Nix (e.g. Ubuntu 24.04):
- Network off before unpacking
- Unpack and start: Trivia.exe (SmartScreen «More info → Run anyway» expected) / ./trivia
- No console window (Windows)
- Starts fullscreen; F11 toggles
- Keyboard-only game to level 3 with an image, an audio and a video question; sound plays
- «Salir del juego», restart: player still there
- Save at %APPDATA%\trivia\save\game.json / ~/.config/trivia/save/game.json
- CREDITS.md in the folder (n/a until plan 47)

On issues: name the failing rows and machine (or fill the tables in the plan file).', '', 'Skipped: Steam only (decision 111). No start test of the plain zip/tar.gz outside Steam; the clean-machine start test happens in the Steam beta test (task 263: write plan: Beta test and S5 close-out). Record the start test as skipped, not failed.', NULL, '2026-10-12T21:18:46Z', '2026-10-13T15:11:31Z', 331, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (40, 'English name for the hint joker «Soplo»?', 'answered', '["Psst", "Little Bird", "Nudge", "Tip-off", "Whisper"]', 'Spanish «Soplo»: the classroom whisper (soplar = whisper the answer to a classmate). Joker: reveals the next of the question''s three hints, vague → strong; hint notes are labelled «Soplo 1/2/3». Light-bulb icon. Candidates keep the sneaky-whisper idea. Not a literal translation (15a: joker names are content). ≤ 13 characters (tray width, «Francotirador»). The name also shows in «Use {name}?», the aria label, «no … left» errors and the printable cards. Key letter stays as in es (S, P, F, T, X) until LUI-4. Answer with one option or your own name.
- Psst: the classroom whisper itself, cheeky, 4 chars; notes read «Psst 1/2/3»
- Little Bird: «a little bird told me», warm, family tone
- Nudge: a gentle push toward the answer
- Tip-off: a sly insider tip, a bit spy-like
- Whisper: plain and clear, least playful', '', 'Hint', NULL, '2026-10-12T21:55:04Z', '2026-10-12T22:29:13Z', 102, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 104: en.ts: joker.hint.name «Hint», hint notes «Hint {n}», «no Hints left»; D-89');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (41, 'English name for the skip joker «Paso»?', 'answered', '["Hard Pass", "Nope", "Next!", "Dodge", "Bye-Bye"]', 'Spanish «Paso»: «I pass». Joker: skips the current question (a new one from the pool), optionally purging its whole subcategory from later draws («Paso, y fuera el tema …»). Door/arrow icon. Not a literal translation (15a: joker names are content). ≤ 13 characters (tray width, «Francotirador»). The name also shows in «Use {name}?», the aria label, «no … left» errors and the printable cards. Key letter stays as in es (S, P, F, T, X) until LUI-4. Answer with one option or your own name.
- Hard Pass: the cheeky idiom for a firm no; keeps P as a matching key
- Nope: shortest, most cheeky; «Nope, and out goes the topic …» reads well
- Next!: the barber''s call, brisk
- Dodge: ducking the question, playground feel
- Bye-Bye: waving the question off, kid-friendly', '', 'Pass & Purge', NULL, '2026-10-12T21:55:04Z', '2026-10-12T22:29:13Z', 102, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 104: en.ts: joker.skip.name «Pass & Purge», purge line «Pass & Purge: goodbye to “{name}”», «no Pass & Purge left»; new key joker.skip.pass (es «Paso», en «Just pass») for the dialog''s plain option, used in Question.svelte, since the name says purge; D-89');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (42, 'English name for the easier joker «Bájale»?', 'answered', '["Dial Down", "Ease Up", "Go Easy", "Simmer Down", "Baby Steps"]', 'Spanish «Bájale»: «turn it down / take it down a notch», colloquial imperative. Joker: swaps the current question for an easier one from the same subcategory; its animation is a difficulty dial («Dificultad») turning down. Down-stairs icon. Not a literal translation (15a: joker names are content). ≤ 13 characters (tray width, «Francotirador»). The name also shows in «Use {name}?», the aria label, «no … left» errors and the printable cards. Key letter stays as in es (S, P, F, T, X) until LUI-4. Answer with one option or your own name.
- Dial Down: matches the dial animation, casual imperative like bájale
- Ease Up: casual plea, same register
- Go Easy: «go easy on us», warm family tone
- Simmer Down: cheeky, playful scolding
- Baby Steps: playful, but may sound condescending to adults', '', 'Fairy', NULL, '2026-10-12T21:55:04Z', '2026-10-12T22:29:13Z', 102, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 104: en.ts: joker.easier.name «Fairy», «no Fairies left»; dial label stays «Difficulty»; D-89');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (43, 'English name for the category joker «Cambiazo»?', 'answered', '["Switcheroo", "Topic Hop", "Plot Twist", "Swap Shop"]', 'Spanish «Cambiazo»: a sneaky swap (dar el cambiazo = swap something behind someone''s back). Joker: swaps the current question for one of similar difficulty from a subcategory the players choose (dialog «Cambiazo: ¿qué tema quieren?»). Compass/wheel icon. Not a literal translation (15a: joker names are content). ≤ 13 characters (tray width, «Francotirador»). The name also shows in «Use {name}?», the aria label, «no … left» errors and the printable cards. Key letter stays as in es (S, P, F, T, X) until LUI-4. Answer with one option or your own name.
- Switcheroo: exactly the sneaky-swap tone of cambiazo, fun to say
- Topic Hop: says what it does, light
- Plot Twist: dramatic, playful
- Swap Shop: rhyming, cheerful', '', 'Ms Picky', NULL, '2026-10-12T21:55:04Z', '2026-10-12T22:29:14Z', 102, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 104: en.ts: joker.category.name «Ms Picky», picker title «Ms Picky: which topic do you want?», «no Ms Picky left»; D-89');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (44, 'English name for the snipe joker «Francotirador»?', 'answered', '["Trick Shot", "Sharpshooter", "Long Shot", "Pot Shot"]', 'Spanish «Francotirador»: sniper. Joker: the players aim at the answer they think is false; a wrong answer hit is struck out and play goes on; hitting the right answer loses the question and the level repeats with fresh cards. Crosshair icon. Not a literal translation (15a: joker names are content). ≤ 13 characters (tray width, «Francotirador»). The name also shows in «Use {name}?», the aria label, «no … left» errors and the printable cards. Key letter stays as in es (S, P, F, T, X) until LUI-4. Answer with one option or your own name.
- Trick Shot: playful, the trick is shooting a wrong answer
- Sharpshooter: clear for kids, 12 chars, closest to the Spanish
- Long Shot: pun on a risky bet, fits the repeat-the-level risk
- Pot Shot: a casual, opportunistic shot, cheeky', '', 'Trick Shot', NULL, '2026-10-12T21:55:04Z', '2026-10-12T22:29:14Z', 102, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-12, task 104: en.ts: joker.snipe.name stays «Trick Shot» (already the draft name); D-89');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (45, 'Health thresholds and selection order for qgen batch --translate runs', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 66 left the subset to the worker. Drafting metrics (drops, slots, axes, media share, fun) don''t exist for translations; $ per approved''s bound (0.35) is sized for drafting. One-at-a-time balancing gives ~2-3 sources per subcategory at TRANSLATE_SIZE 300; the offset keeps a 50-source pilot spread over levels 1-15 instead of all easiest.', '', 'tr-* runs: needs_work rate and needs_work per problem as for batches; rejected rate (confirmed not travelling / sources) under drop rate''s bound; audit/review agreement >= quality.min_agreement once >= spot_check_size are audited; $ per approved shown, not a threshold. The pilot tr-<locale>-1 always stops the next run until qgen health ack. Selection: stale first, then one source at a time from the subcategory with the fewest approved translations (picks count), van der Corput order over difficulty with a per-subcategory offset.', NULL, '2026-10-12T22:29:46Z', '2026-10-12T22:29:46Z', 440, NULL, 'rule', 440, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (46, 'Gamemaster mode: level ranges for custom difficulty and for a number of levels other than 12', 'answered', '[]', 'Decision 33 says levels ramp evenly but not how; plan 13 ''Configure game screen'' (task 390). Keeps age-groups.json at 12 levels (D-38), no new data.', '', 'Custom: level i of n targets start + (end-start)(i-1)/(n-1), range [floor, ceil]. Age group with n levels: level i uses the group''s step round(1 + 11(i-1)/(n-1)); n=1 step 1, n>12 repeats steps.', NULL, '2026-10-12T22:36:39Z', '2026-10-12T22:36:39Z', 390, NULL, 'rule', 390, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (47, 'Replace the files on the licence list', 'answered', '["done"]', 'Open /review?licence=replace in trivia-authoring and pick a new file per listed slot until the queue is empty, then answer done.', '', 'No replacement queue: questions whose files must be replaced go to needs_work like any other flawed question (q-0021, q-1100, q-1194 done 2026-10-14). The gate is: no approved question with a replace file (qgen validate), not an empty licence list.', NULL, '2026-10-12T23:33:15Z', '2026-10-14T01:44:10Z', 312, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 312: 2026-10-14, task 312: no replacement pass and no cache prune; the gate is qgen validate (authoring/tools/qgen.py validate_pool): an approved pick whose providers.licence_verdict is replace (missing data, off allowlist, PD-US only, PD without reason) is an error with its reasons; qgen.licence_problem removed. The licence list need not be empty: q-0021, q-1100, q-1194 stay on it as needs_work until reworked. plans/17-publishing.md PUB-3 [x]; /review?licence=replace remains the list''s view.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (48, 'Where age-group names per locale live', 'answered', '[]', 'The groups follow the game''s question locale like the bundle names already do (data.names, read in fetchChoiceOptions / fetchGameChoice), not the UI language; one place for every play-data display name (D-81), checked by qgen validate like bundles. es reads age-groups.json''s name.', '', 'names.<locale>.json → age_groups (base''s names file only), keyed by group id; fallback age-groups.json name', NULL, '2026-10-13T00:05:57Z', '2026-10-13T00:05:57Z', 619, NULL, 'rule', 619, '2026-10-13, task 619: 2026-10-12, task 619: Names.age_groups (state.ts, data.ts mergeNames, categories.load_names); fetchChoiceOptions / fetchGameChoice read it, fallback age-groups.json name; names.en/de.json age_groups; qgen validate: unknown keys error, age_groups only in base''s file, missing counted in the names warning; D-81 and directory.md note it');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (49, 'credits.json carries no UI text', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 47 put Spanish literals into the generated data, but the UI has locale catalogs (D-70); data stays locale-neutral so the screen (task 233) translates. Task 232.', '', 'Unknown author is null, controller glyphs a boolean; the Credits screen shows its own t() strings («Autor desconocido», «originales, dibujados para el juego»); CREDITS.md uses English', NULL, '2026-10-13T00:10:14Z', '2026-10-13T00:10:14Z', 232, NULL, 'rule', 232, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (50, 'Play-test of age groups and bundles', 'answered', '["all sessions played fine", "problems (listed in the answer)"]', 'Plan 30 (milestone 5): please play-test age groups and bundles in the browser, then answer.

## Agent pre-check (task 478, 2026-10-12)
Throw-away node script on the engine API (`api.gameAction`, `loadEngineData`), fresh player per run; each session: 12 levels answered right, every joker used once (Soplo, Bájale, Cambiazo, Francotirador miss, Paso); checked every card and question on screen: in the group''s level range (Bájale''s swap may go below, by design, plan 09) and in an active bundle; Cambiazo offers only active bundles'' categories.

| Run | Result |
|---|---|
| es kids, base+colombia | won 12/12, 5 jokers, ranges/bundles ok, Cambiazo 34 categories |
| es young_teens, base+colombia | won 12/12, ok, 34 categories |
| es young_adults, base+colombia | won 12/12, ok, 34 categories |
| es adults, base+colombia | won 12/12, ok, 34 categories |
| es young_teens, base only | won 12/12, ok, Cambiazo 28 categories (no colombia) |
| es no choice sent | won 12/12, ok |
| es bundles [] | 409 base_bundle_count, save unchanged |
| es bundles [colombia] | 409 base_bundle_count, save unchanged |
| es temp data, 2nd kind: base bundle, [base, base2] | 409 base_bundle_count, save unchanged |
| en / de bundlesFor | base |
| en / de defaultChoice, fresh player''s choice | base / base |
| en / de [base, colombia] | 409 bundle_not_offered, save unchanged |
| en / de young_teens, defaults (throw-away pools) | won 12/12, ok, 28 categories |
| npm test / check / build | pass (156 tests) / 0 errors / built |
| qgen validate | OK, 1211 questions, 27 warnings (axes, media cache) |

No failures, so no fix tasks.

## Checklist (`trivia`, :8000)
- One session per age group (Niños, Adolescentes, Jóvenes, Adultos); the choice screen by mouse and at least once by keyboard only (IN-1).
- One session with `colombia` off.
- Defaults straight through with Enter: looks as before.
- Básico shown as the selected base bundle (one of N, not a locked toggle); no «Siempre activo»; «¡A jugar!» can''t start without a base bundle (if the screen can''t reach that state: engine-only, covered above).
- Question language `en` and `de` (Esc menu, language): the screen lists only `base`.
  - No en/de pools ship yet; throw-away ones (base questions, Spanish text re-labelled):
    `python3 -c "import json;d=json.load(open(''app/data/pool.json''));d[''questions'']=[q for q in d[''questions''] if q.get(''bundle'',''base'')==''base''];[json.dump(d,open(f''app/data/pool.{l}.json'',''w'')) for l in (''en'',''de'')]"`
  - Remove afterwards (not gitignored, don''t commit them): `rm app/data/pool.en.json app/data/pool.de.json`, then set the language back to es.
- Overlay shows group and bundles; undo and abandon keep the choice.

Answer "problems": list each one; the close-out (task 479) turns them into fix tasks in plan 71, 29 or 27.', '', 'problems:
1. «¿Quién juega?»: with players saved and nothing focused, Enter does nothing; Enter picks the most recent player (shown[0]).
2. Overlay line («Niños · Básico, Colombia») unlabeled and unclear: label each part, e.g. «Edad: Niños», «Paquetes de preguntas: Básico, Regional: Colombia» (en "Age group", "Question bundles"; de likewise). Term = "question bundle" (Steam DLC), never «Temas»; base bundle and the others are all question bundles.
3. Bundle `colombia` named «Regional: Colombia» everywhere (bundles.json, names.{en,de}.json, Choice screen, selector, overlay, credits, Steam DLC).
4. Mode row: «Solo o en grupo» first, before «Modo anfitrión».
5. «Solo o en grupo» has no bundle selection (only gamemaster mode has it): solo needs the bundle selector too; overrides decision 38''s "solo plays the locale''s defaults". Bundle selection, like age group selection, is not session customization: its own step in every mode, apart from «Personalizar partida» / gamemaster settings.
6. Difficulty: «Desde»/«Hasta» always visible, showing the selected age group''s window (age-groups.json, e.g. Niños 1–6), read-only and skipped by arrows; editable only with «A medida».
7. One language setting for UI and questions (replaces D-86''s two rows): chosen at first start (default from Steam, as now); afterwards only via a language flag top right on the very first screen; no language rows in the Esc menu; never changeable once bundles are chosen / in a session (bundles depend on the language). A language without its own pool plays the Spanish questions until its translation ships (all UI languages stay selectable for testing).
Play-tested: age groups, colombia off, keyboard, UI languages es/en/de (fine). Not tested: en/de question language (unreachable in the UI; replaced by 7).', NULL, '2026-10-13T00:47:47Z', '2026-10-14T02:54:37Z', 478, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 479: 2026-10-14, task 479: problems 1–6 → plan 125: Play-test fixes: player Enter, Choice screen, overlay line, Regional: Colombia (400); problem 7 → plan 126: One language setting for UI and questions (500; replaces D-86''s two language rows). Plans 27, 29, 71 are done, so new plans in milestone 5. Play-test raised again as decision 155; task 479 (close-out of AG-7, BN-6) pending on it; no docs closed yet.

2026-10-14, task 1021: 2026-10-14, item 7 (one language for UI and questions): task 1019 one language tag in the save and engine, question locale = the language''s pool if it passes, else es (decision 156); task 1020 Language picker at first start, Start''s language button (globe + endonym, decision 157), no Esc menu language rows; task 1021 docs: D-96 in plans/decisions.md (supersedes D-86 in part), plans 04, 12, 13, 15, 15a, 18, project.md, directory.md.

2026-10-16, task 479: Plans 125 (problems 1–6), 126 (problem 7) done; D-96 (one language for UI and questions: one SaveData.language, language button on Start only, no Esc-menu language rows), D-97 (bundle selection in every mode, own step apart from «Personalizar partida»; replaces pm decision 51''s solo defaults); colombia named «Regional: Colombia»; overlay line labelled «Edad» / «Paquetes de preguntas»; «Desde»/«Hasta» read-only outside «A medida». Docs closed by task 479: plans/22-bundles.md ''In the game (BN-6)''.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (51, '«Solo o en grupo»: which bundles does a game play?', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 13 gives solo the age group only (no configure screen); bundles weren''t specified. Task 378 hides the bundle rows in solo and sends the defaults explicitly, so supply check and game agree; pm decision 33''s fresh default (base only) stays a configure-screen rule.', '', 'The question language''s default bundles (decision 38): first base bundle plus every other bundle offered; no bundle choice on the Choice screen in solo', NULL, '2026-10-13T01:02:55Z', '2026-10-13T01:02:55Z', 378, NULL, 'rule', 378, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (52, 'Safe area on the Question screen: may the credit line and «Respuesta final» sit in the bottom margin?', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 46''s screen check (task 231) flags them at every size, 1080p included, since the layout is all --u and 16:9 = 16:10 by width. The layout passed the TV overscan check (UI-6, VD-9); the Deck has no overscan. Moving them would change the approved TV look and push the long credit line into the button.', '', 'Yes: both stay where the TV-tested layout puts them (credit at 0.3 safe-y, the candy button''s last ~0.2 u in the 4 % margin); every other text stays inside the safe area', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:06:10Z', '2026-10-13T02:06:10Z', 231, NULL, 'rule', 231, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (53, 'Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?', 'answered', '["Keys in the catalog per language (joker.<id>.key, flag.key, screen.question.replayKey, screen.start.newKey, mode/customize keys), mnemonic for the name, collision rule checked per catalog; es unchanged", "Neutral 1–5 row for the jokers in every language (conflicts with pick n)", "F1–F5 for the jokers in every language"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-4, `plans/15a-ui-translation.md`). The shortcut letters are already catalog leaves; `en.ts` still uses the `es` letters for jokers. This decides whether every language picks its own letters.

Current keys (`app/client/src/locales/es.ts`):
- Question screen: answers `A`–`D`; jokers `joker.<id>.key`: Soplo `S`, Paso `P`, Bájale `F`, Cambiazo `T`, Francotirador `X`; replay `screen.question.replayKey` `R`
- every screen: flag `flag.key` `M`, Esc menu, Enter/Space confirm, Backspace back, `1`–`9` = `pick n` (Select cards)
- Start: new game `screen.start.newKey` `N`
- Choice: `mode.gamemasterKey` `A`, `mode.soloKey` `G`, `customize.openKey` `P` (`en`: `G`, `A`, `C`); bundle letters fill in around them

Collision rule per catalog (checked by `check:literals`, task 454): every key a single letter; unique among the keys live on the same screen; not `A`–`D` where answers are shown; no digit (`pick n`).

Why option 1:
- `toIntent` matches `e.key`, not the key position, so letters work on QWERTZ/AZERTY; position-based neutral rows (`Q W E R T` on QWERTY) move around on those layouts
- mnemonic letters keep the on-screen key next to the joker name readable (`S` for Soplo)
- pads use focus and face buttons anyway (decision 9: Gamepad on the Question screen), so keys only matter for keyboard players

Against 2: digits are `pick n` already. Against 3: `F1`–`F5` are awkward on laptops (Fn layer) and the Steam Deck, and clash with browser/OS keys (F1 help, F5 reload, F11 fullscreen).', '', 'Keys in the catalog per language (joker.<id>.key, flag.key, screen.question.replayKey, screen.start.newKey, mode/customize keys), mnemonic for the name, collision rule checked per catalog; es unchanged', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:07:43Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:56Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: D-91: shortcut keys per catalog; en jokers H P F K T, de Z N G W F, es/es-ES unchanged S P F T X; check:literals key rule per catalog passes; D-89''s ''keys stay S P F T X'' no longer holds');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (54, 'German name for the hint joker «Soplo»?', 'answered', '["Spickzettel (S)", "Psst! (P)", "Zaunpfahl (Z)", "Eselsbrücke (E)"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5): playful German names, not literal translations (15a "Joker names are content"); at most 13 characters («Francotirador»). The key letter follows the LUI-4 answer (decision 53); a mnemonic letter is noted per candidate. `de.ts` (task 454) uses the recommended name until this is answered.

- Spanish «Soplo», English «Hint» (decision 40: English name for the hint joker «Soplo»)
- What it does: shows a hint for the current question («Soplo {n}» notes); can be played again for the next hint
- Why: «Spickzettel» (crib note) is the school-cheating image behind «Soplo», family-friendly, keeps `S`; «Psst!» is the whisper itself; «Zaunpfahl» from «Wink mit dem Zaunpfahl» (a heavy-handed hint); «Eselsbrücke» (memory aid) is warm but less about being told', '', 'Zaunpfahl (Z)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:02Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:56Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: de.ts: hint joker «Zaunpfahl» (Z), hint note «Zaunpfahl {n}», spent error (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (55, 'German name for the skip joker «Paso»?', 'answered', '["Weg damit! (W)", "Ich passe (I)", "Tschüss! (U)", "Nächste! (N, collides with screen.start.newKey only on Start)"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5): playful German names, not literal translations (15a "Joker names are content"); at most 13 characters («Francotirador»). The key letter follows the LUI-4 answer (decision 53); a mnemonic letter is noted per candidate. `de.ts` (task 454) uses the recommended name until this is answered.

- Spanish «Paso», English «Pass & Purge» (decision 41: English name for the skip joker «Paso»)
- What it does: skips the question; optionally purges its topic for the rest of the game (stamp «ELIMINADO»). The dialog''s plain option is `joker.skip.pass` («Paso» / «Just pass»), German draft «Nur passen»
- Why: «Weg damit!» covers both skip and purge with attitude; «Ich passe» is the card-game phrase, closest to «Paso»; «Tschüss!» and «Nächste!» are cheeky but say only one half', '', 'Näxt (N)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:02Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:56Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: de.ts: skip joker «Näxt» (N), purge line «Näxt, und tschüss, Thema „{name}“», spent error; plain option stays «Nur passen» (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (56, 'German name for the easier joker «Bájale»?', 'answered', '["Gang runter (G)", "Halblang (H)", "Kinderspiel (K)", "Sachte! (S, collides with Spickzettel)"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5): playful German names, not literal translations (15a "Joker names are content"); at most 13 characters («Francotirador»). The key letter follows the LUI-4 answer (decision 53); a mnemonic letter is noted per candidate. `de.ts` (task 454) uses the recommended name until this is answered.

- Spanish «Bájale», English «Fairy» (decision 42: English name for the easier joker «Bájale»)
- What it does: swaps the question for an easier one of the same topic (the difficulty dial turns down)
- Why: «Gang runter» (shift down a gear, «einen Gang runterschalten» = take it easy) matches the dial animation; «Halblang» from «Mach mal halblang!» is the colloquial «bájale»; «Kinderspiel» (child''s play) says what you get; «Sachte!» is short and soft', '', 'Gang runter (G)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:02Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:56Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: de.ts: easier joker «Gang runter», key F → G (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (57, 'German name for the category joker «Cambiazo»?', 'answered', '["Extrawurst (E)", "Wunschthema (W)", "Kehrtwende (K)", "Themenhopser (T)"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5): playful German names, not literal translations (15a "Joker names are content"); at most 13 characters («Francotirador»). The key letter follows the LUI-4 answer (decision 53); a mnemonic letter is noted per candidate. `de.ts` (task 454) uses the recommended name until this is answered.

- Spanish «Cambiazo», English «Ms Picky» (decision 43: English name for the category joker «Cambiazo»)
- What it does: the players pick another topic; the question is replaced by one of that topic (picker title «Cambiazo: ¿qué tema quieren?»)
- Why: «Extrawurst» («eine Extrawurst wollen» = demanding special treatment) is the German «picky», very idiomatic; «Wunschthema» (topic of your choice) is the plainest; «Kehrtwende» (U-turn) is the swap; «Themenhopser» a playful topic hop', '', 'Wunschzeit (W)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:03Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:56Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: de.ts: category joker «Wunschzeit» (W), picker title «Wunschzeit: Welches Thema wollt ihr?», spent error (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (58, 'German name for the snipe joker «Francotirador»?', 'answered', '["Scharfschütze (X)", "Kunstschuss (K)", "Blattschuss (B is an answer key: X)", "Meisterschuss (M is flag.key: X)"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5): playful German names, not literal translations (15a "Joker names are content"); at most 13 characters («Francotirador»). The key letter follows the LUI-4 answer (decision 53); a mnemonic letter is noted per candidate. `de.ts` (task 454) uses the recommended name until this is answered.

- Spanish «Francotirador», English «Trick Shot» (decision 44: English name for the snipe joker «Francotirador»)
- What it does: the players aim at the answer they think is false; if it is, that answer is gone; if they hit the correct one, the level repeats
- Why: «Scharfschütze» is the clearest image (aim, shoot), exactly 13 characters; «Kunstschuss» is «Trick Shot»; «Blattschuss» (the clean hunting shot) is idiomatic; «Meisterschuss» (masterstroke) is flattering. `X` stays possible as a crosshair key in any of them', '', 'Finte (F)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:03Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:57Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: de.ts: snipe joker «Finte» (F), spent error «keine Finte mehr übrig» (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (59, 'Neutral Spanish UI wording in es.ts (D-78)?', 'answered', '["Apply all (1 and 2)", "Apply listed subset (name the numbers)", "Keep as is"]', 'Plan 69 (LUI-5), decision 27: Spanish variety (OQ-31): `es` is neutral Latin American Spanish (es-419); `es-ES` overrides only where Spain differs. Scan of `app/client/src/locales/es.ts` (every leaf) for Colombian wording; the family sees these lines.

Old → new:
1. `copy.consolation.9` «¡Qué berraquera! Llegaron al nivel {n}.» → «¡Qué maravilla! Llegaron al nivel {n}.» («berraquera» is Colombian only)
2. `overlay.confirm` «¿Seguro? Pulsa otra vez» → «¿Seguro? Presiona otra vez» (not Colombian, but «pulsar» reads Peninsular; «presionar» is the usual es-419 UI verb; `es-ES` keeps «Pulsa»)

Kept (read neutral across Latin America): «ustedes» addressing (D-6), «Bájale», «Le dieron a la correcta», «Tan cerquita», «a un pelo», «sacar pecho», «Video».
Comment only, no screen change: the header comment of `es.ts` says «Colombian usage»; task 455 rewords it to es-419.', '', 'Apply all (1 and 2)', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:08:10Z', '2026-10-13T02:20:57Z', 453, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 455: es.ts: copy.consolation.9 «¡Qué maravilla!», overlay.confirm «Presiona otra vez»; es-ES keeps «Pulsa»; es.ts header says es-419 (D-91)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (60, 'One mechanism for questions with problems: flag or report?', 'answered', '[]', 'Gamemaster, after D25 play-test 2026-10-13: flag (M, GM-5) and «Reportar pregunta» (MD-6) overlap and it isn''t clear where each goes; flag only reached trivia-authoring at its next start, report never. Gamemaster likes the flag icon; wants the report''s dialog on it.', '', 'Flag only, with a dialog. The flag icon and its key (flag.key, M in es) open a confirm dialog like «Reportar pregunta»''s, with an optional free-text description of the issue. The separate overlay item «Reportar pregunta» goes. One save entry per flag (question, player, level, date, optional note).', NULL, '2026-10-13T02:50:43Z', '2026-10-13T02:50:43Z', NULL, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13: Follow-up task in plan 59: merge report into flag; trivia-authoring turns flags into needs-work with the note as feedback; the list with «Copiar» stays for players without authoring tools.

2026-10-13, task 625: 2026-10-13, task 625: FlagDialog.svelte (flag icon / M / pad Select: optional note, Enter flags, Esc/⌫ cancel; flagged: save note or «Quitar marca»; pad: LetterPicker note mode with picker.letters/marks per catalog); overlay item and engine action report gone; FlagList.svelte «Preguntas marcadas» with notes + Copiar; save v4: reports merged into flags {flagged_on, player, level?, note?} (parseSave, save.py, save_file.flags for v3); apply_flags feedback «Marcada en el juego (player, date): <note>», ledger stamp includes the note so an edited note applies again');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (61, 'hyphens: auto only for German UI (LUI-5)', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 69 asks for hyphens: auto on text blocks and no per-language CSS unless unavoidable. Chromium hyphenates Spanish line ends too (checked in headless Chromium 147), so a global rule would rehyphenate the family''s es screens (question cards, explanations); es must stay pixel-identical. Scoping to :lang(de) is the one exception; <html lang> comes from plan 68.', '', '.game:lang(de) { hyphens: auto } in theme.css; es/en keep no hyphenation', NULL, '2026-10-13T04:31:46Z', '2026-10-13T04:31:46Z', 456, NULL, 'rule', 456, '');
