INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (66, 'Price model (OQ-33): how is the game sold on Steam?', 'answered', '["Paid, low band $4.99–$7.99 (e.g. $6.99) with Valve''s regional pricing and a 10–20 % launch discount; bundles as free updates, paid DLC bundles only later once one is big enough", "Paid base + paid DLC bundles from launch (colombia as DLC)", "Free base + paid DLC bundles", "Free"]', 'OQ-33, plan 39. How «Living Room Trivia» / «Trivia en Familia» (D-50) is sold on Steam. Signup and price setting stay S5 (PUB-6, PUB-11). Not legal or tax advice.

**Caveat:** this worker had no web access (WebFetch/WebSearch denied). Figures are from Valve''s docs as known mid-2026; ≈ marks numbers to re-check at PUB-11 (Steamworks pricing tool, store pages).

## Facts
- Revenue share: Valve 30 % up to $10 M gross per app, 25 % $10–50 M, 20 % above. Source: Valve, "Steam Distribution Agreement updates", Nov 2018 (steamcommunity.com/groups/steamworks).
- App credit: $100 per app, non-refundable, recouped once the app grossed $1,000 (store + in-game). DLC: no app credit. Source: partner.steamgames.com/doc/gettingstarted/appfee.
- Free apps pay the $100 too (never recouped without revenue). Same source.
- Payout: monthly, ≈30 days after month end; balance under $100 rolls over. Source: partner.steamgames.com/doc/finance/payments_salesreporting.
- Refunds: any reason within 14 days of purchase and under 2 h playtime. A 12-question game takes ≈20–40 min: a family can finish several games and still refund. Source: store.steampowered.com/steam_refunds.
- VAT/GST/US sales tax: Valve collects and remits where required; the developer gets net of tax. Source: partner.steamgames.com/doc/finance/taxfaq.
- Regional pricing: Valve''s recommended matrix per USD price, ≈ (to verify in the tool):
  - EUR: about the same number ($6.99 → ≈€6.99)
  - MXN: ≈55–65 % of US in USD terms
  - COP: ≈45–55 %
  - ARS: Argentina sells in USD (LATAM-USD region since 2023), ≈35–50 %
  - Source: partner.steamgames.com/doc/store/pricing (and the "Pricing" page in Steamworks).
- Discounts: launch discount allowed; 30-day cooldown between discounts (≈, check partner.steamgames.com/doc/marketing/discounts).

## Comparable trivia/party games (≈, verify at PUB-11)
| Title | Price | Reviews | Question DLC |
|---|---|---|---|
| Jackbox Party Pack 3 (Trivia Murder Party) | $24.99 | ≈25k, very positive | no |
| Jackbox Party Pack 6 (TMP 2) | $29.99 | ≈15k, very positive | no |
| You Don''t Know Jack (2011) | ≈$19.99 | ≈1–2k | yes (episode packs, delisted) |
| Who Wants To Be A Millionaire (Microids, 2020) | ≈$19.99 | ≈1k, mixed | yes (themed packs) |
| Trivial Pursuit Live! (Ubisoft) | ≈$14.99 | ≈few hundred, mixed | no |
| SongPop Party | ≈$14.99 | ≈few hundred | yes (song packs) |
| Trivia Vault series (Ripknot) | $0.99–2.99 | tens–hundreds each | separate apps per topic |
- Pattern: big party titles sell one paid pack, no DLC; smaller quiz titles sell paid packs/DLC; free trivia apps mostly live on mobile, not Steam.

## Free on Steam
- Wishlists and coming-soon visibility work the same as paid.
- No refunds needed, lower barrier; reviews from people with no stake (≈ more negative for small titles).
- Free + paid DLC = "free to play with in-app purchases" label; needs a reason to buy (here: bundles).
- `colombia` today: 102 approved questions, Spanish only, Colombian voice (D-39, D-49, D-78) → too small and too narrow to carry a paid DLC at launch.

## Consequences per option
- **Plan 40 (OQ-35 licence):** paid + public pool → anyone can copy the content, the store sells convenience; free → a public pool costs nothing.
- **Plan 42 (OQ-45 Freesound):** paid base or paid DLC → "commercial" under Freesound API / CC NC terms; free still counts as distribution (CC BY credits stay required either way).

## Options
1. Paid, low band $4.99–$7.99 (e.g. $6.99), Valve''s regional matrix, launch discount 10–20 %; bundles ship as free updates; paid DLC bundles only later once one is big enough (≥ ≈500 questions, translated). One-time purchase, no store/IAP code, fits a living-room game; recoups the $100 at ≈$1,000 gross.
2. Paid base + paid DLC bundles from launch (`colombia` as DLC ≈$1.99): extra depot/app ID per bundle (plan 18), small pack, Spanish-only buyers.
3. Free base + paid DLC bundles: biggest reach; revenue depends on packs that don''t exist yet; F2P label.
4. Free: no revenue, $100 lost; simplest licence story (plan 40), still distribution for plan 42.', '', 'Paid one-time purchase, base price $9.99 (≈10 USD) for now; final check at PUB-11. Valve''s regional matrix, launch discount. Bundles ship as free DLC (own store entries, optional install), never paid: paid packs would push players to their own AI-made questions instead. No paid DLC planned. Bigger picture: player-made bundles via Steam Workshop and modding (own milestone).', NULL, '2026-10-13T05:10:46Z', '2026-10-13T14:55:26Z', 193, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 194: 2026-10-14, task 194: D-98 in plans/decisions.md; OQ-33 resolved (open-questions.md, 11-steam.md, project.md); 17-publishing.md price bullet, PUB-11 rewritten ($9.99, regional matrix, launch discount, free DLC packs). DLC depots already covered by D-94, D-95 (plan 89), no backlog row.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (67, 'Steamworks account holder (OQ-33): person or company?', 'answered', '["Person, after an advisor check; store Developer/Publisher as a label; switch to a company via app transfer if revenue, a partner or the DSA address requires it", "Company from the start"]', 'OQ-33, plan 39. Who signs the Steam Distribution Agreement and gets paid. PUB-6 (S5) does the signup. Not legal or tax advice; the advisor questions below are for the gamemaster to ask.

**Caveat:** no web access for this worker; facts from Valve''s docs as known mid-2026, re-check at PUB-6.

## Facts
- Partner signup: legal name, address, bank, identity check, tax interview; person or company both allowed. Source: partner.steamgames.com/doc/gettingstarted/onboarding.
- Tax interview: person → W-8BEN, company → W-8BEN-E (non-US). Valve withholds 30 % US tax on US-sourced sales unless a tax treaty lowers it (e.g. Germany–US: 0 % on royalties; Colombia has no US income tax treaty → 30 % on US sales). Source: partner.steamgames.com/doc/finance/taxfaq.
- Store "Developer" and "Publisher" are free-text labels, independent of the account holder (a person can publish as e.g. a label name). Source: partner.steamgames.com/doc/store/editing (basic info).
- EU Digital Services Act: Valve asks whether the partner is a "trader"; a trader''s name, address, phone and email are shown to EU customers on the store page (≈, since 2024; check the Steamworks DSA page). For a person that may mean a home address in public: a c/o address or a company avoids it.
- App transfer: an app can be moved to another partner account on request, both sides agree (partner.steamgames.com/doc/gettingstarted, "transferring apps"; ≈ check). Switching later is possible, not free of paperwork.
- Company: formation cost and yearly bookkeeping/filing (≈ hundreds to a few thousand €/year depending on country, e.g. German UG/GmbH, Colombian SAS); limits liability; W-8BEN-E.
- Liability is low for this game (offline, no data collected, no accounts); main risks: media licences (PUB-1..PUB-3), names (PUB-7), AI content terms (PUB-10).

## Advisor questions (text for the gamemaster)
- "I live in <country>. I want to sell a small video game on Steam (Valve, USA) as a private person. Expected revenue: a few hundred to a few thousand USD per year."
- "Do I need to register a business (Gewerbe / RUT / equivalent) for this, or is it hobby income?"
- "Which form for Valve: W-8BEN as an individual; which treaty article and rate apply to US sales; can I credit US withholding at home?"
- "VAT: Valve collects VAT from customers; do I still owe VAT or a filing at home (small-business threshold, e.g. German §19 UStG Kleinunternehmer: €25,000 previous year / €100,000 current; reverse charge on Valve''s fee)?"
- "Income tax: how is it declared, and from what amount does it pay to form a company?"
- "Must my private address be public as an EU ''trader'' (DSA)? Can I use a c/o or business address?"

## Consequences
- Plan 40/42: none directly; "commercial" depends on the price decision, not the holder.
- PUB-6 gets the holder, the form (W-8BEN or W-8BEN-E), the $100 app credit and the advisor check before signup.

## Options
1. Person (recommended for a hobby launch): cheapest, fastest; W-8BEN; store labels as Developer/Publisher; advisor check before signup; switch to a company (app transfer) if revenue passes the advisor''s threshold, a second person joins, or the DSA address can''t be kept private.
2. Company from the start: W-8BEN-E, limited liability, no private address in public; formation and bookkeeping cost before any revenue.', '', 'Person, after an advisor check; store Developer/Publisher as a label; switch to a company via app transfer if revenue, a partner or the DSA address requires it', NULL, '2026-10-13T05:10:47Z', '2026-10-13T16:05:18Z', 193, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 194: 2026-10-14, task 194: D-98; 17-publishing.md account bullet decided, PUB-6 rewritten (person, advisor check first, W-8BEN, label, $100 app credit); 11-steam.md S5 prerequisite cites decision 67.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (68, 'Steamworks SDK downloaded for the Steam binding?', 'answered', '["Done: SDK unzipped to app/desktop/steamworks_sdk/redistributable_bin/ (version …)", "Not yet: build the Linux side from nixpkgs, Windows packaging waits"]', 'Plan 85 (SW-8) needs Valve''s Steamworks SDK `redistributable_bin` (Valve licence, not in git): `linux64/libsteam_api.so` and `win64/steam_api64.dll`. Download the SDK zip from partner.steamgames.com/downloads (Steam login; partner account per decision 67 if Valve asks for one) and unzip `sdk/redistributable_bin/` to `app/desktop/steamworks_sdk/redistributable_bin/` (gitignored). Linux dev can start without it (nixpkgs `steamworks-sdk-redist`, unfree), but the Windows zip (packaging task) needs the dll. Answer with the SDK version.', '', 'Done: SDK unzipped to app/desktop/steamworks_sdk/redistributable_bin/ (version 1.65)', NULL, '2026-10-13T05:17:49Z', '2026-10-14T01:35:02Z', 644, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 650: 2026-10-13, task 650: packaged builds ship the SDK libs: electron-builder.yml per-OS extraResources → resources/steamworks_sdk/redistributable_bin/{linux64/libsteam_api.so,win64/steam_api64.dll}; app/desktop/steam-libs.mjs (in prepare-dist) fails the build without them; the flake''s SDK 1.62 fallback is dev-only, releases need the SDK zip folder');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (69, 'Steamworks SDK libs for dev and the bridge''s SDK path', 'answered', '[]', 'nixpkgs has no steamworks-sdk-redist (plan 85 and decision 68 assumed one). steamworks-ffi-node binds the newest exported interface versions, so 1.62 works in dev (checked: Spacewar 480, SteamID and language). Never shipped: the release builds take the gamemaster''s SDK download (decision 68); task 650 puts redistributable_bin under resources/steamworks_sdk/, the path main.mjs reads when packaged. Bridge: availability reaches the sandboxed preload as --trivia-steam in additionalArguments (Steam init runs before the window); overlay stub is overlay.enabled().', '', 'Dev: flake fetchzip of SDK 1.62 (archive.org URL+hash as nixpkgs rimsort) as TRIVIA_STEAM_SDK in trivia-desktop; app/desktop/steamworks_sdk/ wins when present; packaged: resources/steamworks_sdk/', NULL, '2026-10-13T05:27:05Z', '2026-10-13T05:27:05Z', 645, NULL, 'rule', 645, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (70, 'Steam overlay in the Electron shell', 'answered', '[]', 'Spike task 647 (D-92): steamworks-ffi-node''s frame copy gets no frames before did-finish-load; with the native window attached the Linux main process freezes (windowed and fullscreen, COSMIC/XWayland, Intel Mesa); frame copy far below 60 fps. Wired: addElectronSteamOverlay on win32 after did-finish-load, only with Steam; overlay.enabled() = attached && IsOverlayEnabled. Windows pending a gamemaster check.', '', 'Windows only; Linux without overlay (native GL window freezes the game on XWayland); Deck via Proton', NULL, '2026-10-13T05:39:35Z', '2026-10-13T05:39:35Z', 647, NULL, 'rule', 647, '2026-10-13, task 647: 2026-10-13, task 647: app/desktop/main.mjs attaches addElectronSteamOverlay on win32 after did-finish-load (Steam up only); steam:overlay-enabled = attached && IsOverlayEnabled; Linux unchanged. D-92 in plans/decisions.md. Windows check folded into task 652''s gamemaster decision (needs task 650''s packaged build).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (71, 'Upload the rich presence tokens in Steamworks?', 'answered', '["Uploaded once the App ID exists; presence shows", "Skip rich presence (remove the calls)"]', 'Task 651: the game sets Steam rich presence «Nivel 7 de 12» (token #Level, values level/levels) while a level is on screen. Steam only shows tokens uploaded in Steamworks: App Admin > Community > Rich Presence, upload app/desktop/steam-presence.vdf (latam, spanish, english, german). Needs the real App ID (part 1); under 480 (Spacewar) nothing shows. Check afterwards: a friend''s Steam list shows «Nivel N de 12» during play.', '', 'Keep rich presence. Upload app/desktop/steam-presence.vdf in Steamworks (App Admin > Community > Rich Presence) as part of the Steamworks app setup once the App ID exists (SW-7 checklist); check then that a friend''s list shows «Nivel N de 12».', NULL, '2026-10-13T05:44:44Z', '2026-10-13T16:38:01Z', 651, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (72, 'SW-8 check under Steam and without Steam', 'answered', '["all pass", "issues (name the rows)"]', 'Gamemaster check for plan 85 (Steamworks binding, SW-8). Needs task 650''s packaged builds (`trivia-desktop-build` → app/desktop/release/) and the Steamworks SDK libs (decision 68). App ID 480 (Spacewar) until SW-7: launch through Steam as a non-Steam shortcut with `SteamAppId=480` (or `TRIVIA_STEAM_APPID=480`), or under the real App ID. stderr shows `trivia: steam available, app …, user …, language …`.

Overlay (Windows zip only; Linux has none by design, D-92):
- Shift+Tab opens the overlay and closes it again
- a video and an audio question play smoothly with sound; animations not choppy
- F11 toggles fullscreen; the overlay still opens afterwards
- keyboard and pad still reach the game after closing the overlay

On-screen keyboard (Big Picture on Linux or Windows, or the Deck; a pad):
- Player screen, focus the name field, A (or «Escribir»): Steam''s floating keyboard opens near the field
- typed letters appear in the field; its Enter submits the name
- desktop Steam (not Big Picture) and without Steam: A opens the letter picker as before

Glyphs (under Steam, desktop or Big Picture):
- one DualShock/DualSense: pressing a button shows PlayStation glyphs (prompt chips, answer tiles)
- an Xbox pad or the Deck: Xbox glyphs; one PS + one Xbox pad: Xbox
- pads still work in the game at all (Steam Input on)

Language (fresh save: delete or move save/game.json first):
- Steam''s language German → first-start screen preselects Deutsch/Deutsch; Spanish – Spain → es-ES/es; Spanish – Latin America → es/es
- an existing save keeps its language

Without Steam (Steam closed; Windows zip and Linux tar.gz):
- full game as in S3 (to level 3 with image, audio, video; quit, restart, player still there); save untouched
- browser game (`trivia`) unchanged

On failure name the failing rows; the worker adds follow-ups in plan 85 (drop the Windows overlay, switch to ShowGamepadTextInput, or drop Steam Input).', '', 'Replaced by decision 113: SW-8 check under Steam (same check without the ''without Steam'' rows, decision 111).', NULL, '2026-10-13T05:45:41Z', '2026-10-13T15:45:13Z', 652, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (73, 'Achievement list (SW-11)?', 'answered', '["The draft: 6 achievements as listed, 3 in Steamworks now, the 3 mode wins with MD-8, texts as written", "Draft + WIN_ALL_AGES (a win in each of the 4 age groups), in Steamworks now"]', 'Plan 86 (SW-11). Steam achievements, earned only in qualifying games (decision 19: Default mode: presets, checkpoints and won levels): not gamemaster mode, not customized, no custom difficulty, 12 levels, 4 cards. Derived from the save over all its players, any age group. No hidden ones, no progress pop-ups, Steam''s toast only. Texts go into Steamworks, not into `t()`.

Wording: infinitive / impersonal, so latam and es-ES need no ustedes/vosotros split; tower/top imagery from the catalogs («¡Ganaron!», «llegó a la cima», «Gewonnen!», «auf dem Gipfel»). Mode names = the proposals in `13-game-modes.md`.

## Steamworks now (modes in `BUILT_MODES`: gamemaster, solo)

| API name | Trigger |
|---|---|
| `FIRST_WIN` | any qualifying game with `result === "won"` (also solo''s win) |
| `WIN_NO_JOKERS` | won game with no joker played (`state.jokers` empty), in a mode with jokers |
| `ALL_CATEGORIES` | every broad category of `base` with questions in the loaded pool''s locale has ≥ 1 correct answer across all qualifying games, any result (28 today: ~4–6 games) |

## In the code list, entered in Steamworks with MD-8

| API name | Trigger |
|---|---|
| `WIN_RR_COOP` | won game, mode `rr-coop` |
| `WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE` | a player''s game in `rr-competitive` won |
| `WIN_TIMED` | won game, mode `timed` |

## Texts

`FIRST_WIN`
- latam: «¡A la cima!» / «Ganar una partida: 12 preguntas, hasta arriba de la torre.»
- spanish: same as latam
- english: «To the Top!» / «Win a game: 12 questions, all the way up the tower.»
- german: «Auf dem Gipfel!» / «Ein Spiel gewinnen: 12 Fragen, ganz nach oben.»

`WIN_NO_JOKERS`
- latam: «Sin comodines» / «Ganar una partida sin usar ni un solo comodín.»
- spanish: same as latam
- english: «No Jokers Needed» / «Win a game without playing a single joker.»
- german: «Ganz ohne Joker» / «Ein Spiel gewinnen, ohne einen einzigen Joker zu spielen.»

`ALL_CATEGORIES`
- latam: «De todo un poco» / «Acertar al menos una pregunta de cada tema.»
- spanish: same as latam
- english: «Jack of All Topics» / «Answer at least one question right in every topic.»
- german: «Von allem etwas» / «In jedem Thema mindestens eine Frage richtig beantworten.»

`WIN_RR_COOP` (MD-8)
- latam: «Todos a una» / «Ganar una partida Por turnos en equipo.»
- spanish: same as latam
- english: «All for One» / «Win a round-robin co-op game.»
- german: «Alle für einen» / «Ein Spiel reihum im Team gewinnen.»

`WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE` (MD-8)
- latam: «El último en pie» / «Ganar una partida Por turnos, todos contra todos.»
- spanish: same as latam
- english: «Last One Standing» / «Win a round-robin game, everyone against everyone.»
- german: «Wer zuletzt lacht» / «Ein Spiel reihum, jeder gegen jeden, gewinnen.»

`WIN_TIMED` (MD-8)
- latam: «Contra el reloj» / «Ganar una partida Contrarreloj.»
- spanish: same as latam
- english: «Beat the Clock» / «Win a timed game.»
- german: «Gegen die Uhr» / «Ein Spiel auf Zeit gewinnen.»

## Option 2''s extra

`WIN_ALL_AGES`: a won qualifying game in each of the 4 age groups (`kids`, `young_teens`, `young_adults`, `adults`; `settings.age_group`), any players of the save. Cheap in code (one field), but needs 4 wins, the adult one hard for kids: close to grind for a solo player, natural for a family. Not recommended.
- latam / spanish: «Para todas las edades» / «Ganar una partida en cada grupo de edad.»
- english: «For All Ages» / «Win a game in every age group.»
- german: «Für jedes Alter» / «In jeder Altersgruppe ein Spiel gewinnen.»

Answer with the option, plus any wording changes per line.', '', 'Expanded list, all Steam achievements, earned only in qualifying games (D73''s rules unchanged):
- Tower: FIRST_WIN, WINS_10, WINS_50, WIN_ADULTS, WIN_ALL_AGES (a win in each of the 4 age groups)
- Jokers:
  - first use of each joker: FIRST_SOPLO, FIRST_PASO, FIRST_BAJALE, FIRST_CAMBIAZO, FIRST_FRANCOTIRADOR
  - ALL_HINTS: every hint of one question shown with Soplo
  - PURGE: Paso with the burn-the-whole-category option (skip + purge); title idea «Passing just wasn''t enough»
  - SUPER_PICKY: Paso and Bájale both played on the same question (same level''s slot, either order); title idea «Super picky»
  - WIN_NO_JOKERS, ALL_JOKERS_WIN (all five jokers in one won game), SNIPER_TOP (Francotirador hit on the last level), SOPLO_SAVE (last question won right after a Soplo)
- Knowledge: ALL_CATEGORIES, SPECIALIST (50 correct in one broad category), QUESTIONS_1000 (1000 different questions seen)
- Bundles and languages: one achievement per regional bundle, worded around its region (50 correct answers from that bundle; ships with the bundle''s DLC; first: colombia); POLYGLOT (wins in two question languages)
- Habit: GAME_NIGHTS (games on 7 different days), CHRISTMAS (a game on 24/25 Dec), NIGHT_OWL (a win after midnight, local clock)
- Flagging: FIRST_FLAG (flag a question; needs a Steam user, decision 111)
- Modes, entered with MD-8: WIN_RR_COOP, WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE, WIN_TIMED
- Dropped: MEDIA_TRIO, FAMILY.
- Texts latam/spanish/english/german, no plural address (German style guide, milestone 9); D73''s drafted texts stay, the worker drafts the new ones, the gamemaster checks all of them in the SW-11 close-out (task 658).', NULL, '2026-10-13T05:49:32Z', '2026-10-13T16:11:33Z', 654, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 654: 2026-10-13, task 654: final list replaces plan 86''s table (tasks 655–658 follow it, not the 6-row draft). Rules unchanged: qualifying games only (decision 19: Default mode: presets, checkpoints and won levels; decision 74: Gamemaster mode earns no achievements), derived from the save, never stored.
- Steamworks now (29): FIRST_WIN, WINS_10, WINS_50, WIN_ADULTS, WIN_ALL_AGES (incl. option 2), FIRST_SOPLO, FIRST_PASO, FIRST_BAJALE, FIRST_CAMBIAZO, FIRST_FRANCOTIRADOR, ALL_HINTS, PURGE, SUPER_PICKY, WIN_NO_JOKERS, ALL_JOKERS_WIN, SNIPER_TOP, SOPLO_SAVE, ALL_CATEGORIES, SPECIALIST, QUESTIONS_1000, POLYGLOT, GAME_NIGHTS, CHRISTMAS, NIGHT_OWL, FIRST_FLAG (25 ids; count by the code list).
- With the bundle''s DLC: one per regional bundle, API name `BUNDLE_<ID>` (first `BUNDLE_COLOMBIA`), 50 correct answers from that bundle, texts around the region.
- With MD-8: WIN_RR_COOP, WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE, WIN_TIMED.
- Dropped: MEDIA_TRIO, FAMILY.
- Data the save lacks today (task 655 adds it, save-version bump if needed): hints shown per question (`hints_shown` resets per question; ALL_HINTS needs it in `history[]`); local clock for NIGHT_OWL / CHRISTMAS / GAME_NIGHTS (check `started_on` / `finished_on` format). Derivable already: PURGE (`state.purged`), SUPER_PICKY (`skipped` + `easier` entries at one `level`), jokers per entry (`history[].jokers`), POLYGLOT (`GameRow.locale`), QUESTIONS_1000 (`save.seen`), FIRST_FLAG (`save.flags`).
- FIRST_FLAG: flags aren''t game rows; counts with a valid user only (decision 111), no qualifying-game check.
- Texts: D73''s drafted ones stay; task 657 drafts the rest (latam/spanish/english/german, no plural address); title ideas «Passing just wasn''t enough» (PURGE), «Super picky» (SUPER_PICKY); gamemaster checks all in task 658.
- Icons (task 656): one per id above, bundle ones with their DLC.

2026-10-13, task 654: 2026-10-13, task 654: correction: «Steamworks now» lists 25 achievements, not 29.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (74, 'Gamemaster mode earns no achievements', 'answered', '[]', 'Gamemaster mode has undo, skip, replace, jump to level and any joker budget mid-game (D-74, D-88; decision 34: Gamemaster menu: which cheats?), while outside it a question can never be skipped and nothing changes mid-game (decision 20: Default mode: which admin actions in the Esc menu). Achievements would be free there. Qualifying = decision 19: Default mode: presets, checkpoints and won levels (uncustomized games only), plan 86. earned() skips rows with gameMode() === ''gamemaster''.', '', 'Gamemaster mode never earns Steam achievements; only qualifying games (decision 19) count', NULL, '2026-10-13T05:49:36Z', '2026-10-13T05:49:36Z', 654, NULL, 'rule', 654, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (75, 'Steam Cloud test passed?', 'pending', '["passed", "issues (fill the table)"]', 'Plan 87 part 4: test Steam Cloud saves on real machines.

Preconditions:
- real App ID (masterplan 10 part 1, task 253: write plan: Partner account, name check and AI terms)
- Auto-Cloud values entered in Steamworks (part 2, task 254: write plan: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)); values in plans/18-steam-integration.md "Steam features" → Steam Cloud
- a packaged Steam build: task 650: Package the Steam binding in both builds, or part 7''s upload to the `beta` branch
- machines A and B: one Windows, one Linux or the Deck

Checklist (table to fill: plans/18-steam-integration.md, section "Steam Cloud test"):
- A plays → quit → B shows the same players and seen counts
- two Steam accounts on one OS login → separate saves (save/<id>/ each)
- Family Sharing borrower → own save
- first Steam start with an S3 or local/ save → «Usar el progreso de este equipo» offered; second machine with a cloud save → no question
- offline on both, play on both, then online → Steam''s conflict dialog; the picked side wins whole
- Steam''s cloud file list (game properties, or store.steampowered.com/account/remotestorage) shows only game.json, never .tmp, backup/, local/

On issues: name the failing rows (or fill the table in the plan file); each becomes a task in plan 87.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-13T06:03:27Z', NULL, 663, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (76, 'Store capsule art (PUB-8): who makes the capsules and logo?', 'irrelevant', '["Typographic template in code: «Trivia» wordmark in the game''s fonts (Baloo 2, Nunito) and colours, rendered per size and language by a script; disclosed as AI-assisted if Claude designs it", "The gamemaster designs them (any tool); workers render the sizes from one master file", "Commissioned artist (cost, time, a licence for the art; credit in CREDITS.md)", "AI image generator (must be disclosed on the store page; clashes with «images by people from Commons»)"]', '', '', NULL, 'duplicate of decision 77', '2026-10-13T06:04:45Z', '2026-10-13T14:47:32Z', 258, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (77, 'Store capsule art (PUB-8): who makes the capsules and logo?', 'answered', '["Typographic template in code: «Trivia» wordmark in the game''s fonts (Baloo 2, Nunito) and colours, rendered per size and language by a script; disclosed as AI-assisted if Claude designs it", "The gamemaster designs them (any tool); workers render the sizes from one master file", "Commissioned artist (cost, time, a licence for the art; credit in CREDITS.md)", "AI image generator (must be disclosed on the store page; clashes with «images by people from Commons»)"]', 'Plan 10 part 8 (store page, PUB-8) needs capsule art: header, small, main, vertical capsules, page background, library capsule/hero/logo, community icon; localized per store language (D-50: «Living Room Trivia», «Trivia en Familia»; the word «Trivia» is the main element so both read as one game).

- Steam''s AI disclosure covers pre-generated content; AI-made art must be disclosed. The disclosure already says questions are AI-drafted; image-generator art would add a line and undercut «images by people».
- Option 1: cheapest, localizes automatically (text per language), but plain; the gamemaster approves the look before any upload.
- Option 3: money and a written licence (commercial use, store, marketing).
- The answer shapes the capsule task, the AI disclosure text and CREDITS.md.', '', 'Typographic template in code: «Trivia» wordmark in the game''s fonts (Baloo 2, Nunito) and colours, rendered per size and language by a script; disclosed as AI-assisted if Claude designs it', NULL, '2026-10-13T06:04:54Z', '2026-10-13T16:33:23Z', 258, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (78, 'German store name (PUB-8, D-50): keep «Living Room Trivia» or a localized one?', 'answered', '["Keep «Living Room Trivia» for German (no localized name; no extra name check)", "Localized «Wohnzimmer-Quiz» (needs PUB-7''s name/trademark check, plan 10 part 1)", "Localized «Quiz in Familie» (needs PUB-7''s check)"]', 'Plan 88 task 1 (store texts, LUI-6) writes the German store block in `plans/17a-store-page.md`. D-50: «Living Room Trivia», Spanish «Trivia en Familia»; "other languages get a localized name when they launch".

- Keep: German Steam users read English names often; one name, no extra trademark/Steam-search check; capsules show «Trivia» either way.
- Localized: German says «Quiz», not «Trivia», so the logo''s main word «Trivia» (D-50) would not match; capsules need a German wordmark; PUB-7 check (Steam search, EUIPO/DPMA, domain) before entry; set in Steamworks before the coming-soon page (later changes restricted).
- Own text welcome (another name).', '', 'Localized «Wohnzimmer-Quiz» (needs PUB-7''s name/trademark check, plan 10 part 1)', NULL, '2026-10-13T06:06:31Z', '2026-10-13T16:05:18Z', 665, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (79, 'Store screenshots: which set?', 'answered', '["es/es-ES: 07, 08, 09, 06, 10, 05, 03 (gameplay first); en/de: all 5 for now", "All 10 for es/es-ES; all 5 for en/de", "Other set or other screens (say which)"]', 'Rendered by authoring/store/screenshots.mjs (task 670), 1920×1080, demo save with made-up players. Output in authoring/store/out/screenshots/<lang>/ (gitignored; re-run the script to regenerate).

es and es-ES (10 each): 01-start, 02-player, 03-modes, 04-customize, 05-tower (level 11), 06-cards, 07-image-question (q-0030 cheetah), 08-video-question (q-0055 Apollo 11), 09-joker (Francotirador aiming), 10-victory.
en and de (5 each): 01-start … 05-tower only. There are no en/de question pools yet, and the age-group names still show in Spanish. A follow-up task re-runs these once the pools land.

Valve''s minimum is 5 per language. Pick the set (numbers), or ask for other questions/screens.', '', '7 screenshots per store language:
- 5 informative: mode choice, configure screen, bundle selector, joker presets, Customize game (the worker picks and orders, the gamemaster approves)
- 2 gameplay: a question with a locked-in answer; a question with a joker in use (e.g. Francotirador aiming or Soplo''s hint), for people who skip videos
- Timing: rendered late, after milestone 9''s UI wording fixes and translations, right before the store page goes to Valve''s review; nothing rendered or approved before that.', NULL, '2026-10-13T06:21:11Z', '2026-10-13T16:31:23Z', 670, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (80, 'en/de question pools exported (pool.en.json, pool.de.json)?', 'answered', '["Yes, both exported", "Drop the en/de question screenshots for the beta (keep the 5 menu/tower shots)"]', 'task 673 re-renders the en/de store screenshots (cards, image/video question, Francotirador, victory) and needs app/data/pool.en.json and pool.de.json. As of 2026-10-13 neither exists: translations (qgen batch --translate en|de, then qgen export) haven''t run; plan 70''s release budget (task 463) and the translation pilot gate them. Answer once both pools are exported with approved translations of q-0030, q-0055, q-0019, q-0053 (or say which questions to use instead).', '', 'The 5 menu shots need no question pool. The 2 question shots and the trailer for en/de wait for pool.en.json / pool.de.json; until then the en/de pages carry the 5 menu shots (Valve''s minimum). Like decision 79: rendered late, after UI and translation changes.', NULL, '2026-10-13T06:22:14Z', '2026-10-13T16:31:23Z', 673, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (81, 'Recorded sound effects: approve on the TV?', 'answered', '["approve", "changes: <effect> → <what''s wrong>"]', 'Plan 32 replaced every synthesized effect with a CC0 recording; none kept synthesized. Picked by spectrogram, not by ear, so please listen.

How to check
- TV: `/?efectos` → each effect has «grabado» / «sintetizado» buttons for A/B.
- `/?fuegos=finale` for the fireworks.
- A real game: Paso, card pick, menu, jokers, Soplo note, token pop-back.

Replaced (recorded)
- UI: whoosh, «swoosh que sube», escoba (Paso; quiet source boosted +20 dB, check first), pop/carta (pitch varies), menú abierto / cerrado, desbloqueado, listo/hola.
- Jokers: comodín shimmer, preparado, abrir (card fan), silbato (swanee whistle), trituradora, latido, rebobinar, mira: tic (pitch varies), corcho, rasgado.
- New, previously silent: Soplo paper rustle (+11 dB), token pop-back (chip lay).
- Fireworks: cohete, cañón de confeti (pitch varies), bengalas (quiet source +19 dB), estrellas (pitch varies).

Kept synthesized
- none (synth recipes stay as fallback only).

Answer
- «approve», or «changes:» per effect: swap (another recording), back to synth, louder/quieter, pitch.', '', 'changes: Paso y fuera → a broom sweeping; Soplo → a microwave bell «bing»; Hada madrina → a fairy''s magic wand, sprinkling fairy dust; Doña Exigente and Tiro mágico: keep. The other effects: no changes. Details in milestone 6.', NULL, '2026-10-13T06:41:19Z', '2026-10-17T20:19:06Z', 146, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (82, 'Freesound API for a paid Steam release (OQ-45): replace, ask, or family only?', 'answered', '["(a) Replace the 2 Freesound picks from Commons before release; drop Freesound from the audio order", "(b) Ask Freesound/UPF with the drafted email; keep Freesound until the reply", "(c) Keep Freesound for the family only; exclude its picks from the Steam media bundle (SW-9)"]', 'OQ-45 (Freesound), plan 42. The authoring pipeline uses Freesound''s API only to find sounds (MP-6, `authoring/tools/providers/freesound.py`, audio order `commons → freesound`); the game ships the picked CC0/CC BY MP3 previews, never the API. Is a paid Steam release a problem? **Depends on plan 39 / decision 66: Price model (OQ-33)** (paid = commercial).

**Caveat:** this worker had no web access (WebFetch/WebSearch denied). Terms below are from memory; ≈ marks what to re-check on the pages before answering.

## Facts
- API terms ≈: the API is free for non-commercial use; commercial use needs a separate licence from the MTG (Universitat Pompeu Fabra), arranged by contacting them. Source: freesound.org/help/tos_api/ and freesound.org/docs/api/ ("API terms of use").
- What counts as commercial ≈: an app or service that is sold or earns revenue and uses the API. The terms don''t (≈) address an internal authoring tool whose output feeds a paid product: grey zone. Same source.
- The sound licences are separate from the API: CC0 needs nothing, CC BY allows commercial use with credit. Files already downloaded keep their licence whatever the API terms say. Source: creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/, creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.
- Count (2026-10-13; `freesound` provider or `freesound.org` URL):
  - `authoring/data/questions.json` (1211): 2, both approved, both CC0: q-0752 (mosquito, «El zancudo»), q-1016 (turkey, «Pavo»). The 2026-10-11 count (2) holds; the masterplan''s 9/6 was wrong. (q-0749 only mentions Freesound in a note; its pick is Commons.)
  - `app/data/pool.json` (1136): the same 2.
  - Audio picks overall: 17 (15 Commons, 2 Freesound) → ≈12 % of audio, ≈0.2 % of questions.
  - Batches: batch-7 (the only one with providers; MP-11): picks Commons 602, Openverse 2, Freesound 2. Base deficit ≈3,800 questions → at today''s rates ≈6–10 more Freesound slots for `base`, more with translations/bundles.
- Commons alternatives (provider search, `commons.search(…, "audio")`, no picks, D-36):
  - q-0752: "File:Mosquito attack.ogg", CC0, 88 s (needs a listen; the rest are pronunciation clips).
  - q-1016: xeno-canto wild turkey recordings, CC BY-SA 3.0, e.g. "Meleagris gallopavo - Wild Turkey XC134744.ogg" (29 s); wild, not domestic, and longer clips.
  - Openverse isn''t asked for audio (mostly music, D-13).

## Options
- **(a) Replace (recommended):** re-pick the 2 slots from Commons in the review tool before release; drop `freesound` from `providers.ORDER["audio"]` (or keep it for the family pool only until release batches start). Cost: 2 re-picks, slightly fewer good everyday sounds later. Plan 39: works for paid and free; no contact with UPF.
- **(b) Ask Freesound/UPF:** the gamemaster sends the draft below; Freesound stays until the reply. Plan 39: needed only if paid; a refusal or a fee falls back to (a). Wait time unknown.
- **(c) Family only:** tag Freesound picks (`provider` already exists, plan 26) and exclude them from the Steam media bundle (SW-9, `plans/18-steam-integration.md`); those questions don''t ship or get another pick. Plan 39: paid release ships without them; free release still counts as distribution, so same rule. Adds a filter to SW-9 for 2 questions.

## Email draft (option b)
To: freesound@freesound.org (≈ check the contact on the API terms page)
Subject: Freesound API in an internal authoring tool for a paid game?

Hello,

I''m making a small family trivia game that I plan to sell on Steam. An internal authoring tool (not shipped) uses the Freesound API (token auth, text search) to find sound effects for questions; a person then picks one. The game ships only the picked files (CC0 or CC BY, with credits), never the API or any Freesound access. Expected volume: a few dozen sounds in total, a few hundred API searches a year.

Does this count as commercial use of the API that needs a licence? If so, what would it cost?

Thank you,
Ruben Moor', '', '(a) Replace the 2 Freesound picks from Commons before release; drop Freesound from the audio order', NULL, '2026-10-13T06:42:42Z', '2026-10-13T16:05:18Z', 204, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 205: 2026-10-14, task 205: D-103 in plans/decisions.md; OQ-45 (Freesound) resolved (open-questions.md, project.md, 11-steam.md); plans/23-media-providers.md Freesound row, audio order, MP-6 note; follow-up task 1051: Freesound: re-pick its 2 audio slots from Commons, drop it from the audio order

2026-10-15, task 406: 2026-10-14, task 406: plans/project.md: OQ-45 (Freesound) row dropped from the open-questions table (none left), S2 line names D-103 and pending task 1051; plans/README.md: 17''s row names Freesound out (D-103). Masterplan 10 already defers to plan 42; no milestone body change.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (83, 'Recorded music loops: approve on the TV?', 'answered', '["approve", "changes: <track / cut / level> → <what''s wrong>"]', 'Plan 33 replaced the three generated music loops with one matched CC0 set; please listen on the TV.

Recorded (OpenGameArt «Music loop variations», obscure music, CC0; 100 bpm, 4/4, 8 bars = 19.2 s each, −18 LUFS like `redoble`)
- `normal` (Start/Level/Select): `level1-step1` (calm, F major) → `musica-normal.m4a`
- `question`: `level1-step2-evil` (tense, F minor) → `musica-pregunta.m4a`
- `submitted`: `level1-step3-evil` (most tense, F minor) → `musica-enviada.m4a`
- 707 kB together; folder 2.8 MB (budget 3.5 MB); `CREDITS.md` rows

Kept synthesized
- none of the loops; the generated loops stay only as fallback when a file is missing.
- `roll`, `victory` were already recordings (unchanged).

Settings picked by measurement, not by ear
- Level: `MUSIC_LEVEL` 1.6 (a guess) against effects and question media.
- Seam: loop 0 → 19.2 s; 5 ms fades at each 4-bar end against a jump at the wrap.
- Cut `question` ↔ `submitted` (~80 ms): continues at the old loop''s position, so the beat goes on (alternative: restart at 0).
- `normal` → `question` changes key (major → minor) only across the 600/800 ms fades.

How to check
- TV: `/?efectos` → music: «grabado» / «sintetizado» per loop, «corte» toggles `question` ↔ `submitted`, «parar»; let a loop run > 20 s to hear the seam.
- A real game: Start → Level → Select → question → lock-in → «Respuesta final»; level vs. effects and question media.

Answer
- «approve», or «changes:» per item: louder/quieter, click at the seam, cut from 0 instead of continuing, swap a loop (alternative from the same pack: the «good» step2/step3 in F major, calmer, no key change), back to synth.', '', 'changes: the recordings sound better, but the vibe is wrong. The synthesized loops are chill and relaxing, with a clear rise in tension on submit. Keep the current set as one soundtrack; add 3–4 more recorded soundtracks; make the soundtrack selectable in a menu; the developer picks the default after listening on the TV. Details in milestone 6.', NULL, '2026-10-13T06:49:49Z', '2026-10-17T20:09:42Z', 149, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (84, 'SteamCMD source and depot split for Steam uploads', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 89 (SW-10). nixpkgs pins SteamCMD with the flake and wraps the FHS it needs on NixOS; media changes rarely and is OS-independent, so one shared content depot; default branch stays empty until S6 and is set only in the Steamworks web UI.', '', 'SteamCMD from nixpkgs (unfree) in the dev shell, SDK ContentBuilder via steam-run as fallback; three depots in one install folder: windows, linux (both without resources/media), content (resources/media); SetLive beta only, default never from the repo', NULL, '2026-10-13T06:53:05Z', '2026-10-13T06:53:05Z', 261, NULL, 'rule', 261, '2026-10-13, task 676: 2026-10-13, task 676: D-93; flake.nix: steamcmd (nixpkgs, own HOME ~/.local/share/trivia/steamcmd, not the Steam client''s root) and trivia-steam; unfree predicate + steamcmd, steam-unwrapped; no SDK fallback needed; authoring/steam/ (steam.json, app_build.vdf.in, depot_build.vdf.in, steam.py: trivia-steam vdf); content depot DepotPath resources/media');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (85, 'Packaged smoke game runtime (smoke.mjs)', 'answered', '[]', 'nixpkgs'' steam-run lacks what Electron links (task 330 hit nss too); Steam''s own runtime ships these. unshare -rn leaves loopback down, so --remote-debugging-port is unreachable; the pipe (fds 3/4) passes through unshare, env -i and bwrap. steam-run''s bwrap has its own /tmp, so HOME lives in work/smoke-*. Media types forced per level by swapping the save''s first card and reloading. trivia-release-check''s wrapper (task 679) must run smoke.mjs with this steam-run and Xvfb on PATH (dev shell or runtimeInputs).', '', 'dev shell''s steam-run = steam FHS + nss, nspr, gtk3, atk, at-spi2-*, libXcomposite; CDP over --remote-debugging-pipe; temp HOME under work/', NULL, '2026-10-13T07:41:50Z', '2026-10-13T07:41:50Z', 678, NULL, 'rule', 678, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (86, 'Release check fails on licences and the release bar: fix before the first beta upload, or skip for the beta?', 'answered', '["Fix both before the first beta upload (I replace the 2 files and spot-check two batches)", "Beta: upload with --skip licenses --skip quality (shown in the build Desc); fix both before S6", "Fix licences now, skip quality for the beta"]', 'trivia-release-check (task 679) on main 2026-10-13: checks, nix, desktop, smoke ✓; two content ✗:
- licenses: 2 approved files on the replace list (pd-us-only): q-1100 (HitComicsNo19.jpg, PD-US-not renewed), q-1194 (LCCN2016872269.jpg, PD-Harris-Ewing). Fix: /review?licence=replace.
- quality (pm decision 15): only batch-7 has a QC column and it has no spot check; the bar needs two batches with ≥ 30 spot-checked and ≥ 90 % agreement. Fix: spot checks (/review?batch=…&sample=1) of the last two batches.
Affects task 681 (first beta upload). The beta is password-protected, family only.', '', '- Licences: set a human needs_work review on q-1100 (HitComicsNo19.jpg) and q-1194 (LCCN2016872269.jpg) with the note ''image on the licence replace list (PD-US only): needs a new file''; they drop out of the export, so the licence check passes; they come back once the gamemaster picks new files (decision 47''s queue).
- Quality: skipped for the family beta (--skip quality, shown in the build description); spot checks of two batches are required before launch.', NULL, '2026-10-13T07:58:51Z', '2026-10-13T16:37:23Z', 679, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (87, 'Windows exe icon (B-11): where does the game icon come from?', 'answered', '["Derive it from decision 77''s logo / community icon: task 669''s script also renders a 1024×1024 icon (wait for 669)", "The gamemaster provides a square master PNG (path in the answer)", "A typographic «T» icon in the game''s fonts and colours now, independent of decision 77"]', 'Task 683: Trivia.exe now gets ProductName, FileVersion, CompanyName from app/desktop/package.json (electron-builder 26 edits resources in pure JS via resedit; signExecutable: false, no wine, no new dependency). The icon is still Electron''s: the repo has no game icon. Needed: one square master (PNG ≥ 256×256, ideally 1024×1024, legible at 16×16), set as win.icon (electron-builder makes the .ico); the same file can serve Linux and the Steam client icon. Related: decision 77 (capsules and logo, incl. the 184×184 community icon), task 669.', '', 'Derive it from decision 77''s logo / community icon: task 669''s script also renders a 1024×1024 icon (wait for 669)', NULL, '2026-10-13T08:03:05Z', '2026-10-13T16:05:18Z', 683, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 683: 2026-10-14, task 683: game icon = capsules.mjs''s icon-1024.png (amber «?» on night blue), tracked copy app/desktop/icon.png; electron-builder.yml win.icon + linux.icon (Linux: desktop-file targets only, the tar.gz/Steam build has none; Steam client icons uploaded by hand, 17a); Trivia.exe has the icon (16–256 px) and metadata (ProductName/FileDescription «Trivia» via extraMetadata.description, CompanyName/copyright Ruben Moor, FileVersion 0.1.0), unsigned (decision 88). CREDITS.md «Game icon» section (credits.ts, when app/desktop/icon.png exists). B-11 closed; plan 18 and 17a updated. Shipped before decision 172 (Capsules and icon approved?) is answered: an icon fix there means re-render and copy over app/desktop/icon.png.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (88, 'Windows exe resources: electron-builder''s resedit, no wine, unsigned', 'answered', '[]', 'Task 683, B-11: electron-builder 26 edits Trivia.exe''s version info and icon in pure JS (resedit, already its dependency), so no wine and no new npm dependency. signExecutable: false keeps the edit and skips only signing; Steam doesn''t require signed builds. CompanyName and copyright from app/desktop/package.json author; versions from version.', '', 'win.signExecutable: false (not signAndEditExecutable: false)', NULL, '2026-10-13T08:17:05Z', '2026-10-13T08:17:05Z', 683, NULL, 'rule', 683, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (89, 'Steamworks App ID, depot IDs and beta branch entered? (for the first beta upload)', 'pending', '["entered (App ID …, depots windows …, linux …, content …)", "not yet"]', 'Task 681: First beta upload: checklist and decision needs real Steamworks values before it can fill authoring/steam/steam.json.
Not ready yet:
- task 254: write plan: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7) is open; its "values entered" decision doesn''t exist yet. If it adds one, answer either; mark this one irrelevant only if task 681 should be dropped.
- task 650: Package the Steam binding in both builds is open; the upload needs it done.
Needed:
- App ID
- depot IDs: windows, linux, content (one install folder; media in content, plan 89)
- `beta` branch created in Steamworks (App Admin → SteamPipe → Builds); password stays out of files
Answer once these are entered and task 650 is done.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-13T08:17:37Z', NULL, 681, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (90, 'Store requirements, languages and controller flags?', 'answered', '["approve (real-pad run passed: Full controller support)", "approve with Partial controller support (real-pad run failed or not done)", "fix (say what)"]', 'Plan 88 task 3 (task 668). Values in `plans/17a-store-page.md`, "System requirements, languages, controller". Please check and answer.

Requirements (min / recommended, Windows and SteamOS+Linux):
- OS: Windows 10 64-bit / Windows 11; SteamOS 3 or Ubuntu 22.04+ (untested: only NixOS + steam-run so far)
- CPU: 64-bit dual-core 2 GHz / quad-core
- RAM: 4 GB / 8 GB
- GPU: DirectX 11 (Windows) or OpenGL/Vulkan, H.264 video decode / any GPU from 2018 on
- Storage: 3 GB (measured 2.95 GB installed; placeholder until the media bundle, decision 82)
- Network: none; notes: plays offline, 1280×720+, keyboard/mouse/pads, best on a TV
- Unknown to me: what plays smoothly on weaker machines. Only the author''s laptop (i5-12500H, 64 GB) is known. If you have an older/weaker machine that played fine, name it and I lower or keep the minimum.

Languages: English, Spanish - Latin America, Spanish - Spain, German: Interface ✓, Subtitles ✓, Full audio ✗. English and German question pools are not exported yet (decision 80): tick them only once they ship, or accept interface-only for the beta.

Controller:
- Xbox: Full controller support if a real-pad run passes; else Partial. Pad-only result so far: automated (headless, faked pad) whole game start → existing player → every joker → wrong + victory (task 352) and new-player letter picker (plan 46): pass. Real pad: not run yet. Please play one game pad only: start → new player (letter picker; under Steam the floating keyboard) → victory, and say pass/fail.
- PlayStation: supported, PlayStation glyphs shown ✓
- Steam Input API: glyph type only; Gamepad recommended: no
- Field names are from memory (no web access); recheck in Steamworks at entry.', '', 'Provisional values for the store page entry and coming-soon page: requirements as drafted, storage as an estimate (3 GB now, grows with content), languages: interface ✓ for all four, question content for en/de once their pools ship, controller ''Partial'' until the pad-only run passes. Final values are measured on the release candidate (milestone 11), including a test on a Steam Deck (none at hand yet: borrow or buy one).', NULL, '2026-10-13T08:23:08Z', '2026-10-13T16:40:36Z', 668, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 688: task 688: plans/17a-store-page.md requirements marked provisional; controller Partial until the real-pad run; en/de languages interface only (Subtitles ✓ once their pools ship); storage 3 GB estimate (re-measured 2.96 GB, no media bundle yet)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (91, 'Game version: single source of truth', 'answered', '[]', 'electron-builder and trivia-steam (steam.py version()) already read app/desktop/package.json; flake.nix''s app version = builtins.fromJSON of it, the client build gets it via Vite define. One edit bumps every artefact. Plan for task 265 (masterplan 11 part 2).', '', 'app/desktop/package.json version (semver); flake.nix and the client build read it; tag v<version> per release', NULL, '2026-10-13T08:25:04Z', '2026-10-13T08:25:04Z', 265, NULL, 'rule', 265, '2026-10-13, task 693: 2026-10-13, tasks 690, 693: app/desktop/package.json version is the only source; flake.nix (builtins.fromJSON), app/client/vite.config.ts (__APP_VERSION__), electron-builder artifacts/FileVersion and authoring/steam/steam.py version() read it; Credits.svelte shows it via lib/build.ts buildInfo(); plans/18-steam-integration.md Version bullet (bump, tag, semver), README.md; qgen validate checks id continuity against the newest v* tag (task 692); plans/11-steam.md, project.md note S6 part 2 done');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (92, 'Pool version: export hash in pool.json', 'answered', '[]', 'A hash written by qgen export matches the loaded pool everywhere (browser game serves app/data live; a build-time stamp would go stale). Optional field: older engines ignore it, qgen validate''s staleness check covers it. Shown next to the game version (credits, report text). Plan for task 265.', '', 'qgen export writes "hash" (first 8 hex of sha256 over the exported questions) into app/data/pool.json; pool format stays version 1', NULL, '2026-10-13T08:25:04Z', '2026-10-13T08:25:04Z', 265, NULL, 'rule', 265, '2026-10-13, task 693: 2026-10-13, tasks 690, 693: authoring/tools/pool_export.py writes "hash" (8 hex sha256) into every pool*.json, app/data/pool.json re-exported; engine/pool.ts keeps it (null in old pools); credits header «Versión x · preguntas <hash>»; plans/18-steam-integration.md Version bullet');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (93, 'Question reports: where do players send them?', 'answered', '["Pinned Steam discussions thread only", "Thread + an email address shown in the game (give the address)", "Email only (give the address)"]', 'Plan 93 (ST-5): players on Steam have no authoring tools, so a flagged question reaches you only if they send the copied text by hand. The flag list («Preguntas marcadas») will show one line «Envíalas a: …» with a button; the game never makes a request without a click.
- Steam discussions thread: needs the App ID (masterplan 10 part 1); you create and pin it at launch (part 4, task 269). In the game it opens only via the Steam overlay (Windows, decision 70: Steam overlay in the Electron shell); elsewhere (Linux, Deck, browser) the URL is shown as selectable text.
- Email: opens a `mailto:` on click. The address ships in a public game: your personal data, gets spam, permanent once shipped; use a dedicated address. Name it in the answer if you pick 2 or 3.
- Either way the text you receive is pasted into `qgen flag` (task 3 of plan 93).', '', 'Own server endpoint: the game sends a flagged question report on the player''s click to POST /reports (our small server, e.g. Cloudflare Workers + D1), authenticated by a Steam session ticket (valid Steam user, decision 111); qgen flag --pull fetches the reports. Fallback without the server: copy the report text. Details in milestone 11.', NULL, '2026-10-13T09:00:18Z', '2026-10-13T16:21:01Z', 698, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 701: 2026-10-13, task 701: plan 93 done (tasks 699, 859, 700, 860, 1002): app/desktop/report.mjs + main.mjs report:available / report:send (one POST /reports from main, ticket identity trivia-reports, 5 s/10 s timeouts; URL reportUrl in app/desktop/package.json, empty = copy only until plan 103''s server; dev TRIVIA_REPORT_URL with TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1); FlagList.svelte «Copiar» per flag/«Copiar todo» (decision 142 text), «Enviar»/«Enviar todas», privacy confirm, reported_on on the flag (no save bump); qgen flag (pasted text) and qgen flag --pull (token TRIVIA_REPORT_TOKEN or state/report-token, ledger state/reports-pulled.json) → needs_work via authoring/tools/reviews.py. The Steam report thread and e-mail channel are dropped. Docs: plans/11-steam.md ST-5, 13 MD-6, 04, 18 ''Question reports'', README how-tos, authoring/QC.md, AGENTS.md, directory.md, project.md.

2026-10-17, task 869: Plan 103 closed 2026-10-17 (task 869): server live at the workers.dev URL in reportUrl (decision 147); README how-tos for local run, deploy and secret rotation. Open: STEAM_APP_ID, first real-ticket report.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (94, 'Coming soon page live? date?', 'pending', '["live since <date>, release date shown: <Coming Soon|…>", "submitted, Valve returned fixes (list)", "not yet (what blocks)"]', 'ST-3, plan 94. Full rules (Valve docs, read 2026-10-13) and checklist: `plans/11-steam.md` "Coming soon page (ST-3)".

Prerequisites:
- Store page entered (`task 672`''s decision)
- Names per D-50 set: «Living Room Trivia», «Trivia en Familia» (`task 253`)
- Content survey incl. AI disclosure complete (`task 259`)
- App credit paid (note the date: release ≥ 21 days after it)

Checklist:
1. "Mark as ready for review" (store page), ≥ 7 business days before the wanted live date
2. Valve reviews (3–5 business days); fixes go to `17a-store-page.md` / plan 88, survey → part 9, names → part 1
3. Release date display "Coming Soon" (no date) or coarse "Q<n> <year>"
4. "Post as Coming Soon"; note the live date

Earliest release = later of live + 14 days, app fee + 21 days.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-13T09:03:32Z', NULL, 703, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (95, 'Start the launch release candidate v1.0.0?', 'pending', '["go: all preconditions met, release date <date>", "not yet (which)"]', 'Plan 95 (Launch). Answer `go` only when every row below is ✓; the release date you name must be ≥ the earliest release date and leave room for the timeline. Details: `plans/11-steam.md` "Launch (S6)".

**Earliest release date:** not known yet = later of (Coming soon live date + 14 days, app fee paid + 21 days); comes from decision 94 "Coming soon page live? date?" (task 704). Timeline back from the date R: build review submitted ≥ 7 business days before R (Valve''s figure unverified: check partner.steamgames.com/doc/store/review_process); exact date locks at R − 2 weeks; candidate passed ST-4 on `beta` before the review.

## Preconditions (state 2026-10-13)
- [ ] Coming soon page live, earliest release date recorded (ST-3): ✗ decision 94 pending, task 704 open
- [ ] Content target per launch language (decision 21, decision 37): ✗ `qgen export && qgen report --simulate --locale es,en,de` must end ✓ for es, en, de; today es 1136/5000 approved in `app/data/pool.json`, no `pool.en.json` / `pool.de.json`
- [ ] Beta test passed (masterplan 10 part 11): ✗ `task 263` (write plan: Beta test and S5 close-out) open, waits on decisions 66, 67, 82
- [ ] Price and account answered, PUB-11 written: ✗ decisions 66 and 67 pending; `task 194` open
- [ ] Question reports in the build (plan 93): ✗ tasks 699, 700, 701 open, wait on decision 93
- [ ] Deck review timing settled (plan 90): ✗ `task 687` open; if it says "review in S6", the request is a launch-day row
- [ ] Steamworks app and first `beta` upload (SW-7, decision 89): ✗ decision 89 pending
- [ ] No `PLACEHOLDER(` left in `app/`

## Also check before go
- Valve''s rules marked "unverified" in "Launch (S6)" → "Valve''s rules" (build review lead time and checks, launch discount, Release button / scheduled release, announcements): read the linked pages and note anything that changes the timeline in your answer.

## On go
Task 708 bumps `version` to `1.0.0`, fills the question counts in the announcement texts and raises `Release candidate v1.0.0 passed?` with your steps (tag `v1.0.0`, `trivia-steam upload --branch beta`, manual rows, family sign-off).

## Options
- `go: all preconditions met, release date <date>`
- `not yet (which)`: name the missing rows; a new decision follows when they are done.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-13T09:09:01Z', NULL, 706, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (96, 'Content patch cadence after launch?', 'answered', '["monthly, only if ≥ 100 new approved per launch language or a player-reported fix is waiting; hotfixes any time", "every 250 new approved per launch language; hotfixes any time", "quarterly; hotfixes any time"]', 'Plan 96 (ST-5): after launch, new and fixed questions reach players only as Steam patches. How often should a content patch go out?

What one patch costs you (~1 h):
- ST-4 manual rows, content-only variant (`plans/11-steam.md` "Release checklist (ST-4)"): `offline` (installed `beta` build, network off, a game to level 3 that hits new questions) + `signoff` (your OK)
- Answer the `Release candidate v<x> passed?` decision
- Set the BuildID live on `default` by hand in Steamworks
- Post the patch notes as a Steam event from the draft `qgen patch-notes` writes
- Workers do the rest: version bump, notes, release check, upload to `beta` (after you tag)

What players get: new questions per launch language (es, en, de), fixes for reported questions (plan 93: `qgen flag`, `qgen rework` when you ask), dropped broken ones. Saves survive every content patch (plan 91).

Batch throughput today (`qgen report --cost`, 2026-10-13): batch-7: 504 approved for $120.74 (~$0.24/approved); draft average $0.26/approved; en/de: no translation run yet. es still 3966 below its target.

Hotfix (wrong answer, crash): always any time, same path, no cadence wait, in every option.', '', 'monthly, only if ≥ 100 new approved per launch language or a player-reported fix is waiting; hotfixes any time', NULL, '2026-10-13T09:14:13Z', '2026-10-13T16:05:18Z', 711, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 713: 2026-10-14, task 713: plans/11-steam.md new section ''Content updates (ST-5)'' (cadence, patch path in 12 steps, hotfix path, what a patch may not do, empty ''Patch notes'' log; Valve''s update-review and event-type rules unverified: no web access); plans/16-content-target.md Quality bar bullet; README.md ''Send a content patch''; plans/project.md S6 ST-5 content-patches row. First patch: decision ''Start the first content patch?'' (task 714 waits on it).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (97, 'Patch notes: counts only?', 'answered', '[]', 'qgen patch-notes (plan 96, task 712) prints counts per locale and category, never question text, answers or ids: no spoilers for players reading the Steam event, and nothing leaks if OQ-35 (plan 40) makes the pool private.', '', 'counts only (added/fixed/dropped per language and category)', NULL, '2026-10-13T09:17:18Z', '2026-10-13T09:17:18Z', 712, NULL, 'rule', 712, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (98, 'Browser game: corrupt or newer state/game.json', 'answered', '["Mirror D-72: new POST /api/save/backup?kind=corrupt|newer on app/server (moves game.json to state/backup/game-<kind>-<stamp>.json, returns the path); ServerStore.load backs up and starts fresh like FileStore; takeSaveNotice works in the browser too", "Keep as is: the browser game is the gamemaster''s own setup; document in README how to move a broken state/game.json away"]', 'Found by task 540 (code review part 4). The desktop shell backs up a broken or newer save and starts fresh with a notice (D-72, FileStore). The browser game (trivia, ServerStore) has no such path: GET /api/save returns the file as stored (D-67), parseSave throws, ready() fails and the game shows only the English corner line «can''t load the game: …» on every screen until someone moves state/game.json by hand. Checked with a truncated game.json on a temp TRIVIA_STATE. Fixing it changes the /api/save API and server behaviour.', '', '1, plus: the notice says plainly that the corrupt (or newer) game state file was backed up, and names the backup path.', NULL, '2026-10-13T10:18:50Z', '2026-10-13T14:46:06Z', 540, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 724: 2026-10-13, task 724: app/server: POST /api/save/backup?kind=corrupt|newer moves state/game.json to state/backup/game-<kind>-<stamp>.json (save.backup, as app/desktop/save.mjs), replies {path} (absolute), 404 without a file, 400 bad_request for another kind. lib/store.ts: ServerStore and FileStore share TextStore (read text → parseSave; corrupt/newer → backup + notice + emptySave()); takeSaveNotice works in the browser too. Notice texts save.corrupt/save.newer (es, en, de) now say the save file was damaged/newer and backed up to {path}. Docs: D-67 consequence, README, directory.md (state/backup/), code-review.md row fixed. A browser game with a broken game.json no longer fails with «can''t load the game».');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (99, 'Gamemaster menu: keep the joker preset row («Sin límite» ↔ «Como las cartas»)?', 'answered', '["Drop the preset row: the per-joker rows only, like the configure screen (decision 33)", "Keep a preset row, but cycle Estándar ↔ Sin límite (STANDARD_JOKERS instead of CARDS)", "Keep as is"]', 'The gamemaster menu''s jokers column (Overlay.svelte, «Trucos del anfitrión») starts with a preset row: ←/→ or Enter cycles «Sin límite» ↔ «Como las cartas» (CARDS: 4/2/2/2/2); any other budget shows «Personalizado» and goes to «Sin límite». Decision 33 dropped presets on the configure screen (no Sin límite / Como las cartas / Estándar picker; default STANDARD_JOKERS 3/1/1/1/1). So a fresh gamemaster game shows «Personalizado» and the menu can''t go back to the standard set; per-joker rows below already edit uses left (decision 34). Found by task 545 (code review).', '', 'Own rule: joker presets exist only before a game starts.
- «Como las cartas» (CARDS 4/2/2/2/2) goes everywhere: no preset, constant or string.
- Pre-game configuration (configure screen, also «Personalizar partida»): presets Estándar (STANDARD_JOKERS) | Sin límite (every joker ∞) | Personalizado (one input per joker); picking a preset fills the inputs, editing an input shows Personalizado.
- Gamemaster menu during a game: no presets, no preset row; just one input per joker (uses left).', NULL, '2026-10-13T10:50:34Z', '2026-10-13T14:40:09Z', 545, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 727: task 727: gamemaster menu (Overlay.svelte) has no joker preset row any more, only the per-joker rows (uses left); CARDS («Como las cartas», 4/2/2/2/2) removed from engine/choice.ts, engine/game.ts, lib/api.ts; catalog keys overlay.jokers/preset/unlimited/cards/custom removed (es, en, de); plans/04-ui-tv-display.md and plans/13-game-modes.md specs say no preset row. Pre-game presets (Estándar | Sin límite | Personalizado): task 746.

2026-10-13, task 746: task 746: pre-game joker presets: game/jokers.ts PRESETS/presetOf/stepPreset; preset row «Conjunto» (Estándar | Sin límite | Personalizado) above the joker rows on the configure screen (Choice.svelte) and in «Personalizar partida» (Customize.svelte, its «Estándar» reset button and customize.reset dropped, standard prop gone); strings configure.preset/presets.* (es, en, de); plans/04 and plans/13 specs updated. UI only, engine/save unchanged.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (100, 'Release check header: hash of every shipped pool?', 'answered', '["List every shipped pool: ''pools es fa9887b5, en …'' in the md header; pool_hashes {locale: hash} in the json (pool_hash kept for es); parse the JSON instead of the regex", "Keep es only (pool.json) as today"]', 'trivia-release-check''s header (release-check.md, release-check.json pool_hash) lists only app/data/pool.json''s hash (regex over its first 1000 chars), while Credits shows the hash of the game''s own locale pool (pool.<locale>.json, decision 92). With locale pools shipped, the header can''t be matched against a tester''s Credits screen. Found by task 722, logged by task 720 (code-review.md Part 6).', '', 'List every shipped pool: ''pools es fa9887b5, en …'' in the md header; pool_hashes {locale: hash} in the json (pool_hash kept for es); parse the JSON instead of the regex', NULL, '2026-10-13T11:43:12Z', '2026-10-13T14:47:29Z', 720, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 729: authoring/steam/release_check.py pools(): every app/data/pool*.json parsed as JSON (pool.json = es, null hash if absent); console and release-check.md header ''pools es <hash>, en <hash>, …''; release-check.json gains pool_hashes {locale: hash}, pool_hash stays (es); the regex over pool.json''s first 1000 chars is gone (task 729)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (101, 'qgen.py stays one module (code review part 7)', 'answered', '[]', 'Task 566 (plan 79) judged the 4100-line module after tasks 557-565. A split would touch every importer (health.py, authoring/server/main.py, spot_checks.py use 17 qgen.* names), bin/qgen in flake.nix, directory.md and throw-away scripts that stub qgen.claude; sections share helpers (load_json, save_json, claude, run_dir, natural_key, write_report) and workers navigate by grep and section markers. The real structural cost is the health.py <-> qgen.py cycle (13 local ''import health''); revisit a split (core helpers + claude() in one module both import) only if that cycle or the file size starts causing bugs.', '', 'Keep authoring/tools/qgen.py as one file with accurate section markers; no qgen/ package or sibling-module split for now', NULL, '2026-10-13T12:29:36Z', '2026-10-13T12:29:36Z', 566, NULL, 'rule', 566, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (102, 'Game flags from a translated game: whose review do they change?', 'answered', '["Flags record the question language (locale) of the game; apply_flags reviews the translation (questions.<locale>.json, re-export pool.<locale>.json) for en/de and the source for es; old flags without locale stay on the source", "Keep flags on the source; the feedback names the game''s language only if known (no format change); the gamemaster moves it by hand", "Keep as is"]', 'Found by task 573 (code review part 9). A flag in the save is keyed by question id only ({flagged_on, player, level?, note?}, decision 60); it has no locale. trivia-authoring''s apply_flags (authoring/server/main.py) turns every flag into a human needs_work review of the Spanish source. A flag raised in an English or German game (a bad translation, a wrong word) therefore pulls the source out of every language''s pool (needs_work is not exported; translations.plays needs an approved source), and the translation itself stays approved. Changing this changes the save format (engine/save.ts, save.py, save_file.py, desktop save) and apply_flags.', '', '1, plus: a flag also stores the question text as the player saw it (the translated text in that game''s language: question, answer options/answer), so a flag still makes sense after the question was changed; apply_flags shows that text with the flag.', NULL, '2026-10-13T13:00:45Z', '2026-10-13T14:46:07Z', 573, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 736: 2026-10-13, task 736: save flags gain optional locale (the game''s question locale, absent = es) and shown {question, answer, wrong_answers} (FlagEntry/FlagText in engine/state.ts, setFlag in engine/save.ts, filled by lib/api.ts from the game''s EngineData); no save version bump (additive, optional fields). «Preguntas marcadas» and Copiar show the stored text and the locale. apply_flags (authoring/server/main.py): en/de flag → human needs_work review of questions.<locale>.json + pool.<locale>.json re-export, es/absent → source as before, unknown locale or translation → stderr; feedback «Marcada en el juego (player, date[, locale]): note · Vista: «…» Respuesta: «…»; otras: …». No longer holds: every game flag lands on the Spanish source. Python game server save.py untouched (decision 104). Docs: 08-review-tool.md, decisions.md D-47, main.py and save_file.py docstrings.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (103, 'Start page Game readiness: which bundles does the supply count?', 'answered', '["Count the default game: first base bundle only (pass bundles to supply.ts in overview.py and qgen report), page text says so", "Keep every bundle (upper bound), only reword the start page text", "Two tables: base only and every bundle"]', 'The authoring start page''s ''Game readiness'' table (authoring/server/overview.py supply → authoring/tools/supply.ts) counts candidates per level with every bundle on (supply.ts default). Since decision 33/51 a fresh game plays the locale''s first base bundle only; non-base bundles (colombia) are off by default. So the table overstates the default game''s supply by the non-base questions; qgen report uses the same default. Found by task 578 (code review part 9).', '', '1: count the default game (first base bundle only); the table is purely informative (target 5000 questions anyway).', NULL, '2026-10-13T13:19:07Z', '2026-10-13T14:46:07Z', 578, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 739: 2026-10-13, task 739: supply.ts defaults to the default game (young_teens, es''s first base bundle via bundlesFor) instead of every bundle and returns the bundles it counted; /api/overview supply gains bundles, its unseen/seen_once/seen_twice count only those bundles (Overview.supply.bundles in types.ts); start page ''Game readiness'' and qgen report''s supply line name the default game and its bundle; ''every bundle'' no longer holds for either');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (104, 'Python ↔ Node/TS twins: how to keep save, media cache and serving rules in sync', 'answered', '["Parity check in qgen validate: a step feeds fixed vectors (every pool URL + edge URLs, a Range grid, v2/v3/v4 sample saves) to the Python functions and, through one Node script under authoring/tools (like supply.ts, D-60), to the TS/Node ones; any difference fails validate, which runs before every commit (D-73). No new dependency, no format change.", "Shared JSON constants file (e.g. app/data/rules.json: MAX_BYTES, retries, save LISTS per version, MIME table) loaded by both sides; covers constants only, not the hash/extension rule or the upgrades.", "Won''t fix, documented: keep the cross-reference comments; the parity table in code-review.md part 10 is the record."]', 'Task 582 (code review part 10) listed the rules that exist twice across languages and checked them with a throw-away script (2026-10-13): all match today for every real input.
- media cache name (D-17): `app/server/media_cache.py` `cache_path` ↔ `app/desktop/resolve.mjs` `cacheName` (sha1[:16] + lowercased ext, else `.bin`): 1146 pool URLs identical
- pool URL set: `media_cache.pool_urls`/`picked` ↔ `resolve.mjs` `poolUrls` (also `stage-media.mjs`): identical (1102)
- single `Range`: `http_base.py` `parse_range` ↔ `resolve.mjs` `parseRange`: 60/60 cases identical
- save envelope + atomic write: `app/server/save.py` `check`/`write` ↔ `app/desktop/save.mjs` `envelope`/`write` (10 MB, tmp + fsync + replace, 10 × 100 ms lock retry)
- save upgrades v2→v3→v4: `engine/save.ts` `UPGRADES` ↔ `authoring/tools/save_file.py` `_seen_blocked`/`flags` (live: the family''s state/game.json is still v2): seen counts, blocked, flags identical on v2/v3/v4 samples and the real save
- MIME: `mimetypes` ↔ desktop `MIME` table (only `.wav` audio/x-wav vs audio/wav; both play)
Nothing checks them automatically; each side has a comment pointing to the other. A format bump (SAVE_VERSION) or a changed cache-name rule must touch both.', '', '3: won''t fix. Leave the Python side alone; it will be retired soon (the Node/TS side becomes the only one).', NULL, '2026-10-13T13:41:28Z', '2026-10-13T14:46:07Z', 582, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 741: Task 741 (2026-10-14): no parity check (not in qgen validate); code-review.md `### Python ↔ Node/TS parity` rows all ''won''t fix (decision 104)'' with the Python paths as now (authoring/tools/media_cache.py, http_base.py, paths.py, save_file.py, moved there by task 764); the save-write twin app/server/save.py (envelope check, atomic write) goes with task 765 and is no longer kept in step with app/desktop/save.mjs; cross-reference comments (resolve.mjs parseRange/poolUrls, engine/state.ts SAVE_VERSION) name the authoring/tools files. Rules that still hold by convention only: cache name (D-17), pool URL set, Range parsing, save upgrades v2→v4 in save_file.py ↔ engine/save.ts.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (105, 'Joker steppers: one rule on the configure screen too?', 'answered', '["One rule everywhere: 0–9 then ∞, clamped (stepUses on the configure screen too; JOKER_MAX goes)", "One rule everywhere: 0–99 then ∞, wrapping", "Keep both: the configure screen sets up a whole game, more range is useful there"]', 'Gamemaster configure screen (Choice.svelte stepJoker): 0–99 then ∞, wrapping both ways (JOKER_MAX). «Personalizar partida» (Customize.svelte) and the gamemaster menu (Overlay.svelte): 0–9 then ∞, clamped (game/jokers.ts stepUses, task 584). Customize''s header says it works ''like the overlay''s budget''; the configure screen differs. Found by part 5 (code-review.md), handed to task 584.', '', 'One rule everywhere: 0–9 then ∞, clamped (stepUses on the configure screen too; JOKER_MAX goes)', NULL, '2026-10-13T14:19:31Z', '2026-10-13T14:46:07Z', 584, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 742: 2026-10-14, task 742: Choice.svelte stepJoker now calls stepUses (jokers.ts); JOKER_MAX (99) and the 0–99 wrapping are gone: every joker stepper (configure screen, Customize, gamemaster menu) is 0–9 then ∞, clamped (← stops at 0, → at ∞, ← from ∞ = 9). A saved budget above 9 shows as is; any step from it lands on 9 or ∞. plans/04 and plans/13 updated; code-review.md cluster 26 row closed.

2026-10-15, task 742: Correction to the line above: a saved count above 9 goes to ∞ on either ←/→ (stepUses clamps the index to 10), not to 9.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (106, 'Adopt ESLint + typescript-eslint for no-floating-promises? (code review part 10)', 'answered', '["No: keep the five tsconfig flags only; promise handling stays a review item", "Yes, narrow: ESLint + typescript-eslint + eslint-plugin-svelte with only no-floating-promises/no-misused-promises, inside npm run check, existing hits fixed or marked void", "Yes, broad: recommendedTypeChecked with the rules task 616 found noisy turned off"]', 'Task 617 re-checked task 616''s linter evaluation against parts 2–9 (`### Linter evaluation`, `code-review.md`).
- 115 `(lint: …)` tags; 47 bug rows touch TS/Svelte/.mjs. 4 bug rows name a rule, the rest `(lint: none)` or no tag (races, state, locale).
- Real bugs a linter catches: 1. `JokerFlight.svelte` floating `flight.finished.then(…)` (task 548, low): ESLint `no-floating-promises` flags it on the pre-fix code (trial in /tmp). The rule''s fix (`.catch`) silences the AbortError only; the real defect (timer not cleared on unmount) was found by review.
- Missed: `app/desktop/main.mjs` `app.whenReady().then(start)` (task 554, medium): untyped in `.mjs` (`app` is `any`), not flagged; would need a tsconfig with `checkJs` + electron types.
- Noise: same trial, 41 other no-floating/misused-promises hits in `app/client/src`; the review ruled each won''t fix (async functions catch their own errors).
- Biome, oxlint: no bug caught (no type info). JokerCards `PAGE` bug: only `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` (~300 errors, rejected by task 616).
- Cost: ESLint + typescript-eslint + eslint-plugin-svelte = 132 packages in `package-lock.json` (minimal-dependencies rule, `npmDepsHash`), ~6 s per run.
- Recommended: no. 1 low bug among 42 hits does not pay for 132 packages.', '', 'No: keep the five tsconfig flags only; promise handling stays a review item', NULL, '2026-10-13T14:30:26Z', '2026-10-13T15:45:13Z', 617, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 744: No linter dependency added: no eslint.config.mjs, no ESLint packages in package-lock.json; npm run check stays tsc/svelte-check with the five tsconfig flags; floating/misused promises are a review item, not a check. task 744: Adopt ESLint no-floating-promises (per decision 106) dropped; code-review.md ### Linter evaluation records the answer.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (107, 'Licence (OQ-35): which licence for the code and for the questions?', 'answered', '["Code MIT; questions all rights reserved (personal, non-commercial play from the repo allowed): LICENSE + LICENSE-content.md", "Code MIT; questions CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "Code GPL-3.0 with a Steamworks linking exception; questions all rights reserved", "Code MIT; questions CC BY-SA 4.0 (anyone may resell them)", "Everything all rights reserved (as today, stated in a LICENSE)"]', 'OQ-35, plan 40. Public repo, no `LICENSE`: today all rights reserved. Game is paid, $9.99 one-time, bundles free DLC, Workshop/modding later (decision 66: Price model (OQ-33)). Not legal advice.

At stake (qgen report, 2026-10-13): 1,136 approved questions (base 1,034, colombia 102), es only; en/de translations not started. Each with hint, explanation, media picks: the paid generation work.

Never covered by any repo licence: media (own licence per file, plan 26, PUB-2), fonts (OFL, `app/client/public/fonts/OFL-*.txt`), UI audio (`CREDITS.md`), npm deps.

Facts
- No licence on GitHub: others may view and fork on GitHub (ToS D.5), nothing else (docs.github.com "Licensing a repository"; choosealicense.com/no-permission)
- MIT: anyone may reuse, sell, ship a closed fork; only keep the notice (opensource.org/license/mit)
- GPL-3.0: anyone may build and redistribute (also sell) the game, must pass on source under GPL (gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0). Steamworks SDK (decision 28: steamworks-ffi-node) is proprietary: GPL needs our own linking exception (FSF GPL FAQ "GPLIncompatibleLibs")
- AGPL-3.0: adds a network clause; meaningless for an offline game
- CC BY-SA 4.0: anyone may copy and resell the questions with credit and same licence (creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0)
- CC BY-NC(-SA) 4.0: copying and sharing allowed, commercial use not (creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0); "NC" is fuzzy at the edges
- Facts aren''t protected; a selection/arrangement and the wording of hints and explanations can be (US: Feist v. Rural, 1991; EU: Directive 96/9/EC, plus sui-generis database right for substantial investment)
- AI drafted, human reviewed: US Copyright Office (Part 2 report, Jan 2025; Thaler v. Perlmutter, D.C. Cir. 2025): AI output alone not protectable, human selection/editing can be; EU: "author''s own intellectual creation" (Infopaq). Uncertain: professional check (PUB-10)
- The shipped game holds `pool.json` in plain JSON: every buyer can read it; only the licence forbids reuse
- Licence grants are irrevocable for the versions they come with; commits public without licence stay unlicensed (copies exist, no rights granted)

Trade-offs
- MIT code: the value is the content, not the code; easy for modders and Workshop (decision 66); a closed fork still needs its own questions
- Questions reserved: forbids reselling the pool; personal play from a clone allowed by a line in `LICENSE-content.md`
- NC-SA: friendlier, but anyone may host a free copy of the pool
- GPL: blocks closed forks, but an exception for Steamworks, and anyone may legally sell the full game if the pool is GPL too

Effect on the build: none for any option (`LICENSE`, `LICENSE-content.md` copied into `result/` and the desktop builds; credits get a "Game" section, PUB-2).

Questions for a lawyer (gamemaster''s country + US)
- Is the AI-drafted, human-reviewed pool protectable (copyright, database right)? Does our review count as authorship?
- Wording of "all rights reserved, personal play allowed" for the questions next to MIT code in one public repo
- Anthropic terms: commercial use of outputs under the plan the pipeline runs on (PUB-10)
- Any implied licence for forks of the unlicensed commits?', '', 'Code MIT; questions all rights reserved (personal, non-commercial play from the repo allowed): LICENSE + LICENSE-content.md', NULL, '2026-10-13T14:59:13Z', '2026-10-13T15:45:14Z', 198, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 199: 2026-10-14, task 199: D-102 in plans/decisions.md (code MIT incl. modding/, questions reserved with personal play, lawyer checks owed); OQ-35 resolved (open-questions.md, 11-steam.md, project.md); 17-publishing.md licence section decided; PUB-4 stays open for task 200

2026-10-14, task 200: 2026-10-14, task 200: LICENSE (plain MIT text, GitHub-detectable; Copyright 2026 Ruben Moor), LICENSE-content.md (questions reserved: authoring/data/, app/data/, packs; personal non-commercial play and GitHub forks allowed; modding/ MIT; media, fonts, sounds, npm deps excluded); both at the desktop artefact root (electron-builder.yml extraFiles), app/desktop/package.json license MIT; credits ''Game'' section lists both (credits.ts strips a leading ''#'' from the title); README ''License'', directory.md rows; PUB-4 [x]');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (108, 'Is release content public (OQ-35)?', 'answered', '["Whole repo public, release content included (D-17 stays; the licence protects it)", "Public code + today''s pool; release content (new batches, translations, bundles) in a private submodule", "Whole repo private before release"]', 'OQ-35, plan 40; goes with decision 107 (licence). D-17: "the source code and the question pool are public". Release content = new batches, en/de translations (decision 26), bundles shipped as free DLC (decision 66). Today: 1,136 approved es questions public; no translations yet.

Facts
- Every buyer gets `pool.json` in plain JSON; a private repo only hides content from non-buyers, the licence (decision 107) is what forbids reuse
- What is public now stays copyable: clones and forks exist, whatever licence applied to those commits stays
- Public repo with the full pool: anyone with Node/Nix can build and play the full game free; Steam buyers pay for convenience, Steam features, updates

Options
1. Whole repo public (D-17 stays). Build unchanged. Simplest; open for modders and Workshop (decision 66). Cost: the full translated pool is free to anyone who builds from source.
2. Public code + current pool; release content in a private repo as a git submodule (e.g. `content/`). D-17 amended (pool public up to a cut-off). `qgen` and `qgen export` read/write the submodule; `nix build .#app` needs `?submodules=1` and access to the private repo, else builds with the public pool only; `trivia-desktop-build` and `trivia-release-check` need the submodule checked out. Two repos to commit, pm workers need access. Backlog row, S4/S5.
3. Whole repo private before release. D-17 superseded; existing clones keep the current state. No build change. Ends public code: no outside contributors, modding docs must live elsewhere.', '', 'Whole repo public, release content included (D-17 stays; the licence protects it)', NULL, '2026-10-13T14:59:23Z', '2026-10-13T15:45:14Z', 198, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 199: 2026-10-14, task 199: D-102: whole repo public, release content included, D-17 confirmed; no private content repo, no backlog row

2026-10-14, task 200: 2026-10-14, task 200: nothing to change: no private content repo; LICENSE-content.md covers the public pool and release content in the repo and in builds');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (109, 'Task 751 (packs as optional installs) done: can task 748 (DLC depots) run?', 'answered', '["task 751 done, run task 748", "packs dropped, drop task 748"]', 'task 748: DLC depots for packs needs task 751: Packs as optional installs (plan 98) done first: per-pack pool files under app/data/bundles/<id>/ and a per-pack media key list. pm has no task-to-task dependency, so task 748 waits on this decision. Answer once task 751 is done.', '', 'task 751 done, run task 748', NULL, '2026-10-13T15:02:57Z', '2026-10-13T15:45:13Z', 748, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-13, task 748: 2026-10-13, task 748: DLC depot per pack: authoring/steam/steam.json dlc {colombia: {appid, depot}} (null until SW-7); trivia-steam stage stages app/desktop/build/dlc/<id>/ (resources/data/bundles/<id>/ + build/pack-media.json media) and checks packs in the build = pack-media.json = steam.json dlc and all depots = each archive; OS depots exclude the pack data, content its media; --depots takes W,L,C then packs; dry-run placeholders 481… per depot; smoke.mjs runs a second time without the packs'' files and checks the offered packs (shell --lang=es); D-95, plan 18 ''Builds and depots''');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (110, 'Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)', 'answered', '["1) all recommended (a1 b1 c1 d1)", "2) other (write e.g. a2 mexico, b1, c1, d2)"]', 'RG-5 (plans/15c-regional-questions.md) with OQ-46 folded in (plan 98, task 749). Which question packs (non-base bundles) the Steam release ships, in which languages, on by default or not, and where `colombia` questions sit in the taxonomy. Packs ship as free optional DLC (decision 66: Price model (OQ-33)); packs have no content target of their own (decision 37).

Answer format: one letter-number per question, e.g. "a1 b1 c1 d1"; for a2 name the packs ("a2 mexico").

## Facts (2026-10-13)
- `colombia`: 102 approved / 109 total (7 rejected).
- `colombia` questions on a `base` subcategory: 19, all approved. Historia 3, Piratas 2, Desiertos 2, Navidad 2, Mundiales de fútbol 2; one each: Aves, Cuentos infantiles, Literatura, Islas, Reciclaje, Árboles, Deportes extremos, Museos.
  - Historia: q-0009 Grito de Independencia (año), q-0011 batalla de 1819, q-0107 país separado en 1903
  - Piratas: q-0184 murallas (Cartagena), q-0580 fuerte NO en el Caribe colombiano
  - Desiertos: q-0229 dunas de Taroa, q-0282 desierto colombiano (foto)
  - Navidad: q-0256 gozos de la novena, q-0297 día de la Novena de Aguinaldos
  - Mundiales de fútbol: q-0540 golazo de James, q-0541 Linda Caicedo
  - q-0036 Aves (especies en Colombia), q-0111 Cuentos infantiles (El renacuajo paseador), q-0119 Literatura (María, Isaacs), q-0168 Islas (Gorgona), q-0265 Reciclaje (caneca colombiana), q-0272 Árboles (palma, foto), q-0378 Deportes extremos (municipio colombiano), q-0393 Museos (Balsa Muisca)
- Cost (`qgen report --cost`, plan 70): drafting $0.26 per approved (batch-5..7) × (1 + overhead 0.70) ≈ $0.44 → a 100-question pack ≈ $26 direct, ≈ $44 with overhead. Translating 100: no measured rate yet (no tr-en-*/tr-de-* run merged); a translation pass (translate + rate + review, no drafting) should cost well under drafting, order $10–20 per 100 per language, to be measured by the first tr-* runs.
- Simulation es, games until the first repeat (median strong/typical; 40 seeds, solo; information only):
  - kids: base 7.5/11, base+colombia 8/10.5
  - young_teens: base 10/17.5, base+colombia 10/17.5
  - young_adults: base 10/25, base+colombia 10.5/22.5
  - adults: base 10.5/19.5, base+colombia 11/22.5
  - → `colombia` (102 questions vs. 1034 approved base) barely changes supply; it is flavour, not supply.

## Questions (recommended option first)
- (a) Packs at launch:
  - a1: `colombia` only. It exists and is reviewed; new Spanish packs `mexico`/`argentina` after launch; en/de packs left to Workshop/modding (decision 66).
  - a2: plus new packs before launch (name them). Each needs `qgen bundle new` + taxonomy approval + batches (≈ $44 per 100 approved).
- (b) Languages of `colombia`:
  - b1: es only. Its point is the Colombian connection and voice (decision 27: Spanish variety); es-ES players see it too.
  - b2: also translated to en/de. Needs `qgen batch --translate --bundle`, re-rating for a Colombian-connected player.
- (c) Default on:
  - c1: off on the configure screen for every locale (decision 33, unchanged); the family''s save and old games keep D-85''s es default (base + colombia, D-59).
  - c2: on for es.
- (d) OQ-46: subcategories of `colombia` questions:
  - d1: `colombia` questions use `colombia` subcategories. «Cambiazo» on «Historia» shouldn''t serve a Colombian question when a base category was picked; new subcategories e.g. «Historia de Colombia», «Fútbol colombiano», «Navidad en Colombia», the 19 above move there (qgen migration step, `validate` rule).
  - d2: keep as is.', '', '- (a) Regional bundles, 2000 approved questions each. Pilot: grow colombia from 102 to 2000 and measure the effort ($ per approved via qgen report --cost; gamemaster QC time per 100 from the review tool''s timestamps). Whether more regional bundles ship at launch is decided after the pilot, in a new decision with the measured numbers (candidates mexico, argentina). Launch does not wait for the pilot: it ships what colombia has then; updates bring the rest.
- (b) Every regional bundle in its region''s language plus English (colombia: es + en).
- (c) c1: off by default on the configure screen; the family''s save keeps base + colombia.
- (d) Every bundle has its own categories and subcategories (bundle-scoped taxonomy); the 19 colombia questions on base subcategories move to colombia''s own. Names may repeat verbatim across bundles (e.g. «Historia» in base and in colombia): that''s fine, they are still separate entries of their bundle.
- Shipped as free DLC (visibility on Steam, smaller base download), decision 66.', NULL, '2026-10-13T15:05:25Z', '2026-10-13T15:54:53Z', 749, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 750: 2026-10-14, task 750: D-99 in plans/decisions.md (D-43, D-53, D-84 marked amended by D-99); 15c RG-5 [x]; OQ-46 resolved; 22-bundles.md, project.md, 16-content-target.md notes; qgen report --simulate defaults --bundles to the locale''s first base bundle (packs off, base for es/en/de).

2026-10-14, task 826: 2026-10-14, task 826: bundle-scoped taxonomy in code (D-100): categories.py key/broad_of/category_of by (bundle, name), bundle_of gone; concepts, draft, report, saturation, validate (uniqueness within a bundle), patch notes, media take the bundle; engine subKey/catKey (base bare name, else <bundle>/<name>) for Cambiazo, Bájale, purge, draw categories, exhausted; names files keyed per bundle; Cambiazo view carries key; review/stats pages filter by bundle and tag repeated names. The 19 colombia questions on base subcategories pass validate until task 827 but have no broad category meanwhile.

2026-10-14, task 828: 2026-10-14, task 828: targets.json colombia 2000 (base''s mix scaled, targets.scaled); validate requires an entry per kind:region bundle; qgen bundle new --kind region writes it; qgen report --bundle colombia [--locale en] and --bundle drafting use it (D-101).

2026-10-16, task 643: 2026-10-15, task 643: colombia pilot chain started (plan 84 chain 4): first es pair task 1295 (run colombia batch) + task 1296 (QC colombia batch), -110; the QC records the first effort numbers in plans/15c, adds the next es pair until 2000 es, then the pilot-effort task and the first en pair. ''More bundles only after a new decision with the pilot''s numbers'' no longer holds (milestone 9, 2026-10-15): chain 5 (usa, germany, uk, spain, mexico) starts after this chain''s first QC.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (111, 'Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy', 'answered', '[]', 'Gamemaster, 2026-10-13, while answering decisions 66/100. Plans still carried a browser game bridge (D-59: Python server + browser ''until the Steam build replaces it'', never dated), plan 10''s ''without Steam the game behaves like S3'', and ''without Steam'' rows in plans 85, 86, 87, 93 and decisions 39, 72. The code is public and the game runs offline, so nothing can be enforced hard; the Steam integration itself is the incentive to buy.', '', 'Steam only.
- Effort goes only into the Steam build (Windows, Linux/SteamOS/Deck, launched by Steam). If it also works outside Steam: fine, but no work, checks, fixes or docs for that. No ''without Steam'' rows in checklists or done-whens.
- No DRM code (no restartAppIfNecessary, no anti-tamper): costs nothing and the code is public anyway.
- Buying on Steam is incentivized by the Steam integration:
  - Saves need a valid Steam user (steam.available and a non-zero SteamID; save per user, Steam Cloud). Without one the game plays but nothing persists (memory-only save), with a short notice that progress needs Steam.
  - Flagging questions needs a valid Steam user too; without one the flag action is hidden.
  - Enforcement is soft: a check of the Steam bridge in the shell, nothing more (patchable, that''s accepted). Dev runs and agent checks get an explicit dev switch so they keep working.
  - Eventually online co-op (Steam networking); not planned yet.
- Supersedes D-59''s bridge (plans/decisions.md) and plan 10''s ''without Steam behaves like S3'' rule. Fallbacks that also serve under Steam stay (e.g. letter picker in desktop mode).', NULL, '2026-10-13T15:09:01Z', '2026-10-13T15:09:01Z', NULL, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 781: 2026-10-13, task 781: plan 87: Steam Cloud saves (tasks 779-781): app/desktop/main.mjs saves only for a valid Steam user: save/<steamid64>/game.json, dev switch without a SteamID TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR or save/dev/game.json (decision 114); no valid user → no save file or folder, save:* refused, --import-save exits 1; lib/engine.ts ready() picks FileStore by validUser, else MemoryStore (memory-only, one dismissable notice save.unsaved «Sin Steam no se guarda el progreso» per start); flag icon, M key, pad Select and «Preguntas marcadas» hidden without a valid user. Gone: save/local/, the S3 migration (migrateToLocal), save:local-offer/save:adopt-local and LocalProgress.svelte («Usar el progreso de este equipo»). Docs: plans/18-steam-integration.md Steam Cloud bullet and ''Steam Cloud test'' table (local/ and ''no question'' rows dropped, ''Steam not running'' row added, listing row names dev/), D-72, plans/12-client-engine.md Store, README.md, directory.md. Decision 75 ''Steam Cloud test passed?'' still lists the old local/ row: plan 18''s revised table is what counts.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (112, 'Pack layout: a pool file per bundle (optional install)', 'answered', '[]', 'decision 66 (bundles as free DLC, optional install) needs a pack to be a separate file set a DLC depot can carry. D-94 in plans/decisions.md.', '', 'Each non-base bundle''s questions in app/data/bundles/<id>/pool[.<locale>].json; base''s pool keeps base only; a missing pack file = pack not offered in that locale (stored choices fall back to defaults); build/pack-media.json lists media only a pack uses', NULL, '2026-10-13T15:11:54Z', '2026-10-13T15:11:54Z', 751, NULL, 'rule', 751, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (113, 'SW-8 check under Steam (replaces decision 72)', 'pending', '["all pass", "issues (name the rows)"]', 'Gamemaster check for plan 85 (Steamworks binding, SW-8). Replaces decision 72: same check without its "Without Steam" rows (decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam), plus the valid-user row (task 776). Answer decision 72 as "replaced by this decision", not irrelevant (that would drop tasks 685–687).

Needs task 650''s packaged builds (`trivia-desktop-build` → app/desktop/release/) and the Steamworks SDK libs (decision 68). App ID 480 (Spacewar) until SW-7: launch through Steam as a non-Steam shortcut with `SteamAppId=480` (or `TRIVIA_STEAM_APPID=480`), or under the real App ID. stderr shows `trivia: steam available, app …, user …, language …`.

Valid user:
- logged-in Steam user: stderr shows the user as valid; the game saves (quit, restart, player still there)

Overlay (Windows zip only; Linux has none by design, D-92):
- Shift+Tab opens the overlay and closes it again
- a video and an audio question play smoothly with sound; animations not choppy
- F11 toggles fullscreen; the overlay still opens afterwards
- keyboard and pad still reach the game after closing the overlay

On-screen keyboard (Big Picture on Linux or Windows, or the Deck; a pad):
- Player screen, focus the name field, A (or «Escribir»): Steam''s floating keyboard opens near the field
- typed letters appear in the field; its Enter submits the name
- desktop Steam (not Big Picture): A opens the letter picker as before

Glyphs (under Steam, desktop or Big Picture):
- one DualShock/DualSense: pressing a button shows PlayStation glyphs (prompt chips, answer tiles)
- an Xbox pad or the Deck: Xbox glyphs; one PS + one Xbox pad: Xbox
- pads still work in the game at all (Steam Input on)

Language (fresh save: delete or move this user''s save/game.json first):
- Steam''s language German → first-start screen preselects Deutsch/Deutsch; Spanish – Spain → es-ES/es; Spanish – Latin America → es/es
- an existing save keeps its language

On failure name the failing rows; the worker adds follow-ups in plan 85 (drop the Windows overlay, switch to ShowGamepadTextInput, drop Steam Input, or fix the valid-user check).', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-13T15:25:03Z', NULL, 775, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (114, 'Desktop save folder under the dev switch without a SteamID', 'answered', '[]', 'decision 111 drops plan 87''s local/ folder; TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER (plan 85) needs a fixed folder when no SteamID exists. dev/ keeps dev saves apart from real Steam users'' folders and outside Auto-Cloud''s {64BitSteamID} path. Plan 87.', '', 'TRIVIA_SAVE_DIR if set, else <save base>/dev/game.json; no valid user → no save file at all', NULL, '2026-10-13T15:28:12Z', '2026-10-13T15:28:12Z', 771, NULL, 'rule', 771, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (115, 'Screen gallery: how does trivia-gallery drive a browser?', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan for part 13 of plan 9 (task 796). Decision 6''s throw-away Playwright already worked for plans 21, 23, 69 walks, but the gallery must be re-runnable by the gamemaster with one command. A flake wrapper (fromCheckout, authoring/tools/gallery.py) pins the same nixpkgs packages, so no npm devDependency, no download at run time, offline; dev shell only, never shipped. Known quirk from decision 6: unset LD_LIBRARY_PATH for the browser (dev shell''s alsa-lib vs the browser''s glibc).', '', 'nixpkgs Playwright (python3 playwright + playwright-driver.browsers) in a flake wrapper trivia-gallery, like qgen''s pinned tools; nothing in package.json', NULL, '2026-10-13T15:40:34Z', '2026-10-13T15:40:34Z', 796, NULL, 'rule', 796, '2026-10-13, task 796: 2026-10-13, task 796: plan 100 (UI wording: style guides, TV-check fixes, screen gallery) builds trivia-gallery this way (task 4 of its split).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (116, 'Store media: render screenshots and trailer now?', 'pending', '["go: UI final, render now", "not yet (say what''s missing)"]', 'Plan 88 (decisions 79, 80): store screenshots and trailers render late: after milestone 9''s UI wording fixes (plan 100) and UI translations (plan 69), right before the store page goes to Valve''s review; nothing rendered or approved before that. The scripts are built earlier (authoring/store/screenshots.mjs, trivia-trailer). Answer when the UI wording and translations are final and the store page is about to go to review; the render task then renders es/es-ES (7 shots + trailer) and en/de (5 menu shots), and asks for approval. en/de question shots and trailers additionally wait for their pools (decision 80).', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-13T17:00:10Z', NULL, 842, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (117, 'Report server tooling: wrangler from nixpkgs in the flake?', 'answered', '["wrangler from nixpkgs (pkgs.wrangler, 4.141 in our pin) in a flake wrapper trivia-report-server; nothing in any package.json; Worker types written by hand (no @cloudflare/workers-types)", "npx wrangler@<pinned> from the wrapper (downloads from npm at first run, not pinned by the flake lock)", "wrangler + @cloudflare/workers-types as devDependencies of a report-server/ npm workspace"]', 'Plan "Report server (POST /reports)" (masterplan 11 part 8, decision 93: Question reports: where do players send them?) runs a Cloudflare Worker + D1. Deploying, running it locally (`wrangler dev --local`: Miniflare + local D1, no account needed) and applying the D1 schema all need Cloudflare''s CLI `wrangler`. AGENTS.md: minimal dependencies, a new one needs a pm decision.

- Authoring/ops tool only: never in the game build, never in `app/`.
- nixpkgs has `wrangler` (4.141.0 in our flake''s nixpkgs pin), so the flake can pin it like qgen''s tools (decision 115: Screen gallery: how does trivia-gallery drive a browser? did the same for Playwright).
- Type-checking the Worker (`npm run check`) works with a small hand-written `env.d.ts` (D1 binding, `ExportedHandler` shapes we use) instead of the `@cloudflare/workers-types` package.
- Licence: wrangler is MIT/Apache-2.0; not shipped, so no CREDITS entry.

Waiting on this: the plan''s tasks that run wrangler (server code, local dev mode, deploy wrapper).', '', 'wrangler from nixpkgs (pkgs.wrangler, 4.141 in our pin) in a flake wrapper trivia-report-server; nothing in any package.json; Worker types written by hand (no @cloudflare/workers-types)', NULL, '2026-10-13T17:06:32Z', '2026-10-14T01:26:15Z', 854, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-17, task 869: wrangler comes from nixpkgs through the flake wrapper trivia-report-server (dev, deploy, tail, secret, seed-telemetry); report-server/ has no package.json, Worker types are hand-written in env.d.ts; npm run check type-checks it; README how-tos ''Run the report server locally'' and ''Deploy the report server, rotate secrets''.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (118, 'Telemetry server storage and pull token', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 105 (milestone 14 part 1). D1''s free plan allows ~100k row writes/day; a row per answered question would hit it at a few thousand sessions, and analysis happens in authoring after the pull anyway. One gamemaster, one token file (state/report-token) for qgen flag --pull and the telemetry pull: a second token adds setup for no gain.', '', 'One D1 row per session (validated body as JSON, known fields only), raw rows deleted on ack or after 30 days; pull/ack use the reports'' PULL_TOKEN', NULL, '2026-10-13T17:27:32Z', '2026-10-13T17:27:32Z', 872, NULL, 'rule', 872, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (119, 'Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 106 (milestone 14 part 2). The save follows the Steam user through Steam Cloud, so a buffer in it would be sent once per machine and a ''no'' would have to edit family progress; the save already holds mode, settings, locale, result and per-answer level/correct/jokers, so deriving avoids a second source of truth (undo also undoes telemetry). The sandboxed page can''t write files, so the shell owns ids, clock (process.uptime) and the atomic file; rollover at plan 105''s caps, at most 5 pending files.', '', 'The page rebuilds this run''s games from the save after each action (history slice from the first touch) and the shell stores them in <userData>/telemetry/sessions/<session>.json (install.json holds consent + install id); no save field, no SAVE_VERSION bump', NULL, '2026-10-13T17:30:49Z', '2026-10-13T17:30:49Z', 873, NULL, 'rule', 873, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (120, 'Telemetry send: at quit, one later try at the next start', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 107 (part 3 of plan 101). The server dedups by session and never updates a row (plan 105), so a game-end send would lose later games or force a session per game; calibration isn''t time-critical, so the next-start try covers crashes, Steam Stop, Windows TerminateProcess and Deck sleep. At most two sends per file keeps it bounded; server dedup makes a crash between send and delete harmless.', '', 'The shell sends each session file once in before-quit (4 s budget, window hidden first); retryable failures (401, 429, 5xx, no connection) and files left by a crash/kill get one more try 30 s after the next start, then are deleted whatever the answer; no send at game end', NULL, '2026-10-13T17:33:09Z', '2026-10-13T17:33:09Z', 874, NULL, 'rule', 874, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (121, 'Telemetry consent: stored per install, not in the save', 'answered', '[]', 'The install id and the session buffer are per install (decision 119); a yes in the cloud save would make every machine the account plays on send without being asked there; a no must wipe the id and buffer on that machine, which the save can''t do elsewhere; the save shape stays unchanged (decision 119). Cost: a second Steam account on the same PC inherits the answer (it is shown and changeable in the Esc menu).', '', 'The yes/no lives in the shell''s per-install <userData>/telemetry/install.json (plan 106), not in the Steam Cloud save; every Steam user on that install shares it; a new machine asks again', NULL, '2026-10-13T17:34:04Z', '2026-10-13T17:34:04Z', 875, NULL, 'rule', 875, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (122, 'Played difficulty: calibration model for qgen report --played', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 109 (part 5 of masterplan 14). Relative, not absolute: the curve comes from the played data per age group window (app/data/age-groups.json), so it finds questions mis-rated against their peers; whole-group or per-level difficulty is shown in a per-level table as information only. Rated = the locale''s own difficulty (D-81). Answers before the entry''s last review date don''t count. A filter instead of needs_work because most outliers need a new difficulty, and needs_work would feed qgen rework unasked (plan 101). Local data is aggregated only (state/played/stats.json, no install or session ids), matching plan 108''s privacy text (decision 121).', '', 'Per age group, an empirical monotone curve right rate ← rated difficulty (clean answers: no hint/snipe), inverted per question after shrinkage (k=4); outlier when n≥12, |observed−rated|≥2 and the 90% Wilson interval excludes the curve at the rated value; candidates go to a /review?played=outliers filter, never to needs_work automatically', NULL, '2026-10-13T17:37:33Z', '2026-10-13T17:37:33Z', 876, NULL, 'rule', 876, '2026-10-14, task 892: 2026-10-14, task 892: constants tightened after the generator check (4000 sessions, ~67k answers, 6 planted ids ±3–5): with MIN_N 12, SHRINK 4, Z 1.645 all planted ids came out right but with 26–32 false candidates (a 90 % interval per cell over thousands of cells); now MIN_N = 20, SHRINK = 8, Z = 3.29 (99.9 %): planted 6/6 in the right direction on 6 seeds, 0–1 false per ~1300 testable cells. BUCKET_MIN, GROUP_MIN, DELTA, HELP_JOKERS unchanged. Curve points: PAV blocks at their answer-weighted mean difficulty (strictly decreasing, so the inverse is unique); a bound (≤ first / ≥ last point) only counts in its own direction. Store: games.reached keys now day|group|mode|reached|result, levels values [n, right, Σ rated, n rated] (mean rated difficulty per level).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (123, 'Achievements in games with mods on: allowed or off?', 'answered', '["Off whenever any mod is enabled in that run; the game says so once on the mods screen (simple, clear; player bundles also turn them off)", "Allowed with content-only mods (only bundle data and CSS, no .js/.html of any kind); off as soon as an enabled mod has code or a full conversion", "Always allowed; mods may change anything anyway"]', 'Milestone 15 (Modding and Steam Workshop) leaves this open. Achievements are earned only in qualifying games (decision 19, decision 73, decision 74: gamemaster mode never). Mods run in the page and can patch the engine and call the Steam bridge themselves (soft enforcement, decision 111), so any rule is a convention, not protection. Player bundles add questions that aren''t ours (they never count for our seen counts or reports). Answer this before plan 102''s part ''Achievements, flags and telemetry with mods on'' is written.', '', 'Always allowed; mods may change anything anyway', NULL, '2026-10-13T17:44:58Z', '2026-10-14T01:27:38Z', 834, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 906: 2026-10-13, task 906: plan 124: Achievements, flags and telemetry with mods on. No change to engine/achievements.ts earned()/qualifies() or lib/achievements.ts'' unlock gate: no modsActive, no mod kinds, no save field in the game row (the retroactive pass needs none); player questions count like ours except BUNDLE_* and ALL_CATEGORIES (ours only, as built); no achievements line on the mods screen (plan 118); rich presence unchanged (decision 146). Telemetry games[].mods = this run''s /mods.js overlay non-empty (lib/mods.ts modsOn(), engine/telemetry.ts parameter), per run, no save field. No longer holds: plan 102 part 7''s ''per-run modsActive in earned()'' and ''games with mods recorded in the game row''.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (124, 'Readable client build: output naming rule for mod overrides', 'answered', '[]', 'Milestone 15 (plan 102, part 1): a mod replaces one module by its path, so the path must be predictable from the source tree and stable across updates. Vite''s default [name] drops ''.svelte'' (Game.svelte → Game.js) and collides App.svelte with app.css (App2.js, seen in a test build); keeping the source extension avoids both. vendor/ instead of node_modules/: packagers (electron-builder filters) and readers treat node_modules specially. Stable cssHash: Svelte''s default hashes the CSS text, so .svelte-xxxx classes would change with every style edit and break theme mods.', '', 'Output path = source path under app/client/src + ''.js'' (Svelte: game/Game.svelte → game/Game.svelte.js; runes modules game/sound.svelte.ts → game/sound.svelte.js; lib/data.ts → lib/data.js); a component''s CSS next to it as game/Game.svelte.css; global CSS keeps its path (app.css, game/theme.css); third-party modules under vendor/<package>/<path> (no node_modules/ in dist); Vite helpers under _virtual/; no hashes; Svelte scoped class names stable per component path (cssHash), not per CSS content', NULL, '2026-10-13T17:48:56Z', '2026-10-13T17:48:56Z', 899, NULL, 'rule', 899, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (125, 'Steam Deck: best effort, review without a Deck at hand', 'answered', '[]', 'Panels over the full-screen image can hide it at 1280×800; a hold-to-peek is simpler than guaranteeing a visible third. Replaces ''test on a real Deck before applying'' in plans/18-steam-integration.md.', '', 'Deck support is best effort until the gamemaster has a Deck: fit at 1280×800 (done, plan 46), an image peek on image questions (milestone 8), the Gamepad template as Steam Input default (milestone 10); with those in, request Valve''s Deck compatibility review (SW-12) without a prior real-Deck test. The real-Deck test and further tuning come once a Deck is at hand.', NULL, '2026-10-13T17:52:21Z', '2026-10-13T17:52:21Z', NULL, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (126, 'Image peek: which pad button and key?', 'answered', '[]', 'Decision 9 and plan 45 already use every other button on the Question screen: Y/X/B/A pick, RT submit, LT unlock, LB/RB tray, Start menu, View flag (gamemaster). The right stick is otherwise unused, so holding R3 can''t trigger anything else, and on the Deck the right thumb reaches it. V is free on the Question screen in every catalog (es S P F T X R M, en H P F K T R M, de Z N G W F R M; A-D are answers) and reads as a mnemonic in each language. Per decision 53 it lives in the catalog, so a later language can pick its own letter.', '', 'Pad: R3 (right stick click, standard button 11; glyph RS / R3). Key: per catalog screen.question.peekKey, V in es, es-ES, en and de (ver / view / Vorschau); in the Question collision set of check-literals.', NULL, '2026-10-13T17:55:34Z', '2026-10-13T17:55:34Z', 919, NULL, 'rule', 919, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (127, 'Workshop mods: identity and duplicates', 'answered', '[]', 'Part 3 of masterplan 102 (plan for task 901). Part 2 (plan 112) keys mods.json and question-id namespaces (part 5) by the mod.json id and leaves the Workshop relation to part 3. A slug key keeps the load order, the local-shadows-Workshop dev flow and part 5''s question namespaces stable across republishing; published file ids are bigints in the binding and only identify the item on Steam. Lowest id = oldest item, so a newer copycat never displaces an existing mod.', '', 'A Workshop item is known by its mod.json id (slug), like a local mod; the published file id travels beside it (string, runtime and mods list) and is shown, never used as the settings key. Duplicates: local before Workshop (local copy shadows its Workshop original); between two Workshop items the one with the lower published file id wins, the other is listed invalid duplicate_id naming the winner; the player unsubscribes one.', NULL, '2026-10-13T18:05:07Z', '2026-10-13T18:05:07Z', 901, NULL, 'rule', 901, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (128, 'Bundles from mods: the shell merges bundles.json; mod ids namespaced <mod id>:<id>', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 102 part 5 (task 902). Splitting bundles.json into per-bundle files would touch ~20 readers (qgen export/validate, categories.py, release_check.py, stage-media.mjs, steam.py stage, smoke.mjs, sim, review UI) for no player gain; overlaying one shared file can''t merge several mods. The merge is JSON data read by the shell (no mod code in main, plan 102). Namespacing both bundle and question ids with the unique mod id (plan 112, decision 127) means no collision with ours or between mods, now or after we add bundles; '':'' is a legal URL path character, and the shell maps it to <mod dir>/data/bundles/<bundle>/ so no colon reaches the file system. Not overlaying our other data files keeps our data ours: a mod replacing our pool would put its content under our ids and into our seen counts and reports; rules tweaks go through window.trivia (part 4).', '', 'One bundle format and one loader: a mod carries data/bundles.json (rows as ours) and data/bundles/<bundle>/ (categories, names, pool[.<locale>].json, media) like app/data/; the shell serves one merged /data/bundles.json (ours first, then enabled mods in load order, mod rows tagged source: mod, mod, modName, ids namespaced <mod id>:<bundle id>); /data/bundles/<mod id>:<bundle>/… is served from that mod''s folder only; every other /data/ file is ours and never overlaid by mods; mod question ids become <mod id>:<id> at load ('':'' never in our ids: the test for ''not ours''). Our bundles.json stays one file (no per-bundle bundle.json split).', NULL, '2026-10-13T18:08:42Z', '2026-10-13T18:08:42Z', 902, NULL, 'rule', 902, '2026-10-13, task 963: One bundles format and loader for mods (plan 115, tasks 959-963): app/desktop/mods.mjs bundleRows() checks a mod''s data/bundles.json; app/desktop/resolve.mjs serves merged /data/bundles.json (ours first, mod rows tagged source/mod/modName, ids <mod>:<id>) and /data/bundles/<mod>:<id>/ from that mod only, no other /data/ overlay; app/client/src/engine/pool.ts isModId/isOurs + modPool() (namespaced ids, media rewrite, invalid questions dropped); app/client/src/lib/data.ts loads mod bundles as packs, modIssues(); Game.svelte hides flags, engine/telemetry.ts and authoring/tools/save_file.py ignore mod ids. Docs: plans/22-bundles.md ''Player bundles (mods)'', plans/18-steam-integration.md ''Modding'', directory.md.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (129, 'Credits for mod media: runtime section on the Credits screen from the mod''s own pool', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 102 part 5 (task 902). CC BY files need attribution where the game shows them; the build-time credits.json can''t know mods, a runtime list from the data the game already loaded can. No mod file of its own to parse, one place for players to look.', '', 'Mod media lives in the mod folder (relative file_url, served by the overlay, never downloaded); the Credits screen adds a section per loaded mod bundle built at runtime from its questions'' media/background credit and source_url (deduped); credits.json, CREDITS.md and credits_check stay ours only; the guide tells modders to fill credit for every file they didn''t make.', NULL, '2026-10-13T18:08:42Z', '2026-10-13T18:08:42Z', 902, NULL, 'rule', 902, '2026-10-13, task 963: app/client/src/game/Credits.svelte adds a section per loaded mod bundle (heading t(''credits.playerMade'')) from its questions'' media/background credit + source_url, deduped, at runtime (task 961); credits.json, CREDITS.md, credits_check unchanged (ours only). Docs: plans/22-bundles.md ''Player bundles (mods)''.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (130, 'Preload bridge renamed window.trivia → window.triviaShell; window.trivia is the mod API', 'answered', '[]', 'contextBridge objects are frozen and the name window.trivia is the natural public mod API (milestone 15). The bridge has one reader (lib/desktop.ts), so the rename is cheap; hiding the bridge from mod code isn''t possible in one page and isn''t a goal (page-only rule protects the PC, not the save). Plan 117''s task 1 (task 904''s plan).', '', 'The shell''s contextBridge object moves to window.triviaShell (lib/desktop.ts its only reader, plus plan 99''s dev page shim); window.trivia becomes the page''s mod API (lib/mods.ts). Mods can still reach window.triviaShell: accepted, the one-time notice says mods run with the game''s access.', NULL, '2026-10-13T18:13:46Z', '2026-10-13T18:13:46Z', 904, NULL, 'rule', 904, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (131, 'Code add-ons: shell-generated /mods.js, entry default export setup(trivia), mods run before data and language load', 'answered', '[]', 'Generated by the shell: the shell already has the arranged, validated list (plan 112), so no extra IPC or list file, and a full conversion can import /mods.js too; outside the shell /mods.js is missing and the game runs without mods. Before data load: data hooks and new UI locales must be in place before lib/engine.ts ready() and initLang() run; a ready event covers what needs the mounted game. Per-mod namespace /mods/<id>/ keeps two mods'' main.js apart and gives import.meta.url a stable base.', '', 'The shell generates /mods.js per run (an ES module exporting the loaded mods in run order: bottom of the load order first, with entry and style URLs under /mods/<id>/); main.ts imports it first, links each mod''s root style.css, imports each entry and awaits its default export setup(trivia) with a per-mod view of the API (5 s timeout); a failing or slow mod is reported and skipped, the game still starts. Everything a mod changes is a registration (data hooks, action hooks, catalogs, screens, events); a ready event fires after mount. /mods/<id>/<rel> serves only that mod''s folder.', NULL, '2026-10-13T18:13:46Z', '2026-10-13T18:13:46Z', 904, NULL, 'rule', 904, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (132, 'Workshop publishing: where the published file id lives', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 119 (task 907). setItemContent uploads the whole folder, so a sidecar would ship anyway; in mod.json the id travels to subscribers, where plan 114''s workshop_id_mismatch warning checks it. Optional field in plan 112''s validator, ^[1-9]\d{0,19}$; delete it to publish as a new item. First publish defaults to private visibility; updates change visibility only with --visibility.', '', 'mod.json field workshopId (decimal string), written by trivia --publish-mod on first publish; first publish private', NULL, '2026-10-13T18:19:35Z', '2026-10-13T18:19:35Z', 907, NULL, 'rule', 907, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (133, 'Player bundle kit: check with trivia --check-mod, kit in modding/ shipped in the install folder', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 102 part 9 (task 908). An AI-made pool needs per-question reasons a player can act on; the mods screen (plan 118) shows only counts per bundle and needs the mod installed and a restart. One validator for loader, check and publish keeps no second path. The game runs offline and the template must be copied into mods/: shipping a few KB of text and one small image next to the executable (Steam''s Browse local files) needs no network and no GitHub; the repo copy is what the store page links.', '', 'Players check a mod folder with trivia --check-mod <folder> (headless, no Steam, same validators as the loader: readManifest, bundleRows, modPool with per-question reasons), not only the mods screen; the kit (modding/bundles.md, modding/bundle-prompt.md, modding/template-bundle/) lives in the repo''s modding/ (part 10''s guide folder) and ships in the game''s install folder as modding/ (electron-builder extraFiles), also readable online in the public repo', NULL, '2026-10-13T18:21:44Z', '2026-10-13T18:21:44Z', 908, NULL, 'rule', 908, '2026-10-14, task 986: 2026-10-14, task 986: plan 120: Player bundle kit (tasks 981-986): app/client/src/engine/pool.ts modPool (text-only questions, per-question drop reasons); app/desktop/check-mod.mjs checkMod + main.mjs --check-mod (headless, exit 0/1/2, Windows <folder>-check.log); publish.mjs preparePublish runs checkMod (warnings); modding/bundles.md, modding/bundle-prompt.md, modding/template-bundle/; electron-builder.yml extraFiles modding/; credits_check.mjs skips modding/; trivia-release-check step modkit. Docs: directory.md (modding/, check-mod.mjs), AGENTS.md trivia-desktop line, plans/18-steam-integration.md ''Modding'', plans/22-bundles.md ''Player bundles (mods)''. README.md unchanged (decision 144: modding how-tos go in modding/README.md, task 988).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (134, 'Modding guide: path, language, examples', 'answered', '[]', 'One folder for everything a modder needs (decision 133 already puts the kit in modding/ and ships it); a player in the install folder finds the guide offline, the store page links the public repo (decision 108). English only: modders'' common language, one text to keep in step with the code; store bullets per language link to it. One bundle mod to keep valid (the template is already release-checked by plan 120''s modkit step). No media in the examples keeps credits_check unchanged.', '', 'Guide at modding/README.md (English only), beside the player bundle kit (decision 133), shipped in the install folder as modding/ and read online at github.com/rubenmoor/trivia/blob/main/modding/README.md; example mods in modding/examples/{theme,rules-tweak,conversion}/; the bundle example is modding/template-bundle/ (plan 120), not a second bundle mod; examples carry no media and are MIT like the code (decision 107)', NULL, '2026-10-13T18:23:55Z', '2026-10-13T18:23:55Z', 909, NULL, 'rule', 909, '2026-10-14, task 989: 2026-10-14, task 989: modding/README.md and modding/examples/{theme,rules-tweak,conversion}/ ship in both unpacked builds as modding/ (electron-builder.yml extraFiles, unchanged); trivia-release-check step modkit runs the packaged --check-mod on template-bundle and each modding/examples/* (authoring/steam/release_check.py); credits_check.mjs unchanged (skips modding/, examples have no media). Links: README.md ''Mod the game'' (replaces ''Publish a mod to the Workshop'', decision 144), directory.md modding/ row, plans/18-steam-integration.md player kit line; plans/18 and 22-bundles.md already link the guide (task 988). LICENSE-content.md doesn''t exist yet: task 200 states modding/ is MIT.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (135, 'Steamworks: enable Workshop for ¡Trivia! and a second Steam account?', 'pending', '["done", "not yet"]', 'Plan 114 (Workshop source). Needed for the Workshop check under Steam (task 958) and plan 119''s publishing. Only once the real App ID exists (SW-7, plans 39/85); dev tests under Spacewar 480 are not Workshop tests.

Steamworks (App Admin):
- Workshop → General: enable "ISteamUGC for file transfer"
- visibility: public (items may be public/friends/private)
- tags: bundle, theme, code, conversion; languages es, en, de, …
- Workshop legal agreement: Steam''s own; creators accept it before items go public (plan 119 shows its URL)
- content descriptors: none set by us (creators pick per item; the base game''s from plan 88 stay)
- publish the Steamworks changes

Also: a second Steam account owning the game (beta key or family sharing), for milestone 15''s "Done when".

Answer: done + the tag list as entered.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-13T18:30:44Z', NULL, 934, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (136, 'Mod settings: per machine in <userData>/mods.json, one ordered list, top wins', 'answered', '[]', 'Mods are files on this machine, the save is Steam Cloud''s and per user: like decision 121 (telemetry consent per install), the settings live per install, shared by every Steam user on it. One list keeps on/off and order together; appending new mods on makes dropping a folder in mods/ or subscribing the opt-in (part 6 may hold them off until its notice). Keeping unknown ids keeps a still-downloading Workshop item''s place. Unreadable file: treated as empty, one stderr line, left alone until the next write. Implemented in app/desktop/mods.mjs (task 950).', '', '<userData>/mods.json (dev state/desktop/mods.json): { version: 1, mods: [{ id, on }] }; one ordered list = load order, index 0 = top = wins the overlay; discovered mods missing from it appended on; listed ids not found kept (state missing); read once per run, changes apply on restart; written atomically (temp + rename)', NULL, '2026-10-13T18:45:26Z', '2026-10-13T18:45:26Z', 950, NULL, 'rule', 950, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (137, 'Task 780 (memory-only save, «progress needs Steam» notice) done: can task 786 (smoke game under the dev switch) run?', 'answered', '["task 780 done, run task 786", "run task 786 now without the notice assertion (follow-up task adds it)"]', 'Task 786 needs task 780''s notice element to assert its absence in the packaged smoke game; task 780 is still open (priority 440). Tasks 776 and 779 are done.', '', 'task 786 runs after task 780: priority 430 (below task 780''s 440), with the notice assertion', NULL, '2026-10-13T19:38:33Z', '2026-10-14T01:29:47Z', 786, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 786: 2026-10-13, task 786: authoring/steam/smoke.mjs runs the packaged build with TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1, reads/asserts the save at save/dev/game.json (decision 114; no more save/local/), fails on the «progress needs Steam» notice (.start .notice) on the first start screen and after the restart, level check points at .level .title.big / .hud .level; release_check.py smoke docstring names the switch, OFFLINE manual row reads ''beta install from Steam, network off (Steam offline mode…)''; plans/18-steam-integration.md smoke row: dev switch, network off, no start test without Steam and without the switch (decision 39). Without the switch the smoke game now fails at ''start screen'' with the notice text.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (138, 'Smoke game muted', 'answered', '[]', 'authoring/steam/smoke.mjs runs with env -i, so PM_WORKER never reaches the shell; it checks media readyState, not audibility, and sound stays a manual release-check row. TRIVIA_MUTE=1 is in its env list (plan 123: Silent game for agents: muted by default under PM_WORKER, opt-in sound).', '', 'smoke game muted: checks load, not audio; sound is the manual row', NULL, '2026-10-13T20:17:12Z', '2026-10-13T20:17:12Z', 997, NULL, 'rule', 997, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (139, 'Achievement triggers derived without a save change (SW-11)', 'answered', '[]', 'decision 73: Achievement list (SW-11)? asked task 655 to add hints per question and a local clock if needed. Both are already in the save: each Soplo pushes «hint» into the question''s jokers, recorded in its history entry, and every timestamp is local time without zone. save.seen would count gamemaster games, against decision 74: Gamemaster mode earns no achievements.', '', 'No save field, no version bump: hints per question = «hint» count in history[].jokers; QUESTIONS_1000 = distinct question ids in qualifying games'' history (not save.seen, which includes gamemaster games); local dates/hours from started_on/finished_on (local ISO, no zone); NIGHT_OWL = a win finished 00:00–04:59; GAME_NIGHTS = 7 distinct started_on dates', NULL, '2026-10-13T20:25:46Z', '2026-10-13T20:25:46Z', 655, NULL, 'rule', 655, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (140, 'Achievements entered and published in Steamworks?', 'pending', '["Entered and published (25 achievements, VDF uploaded; note any token renames)", "Issues (name them)"]', 'Plan 86 (SW-11), `task 657: Steamworks achievement setup values and VDF`. Values: `plans/18-steam-integration.md` → "Achievements in Steamworks".

Needs the real App ID first (SW-7, `task 254: write plan: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)`; decision 89 for the App ID); Spacewar 480 has only its own achievements.

Steps:
- Steamworks → Stats & Achievements → Achievements: enter the 25 of the "Now" table in its order (API name, English name + description, Hidden no, Set by Client, no stat).
- Icons: `app/desktop/achievements/render.sh`, then upload `png/<API>_achieved.png` / `_unachieved.png` (256×256) per achievement.
- Localization: download Steamworks'' localization file, compare token names with `app/desktop/steam-achievements.vdf` (`NEW_ACHIEVEMENT_1_<n>`, assumed from the order); rename if they differ, then upload the VDF (latam, spanish, english, german).
- Publish.
- Not now: WIN_RR_COOP, WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE, WIN_TIMED (MD-8), BUNDLE_COLOMBIA (with its DLC).

Texts are drafts; their wording check is task 658''s (SW-11 close-out), so a wording change later only means re-uploading the VDF.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-13T20:34:53Z', NULL, 657, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (141, 'Achievements check under Steam (SW-11)', 'pending', '["passes", "issues (describe them)"]', 'Developer check for `plan 86: Achievements (SW-11)`, after decision 140: Achievements entered and published in Steamworks? (needs the real App ID, SW-7). Under Steam with a logged-in user, fresh account or stats reset (`steam://` console `reset_all_stats <appid>` or `ResetAllStats`):
- Texts: read all 25 names/descriptions in Steamworks (latam, spanish, english, german; table in `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Achievements in Steamworks"); wording changes go in the answer.
- Win a solo game (standard settings) → Steam toast `FIRST_WIN` (plus the joker ones played on the way).
- A customized solo game (Personalizar partida) and a gamemaster-mode game: nothing new unlocks.
- A save with earlier qualifying wins (e.g. the family''s save via `trivia-desktop --import-save`, plan 99), stats reset: its achievements unlock on the next start.
- A refused unlock logs `trivia: steam: unlock <id> refused` on stderr.
Answer passes, or issues with what went wrong (each becomes a follow-up task).', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-13T20:35:45Z', NULL, 658, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (142, 'Report text format (copy fallback, qgen flag)', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 93 task 3 (task 859). Shape, for task 700 (qgen flag) and task 860 (qgen flag --pull):
- Header tokens fixed and untranslated, separated by '' · '' (space, U+00B7, space): ''¡Trivia!'', ''#<question id>'', question language (flag locale, else es), ''v<game version>'', ''pool <8-hex export hash>'' (''pool ?'' when unknown, e.g. a locale without a pool), flag date YYYY-MM-DD.
- Then one line each, ''<label>: <value>'': question (from shown), answer (as the list shows it; the running question''s answer is the UI''s hidden text, e.g. ''(en juego)''), note only if there is one. Player and level are not in the text.
- Labels per UI language (catalog flag.question / flag.answer / flag.note): es and es-ES Pregunta / Respuesta / Nota; en Question / Answer / Note; de Frage / Antwort / Notiz. A parser should accept all of them.
- Sent field text = the question and answer lines only (no header, no note); note, lang, version, pool go as their own fields.
- Sample from the live check (trivia-desktop, two flags):
¡Trivia! #q-0002 · en · v0.1.0 · pool ? · 2026-10-13
Pregunta: What is the capital of France?
Respuesta: Paris

¡Trivia! #q-0001 · es · v0.1.0 · pool 1f30d10c · 2026-10-12
Pregunta: ¿Qué bebida caliente, hecha con granos tostados, hace famosa a Colombia en todo el mundo?
Respuesta: El café
Nota: la respuesta está mal
Code: app/client/src/game/report.ts.', '', 'One block per flag, blocks separated by one blank line; header: ¡Trivia! #<id> · <lang> · v<version> · pool <hash or ?> · <YYYY-MM-DD flag date>; then <Question>: …, <Answer>: …, optional <Note>: … with labels in the UI language', NULL, '2026-10-13T20:44:05Z', '2026-10-13T20:44:05Z', 859, NULL, 'rule', 859, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (143, 'Readable build: start time on the Steam Deck ok?', 'answered', '["ok (≤ +0.5 s)", "too slow: bundle the Svelte runtime", "too slow: other"]', '`plan 111: Readable client build` part 5, `task 948: Start time on the Steam Deck: gamemaster check (decision once)`. The readable client (`task 944: Readable build config: preserveModules, decision 124 names, stable cssHash`) loads ~200 modules over `app://` instead of 3 files; this may slow the start. Budget: ≤ +0.5 s on the Deck.

No Deck at hand (`decision 125: Steam Deck: best effort, review without a Deck at hand`): time on your PC now, the Deck later; answer from the PC numbers if the Deck must wait.

Builds to compare
- previous (hashed): commit `c17aaa7` (last before `task 944`); readable: `main`
- with the next beta upload: install the beta build under Steam (`trivia-steam upload --branch beta`), compare with the build before it
- no beta upload due: `git worktree add /tmp/hashed c17aaa7`, `trivia-desktop-build --dir` in both trees; on the Deck only as a non-Steam test, copy `app/desktop/release/win-unpacked/`

Steps (each build, three times)
- start the game (`TRIVIA_MUTE=1`), time launch → start menu visible (stopwatch or screen recording)
- note the median per build and machine; compare readable − hashed

Options
- ok (≤ +0.5 s): keep the readable build as is
- too slow: bundle the Svelte runtime: one `vendor/svelte.js`, our modules still one file each (follow-up task in plan 111)
- too slow: other: say what in the answer', '', 'i think we should measure the impact of the "readable build" once. e.g. keep a configuration for an optimized build around and build both, the readable one and the optimized one. then measure the impact on my system, not on a steam deck. then we see from there', NULL, '2026-10-13T21:49:32Z', '2026-10-14T04:04:11Z', 948, NULL, 'once', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 948: Measured once (task 948, 2026-10-13): `npm run build:optimized -w app/client` (Vite defaults: hashed, minified) kept next to the readable `npm run build`; repo shell under Xvfb on the developer''s PC, launch → start menu, median of 20 runs each: readable 527 ms vs. hashed 388 ms (+0.14 s; in-page part 346 vs. 202 ms, 198 JS files vs. 3). Numbers in `plans/01-architecture.md`.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (144, 'README.md is customer-facing: modding docs live in modding/README.md', 'answered', '[]', 'The developer, 2026-10-13: the GitHub README is effectively customer-facing and too long; ''Upload to Steam'' removed from it (already in plans 11 and 18).', '', 'README.md has one short ''Mod the game'' section: a link to modding/README.md, nothing else on modding; how-tos for publishing mods, player bundles and testing mods locally go in the guide; Steam release/upload how-tos stay in plans/11-steam.md and plans/18-steam-integration.md, not in README.md', NULL, '2026-10-13T23:31:16Z', '2026-10-13T23:31:16Z', NULL, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (145, 'Svelte runtime ships with every export for precompiled mod components', 'answered', '[]', 'Task 971: precompiled mod components (svelte/compiler, imports rewritten to /vendor/svelte/src/internal/client/index.js) found an index.js with only side-effect imports: Rolldown had dropped every export our app doesn''t use. As extra entries the runtime keeps its full export signature under the same vendor/ paths (decision 124); a mod''s component shares our runtime instance.', '', 'vite.config.ts: svelte, svelte/internal/client, svelte/internal/disclose-version as extra rolldown inputs, preserveEntrySignatures strict', NULL, '2026-10-14T01:30:44Z', '2026-10-14T01:30:44Z', 971, NULL, 'rule', 971, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (146, 'Achievements, mods screen and rich presence with mods on', 'answered', '[]', 'Follows decision 123: Achievements in games with mods on: allowed or off? (always allowed). With no mods gate there is nothing to record per game for the retroactive pass; a ''modded'' presence token would need a VDF token, a Steamworks re-upload (decision 71) and 4 languages for no player benefit. Plan 124: Achievements, flags and telemetry with mods on.', '', 'No change: earned() and the unlock gate ignore mods (no modsActive, no save field); player questions count like ours except BUNDLE_* (our regional bundles) and ALL_CATEGORIES (our base); no achievements line on the mods screen; rich presence unchanged (no ''modded'' token)', NULL, '2026-10-14T01:32:44Z', '2026-10-14T01:32:44Z', 906, NULL, 'rule', 906, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (147, 'Report server: deployed on Cloudflare? URL and date', 'answered', '["workers.dev, deployed: <URL>, <date>, database_id <id>, test report ok/not yet", "own domain, deployed: <URL>, <date>, database_id <id>, test report ok/not yet"]', 'Task 868 (plan 103 part 4). Set up the question report server (`report-server/`, Cloudflare Workers + D1) and send a first test report. Every step runs in the repo''s dev shell (`direnv allow` or `nix develop`); workers never log in or handle secrets.

## 1. Cloudflare account
- Sign up at dash.cloudflare.com, free plan; turn on 2FA (My Profile → Authentication).
- Free-tier numbers not re-checked (no web access for this worker): check developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits and /d1/platform/pricing against `plans/11-steam.md` ST-5 (Workers 100k requests/day, 10 ms CPU/request; D1 5 GB, 5M rows read and 100k written/day); differences in your answer.

## 2. Endpoint name
- 1) `workers.dev` (recommended): `https://trivia-reports.<account-subdomain>.workers.dev`, free, nothing to renew; moving off Cloudflare later needs a game patch with a new `reportUrl`.
- 2) Own domain (≈ $10/year): e.g. `reports.<domain>`; the server can move later without a game patch. Domain on Cloudflare (Registrar or nameservers), then a Custom Domain on the Worker (Workers → trivia-reports → Settings → Domains & Routes) after step 6.

## 3. Log in
```
cd report-server && wrangler login
```

## 4. D1 database
```
cd report-server && wrangler d1 create trivia-reports
```
- Copy the printed `database_id` into `report-server/wrangler.toml` (replaces `PLACEHOLDER(868)` and the zero id); not a secret: commit it or put it in the answer.

## 5. Secrets (Worker secrets only, never in git)
- First deploy creates the Worker; if `secret` complains that it doesn''t exist, run step 6 first, then come back.
```
trivia-report-server secret STEAM_WEB_API_KEY   # publisher Web API key: Steamworks → Users & Permissions → Manage Groups → your group → Web API key (needs decision 67''s account)
openssl rand -base64 32 | tr ''+/'' ''-_'' | tr -d ''=''   # pull token: copy it
trivia-report-server secret PULL_TOKEN          # paste the pull token
openssl rand -hex 32 | trivia-report-server secret HASH_SALT
```
- Save the same pull token for `qgen flag --pull`: `state/report-token` (gitignored) or env `TRIVIA_REPORT_TOKEN`:
```
printf ''%s\n'' ''<pull token>'' > state/report-token && chmod 600 state/report-token
```

## 6. Deploy and check
```
trivia-report-server deploy      # applies migrations remotely, then deploys
curl https://<url>/health        # → {"ok":true,"api":1}
qgen flag --pull --url https://<url> --dry-run   # token check: no error, 0 reports
```

## 7. First test report (needs the App ID, decision 89)
- `STEAM_APP_ID` in `report-server/wrangler.toml` stays `""` until `authoring/steam/steam.json` has the App ID (decision 89: Steamworks App ID, depot IDs and beta branch entered?); until then every `POST /reports` → 502 and the game falls back to copy. Once known: set it there, `trivia-report-server deploy` again.
- A `beta` build with `reportUrl` set (the next worker sets it from your answer), started under Steam: flag a question, add a note, «Enviar» → «enviada».
- `qgen flag --pull` → the report shows up as a `needs_work` review; a second pull is empty.
- If it fails: `trivia-report-server tail` while sending (no bodies logged), note the error code.

## Answer
- URL + date, e.g. `https://trivia-reports.<sub>.workers.dev, deployed 2026-10-20; database_id <id>; test report: ok / not yet (App ID)`.
- The next worker puts the URL into `reportUrl` in `app/desktop/package.json` and ST-5. If the test report is still waiting on the App ID, say so: a follow-up task covers it.', '', 'database id: 0f05920c-214a-496a-9469-2877961ad88e

url: https://trivia-reports.trivia-question-reports.workers.dev

deployed: 2026-10-17

test report: {"ok":true,"api":1}

still waiting for the APP id from steamworks', NULL, '2026-10-14T02:21:21Z', '2026-10-17T19:55:38Z', 868, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-17, task 868: reportUrl set in app/desktop/package.json to https://trivia-reports.trivia-question-reports.workers.dev; D1 database id in report-server/wrangler.toml; ST-5 notes the deploy. Open: STEAM_APP_ID var (empty until Steamworks gives it), then the first real-ticket test report.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (148, 'Overlay: a mod''s entry and root style.css never shadow our files', 'answered', '[]', 'task 1004: Overlay: a code mod''s root main.js shadows our /main.js, the game never starts. Option (a) over a warning: an entry or style.css is loaded by /mods.js through /mods/<id>/, never meant as an override, so hiding it from the top-level overlay can''t break an intended override and fixes the accident (entry main.js replacing our /main.js, blank page) without the modder having to read a warning. Overrides stay any other file by path.', '', 'The overlay never serves a mod''s mod.json, its mod.json entry file or its root style.css at the top level; they stay reachable under /mods/<id>/ only', NULL, '2026-10-14T03:48:58Z', '2026-10-14T03:48:58Z', 1004, NULL, 'rule', 1004, '2026-10-14, task 1004: 2026-10-13, task 1004: app/desktop/resolve.mjs firstHit() skips each layer''s own files (mod.json, mod.json entry, root style.css; ownFiles()); main.mjs passes entry per loaded mod; resolve.test.mjs covers entry main.js vs our /main.js; plans/18-steam-integration.md ''Not overlaid''.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (149, 'Readable build costs +0.14 s at start on your PC: keep it?', 'answered', '["keep the readable build as is", "bundle the Svelte runtime", "other"]', 'Follow-up of `decision 143: Readable build: start time on the Steam Deck ok?` (`task 948: Start time on the Steam Deck: gamemaster check (decision once)`).

Measured 2026-10-13 on your PC (repo shell, Xvfb, fresh save, median of 20 runs, first run of each batch dropped)
- launch → start menu: readable 527 ms, hashed/minified 388 ms: +0.14 s
- page part alone (navigation → start menu): 346 vs. 202 ms; 198 JS modules vs. 3 files
- budget from `plan 111: Readable client build`: ≤ +0.5 s on the Deck; a Deck is roughly 2–4× slower, so +0.3–0.6 s there (estimate, not measured)
- repeat: `npm run build:optimized -w app/client` vs. `npm run build -w app/client`, then `trivia-desktop`

Options
- keep the readable build as is
- bundle the Svelte runtime: one `vendor/svelte.js` (≈ 100 of the 198 files), our modules still one file each; mods importing `/vendor/svelte/…` by path change (follow-up task in plan 111)
- other: say what', '', 'bundle the Svelte runtime', NULL, '2026-10-14T04:11:27Z', '2026-10-14T15:18:56Z', 948, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 948: 2026-10-14, task 948: The readable build''s per-file Svelte runtime (vendor/svelte/src/…, decision 124''s third-party rule) no longer holds: task 1025 (plan 111) bundles it into vendor/svelte.js (or shared-chunk files), every export kept (decision 145), our src/ modules still one file each; mods importing /vendor/svelte/… by path move to the new path; docs (18-steam-integration.md, directory.md, mods.ts) and the start-time numbers in 01-architecture.md updated there.

2026-10-14, task 1025: 2026-10-14, task 1025: Svelte''s runtime ships as one vendor/svelte.js (decision 159: Svelte runtime as one file: vendor/svelte.js); launch → first screen 529 ms vs. 573 ms per-file, 457 ms hashed (plans/01-architecture.md).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (150, 'Family save imported into trivia-desktop?', 'pending', '["imported, family plays trivia-desktop", "not yet"]', '`plan 99: Retire the browser game and the Python game server`, step 2 (`task 763`). The family''s save moves from the browser game (`state/game.json`) into the desktop build; `task 765: Delete app/server, ServerStore, the trivia command and nix build .#app` waits for this answer.
- Start Steam, logged in with the family''s Steam account (the save folder is per Steam user, `plan 87`).
- From the repo''s dev shell: `trivia-desktop --import-save state/game.json`
  - prints the source and the target `game.json` (the Steam user''s `<steamid64>/` folder); `state/game.json` stays untouched
  - refuses if that user already has a save; `--force` replaces it and keeps the old one in `backup/game-import-<stamp>.json`
  - the game starts right after the import
- Check: «¿Quién juega?» lists the family''s players with their games; recently seen questions don''t come back; a round plays.
- From then on the family plays `trivia-desktop` (later the Steam beta); the browser game and `trivia` go with `task 765`.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T04:13:54Z', NULL, 763, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (151, 'Mods notice per install in mods.json; new mods held off until it', 'answered', '[]', 'Every Steam user on the machine shares the mods, so one notice per machine (decision 121''s precedent for per-install settings). Holding new mods off is the only way to guarantee that the notice is seen before any mod runs. From plan 118: Mods screen and safe start, task 973.', '', 'mods.json gains notice: true + noticeAt (per machine, like decision 136: Mod settings: per machine in <userData>/mods.json, one ordered list, top wins); while notice is missing arrange() appends newly discovered mods on: false, so no mod code runs before the notice; after it new mods are appended on; accepting never touches existing rows', NULL, '2026-10-14T07:15:08Z', '2026-10-14T07:15:08Z', 973, NULL, 'rule', 973, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (152, 'Manual safe start: --no-mods only', 'answered', '[]', 'The overlay is fixed before the page starts, so a key check would cost a relaunch; a pad isn''t readable before the page; a second launch option makes Steam ask on every start. From plan 118: Mods screen and safe start.', '', 'Playing without mods is --no-mods in Steam''s per-game launch options; no held key or pad button, no second Steamworks launch option', NULL, '2026-10-14T07:15:09Z', '2026-10-14T07:15:09Z', 973, NULL, 'rule', 973, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (153, 'Mods crash marker: mods-start.json, cleared on ready or a live page after 20 s', 'answered', '[]', 'A crashed or hung start with mods is followed by one start without mods that tells the player why; no loop because a safe start has no layers and writes no marker. The ping instead of a plain 20 s timer catches a page blocked by a mod''s synchronous loop (Chromium''s unresponsive event needs pending input, so it can''t be relied on). Full conversions that never call ready are confirmed by the ping. From plan 118, task 973.', '', '<userData>/mods-start.json (dev state/desktop/), { at, mods: [active ids] }, written atomically before loadURL only when the run has layers; cleared on mods:ready or when the page answers a ping 20 s after did-finish-load (3 s answer window); a page that doesn''t answer, render-process-gone (not clean-exit) or a main-frame load failure relaunches; not cleared on quit; marker found at start → deleted, no layers, safeStart { reason: crashed, mods }', NULL, '2026-10-14T07:15:09Z', '2026-10-14T07:15:09Z', 973, NULL, 'rule', 973, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (154, 'Mods restart drops our own flags', 'answered', '[]', 'A restart applies the mods list; repeating --no-mods would defeat it and repeating --import-save would import the old file again. From plan 118, task 973.', '', 'mods:restart (and the crash relaunch) flushes the save queue and telemetry like a quit, then app.relaunch({ args }) with every own flag (--no-mods, --import-save <file>, --force) dropped and Electron/Chromium/Steam args kept, then app.exit(0); SteamAppId stays in the environment', NULL, '2026-10-14T07:15:09Z', '2026-10-14T07:15:09Z', 973, NULL, 'rule', 973, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (155, 'Play-test of age groups and bundles (again, after the decision 50 fixes)', 'answered', '["all sessions played fine", "problems (listed in the answer)"]', 'Plan 30 (milestone 5): play-test again once `plan 125: Play-test fixes: player Enter, Choice screen, overlay line, Regional: Colombia` and `plan 126: One language setting for UI and questions` are done (their tasks closed); answer then.

## Previous round
`decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` → problems 1–7; fine: age groups, colombia off, keyboard, UI languages es/en/de. The engine pre-check of task 478 passed (every group, `base` only, refusals `base_bundle_count` / `bundle_not_offered`, en/de `bundlesFor` = `base`); see decision 50''s body for the table.

## Checklist (`TRIVIA_MUTE=1 trivia`, :8000, or `trivia-desktop`)
- Fixes of decision 50:
  1. «¿Quién juega?» with saved players: Enter picks the most recent player.
  2. Overlay: «Edad: …», «Paquetes de preguntas: …» (labelled; en/de likewise).
  3. «Regional: Colombia» on the Choice screen, bundle selector, overlay, credits.
  4. Mode row: «Solo o en grupo» first.
  5. «Solo o en grupo» has the bundle selector (own step, not in «Personalizar partida»); gamemaster mode too.
  6. «Desde»/«Hasta» always shown with the group''s window, read-only; editable only with «A medida».
  7. Language: one setting; flag top right on the first screen only; no language rows in the Esc menu; en/de play the Spanish questions with only `base` offered.
- Still: one session per age group (mouse, and once keyboard only, IN-1); one with `colombia` off; defaults straight through with Enter; Básico as the selected base bundle (one of N), no «Siempre activo»; undo/abandon keep the choice.

Answer "problems": list each one; the close-out (`task 479: Close out AG-7 and BN-6`) turns them into fix tasks.', '', 'all sessions played fine', NULL, '2026-10-14T07:42:18Z', '2026-10-15T04:30:23Z', 479, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 479: Milestone 5 play-tested fine; AG-7 and BN-6 [x] in plans/21-age-groups.md, plans/22-bundles.md, plans/project.md (BN-6: exactly one base bundle). ''until AG-7'' and every always_on/always-on wording gone from plans 21/22, project.md and the about texts of app/data/age-groups.json, bundles.json; D-68 marked superseded in part by D-85. No new D entry.

2026-10-16, task 1379: BN-6''s ''exactly one base bundle'' dropped (milestone 8''s any-combination line): base_bundle_count and its error texts are gone; a selection with no question for the choice is refused with no_questions (new and in-game settings), supply_short stays for short-but-nonzero; the Bundles screen shows the reason and keeps start off.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (156, 'One language for UI and questions', 'answered', '[]', 'From `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` (item 7), `plan 126: One language setting for UI and questions`. Supersedes in part D-86 (two settings, question-language option list): options = UI_LANGS only. es-ES, en, de (no pools yet) and mod UI languages play the Spanish pool with the es bundles. newGame takes its locale from the loaded data (data.locale); a running game keeps GameRow.locale, so POLYGLOT counts a de UI on Spanish questions as an es game. No bump: parseSave already read a missing language as es (D-86), the old object still parses, and save_file.py doesn''t read language.', '', 'SaveData.language is one tag (UI = questions); the question locale is the language if pool.<language>.json exists and its default bundles'' supply passes, else es (lib/engine.ts nextLocale / localeOf); old {ui, questions} saves read as ui, no save-version bump', NULL, '2026-10-14T07:47:44Z', '2026-10-14T07:47:44Z', 1019, NULL, 'rule', 1019, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (157, 'Start''s language button: globe and endonym, key per catalog, pad Y', 'answered', '[]', 'plan 126: One language setting for UI and questions asked for a language flag; a flag can''t stand for es (no single country) and would mislabel es vs es-ES. The endonym is TV-readable and unambiguous. Under the menu button keeps it clear of the corner error line. Y is free on Start (replay is Question-only).', '', 'Top right on Start, under the ☰ menu button: a globe icon plus the current language''s endonym (ENDONYMS, e.g. «Español (Latinoamérica)»), no national flag (es is Latin American Spanish). Key per catalog screen.start.languageKey: I (es, es-ES), L (en), S (de), in Start''s collision set of check-literals; pad Y (button 3) via Start''s Scope.pad. Opens the first-start Language screen with a «Atrás» button (Backspace / B) back to Start; hidden while the save notice shows.', NULL, '2026-10-14T07:53:17Z', '2026-10-14T07:53:17Z', 1020, NULL, 'rule', 1020, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (158, 'Bundle selection in every mode, apart from customization', 'answered', '[]', 'From `decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles` (problem 5), task 1017. Supersedes `decision 51: «Solo o en grupo»: which bundles does a game play?` (solo plays the language''s defaults, no bundle choice) and the parts of `decision 38: Base bundles and bundle languages` / `decision 33: Configure game screen: which fields?` that keep the fresh default (base only) to the configure screen: it now holds in solo too, so a non-base mod bundle is off by default in solo as well. D-97 in plans/decisions.md.', '', '«Solo o en grupo» shows the shared BundleSelector (letter keys, mouse, pad) like gamemaster mode; bundle selection is its own section in every mode, never part of «Personalizar partida» nor counted in customized; preset in both modes = playerChoice: the player''s newest game''s bundles, else the locale''s first base bundle with non-base bundles off (decision 33)', NULL, '2026-10-14T08:15:16Z', '2026-10-14T08:15:16Z', 1017, NULL, 'rule', 1017, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (159, 'Svelte runtime as one file: vendor/svelte.js', 'answered', '[]', 'decision 149: Readable build costs +0.14 s at start on your PC: keep it? → bundle the runtime; decision 145: Svelte runtime ships with every export for precompiled mod components. One file serves all specifiers: the only names svelte and svelte/internal/client share (tick, untrack) are the same bindings, so export * keeps them; one module = one runtime instance, no shared chunk needed. preserveModules can''t group modules, hence the nested build (Vite''s own build(), no new dependency). Replaces decision 124''s vendor/svelte/src/… paths for the runtime; our src/ paths unchanged. Measured (task 1025): launch → first screen 529 ms vs. 573 ms with the per-file runtime, 457 ms hashed.', '', 'One file vendor/svelte.js (+ .map): every svelte and svelte/* import in our build points at /vendor/svelte.js; a second Vite build in vite.config.ts''s svelteRuntime() plugin bundles an entry of export * from svelte, svelte/internal/client, svelte/internal/disclose-version and every other svelte/* we import; precompiled mod components rewrite their svelte imports to /vendor/svelte.js', NULL, '2026-10-14T15:54:44Z', '2026-10-14T15:54:44Z', 1025, NULL, 'rule', 1025, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (160, 'Translation prompts: add the style guide''s address and glossary?', 'answered', '["approve as drafted", "{style} placeholder: prompt(..., locale=) pastes the guide''s Address and Glossary sections", "no change: prompts stay as they are"]', '`task 801: Translation prompts follow the style guides (decision draft)`: the question prompts (`authoring/tools/prompts/locale-<l>.md`, filled into house style''s Language section) should address players the way the UI style guides (`app/client/src/locales/style/<locale>.md`) do. The draft below changes only what applies to question texts.

Findings
- The guides are mostly UI-only: Esc rows, Steam terms, shortcut letters, `Prompt` chip, button length; none of it appears in questions. Pasting a whole guide (or a `{style}` placeholder pulling its sections) adds noise and can contradict the pool.
- The Spanish pool addresses one generic «tú» (about 470 of 1211 questions: «Escucha: …», «si estornudas…», «tu papá parqueando»); the UI addresses the group with «ustedes». A generic «tú» in a joke isn''t group address, so `es` keeps it.
- Real conflict only in `de`: `locale-de.md` says «du» (one player) or «ihr» (the team); the `de` guide says never assume a plural (TV check 2026-10-13).
- No `locale-es-ES.md`: questions are neutral `es` for both Spanish markets (decision 27: Spanish variety); the es-ES guide''s «vosotros» is UI-only.

Recommended: a short block pasted into each prompt (not a placeholder): only the rules that fit questions, readable as the prompt the developer approves, no parsing of guide sections.

Draft
- `locale-de.md`: replace the line «Address the players with "du" (one player) or "ihr" (the team), never "Sie".» with:
  - Address (UI style guide `de`): never assume a plural: no "ihr", "euch", "euer", no plural imperatives ("Hört zu", "Schaut"). Where the Spanish speaks to the players ("tú"), use a generic "du" ("Hör zu: …", "wenn du niest") or an impersonal form ("Zu hören ist …"); never "Sie".
  - Quotes in the text fields: „…" (German quotes).
- `locale-en.md`: add
  - Address (UI style guide `en`): "you", for one player or the whole family; never "you all", "you guys", "yourselves".
  - Quotes in the text fields: "…" (curly double quotes).
- `locale-es.md`: extend the neutral-words line''s «"tú", never "vos" or "vosotros"» into its own bullet:
  - Address: one generic "tú" where a question speaks to the players ("Escucha: …", "si estornudas…"), as the pool does; never "vos", "vosotros", "usted". (The UI''s «ustedes» is for the game''s own prompts, not question texts.)
- Glossary: none of the guides'' terms occur in question texts; no glossary block. If one does later (a joker, «Steam»), the guide''s term holds.
- The guides get no change; the `translate-review.md` reviewer reads the same Language section, so it checks the new rules without an edit.

Options
- approve as drafted: the three edits above, `qgen validate`
- `{style}` placeholder: `prompt(..., locale=)` pastes the guide''s Address and Glossary sections into the Language section (UI-only rules included)
- no change: prompts stay as they are; `de` keeps «ihr» in question texts', '', 'approve as drafted', NULL, '2026-10-14T16:11:34Z', '2026-10-14T22:47:00Z', 801, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-14, task 801: Applied as drafted (task 801): locale-de.md replaces «du»/«ihr» with the style guide''s no-plural rule (generic «du» or impersonal, no ihr/euch/euer, never Sie) and adds German quotes „…“; locale-en.md adds address «you» (no «you all»/«you guys») and curly quotes; locale-es.md moves «tú» into its own Address bullet (generic tú, never vos/vosotros/usted; UI «ustedes» not for questions). No glossary block, no {style} placeholder, guides and translate-review.md unchanged. «ihr» in German question texts no longer holds.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (161, 'Screen gallery reviewed? (en)', 'answered', '["reviewed, flags in /gallery", "reviewed, nothing to fix"]', 'Review the screen gallery in `en` (`plan 100: UI wording: style guides, TV-check fixes, screen gallery`). Gallery rendered 2026-10-14 by `task 804: Screen gallery review decisions per UI language`: 44 shots, every visible text keyed.

