INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (165, 'Subcategory keys in code: bundle + name; base keeps bare names', 'answered', '[]', 'Decision 110 (d) makes a subcategory bundle + name. A one-string key where base keeps its bare name means existing saves (purged, swapped_to, notified_exhausted) stay valid without a save migration, and the frozen engine fixtures replay through a small normalizer. D-100 in plans/decisions.md.', '', 'Python: (bundle, name); engine, names files and reports: one string, base''s bare name, another bundle''s <bundle>/<name> (subKey, categories.sub_key)', NULL, '2026-10-14T18:25:57Z', '2026-10-14T18:25:57Z', 826, NULL, 'rule', 826, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (166, 'colombia subcategories (OQ-46): where the 19 go, and the list for 2000', 'answered', '["Proposed list as in the body (10 categories, 51 subcategories)", "Only map the 19 now (same targets), add more subcategories later from qgen batch --bundle colombia", "Changes (name them: renames, merges, moves, drops, additions)"]', '`task 827: colombia subcategories (OQ-46)`, `decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)` (d). Taxonomy is the developer''s.

## Today
- `colombia`: 109 questions (102 approved, 7 rejected), 6 categories, 31 subcategories (`app/data/bundles/colombia/categories.json`).
- 19 approved on `base` subcategories (pool checked): Historia 3, Piratas 2, Desiertos 2, Navidad 2, Mundiales de fútbol 2; Aves, Cuentos infantiles, Literatura, Islas, Reciclaje, Árboles, Deportes extremos, Museos 1 each.
- Scale: `base` 198 subcategories for a 5000 target (~25 each); 2000 over 51 subcategories ≈ 40 each (narrow ones like «Feria de las Flores» fewer, broad ones like «Animales de Colombia» more).

## Proposal (new = *, ← the 19 moved there)
1. Colombia (existing): Regiones de Colombia; *Departamentos de Colombia; Ciudades de Colombia; Ríos de Colombia; *Paisajes de Colombia ← Desiertos 2 (Taroa, Tatacoa); *Destinos turísticos de Colombia ← Deportes extremos 1 (San Gil); Símbolos patrios de Colombia
2. *Naturaleza de Colombia: Animales de Colombia (moved from 1); *Aves de Colombia ← Aves 1; *Plantas y flores de Colombia ← Árboles 1 (palma de cera); Parques naturales de Colombia (moved from 1); *Islas y mares de Colombia ← Islas 1 (Gorgona)
3. *Historia de Colombia: *Historia de Colombia ← Historia 1 (Panamá 1903); *Independencia de Colombia ← Historia 2 (Grito, Boyacá); *Colombia colonial y piratas ← Piratas 2 (murallas de Cartagena, fuertes); *Culturas precolombinas de Colombia ← Museos 1 (Balsa Muisca, Museo del Oro); *Personajes históricos de Colombia
4. Fiestas, mitos y tradiciones de Colombia (existing 6) + *Navidad en Colombia ← Navidad 2 (novena)
5. Comida colombiana (existing 5) + *Café de Colombia
6. Música y gente de Colombia (existing 3) + *Vallenato, *Instrumentos musicales colombianos
7. *Arte, letras y pantalla de Colombia: *Literatura colombiana ← Literatura 1 (María), Cuentos infantiles 1 (El renacuajo paseador); *Pintores y artistas colombianos; *Artesanías colombianas; *Cine y televisión colombianos
8. Deporte colombiano (existing 5) + *Colombia en los Mundiales ← Mundiales de fútbol 2 (James, Linda Caicedo)
9. Así hablamos en Colombia (existing 2) + *Gentilicios colombianos (paisa, rolo, costeño…)
10. *Vida diaria en Colombia: *Vida cotidiana en Colombia ← Reciclaje 1 (canecas); *Billetes y monedas de Colombia; *Transporte en Colombia (chiva, TransMilenio, Metrocable)

- Totals: 10 categories (4 new), 51 subcategories (20 new); every one of the 19 lands on a `colombia` subcategory; none repeats a `base` name except the category «Historia de Colombia» shares its name with its own subcategory (fine within a bundle? if not, the category becomes «Historia colombiana»).
- Names en/de: drafted by `qgen` after the answer, not part of this decision.

## Options
1. The list above.
2. Only the 19''s targets now (Historia de Colombia, Independencia…, etc. as above), nothing else new; more subcategories later.
3. Changes: name them.', '', 'i want to completely rework the categories of the colombia regional question bundle. my suggestion: keep a general list of categories for regional question bundles. this needs to be created and will be an ingredient to generate regional question bundles later. then: use this list as a starting point and add categories based on the actual region. then: follow our general strategy to derive subcategories and concepts for question generation.

given that we have already questions in the colombia bundle: final step (only for this colombia regional bundle): work the existing questions into the bundle-specific categories and subcategories: if no suitable subcategory or category can be found, add it. otherwise change the questions subcategory to the fitting existing one', NULL, '2026-10-14T18:27:43Z', '2026-10-15T15:02:27Z', 827, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 827: 2026-10-15, task 827: the rework is plan-sized: `plan 138: Regional taxonomy: a general list, colombia reworked` (310): general regional category list (pm decision), `qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>` (propose/apply), colombia''s taxonomy (pm decision), remap of all colombia questions + validate rule. `task 827: colombia subcategories (OQ-46)` dropped; `task 752: Close-out of regional packs` and `task 643: Regional pilot colombia: start` wait for plan 138.

2026-10-16, task 1140: `qgen remap --bundle colombia` (new: opus proposal in work/remap/colombia/, then --apply) moved all 109 colombia questions onto decision 249''s list: 91 changed subcategory (the 19 on base subcategories included), no subcategory or category added; concepts per BN-13: 17 kept, 41 cleared; concept lists renamed to «Frutas de Colombia», «Fútbol colombiano de clubes», «Parques naturales y ecosistemas de Colombia», 7 deleted. qgen validate: a question''s subcategory must be in its own bundle''s list (D-100''s grace gone). D-109 in plans/decisions.md; 22-bundles.md, 15c RG-6, README.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (167, 'Translation prompt for a regional bundle (en for colombia)', 'answered', '["a: the draft as written: prompts/translate-region.md, added to translate, rate, review, fix and audit in a regional bundle''s tr-* run", "b: the draft, but questions about a regional word or saying don''t travel (about_spanish as for base)", "c: no regional note: colombia translated for locale-en''s market as is (players not in Colombia)"]', '', '', 'a, with changes:
- Market prompts say nothing about where the players are or aren''t (no "not in Colombia", no countries); spelling and usage standards stay:
  - `prompts/locale-en.md`: first bullet "All content is in English." (no "for families in the United States and the United Kingdom"); "Names and titles as English speakers know them"; the "players are not in Colombia" bullet becomes "Difficulty and distractors on the same scale 1–15 (the calibration examples are about Spanish speakers, the scale isn''t)."
  - `prompts/locale-de.md`: the same: "All content is in German: standard German, spelled as in Germany (with "ß")."; "as German speakers know them"; same difficulty bullet
- `prompts/translate-region.md`: the draft as written, except the difficulty bullet drops "where the section above says the players are not in the region, read:": "Difficulty and distractors: they live outside the region but know what such a family talks about at home; less than someone living there, more than the general market. Judge difficulty (scale 1–15) and distractors for them."', NULL, '2026-10-14T18:31:51Z', '2026-10-15T15:19:47Z', 829, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 829: Applied by task 829: authoring/tools/prompts/translate-region.md (the draft, difficulty bullet as answered), appended to the locale block in translate, rate, review, fix and audit of a regional bundle''s tr-* run (qgen.py prompt(..., bundle=), run.json bundle); locale-en.md and locale-de.md no longer name countries or player location; D-87, 15b, directory.md note it.

2026-10-16, task 1202: decision 241: Calibration examples for an international English pool: apply? (task 1202): locale-en.md''s and locale-de.md''s difficulty bullet no longer says the calibration examples are about Spanish speakers; the examples are international now.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (168, 'Store texts name only the built game modes', 'answered', '[]', 'task 666: Store texts per language in 17a (LUI-6). Plan 88''s rule: no claim the game can''t keep. BUILT_MODES has two modes today; rr-coop, rr-competitive and timed are MD-8 (plans/13-game-modes.md), not built.', '', 'Store texts (plans/17a-store-page.md) list Gamemaster mode and Alone or as group only; the three multiplayer modes of D-74 join the texts when MD-8 ships them', NULL, '2026-10-14T18:37:15Z', '2026-10-14T18:37:15Z', 666, NULL, 'rule', 666, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (169, 'Store texts approved? (en)', 'pending', '["Approved as drafted", "Approved with fixes (list them)"]', 'Read plans/17a-store-page.md, section ''Store texts'' (fields and limits) and its ''en'' block(s): name, short description (≤ 300), About This Game with feature bullets, privacy line, controller line.
- Wording from the in-game catalogs (mode and joker names, Steam terms).
- Modes: only the two built ones (Gamemaster mode, Alone or as group); multiplayer modes join when MD-8 ships them.
- Privacy line deviates from plan 88''s ''collects nothing, sends nothing'': the build sends opt-in telemetry (plan 106) and a question report on the player''s click (decision 93), so the line says ''only sends something if you allow it''. Confirm or reword.
- Controller line names gamepads, keyboard and mouse, no ''full controller support'' (decision 90: Partial).
- Language note: until pool.en.json ships, the page says the questions are in Spanish for now (decision 80, D-96).
- A native-speaker read by LUI-5''s testers (plan 69) where one is available.
Answer ''approved'', or list fixes (they go into a follow-up task of plan 88).', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T18:37:16Z', NULL, 666, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
