- Says: free, needs the base game, optional install, off by default (switched on in the «Paquetes de preguntas» step), its own Steam achievement (BUNDLE_COLOMBIA), grows with updates; no question count (`decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)`).
- es-ES: the es text unchanged (pack in Colombian Spanish, «ustedes»); say if you want a vosotros version.
- en: drafted, entered only once app/data/bundles/colombia/pool.en.json ships.
Answer ''approved'', or list fixes (they go into a follow-up task of plan 88).', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T19:14:48Z', NULL, 783, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (174, 'Store requirements: beta test distro and real-pad run?', 'pending', '["Answer after the beta test: Linux distro (name, version) the beta ran on, if any; real-pad run passed yes/no (failing step if no)", "Keep provisional values (Ubuntu 22.04, Partial) for the beta store page"]', '`task 1028: Store requirements: storage after the media bundle, Linux distro after the beta test` needs inputs that don''t exist yet (2026-10-14):
- Storage: the media bundle (`task 260: write plan: Media bundle for shipping (SW-9)`, still unplanned) hasn''t written `app/desktop/build/media/`; today it holds the raw cache copy (2.55 GB), already measured by `task 688` (3 GB estimate stays).
- Linux OS row: the non-Nix start test is the Steam beta test (decision 39, `task 263: write plan: Beta test and S5 close-out`); not played yet.
- Controller Full (decision 90): needs your real-pad run: start → new player via letter picker or Steam''s floating keyboard → victory, pad only.
- en/de Subtitles: wait for `pool.en.json` / `pool.de.json` (decision 80).

Answer once the beta test is played (the beta upload needs the media bundle, so storage can be measured then too):
- distro and version played on, if Linux; else "none"
- real-pad run: passed, or the failing step', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T19:40:33Z', NULL, 1028, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (175, 'Store texts: modding bullet and guide link?', 'answered', '["approved as drafted", "link only on the Workshop page, no store bullet", "changes: …"]', 'Plan 121 part 4 (`task 990: Store page and Workshop texts: modding bullet and guide link`). Drafts: `plans/17a-store-page.md` section "Modding" (en, es, es-ES, de): one feature bullet per language in About This Game''s Features list, a link line to the guide `https://github.com/rubenmoor/trivia/blob/main/modding/README.md` (decision 134, English only, marked «en inglés» / «auf Englisch»), and the Workshop hub description per language with the link.

en bullet: «Make it yours: question bundles, themes and full mods, shared on the Steam Workshop»

Link rules: no web access at the task, so from memory, recheck at entry: About This Game accepts BBCode [url] links, Steam routes them through its link filter; no links to other stores. Not known whether Steamworks'' Workshop configuration has a description field; else the community hub''s first (pinned) announcement carries the text. If Valve''s review rejects the link in About This Game: keep the bullet, the link stays on the Workshop page only.

Timing: entered at launch (milestone 11) once the Workshop works for players (plan 122), not on the beta page.', '', 'approved as drafted', NULL, '2026-10-14T20:25:31Z', '2026-10-16T01:43:37Z', 990, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 990: plans/17a-store-page.md: Modding section marked approved; each language block (en, es, es-ES, de) gets an ''At launch'' line placing the modding bullet and guide link; task 672: Store page entry checklist and PUB-8 close-out gains launch rows ''modding bullet per language'' and ''guide link'' (entered at milestone 11 after plan 122''s check, never on the beta page).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (176, 'Store names pass PUB-7?', 'answered', '["Pass all three (recommended: no live identical mark in classes 9/41, no Steam game of that name)", "Pass some (list which; the rest reopen OQ-34)", "Fail: reopen OQ-34"]', 'Name and trademark check for the three store names (`plan 129: Partner account, name check and AI terms (PUB-6, PUB-7, PUB-10)`, `task 1038: PUB-7 name and trademark check: findings and decision`). Full findings table: `plans/17-publishing.md` "Name check (PUB-7)", read 2026-10-14. Not legal advice; a professional clearance search is optional, your call.

- «Living Room Trivia» (en): no Steam game, no exact mark (USPTO, TMview: EUIPO, EU national offices, WIPO Madrid), no exact app; livingroomtrivia.com free. Riskiest: «LIVING ROOM» word marks in classes 9/41 (AT 538/2018, Thomas E. Pausch; FR 4360442 «THE LIVING ROOM», Bercy Services XXIX; US 97883498/97883506 nightclub events and music, 78698523 cinemas), none for games; an Instagram account «Living Room Trivia» (93 followers).
- «Trivia en Familia» (es): no Steam game, no mark with «trivia» + «familia». Riskiest: «EN FAMILIA» class 41 in Spain (M2994232, Asociación Española de Pediatría) and Chile (TVN); app «Trivia Family - En Español» (TITANWARE SL) on the Spanish App Store. .com and .com.co free; .es likely free.
- «Wohnzimmer-Quiz» (de, `decision 78: German store name (PUB-8, D-50): keep «Living Room Trivia» or a localized one?`): no Steam game, no mark, no app. Closest: «Wohnzimmerwissen» (DE, classes 9/41/44, filed), «WORLD WIDE WOHNZIMMER» (DE, 9/41). wohnzimmer-quiz.de free.
- Gaps: WIPO Global Brand Database (captcha; Madrid marks covered via TMview), BoardGameGeek (blocked) and a general web search for the es/de names weren''t reachable.

Pass → D-50 and OQ-34 final, `task 1039: PUB-7 result: store names final or OQ-34 reopened` updates the plans. Fail → OQ-34 reopens as a new decision with new name candidates.', '', 'Pass all three (recommended: no live identical mark in classes 9/41, no Steam game of that name)', NULL, '2026-10-14T21:43:29Z', '2026-10-15T20:42:44Z', 1038, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 1039: D-50 and OQ-34 final for «Living Room Trivia», «Trivia en Familia», «Wohnzimmer-Quiz» (plans/decisions.md, open-questions.md, 11-steam.md, 17-publishing.md PUB-7 [x], 17a-store-page.md, 18-steam-integration.md); build rename follow-up in plan 89.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (177, 'Steamworks app created? App ID?', 'pending', '["Created: App ID …, app credit paid on YYYY-MM-DD, label …", "Not yet"]', 'The checklist is in plans/17-publishing.md, section "Steamworks signup (PUB-6)" (`plan 129: Partner account, name check and AI terms (PUB-6, PUB-7, PUB-10)`). Start with the advisor check (`decision 67: Steamworks account holder (OQ-33): person or company?`); the questions are ready there. Then: partner signup, the $100 app credit, bank details, tax interview (W-8BEN), app creation (the name follows PUB-7''s decision).
Report in the answer:
- App ID
- payment date of the app credit (release comes ≥ 21 days later)
- store Developer/Publisher label
`task 1041: PUB-6 result: App ID and payment date into the plans` waits on this answer.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T21:44:54Z', NULL, 1040, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (178, 'Start the first content patch?', 'pending', '["go: version 1.0.<n>", "not yet (why)"]', 'First content patch after launch, per `plans/11-steam.md` "Content updates (ST-5)" (`plan 96: Content updates as patches (ST-5)`). Answer `go` only when every precondition is ✓:

| precondition | how it''s checked | ✓/✗ |
|---|---|---|
| Released | decision "Released? date, build id" (`plan 95: Launch`) answered and recorded by `task 710` | |
| Cadence due (decision 96: monthly, only if ≥ 100 new approved per launch language or a player-reported fix is waiting) | `qgen patch-notes v1.0.0`: "added" per locale (es, en, de); at 2026-10-14 no `v1.0.0` tag yet, so no numbers: fill them in when answering | |
| Reports pulled, fixes done | `qgen flag --pull` run; every reported question reworked or dropped (`/review?status=needs_work` holds no player report) | |
| Pool clean | `qgen export && qgen validate` exit 0 | |

Options: `go: version 1.0.<n>` (the next patch number after the newest `v*` tag; minor if `SAVE_VERSION` changed, decision 91), `not yet (why)`.
On `go`, `task 714: First content patch candidate` bumps the version, drafts the notes and raises `Release candidate v<x> passed?`.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T21:47:16Z', NULL, 713, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (179, 'Steamworks app configured (SW-7)? IDs?', 'pending', '["configured: App ID …, depots windows … linux … content …, colombia DLC … depot …", "not yet", "issues (rows)"]', 'After `decision 177: Steamworks app created? App ID?`. Follow `plans/18-steam-integration.md` "Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)" (`plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)`), tick its rows, then report:
- App ID; depot IDs `windows`, `linux`, `content`; `colombia` DLC app ID + its depot ID
- `beta` branch created (password-protected; don''t write the password here)
- Gamepad template set as Steam Input default
- Steam Cloud (Auto-Cloud) values entered
- launch options (Windows `Trivia.exe`, Linux/SteamOS `trivia`)
- rich presence uploaded (`app/desktop/steam-presence.vdf`)
- published
- issues: the failing rows

`decision 89: Steamworks App ID, depot IDs and beta branch entered? (for the first beta upload)` asks for the same IDs: answer it "see decision <this one>".
Not here: achievements (`decision 140: Achievements entered and published in Steamworks?`), Workshop (`decision 135: Steamworks: enable Workshop for ¡Trivia! and a second Steam account?`), store page (`task 672: Store page entry checklist and PUB-8 close-out`).', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T21:52:12Z', NULL, 1044, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (180, 'AI disclosure approved?', 'pending', '["Approved as drafted", "Approved without the code sentence", "Fixes: (list)"]', 'Draft in plans/17a-store-page.md, section ''AI disclosure'' (task 667: AI disclosure text (Steam survey + store wording)): survey answers (pre-generated yes, live-generated no), store text en, es, es-ES (diff), de, and a colombia DLC line (es, en). Points to check:
- Honesty about review: 745 of the 1,134 approved base questions were approved by the LLM review only (D-32, D-33); 389 by you. D-56''s blind human spot checks: none recorded yet. So the text says ''reviewed by the developer or by a separate AI review'', not ''a person approves every question''. Native-speaker playtests (LUI-5) aren''t claimed because none are recorded; add them if they''ve happened.
- Code: Valve''s January 2026 survey update (from memory) says dev tools such as code assistants aren''t the focus. The draft discloses code anyway, because players see and hear what the code produces: the tower, glyphs, the capsule template (decision 77: disclosed as AI-assisted) and the synthesized UI sound effects. Option: drop the code sentence and keep only the store art and graphics/sounds part.
- Unchecked (the worker had no web access; part 9 rechecks at entry, task 259): Valve''s current page and form (partner.steamgames.com/doc/gettingstarted/contentsurvey), whether the description field is localized or English only, its length limit, and whether each DLC app has its own survey (if not, the colombia line goes unused).
- No ''Claude''/''Anthropic'' in public text (PUB-10, trademarks).', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T21:53:55Z', NULL, 667, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (181, 'Content survey answers approved? (PUB-9)', 'pending', '["Approved as drafted, B1 (a): replace the 3 pictures, B2 ''no violence'', no IARC", "Approved with IARC changed (state)", "Fixes: (list, e.g. B1 (b) or (c))"]', 'Draft: plans/17a-store-page.md, section ''Content survey (PUB-9)'' (task 1047: Content survey and age rating: research and draft (PUB-9)); Valve''s pages read 2026-10-14, cited there.

Valve today: the survey has three sections (General Content → Steam''s own generated ratings, e.g. Germany and Indonesia; Mature Content → descriptors that drive customers'' filters; Generative AI). Germany hides unrated games since 2024-11-15 and accepts Valve''s survey rating. Some answers can''t be changed after approval without Steam Support.

Scan of the shipped pools (base 1,032, colombia 102, es; 1,146 Commons media): no sex, gore, profanity, gambling or purchases; war, death, crime only as history, myth and cartoons in text; alcohol named in 3 questions, never shown; no chat, no online play; question reports and telemetry only on the player''s click / opt-in; Workshop mods tagged by their creators.

Proposed: General Content all ''no'' (or the lowest ''references'' level for historical war and alcohol mentions, if the form has one); Mature Content: no descriptor; AI: decision 180''s text. Expected ratings like Bible Trivia''s (Germany 6, IGRS 3).

Borderline:
- B1 nudity, 3 pictures: q-0135 (figure-drawing study with genitals, illustrative for ''skin''), q-0747 (Farnese Hercules, full-frontal statue, the picture is the question), q-0852 (Botticelli''s Birth of Venus). (a) replace them before the build goes to review, answer ''no nudity'' (recommended; then a follow-up task swaps the three pictures, and future pools stay nudity-free or the survey changes via Steam Support); (b) keep, descriptor 1 ''Some Nudity or Sexual Content'' (families filtering nudity may not see the game); (c) keep, descriptor 5 ''General Mature Content'' with a note.
- B2 war history (Bastille painting q-0108, WWII and battle questions): ''no violence'' (recommended) or ''historical references, non-graphic''.

IARC: none (recommended). Steam doesn''t offer it; Germany/Indonesia use Valve''s rating; IARC-generated USK ratings from other stores must not be entered.

DLC colombia: DLC apps carry their own descriptors and ratings on the store, so expect its own survey (same answers, no nudity); its AI line in 17a ''Free DLC (colombia)'' stays.

Decision 180''s open points: the description field''s localization and length limit aren''t on Valve''s public pages, only in the form: checked at entry; the AI draft is unchanged.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T22:01:20Z', NULL, 1047, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (182, 'Price, regional prices and launch discount? (PUB-11)', 'pending', '["$9.99, Valve''s regional matrix, launch discount 15 % for 7 days", "other base price (state)", "no launch discount", "other launch discount (% 10–40, days 7–14)"]', 'PUB-11, `plan 131: Content survey, rating and price (PUB-9, PUB-11)`; binding `decision 66: Price model (OQ-33): how is the game sold on Steam?` ($9.99 "for now; final check at PUB-11"). Details and sources: `plans/17-publishing.md` "Price (PUB-11)" (Valve''s docs read 2026-10-14).

## Summary
- Base: $9.99, paid one-time. Comparables today: Jackbox packs $24.99–29.99, Millionaire $29.99, Trivia Murder Party 3 $14.99, indie party quizzes $11.99–14.99 (Party Quiz, Trivia Tricks, Trivia About You, Papa''s Quiz), small quizzes $9.99 (The You Quiz, Trivia War), $1–5 single-topic packs. $9.99 sits at the low end of party trivia, fine for ~1,000 Spanish questions and free packs.
- Regional: accept Valve''s suggested prices in Steamworks → Propose Pricing for all 37 currencies + 4 region groups (the matrix is Valve Confidential, behind login; a missing currency = not buyable there). Valve reviews prices in 1–2 business days. Plausibility from $9.99 titles today: EUR ≈9.75–9.99, GBP ≈7–9, MXN ≈110–140, COP ≈23,500–27,000, Argentina (USD_LATAM) ≈$5.80–6.30.
- Launch discount: 15 % for 7 days ($8.49). Valve: 10–40 %, 7–14 days, suggests 10–15 %; set only before release, on the app landing page. Blocks other discounts until release + 37 days; seasonal sales open from release + 30 days (so release ≥ 30 days before a sale to join it); no price change in the first 30 days.
- DLC: `colombia` and every later pack a free DLC app ("This is a free product"), no price rows, own store page and review.

## Options
- 1 (recommended): as above.
- 2: other base price (state it), rest as above.
- 3: no launch discount.
- 4: other launch discount (state % 10–40 and days 7–14).', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T22:05:50Z', NULL, 1048, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (183, 'Content survey and prices entered in Steamworks? (PUB-9, PUB-11)', 'pending', '["Entered: survey submitted (date), prices entered (approved/pending), DLC free", "Not yet", "Issues (list the rows)"]', 'Checklist: `plans/17a-store-page.md` "Content survey and pricing: entry" (`task 1049: Content survey and pricing: entry checklist and the ''entered'' decision (PUB-9, PUB-11)`); field names from Valve''s public docs, recheck in the forms.

Answer only after these are answered: decision 177 "Steamworks app created? App ID?", decision 179 "Steamworks app configured (SW-7)? IDs?", decision 180 "AI disclosure approved?", decision 181 "Content survey answers approved? (PUB-9)", decision 182 "Price, regional prices and launch discount? (PUB-11)".

Please report:
