- `colombia` DLC: free
- Steamworks changes published
- launch discount: not entered now (launch day, plan 95)

Task 1050: Close-out of PUB-9 and PUB-11 waits on this answer.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-14T22:06:47Z', NULL, 1049, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (184, 'Freesound re-pick: which Commons sounds for q-0752 (mosquito) and q-1016 (turkey)?', 'answered', '["Pick in the review tool (/review?q=…, search modal): q-0752 ''File:Mosquito attack.ogg'' (CC0, 88 s) if it buzzes clearly near the start, else set it to needs_work; q-1016 ''File:Gobbler.ogg'' (Public domain, PD-author, 10.6 s, domestic gobble)", "q-1016 a xeno-canto wild turkey instead: ''Meleagris gallopavo - Wild Turkey XC134744.ogg'' (CC BY-SA 3.0, 29 s)", "Both to needs_work: no usable Commons sound; drop the Freesound picks without a replacement"]', '`task 1051: Freesound: re-pick its 2 audio slots from Commons, drop it from the audio order`; `decision 82: Freesound API for a paid Steam release (OQ-45): replace, ask, or family only?` → (a), D-103. No `qgen` path re-picks a single question''s media; D-36: picks only through the review tool, so the developer picks (needs a listen).

Done already: `freesound` out of `providers.ORDER["audio"]` (the review tool''s search modal now asks Commons only); `plans/23-media-providers.md` audio row, MP-6.

Commons candidates (allowlisted, D-45; searched 2026-10-14, review tool search terms in brackets):
- q-0752 «El zancudo» (Ronald Ross, malaria; search "mosquito buzzing"):
  - File:Mosquito attack.ogg: CC0, Yesthatbruce, 87.6 s; the only real mosquito recording; the rest are spoken-word pronunciations (LL-Q…, En-uk-mosquito)
- q-1016 «Pavo» (search "turkey gobble" or "Meleagris gallopavo"):
  - File:Gobbler.ogg: Public domain (PD-author, PD-pdsounds.org; worldwide, not US-only), bod, 10.6 s: shortest real gobble
  - File:Meleagris gallopavo - Wild Turkey XC134744.ogg: CC BY-SA 3.0, xeno-canto, 29.1 s (wild turkey)
  - other xeno-canto clips: XC104532 (102 s), XC104533 (118 s), XC136045 (173 s), XC320490, XC134155: long

After the picks the worker resumes task 1051: `qgen export`, no `freesound.org` URL left in `authoring/data/questions.json` / `app/data/pool.json`, `qgen validate`, `trivia-media sync --status approved`.', '', 'Both to needs_work: no usable Commons sound; drop the Freesound picks without a replacement', NULL, '2026-10-14T22:09:21Z', '2026-10-16T02:27:46Z', 1051, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1051: 2026-10-15, task 1051: q-0752 and q-1016 media slot unpicked (media.unpicked: no source_url/file_url/credit/licence fields; query and note kept), status needs_work with a human review naming decision 184; qgen export: no freesound.org URL or provider: freesound left in questions.json / pool.json. D-103''s ''re-picked from Commons'' no longer holds: plans/decisions.md (D-103 title, consequence line), plans/23-media-providers.md (Freesound row, MP-6), plans/open-questions.md, plans/11-steam.md, plans/project.md updated. qgen rework may give them a new audio pick (Commons only).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (185, 'Shipped media: formats, names and where the encode runs (SW-9)', 'answered', '[]', 'plan 132: Media bundle for shipping (SW-9). stage-media.mjs already builds build/media and pack-media.json that plan 89''s depots read; trivia-media is authoring tooling. WebP over AVIF: no AVIF encoder in the shell, slower, WebP meets the < 1 MB target. Deterministic names keep D-17''s keys without a manifest. Credits stay one list: credits.json lives in the OS depots and already covers every pack.', '', 'stage-media.mjs encodes: images WebP fit 3840×2160 (q 82→60 while > 1 MB), audio Opus 96 kb/s, video WebM VP9 ≤ 1080p, GIF/SVG as is; shipped name = cacheName''s stem + new extension (shippedName in resolve.mjs, resolver tries cacheName then shippedName); one CREDITS.md for all depots; budgets in app/desktop/media-budget.json', NULL, '2026-10-14T22:12:28Z', '2026-10-14T22:12:28Z', 260, NULL, 'rule', 260, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (186, 'Language flags instead of the globe', 'answered', '[]', 'Developer, 2026-10-14 (milestone 6, plan 135: Playful icons and language flags before a game session): flags read faster and are more playful than a globe; several Latin American flags avoid the ''es is one country'' problem decision 157 raised, the endonym still names the language.', '', 'Start''s language button and each Language option show the language''s national flags (app/client/src/game/Flags.svelte, own simplified inline SVG, fixed colours, small overlapping fanned row, aria-hidden): es Mexico, Colombia, Argentina; es-ES Spain; en UK, US; de Germany, Austria, Switzerland; any other tag (a mod''s language) the globe icon. Supersedes the globe and ''no national flag'' of decision 157: Start''s language button: globe and endonym, key per catalog, pad Y; its key per catalog, pad Y, endonym and place stay.', NULL, '2026-10-15T02:04:37Z', '2026-10-15T02:04:37Z', 1082, NULL, 'rule', 1082, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (187, 'Icons and flags reviewed in /gallery?', 'answered', '["approved", "flags in /gallery"]', '`plan 135: Playful icons and language flags before a game session`: the new button icons (`Icon.svelte`) and language flags (`Flags.svelte`) on the screens before a game session; please review them in all four UI languages.

How to review:
- Screenshots are in `work/gallery/` (run 2026-10-14 by `task 1083: Gallery run and review decision for icons and flags`); to refresh: `trivia-gallery --only language,consent,start,language-from-start,start-resume,start-save-notice,player,player-delete-confirm,choice-gamemaster,choice-solo,customize,supply-notice,credits,mods,mods-notice,mods-crashed,mods-empty`
- `trivia-authoring` → `/gallery`: per locale, the shots above
- Flag what to change with a note: a drawing (unclear, not playful, wrong icon for the button), a flag (colours, shape, set per language), placement or size
- Known, already a task: choice-gamemaster shows solo mode (`task 1102: Gallery: choice-gamemaster shot stays on solo mode`)', '', 'flags in /gallery; country flags are awesome! joker icons still need work', NULL, '2026-10-15T02:10:56Z', '2026-10-15T15:27:11Z', 1083, NULL, 'once', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 1103: 2026-10-15, task 1103: no open review flags on the plan-135 shots (ui-flags.json: all fixed); flags approved as they are; no change to Icon.svelte, Flags.svelte or the screens. ''Joker icons still need work'' → `task 1135: Joker symbols: redraw to fit the kept names, decision first` in `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again` (joker symbols are plan 136''s; incl. symbols on Customize''s and Choice''s joker rows).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (188, 'Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)', 'answered', '[]', 'Milestone 9 "Joker names, defined again" (developer, 2026-10-14), `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`.

- One symbol per joker, the same in every language: today''s tray icons (`TOKENS` in `app/client/src/game/jokers.ts`): `hint` bulb, `skip` door, `easier` stairs, `category` compass, `snipe` crosshair; a new one only if an English answer needs it
- English names first, to fit the symbol (one decision per joker); `es`, `es-ES`, `de` translated from the English answers (one decision per locale, `task 1097: Decisions: es, es-ES, de joker names and keys`)
- `es` included: a decided exception to `decision 59: Neutral Spanish UI wording in es.ts (D-78)?`, so the family''s game gets the new names
- Replaces the old names: en `decision 40: English name for the hint joker «Soplo»?` … `decision 44: English name for the snipe joker «Francotirador»?` (Hint, Pass & Purge, Fairy, Ms Picky, Trick Shot); de `decision 54: German name for the hint joker «Soplo»?` … `decision 58: German name for the snipe joker «Francotirador»?` (Zaunpfahl, Näxt, Gang runter, Wunschzeit, Finte). Supersede links: the developer''s to set (a worker may not supersede a human answer)
- Stays: code ids, Steam API names (`FIRST_SOPLO` …), save fields; keys follow `decision 53: Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?` (mnemonic per catalog, `check:literals`)', '', 'names made in English to fit one shared symbol; es, es-ES, de translated from them; es an exception to D-59', NULL, '2026-10-15T02:13:18Z', '2026-10-15T02:13:18Z', 1096, NULL, 'rule', 1096, '2026-10-16, task 1098: applied in D-108 (plans/decisions.md): es/es-ES/de catalogs carry the new names, es changed as the D-59 exception; style guides list old names as bad patterns; plans 09, 15a, 04, 13 updated; store/achievement texts left to task 1100');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (189, 'Supersede decisions 40–44 and 54–58 with decision 188?', 'answered', '["yes, links set", "no, keep the old ones in the log"]', '`decision 188: Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)` records the milestone 9 rule (developer, 2026-10-14) that replaces the old joker names. pm refuses a worker superseding a human answer, so the links are missing and the old names still show in `pm decision list --answered`.

How (developer):
```sh
for d in 40 41 42 43 44 54 55 56 57 58; do pm decision supersede 188 $d; done
```
No task waits on this.', '', 'yes, links set', NULL, '2026-10-15T02:13:45Z', '2026-10-15T15:08:00Z', 1096, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (190, 'English name for the hint joker (symbol bulb)?', 'answered', '["Bright Idea (B)", "Brainwave (W)", "Lightbulb (L)", "Aha! (H)", "Hint (H), keep"]', '`decision 188: Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)`, `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`. ≤ 13 characters, playful, fitting the symbol; candidates in `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` "Joker names". The name also shows in «Use {name}?», the aria label, «no … left» errors, the hint notes («<name> 1/2/3»), `/comodines`. Key letter (mnemonic) in brackets; en Question screen keeps `A`–`D`, `R` (replay), `M` (flag) free.

- Does: shows the next of the question''s three hints, vague → strong; up to three per question
- Symbol: `bulb` (light bulb), stays for every candidate
- Today: es/es-ES «Soplo» (S), en «Hint» (H), de «Zaunpfahl» (Z)
- Why:
  - Bright Idea: the bulb is the cartoon «bright idea»; warm, family tone; notes «Bright Idea 2»
  - Brainwave: a sudden idea, a bit cheekier; `B` free for another joker
  - Lightbulb: names the symbol itself, clearest for kids, least playful
  - Aha!: the moment the bulb lights up, shortest; `A` is an answer key, so `H`
  - Hint: today''s name, plain (en style guide: joker names playful)', '', 'Hint (H), keep', NULL, '2026-10-15T02:13:46Z', '2026-10-15T14:43:11Z', 1096, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1098: applied in D-108 (plans/decisions.md): en name and key unchanged in en.ts; en style guide cites D-108');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (191, 'English name for the skip joker (symbol door)?', 'answered', '["Way Out (W)", "Door Slam (S)", "Back Door (K)", "Escape Hatch (E)", "Pass & Purge (P), keep"]', '`decision 188: Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)`, `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`. ≤ 13 characters, playful, fitting the symbol; candidates in `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` "Joker names". The name also shows in «Use {name}?», the skip dialog heading, the purge line («<name>: goodbye to “{topic}”»), «no … left» errors, `/comodines`. The dialog''s plain option stays its own leaf (`joker.skip.pass`, «Just pass»). Key letter (mnemonic) in brackets; `A`–`D`, `R`, `M` taken.

- Does: swaps the question for another card; optionally its whole topic leaves the game (stamp «GONE»)
- Symbol: `door` (a door with an arrow out), stays for every candidate
- Today: es/es-ES «Paso» (P), en «Pass & Purge» (P), de «Näxt» (N)
- Why:
  - Way Out: the door''s exit arrow, covers both skip and purge, short and clear
  - Door Slam: slamming the door on the question (and its topic), the most playful; `S` may collide with `easier`''s «Step Down»
  - Back Door: sneaking out, cheeky; `B` taken by «Bright Idea», so `K`
  - Escape Hatch: escape-room feel, 12 characters; a hatch, but the door symbol still reads
  - Pass & Purge: today''s name, says what it does, doesn''t fit the door', '', 'Pass & Purge (P), keep', NULL, '2026-10-15T02:13:46Z', '2026-10-15T14:56:50Z', 1096, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1098: applied in D-108 (plans/decisions.md): en name and key unchanged in en.ts; en style guide cites D-108');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (192, 'English name for the easier joker (symbol stairs)?', 'answered', '["Step Down (S)", "Easy Steps (E)", "Downstairs (W)", "Baby Steps (Y)", "Fairy (F), keep"]', '`decision 188: Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)`, `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`. ≤ 13 characters, playful, fitting the symbol; candidates in `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` "Joker names". The name also shows in «Use {name}?», the difficulty dial label, «no … left» errors, `/comodines`. Key letter (mnemonic) in brackets; `A`–`D`, `R`, `M` taken.

- Does: swaps the question for an easier one on the same topic; the difficulty dial turns down
- Symbol: `stairs` (steps with an arrow going down), stays for every candidate
- Today: es/es-ES «Bájale» (F), en «Fairy» (F), de «Gang runter» (G)
- Why:
  - Step Down: one step down the stairs, matches the dial too; closest to «Bájale»; `S` may collide with «Door Slam»
  - Easy Steps: the steps become easy, friendly
  - Downstairs: the symbol itself, playful sound; `D` is an answer key, so `W`
  - Baby Steps: playful, but may sound condescending to adults (as in `decision 42: English name for the easier joker «Bájale»?`)
  - Fairy: today''s name, doesn''t fit the stairs (would need a wand symbol)', '', 'Fairy (F), keep', NULL, '2026-10-15T02:13:46Z', '2026-10-15T14:57:05Z', 1096, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1098: applied in D-108 (plans/decisions.md): en name and key unchanged in en.ts; en style guide cites D-108');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (193, 'English name for the category joker (symbol compass)?', 'answered', '["Change Course (C)", "True North (N)", "Detour (T)", "Compass (O)", "Ms Picky (K), keep"]', '`decision 188: Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)`, `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`. ≤ 13 characters, playful, fitting the symbol; candidates in `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` "Joker names". The name also shows in «Use {name}?», the topic picker title («<name>: which topic do you want?»), «no … left» errors, `/comodines`. Key letter (mnemonic) in brackets; `A`–`D`, `R`, `M` taken.

- Does: the players pick another topic; the question is replaced by one of about the same difficulty from it
- Symbol: `compass`, stays for every candidate
- Today: es/es-ES «Cambiazo» (T), en «Ms Picky» (K), de «Wunschzeit» (W)
- Why:
  - Change Course: steer by the compass to a new topic; exactly 13 characters
  - True North: you set the direction you want, a little poetic; «True North: which topic do you want?» reads well
  - Detour: short, says «somewhere else»; `D` is an answer key, so `T` (collides with «Trick Shot», then `snipe` takes another letter)
  - Compass: the symbol itself, plain; `C` free, `O` if `C` is taken
  - Ms Picky: today''s name, doesn''t fit the compass', '', 'Ms Picky (K), keep', NULL, '2026-10-15T02:13:46Z', '2026-10-15T14:57:16Z', 1096, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1098: applied in D-108 (plans/decisions.md): en name and key unchanged in en.ts; en style guide cites D-108');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (194, 'English name for the snipe joker (symbol crosshair)?', 'answered', '["Trick Shot (T), keep", "Sharpshooter (S)", "Long Shot (L)", "Pot Shot (O)"]', '`decision 188: Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)`, `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`. ≤ 13 characters, playful, fitting the symbol; candidates in `plans/15a-ui-translation.md` "Joker names". The name also shows in «Use {name}?», the aim prompt («Pick the answer you think is wrong»), «no … left» errors, `/comodines`. Key letter (mnemonic) in brackets; `A`–`D`, `R`, `M` taken.

- Does: the players aim at the answer they think is wrong; a wrong one hit is crossed out and play goes on; hitting the right one loses the question and the level starts over
- Symbol: `crosshair` (already shown in `question/Scope.svelte`), stays for every candidate
- Today: es/es-ES «Francotirador» (X), en «Trick Shot» (T), de «Finte» (F)
- Why:
  - Trick Shot: today''s name already fits the crosshair; the trick is shooting a wrong answer; nothing to relearn
  - Sharpshooter: closest to «Francotirador», clear for kids, 12 characters; `S` may collide with «Step Down» / «Door Slam»
  - Long Shot: pun on the risky bet (the level may start over)
  - Pot Shot: casual, opportunistic shot, cheeky; `P` free if `skip` leaves it, else `O`', '', 'Trick Shot (T), keep', NULL, '2026-10-15T02:13:46Z', '2026-10-15T14:57:24Z', 1096, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1098: applied in D-108 (plans/decisions.md): en name and key unchanged in en.ts; en style guide cites D-108');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (195, 'Supply notice: bundles running out instead of exhausted subcategories', 'answered', '[]', 'Developer''s gallery flag (decision 161: Screen gallery reviewed? (en)): subcategory names in the question language meant nothing to the player. Per-bundle count instead of per-level Hall check: a small regional bundle can never fill every level alone, so per-level tightness would warn from the first game. ≤ 1 unseen keeps decision 31: Low-supply warning (super tight, no early notice). Keeping the field name avoids a v5 save across the TS and Python save code; a stale key only costs one missed or repeated notice (same trade as decision 165).', '', 'A chosen bundle is running out when, in the game''s difficulty window, some of its available questions are seen and at most 1 is unseen; the notice names it (displayName bundle); notified_exhausted holds bundle ids, old subcategory keys pruned at the next start, no save version bump', NULL, '2026-10-15T02:21:21Z', '2026-10-15T02:21:21Z', 1104, NULL, 'rule', 1104, '2026-10-15, task 1104: 2026-10-14, task 1104: outlook.ts runningOutBundles/noteRunningOut (Outlook.runningOut), SupplyNotice shows outlook.exhausted as a plural map with bundle names (en, es, de; es-ES override dropped, es impersonal), gallery demo save ''seen'' = base + colombia with colombia seen; plans 03, 04, decisions.md D-82 notes');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (196, 'Per-commit check: directory.md names every tracked file? (code review part 11)', 'answered', '["Yes: a committed script inside npm run check, failing on unnamed files and stale paths", "Release check only: trivia-release-check runs it, commits don''t", "No: directory.md stays a review item"]', '`task 589: Part 11: propose process changes as decisions` (milestone 13). AGENTS.md says "Every path: `directory.md`", but nothing checks it; workers add files without a row.
- Would have prevented (`code-review.md`): part 1 `### directory.md vs git ls-files`: 79 of 174 code/config files unnamed (64 in one row, fixed by task 525), `sim/` files, en/de pools read as existing; part 10 stale `authoring/ui/.gitignore` row (task 620); part 11 `engine/telemetry.ts`, `lib/telemetry.ts` unlisted (task 1109); 22 docs-drift rows overall (`directory.md`, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`), all low.
- Check: part 1''s throw-away `dircheck.py` as a committed script: every `git ls-files` path (minus data/prompts/media globs) named by backticks or a directory row; backticked paths that exist neither tracked nor on disk reported (gitignored/generated ones on an allow-list).
- Cost per commit: < 0.2 s, no dependency; a worker adding a file adds one `directory.md` line.
- Not the linter (`### Linter evaluation`, part 10): no linter reads docs.', '', 'directory.md is outdated, no need to keep it up-to-date as described above. adjust its purpose: it should only explain ultra-short the meaning of all .md files and directories on the top-level', NULL, '2026-10-15T03:12:06Z', '2026-10-15T15:04:31Z', 589, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 1114: 2026-10-15, task 1114: no directory.md check (no script, nothing in npm run check or trivia-release-check); directory.md rewritten to name only the top-level .md files and directories, one short line each; the per-path tables (app/, authoring/, state/, work/ rows) are gone and no longer maintained: workers no longer add a directory.md line per new file. README.md pointer reworded; code-review.md part 11 pending/process rows updated. Still says otherwise: AGENTS.md ''Every path: directory.md'' and milestone 13''s scope bullet (the developer''s to edit).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (197, 'Per-commit check: unused TS/JS exports? (code review part 11)', 'answered', '["Yes: committed scan inside npm run check, fails on DEAD and TESTONLY, allow-list for false positives", "Report only: printed by trivia-release-check, never fails", "No: unused exports stay a review item"]', '`task 589: Part 11: propose process changes as decisions` (milestone 13). Worker refactors leave exports behind (a caller moved, a feature rewired); `### Linter evaluation` (part 10) found that neither the five `tsconfig` flags nor Biome/oxlint/ESLint see unused exports: a gap the linter outcome leaves.
- Would have prevented (`code-review.md`): 34 unused-export rows (parts 1, 3–6, 8–11, all low), e.g. `bundleOf`/`MemoryStore` used only by tests (tasks 537, 538), `CARDS` exported while `Overlay.svelte` kept a copy (task 535), `buildCredits`; part 11 re-run: 7 `DEAD` raw, 2 real and new since part 1 (`ServerStore` after task 780, `modIssues()` never wired, `task 1112: Mods screen: show modIssues() per mod bundle`).
- Check: part 1''s throw-away `exports.py` (task 526, reproduced in part 1) as a committed script: fails on `DEAD` (no importer) and `TESTONLY` (only tests import it); allow-list for its known false positives (namespace imports, dynamic `import()`, `electron-builder.yml` hooks, Svelte component exports); `LOCAL` (exported, used only in its own file, 54) stays a report line, too noisy to fail on.
- Cost per commit: one pass over ~175 files, seconds; no dependency.', '', 'try to find a config or linter that checks and reports on unused exports and implement it in our pipeline. if that doesn''t exist, file a decision again', NULL, '2026-10-15T03:12:16Z', '2026-10-15T15:06:27Z', 589, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 1115: 2026-10-15, task 1115: knip 6.41 (root devDependency, knip.jsonc) instead of our own exports.py script; npm run check runs npm run knip = knip (unused exports, files, dependencies, binaries in app/client, authoring/ui, app/desktop, authoring scripts, modding/examples, report-server) + knip --production (! entries only, tests ignored: a test-only export fails; @internal keeps one on purpose). Exports used only in their own file now fail too (values; types stay exported); ServerStore ignored until task 765 (its body says to drop the entry). 17 exports un-exported, subcategories/subKeys and the Key type deleted, @tsconfig/svelte dropped from authoring/ui; flake.nix npmDepsHash updated. No new decision needed: the tool exists.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (198, 'Per-commit check for Python: ruff with a narrow rule set? (code review part 11)', 'answered', '["Yes: ruff in the dev shell, narrow rules (F, PLW1514 with preview), run by npm run check; the 3 hits fixed when adopted", "Yes, broader: also BLE and bugbear (B); deliberate sites marked noqa with a reason", "No: fix the 3 hits once, Python stays a review item"]', '`task 589: Part 11: propose process changes as decisions` (milestone 13). `### Linter evaluation` (part 10) covered TypeScript only; the ~40 Python files (`authoring/tools`, `authoring/server`, `authoring/steam`; `app/server` goes with task 765) have no check beyond review. 321 of 762 finding rows are on `.py` files.
- Would have prevented (`code-review.md`): 5 platform-encoding rows (text read/decoded without `encoding="utf-8"`, cp1252 on Windows: `qgen.costs` task 563, `health.batch_health` task 567, `engine.node` and `patch_notes.git` task 572, `gallery.py` manifest task 1111): ruff `PLW1514` `unspecified-encoding`; unused imports/locals (`F401`, `F841`).
- Trial 2026-10-14 (`nix shell nixpkgs#ruff`, ruff 0.15, `--preview --select F,PLW1514,BLE`): 4 hits, 3 real and new to the report: `authoring/server/main.py:95` unused `import pool_export`, `authoring/tools/qgen.py:2298` unused `versions` Counter, `authoring/steam/release_check.py:211` `read_text()` without encoding; 1 deliberate (`gallery.py:693` blind except, commented). Default rule set: 169 hits, all style (`E741`, `E701`, `E401`, `E731`): too noisy.
- Cost: ruff from nixpkgs in the flake dev shell (one binary, no npm/pip package); `ruff check` < 0.1 s per commit; a `ruff.toml` (or `pyproject` section) with the narrow selection.', '', 'Yes: ruff in the dev shell, narrow rules (F, PLW1514 with preview), run by npm run check; the 3 hits fixed when adopted', NULL, '2026-10-15T03:12:27Z', '2026-10-15T15:07:12Z', 589, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 1116: 2026-10-15, task 1116: ruff (nixpkgs) in the flake dev shell; ruff.toml at the root (select F, PLW1514; preview = true, explicit-preview-rules); npm run ruff (ruff check over git ls-files ''*.py'') is the last step of npm run check, so every commit runs it (D-73); 3 trial hits fixed (main.py unused pool_export import, qgen.py unused versions Counter, release_check.py read_text encoding), 0 hits, no noqa, no baseline; README dev-shell list and npm run check line, code-review.md ### Python check. Python is no longer a review-only item for unused names and platform encoding; broad excepts (BLE) stay a review item.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (199, 'AGENTS.md rule: import, don''t copy; a copy across a boundary names its source? (code review part 11)', 'answered', '["Yes: the rule in AGENTS.md", "Rule plus a copy detector (jscpd, new npm dependency) in npm run check", "No: copies stay a review item"]', '`task 589: Part 11: propose process changes as decisions` (milestone 13). The biggest finding cause: a worker sees its task''s files only and writes a helper, constant or CSS block again instead of finding the existing one.
- Would have prevented (`code-review.md`): 118 copy/duplication rows in all 11 parts (61 fixed, 12 won''t fix, 2 follow-ups), part 10''s 38 duplication clusters; e.g. five copies of the "newest game" `reduce` (part 4, task 541), `CARDS` re-declared in `Overlay.svelte` (task 535), `PLAYED_GROUP` copying `DEFAULT_AGE_GROUP` (task 577), report-server JSON parse 4× (task 1110), screen `section`/`.error-box`/`@keyframes` copied by the screen split (tasks 1106–1108), shell launch and demo-save builders 3× (`task 1113: Store and gallery scripts: one shell launcher and one demo-save builder`).
- Rule (AGENTS.md "Rules", one bullet): before writing a helper, constant, type or CSS block, `rg` for an existing one and import it (`authoring/` may import from `app/`); where importing is impossible (Python ↔ TS, `app/desktop` `.mjs` ↔ client TS, `report-server/`), a comment names the source.
- Cost per commit: none (a search the worker runs anyway); no dependency.
- Not the linter: no candidate in `### Linter evaluation` detects copies; a copy detector (e.g. jscpd) is option 2 and a new npm dependency.', '', 'Yes: the rule in AGENTS.md', NULL, '2026-10-15T03:12:42Z', '2026-10-15T21:08:29Z', 589, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15: AGENTS.md "Rules": bullet "Import, don''t copy" (rg first, import; cross-boundary copy names its source); no copy detector');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (200, 'AGENTS.md rule: after a move, rename or delete, fix every comment and doc naming the old? (code review part 11)', 'answered', '["Yes: the rule in AGENTS.md", "No: stale comments stay a review item"]', '`task 589: Part 11: propose process changes as decisions` (milestone 13). Comments and docstrings lie mostly because a later task moved or removed what they name, and only grepped code, not prose.
- Would have prevented (`code-review.md`): 39 lying/stale comment and docstring rows in parts 2–11 (35 fixed, 1 medium: `SAVE_VERSION` bump needing `save.py` too, task 532), e.g. `pool.ts` "Mirrors app/server/categories.py" after task 302, `rng.ts`/`pool.ts` pointing at the deleted `game.py` (task 537), `JokerTray`/`JokerFlight` "jokers are unlimited (D-27)" after decision 33 (tasks 547, 548), `main.mjs` "Stubs filled by later tasks" (task 554), padlock "CSS below" after the split (task 1106); plus docs-drift rows (`directory.md`, `README.md`) covered by `decision 196: Per-commit check: directory.md names every tracked file? (code review part 11)`.
- Rule (AGENTS.md "Rules", one bullet): after moving, renaming or deleting a file, function, constant or decided behaviour, `rg` its old name/path over code comments and `.md` files and fix every hit in the same commit.
- Cost per commit: one `rg` per moved name; no dependency, no check script (no tool tells a stale sentence from a true one).
- Not the linter: no lint rule reads comments.', '', 'Yes: the rule in AGENTS.md', NULL, '2026-10-15T03:12:42Z', '2026-10-15T21:08:33Z', 589, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15: AGENTS.md "Rules": bullet: after a move, rename or delete, rg the old name over comments and .md files, fix in the same commit');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (201, 'Recurring code review: who reviews new code after milestone 13? (code review part 11)', 'answered', '["Per milestone: one review item in pm''s cleanup_prompt over the milestone''s diff", "Per release: a review milestone over the diff since the last review", "No recurring review: milestone 13 stays a one-off"]', '`task 589: Part 11: propose process changes as decisions` (milestone 13). Milestone 13 reviewed the code once; other milestones kept adding code while it ran, and nothing reviews code as a whole after it.
- Evidence (`code-review.md` part 11 `### Completeness`, `### Scans`): 69 code/config files (~9400 lines: screens split, mods, telemetry, reports, achievements, gallery, store renders, dev server, report server) added during the milestone, unreviewed until tasks 1106–1111; those 6 tasks logged 53 rows: 9 bugs (2 medium: duplicate `{#each}` keys on the mods screen, task 1108; dev server killed by a dropped video in `resolve.mjs`, task 1111), 1 medium performance (`devserver.ts` read a 90 MB video whole per request, task 1111), 18 complexity (mostly copies from the split). Scan growth since part 1 came from the new files: `as` 118 → 146, `!` 74 → 90, swallowed `.catch` 21 → 38.
- Option 1: pm''s `cleanup_prompt` (`project-manager.toml`, "post-milestone cleanup") gets one item: review the files the milestone added or changed (`git diff` since its first commit) per milestone 13''s "What to look for", rows appended to `code-review.md`, larger fixes as tasks. Cost: one worker run per milestone, none per commit.
- Option 2: a review milestone before each release (`v1.0.0`, each content patch, decision 96 cadence), like milestone 13 but over the diff since the last review.
- Changing `project-manager.toml` and AGENTS.md is the developer''s (AGENTS.md "Outside pm workers").', '', 'Per milestone: one review item in pm''s cleanup_prompt over the milestone''s diff', NULL, '2026-10-15T03:12:51Z', '2026-10-15T21:08:38Z', 589, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15: project-manager.toml cleanup_prompt: new item, review the files the milestone added or changed per milestone 13 "What to look for", rows in code-review.md, larger fixes as tasks');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (202, 'Run qgen neutralize on base now?', 'answered', '["go", "not now"]', '`task 632: run neutralize-1`, `plan 64: Spanish variety (neutral Spanish)` (decision 27: base in es-419, colombia keeps its voice; decision 32: prompts approved, RAE numbers). Runs before the translation pilot (D-81).

`qgen neutralize --dry-run` (scan done, $4.18 spent; `work/neutralize-1/`):
- 388 of 1066 base questions flagged (Colombianisms like plata, carro→…, gaseosa, computador, afán; many are only number formatting 10.000 → 10 000)
- 26 with no neutral form, left as they are (carro, papas, durazno, arveja, ají, patineta, …)
- estimated rest: about $47.80 at list price ($0.12 per flagged question, $0.05 per audit call × 60)

"go": the worker runs `qgen neutralize` (no arguments; continues from this scan), then `task 633: QC neutralize-1`.
"not now": tasks 632 and 633 dropped.', '', 'go', NULL, '2026-10-15T03:34:24Z', '2026-10-15T15:27:48Z', 632, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (203, 'Spot check backaudit-1 done?', 'pending', '["done"]', 'Back-audit pilot slice for `plan 57: Release quality bar and back-audit (CT-5)`: 100 of the oldest approved questions (pilot 73, first-120 27) were audited by opus. 19 have a major finding (19 %); report: authoring/reports/backaudit-1.md. Cost: $3.77, about $0.038 per question.
Blind spot check: 30 random approved questions of the slice, decide each one without seeing the audit. Start `trivia-authoring`, then open http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?run=backaudit-1&sample=1 (about 15 min).
Afterwards, the 19 flagged questions with the audit notes: http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?run=backaudit-1&audit=flagged. Send to needs_work whatever you want reworked; `qgen rework` runs only when you ask for it.
Answer once the 30 are decided. Then task 339 runs `qgen report --qc backaudit-1` (release bar, decision 15) and asks the cost decision for the remaining slices.', '', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-15T03:41:00Z', NULL, 339, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (204, 'Translation pilot done (tr-en-1, tr-de-1)?', 'irrelevant', '["done"]', '`task 463: Release budget per language (pm decision, CT-3)` needs the translation pilot''s cost numbers (`qgen report --cost`, `tr-<locale>-*` runs). Today (2026-10-14) no `work/tr-en-1`, `work/tr-de-1` or `authoring/reports/tr-*-1.md` exist: `task 634: run tr-en-1` … `task 638: Translation pilot go/no-go en, de (QT-5)` all wait on decision 202 (Run qgen neutralize on base now?).
Answer "done" once tasks 634–638 are done (pilot run, QC''d, go/no-go answered); then task 463 builds the release budget table.', '', NULL, 'developer, 2026-10-16: no dollar budget (milestone 9), task 463 dropped', '2026-10-15T03:42:39Z', '2026-10-16T03:52:25Z', 463, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (205, 'batch-8 fails at media: how to go on?', 'answered', '[]', 'qgen batch (batch-8) exited 1 at `media` three runs in a row (runs 3–5 of task 51; runs 1–2 failed at rate and revise, then got past them). Always the same item: q-1425 (Eurovisión, "Jaja Ding Dong", media query "Iceland map outline", stimulus map_outline). Looks deterministic (a code bug in the media step, likely a JSON list where a dict is expected), not a flaky call. Under the RUNBOOK the worker may not change qgen.py/media.py. Options: a fix task for the media step, then rerun batch-8; or something else.

Last 30 lines:
```

== [3/23] rate
   rate took 0s (batch: 0s)

== [4/23] factcheck
   factcheck took 0s (batch: 0s)

== [5/23] revise
   revise took 0s (batch: 0s)

== [6/23] apply
applied: . Next: rate and factcheck (revised drafts only), then merge
   apply took 0s (batch: 0s)

== [7/23] rate
   rate took 0s (batch: 0s)

== [8/23] factcheck
   factcheck took 0s (batch: 0s)

== [9/23] merge
merged 0 question(s) into authoring/data/questions.json; 144 dropped in total (see dropped.json)
   merge took 0s (batch: 0s)

== [10/23] media
  FAILED media q-1425 media: ''list'' object has no attribute ''get''
  media: 1/1 searches in 0s, 1 failed
   media took 0s (batch: 1s)

Stopped at `media` with 1 error(s). Run `qgen batch` again; if the same step fails three times in a row, stop and report the output.
```', '', 'Script bugs become fix tasks; the queue never waits for the developer on them. Task 51''s worker:

1. Partial batch into git, not a stash:
   - `git stash apply 6d1be84` (batch-8''s pool edits from run 1068; pm stashed them as "left")
   - `qgen validate`; passes → `git add authoring/data` (pm commits it with task 51, like WIP d7fb13f); `work/batch-8` stays as it is
   - fails → stage nothing, new decision with the output, stop
2. Fix task:
   `pm task add 17 "Fix qgen media: Commons extmetadata [] crashes the search" --priority 0`, body:
   - `authoring/tools/providers/commons.py` `search()`: Commons sends `extmetadata: []` instead of `{}` for some files (here "File:Iceland Boreal Birch Forests and Alpine Tundra Ecoregion - Relief Map Zoom.png", query "Iceland map outline") → `''list'' object has no attribute ''get''`
   - fix: `meta = i.get("extmetadata") or {}`; look for the same pattern in the other providers
   - check: `media.fetch_for` on q-1425 slot `media` succeeds; no test
3. Resume task:
   `pm task add 17 "Finish batch-8 after task <fix id>: Fix qgen media: Commons extmetadata [] crashes the search" --priority -99`, body: follow the RUNBOOK (plain `qgen batch` resumes at media); -99: after the fix (0), before the other batch tasks (-100)
4. RUNBOOK, "Under `pm run`": the row "exit 1, same step three times in a row" no longer opens a decision; instead, generic versions of 1–3:
   - partial batch: `qgen validate`, `git add authoring/data`
   - a fix task in the batch task''s plan, `--priority 0`: failing step, last 30 lines, the worker''s read-only diagnosis (file, cause, suggested fix), how to check it
   - a resume task in the same plan, `--priority -99`: "Finish <batch> after task <fix id>: <fix subject>"
   - `pm task done <task>`, note: "stopped at <step>; fix: task <id>, resume: task <id>"
   - the batch worker still never edits qgen code itself
   - exit 75, exit 2, other exit codes, "More than one unfinished batch", "unfinished batch for another bundle": unchanged, still decisions
5. Plan 17, same rule (after 2–3, so pm''s re-split of plan 17 sees the new tasks): `pm show p17` → body; edit; `pm plan edit 17 --body - <<''EOF''`
   - "Batch tasks under `pm run`": exit 1 three times at one step leaves the decision bullet; new bullet as in 4 (fix task 0, resume task -99, partial batch committed, task closed)
   - "State": batch-8 stopped at media in task 51; fix and resume task ids
   - the "create tasks for plan 17" task the edit queues is expected
6. `pm task done 51`, note: stopped at media; fix and resume task ids; RUNBOOK and plan 17 changed.', NULL, '2026-10-15T06:04:34Z', '2026-10-15T13:14:15Z', 51, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 51: 2026-10-15, task 51: batch-8''s pool up to media committed with task 51 (no stash); fix task 1128 (Commons extmetadata [] crash, priority 0) and resume task 1129 (priority -99) in plan 17. RUNBOOK ''Under pm run'' and plan 17: exit 1 at the same step three times no longer opens a decision; the worker stages the partial batch after qgen validate, adds a fix task (0) and a resume task (-99) in its plan and closes the batch task. Exit 75, exit 2, other codes and the unfinished-batch cases stay decisions.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (206, 'Play-test: no supply report on Start, report on the Choice screen only', 'answered', '["both fine", "problems (listed in the answer)"]', '`decision 155: Play-test of age groups and bundles (again, after the decision 50 fixes)` was answered "fine", but its checklist predates `plan 133: No supply report on the Start screen` (done, `task 1064: Drop the supply report from the Start screen`). Two items left before `task 479: Close out AG-7 and BN-6` closes milestone 5:

1. Start shows no supply report, also with a nearly empty pool for the default choice.
2. A choice too small for the pool: the report shows on the Choice screen only, «¡A jugar!» disabled; by mouse and by keyboard (IN-1).

How: the gallery''s `blocked` save (every question blocked) covers both: `trivia-gallery --only start,choice-supply-report --visible`, or look at `work/gallery/<locale>/choice-supply-report.png`; by hand in `trivia-desktop` with a save whose questions are mostly blocked («Bloquear pregunta»).

Answer "problems": list each; task 479 turns them into fix tasks.', '', 'both fine', NULL, '2026-10-15T13:47:49Z', '2026-10-16T01:56:51Z', 479, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 479: Start shows no supply report; the Choice screen''s report and disabled «¡A jugar!» confirmed by mouse and keyboard; plan 133 stands, nothing changed.

2026-10-16, task 1360: the supply report and the disabled «¡A jugar!» now sit on the Bundles screen, after Choice (Player → Choice → Bundles → Level; decisions 264, 268); Choice shows none; Start still shows none.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (207, 'Task 1129 left unstaged changes after `pm task done`: investigate', 'answered', '[]', 'Run 1084 of task 1129 closed the task but left 2 files unstaged. pm committed them on the branch `pm/task-1129-run-1084-left` and cleaned the tree.

     M authoring/data/ui-flags.json
     M authoring/reports/batches.md

Look: `git show pm/task-1129-run-1084-left`. Keep: `git merge pm/task-1129-run-1084-left`. Then `git branch -D pm/task-1129-run-1084-left`.', '', 'kept: the 5 gallery icon flags (ui-flags.json) appended as ids 17–21 in 2e9cd86; batches.md dropped (stale, regenerated on main since); branch deleted', NULL, '2026-10-15T17:40:17Z', '2026-10-16T14:18:47Z', NULL, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (208, 'What must a script that calls claude report to its caller?', 'answered', '[]', 'task 1129: Finish batch-8 … ran 3h49m and pm recorded $0.37: only the worker''s own session. The qgen claude calls it started, the real cost, were invisible to pm and to the developer. Applies to qgen and to any future script that calls claude.', '', 'Everything a direct claude -p call would report, as a summary at the end of every run, also on failure or abort: number of calls (ok / failed / retried), models, turns, input/output/cache tokens, cost in $, wall time; per call a log line. An agent that runs the script copies the summary into its task note.', NULL, '2026-10-15T18:41:13Z', '2026-10-15T18:41:13Z', NULL, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (209, 'Joker symbols for the kept names?', 'answered', '["All ★: bulb with rays, broom with swoosh, wand with star, pointing hand, crosshair with curved arrow", "Keep today''s five (bulb, door, stairs, compass, crosshair), only redraw them VD-8 style", "Mixed: letters per joker from the list (e.g. H1 P2 F1 K2 T2)"]', '`decision 187: Icons and flags reviewed in /gallery?`: "joker icons still need work". English names kept (`decision 190: English name for the hint joker (symbol bulb)?` … `decision 194: English name for the snipe joker (symbol crosshair)?`); today''s symbols were drawn for the rejected symbol-first names. `decision 188: Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)` allows a new symbol. Whatever is picked: drawn VD-8 style like plan 135''s icons (24×24, stroke 2.4, rounded, body fill-opacity 0.25, playful), same symbol in every language, tray, follow-up dialogs, /comodines, Customize and gamemaster config rows; achievement icons redrawn if a symbol changes.

Candidates per joker (★ = recommended; answer with letters, e.g. "all ★" or "H1 P2 F1 K1 T1"):

- **Hint** (H; es Soplo, de Zaunpfahl): shows the next hint, vague → strong
  - H1 ★ bulb with rays: today''s bulb, three short rays above, glass filled, rays bouncing out
  - H2 speech bubble with a small "!" or "…": a whispered tip, fits «Soplo» too
  - H3 keep today''s bulb, only redrawn
- **Pass & Purge** (P; es Paso, de Näxt): drops the question; optionally purges its whole subcategory
  - P1 ★ broom with a swoosh: bristles filled, two motion arcs; fits "purge" and plan 09''s sweep animation
  - P2 door with a swoosh: today''s door ajar, a motion arc leaving through it ("pass")
  - P3 fast-forward double chevron with a dust puff
- **Fairy** (F; es Bájale, de Gang runter): swaps for an easier question of the same subcategory
  - F1 ★ wand with a star: tilted wand, filled five-point star at the tip, two sparkles
  - F2 fairy wings: two pairs of rounded wings, filled, a small dot body
  - F3 keep stairs (going down), only redrawn
- **Ms Picky** (K; es Cambiazo, de Wunschzeit): the players choose another subcategory, similar difficulty
  - K1 ★ pointing hand: index finger pointing at a small card, picking one
  - K2 magnifier over a card: picky inspection
  - K3 keep compass, only redrawn
- **Trick Shot** (T; es Francotirador, de Finte): aim at an answer; wrong one struck out, right one repeats the level
  - T1 ★ crosshair with a curved arrow: today''s ring + ticks, an arc arrow curving into the centre
  - T2 suction-cup dart in a target: filled target rings, dart stuck in (plan 09''s cartoon shot)
  - T3 keep crosshair, only redrawn', '', 'All ★: bulb with rays, broom with swoosh, wand with star, pointing hand, crosshair with curved arrow', NULL, '2026-10-15T18:57:38Z', '2026-10-16T02:01:47Z', 1135, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1101: Symbols bulb with rays, broom with swoosh, wand with star, pointing hand, crosshair with curved arrow drawn in app/client/src/game/Icon.svelte, ids via TOKENS/jokerIcon() in jokers.ts; shown in tray, Customize, skip dialog, category picker, scope, difficulty dial, hint notes, /comodines; old door/stairs/compass symbols no longer hold. Reviewed in decision 248.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (210, 'Spanish joker names and keys (es), translated from the English?', 'answered', '["As recommended: Soplo (S), Paso y fuera (P), Hada madrina (H), Doña Exigente (E), Tiro mágico (T)", "Closer to the English: Pista (S), Paso y purga (P), Hada (H), Quisquillosa (Q), Carambola (L)", "Keep today''s: Soplo (S), Paso (P), Bájale (F), Cambiazo (T), Francotirador (X)", "Mixed: one candidate per joker from the list (keys as listed, clashes resolved as noted)"]', '`decision 188: Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)`, `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`; English answers `decision 190: English name for the hint joker (symbol bulb)?` … `decision 194: English name for the snipe joker (symbol crosshair)?`: Hint, Pass & Purge, Fairy, Ms Picky, Trick Shot (all kept). `es` is the family''s catalog (exception to D-59); `es-ES` follows it (own decision). Neutral Latin American Spanish, «ustedes» (`locales/style/es.md`). ≤ 13 characters, playful. Symbols: pending `decision 209: Joker symbols for the kept names?` (★ wand fits «Hada madrina», pointing hand fits «Doña Exigente»).

Keys (`decision 53: Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?`, `check:literals`): Question screen has `A`–`D`, `R` replay, `V` peek, `M` flag taken; today S P F T X; a key changes only where the new name needs it.

Candidates, recommended first, key in brackets:
- **Hint** (today «Soplo»)
  - Soplo (S): already means a whispered hint, playful, the family knows it
  - Pista (S): the literal «hint», plain like the English
  - Pistita (S): diminutive, playful
- **Pass & Purge** (today «Paso»)
  - Paso y fuera (P): pass, and the topic is out; echoes today''s purge line «Paso, y fuera el tema»
  - Paso y purga (P): closest to the English alliteration; «purga» sounds harsh
  - Paso (P): today''s, says nothing of the purge
- **Fairy** (today «Bájale»)
  - Hada madrina (H): the fairy godmother makes things easier; 12 characters
  - Hada (H): literal, short
  - Bájale (F): today''s, not a fairy
- **Ms Picky** (today «Cambiazo»)
  - Doña Exigente (E): a character like «Ms», picks the topic she wants; 13 characters; `D` is an answer key
  - Quisquillosa (Q): «picky», one word
  - Cambiazo (T): today''s, a swap, not picky
- **Trick Shot** (today «Francotirador»)
  - Tiro mágico (T): the trick shot that strikes a wrong answer; `T` free once «Cambiazo» goes (if «Cambiazo» stays: `I`)
  - Carambola (L): billiards trick shot, also a lucky fluke; `C`, `A`, `R`, `M`, `B` taken
  - Francotirador (X): today''s

Leaves for the recommended set (es; `es-ES` gets «os»/«queréis» per its decision):
- `joker.<id>.name`/`key`: Soplo S, Paso y fuera P, Hada madrina H, Doña Exigente E, Tiro mágico T
- `error.joker_spent.*`: «ya no les quedan Soplos», «ya no les queda ningún Paso y fuera», «ya no les quedan Hadas madrinas», «ya no les queda ninguna Doña Exigente», «ya no les quedan Tiros mágicos»
- hint note `screen.question.hint`: «Soplo {n}» (Pista: «Pista {n}»)
- `joker.skip.pass` «Solo paso» (was «Paso», now part of the name); `stamp` «ELIMINADO» stays; `purge` «Paso y fuera: adiós al tema «{name}»»
- `joker.easier.dial` «Dificultad» stays
- `joker.category.title` «Doña Exigente: ¿qué tema quieren?»
- `joker.snipe.*` (aim, false, shoot, hit) name no joker: stay; `arm` «¿Usar {name}?» and `rule` leaves stay', '', 'As recommended: Soplo (S), Paso y fuera (P), Hada madrina (H), Doña Exigente (E), Tiro mágico (T)', NULL, '2026-10-15T18:59:39Z', '2026-10-16T02:02:55Z', 1097, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1098: applied in D-108 (plans/decisions.md): es.ts names Soplo S, Paso y fuera P, Hada madrina H, Doña Exigente E, Tiro mágico T; skip.pass «Solo paso», purge, category title, joker_spent leaves as listed; xx.ts follows; qgen supply/simulate output says «Hada madrina» / «Doña Exigente»

2026-10-16, task 1101: es catalog: Soplo (S), Paso y fuera (P), Hada madrina (H), Doña Exigente (E), Tiro mágico (T) in es.ts (xx.ts follows), style guide glossary, /comodines, store and achievement texts; Bájale, Cambiazo, Francotirador are old names (bad-patterns list). Reviewed in decision 248; purge text rewrite in task 1342.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (211, 'Spain joker names (es-ES): same as es?', 'answered', '["Same names and keys as es; only the vosotros leaves differ", "Own names where Spain differs (note which joker and name)"]', '`decision 188: Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)`, `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`. `es-ES.ts` overrides `es` only where it differs (`locales/style/es-ES.md`); names follow `decision 210: Spanish joker names and keys (es), translated from the English?`. None of its candidates (Soplo, Paso y fuera, Hada madrina, Doña Exigente, Tiro mágico; Pista, Paso y purga, Hada, Quisquillosa, Carambola) reads oddly in Spain, so no Spain-only names are proposed.

Overrides with the recommended es set (address «vosotros»):
- `error.joker_spent.*`: «ya no os quedan Soplos», «ya no os queda ningún Paso y fuera», «ya no os quedan Hadas madrinas», «ya no os queda ninguna Doña Exigente», «ya no os quedan Tiros mágicos»
