- keys, hint note, `skip.pass`/`stamp`/`purge`, `easier.dial`, `snipe.*` names: as `es`; existing `rule`/`aim`/`hit` overrides stay', '', 'Same names and keys as es; only the vosotros leaves differ', NULL, '2026-10-15T18:59:56Z', '2026-10-16T02:03:12Z', 1097, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1098: applied in D-108 (plans/decisions.md): es-ES.ts overrides only joker.category.title and error.joker_spent.* (vosotros)

2026-10-16, task 1101: es-ES.ts overrides only the vosotros leaves (error.joker_spent.*, joker.category.title); names and keys from es. Reviewed in decision 248.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (212, 'German joker names and keys (de), translated from the English?', 'answered', '["As recommended: Zaunpfahl (Z), Näxt & weg (N), Gute Fee (F), Frau Pingelig (P), Trickschuss (T)", "Alternative set: Tipp (I), Und tschüss! (U), Glücksfee (F), Frau Mäkelig (K), Kunstschuss (S)", "Keep today''s: Zaunpfahl (Z), Näxt (N), Gang runter (G), Wunschzeit (W), Finte (F)", "Mixed: one candidate per joker from the list (keys as listed, clashes resolved as noted)"]', '`decision 188: Joker names English first, one symbol per joker (milestone 9)`, `plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`; English answers `decision 190: English name for the hint joker (symbol bulb)?` … `decision 194: English name for the snipe joker (symbol crosshair)?`: Hint, Pass & Purge, Fairy, Ms Picky, Trick Shot (all kept). Replaces today''s names from `decision 54: German name for the hint joker «Soplo»?` … `decision 58: German name for the snipe joker «Francotirador»?`. `locales/style/de.md`: no plural address, infinitive prompts, „…“ quotes. ≤ 13 characters, playful. Symbols: pending `decision 209: Joker symbols for the kept names?` (★ wand fits «Gute Fee», pointing hand fits «Frau Pingelig»).

Keys (`decision 53: Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?`, `check:literals`): Question screen has `A`–`D`, `R` replay, `V` peek, `M` flag taken; today Z N G W F.

Candidates, recommended first, key in brackets:
- **Hint** (today «Zaunpfahl»)
  - Zaunpfahl (Z): «Wink mit dem Zaunpfahl», a broad hint; playful, already a translation of «Hint»
  - Tipp (I): literal, plain; `T` goes to «Trickschuss»
  - Geistesblitz (G): fits the bulb, but a flash of insight, not a hint
- **Pass & Purge** (today «Näxt»)
  - Näxt & weg (N): keeps «Näxt» (pass), adds the purge like the English «&»
  - Und tschüss! (U): getting rid of question and topic, cheeky
  - Weg damit! (W): «away with it»; clashes with «Wunschzeit» (W) if that stays
- **Fairy** (today «Gang runter»)
  - Gute Fee (F): the fairy godmother who makes things easy; `F` free once «Finte» goes
  - Glücksfee (F): «lucky fairy», common idiom
  - Fee (F): literal, shortest
- **Ms Picky** (today «Wunschzeit»)
  - Frau Pingelig (P): a character like «Ms», fussy; 13 characters
  - Frau Mäkelig (K): «mäkelig» = picky (eater); `M` taken; clashes with «Kunstschuss» (K), then that one takes `S`
  - Wunschzeit (W): today''s, a wish, not picky
- **Trick Shot** (today «Finte»)
  - Trickschuss (T): closest to the English
  - Kunstschuss (S): the billiards trick shot; `K` if «Frau Mäkelig» isn''t picked
  - Finte (F): today''s, a feint; clashes with the fairy names (F), then those take `E`

Leaves for the recommended set:
- `joker.<id>.name`/`key`: Zaunpfahl Z, Näxt & weg N, Gute Fee F, Frau Pingelig P, Trickschuss T
- `error.joker_spent.*`: «kein Zaunpfahl mehr übrig», «kein „Näxt & weg“ mehr übrig», «keine „Gute Fee“ mehr übrig», «keine „Frau Pingelig“ mehr übrig», «kein Trickschuss mehr übrig»
- hint note `screen.question.hint`: «Zaunpfahl {n}» (Tipp: «Tipp {n}»)
- `joker.skip.pass` «Nur passen» and `stamp` «WEG» stay; `purge` «Näxt & weg: tschüss, Thema „{name}“»
- `joker.easier.dial` «Schwierigkeit» stays
- `joker.category.title` «Frau Pingelig: Welches Thema soll es sein?»
- `joker.snipe.*` (aim, false, shoot, hit) name no joker: stay; `arm` «{name} einsetzen?» and `rule` leaves stay', '', 'Wink, Näxt & Weg, Glücksfee, Wunschzeit, Finte', NULL, '2026-10-15T18:59:56Z', '2026-10-15T20:47:14Z', 1097, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1098: applied in D-108 (plans/decisions.md): de.ts Wink K, Näxt & Weg N, Glücksfee G, Wunschzeit W, Finte F (keys: decision 247); hint note «Wink {n}», purge «Näxt & Weg: tschüss, Thema „{name}“», joker_spent leaves; rules-tweak mod blurb «ein Wink mehr»

2026-10-16, task 1101: de catalog: Wink (K), Näxt & Weg (N), Glücksfee (G), Wunschzeit (W), Finte (F) in de.ts (keys decision 247), style guide glossary, /comodines, store and achievement texts; Zaunpfahl, Gang runter are old names. Reviewed in decision 248; purge text rewrite in task 1342.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (213, 'General category list for regional bundles', 'answered', '["the list as drafted (14)", "the shorter core list (10)", "changes (name them)"]', 'General list of broad categories every regional bundle starts from (`plan 138: Regional taxonomy: a general list, colombia reworked`, part 1; `decision 166: colombia subcategories (OQ-46): where the 19 go, and the list for 2000`). On the answer it becomes `authoring/data/regional-categories.json` (authoring only), the input of `qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>` (task 1138), which adds the region''s own categories and proposes subcategories for your approval (colombia: task 1139).

## How it is used
- Placeholders: `{región}` = the region''s name («Colombia», «Andalucía»); patterns built on `de {región}` / `en {región}` avoid gender agreement (no `{gentilicio}` needed: «Comida colombiana» needs the feminine form).
- Names repeat across bundles (`decision 110: Regional packs at launch (RG-5, OQ-46)` (d)): «Historia de Colombia», «Historia de México» are separate entries of their bundles.
- Sizing at 2000 approved: ≈ 50 subcategories (≈ 40 approved each), so 14 + 1–3 regional ones ≈ 3–4 subcategories per category, more for the big ones (history, geography, food, music).
- `qgen taxonomy` may leave a category out for a region with too little to ask (reason in the proposal), you see it in the region''s decision.
- Excluded everywhere (bundle rule, D-49): anything players anywhere in the Spanish-speaking world answer without a connection to the region (capital, flag, coffee, García Márquez, Shakira as a name) stays in `base`; world topics stay in `base`''s subcategories.

## The list (14)
1. **Geografía de {región}**: provinces/departments, cities and towns, rivers, mountains, coasts, islands, landmarks and monuments, roads and distances. Excludes: country-level facts known worldwide (base Capitales del mundo, Países del mundo, Monumentos famosos).
2. **Naturaleza de {región}**: native animals and plants, national parks and reserves, ecosystems, climate and seasons, natural phenomena. Excludes: animals and plants known worldwide without a regional angle (base Animales, Plantas, Amazonas).
3. **Historia de {región}**: indigenous peoples before the conquest, colony, independence, wars and founding figures, 19th–20th century, presidents and turning points. Excludes: world history (base Historia); current party politics.
4. **Personajes de {región}**: well-known people not covered by music, sport, arts or TV: scientists, inventors, business founders, heroes of daily life, popular characters. Excludes: names known worldwide (base); musicians, athletes, writers, actors go to their categories.
5. **Comida y bebida de {región}**: typical dishes, sweets and desserts, drinks, fruits and ingredients, regional variants, markets and street food. Excludes: international food (base Comida y bebida, Comida latinoamericana: arepa as a name, coffee in general).
6. **Fiestas y tradiciones de {región}**: festivals, carnivals, fairs, holidays, family customs, crafts, traditional dress and games. Excludes: world festivals and customs (base Fiestas y tradiciones, Trajes típicos del mundo).
7. **Mitos y leyendas de {región}**: legendary creatures, ghost stories, popular beliefs and superstitions, indigenous myths. Excludes: world mythologies and generic superstitions (base Mitos y leyendas, Leyendas y supersticiones).
8. **Música y baile de {región}**: rhythms and dances, instruments, singers and bands, famous songs, music festivals. Excludes: world music and global stars by name only (base Música).
9. **Arte y literatura de {región}**: writers and books, poets, painters and sculptors, architecture, museums, comics. Excludes: world literature and art (base Arte y literatura; García Márquez basics).
10. **Cine y televisión de {región}**: telenovelas, series, films, presenters, actors, radio, cartoons, internet celebrities. Excludes: international film and TV (base Cine, series y superhéroes).
11. **Deporte de {región}**: national teams, clubs, athletes, Olympic medals, the region''s favourite sports, traditional games and sports. Excludes: world football and sport (base Fútbol, Deportes).
12. **Así se habla en {región}**: words and slang, sayings and expressions, accents, loanwords from indigenous languages, the region''s own languages. Excludes: Spanish in general (base Idiomas y palabras, Refranes y dichos).
13. **Vida diaria en {región}**: money and banknotes, brands and products, shops, transport, school, home, everyday objects and habits, public services. Excludes: world brands and money (base Marcas y logotipos, Monedas y dinero).
14. **Símbolos de {región}**: flag, anthem, coat of arms, national symbols (bird, tree, flower), emblems of the provinces/cities. Excludes: the flag as recognised worldwide (base Banderas del mundo).

## colombia today vs. this list
- Today 6 categories, 31 subcategories; all fit into 1, 2, 5, 6, 7, 8, 11, 12, 14 (e.g. «Colombianos famosos» → 4 or 8/11; «Animales de Colombia» → 2). Missing today: 3, 9, 10, 13. Region-specific extras come in task 1139 (e.g. «Café de Colombia», «Región Caribe»).

## Shorter core list (option 2, 10)
- 4 Personajes folded into the field each person is known for, else 3 Historia.
- 14 Símbolos folded into 3 Historia.
- 10 Cine y televisión and 13 Vida diaria merged: «Vida diaria y televisión en {región}».
- 7 Mitos y leyendas folded into 6: «Fiestas, tradiciones y leyendas de {región}».', '', 'the list as drafted (14)', NULL, '2026-10-15T19:04:01Z', '2026-10-16T02:04:11Z', 1137, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1137: authoring/data/regional-categories.json holds the 14 categories as drafted (name with {región}, scope, excludes); qgen validate checks it (fields present, unique names); input of task 1138: qgen taxonomy --bundle <id>: propose and apply a region''s taxonomy.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (214, 'neutralize-1: qgen validate fails after fix', 'answered', '["fix first: task 632 waits for task 1142, then resumes with plain `qgen neutralize`", "discard: revert questions.json, drop tasks 632 and 633"]', '`task 632: run neutralize-1` (decision 202: Run qgen neutralize on base now? → go).

- Run 1: `qgen neutralize` exit 1 at `fix` (1 of 31 fact-check calls: `no fact check for q-1162`).
  `claude: 70 calls (0 failed, 0 retried), opus 39 / sonnet 31, 181 turns, 2.3M tokens (1.9M cache), $14.08, 46m56s in calls`
- Runs 2, 3: exit 1 at the scan''s `validate`, before `fix` is retried (no claude calls):
  ```
  Resuming neutralize-1.
  == [1/2] scan
     scan took 0s (batch: 0s)
  == [2/2] validate
  app/data/pool.json is not the current export of the pool: run `qgen export`
  `qgen validate` failed. Stop and report the output.
  ```
- `qgen validate` on the partial state: same error. So the RUNBOOK''s partial-batch path (validate passes → stage `authoring/data`) doesn''t apply. Nothing staged.
- Cause: a qgen bug. Every resume validates after the scan, but `export` only runs at the end. Fix: `task 1142: Fix qgen neutralize: resume fails validate (stale pool.json after a partial fix)`.
- Working tree: `authoring/data/questions.json` has `fix`''s uncommitted rewording (~5000 lines changed). Other batch tasks will see a dirty tree until this resumes or is reverted.

"fix first": task 632 resumes after task 1142, with plain `qgen neutralize`.
"discard": `git checkout authoring/data/questions.json`, `work/neutralize-1/` stays, tasks 632 and 633 dropped.', '', 'fix first: task 632 resumes with plain qgen neutralize. Restoring stash@{0} conflicts in questions.json (36 hunks): resolve per question, stash''s version for the neutralized ones except q-0476, q-0590, q-0641, q-0768, q-0896, q-0931, q-0941, q-1100, q-1112, q-1178, q-1194 (reworked on main since, keep main''s; they stay un-neutralized, QC neutralize-1 notes them)', NULL, '2026-10-15T19:36:54Z', '2026-10-15T23:05:45Z', 632, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-24, task 639: Task 639 ran after neutralize-1''s validate fix; es-sourced questions are translated to en as normal.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (215, 'Spot check batch-8 done?', 'answered', '["done"]', 'Blind spot check of batch-8 (QC.md step 2, `plan 16: Quality control after every batch`): 992 merged, 947 approved, 45 needs_work; report authoring/reports/batch-8.md (Audit: 1 of 57 approved with a major finding, audit/review agreement 95 %).
Start `trivia-authoring`, then open http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?batch=batch-8&sample=1: 30 questions of the audit sample (`quality.spot_check_size`), LLM decision and audit hidden until you decide; about 10–15 min.
Afterwards, the audit''s major findings on approved questions: http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?batch=batch-8&audit=flagged.
Answer once the 30 are decided. Then `task 53: QC batch-8` runs `qgen report --qc batch-8` and asks the proposals decision.', '', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-15T19:39:56Z', '2026-10-15T21:31:25Z', 53, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 53: spot check of batch-8 recorded in authoring/data/spot-checks.json (30 of 30); qgen report --qc batch-8 wrote the Quality control section of authoring/reports/batch-8.md (agreement 26/30, 87 %, below quality.min_agreement 90 %: release bar ✗), basis of decision 226.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (216, 'Fable for qgen rework: keep, drop or try for batch review? (plan 58)', 'answered', '["drop: default stays opus, --model fable stays opt-in", "keep: fable becomes rework''s default (RUNBOOK + D-65 update)", "extend: new plan to try fable for batch review"]', 'Experiment in `plan 58: Fable as an opt-in model for qgen rework` (section Result). rework-2 with fable: 52/79 approved (66 %), $20.08, $0.39 per approved. rework-1 with opus: 28/43 (65 %), $5.57, $0.20 per approved. Same approval rate at ~2× the cost per approved. Caveat: review 2 (opus) ran for no question, so Fable judged its own fixes; the rates are not strictly comparable. /usage delta not measured. Recommendation: drop, default stays opus.', '', 'drop: default stays opus, --model fable stays opt-in', NULL, '2026-10-15T20:01:21Z', '2026-10-15T21:12:50Z', 345, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-15, task 1144: D-65 in plans/decisions.md: result of rework-2 vs rework-1 (52/79, $0.39/approved vs 28/43, $0.20/approved), outcome drop, caveat that review 1 gives the final verdict in rework (review 2 only after a new media search). qgen rework default stays opus, --model fable stays opt-in; no code, RUNBOOK or AGENTS.md change; no Fable batch-review plan.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (217, 'chinese-base membership: how does a translated base question count for chinese-base?', 'answered', '["1: fit flag on the zh translation, export maps it into chinese-base", "2: bundle per locale on the source question", "3: copy fitting base questions into chinese-base"]', 'Milestone 12 (`plan 60: masterplan`, part 2). The zh game (`zh-Hans`) plays `chinese-base` instead of `base`; part of `chinese-base` is translated `base` questions that a fit pass picks (not about the Spanish-speaking world, no Spanish wordplay), the developer corrects.

Today: D-39 one `bundle` per question; D-81 a translation (`questions.<locale>.json`) takes `bundle`, `subcategory`, media from its source by id, and exports to `app/data/pool.<locale>.json`; D-82 seen counts by id across locales; D-100 subcategory keys are bundle + name, so a `chinese-base` question needs a `chinese-base` subcategory (reused `base` names may repeat, D-99).

Options:
1. Fit flag on the zh translation: the `questions.zh-Hans.json` entry gets `fit` (true / false / absent = not checked yet); the fit pass writes it, the developer flips it in `/review?locale=zh-Hans`. The source keeps `bundle: base`. `qgen export` writes a fitting, approved translation into the `chinese-base` pool with `bundle: chinese-base` and the same-named subcategory of `chinese-base`''s taxonomy (one reused from `base`); not fitting, or a subcategory `chinese-base` doesn''t reuse: not exported. Ids shared (seen counts), no source change, one pipeline.
2. Bundle per locale on the source: `questions.json` gets `bundles: {"zh-Hans": "chinese-base"}` beside `bundle`; the fit pass writes the source. Same export and taxonomy rule as 1; the source file grows a locale-specific field.
3. Copies: a fitting `base` question is copied into a new `chinese-base` source question (own id, `bundle: chinese-base`), then translated like the new ones. Simplest model (D-39 unchanged), but double text: fixes to the `base` source don''t reach the copy, and seen counts don''t match across languages.', '', '3: copy fitting base questions into chinese-base', NULL, '2026-10-15T20:07:50Z', '2026-10-16T02:33:38Z', 374, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (218, 'New China-centric questions for chinese-base: drafted in Spanish and translated, or drafted in Chinese?', 'answered', '["1: drafted in Spanish, translated with --translate zh-Hans", "2: drafted in Chinese (zh-Hans as a second source language)", "3: Spanish by default, Chinese-language subcategories drafted in Chinese"]', 'Milestone 12 (`plan 60: masterplan`, part 6). `chinese-base` needs new China-centric questions (Chinese history, places, food, festivals, people, language, pop culture) on top of the translated `base` questions that fit, to reach 5000 approved (pm decision 21).

Today: `questions.json` is the Spanish source (D-81); `qgen batch --bundle <id>` drafts a bundle''s Spanish source, `qgen batch --translate <locale> --bundle <id>` translates it (D-87); the developer reviews in Spanish; the milestone says "no new pipeline per language". No one in the family reads Chinese.

Options:
1. Drafted in Spanish as `chinese-base` source questions (`qgen batch --bundle chinese-base`, `languages` zh-Hans only, so the Spanish text never ships), then `qgen batch --translate zh-Hans --bundle chinese-base`. One pipeline; the developer can review every source. Cost: two passes per question; questions about the Chinese language (characters, 成语 idioms, wordplay) are hard to write and check through Spanish: the language subcategories stay thin or are dropped.
2. Drafted in Chinese: `zh-Hans` becomes a second source language (draft, review, fix, audit prompts in Chinese, a source file for zh-only questions). Natural Chinese and language questions possible; a new pipeline path, against the milestone''s constraint, and only native reviewers can check the sources.
3. Spanish by default (1); only the language subcategories (characters, idioms, wordplay) drafted in Chinese, reviewed by the native reviewers only.', '', '2: drafted in Chinese (zh-Hans as a second source language)', NULL, '2026-10-15T20:07:50Z', '2026-10-16T02:31:49Z', 374, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (219, 'Do the new locales (zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR) steer es drafting from the start?', 'answered', '[]', 'D-84 / decision 37: the translations'' source shortfall drives es drafting once es meets its target. Counting ru/pt-BR''s empty pools at once would steer es drafting before anyone decided to pay for those pools (plan 60 part 7 puts that into its budget decision); zh-Hans plays chinese-base, not base. Until part 2 adds chinese-base, zh-Hans is listed by no bundle: a validate warning, not an error, so validate passes. Plan 139: New locales in data and pipeline.', '', 'No: source shortfall counts only locales in translations.DRIVES_DRAFTING (en, de) that the bundle lists; ru and pt-BR join by part 7''s budget decision; zh-Hans never steers base; a locale no bundle lists only warns in qgen validate', NULL, '2026-10-15T20:11:30Z', '2026-10-15T20:11:30Z', 1147, NULL, 'rule', 1147, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (220, 'Native reviewers for zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR: paid freelancers, volunteers, or mixed?', 'answered', '["1: paid freelancer per language, the pilot spot check as the paid trial", "2: volunteers (community after launch, native-speaking acquaintances), credited, unpaid", "3: mixed: paid for the pilot, prompt read, UI playtest and store texts; volunteers for the per-run spot checks, paid fallback"]', 'Milestone 12 (`plan 60: masterplan`, part 4): no one in the family reads Chinese, Russian or Portuguese, but every `tr-<locale>-<n>` run needs a native spot check (`authoring/QC.md` "Translation runs", D-87) at the release bar (D-79: 30 questions, ≥ 90 % agreement), and the pilot''s go (`qgen health ack`) reads it. No `tr-zh-Hans-*`, `tr-ru-*`, `tr-pt-BR-*` or `chinese-base` run starts before a reviewer is engaged for its locale.

One reviewer per language, for everything native in the milestone:
- read the approved locale prompt (`plan 140: Translation prompts and markets per locale`) before the pilot
- spot check of each run: 30 questions, English reference beside the translation (they need not read Spanish), returned as a verdict file (offline sheet, no access to the developer''s machine)
- zh only: the `chinese-base` fit pass sample (does this `base` question fit a Chinese family?)
- UI: screen gallery read + one playtest via a Steam key on the beta branch (part 5, "Playtest passed? (<lang>)")
- store texts (part 8)

Workload per language (estimate, mine):
- runs to 5000 approved: pilot + ~18–20 runs of 300 → ~20 spot checks × ~45 min ≈ 15 h
- prompt read 1 h, UI gallery + playtest 3–4 h, store texts 1–2 h
- zh: + fit samples ~3 h
- total ≈ 20–25 h per language, spread over months (one check per run, as runs happen)
- if `decision 218: New China-centric questions for chinese-base: drafted in Spanish and translated, or drafted in Chinese?` makes China-centric sources Chinese-drafted (option 2, or 3 for the language subcategories), the zh reviewer is their only human reviewer: a full review of every such source (~1 min each; 2000 sources ≈ 35 h more), not a spot check. Weigh that in decision 218.

Costs (rough, from general knowledge of freelance rates; not checked on the web):
- paid native reviewer / proofreader on a freelance platform (e.g. Upwork, ProZ): ~$20–40 per hour for zh, ru, pt-BR (pt-BR and ru usually at the low end)
- option 1: ≈ $500–1000 per language, ≈ $1500–3000 for all three (+ ≈ $700–1400 for zh if decision 218 goes Chinese)
- option 2: $0; credit in the game''s credits (with their consent) and a free key
- option 3: ≈ $150–300 per language (pilot, prompt read, UI, store texts ≈ 7 h), the rest free while volunteers deliver

Trade-offs:
- 1: reliable, on the developer''s schedule, comparable checks run after run (same person); costs money; the developer''s own freelance account (outside the repo, no project account)
- 2: free, but no community exists before these languages ship (chicken and egg: volunteers come from players of the language), slow and uneven; ~20 checks per language is a lot to ask unpaid; a missed check stalls the runs (the next run waits for it)
- 3: pays for the one-off, high-leverage reviews; per-run checks depend on volunteers who may not exist yet, paid fallback when they don''t deliver within ~2 weeks

Recommended: 1. Every run stops until its spot check is in (QC step 5), so the per-run checks are the bottleneck; a paid reviewer per language keeps them coming at a known cost. Start with the pilot spot check as a paid trial; keep the reviewer if their verdicts are consistent (3 planted control items per sheet, see the plan), else hire another. Names and payments stay outside the public repo.', '', '2: volunteers (community after launch, native-speaking acquaintances), credited, unpaid', NULL, '2026-10-15T20:15:09Z', '2026-10-16T02:32:12Z', 1150, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (221, 'How does an outside native reviewer reach the review tool?', 'answered', '[]', 'The review tool (trivia-authoring) binds 127.0.0.1 on the developer''s machine, has no accounts and writes the pools directly; opening it to the internet (tunnel, port forward) would need auth and trust in an outside person writing to authoring/data/. Hosting it on the report server would add a second server with writable content. AGENTS.md: no accounts of our own, no secrets in the repo. A file per run by e-mail needs neither, keeps the check blind by construction (the sheet holds no LLM verdicts), and fits the per-run rhythm of QC.md. Plan: plan 60 part 4.', '', 'Offline sheet per run: qgen spotcheck export writes one self-contained HTML file (blind sample, English reference, no LLM data); the reviewer returns a verdict JSON; qgen spotcheck import records it as the human review and spot check. No reachable review page.', NULL, '2026-10-15T20:15:14Z', '2026-10-15T20:15:14Z', 1150, NULL, 'rule', 1150, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (222, 'New UI languages (zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR): offered only once their pool ships', 'answered', '[]', 'From task 1151 (plan for part 5 of `plan 60: masterplan`). `decision 156: One language for UI and questions` lets a UI language without a pool play the Spanish pool; fine for es-ES/en/de at launch, useless for a Chinese, Russian or Brazilian family. Part 9 ships the fonts and catalogs as a full patch and the pools as content patches after it, so the catalogs reach players before the questions. The gate hides each new language until its pool arrives; a Steam client in schinese/russian/brazilian guesses es/en meanwhile (the existing fallback).', '', 'Start''s language picker and the first-start guess list zh-Hans, ru, pt-BR only when pool.<locale>.json is present (the decision 156 test: its default bundles'' supply passes); before that only in dev (?lang=) and under TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER; es/es-ES/en/de unchanged', NULL, '2026-10-15T20:17:51Z', '2026-10-15T20:17:51Z', 1151, NULL, 'rule', 1151, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (223, 'Build names after PUB-7: productName «Living Room Trivia», space-free exe and artefact names', 'answered', '[]', 'Task 1179 settles the contradiction in plans/18 (Exe metadata vs names row): exe/artefact names follow the en store name (decision 176: Store names pass PUB-7?), space-free so terminal commands (--check-mod, --publish-mod) need no quotes; the pinned userData keeps saves, mods and the Steam Cloud path; in-game title stays the UI catalog''s (D-50). D-106.', '', 'productName «Living Room Trivia»; LivingRoomTrivia.exe, Linux living-room-trivia(-bin), artefacts LivingRoomTrivia-<v>-…; userData <appData>/trivia, app://trivia/, window and in-game titles unchanged', NULL, '2026-10-15T21:01:17Z', '2026-10-15T21:01:17Z', 1179, NULL, 'rule', 1179, '');
