Look: `git show pm/task-1205-run-1194-left`. Keep: `git merge pm/task-1205-run-1194-left`. Then `git branch -D pm/task-1205-run-1194-left`.', '', 'developer''s qgen health ack batch-8 ran in the main checkout during task 1205; restored from d48eadd (176a90d); AGENTS.md: human review work only in ../trivia-review', NULL, '2026-10-16T01:37:44Z', '2026-10-16T13:12:03Z', NULL, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (244, 'Unused base concepts that fail the international angle: retired as unaskable', 'answered', '[]', 'Task 1204 (`plan 147: English-first batches: calibration, overlap and QC across languages`, part 2). `qgen concepts --top-up` only adds concepts; drawing (`concepts.draw_concepts`) ignores facets and prefers unused concepts, so the ~3500 Spanish-world-only or US/UK-only unused concepts of the es-era lists would keep being drawn for English drafts, which draft.md then skips with retire "no" (a wasted slot, every batch). The house style''s "International angle" (`decision 239: English-first drafting prompts: apply?`, `decision 242: International angle for base concept lists: apply?`) makes them unaskable for base, so the existing PE-10 retire mechanism (`qgen.retire`) marks them; nothing is deleted, a retired concept is still visible in the list and can be un-retired. Concepts families everywhere know (Frida Kahlo, Machu Picchu, Statue of Liberty) are kept. Facets stay (no tooling removes them, drawing doesn''t use them).', '', 'Retire them (retired: ''unaskable: international angle, <spanish|anglo>-world only (task 1204)''), used ones stay; lists that lost ≥ 25 % of their unused concepts topped up with qgen concepts --fill', NULL, '2026-10-16T02:12:36Z', '2026-10-16T02:12:36Z', 1204, NULL, 'rule', 1204, '2026-10-16, task 1204: 2026-10-15, task 1204: 3781 unused base concepts retired (3515 from the es-era lists, 266 from the top-up); 27 lists topped up with --fill plus Empresas famosas (--top-up), 2181 new concepts; no pool question changed.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (245, 'base subcategories scoped to one language area: widen for the international pool?', 'answered', '["Widen four: Telenovelas → «Telenovelas del mundo», Comida latinoamericana → «Cocinas del mundo», Refranes y dichos → «Refranes del mundo», Idioma → «Lenguaje»; keep the rest", "Widen only Telenovelas and Comida latinoamericana", "Keep all names; the concept angle and draft.md''s skip rule are enough"]', 'Task 1204 (`plan 147: English-first batches: calibration, overlap and QC across languages`, part 2) judged every `base` subcategory by `decision 18: Which new base subcategories?`''s rules (no Colombia-only topic, D-49) for the English-first, international pool (house style "International angle"). A rename widens the scope; existing questions move with it (they fit the wider scope), `app/data/categories.json`, `names.*.json`, the concept file and question `subcategory` fields follow in a follow-up task (no rename tool yet).

Scoped to the Spanish-speaking world or one language:
- **Telenovelas** (9 approved): 106 of its 190 unused concepts were Spanish-world-only (retired, `decision 244: Unused base concepts that fail the international angle: retired as unaskable`), 3 of 12 facets national (Colombian, Mexican/Televisa, Venezuelan…). Wider: telenovelas exported worldwide (Betty la fea, Rebelde, El clon), Turkish dizi, K-dramas, soaps (Dallas, Neighbours).
- **Comida latinoamericana** (5 approved, no concept list yet; its questions are Colombian: arepas, merengón bogotano, cocadas): the only regional cuisine next to the national ones (italiana, japonesa, mexicana). «Cocinas del mundo» covers Indian, Thai, Middle Eastern, African, Latin American … cuisine.
- **Refranes y dichos** (12 approved): Spanish sayings; the house style rules out questions that live on one language. «Refranes del mundo»: proverbs that exist across languages, their origins and equivalents.
- **Idioma** (8 approved, no list): Spanish grammar and spelling (ñ, plural of «lápiz»). «Lenguaje»: word kinds, palindromes, antonyms, alphabets, punctuation: what every language has.

Kept (recommended): Presidentes de Estados Unidos, Monarquía británica (only ~10 % of their unused concepts were US/UK-only; Lincoln, Obama, Elizabeth II are known everywhere), Comida mexicana (a world cuisine like Italian, Japanese), the Amazonas subcategories, Eurovisión, Críquet, Rugby. No new subcategory candidates.

batch-9 (`task 1185: run batch-9`) doesn''t wait: the four are small, and their batch-9 questions move with a rename.', '', '1, with a change: «Cocinas del mundo» covers only cuisines without their own subcategory (italiana, mexicana, japonesa stay separate); «Telenovelas del mundo» = melodramatic serials (telenovelas, dizi, K-drama, soaps), other TV stays in «Series».', NULL, '2026-10-16T02:12:49Z', '2026-10-16T02:35:42Z', 1204, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1247: 2026-10-15, task 1247: base subcategories renamed: Telenovelas → «Telenovelas del mundo», Comida latinoamericana → «Cocinas del mundo», Refranes y dichos → «Refranes del mundo», Idioma → «Lenguaje» (app/data/categories.json, names.en/de.json, 34 approved questions'' subcategory, pool.json; concept files telenovelas-del-mundo.json, refranes-del-mundo.json renamed, cocinas-del-mundo.json and lenguaje.json new). Scope held by retiring concepts (`retired` names decision 245): Cocinas del mundo without Italian/Mexican/Japanese dishes; Lenguaje without single languages (Idiomas del mundo); Refranes del mundo without film quotes and untranslatable words. Old names no longer exist in base; saves need no mapping (seen is by question id; only a running game''s `purged` holds a subcategory key).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (246, 'Decisions 224 and 225 point at deleted branches: mark them irrelevant?', 'answered', '["Yes: mark 224 and 225 irrelevant (pm decision irrelevant 224/225)", "No: keep them pending"]', 'Post-milestone cleanup of milestone 5 (`task 1253: post-milestone cleanup of milestone 5: Age groups and bundles in the game`) checked the pending decisions. `decision 224: Task 1181 left unstaged changes after `pm task done`: investigate` and `decision 225: Task 1144 left unstaged changes after `pm task done`: investigate` ask to look at `pm/task-1181-run-1143-left` and `pm/task-1144-run-1144-left`; neither branch exists any more (`git branch`: only `pm/task-1129-run-1084-left`, `pm/task-1205-run-1194-left`, `pm/task-632-run-1159-left`), so they were merged or discarded already. Decisions 207 and 243 still have their branches; `pm/task-632-run-1159-left` has no pending decision.', '', 'Yes: mark 224 and 225 irrelevant (pm decision irrelevant 224/225)', NULL, '2026-10-16T02:26:05Z', '2026-10-16T02:36:55Z', 1253, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (247, 'German joker keys for the new names (decision 212)', 'answered', '[]', '`decision 212: German joker names and keys (de), translated from the English?` was answered with names only. Per `decision 53: Joker and action keys per UI language (LUI-4)?` keys are mnemonic and unique on the Question screen (A–D, R, V, M taken): Wunschzeit keeps W and Finte keeps F, so Wink takes K (W taken, N is Näxt & Weg''s) and Glücksfee takes G (F taken; G was Gang runter''s key, so no relearning). D-108.', '', 'Wink K, Näxt & Weg N, Glücksfee G, Wunschzeit W, Finte F', NULL, '2026-10-16T02:48:16Z', '2026-10-16T02:48:16Z', 1098, NULL, 'rule', 1098, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (248, 'Joker names and symbols reviewed?', 'answered', '["Reviewed, no changes", "Flags in /gallery (fix task follows)"]', '`plan 136: Joker names and symbols, defined again`, task 6 (`task 1101: Gallery check and review of joker names and symbols`). New names (D-108, decisions 190–194, 210–212, keys decision 247) and symbols (decision 209) are in every catalog, the follow-up UI (skip dialog, category picker, scope, difficulty dial, hint notes), `/comodines`, store and achievement texts.

Worker check (2026-10-15): gallery shots question, joker-hint-armed, joker-hint, joker-skip, joker-category, joker-snipe, joker-easier, credits in en, es, es-ES, de at 1920 × 1080 and 1280 × 800: nothing clips; the purge button wraps its key badge to a second line with long topic names (all locales), readable.

How to review:
