- Colombianos famosos: 1 (1 approved)', '', 'the proposal as is (14 categories, 53 subcategories)', NULL, '2026-10-16T03:20:51Z', '2026-10-16T03:25:18Z', 1139, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1139: `qgen taxonomy --bundle colombia --apply work/taxonomy/colombia/proposal.json` (proposal unchanged) wrote `app/data/bundles/colombia/categories.json` (14 categories, 53 subcategories; old 6/31 replaced) and en/de names in `names.{en,de}.json`; `pool.test.ts` now checks «Regiones y departamentos de Colombia». `qgen validate` fails only on the 67 colombia questions on removed subcategories, fixed by `task 1140: Remap colombia''s existing questions onto its new taxonomy`; `qgen export` not run until then.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (250, 'Regional drafting in en, de, es-ES: prompts apply?', 'answered', '["apply", "apply with changes", "don''t apply"]', '`task 1275: Regional drafting in any launch language (en US/UK, de, es-ES, es)` (`plan 98: Regional packs (RG-3..RG-5)`, part 10). The bundles `usa` (en, US English), `germany` (de), `uk` (en, British English), `spain` (es-ES), `mexico` (es, Mexican Spanish) draft in their region''s language and variety; today the regional prompts assume Spanish (`colombia`). Below: each prompt change as verbatim old → new, in `authoring/tools/prompts/` (and `authoring/data/regional-categories.json`, the general list of `decision 213: General category list for regional bundles`, which the taxonomy prompt reads). Nothing applied yet.

Already done in code (staged, no prompt text):
- `qgen bundle new --kind region --language <L> --voice "…"`: `languages: [L]`; both required for a region.
- A bundle''s `voice` describes its own text in one locale: a regional bundle''s drafts (its first `languages` entry), base''s es text. `bundle_text()` passes it to drafts in that locale, whatever the language; `{voices}` lists the voices of the prompt''s locale only (es: base, colombia, later mexico; en: later usa, uk; de: germany; es-ES: spain). Side effect: base''s es-419 voice no longer reaches es-ES text (it contradicted `locale-es-ES.md`).
- `qgen taxonomy --apply`: the bundle''s voice goes to the names call for its own language (British spelling in uk''s `names.en.json`).

How variety inside one question locale works (the task''s proposal): **the voice wins over the locale prompt''s spelling/word lines, for the bundle''s own questions only**; no `locale-<L>-<region>.md` files. Every step (draft, rate, review, audit, fix) reads `locale-<L>.md` with its `{voices}`, so a reviewer sees uk''s British voice next to the US line and won''t flag "colour"; translations into en of other bundles (colombia, germany) aren''t listed there and keep US English.

Names stay Spanish keys in every bundle (no prompt choice, what the game needs): `namesOf` in `app/client/src/lib/data.ts` shows es and es-ES the categories.json names as they are and reads en/de from `names.<locale>.json`; a German or English key would show untranslated to a Spanish UI. So `usa`''s categories are «Geografía de Estados Unidos» etc., with en/de names drafted on `--apply`, like base''s (drafted in English since batch-9, Spanish keys).

Not changed: `house-style.md` (its "International angle" already sends regional bundles to their own rule; it has no `{voices}`), `draft.md`, `rate.md`, `review.md`, `audit.md` (language-neutral since `decision 239: English-first drafting prompts: apply?`), `translate.md`.

---

## 1. `taxonomy.md`

### 1a. Intro
old:
```
A regional bundle is a pack of trivia questions for families with a connection to one region: they live there, come from there or have family there. Its questions need that connection to answer (the bundle''s rule below). Everything players anywhere in the Spanish-speaking world answer without it stays in `base`, the main pool (its subcategories are listed below).

You propose the bundle''s broad categories and their subcategories. Drafting later picks concepts per subcategory (150–250 each) and writes questions about them, at every difficulty from 1 to 15.
```
new:
```
A regional bundle is a pack of trivia questions for families with a connection to one region: they live there, come from there or have family there. Its questions need that connection to answer (the bundle''s rule below). Everything families anywhere in the world answer without it, whatever their language, stays in `base`, the main pool (its subcategories are listed below).

You propose the bundle''s broad categories and their subcategories. Drafting later picks concepts per subcategory (150–250 each) and writes questions about them, at every difficulty from 1 to 15, in the bundle''s language and voice (under "Bundle").

Category and subcategory names are the game''s keys and are always Spanish, whatever language the bundle''s questions are in: Spanish-speaking players see them as written, English and German names are made from them later.
```

### 1b. Step 1
old:
```
1. **General list.** Start from the general category list for regional bundles. Fill `{región}` with the region''s name, in the Spanish form the players use («Comida y bebida de Colombia»). Keep a general category unless the region has too little to ask in it; a left-out one goes into `left_out` with the reason.
```
new:
```
1. **General list.** Start from the general category list for regional bundles. Fill `{región}` with the region''s name in Spanish, with the article Spanish needs («Comida y bebida de Colombia», «Deporte de Alemania», «Historia del Reino Unido»). Keep a general category unless the region has too little to ask in it; a left-out one goes into `left_out` with the reason.
```

### 1c. Each subcategory
old:
```
- `name`: Spanish, short, in the bundle''s voice; unique within the bundle (it may repeat a `base` name only if the region''s angle is clear from the name: «Ríos de Colombia», not «Ríos»).
```
new:
```
- `name`: Spanish, short; in the bundle''s voice when the bundle is Spanish-speaking, else plain Spanish with the region''s own names as Spanish speakers write them («Ríos de Alemania», «Comida del sur de Estados Unidos»); unique within the bundle (it may repeat a `base` name only if the region''s angle is clear from the name: «Ríos de Colombia», not «Ríos»).
```
old:
```
- `samples`: about 10 concepts from easy to hard, each with `known_at`.
```
new:
```
- `samples`: about 10 concepts from easy to hard, each with `known_at`, named in the bundle''s language as its families say them.
```

## 2. `taxonomy-names.md`
old:
```
- English: sentence case. German: standard German, «ß».
```
new:
```
- English: sentence case. German: standard German, «ß».
- A language under "Voice" is the bundle''s own: its names follow that voice ("Colours of …" for a British voice).
```

## 3. `authoring/data/regional-categories.json` (general list, input of `qgen taxonomy`)
`about`, old:
```
… {región} = the region''s name; names repeat across bundles (decision 110 (d)). Everywhere excluded (D-49): what players anywhere in the Spanish-speaking world answer without a connection to the region, and world topics: they stay in base.
```
new:
```
… {región} = the region''s name in Spanish (names are Spanish keys in every bundle; en/de names files); names repeat across bundles (decision 110 (d)). Everywhere excluded (D-49): what families anywhere answer without a connection to the region, whatever their language, and world topics: they stay in base.
```
«Comida y bebida de {región}» `excludes`, old → new (base names since `decision 245: base subcategories scoped to one language area: widen for the international pool?`):
```
International food (base Comida y bebida, Comida latinoamericana: arepa as a name, coffee in general).
International food (base Comida y bebida, Cocinas del mundo: a dish known worldwide by name, coffee in general).
```
«Así se habla en {región}» `excludes`, old → new:
```
Spanish in general (base Idiomas y palabras, Refranes y dichos).
The region''s language in general (base Idiomas y palabras, Refranes del mundo).
```

## 4. `locale-en.md`
old (first two bullets):
```
- All content is in English, whether you write the question or translate it.
- Plain, natural English that every English speaker reads easily: short common words, no slang, no idioms of one country.
```
new:
```
- All content is in English, whether you write the question or translate it.
- A bundle with a voice below writes its own questions in that variety; for them, the voice wins over this section''s spelling, words, idioms and date format (a British voice: "colour", "football", "biscuit", "20 July 1969"). Every other question, translations into English included, follows this section as written:
{voices}
- Plain, natural English that every English speaker reads easily: short common words, no slang, no idioms of one country.
```

## 5. `locale-es.md`
old:
```
- `colombia` only: Colombian references where they fit naturally (places, food, music, sport, people, Encanto); don''t force them. A `base` question never needs a connection to Colombia or any one country to answer (house style "International angle"); a Colombian voice is the `colombia` bundle''s.
```
new:
```
- A regional bundle (its voice above, e.g. `colombia`): its region''s references where they fit naturally (`colombia`: places, food, music, sport, people, Encanto); don''t force them. For its own questions its voice''s words win over the `base` line above. A `base` question never needs a connection to one country to answer (house style "International angle"); a national voice is a regional bundle''s.
```

## 6. `locale-es-ES.md`
old:
```
- All content is in Spain''s Spanish (castellano de España), whether you adapt a Spanish question from Latin America or translate one: the words, spelling and usage a family in Spain uses.
```
new:
```
- All content is in Spain''s Spanish (castellano de España), whether you write the question, adapt a Spanish question from Latin America or translate one: the words, spelling and usage a family in Spain uses.
- A bundle with a voice below writes its own questions in that voice, with its region''s references where they fit naturally; every other question follows this section:
{voices}
```

## 7. `locale-de.md`
old:
```
- All content is in German: standard German, spelled as in Germany (with "ß").
```
new:
```
- All content is in German, whether you write the question or translate it: standard German, spelled as in Germany (with "ß").
- A bundle with a voice below writes its own questions in that voice, with its region''s references where they fit naturally; every other question follows this section:
{voices}
```
old:
```
- Address (UI style guide `de`): never assume a plural: no "ihr", "euch", "euer", no plural imperatives ("Hört zu", "Schaut"). Where the source speaks to the players ("you", "tú"), use a generic "du" ("Hör zu: …", "wenn du niest") or an impersonal form ("Zu hören ist …"); never "Sie".
```
new:
```
- Address (UI style guide `de`): never assume a plural: no "ihr", "euch", "euer", no plural imperatives ("Hört zu", "Schaut"). Where a question speaks to the players (yours, or the source''s "you", "tú"), use a generic "du" ("Hör zu: …", "wenn du niest") or an impersonal form ("Zu hören ist …"); never "Sie".
```

## 8. `translate-region.md` (any source language; `{source_language}` is filled since plan 148)
old:
```
- **The region''s own things keep their own names:** dishes, festivals, places, people, music, sayings ("arepa", "bandeja paisa", "Feria de las Flores", "vallenato"). Add a short gloss in the target language only where the question can''t be understood without it ("tinto (black coffee)"), never one that gives the answer away.
- **Regional words travel:** a question about a regional Spanish word or saying (what a «tinto» is, what «parcero» means) is asked in the target language about the Spanish word; these players know such words. `about_language` stays for questions on Spanish spelling, grammar or wordplay.
```
new:
```
- **The region''s own things keep their own names:** dishes, festivals, places, people, music, sayings ("arepa", "Feria de las Flores", "vallenato"; "Spätzle", "Schützenfest"). Add a short gloss in the target language only where the question can''t be understood without it ("tinto (black coffee)"), never one that gives the answer away.
- **Regional words travel:** a question about a word or saying of the region (what a «tinto» is, what a „Schultüte“ is) is asked in the target language about the original word; these players know such words. `about_language` stays for questions on the spelling, grammar or wordplay of {source_language}.
```

---
Options: "apply" applies 1–8 as drafted; "apply with changes" — say which.', '', '3: don''t apply; redraft after slug category keys (milestone 9): taxonomy prompts and regional-categories.json propose slugs + en names; the locale-prompt parts (4–8) come back mostly unchanged', NULL, '2026-10-16T03:59:29Z', '2026-10-16T12:29:42Z', 1275, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1305: slug keys in plan 149: Slug keys for categories; its slug list is decision 258: Slug keys for base and colombia: the list (tasks 1275–1280 pending on it); the taxonomy prompt redraft is plan 149''s task 6, task 1275 builds on it.

2026-10-16, task 1275: Superseded by decision 266: Regional drafting in en, de, es-ES: prompts apply? (after slug keys); applied there.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (251, 'Scan runs: which slots keep their pick after fix?', 'answered', '[]', 'task 1244: qgen scan runs: review shows the kept pick, not candidates. kept_slots used fix.changed, so a note-only change dropped the slot from kept_slots and deleted its candidates while the file stayed: a pointless re-search and re-pick. revise_in_pool already unpicks on a type/query change, so a remaining file_url is the signal; the review sees the kept file and can send the question to needs_work if it no longer fits the new wording.', '', 'Every slot still picked with a usable licence; fix unpicks a slot only when its type or query changes (a note or role change keeps the file and its candidates)', NULL, '2026-10-16T04:11:19Z', '2026-10-16T04:11:19Z', 1244, NULL, 'rule', 1244, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (252, 'review.md: lines for a scan run''s kept media: apply?', 'irrelevant', '["apply as drafted", "apply with changes"]', '`task 1244: qgen scan runs: review shows the kept pick, not candidates`: in a scan run (`qgen neutralize`, `qgen tighten`) a kept slot''s review input is now `{type, role, query, note, kept: true, title}`: no candidates, no sheet, `can_search_again: false` (code done, staged). `authoring/tools/prompts/review.md` needs to say what to do with it (D-36: prompt changes need your OK). Exact text:

1. Input, new bullet after `background`:
   - `kept` on `media` or `background` (scan runs, `qgen neutralize` and `qgen tighten`): the slot keeps the file it already has in the game; you see its `title`, no candidates and no sheet.

2. "Pick the media", new first paragraph:
   **Kept media:** for a slot with `kept: true` there is nothing to pick and no new search: leave its `pick` or `background_pick` null, and `new_query` null. Judge the kept file by its title, type, role and note against the question''s current wording: if it now gives the answer away (reason 3) or no longer shows what the question names, decide `needs_work` with problem `giveaway` or `media` and say so in `feedback`; a media-only problem leaves `fix` empty. Text in the media is never a problem by itself.

3. Reason 5 becomes: "5. No candidate is adequate (below), and a new search can''t help or was already tried; or a kept file no longer fits (below)."

`record` already keeps the model''s needs_work and feedback for such a slot (unchanged).', '', NULL, 'replaced by 254; its ''text in the media is never a problem'' sentence contradicts the essential rule', '2026-10-16T04:11:25Z', '2026-10-16T14:14:07Z', 1244, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (253, 'review.md: lines for a scan run''s kept media: apply?', 'answered', '["apply as drafted", "apply with changes"]', '', '', 'see 254', NULL, '2026-10-16T04:11:38Z', '2026-10-16T14:14:07Z', 1244, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1244: Superseded by decision 254: review.md text applied (see its consequences).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (254, 'review.md: lines for a scan run''s kept media (corrected text): apply?', 'answered', '["apply as drafted", "apply with changes"]', 'Replaces decisions 252 and 253 (same subject; 252 has a wrong sentence, 253 an empty body, both worker mistakes: answer 253 "see 254", close 252 as irrelevant, it blocks nothing).

`task 1244: qgen scan runs: review shows the kept pick, not candidates`: in a scan run (`qgen neutralize`, `qgen tighten`) a kept slot''s review input is now `{type, role, query, note, kept: true, title}`: no candidates, no sheet, `can_search_again: false` (code done, staged; `decision 251: Scan runs: which slots keep their pick after fix?`). `authoring/tools/prompts/review.md` needs to say what to do with it (D-36: prompt changes need your OK). Exact text:

1. Input, new bullet after `background`:
   - `kept` on `media` or `background` (scan runs, `qgen neutralize` and `qgen tighten`): the slot keeps the file it already has in the game; you see its `title`, no candidates and no sheet.

2. "Pick the media", new first paragraph:
   **Kept media:** for a slot with `kept: true` there is nothing to pick and no new search: leave its `pick` or `background_pick` null, and `new_query` null. Judge the kept file by its title, type, role and note against the question''s current wording: if it now gives the answer away (reason 3) or no longer shows what the question names, decide `needs_work` with problem `giveaway` or `media` and say so in `feedback`; a media-only problem leaves `fix` empty.

3. Reason 5 becomes: "5. No candidate is adequate (below), and a new search can''t help or was already tried; or a kept file no longer fits (below)."

`record` already keeps the model''s needs_work and feedback for such a slot (unchanged). After the answer, task 1244''s worker applies the text, runs `npm run check` and closes the task.', '', 'apply with changes: 254''s text, plus (a) in the kept paragraph: ''A null pick on a kept slot is not by itself a reason for needs_work.'' (b) problems → media: ''no adequate candidate, or a kept file that no longer fits (reason 5)''. (c) reasons: ''naming what you saw on the sheet (for a kept slot, its title)''.', NULL, '2026-10-16T04:12:10Z', '2026-10-16T14:14:07Z', 1244, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1244: authoring/tools/prompts/review.md: new input bullet `kept`, reason 5 extended, ''Kept media'' paragraph (null pick on a kept slot is no reason for needs_work), problems → media and reasons wording include kept slots. Scan-run review payload for kept slots has no candidates/sheet (task 1244).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (255, 'Spot check neutralize-1 done?', 'answered', '["done"]', 'Blind spot check of `neutralize-1` (`task 632: run neutralize-1`; report authoring/reports/neutralize-1.md: 1066 scanned, 388 reworded, 367 approved, 21 needs_work, $2.74). Start `trivia-authoring`, open http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?run=neutralize-1&sample=1 and decide 30 random questions blind (about 15 min). Extra check (authoring/QC.md "Neutralize runs"): the wording is neutral, the meaning unchanged. Flagged audit findings afterwards: http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?run=neutralize-1&audit=flagged. Answer once the 30 are decided; then `task 633: QC neutralize-1` runs `qgen report --qc neutralize-1` and asks for the changes. Not answered by an LLM.', '', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-16T04:17:27Z', '2026-10-16T13:01:22Z', 633, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-24, task 639: No wait: neutralize-1''s spot check was done; tr-en-2 ran on the neutralized pool.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (256, 'tr-es-1: wait for batch-9''s English sources?', 'answered', '["wait: batch-9''s QC is done, run tr-es-1", "lower task 1223 below -100 so batch-9 runs first"]', '`task 1223: run tr-es-1` (en → es pilot, 50 sources) needs ≥ 50 approved en-sourced `base` questions. Checked 2026-10-15: `plan 148: English-first drafting for base` is done (`--translate es` ready), but no en sources exist yet: `task 1185: run batch-9` and `task 1186: QC batch-9` are open. No open decision blocks task 1185 (`decision 229: Continue batch-9 after the extended batch-8 review?` is answered); it waits only because the queue runs -90 before -100. Answer once task 1186 is done; task 1223 then runs `qgen batch --translate es`.', '', 'wait: batch-9''s QC is done, run tr-es-1', NULL, '2026-10-16T04:19:58Z', '2026-10-21T21:43:28Z', 1223, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-23, task 1228: tr-es-2 ran after batch-9''s QC; the es chain continues with tr-es-3 (task 1733).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (257, 'batch-9: health stop, ack?', 'answered', '["acked now: rerun batch-9", "not yet"]', '`task 1185: run batch-9` reran plain `qgen batch` after `decision 229: Continue batch-9 after the extended batch-8 review?` ("go: acked, run batch-9"), but batch-8''s ack isn''t recorded (no `batch-8` in the health acks file), so the batch stopped again with exit 2. The worker never acks (RUNBOOK). Please run `qgen health ack batch-8 "<note>"`, then answer here.

Output verbatim:

    batch-8 fails the batch health thresholds: overlap rate, max final−target gap 11–15, media share.
    See `qgen report --batches` or authoring/reports/batches.md. The developer looks at it and clears the stop with: qgen health ack batch-8 "<note>"

No claude calls (stopped before any step; no `claude:` line printed).', '', 'acked now: rerun batch-9', NULL, '2026-10-16T04:21:02Z', '2026-10-16T13:12:03Z', 1185, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (258, 'Slug keys for base and colombia: the list', 'answered', '["as proposed", "with changes (name the rows and their slugs)", "keep the region in colombia''s slugs"]', 'Milestone 9, "Slug keys for categories" (developer, 2026-10-16); `plan 9: masterplan` part 16, written by `task 1305: write plan: Slug keys for categories`. Every category and subcategory of `base` and `colombia` gets an English slug as its key: questions'' `subcategory`, `targets.json`, concept file names, engine key (`subKey`: base bare, else `<bundle>/<slug>`), saves (old keys mapped on load), reports, review tool. Display names, en included, then come only from `names.<locale>.json` (`names.es.json` new, holding today''s Spanish names unchanged; the family''s game shows the same names, D-59).

How the list below was made (no claude call):
- Slug = today''s en name in `names.en.json`, lowercased, accents and apostrophes dropped, other runs of non-letters → `-` (form `^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$`). Kept as the en names are spelled today (e.g. `maths`, `colours`); the en names themselves don''t change.
- `colombia`: the region dropped from its slugs (`colombia/animals`, not `colombia/animals-of-colombia`): the engine key already carries the bundle; a few cut by hand (`19th-century`, `national-symbols`, `people` for «Personajes de Colombia», `how-colombia-speaks`).
- Unique within each bundle, per kind; a category and one of its subcategories may share a slug (`history` / `history`, `football` / `football`): they live in separate maps (categories vs. subcategories); the migration task checks no code mixes them.
- Format per row: **old category slug → new**: «Spanish name» / en name; under it each subcategory: `new slug`: «Spanish name (today''s key)» / en name.
- Not in scope: bundle ids (already English slugs) and `bundles.json`''s Spanish `name`/`description` stay as they are.

