left out: []', 'The new German question pack needs its own list of topics, so its questions cover life in Germany evenly. The proposal keeps the general topics every regional pack has, adds one topic of its own (the former East Germany), and splits them into 53 subtopics, about 38 questions each at 2000 questions. Applying it fixes the pack''s structure; the Spanish topic names are drafted at that point.', 'the proposal as is (15 categories, 53 subcategories)', NULL, '2026-10-16T21:10:05Z', '2026-10-16T21:20:35Z', 1277, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1277: germany taxonomy applied: app/data/bundles/germany/categories.json holds 15 categories and 53 subcategories keyed by English slugs; names.en/es/de.json written (68 names each, es/en drafted on apply).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (295, 'Timed mode: the claimer answers with one press, no final-answer step, a short reveal', 'answered', '[]', 'Decision 290 and decision 275 say the claimer answers as on the Question screen; that names the inputs, not the two-step lock-in. The lock-in plus PADLOCK_MS (1.4 s) leaves under 5 s to think and invites claim timeouts that feel like input failures. The pace of the race needs a quick reveal; the drama is in the clock, not the wait.', 'In the timed race, the player who grabs a question has only six seconds to answer. The normal game makes players pick an answer, wait for a padlock and confirm it as their final answer, then holds a drum roll of several seconds before the reveal; that would eat most of the six seconds and slow the race. Here a single press is the answer, and the result shows after a short fixed beat.', 'In timed, the claimer''s first pick (pad face button, A–D/1–4, or a click) is the answer: no lock-in, no padlock, no «Respuesta final», no level-dependent drum roll; the reveal follows after a fixed TIMED_REVEAL_MS beat (about 1.2 s, timing.ts), visible to everyone, then the next question or the round end', NULL, '2026-10-16T21:13:18Z', '2026-10-16T21:13:18Z', 1399, NULL, 'rule', 1399, '2026-10-16, task 1399: written into plan 164: Timed game screens, drama and sound (Timed screen, Answer).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (296, 'Timed mode: a round screen with a countdown before each round, and the question clock starts when the question is on screen', 'answered', '[]', 'With shown_at set at the previous question''s end (plan 159 as written), the reveal beat, the fade and a round screen would come off the next question''s 30 s, and a slow machine would lose more. A press to continue would need a rule for which player may press; the countdown is fair to all and keeps the pace.', 'Between rounds of the timed race, the screen shows the round number and every player''s hearts, including the hearts just lost. Somebody has to move on from there, and the question''s 30 seconds must not start ticking while the screen is still fading in or showing the last answer. This rule moves on by itself after a short countdown, and starts each question''s clock only once the question is visible.', 'Each round opens on the Level screen as a round screen (round n of 12 or sudden death, hearts per player, the hearts lost at the last round end break there, players out marked) and moves on by itself after a 3-2-1 countdown (no press, so no player has to be the one to press; the Esc menu still opens); inside a round the next question follows the reveal directly; the engine starts a question''s 30 s on a show action the client sends once the question has faded in, not at the end of the previous one', NULL, '2026-10-16T21:13:18Z', '2026-10-16T21:13:18Z', 1399, NULL, 'rule', 1399, '2026-10-16, task 1399: written into plan 164: Timed game screens, drama and sound (Flow); engine side: task 1447: Timed: the question clock starts on show, not at the previous question''s end (plan 159).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (297, 'Timed mode visuals: what should change in the hearts, red frame and claim banner?', 'pending', '["Changes (name them)", "Keep as they are; just remove the PLACEHOLDER marks"]', 'Play a timed session on the TV after `task 1449: Timed screen and flow: round screen, question for all, clock, claims, one-press answer`, `task 1451: Timed drama and sound: heart pulses, heartbeat, last-3-s ticks, red frame, timed track` and `task 1452: Timed sudden death and ends: «Muerte súbita», winner, last standing, nobody wins, resume line` are done. Answer with what to change; `task 1453: Timed visuals polish: hearts, red frame, claim banner` applies it and removes the PLACEHOLDER marks.', 'The fast-paced competitive mode shows each player''s lives as hearts, a pulsing red frame when time is running out, and a banner naming the player who grabbed the question. These first versions are rough. Once you have played the mode on the TV, say what to change, or keep them as they are; the answer is what the final visual pass builds.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-16T21:15:41Z', NULL, 1448, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (298, 'uk taxonomy: categories and subcategories', 'answered', '["Apply the proposal as written", "Apply with changes (say which)"]', 'Bundle `uk` (British English, `languages: ["en"]`, country GB, target 2000 ≈ 36 per subcategory).

Rule: Answering needs a connection to the United Kingdom: British places, food, customs, holidays, people, music, sport, media, words, sayings or history that players outside the UK mostly wouldn''t know; topics shared across the English-speaking world, and American-only ones (those belong to `usa`), are not here. 

Voice: British English: UK spelling ("colour", "grey", "realise"), UK words ("football", "biscuit", "lorry", "holiday", "pavement"), dates as "20 July 1969", metric units with miles and pints where Britons use them 

Proposal (`qgen taxonomy --bundle uk`, from the general list of `decision 213: General category list for regional bundles`): 15 categories, 56 subcategories, one region category (`comedy`). Slug and English name (the bundle''s language is en; es and de names are drafted on apply). Full proposal with scopes and samples: `work/taxonomy/uk/proposal.md`.

- `geography` Geography of the UK (6, general)
  - `cities-and-towns` British cities and towns
  - `london` London
  - `counties-and-regions` Counties and regions
  - `rivers-coasts-and-islands` Rivers, coasts and islands
  - `hills-moors-and-national-parks` Hills, moors and national parks
  - `landmarks-and-castles` Landmarks and castles
- `nature` Nature of the UK (4, general)
  - `wildlife` British wildlife
  - `birds` British birds
  - `plants-and-gardens` Plants and gardens
  - `weather-and-seasons` British weather
- `history` History of the UK (6, general)
  - `early-britain` Early Britain
  - `middle-ages` Medieval Britain
  - `tudors-and-stuarts` Tudors and Stuarts
  - `georgians-and-victorians` Georgians and Victorians
  - `twentieth-century` Britain in the 20th century
  - `parliament-and-prime-ministers` Parliament and prime ministers
- `people` People of the UK (2, general)
  - `scientists-and-inventors` British scientists and inventors
  - `pioneers-and-heroes` British pioneers and heroes
- `food-and-drink` British food and drink (5, general)
  - `classic-dishes` Classic British dishes
  - `regional-specialities` Regional specialities
  - `cakes-puddings-and-biscuits` Cakes, puddings and biscuits
  - `sweets-and-crisps` Sweets, crisps and snacks
  - `drinks` British drinks
- `festivals-and-traditions` British festivals and traditions (3, general)
  - `holidays-and-celebrations` British holidays and celebrations
  - `christmas-in-britain` A British Christmas
  - `customs-and-ceremonies` Customs and ceremonies
- `myths-and-legends` British myths and legends (2, general)
  - `legendary-heroes` Legendary British heroes
  - `creatures-ghosts-and-superstitions` Creatures, ghosts and superstitions
- `music-and-dance` British music and dance (3, general)
  - `pop-and-rock` British pop and charts
  - `traditional-music-and-dance` Traditional music and dance
  - `nursery-rhymes-and-singalongs` Nursery rhymes and singalongs
- `art-and-literature` British art and literature (3, general)
  - `writers-and-poets` British writers and poets
  - `childrens-books-and-comics` Children''s books and comics
  - `art-and-architecture` British art and architecture
- `film-and-television` British film and television (4, general)
  - `childrens-tv` Children''s TV
  - `soaps-and-dramas` Soaps and dramas
  - `game-shows-and-presenters` Game shows and presenters
  - `british-films` British films
- `comedy` British comedy (2, region)
  - `sitcoms` British sitcoms
  - `comedians-and-panel-shows` Comedians and panel shows
- `sports` Sport in the UK (5, general)
  - `football` British football
  - `rugby-and-cricket` Rugby and cricket in Britain
  - `team-gb-and-olympians` Team GB and Olympians
  - `sporting-events` Big British sporting events
  - `pub-and-playground-games` Pub and playground games
- `how-people-speak` How Britain speaks (4, general)
  - `slang-and-words` British slang and words
  - `sayings-and-idioms` British sayings and idioms
  - `accents-and-dialects` Accents and dialects
  - `languages-of-britain` Languages of Britain
- `daily-life` Daily life in the UK (5, general)
  - `money-and-shopping` Money and shopping
  - `brands-and-adverts` British brands and adverts
  - `transport` Getting around Britain
  - `school-and-childhood` School and childhood
  - `home-and-public-services` Home and public services
- `symbols` Symbols of the UK (2, general)
  - `flags-and-emblems` Flags and emblems
  - `crown-and-state` Crown and state symbols', 'The new British question pack needs its own list of topics, so its questions cover life in the United Kingdom evenly. The proposal keeps the general topics every regional pack has, adds one topic of its own (British comedy), and splits them into 56 subtopics, about 36 questions each at 2000 questions. Applying it fixes the pack''s structure; the Spanish and German topic names are drafted at that point.', 'Apply the proposal as written', NULL, '2026-10-16T21:16:18Z', '2026-10-16T21:19:37Z', 1278, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1278: uk taxonomy applied: app/data/bundles/uk/categories.json holds 15 categories and 56 subcategories keyed by English slugs; names.en/es/de.json written (71 names each, es/de drafted on apply).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (299, 'Local multiplayer stays in the release check: smoke step multiplayer and a real-pad row', 'answered', '[]', 'Decided by task 1402 for plan 152 part 11 (milestone 16 close-out). Always, not full only: a content-only patch changes the pool, and session supply per seat (plans 158, 159) can fail on data alone. Fake pads can''t see Chromium''s or Steam Input''s real pad limits (task 1431), hence the manual row on full releases, where shell or client code changes. Same pattern as plan 122''s mods step and workshop row.', 'The three multiplayer modes have no other check that plays a whole game on the real, packaged build, so a later change could quietly break them before a Steam upload. This settles that every release candidate plays each mode through automatically, with pretend controllers, and that full releases add one short hand check with real controllers under Steam.', 'Yes: release-check step multiplayer (always, after smoke: smoke.mjs --multiplayer on the packaged Linux build, fake pads, every mode with pads only, keyboard only and 4 pads + keyboard and mouse) and manual row multiplayer-pads (full only: real pads under Steam Input on the beta, one session per mode to its first turn change or claim).', NULL, '2026-10-16T21:20:14Z', '2026-10-16T21:20:14Z', 1402, NULL, 'rule', 1402, '2026-10-16, task 1402: written into plan 167: Local multiplayer close-out and family playtest (task 1 adds the step and the row).

2026-10-17, task 1473: 2026-10-16, task 1473: authoring/steam/smoke.mjs --multiplayer (9 sessions, fake pads from authoring/tools/fake_pads.js shared with gallery.py), release_check.py step multiplayer after smoke and MANUAL row multiplayer-pads (full); AGENTS.md, plans/11-steam.md. Found: plan 172 (keyboard seats can''t be taken after a restart), task 1519 (pool-less packs break smoke''s without-packs stage).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (300, 'spain taxonomy: categories and subcategories', 'answered', '["Apply the proposal as it stands", "Apply with changes (name them in the answer)"]', 'Bundle `spain` (Spain''s Spanish, `languages: ["es-ES"]`, en joins after translation, country ES, target 2000 ≈ 38 per subcategory).

Rule: Answering needs a connection to Spain: Spanish places, food, customs, fiestas, people, music, sport, media, words, sayings or history that players outside Spain mostly wouldn''t know; things families anywhere know (Madrid as a capital, Don Quixote, paella as a dish) stay in `base`, and the topics of Latin American regions (`colombia`, `mexico`) are not here.

Voice: Spanish as spoken in Spain (es-ES): peninsular words ("ordenador", "móvil", "coche", "zumo", "patata", "vale"), "vosotros" forms, dates as "20 de julio de 1969", metric units

Proposal (`qgen taxonomy --bundle spain`, from the general list of `decision 213: General category list for regional bundles`): 14 categories, 53 subcategories. Slug, English name, Spanish (Spain) name in brackets (the bundle''s language; de names are drafted on apply). Full proposal with scopes and samples: `work/taxonomy/spain/proposal.md`. Left out of the general list: none.

- `geography` Geography of Spain (Geografía de España) (5, general)
  - `regions-and-provinces` Spanish regions and provinces (Comunidades y provincias)
  - `cities-and-towns` Spanish cities and towns (Ciudades y pueblos de España)
  - `rivers-and-mountains` Rivers and mountains of Spain (Ríos y montañas de España)
  - `coasts-and-islands` Coasts and islands of Spain (Costas e islas de España)
  - `monuments` Monuments of Spain (Monumentos de España)
- `nature` Nature of Spain (Naturaleza de España) (3, general)
  - `wildlife` Spanish wildlife (Fauna ibérica)
  - `plants-and-climate` Spanish plants, landscapes and weather (Flora, paisajes y clima de España)
  - `protected-areas` Spanish national parks (Parques naturales de España)
- `history` History of Spain (Historia de España) (6, general)
  - `ancient-hispania` Ancient Hispania (Prehistoria e Hispania antigua)
  - `al-andalus-and-reconquista` Al-Andalus and the medieval kingdoms (Al-Ándalus y los reinos medievales)
  - `empire` The Spanish empire (Reyes Católicos y los Austrias)
  - `bourbons-and-19th-century` Bourbons and the 19th century (Los Borbones y el siglo XIX)
  - `20th-century` Spain in the 20th century (España en el siglo XX)
  - `transition-and-democracy` Transition and democracy (La Transición y la democracia)
- `people` People of Spain (Personajes de España) (2, general)
  - `scientists-and-explorers` Spanish scientists, inventors and explorers (Científicos, inventores y exploradores)
  - `famous-figures` Spanish chefs, entrepreneurs and celebrities (Cocineros, empresarios y famosos)
- `food-and-drink` Spanish food and drink (Gastronomía de España) (5, general)
  - `regional-dishes` Spanish regional dishes (Platos regionales)
  - `tapas` Tapas and bar food (Tapas y bares)
  - `sweets-and-desserts` Spanish sweets and desserts (Dulces y postres)
  - `ham-cheese-and-produce` Spanish ham, cheese and produce (Jamón, quesos y productos)
  - `drinks` Spanish drinks (Bebidas de España)
- `festivals-and-traditions` Spanish festivals and traditions (Fiestas y tradiciones de España) (3, general)
  - `fiestas` Spanish fiestas (Fiestas populares)
  - `christmas-and-holidays` Christmas and Holy Week in Spain (Navidad, Semana Santa y festivos)
  - `dress-crafts-and-games` Spanish traditional dress, crafts and games (Trajes, artesanía y juegos tradicionales)
- `myths-and-legends` Spanish myths and legends (Mitos y leyendas de España) (2, general)
  - `creatures` Spanish legendary creatures (Criaturas legendarias)
  - `legends-and-superstitions` Spanish legends and superstitions (Leyendas y supersticiones)
- `music-and-dance` Spanish music and dance (Música y baile de España) (4, general)
  - `flamenco-and-copla` Flamenco and copla (Flamenco y copla)
  - `folk-music-and-dance` Spanish folk music and dance (Música y bailes tradicionales)
  - `pop-and-rock` Spanish pop and rock to 2000 (Pop y rock español hasta 2000)
  - `current-music` Spanish music today (Música española actual)
- `art-and-literature` Spanish art and literature (Arte y literatura de España) (4, general)
  - `classic-literature` Classic Spanish literature (Literatura clásica española)
  - `modern-literature` Modern Spanish literature (Literatura española moderna)
  - `painting-and-architecture` Spanish painters, sculptors and architects (Pintores, escultores y arquitectos)
  - `comics-and-childrens-books` Spanish comics and children''s books (Tebeos y libros infantiles)
- `film-and-television` Spanish film and television (Cine y televisión de España) (5, general)
  - `spanish-cinema` Spanish cinema (Cine español)
  - `tv-series` Spanish TV series (Series españolas)
  - `tv-shows-and-presenters` Spanish TV shows and presenters (Programas y presentadores de televisión)
  - `childrens-tv` Spanish children''s TV (Televisión infantil en España)
  - `radio-and-internet` Spanish radio and internet stars (Radio, youtubers y streamers)
- `sports` Sport in Spain (Deporte en España) (4, general)
  - `football-clubs` Spanish football clubs (Clubes de fútbol españoles)
  - `footballers-and-national-team` Spanish footballers and La Roja (Futbolistas y la Selección)
  - `sportspeople` Spanish sportspeople (Deportistas españoles)
  - `team-and-traditional-sports` Spanish basketball, team and traditional sports (Baloncesto, otros deportes y deportes tradicionales)
- `how-people-speak` How Spain speaks (Cómo se habla en España) (4, general)
  - `slang` Spanish slang (Jerga y palabras coloquiales)
  - `sayings` Spanish sayings and expressions (Refranes y frases hechas)
  - `regional-speech` Regional accents and words of Spain (Acentos y palabras regionales)
  - `co-official-languages` Languages of Spain (Lenguas de España)
- `daily-life` Daily life in Spain (Vida cotidiana en España) (4, general)
  - `brands-and-shops` Spanish brands and shops (Marcas y tiendas españolas)
  - `transport` Transport in Spain (Transporte en España)
  - `school-and-home` School and home in Spain (Colegio, casa y costumbres)
  - `money-and-services` Money and public services in Spain (Dinero, trámites y servicios)
- `symbols` Symbols of Spain (Símbolos de España) (2, general)
  - `national-symbols` National symbols of Spain (Símbolos nacionales)
  - `regional-symbols` Regional flags and emblems of Spain (Banderas y emblemas regionales)', 'The new Spanish question pack needs its own list of topics, so its questions cover life in Spain evenly. The proposal uses the general topics every regional pack has, all 14 of them, and splits them into 53 subtopics, about 38 questions each at 2000 questions. Applying it fixes the pack''s structure; the English and German topic names are drafted at that point.', 'Apply the proposal as it stands', NULL, '2026-10-16T21:20:43Z', '2026-10-16T21:21:36Z', 1279, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1279: spain taxonomy applied as proposed: app/data/bundles/spain/categories.json holds 14 categories, 53 subcategories keyed by English slugs; names in names.en.json, names.es.json (read by es-ES), names.de.json of the bundle. qgen validate and export pass. Bundle, target 2000, plans 22/15c and the DLC tasks 1470-1472 were already in place.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (301, 'Remote Play API from the shell: own koffi load of the Steam library, v003 calls, sessions by polling', 'answered', '[]', 'Task 1418 (2026-10-16): nm on SDK 1.62''s libsteam_api.so and steam_api64.dll lists every ISteamRemotePlay v003 call above (no GetSessionGuestID, avatars, BSessionRemotePlayTogether: v004, newer SDK). steamworks-ffi-node 0.11.3 binds only ISteamInput_GetRemotePlaySessionID and the overlay invite dialog; its loader is a private field. Throw-away Node probe, Steam running, App ID 480: koffi.load of SDK 1.62''s lib → SteamAPI_InitSafe true, v003 accessor, GetSessionCount 0, a second koffi.load of the same path works, BEnableRemotePlayTogetherDirectInput true, GetInput(null, 0) 0; the same with the newer libs in the trunk''s app/desktop/steamworks_sdk/ (v004). Polling over callbacks: the binding''s CCallbackBase vtable pattern needs different slots on Windows and Linux (its own comment), while session lists change rarely and a 100 ms poll is enough. Builds on decision 28: Steam binding for the Electron shell? and decision 69: Steamworks SDK libs for dev and the bridge''s SDK path.', 'Steam''s Remote Play Together lets friends far away join a local game through Steam''s stream. To know who joined, and to tell a friend''s keyboard from the host''s, the desktop shell has to call parts of Steam that our Steam library wrapper doesn''t cover. This settles how the shell reaches them: by loading Steam''s own library a second time and calling it directly, and by checking the list of connected friends regularly rather than waiting for Steam to call back.', 'app/desktop/main.mjs koffi.load()s the same libsteam_api the binding loaded (steamSdkDir()), takes the newest exported SteamAPI_SteamRemotePlay_v00N accessor (v003 in SDK 1.62, v004 in newer libs) and calls only v003''s flat functions (GetSessionCount, GetSessionID, GetSessionSteamID, GetSessionClientName, GetSessionClientFormFactor, BEnableRemotePlayTogetherDirectInput, DisableRemotePlayTogetherDirectInput, GetInput, SetMouseVisibility/Position, CreateMouseCursor, SetMouseCursor; Steam Input''s GetRemotePlaySessionID through the binding). Sessions: polled on the existing runCallbacks tick and diffed into connect/disconnect events; no SteamAPI_RegisterCallback of our own. A guest is a session whose GetSessionSteamID differs from the host''s (the developer''s own Steam Link device has the host''s id; BSessionRemotePlayTogether is v004 only). koffi becomes a direct dependency of app/desktop at the binding''s version (3.3.3). No fork, no wait for upstream.', NULL, '2026-10-16T21:24:59Z', '2026-10-16T21:24:59Z', 1418, NULL, 'rule', 1418, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (302, 'Remote Play Together live probe: guests'' pads, keyboard and mouse on a Windows and a Linux host', 'pending', '["done (notes per step and host)", "not possible yet (why)"]', 'Live part of the Remote Play investigation (`milestone 17: Remote Play Together`, part 1). Needs part 2''s setup decision answered (Remote Play Together on for the real App ID, a `beta` build, second account and machine; Spacewar 480 is no test) and a `beta` build with the probe switch `--rp-probe` (task "Remote Play probe switch in the shell" of `plan` "Investigation: Remote Play input and session API").

Setup: the host launches ¡Trivia! from Steam with launch option `--rp-probe` (Linux: `%command% --rp-probe`); the probe logs to `rp-probe.log` in the shell''s userData dir (path printed at start and shown on screen) and shows its last lines in a corner. The guest joins through the Steam overlay''s Remote Play invite (Windows host) or the friends list (Linux host). Run every step on a Windows host and on a Linux host (the Deck as host if at hand); the guest on any machine.

Steps (note per host what happened; attach or paste the log):
1. Guest connects: log shows `session +` with name, form factor, Steam id; leaves and rejoins: `session -`, then `+` with the same or a new session id
2. Guest''s pad: listed by `pads` (index, id) and `steam-input` (handle, type, session id ≠ 0, gamepad index); press A on it: which index reacts; a second pad on the guest, if at hand
3. Host''s own pad meanwhile: session id 0, its index unchanged
4. Direct input off (F9 toggles, starts off): the guest types and moves the mouse: do the host''s cursor and the game window react (`dom key`/`dom mouse` lines)?
5. Direct input on: the guest types, clicks, moves: `rp key`/`rp mouse` lines with the guest''s session; any `dom` lines (there should be none)? The host''s keyboard and mouse still give `dom` lines? What does the guest see as cursor: none, Steam''s arrow, the probe''s cursor (F10 sets a custom one)?
6. Steam overlay on the host: which per-guest toggles exist (keyboard, mouse, controller); with direct input off, does turning off the guest''s keyboard and mouse stop their `dom` lines?
7. Lag feel: the probe flashes (F11), the guest presses A at once; the log prints the delay as the host sees it (rough; the timed-mode measurement is separate)
8. Your own Steam Link (phone, TV or a second PC on your account), if at hand: `session +` with the host''s own Steam id

Answer «done» with the notes; a step that didn''t work as one line each.', 'Before friends can join a game over the internet through Steam, we need to see on real machines how their controllers, keyboards and mice reach the game. Only the developer can do this, with a second Steam account on a second computer. The answers decide whether a friend''s keyboard and mouse can count as a player of their own, or whether friends far away must play with a controller.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-16T21:25:25Z', NULL, 1418, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (303, 'Remote Play Together test setup ready? Switch on, beta build, two machines, second account', 'pending', '["ready (App ID, BuildID, host OSes, what Steamworks required)", "not yet (why)", "issues (rows)"]', 'One-time setup for every live Remote Play run of `milestone 17: Remote Play Together` (`plan 169: Steamworks switch and Remote Play test setup`; checklist in `plans/18-steam-integration.md`, section "Remote Play Together setup (SW-13)", once written). Valve''s page and field names unverified: recheck at entry.

- Preconditions: `decision 179: Steamworks app configured (SW-7)? IDs?` answered (real App ID, `beta` branch; Spacewar 480 is no test); first `beta` upload done (`task 681: First beta upload: checklist and decision`)
- Steamworks, the app''s Remote Play settings: Remote Play Together on; TV/phone/tablet at Steam''s default
  - categories required (local multiplayer / co-op / PvP)? set what milestone 16''s modes justify; note which
  - publish the changes
  - Steam refuses for an unreleased app or a password `beta` branch: report, don''t work around
- `beta` build: `trivia-steam upload --branch beta` of a commit with the live run''s code (first: the `--rp-probe` switch of `plan 168: Investigation: Remote Play input and session API`); note BuildID and `v<version>` tag
- Machines: host A Windows (overlay invite, `decision 70: Steam overlay in the Electron shell`); host B Linux or the Deck (invite from the friends list); each hosts once, the other is the guest
- Accounts: yours on the host; a second one (`decision 135: Steamworks: enable Workshop for ¡Trivia! and a second Steam account?`, or a family member''s) on the guest, Steam friends with yours; guests need no copy
- Pads: one on the guest machine, one on the host; a second guest pad if at hand
- Smoke: host starts ¡Trivia! from `beta`, invites the guest; guest sees the picture, hears the sound; one guest pad press moves the focus

Answer `decision 302: Remote Play Together live probe: guests'' pads, keyboard and mouse on a Windows and a Linux host`''s setup line by this.', 'Before friends far away can join a game through Steam''s Remote Play Together, the feature has to be switched on in Steam''s developer settings, a test version has to be on Steam, and there have to be two computers with two Steam accounts that are friends. Only the developer can do this. Choose whether everything is ready, not yet ready, or ready with problems; every real test of remote play waits for this answer.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-16T21:27:54Z', NULL, 1480, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (304, 'mexico taxonomy: categories and subcategories', 'answered', '["Apply the proposal as it stands", "Apply with changes (say which)"]', 'Bundle `mexico` (Mexican Spanish, `languages: ["es"]`, en joins after translation, country MX, target 2000 ≈ 34 per subcategory).

Rule: Answering needs a connection to Mexico: Mexican places, food, customs, fiestas, people, music, sport, media, words, sayings or history that players outside Mexico mostly wouldn''t know; things families anywhere know (Mexico City as a capital, tacos as a dish) stay in `base`, and the topics of other Latin American regions (`colombia`) and of Spain (`spain`) are not here.

Voice: Mexican Spanish: "computadora", "celular", "carro", "camión" (bus), "platicar", "chamarra", "padre" (cool), "ahorita", "ustedes" (no vosotros), dates as "20 de julio de 1969", metric units

Proposal (`qgen taxonomy --bundle mexico`, from the general list of `decision 213: General category list for regional bundles`): 15 categories, 58 subcategories. Slug, English name, Spanish (Mexico) name in brackets (the bundle''s language; de names are drafted on apply). Full proposal with scopes and samples: `work/taxonomy/mexico/proposal.md`. Left out of the general list: none.

- `geography` Geography of Mexico (Geografía de México) (4, general)
  - `states-and-capitals` Mexican states and capitals (Estados de México y sus capitales)
  - `cities-and-towns` Cities and Pueblos Mágicos (Ciudades y Pueblos Mágicos)
  - `landscapes` Volcanoes, rivers and coasts of Mexico (Volcanes, ríos, lagos y costas)
  - `landmarks` Mexican landmarks and monuments (Monumentos y lugares emblemáticos)
- `nature` Nature of Mexico (Naturaleza de México) (3, general)
  - `animals` Animals of Mexico (Animales de México)
  - `plants` Plants and flowers of Mexico (Plantas y flores de México)
  - `reserves-and-climate` Mexican reserves, climate and quakes (Reservas, clima y fenómenos naturales)
- `history` History of Mexico (Historia de México) (4, general)
  - `conquest-and-colony` Conquest and New Spain (Conquista y Colonia)
  - `independence-and-19th-century` Independence and the 19th century (Independencia y siglo XIX)
  - `revolution` The Mexican Revolution (La Revolución Mexicana)
  - `20th-century` Mexico in the 20th century (México en el siglo XX)
- `ancient-mexico` Ancient Mexico (México prehispánico) (3, region)
  - `mexica` The Mexica (Los mexicas)
  - `maya` The Maya (Los mayas)
  - `other-cultures` Olmecs, Teotihuacan and other cultures (Olmecas, teotihuacanos y otras culturas)
- `people` People of Mexico (Personajes de México) (2, general)
  - `scientists-and-inventors` Mexican scientists and inventors (Científicos, inventores y emprendedores)
  - `indigenous-peoples` Indigenous peoples of Mexico today (Pueblos indígenas de hoy)
- `food-and-drink` Mexican food and drink (Comida y bebida mexicana) (5, general)
  - `antojitos-and-street-food` Antojitos and street food (Antojitos y comida callejera)
  - `regional-dishes` Mexican regional dishes (Platillos y guisos regionales)
  - `sweets-and-bread` Mexican sweets and pan dulce (Dulces típicos y pan dulce)
  - `drinks` Mexican drinks (Bebidas mexicanas)
  - `ingredients` Chiles, corn and Mexican ingredients (Chiles, maíz y otros ingredientes)
- `festivals-and-traditions` Mexican festivals and traditions (Fiestas y tradiciones mexicanas) (6, general)
  - `day-of-the-dead` Day of the Dead (Día de Muertos)
  - `christmas-season` Posadas, Christmas and Reyes (Posadas, Navidad y Reyes)
  - `civic-holidays` Fiestas patrias and civic days (Fiestas patrias y días cívicos)
  - `regional-fiestas` Mexican fairs and regional fiestas (Ferias y fiestas regionales)
  - `crafts-and-dress` Mexican crafts and traditional dress (Artesanías y vestimenta tradicional)
  - `traditional-games` Mexican games and toys (Juegos y juguetes tradicionales)
- `myths-and-legends` Myths and legends of Mexico (Mitos y leyendas de México) (3, general)
  - `legends` Mexican legends and ghost stories (Leyendas y relatos de espantos)
  - `pre-hispanic-gods` Pre-Hispanic gods and myths (Dioses y mitos prehispánicos)
  - `folk-beliefs` Mexican beliefs and folk remedies (Creencias, remedios y supersticiones)
- `music-and-dance` Music and dance of Mexico (Música y baile de México) (5, general)
  - `mariachi-and-ranchera` Mariachi, ranchera and bolero (Mariachi, ranchera y bolero)
  - `regional-mexican` Banda, norteño and regional sounds (Banda, norteño y sones regionales)
  - `pop-and-rock` Mexican pop and rock (Pop y rock mexicano)
  - `traditional-dances` Mexican folk dances (Danzas y bailes tradicionales)
  - `childrens-songs` Cri-Cri and children''s songs (Cri-Cri y canciones infantiles)
- `art-and-literature` Art and literature of Mexico (Arte y literatura de México) (3, general)
  - `painters-and-muralists` Mexican painters and muralists (Pintores y muralistas)
  - `writers-and-poets` Mexican writers and poets (Escritores y poetas)
  - `comics` Mexican comics and cartoonists (Historietas y moneros)
- `film-and-television` Film and television of Mexico (Cine y televisión de México) (5, general)
  - `golden-age-cinema` Golden age of Mexican cinema (Época de Oro del cine mexicano)
  - `contemporary-cinema` Contemporary Mexican cinema (Cine mexicano contemporáneo)
  - `telenovelas` Mexican telenovelas (Telenovelas mexicanas)
  - `chespirito` Chespirito''s shows (El Chavo, el Chapulín y Chespirito)
  - `tv-shows-and-hosts` Mexican TV shows, hosts and youtubers (Programas, conductores e internet)
- `sports` Sport in Mexico (Deporte en México) (5, general)
  - `liga-mx` Liga MX and its clubs (Liga MX y sus clubes)
  - `national-team` Mexico national football team (La Selección Mexicana)
  - `lucha-libre` Lucha libre (Lucha libre)
  - `boxing` Mexican boxing (Box mexicano)
  - `other-sports` Mexican Olympians and other sports (Atletas olímpicos y otros deportes)
- `how-people-speak` How Mexico speaks (Así hablamos en México) (3, general)
  - `slang` Mexican slang and words (Modismos y palabras mexicanas)
  - `sayings` Mexican sayings and expressions (Dichos y refranes)
  - `indigenous-words` Nahuatl and indigenous languages (Náhuatl y lenguas indígenas)
- `daily-life` Daily life in Mexico (La vida diaria en México) (5, general)
  - `money` Mexican money and banknotes (Dinero, billetes y monedas)
  - `brands-and-snacks` Mexican brands and snacks (Marcas y botanas mexicanas)
  - `transport` Metro, buses and Mexican transport (Metro, camiones y transporte)
  - `school-and-services` Mexican school and public services (Escuela y servicios públicos)
  - `home-and-street` Life at home and on the street (Vida en la casa y en la calle)
- `symbols` Symbols of Mexico (Símbolos de México) (2, general)
  - `national-symbols` Mexican flag, coat of arms and anthem (Bandera, escudo e himno)
  - `state-symbols` Mexican demonyms, nicknames and state emblems (Gentilicios, apodos y escudos de los estados)', 'The new Mexican question pack needs its own list of topics, so its questions cover life in Mexico evenly. The proposal starts from the general topics every regional pack has, adds one for ancient Mexico, and splits them into 58 subtopics, about 34 questions each at 2000 questions. Applying it fixes the pack''s structure; the English and German topic names are drafted at that point.', 'Apply the proposal as it stands', NULL, '2026-10-16T21:35:56Z', '2026-10-16T21:38:32Z', 1280, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1280: mexico: 15 categories, 58 subcategories applied as proposed; app/data/bundles/mexico/categories.json (slugs) and names.{en,es,de}.json written; plans/22-bundles.md lists the taxonomy; engine tests now expect mexico among es defaults and skip packs without a pool file.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (305, 'Spot check tr-en-1 done?', 'answered', '["done: spot check finished", "not yet"]', 'Native speaker of English needed. Start `trivia-authoring` and open http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?batch=tr-en-1&locale=en&sample=1 (30 questions, source left, translation right). Extra checks (authoring/QC.md): faithful to the source, natural English, hints and wrong answers that work in English, difficulty fits the English-speaking market. Text in media is never a problem (decision 35: text in media is never a problem). Stale translation: don''t approve; question that only works in Spanish: mark "doesn''t travel". Agreement should be ≥ 90 %.', 'The first batch of questions translated into English needs a check by someone whose first language is English. They compare each translation with its original and judge whether it is faithful and sounds natural. Without that check the translation pilot cannot be judged.', 'done: spot check finished', NULL, '2026-10-16T21:49:55Z', '2026-10-16T22:28:42Z', 635, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1505: every tr-en-1 translation found good; with milestone 9 (developer 2026-10-16) no QC follows: task 635 (QC tr-en-1) and task 638 (pilot go/no-go en, de) dropped; tr-en-1''s numbers go to task 1506: Translation pilot numbers (QT-5); full runs need no ack');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (306, 'Spot check tr-de-1 done?', 'answered', '["done: spot check finished  (recommended)", "not yet"]', 'Native speaker of German needed. Start `trivia-authoring` and open http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?batch=tr-de-1&locale=de&sample=1 (30 questions, source left, translation right). Extra checks (authoring/QC.md): faithful to the source, natural German, hints and wrong answers that work in German, difficulty fits the German-speaking market. Text in media is never a problem (decision 35: text in media is never a problem). Stale translation: don''t approve; question that only works in its source language: mark "doesn''t travel". Agreement should be ≥ 90 %.', 'The first batch of questions translated into German needs a check by someone whose first language is German. They compare each translation with its original and judge whether it is faithful and sounds natural. Without that check the German translation pilot cannot be judged.', 'done: spot check finished  (recommended)', NULL, '2026-10-16T22:03:57Z', '2026-10-16T22:28:42Z', 637, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-16, task 1505: every tr-de-1 translation found good; with milestone 9 (developer 2026-10-16) no QC follows: task 637 (QC tr-de-1) and task 638 (pilot go/no-go en, de) dropped; tr-de-1''s numbers go to task 1506: Translation pilot numbers (QT-5); full runs need no ack');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (307, 'Remote Play lag measured? Picture and input delay per host and network', 'pending', '["measured (numbers per row)", "partly (which rows)", "not possible (why)"]', '**Answer only after `decision 303: Remote Play Together test setup ready? Switch on, beta build, two machines, second account` is answered «ready»** (decisions can''t wait on decisions).

Part of `plan 170: Timed mode over a Remote Play stream`. The probe (`--lag-probe`, `task 1485: Lag probe switch in the shell (--lag-probe)`) is a page with a running ms counter and a white flash every 2–5 s; any pad button or key press is logged with the ms since the last flash. It needs a `beta` upload containing it (`plan 89: Builds, depots and upload (SW-10, SW-6)`); that task doesn''t upload, and it may ride the same upload as `--rp-probe`.

Launch: Steam launch option `--lag-probe` (Linux: `%command% --lag-probe`). Log: `<userData>/lag-probe.log` (path shown on screen). Steam''s streaming overlay may show latency figures (unverified; recheck at the session): note them if so.

Checklist, per row of the matrix:
- [ ] `R_local`: 20 flashes, one person presses a pad at the host machine → median
- [ ] `R_remote`: 20 flashes, the same person presses a pad at the guest machine, watching the guest''s screen → median
- [ ] `V + I ≈ R_remote − R_local`
- [ ] Picture delay `V`: guest machine next to the host; 5 photos (a phone is enough) showing both counters → `V` = host''s counter − guest''s counter; `I ≈ (V + I) − V`
- [ ] Steam''s streaming overlay figures on the guest, if any

Matrix, as available:
- [ ] Windows host
- [ ] Linux (or Deck) host
- [ ] guest wired
- [ ] guest on Wi-Fi
- [ ] at least one internet row (guest on another network, e.g. a phone hotspot)

Report per row: `V`, `V + I`, spread, anything odd (stutter, dropped presses). Attach the log.', 'When friends far away play through Steam''s Remote Play, they see each question a little later than the person at the host computer, and their button presses also arrive a little later. In the timed mode, where everyone races to grab a question first, that delay could matter. A small test tool measures it on real sessions; this asks whether you have run those measurements.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-16T22:11:12Z', NULL, 1485, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (308, 'Spot check tr-es-ES-1 done?', 'answered', '["done: the spot check is recorded", "not yet"]', 'Native speaker of Spain''s Spanish needed. Open trivia-authoring and go to http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?batch=tr-es-ES-1&locale=es-ES&sample=1 (in ../trivia-review per the README). Extra checks (QC.md): faithful to the source, natural in Spain''s Spanish, hints and wrong answers that work, difficulty for the Spanish market. Text in media is never a problem (decision 35). Note: six questions (q-0514, q-0693, q-0725, q-0751, q-1697, q-1834) have an essential image with no file picked, a source-media issue.', 'The first batch of 50 questions translated into Spain''s Spanish needs a check by someone who speaks that variety natively. They read each translation next to its source and say whether it is faithful and sounds natural. The quality report that decides the next changes waits for this check.', 'no more spot check for translations; consider it good', NULL, '2026-10-16T22:15:09Z', '2026-10-16T23:15:33Z', 1222, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (309, 'Pad measurements on real hardware: how many pads, in which order, with which style?', 'pending', '["Done: results reported", "Skip: keep the defaults (bind by index, style from Gamepad.id)"]', 'Steps (about 15 min; real pads, as many as you have, ideally 2 different types, e.g. Xbox and PlayStation):
1. Linux or Windows, shell from the flake: `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1 trivia-desktop --rp-probe` (log `<userData>/rp-probe.log`; it logs Steam Input handles with type and pad index, and the page''s pads, every second).
2. Connect pads one by one up to 5 (or as many as you have). Note after each how many pads the log lists (expect max 4) and each pad''s `index`/`id`.
3. Unplug pad 1, then plug in a different pad, then replug pad 1. Report the indexes after each step.
4. Run it twice: with Steam running and Steam Input on for the game, then with Steam Input off (Properties > Controller > Disable Steam Input), and once on the Deck (built-in pad plus one external).
5. With one Xbox and one PlayStation pad under Steam Input: report the `type` of each handle and the `pad` index the log shows next to it, and which page index each physical pad has (press a button, see which index changes).
Report: the pad cap seen per OS, whether indexes behave as in plans/14-input.md section 3, whether handle `pad` equals the page `index` (yes/no, per case), and the Deck''s pads.', 'The game will let several people play with their own controllers at once, so we need to know how many controllers the game really sees and how it tells them apart. Reading the browser''s source tells us the limit and the rules, but only real controllers on Windows, under Steam and on the Steam Deck can confirm them. Your results decide whether each player''s button pictures can follow their own controller type or must stay shared. Nothing is blocked on this: the work proceeds with safe defaults.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-16T23:13:11Z', NULL, 1431, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (310, 'Pad measurements on real hardware: how many pads, in which order, with which style?', 'pending', '["Done: results reported", "Skip: keep the defaults (bind by index, style from Gamepad.id)"]', 'Steps (about 15 min; real pads, as many as you have, ideally 2 types, e.g. Xbox and PlayStation):
1. Dev shell: `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1 trivia-desktop --rp-probe` (log `<userData>/rp-probe.log`: Steam Input handles with type and pad index, and the page''s pads, every second).
2. Connect pads one by one up to 5 (or as many as you have). After each, note how many pads the log lists (expect max 4) and each pad''s `index` and `id`.
3. Unplug pad 1, plug in a different pad, then replug pad 1. Report the indexes after each step.
4. Repeat with Steam running and Steam Input on for the game, with Steam Input off (Properties > Controller > Disable Steam Input), and on the Deck (built-in pad plus one external), and on Windows.
5. With one Xbox and one PlayStation pad under Steam Input: report each handle''s `type` and `pad`, and which page index each physical pad has (press a button, see which index changes).
Report: pad cap per OS, whether indexes behave as in `plans/14-input.md` section 3, whether handle `pad` equals page `index` (per case), the Deck''s pads.', 'The game will let several people play with their own controllers at once, so we need to know how many controllers the game really sees and how it tells them apart. Reading the browser''s source tells us the limit and the rules, but only real controllers on Windows, under Steam and on the Steam Deck can confirm them. Your results decide whether each player''s button pictures can follow their own controller type or must stay shared. Nothing is blocked on this: the work proceeds with safe defaults.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-16T23:13:24Z', NULL, 1431, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (311, 'README: link to the Steam page', 'answered', '[]', '', 'The developer wants the README to point readers to the game on Steam as soon as the store page exists; until then no link.', 'Once the game''s Steam store page is public, README.md links to it', NULL, '2026-10-16T23:45:09Z', '2026-10-16T23:45:09Z', NULL, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (312, 'Bundle screen (flowing tiles) reviewed in /gallery?', 'answered', '["approved", "problems (listed in the answer)"]', 'Shots in work/gallery/<locale>/ (es, es-ES, en, de) at 1920x1080 and work/gallery/<locale>@1280x800/: bundles (base + Colombia both on), bundles-supply-report (short supply: report, start disabled), bundles-no-questions (no question for the choice: start disabled with the reason), choice-solo and choice-gamemaster (Choice with «Seguir», no bundle line or supply).
Changed since decision 264: flow Player → Choice → Bundles → Level; narrow base column with toggle tiles and a vertical ruler; flowing fixed-width tiles for optional bundles; clear focus and selected states; counts «5000+» / «2000+»; any combination (base may be off), start check with a reason; supply report on Bundles.
Not shown: the gallery cannot load a mods folder, so no shot with ~15 fake mod bundles (scroll, fade, focus follow) and none for base off / nothing selected by clicking (the no-questions shot uses a save with every question blocked). Check those in the dev server if wanted.
Manifest: only the intended PLACEHOLDER(1465..1467) texts of unbuilt modes are unmatched.', 'The screen where the family picks which question bundles to play has been rebuilt: a narrow column for the base bundle, a divider, and tiles for the optional bundles that flow to fit the screen. Any combination of bundles is now allowed, and the game can only start when the chosen bundles hold questions. Please look at the new screenshots and say whether the screen is right or what still needs work.', 'problems: selected bundle tiles: the solid cyan fill is too different; use the existing selected look (dark tile, outline + tint, as on Choice); everything else approved', NULL, '2026-10-17T00:04:16Z', '2026-10-17T03:56:43Z', 1340, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-17, task 1340: selected tiles on the Bundles screen use the Choice look (dark tile, sky outline + tint, check mark in sky): the solid sky fill and ink text are gone from BundleSelector.svelte (large mode); plans/04-ui-tv-display.md updated. Reshot es, es-ES, en, de at 1920x1080 and 1280x800 (bundles, bundles-supply-report, choice-solo, choice-gamemaster); 0 unmatched. The gallery''s en ''supply'' step timed out in both runs (not part of these shots).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (313, 'Pilot translation run no longer stops the next run', 'answered', '[]', 'Partly supersedes decision 45: only the clause that the pilot always stops the next run until qgen health ack. Thresholds and selection order stay. Reason: milestone 9 (developer, 2026-10-16): the LLM translation review is a translation''s only review; the tr-en-1 and tr-de-1 spot checks found every translation good. Also: the run report offers an optional review link instead of a native-speaker spot check, and the home page no longer offers a sample link on translation runs.', 'Translated questions are first tried on a small batch of 50. Until now the next translation run waited for the developer to look at that batch and give a go. Translations are now checked by the automatic reviewer alone, so the batch no longer holds anything up; only a run that fails the quality limits still stops.', 'The pilot tr-<locale>-1 no longer stops the next run; only a run failing a health threshold does, until qgen health ack', NULL, '2026-10-17T02:46:43Z', '2026-10-17T02:46:43Z', 1508, NULL, 'rule', 1508, '2026-10-17, task 1508: 2026-10-16, task 1508: health.translate_stop_reason drops the pilot clause; tr-en-1 still stops the next en run because it fails the audit/review agreement threshold, not as a pilot.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (314, 'Multiplayer screens reviewed in /gallery?', 'answered', '["reviewed, mode names as proposed", "flags in /gallery, fix task follows"]', 'How to review: run `trivia-authoring`, open `/gallery`, pick each language and both sizes (1920×1080 and 1280×800), and flag any string that reads wrong, clips or doesn''t fit. The 31 multiplayer shots: choice-multiplayer, join-empty, join-name-picker, join-5, greeting-session, join-8, join-keyboard-timed, join-age-groups, bundles-session, start-resume-session, menu-session, level-rr-coop, select-rr-coop, correct-rr-coop, wrong-rr-coop, victory-rr-coop, level-rr-competitive, wrong-rr-competitive, victory-rr-competitive, victory-last-standing, timed-question, timed-claimed, timed-claim-last, timed-paused, timed-time-up, timed-round, timed-last-heart, timed-all-at-risk, timed-nobody-wins, timed-sudden-death, victory-timed.

Mode names per locale (es-ES has no override and uses es). 15a «Mode names» still lists them as proposals.
- Round-robin co-op: es «Por turnos en equipo», en «Round-robin co-op», de «Reihum im Team»
- Round-robin competitive: es «Por turnos, todos contra todos», en «Round-robin competitive», de «Reihum gegeneinander»
- Competitive (timed): es «Contrarreloj», en «Competitive (timed)», de «Auf Zeit»

The gallery shows the unbuilt modes with PLACEHOLDER marks (decision 293: Unbuilt multiplayer modes: on the mode row in dev mode only).', 'The new local multiplayer screens (joining, the three game modes, the timed round with its hearts and countdowns) are now photographed in all four languages at two screen sizes. The developer has to look at them and say whether the wording and the mode names read well, or flag the strings that don''t. If everything is fine the work is done; if there are flags, a follow-up pass fixes them.', 'flags: start, menu, join-*, timed-*, victory-* approved; mode names as proposed. Mode selection leaves Choice, becomes its own screens: (1) «Solo o en grupo» or «Multijugador»; (2a) single: standard or Gamemaster mode; (2b) multiplayer: collaborative (round-robin co-op) and competitive (round-robin competitive, timed) as visually separated groups, one pick; (3) age group on its own screen: one per game, except round-robin competitive: one per player (so after the join screen); then Bundles → Level. «Personalizar partida» on the age screen. Selected state everywhere: the existing tile look (outline + tint). Iterate via review decisions in one task.', NULL, '2026-10-17T02:48:33Z', '2026-10-17T03:56:43Z', 1462, NULL, 'once', NULL, '2026-10-17, task 1463: built as screens mode-kind, mode-single, mode-multi and a separate age screen; names final in plans/15a-ui-translation.md ''Mode names''; plans/13-game-modes.md updated.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (315, 'Ship Round-robin co-op: WIN_RR_COOP in Steamworks and store texts', 'pending', '[]', 'Readiness (throw-away run, dev server): the mode played from join screen to victory with 2 fake pads and with keyboard only (two seats sharing keyboard and mouse); both won at level 12. The mode needs no keyboard with pads only, so the controller line stays ''Partial'' (decision 90).
Steps:
1. After decision 140 (or together with it): Steamworks → Stats & Achievements → new achievement with API name WIN_RR_COOP, Hidden no, Set by Client, no stat.
2. English name and description from the WIN_RR_COOP row in plans/18-steam-integration.md (''Achievements in Steamworks''); per-language names and descriptions (latam, spanish, english, german) typed in or via the localization upload.
3. Icons app/desktop/achievements/png/WIN_RR_COOP_achieved.png and WIN_RR_COOP_unachieved.png (render.sh). Publish.
4. Read the store text draft in plans/17a-store-page.md (en, es, es-ES, de: ''Ways to play'' bullet, Features bullet); wording changes go in your answer.
5. Answer with the token Steamworks gave the achievement (NEW_ACHIEVEMENT_1_<n>, from its localization download).', 'Round-robin co-op, where the family takes turns answering and plays together against the game, is finished and checked, and can now be offered to players. Doing so needs its win achievement set up on Steam''s side and the store page to mention the mode. This asks you to do the Steam setup and to read the drafted store wording; once answered, the mode is switched on for the next build.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17T03:05:47Z', NULL, 1465, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (316, 'Ship Round-robin competitive: WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE in Steamworks and store texts', 'pending', '[]', 'Readiness (throw-away run, dev server): the mode played from the join screen with 2 fake pads through level, wrong answer, knocked out, winner (last standing and first to level 12); keyboard only (two seats on keyboard and mouse): join, start, first question, wrong answer knocks the seat out. Engine session tests pass. The mode needs no keyboard with pads only, so the controller line stays ''Partial'' (decision 90).
Steps:
1. After decision 140 (or together with it): Steamworks → Stats & Achievements → new achievement with API name WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE, Hidden no, Set by Client, no stat.
2. English name and description from the WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE row in plans/18-steam-integration.md (''Achievements in Steamworks''); per-language names and descriptions (latam, spanish, english, german) typed in or via the localization upload.
3. Icons app/desktop/achievements/png/WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE_achieved.png and WIN_RR_COMPETITIVE_unachieved.png (render.sh). Publish.
4. Read the store text draft in plans/17a-store-page.md (en, es, es-ES, de: ''Ways to play'' bullet, Features bullet); wording changes go in your answer.
5. Answer with the token Steamworks gave the achievement (NEW_ACHIEVEMENT_1_<n>, from its localization download).', 'Round-robin competitive, where everyone takes turns but plays their own separate game with their own jokers and age group, is finished and checked, and can now be offered to players. Doing so needs its win achievement set up on Steam''s side and the store page to mention the mode. This asks you to do the Steam setup and to read the drafted store wording; once answered, the mode is switched on for the next build.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17T03:11:03Z', NULL, 1466, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (317, 'DLC store texts approved? (usa)', 'pending', '["Approved as drafted", "Approved with changes (say which)"]', 'Text: plans/17a-store-page.md, Free DLC, section usa (English only). Capsules: authoring/store/out/capsules/dlc-usa/en/ (render with the other DLC capsules). No Steam achievement is mentioned (none exists for usa).', 'The free United States question bundle needs its own store page text and capsule art before it can be entered on Steam. The English name, short description and long description are drafted in the store-page plan, and the capsules render from the bundle''s name. Approving lets the text be entered when the bundle''s English questions ship; changes are applied first.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17T03:32:03Z', NULL, 1417, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (318, 'DLC store texts approved? (germany)', 'pending', '["Approved as drafted", "Approved with changes (say which)"]', 'Text: plans/17a-store-page.md, Free DLC, section germany (de, en). Capsules: authoring/store/out/capsules/dlc-germany/de/ (en capsules added with the en text). No Steam achievement is mentioned.', 'The free Germany question bundle needs its own store page text before it can be entered on Steam. German and English versions of the name, short description and long description are drafted; the English one is only entered once the bundle has English translations. Approving lets the text be entered when the bundle''s questions ship; changes are applied first.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17T03:32:36Z', NULL, 1443, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (319, 'DLC store texts approved? (uk)', 'pending', '["Approved as drafted", "Approved with changes (say which)"]', 'Text: plans/17a-store-page.md, Free DLC, section uk (English only). Capsules: authoring/store/out/capsules/dlc-uk/en/. No Steam achievement is mentioned.', 'The free United Kingdom question bundle needs its own store page text before it can be entered on Steam. The English name, short description and long description are drafted in British English. Approving lets the text be entered when the bundle''s questions ship; changes are applied first.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17T03:32:56Z', NULL, 1456, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (320, 'Multiplayer smoke run: the engine plays a session''s middle on the save, the screens its start and end', 'answered', '[]', 'Like the solo smoke''s card swap (it also writes the save and reloads). Timed can''t be edited under a running page (the round screen''s countdown writes the save), so its fast-forward rides the quit and restart that checks decision 289''s rebind. ~10 min for the nine sessions on 2026-10-16. Keyboard-only round-robin seats share the keyboard (decision 273): no seat there may not act, so those two sessions have no refused press; keyboard-only timed seats'' answer keys act for the claimer (decision 290), so only another seat''s claim key is refused there.', 'The release check plays every local multiplayer mode with simulated controllers before each upload. Playing every one of the twelve levels on screen for all nine setups would make that check take most of an hour, so the start and the end of each session go through the real screens and the middle is played directly by the game''s rules on the saved game. The check stays short enough to run every time while still covering every screen, control and ending.', 'Each session: Choice, Join, Bundles and the first turns or claims on screen with fake pads and real key and mouse events; then the engine plays on to the session''s last level on the save (reload, or for the timed pads session quit and restart); the end on screen', NULL, '2026-10-17T04:15:53Z', '2026-10-17T04:15:53Z', 1473, NULL, 'rule', 1473, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (321, 'Local multiplayer: each seat''s device kind lives in the save', 'answered', '[]', 'Simpler than a keyboard take-over dialog plus a Join-style key re-pick, and the keys of timed key seats survive without asking again. Refines decision 277: Multiplayer sessions in the save: one games[] row per session, with seats (the binding itself stays device-agnostic by index; only the kind is saved). task 1517, plan 172.', 'In a local multiplayer game each player is tied to a controller, the keyboard and mouse, or a single key. That tie used to live only in the running window, so after the game was closed and reopened nobody could take a keyboard player''s place and the game got stuck. The choice was between keeping the kind of controller with the saved game or letting the keyboard re-claim seats by hand after a restart; the game now keeps it with the save, so keyboard players carry on at once.', 'The save''s session row keeps each seat''s device kind: seats[].device = "pad" | "kbm" | "shared" | { key } (no pad index, pad numbering changes across restarts), sent with the session''s new action. After a restart (no sessionStorage binding) keyboard seats are bound from it at once; pad seats stay unbound and wait for a pad (decision 289); only a pad seat can be lost. Optional field, no SAVE_VERSION bump: sessions saved without it keep the old behaviour (every seat asks for a pad).', NULL, '2026-10-17T04:24:39Z', '2026-10-17T04:24:39Z', 1517, NULL, 'rule', 1517, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (322, 'Task 1514 left unstaged changes after `pm task done`: investigate', 'answered', '[]', 'Run 1531 of task 1514 closed the task but left 1 file unstaged. pm committed them on the branch `pm/task-1514-run-1531-left` and cleaned the tree.

     M authoring/reports/batches.md

Look: `git show pm/task-1514-run-1531-left`. Keep: `git merge pm/task-1514-run-1531-left`. Then `git branch -D pm/task-1514-run-1531-left`.', 'A piece of automated work finished but left changes behind that it didn''t hand in. They were set aside, nothing is lost. Decide whether to keep them or throw them away.', 'Discard: out-of-date batches.md, batch-9 column already on main; replaced by a fresh qgen batch-report commit, branch deleted', NULL, '2026-10-17T04:30:36Z', '2026-10-17T14:12:25Z', NULL, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (323, 'Spot check batch-9 done?', 'answered', '["done"]', 'Blind spot check of batch-9 (first English `base` batch, `decision 234: Spot-check size for batch-9 and batch-10 (first English batches)?`).
- Size: 30 questions (`quality.spot_check_size`), checked in English.
- Start `trivia-authoring` (in `../trivia-review`, per AGENTS.md), open http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?batch=batch-9&sample=1
- Mark the problem kinds in the feedback box; answer "done" when finished.
- Batch report: `authoring/reports/batch-9.md` (874 approved, 77 needs work of 951).', 'A new batch of trivia questions, the first written in English, has been produced and checked by an automated reviewer. To learn whether that reviewer judges like a person, a small random sample has to be checked blind by the developer. The answer "done" lets the quality report be written and the next steps follow.', 'done: 30/30 approved; q-2301 approved over the LLM''s style concern (a.m./p.m. doesn''t travel), q-2441 kept needs_work for its pd-us-only picture', NULL, '2026-10-17T04:30:46Z', '2026-10-17T05:33:59Z', 1186, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (324, 'Regional bundle usa: start before colombia''s first batch QC?', 'answered', '["wait: start usa after colombia''s first batch QC is done (the plan''s rule)", "start usa now: add its first drafting pair without colombia''s numbers"]', 'Plan 84 chain 5 needs `task 1296: QC batch-12 (colombia)` done, with the first effort numbers in `plans/15c-regional-questions.md`. Today `task 1295: run colombia batch (batch-<n>)` hasn''t run, so `task 1296: QC batch-12 (colombia)` can''t be done. Plan 98''s `usa` tasks (`task 1276: Set up regional bundle usa`, taxonomy decision 287) are done.', 'The American-English question pack is set up and ready to start writing questions. The plan says to wait until the Colombian pilot has produced and reviewed its first batch, so its cost and review effort are known. That batch hasn''t run yet, and nothing else is holding it back except queue order.', 'Start now: task 1296: QC batch-12 (colombia) is done (2026-10-23, $0.28 per approved), the plan''s condition is met', NULL, '2026-10-17T04:32:36Z', '2026-10-29T03:44:59Z', 1268, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (325, 'Regional bundle spain: start before colombia''s first batch QC?', 'pending', '["wait: start spain after colombia''s first batch QC is done (the plan''s rule)", "start spain''s first drafting pair now"]', 'Plan 84 chain 5 needs `task 1296: QC batch-12 (colombia)` done, with the first effort numbers in `plans/15c-regional-questions.md`. Today `task 1295: run colombia batch (batch-<n>)` hasn''t run, so task 1296 can''t be done. Plan 98''s `spain` tasks (`task 1279: Set up regional bundle spain`, taxonomy decision 300) are done. Same question as decision 324 for `usa`.', 'The Spain-Spanish question pack is set up and ready to start writing questions. The plan says to wait until the Colombian pilot has produced and reviewed its first batch, so its cost and review effort are known. That batch hasn''t run yet, and nothing else is holding it back except queue order.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17T04:33:49Z', NULL, 1271, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (326, 'Regional bundle mexico: start before colombia''s first batch QC?', 'pending', '["wait: start mexico after colombia''s first batch QC is done (the plan''s rule)", "start mexico now: add its first drafting pair without colombia''s numbers"]', 'Plan 84 chain 5 needs `task 1296: QC batch-12 (colombia)` done, with the first effort numbers in `plans/15c-regional-questions.md`. Today `task 1295: run colombia batch (batch-<n>)` hasn''t run, so task 1296 can''t be done. Plan 98''s `mexico` tasks (`task 1280: Set up regional bundle mexico`, taxonomy decision 304) are done. Same question as decisions 324 and 325.', 'The Mexican-Spanish question pack is set up and ready to start writing questions. The plan says to wait until the Colombian pilot has produced and reviewed its first batch, so its cost and review effort are known. That batch hasn''t run yet, and nothing else is holding it back except queue order.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17T04:34:07Z', NULL, 1272, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (327, 'batch-9: health stop, ack?', 'answered', '["Ack batch-9 (qgen health ack batch-9 \"<note>\"), then rerun", "Do not ack; drop the run"]', 'colombia run (task 1295), exit 2, again after decision 257''s ack. Output:

batch-9 fails the batch health thresholds: drop rate, overlap rate, top clue.
See `qgen report --batches` or authoring/reports/batches.md. The developer looks at it and clears the stop with: qgen health ack batch-9 "<note>"

claude: no call made (stopped before any step).', 'A run of new trivia questions stopped itself because the previous batch scored badly on the quality checks: too many questions dropped, too much overlap with existing ones, and one clue used too often. Only the developer can clear that stop. Until they do, no further batch can start.', 'Ack batch-9 (qgen health ack batch-9 "<note>"), then rerun', NULL, '2026-10-17T04:34:29Z', '2026-10-17T05:34:58Z', 1295, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (328, 'Bundle screen (selected look) reviewed in /gallery?', 'answered', '["approved", "problems (listed in the answer)"]', 'Shots: bundles, bundles-supply-report, choice-solo, choice-gamemaster, all four languages, at 1920x1080 and 1280x800. Changed since the last review: selected bundle tiles now use the same look as on the Choice screen (dark tile, light-blue outline and tint, small check mark) instead of a solid light-blue fill. Unchanged: flow, narrow base column with toggle tiles, ruler, flowing tiles, counts, any combination with the start check. The gallery cannot load a folder of fake mod bundles or set ''nothing selected'', so those cases were not shot.', 'The screen where players choose which question bundles to play was changed so that a chosen bundle looks like a chosen option on the earlier screen, rather than a bright solid block. Please look at the new screenshots and say whether the screen is good now.', 'approved', NULL, '2026-10-17T07:14:35Z', '2026-10-17T18:26:45Z', 1340, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-17, task 1340: Approved as is: no change. The Bundles screen with the Choice-style selected look (decision 312) is final; plan 151''s review loop is closed. Gallery flag 16 on choice-gamemaster was already marked fixed (2026-10-16).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (329, 'Mode and age screens reviewed in /gallery?', 'answered', '["approved", "changes (listed in the answer)"]', 'Shots (work/gallery/<locale>[@1280x800]/, es, es-ES, en, de at 1920x1080 and 1280x800): mode-kind (step 1), mode-single (standard / gamemaster), mode-multi (collaborative and competitive groups, PLACEHOLDER marks only in dev mode), choice-solo and choice-gamemaster (age screen), choice-rr-competitive (one age line per player), join-5 / join-8 (no age steppers any more), bundles, bundles-session.
Changes since decision 314: new Mode screen (two steps, selected tile = outline + tint, a pick then «Seguir»); Choice lost its mode row; rr-competitive age lines moved from the Join screen to the age screen; flow Player → Mode → (Join) → Age → Bundles → Level; new strings: kindTitle, title, soloKind, multi, multiAbout, multiKey, standard, collab, versus (the standard mode is now named «Estándar» / Standard, the single-player step keeps «Solo o en grupo»). Gallery, smoke, store screenshots follow the new flow.', 'Choosing how to play has been split into separate screens: first «Solo o en grupo» or «Multijugador», then the mode itself, then the age group on its own screen (one per player in the all-against-all turn mode). Please look at the new screens in all four languages and say whether the design is right or what should change.', 'changes: en mode names and descriptions on mode-multi, ui-flags.json flags 22–29 (flag 25 dropped, superseded by 26); es, es-ES, de follow the same meaning where they share the problem; rest approved', NULL, '2026-10-17T07:43:59Z', '2026-10-17T18:25:54Z', 1463, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (330, 'Local multiplayer: each mode played on the TV with the family?', 'pending', '["passed", "failed (list: mode, setup, screen, what happened)"]', 'Task 1473 (headless `smoke.mjs --multiplayer`, 9 sessions on fake pads) is green; this is the by-hand check with real pads. Workers never play for you.

## Setup (answer says which)
- Modes are not in `BUILT_MODES` (`app/client/src/engine/game.ts`: only `gamemaster`, `solo`), so the Steam `beta` can''t have them yet. Use the dev build (decision 293): `TRIVIA_DEV_STEAM_USER=1 TRIVIA_SOUND=1 trivia-desktop` (mode row shows the multiplayer modes as PLACEHOLDER).
- Media synced first: `trivia-media sync --status approved`.
- If plan 166 has shipped the modes and a `beta` is uploaded by the time you play: use that under Steam (Steam Input as players have it) and say so.

## Rows (each start to finish: Choice → mode row → Join → setup → Bundles → game → end)
Per mode (`rr-coop`, `rr-competitive`, `timed`):
1. pads only (as many as you have, note the count)
2. keyboard only (no pads): rr-*: seats share keyboard and mouse; timed: each player picks a claim key on Join; the claimer answers by mouse click or A–D/1–4 (decision 275)
3. every pad you own + keyboard and mouse (4 pads + kbm = 5 seats; note the count and whether a 5th pad is listed, task 1431''s finding)

## Also check
- Prompts follow the last input; each pad''s glyphs show on its turn
- A pad unplugged and replugged mid-session: «Mando de … desconectado» dialog, A on a pad takes the seat back (decision 289)
- Esc menu from any seat (decision 288); in timed it pauses the clock
- Timed: pulsing heart at a last chance, last-3-s ticks and red frame after a claim, red frame when everyone is at risk, sudden death in round 12, all with sound; claim: LB/RB on pads, Space or click for keyboard and mouse
- Text fits on the TV

## Answer format
Date, build (dev or beta), ✓/✗ per row (9 rows) with a note. "passed" or "failed (list: mode, setup, screen, what happened)".

Passed: decision 284''s C row gets a note. Failed: follow-up fixes are routed per area, then the playtest is raised again.', 'Three new ways to play together in one room are built: taking turns as a team, taking turns against each other, and a timed race where anyone can grab a question. Automated tests have run them with fake controllers, but only you can tell whether they work and feel right on the TV with real controllers and the family. If you say passed, this step of the project is closed; if not, the problems you list are fixed and the check is repeated.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17T07:44:27Z', NULL, 1474, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (331, 'Task 1523 left unstaged changes after `pm task done`: investigate', 'answered', '[]', 'Run 1569 of task 1523 closed the task but left 1 file unstaged. pm committed them on the branch `pm/task-1523-run-1569-left` and cleaned the tree.

