INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (334, 'batch-10: health stop, ack?', 'answered', '["Ack batch-10 (qgen health ack batch-10 \"<note>\"), then rerun", "Investigate batch-10 first"]', 'Task 1295 (`qgen batch --bundle colombia`) exit 2, output verbatim:

batch-10 fails the batch health thresholds: drop rate, overlap rate, top clue.
See `qgen report --batches` or authoring/reports/batches.md. The developer looks at it and clears the stop with: qgen health ack batch-10 "<note>"

No claude: line printed (no claude call made). Nothing staged.', 'A run of the question generator refused to start because the previous batch of questions fell below the quality thresholds for dropped drafts, overlap with existing questions and top clue. Only the developer can clear that stop. Choose whether to accept that batch as it is and let the next run proceed, or to look into it first.', 'Ack batch-10 (qgen health ack batch-10 "<note>"), then rerun', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:17:09Z', '2026-10-17T15:33:51Z', 1295, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (335, 'Playable demo: a build variant of the same code, switched at build time', 'answered', '[]', 'Masterplan of milestone 18: Playable demo (task 1367). A runtime toggle would need hiding from players; a fork would drift. The code is public, so the flag is no protection (decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy).', 'The free demo of the game is made from the same program as the full game, with a switch set when the game is packaged, rather than a separate program or a mode players can turn on. That way every feature and fix reaches both at once, and nobody can turn the full game into the demo or back from a menu.', 'One codebase; a build-time demo flag (Vite define for the client, a build argument for the desktop shell; a dev env switch for the dev server and trivia-desktop) decides demo vs. full; the engine takes ''demo'' as an input (no global), so tests run both; no runtime toggle for players', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:20:22Z', '2026-10-17T13:20:22Z', 1367, NULL, 'rule', 1367, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (336, 'Demo save: separate from the full game''s, or shared/imported on purchase?', 'answered', '["Separate: own userData <appData>/trivia-demo (save, mods.json, telemetry), no carry-over to the full game", "Separate, and the full game offers a one-time import of the demo save on its first start", "Shared: the demo uses the full game''s <appData>/trivia save"]', 'Part 1 of `plan 154: masterplan` (milestone 18: Playable demo). Today the packaged shell fixes `userData` at `<appData>/trivia` (`app/desktop/main.mjs`, `decision 223: Build names after PUB-7: productName «Living Room Trivia», space-free exe and artefact names`); save, `mods.json`, telemetry `install.json` all live there. The demo is its own Steam app (own App ID), so Steam Cloud already keeps its files apart.

- Separate: demo `userData` `<appData>/trivia-demo`; demo plays never touch the family''s seen counts; the full game starts fresh. Demo questions are base questions, so the full game may serve them again (they were seen in the demo).
- Import on purchase: as separate, plus the full game''s first start finds `<appData>/trivia-demo/save` and offers one import (the existing `--import-save` path); the full game then avoids the demo''s ~200 seen questions. Extra work: detection, a dialog in four locales, save version checks.
- Shared: the demo writes `<appData>/trivia` itself; demo plays (fixed, seen counts disregarded) still bump the family''s counts; both apps'' Steam Cloud would fight over one folder.', 'The free demo keeps a save file like the full game: which questions the family has seen, achievements, settings. It can keep its own save in its own folder, untouched by and not touching the full game''s, or the full game can offer to take it over once it is bought, or both can share one save. The answer decides where the demo writes and whether buying the game carries the demo''s progress over.', 'Shared: the demo uses the full game''s <appData>/trivia save', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:23:35Z', '2026-10-17T14:07:02Z', 1525, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-17, task 1538: no code change. Demo and full game share <appData>/trivia (packaged) and state/desktop/ (dev): main.mjs''s fixed userData path is not demo-aware, so save, mods.json, telemetry and the single-instance lock are shared (a second launch of either focuses the running window). No separate demo paths, no import task. Comment in main.mjs.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (337, 'Steam features in the demo: Cloud, achievements, Workshop/mods, telemetry, question reports', 'answered', '["Cloud on, question reports on, telemetry on with demo games marked, mods and Workshop off, achievements only if Valve allows them for demos (off until part 6''s reading)", "Minimal: Cloud on, everything else off", "Everything as in the full game, mods and Workshop included"]', 'Part 1 of `plan 154: masterplan` (milestone 18: Playable demo). Nothing is enforced hard (`decision 111: Steam only: no effort outside Steam; Steam features are the reason to buy`); "off" means the demo build skips the feature and hides its screen. Answer with one option or a mix per feature.

Per feature, what changes:
- Steam Cloud: set up in Steamworks for the demo''s App ID (`plan 130: Steamworks app configuration (SW-7)`); no code change.
- Achievements: on → `app/desktop/steam-achievements.vdf` uploaded to the demo app too; off → the shell skips unlock calls in the demo. Valve''s demo rules are read by part 6 (task 1530: write plan: Steamworks demo app and store); recommended: as Valve allows, off until that reading says yes.
- Workshop/mods: off → no mod scan, no `/mods.js` overlay, no Workshop, mods screen hidden; mod bundles would also break "only the demo bundle".
- Telemetry (opt-in, `decision 119: Telemetry recording: derived from the save into a per-install side file`): on → sessions carry a demo mark, `qgen telemetry` keeps them out of calibration (part 3); report server accepts the mark.
- Question reports (`decision 93: Question reports: where do players send them?`): on → the report server validates tickets of the demo App ID too (`report-server/wrangler.toml` `STEAM_APP_ID` is one id today).', 'The full game uses several Steam features: cloud saves, achievements, player-made question packs (mods and the Workshop), opt-in play statistics and reporting a wrong question. For the free demo each can be kept or switched off; Valve also limits what a demo app may have. The answer decides which of these the demo shows and which code paths the demo build turns off.', 'Minimal: Cloud on, everything else off', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:23:35Z', '2026-10-17T14:06:51Z', 1525, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-18, task 1562: Demo build ships no modding/ (electron-builder.yml modding filter via TRIVIA_MODDING_FILTER, ''!**/*'' in the demo scripts); trivia-release-check --demo has no modkit/mods steps and no report, telemetry, workshop rows, and adds the manual row cloud (demo App ID); full build and check unchanged.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (338, 'Demo flag: TRIVIA_DEMO at build, dist-demo, package.json demo, EngineData.demo', 'answered', '[]', 'Follows decision 335: Playable demo: a build variant of the same code, switched at build time. One env name everywhere (dev server, vite preview, trivia-desktop, trivia-gallery). A separate outDir keeps a demo dev build from replacing the full dist/ the shell, gallery and builds read. package.json mirrors reportUrl''s existing read. EngineData (built once per pool) is the loaded data the engine already takes; Io stays per action.', 'The demo and the full game are built from the same program; this settles how the program knows which one it is. The switch is set when the game is built or started for testing, kept apart in its own build folder so the two can''t mix, and handed to the game''s rules as plain input so both variants can be tested side by side.', 'Client: TRIVIA_DEMO=1 at vite build/dev time → define __DEMO__, outDir app/client/dist-demo (full dist/ untouched), buildInfo().demo; engine: EngineData.demo set by engineData()''s caller (lib/data.ts from buildInfo().demo), never a global. Shell: package.json "demo": true (electron-builder extraMetadata of app/desktop/electron-builder.demo.yml) packaged, TRIVIA_DEMO=1 unpackaged; demo shell loads dist-demo and refuses to start without it. No runtime toggle.', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:23:41Z', '2026-10-17T13:23:41Z', 1525, NULL, 'rule', 1525, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (339, 'Demo bundle format: an id list of base questions, exported to app/data/demo/ pools, questions stay in base', 'answered', '[]', 'Follows plan 154 part 2 (format left to this plan) and decision 338: Demo flag: TRIVIA_DEMO at build, dist-demo, package.json demo, EngineData.demo. An own bundle id demo (kind base) would make every subKey demo/<slug> (decision 259: Category and subcategory keys: English slugs), needing a copied categories.json and names files, and would split Cambiazo''s categories, old-keys mapping and telemetry per subcategory from base''s; copies (as decision 217 did for chinese-base) would also break ''exactly one bundle'' and seen counts by id. The list lives in authoring/data/ because app/ never reads it: the game needs only the exported pools (app/ never reads authoring/data/). app/data/demo/ mirrors bundles/<id>/ (D-43), so part 4 ships it instead of base''s pools.', 'The free demo plays a fixed selection of roughly a few hundred questions taken from the full game''s main question set. This settles how that selection is stored and shipped: as a plain list of question numbers kept with the authoring tools, from which the export writes the demo''s own small question files, while the questions themselves stay where they are in the main set. The alternative, a separate question pack with its own categories, would duplicate the category setup and break features that work by category.', 'List: authoring/data/demo.json {version: 1, ids: [...] sorted, approved: <decision id>} of approved base question ids, picked by qgen demo, approved by the developer. Export: qgen export writes app/data/demo/pool.json (es) and pool.<locale>.json (es-ES, en, de): base''s pool entries of the listed ids, unchanged (bundle base, base subcategories, same ids). No bundle id demo, no bundles.json entry, no own taxonomy: in a demo build the engine loads app/data/demo/ in place of base''s pools and no packs; the base bundle''s tile shows the demo''s name and count (part 5). Every question stays in exactly one bundle (base); the demo is a subset of base, not a bundle. qgen validate checks the list and flags stale demo pools.', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:28:15Z', '2026-10-17T13:28:15Z', 1526, NULL, 'rule', 1526, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (340, 'Demo selection: every shuffle seeded from its site and the items it shuffles', 'answered', '[]', 'The candidates of every rng site (draw, pick, replacement, swap_in, timed rounds) already follow from the game''s inputs (mode, age group, bundles, seats, level, offered and purged questions, blocked), so keying the shuffle by them is a function of the game state, as plan 154 part 3 asks, without threading mode, seats and an action count to each site. Order-independent: joker availability trials and undo can''t shift later draws. Same question → same answer order each time it shows, which a fixed demo wants.', 'In the free demo every play-through must get the same questions in the same order, on every computer. The game normally shuffles with fresh randomness; in the demo each shuffle instead derives its order from what it is shuffling, so the same situation always gives the same result without passing extra game details around.', 'In the demo (EngineData.demo) the action''s Io.rng is demoRng() (engine/rng.ts): each shuffle seeds mulberry32 from a hash of a fixed salt, the site label and the shuffled items'' keys (a PoolQuestion''s id, a string itself), then Fisher–Yates; no call counter, no time, game id or randomSeed(). The full game keeps seededRng(randomSeed()). The choice is one engine function actionRng(data) that lib/engine.ts io() calls.', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:31:05Z', '2026-10-17T13:31:05Z', 1527, NULL, 'rule', 1527, '2026-10-17, task 1527: written into plan 175: Deterministic selection in the demo (Rng sites, task 1).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (341, 'Demo bundle tile: its name and question count', 'answered', '[]', 'decision 267''s fixed «5000+» is a target promise the demo can''t keep; decision 339 gives the demo no bundles.json entry, so its name comes from the catalogs; the rounding rule already exists for small bundles (countShown), reused rather than a new rule; toggling stays as plan 151 made every tile, nothing special-cased.', 'The free demo holds only a few hundred questions, so the general set''s tile cannot promise «5000+» as the full game does. This settles what the one tile on the demo''s bundle screen is called and which number it shows.', 'In a demo build the base bundle''s tile (large and compact selector) shows a demo name from the UI catalogs (bundles.demoName, all four locales, style guides first) and its own count from the loaded demo pool of the UI language, rounded down like a mod bundle''s under decision 267 (≥ 100 to the hundred, ≥ 10 to the ten, «+» when rounded), no cap; the tile still toggles like every tile (plan 151), off → the start reason.', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:33:05Z', '2026-10-17T13:33:05Z', 1528, NULL, 'rule', 1528, '2026-10-17, task 1528: written into plan 176: Demo on screen (Bundle screen, task 2).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (342, 'Demo packaging: own staging folders, three depots, own reports, no nix output', 'answered', '[]', 'Separate folders let the full and demo builds sit side by side so trivia-steam stage checks each against its own archives; one media layout and three depots keep steam.py''s code paths shared (decision 84: SteamCMD source and depot split for Steam uploads); the demo ships the base game''s code, so one tag covers both.', 'The free demo is packaged from the same code as the full game but must not mix its files with the full game''s when both are built on the same machine. This settles where the demo''s build pieces go, how it is split for Steam''s download system, where its checks report, and that it gets no separate package for the project''s own build tool.', 'Demo media staged into app/desktop/build/media-demo/ (encode cache work/ship-media/ shared, no pack-media); demo unpacked builds and archives in app/desktop/release/demo/ (plan 173); demo app depots windows, linux, content like decision 84, no DLC depots; same version and tag v<version> as the full build, uploaded from the same tagged commit; release-check report work/steam/<tag>/demo/release-check.{md,json}, VDFs work/steam/<tag>/demo/vdf/; budget media-budget.json demo.content; no nix build output for the demo (no use: Steam only, decision 111).', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:34:59Z', '2026-10-17T13:34:59Z', 1529, NULL, 'rule', 1529, '2026-10-17, task 1529: written into plan 177: Demo packaging, release check and upload (Build contents, Staging and VDFs, release check, upload).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (343, 'Demo store presence: own store page, or only the Download demo button on the full game''s page?', 'answered', '["Button only: the demo appears as ''Download demo'' on the full game''s store page, no own page, no demo-specific store media", "Own store page: demo texts in es, es-ES, en, de, 5+ demo screenshots, a demo trailer, demo-marked capsules, own content survey"]', '', 'Steam can show the free demo in two ways: as a ''Download demo'' button on the full game''s store page, or with a store page of its own. An own page lists the demo in Steam''s demo lists and takes player reviews, but Valve then wants its own description, at least five screenshots and a trailer of the demo''s content, capsule art marked as a demo and its own content survey. The answer decides how much store material is made for the demo.', 'Button only: the demo appears as ''Download demo'' on the full game''s store page, no own page, no demo-specific store media', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:38:16Z', '2026-10-17T14:06:30Z', 1530, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-18, task 1566: Button only: plans/17a-store-page.md gained a ''Free demo'' section (one feature bullet per language, launch only); no demo capsules, screenshots, trailer or demo store-page block were made; the content-survey row and own-page rules of plan 178 do not apply. The demo''s Library art, if Steamworks asks, reuses the full game''s art.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (344, 'Demo release: with the full game''s launch, or earlier from the coming-soon page?', 'answered', '["With the launch: the demo is released on the full game''s launch day (Valve''s general recommendation)", "Before the launch: from the coming-soon page, e.g. for a Steam Next Fest (registration from the base game, review 3–5 weeks ahead)"]', '', 'The free demo can go live on Steam together with the full game, or before it, while the full game''s page still says ''coming soon'' (for example for a Steam Next Fest, where players try demos of upcoming games). Valve generally advises waiting for the launch, and moving demo saves into the full game through Steam''s cloud only works once the full game is out. The answer decides when the demo''s release steps are due.', 'With the launch: the demo is released on the full game''s launch day (Valve''s general recommendation)', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:38:16Z', '2026-10-17T14:06:24Z', 1530, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-18, task 1566: Demo released with the full game''s launch: the Free demo bullet in plans/17a-store-page.md is an ''At launch'' item, not on the beta page; no Next Fest or coming-soon demo work.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (345, 'Demo save and Steam''s shared cloud: keep the demo''s save apart, or share it with the full game''s cloud?', 'answered', '["Separate: no shared cloud, the demo keeps its own cloud and its own save folder (as the pending save choice recommends)", "Shared cloud: the demo''s ''Shared cloud APP ID'' is the full game, the demo writes the full game''s save; only after the full game''s release"]', '', 'Steam offers a setting that stores a demo''s cloud saves in the full game''s cloud, so a player who buys the game continues where the demo left off. Our pending choice about the demo''s save weighed a separate save, a one-time import and a shared save, and assumed two clouds would fight over a shared folder; Valve''s setting removes that conflict, but it also brings the demo''s plays into the family''s record of questions already seen, and only works once the full game is released. The answer decides whether the demo''s cloud setting points at the full game and where the demo writes its save.', 'Shared cloud: the demo''s ''Shared cloud APP ID'' is the full game, the demo writes the full game''s save; only after the full game''s release', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:38:31Z', '2026-10-17T14:06:11Z', 1530, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-17, task 1538: nothing to change in the shell; the demo already writes the full game''s save folder. The Steam Cloud side (demo''s ''Shared cloud APP ID'' = the full game, only after the full game''s release) is Steamworks configuration for plan 178: Steamworks demo app and store.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (346, 'Achievements in the demo: off, as Valve recommends?', 'answered', '["Off: the demo unlocks no achievements and the demo app defines none", "On: the demo app gets the full game''s achievement list and the demo unlocks them as the full game does"]', '', 'The full game has Steam achievements. Valve''s advice for demos is to turn achievements off, because players who unlock a few in a demo see the rest as locked in their Steam profile; achievements are allowed, though. Our pending choice about the demo''s Steam features left achievements open until Valve''s rules were read; the answer settles whether the demo unlocks any.', 'Off: the demo unlocks no achievements and the demo app defines none', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:38:31Z', '2026-10-17T14:05:37Z', 1530, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-17, task 1539: main.mjs steam:unlock returns false in the demo (nothing reaches Steam); the demo app defines no achievements (Steamworks, plan 178). Same task, decision 337: loadMods/listMods/setMods/acceptNotice are empty no-ops in the demo (no scan, no Workshop, mods.json untouched, no crash marker), --check-mod/--publish-mod exit 2 with a one-line message.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (347, 'Demo close-out: the mode × age group run stays in the demo release check', 'answered', '[]', 'Plan 177''s demo smoke plays each mode once, not every age group, and not to the end. The demo list can change later (plan 174''s replacement rule: a flagged or retired question gets replaced), and a replacement can leave one age group short; only a full run per mode × group catches that before upload. One kept check, per AGENTS.md''s few useful tests.', 'Before every upload of the free demo, the computer plays the demo once in every game mode for every age group, all the way to the end, twice, and checks that both runs showed the same questions. This proves the small fixed question set still lasts a full game everywhere, even after questions in it get replaced later. The choice was between running this only once at the end of the demo work, or keeping it as a check before every release; it stays.', 'smoke.mjs --demo --matrix plays every BUILT_MODES mode × every age group of app/data/age-groups.json to an end on the packaged demo build, with --trace; trivia-release-check --demo gains step matrix (after determinism): the matrix run twice, traces compared, ✗ naming the first difference or a game that ran short of questions; kept, not throw-away', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:39:55Z', '2026-10-17T13:39:55Z', 1531, NULL, 'rule', 1531, '2026-10-17, task 1531: written into plan 179: Close-out: play the demo (task 1: smoke.mjs --demo --matrix, release-check step matrix)');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (348, 'Demo: cover multiplayer sessions up to how many seats?', 'answered', '["S = 4: 384 questions, ≈ 1010 translations", "S = 5: 473 questions, ≈ 1280 translations (every pad + keyboard and mouse)", "S = 3: 296 questions", "S = 2: 209 questions", "S = 1: 125 questions, no multiplayer guarantee"]', '`qgen demo --sizes` on today''s pool (2026-10-17, `task 1543: qgen demo: candidates, supply check, picker; raise the seat decision`): the smallest fixed list that passes the engine''s supply check, plus the joker reserve (4 cards + R = 8 at one level), in every mode × age group, with media on and off, in es, es-ES, en and de, for multiplayer sessions of up to S seats.

Candidates: 46 full (approved in all four locales), 3746 pending (missing translations).

| seats S | list size | full | pending | binding configuration |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 (no multiplayer) | 125 | 46 | 79 | solo / gamemaster / rr-coop, kids, media off |
| 2 | 209 | 46 | 163 | rr-competitive, kids + kids, media off |
| 3 | 296 | 46 | 250 | rr-competitive, kids + kids + kids, media off |
| 4 | 384 | 46 | 338 | rr-competitive, 4 × kids, media off |
| 5 | 473 | 46 | 427 | rr-competitive, 5 × kids, media off |

- Size grows ≈ 85–90 questions per seat; rr-competitive binds (no card twice per session, kids'' narrow window)
- Translations to make: ≈ 3 per pending question (es, es-ES, en, de minus its source); at S = 5: 1281 (es-ES 427, de 427, en 348, es 79) ≈ 26 translation runs of 50; at S = 4 ≈ 1010 (≈ 21 runs); at S = 1 ≈ 240 (≈ 5 runs); 3 runs done so far
- Sessions with more seats than S still start when the list happens to suffice; otherwise the demo shows its usual "not enough questions" notice
- Recommendation S = 4: S = 5''s list (473) is above ≈ 400 and its ≈ 26 translation runs are far beyond the 3 done so far
- The answer goes into `authoring/data/demo.json`''s `seats` (`task 1547: Pick and approve the demo question list`)', 'The free demo of the trivia game ships a small, fixed set of questions. The more players a multiplayer session in the demo may have, the more questions the set needs, because players in a competitive session never share a card: one player needs about 125 questions, five players about 470. Every question in the set must also be translated into all four game languages, so a larger set means much more translation work before the demo can ship. Choose the largest number of players a demo session must be guaranteed to support.', 'S = 1: 125 questions, no multiplayer guarantee', NULL, '2026-10-17T13:48:27Z', '2026-10-17T14:05:31Z', 1543, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-18, task 1547: Demo list sized for S = 1 (125 questions): authoring/data/demo.json has seats 1 and is approved (decision 349); multiplayer sessions beyond one seat start only if the list happens to suffice, else the usual not-enough-questions notice. Pending translations (79 es-ES/de, 74 en, 5 es) make qgen validate fail on the demo list until translation runs fill them.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (349, 'Demo question list: approve?', 'answered', '["Approve the list as proposed", "Replace these ids (name them)", "Change the rules (say which)"]', 'Proposal: `qgen demo --propose --seats 1` (decision 348: S = 1, no multiplayer guarantee) → `authoring/data/demo.json`: 125 base questions, `approved` empty. Exported to `app/data/demo/` (es 120, es-ES 46, en 51, de 46 questions today); `qgen demo --check` and `qgen validate` pass.

Review the list: `trivia-authoring`, then `/review?demo=1` (add `&locale=en` etc. for a translation). Full proposal: `work/demo/proposal.md` (main checkout).

## Configurations
All 4 age groups × solo / Gamemaster / rr-coop, with and without video/audio: pass in es, es-ES, en, de, with the joker reserve (4 cards + 8 at one level). Binding: kids, media off (68 questions added for it).

## Spread
- Difficulty (es) listed/target: 1: 12/5, 2: 12/6, 3: 7/8, 4: 16/14, 5: 14/15, 6: 8/12, 7: 5/9, 8: 8/11, 9: 9/13, 10: 6/11, 11: 8/8, 12: 7/6, 13: 6/5, 14: 4/2, 15: 3/2 (easy end over target: kids need it)
- Categories: 28, close to the pool''s shares (history 12/14, film 10/12, animals 9/5, planet-earth 8/5 the largest gaps)
- 106 of 198 subcategories, at most 2 each
- Media: image 124, video 1 (the pool''s audio + video share is ~1 %)
- «Bájale»: 15 % of listed questions have an easier one of their subcategory in the list (no hard bar)

## Pending translations (listed ids not yet approved in the locale)
Only 46 of 125 are approved in all four locales; the rest need translation runs, which now take the listed ids first (`task 1545: Translation runs take demo-listed ids first`).
- es-ES: 79
- en: 74
- de: 79
- es: 5 (q-2386, q-2485, q-2873, q-3018, q-3201: their source is another locale)
- Ids (es-ES and de): q-0016, q-0037, q-0045, q-0056, q-0061, q-0073, q-0074, q-0076, q-0078, q-0083, q-0095, q-0097, q-0100, q-0102, q-0109, q-0110, q-0116, q-0142, q-0148, q-0153, q-0176, q-0177, q-0203, q-0208, q-0212, q-0236, q-0248, q-0263, q-0303, q-0334, q-0335, q-0339, q-0366, q-0368, q-0392, q-0531, q-0551, q-0622, q-0624, q-0635, q-0655, q-0715, q-0722, q-0824, q-0826, q-0842, q-0872, q-1032, q-1071, q-1084, q-1099, q-1104, q-1214, q-1217, q-1247, q-1248, q-1292, q-1354, q-1355, q-1358, q-1395, q-1396, q-1401, q-1412, q-1422, q-1475, q-1542, q-1561, q-1614, q-1772, q-1777, q-1791, q-1922, q-2156, q-2386, q-2485, q-2873, q-3018, q-3201 (en lacks the first 74 of these, up to q-2156)

## Options
- Approve: `approved` set, the list stays; the translation runs fill the gap, and until every id is a full candidate `qgen validate` errors on the pending ones.
- Replace these ids: name the ids to swap; a new proposal is made and asked again.
- Change the rules: say which (size, spread, media share, subcategory cap); a new proposal follows.', 'The demo needs a fixed list of questions that every player gets, so every run plays the same. A first list of 125 questions has been picked automatically so that every game mode and age group can be played once, and it is ready for you to look through. You can accept it, swap out particular questions, or change the rules it was picked by. Accepting it fixes the list for the demo; the missing translations are then filled by the normal translation runs.', 'Approve the list as proposed', NULL, '2026-10-17T14:09:09Z', '2026-10-17T18:10:48Z', 1547, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (350, 'Overlap rate in drafting: which changes?', 'answered', '["1 (recommended): recalibrate + cross-subcategory context. (a) targets.json: ''overlap rate'' max 3 % → 20 % (a runaway alarm; ''needs_work: overlap'' ≤ 1 % stays the quality gate); (b) draw_slots: each slot''s already_asked also gets the pool questions a lexical probe on its concept finds in every subcategory (overlap_candidates, rank ≤ 2, English via as_locale), and the avoid list goes through as_locale too; (c) a run-wide check so two subcategories of one run don''t both draw a concept the probe ties together. Expected overlap rate ≈ 10–11 % (passes), drop rate back under 20 %; ≈ −$4–6 wasted drafts/rates, +$1–2 longer draft prompts: net ≈ −$3–5 per batch, +≈ 50–70 merged per batch", "2: option 1 plus rater recalibration: rate.md says the same answer to a different fact is only a shared topic (fine) unless knowing one gives the other away. Expected ≈ 6–8 %; net ≈ −$5–8 per batch, +≈ 90–110 merged; risk: ''needs_work: overlap'' rises from 0.7 % towards 1–2 % (review catches them)", "3: threshold only: ''overlap rate'' max → 20 %, no pipeline change. Rate stays ≈ 15 % and creeps up with the pool; ≈ $10–12 per batch keeps going to discarded drafts; $0 to do", "4: health per bundle only: a failing base batch stops only the next base batch, not colombia''s or another region''s. Base keeps failing and is acked each batch; $0 per batch, a small health.py change", "5: concept-level fixes (retire saturated concepts, skip saturated slots, new concepts for saturated subcategories): not recommended, same-concept overlaps are 2–5 % and same-subcategory 7–9 % of the drops, spread over 75–80 of 99 subcategories; expected ≤ 1 pp", "6: leave as is: ack each batch \"for now\""]', '`task 1573: Investigate: options to reduce the overlap rate when drafting new questions` (numbers in its note).

## Where overlap is caught today
- Drafter (`cmd_draft`) sees only its own subcategory''s pool questions (`existing_answers`, all statuses, source language: Spanish for es-sourced ones) and the slot concept''s `already_asked` (same subcategory + same concept name).
- `rate` (opus) scores `no_overlap` against ≤ 8 lexical `overlap_candidates` from the whole pool (all bundles, English keys per decision 232) and earlier drafts of the run; merge drops `no_overlap` < 4. Plus lexical `duplicates()` at merge.
- Rule (`rate.md`) unchanged since task 274 (2026-10-11); merge-time rater drops started with batch-8. The 3 % threshold (`decision 13: Batch health thresholds and stop rule?`) was set on batch-4…7, which had no rater drops.

## batch-9 / batch-10 overlap + duplicate drops (184 / 168)
- 90–92 % cross-subcategory (partner in another subcategory, invisible to the drafter); same concept 2–5 %.
- Partner: earlier pool 67 % / 83 %; same run 33 % / 17 %. Partner language: es-sourced 67 % / 52 %, en 33 % / 48 %.
- Easy levels collide most: 1–4 drop 15–25 %, 11–15 drop 3–7 %.
- Spread: 80 / 75 of 99 subcategories, ≤ 9 per subcategory.
- Sample of 50: ≈ 55 % the same fact (Colosseum gladiators, Olympic torch, Ursula, James Webb infrared), ≈ 45 % only a shared answer or topic (Wallander → Sweden vs Stieg Larsson → Sweden). Rater score 3 is 46 % / 35 % of the drops.

## Why the jump at batch-9
- Pool growth: drafts with a same-answer pool candidate 7 % (b8, pool 1168) → 13 % (b9, 2159) → 14 % (b10, 3110); drafts with no candidate at all 32 % → 12 % → 6 %.
- Candidate → drop conversion rose too: 29 % (b8) → 54 % (b9) → 40 % (b10): English drafting with the international, fame-first concepts (`decision 239: English-first drafting prompts: apply?`, `decision 242: International angle for base concept lists: apply?`) aims at the world-famous facts the es pool already asked; batch-9 also had 61 same-run collisions (5 % of drafts).

## Cost
- An overlap-dropped draft wasted draft + rate (+ some factcheck) ≈ \$0.065: ≈ \$10–12 per batch (≈ 5 % of \$210–235); no review cost.
- The bigger costs: ≈ 160 fewer merged per batch, and the global stop (`health.stop_reason`, any bundle) blocks `task 1295: run colombia batch (batch-<n>)` after every base batch.

## Estimates for option 1(b)
- Throw-away simulation: a concept-name probe finds the partner of 40 % / 37 % of the pool-overlap drops; it flags 15 % / 14 % of slots. If the drafter avoids most of those: pool overlaps −30 %, overall ≈ −25–30 %; (c) takes part of the same-run share.', 'When the question generator drafts new trivia questions, about one draft in seven is now thrown away because it asks something the game already asks. The questions that survive are fine, but the waste trips an automatic quality alarm that halts every following generation run, including the regional ones, until someone signs it off by hand. The choice is whether to recalibrate that alarm, give the drafting model more of what''s already in the game so it avoids repeats, loosen how strictly near-repeats are judged, or some mix of these; the answer decides how often runs halt and how many usable questions each run yields.', '1 (recommended): recalibrate + cross-subcategory context. (a) targets.json: ''overlap rate'' max 3 % → 20 % (a runaway alarm; ''needs_work: overlap'' ≤ 1 % stays the quality gate); (b) draw_slots: each slot''s already_asked also gets the pool questions a lexical probe on its concept finds in every subcategory (overlap_candidates, rank ≤ 2, English via as_locale), and the avoid list goes through as_locale too; (c) a run-wide check so two subcategories of one run don''t both draw a concept the probe ties together. Expected overlap rate ≈ 10–11 % (passes), drop rate back under 20 %; ≈ −$4–6 wasted drafts/rates, +$1–2 longer draft prompts: net ≈ −$3–5 per batch, +≈ 50–70 merged per batch', NULL, '2026-10-17T14:26:59Z', '2026-10-17T15:32:30Z', 1573, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (351, 'First-person riddle questions: which changes?', 'answered', '["1: Riddle only where the answer is the speaker: rule clue riddle → move identify, who or name_concept; draft prompt defines it (the answer is the speaker and is never named, clues build from vague to specific, only when the guess is the fun, else direct or three_facts); review reason 6 sends a riddle that names itself, asks another fact or reads as a plain question to needs_work with a fix rewriting it as a direct question; three_facts weight 1 → 2. Riddle ≈ 5 %, top clue ≈ 51–53 % (about as now)", "2: Retire riddle (weight 0, still valid on old questions), three_facts weight 1 → 2. Riddle 0 %, top clue ≈ 55 %", "3: Lower riddle weight 1 → 0.5 only. Riddle ≈ 8 %, top clue ≈ 56 %", "4: Prompt definition and review check of option 1 only, weights and rules unchanged. Riddle ≈ 15–20 %, disguised ones rewritten by the review, top clue ≈ 51–53 %", "5: Existing approved riddles (719): keep all", "6: Existing: qgen rework the ≈ 310 that name themselves, ask another fact or aren''t in the first person (43 %) into direct questions; keep the ≈ 409 where the answer is the speaker", "7: Also: top clue bound ≤ 50 % → ≤ 60 % in targets.json (direct is ≈ 50 % by the rules alone, so the bound stops batches over a structural share)"]', 'Findings of `task 1574: Investigate: fewer first-person ''What am I?'' riddle questions` (numbers: approved `base` questions, `axes.clue`).

Share per batch: riddle 0–2 % up to batch-5 (no axes yet), 19 % batch-6, 22 % batch-7, 24 % batch-8, 20 % batch-9, 20 % batch-10; 719 approved riddles in the pool.

Why so many:
- `clue` values drawn with base weights direct 1, riddle 1, three_facts 1, completion 1, scenario 0.4; each value''s weight shrinks when it''s used more than its expected share (1/4.4 ≈ 23 %).
- Rules force `direct` for every media stimulus and `direct`/`scenario` for count, estimate, when, analogy, odd_one_out, sequence → `direct` is over its share pool-wide → in the free slots (no media, other moves) it''s pushed down and riddle fills the gap: there riddle 42 %, three_facts 32 %, direct 17 % (batch-8..10).
- Drafter: picks riddle in 53 % of the slots offering it, like direct (57 %); no preference of its own.
- Prompts: draft.md only has the axis text («a riddle in the first person: "Tengo…, vivo en…, ¿qué soy?"»); review.md and audit.md check riddles only for ambiguity and an unquoted inner question; rate.md gives riddles the highest mean fun (3.79 vs direct 3.56); approval 98 % (direct 94 %). Nothing pushes back.

Plain question in disguise (582 approved riddles, batch-8..10, regex + 60 read by hand):
- 60 % the answer is the speaker ("… Who am I?"); 34 % the speaker names itself and asks another fact ("I''m a dance where metal plates… In which country was I born?", "Soy Lillehammer: … ¿En qué país estoy?"); 6 % not in the first person at all (tag only).
- Moves: who 129, name_concept 101, cause_effect 71, origin 68, purpose 52, identify 50, word_meaning 49, made_of 32, record 30; disguise mostly in purpose, origin, cause_effect, made_of, word_meaning (riddle allowed with any move but count/estimate/when/analogy/odd_one_out/sequence).
- Hand sample of 60: 31 add something (12 playful guesses, mostly difficulty 1–4 and everyday objects: stapler, ghost in a sheet, boredom; 19 identity puzzles whose clues build up, e.g. Vespasian, Al Capone, which would work as well as three_facts), 29 a plain question in disguise.
- Same picture across difficulty (18–24 % riddle at every level), age bands and source language (en 20 %, es 24 %; disguise en 38 %, es 42 %).

Effect of changes (throw-away simulation of the draw on batch-10''s subcategories and today''s pool, scaled to batch-10''s actual riddle 20 % / direct 50 %; a guide, not a forecast). `top clue` = direct''s share, bound ≤ 50 % (decision 13); batch-9 52.8 %, batch-10 51.4 %:
- Riddles go to direct first: every cut of riddles raises `top clue`, unless three_facts takes the slack. Even then no option brings it reliably under 50 %: direct is structurally ≈ 50 % since media and number/time questions must be direct; only scenario at weight 1 would (direct ≈ 41 %), but its 0.4 is from QG-24 (long-winded questions).

Options 1–4 are alternatives for new questions; 5/6 for the existing ones; 7 independent.', 'About one question in five in the newest batches is a first-person riddle (''I have…, I live in…, what am I?''), and many of them are ordinary questions dressed up: the riddle names itself and then asks something else. The developer chooses how much of this form new questions should use and how strictly it is defined, and whether the riddles already approved stay as they are or are rewritten as plain questions. The answer changes how varied and how natural the questions sound, and how close the question mix stays to its variety limit.', '1: Riddle only where the answer is the speaker: rule clue riddle → move identify, who or name_concept; draft prompt defines it (the answer is the speaker and is never named, clues build from vague to specific, only when the guess is the fun, else direct or three_facts); review reason 6 sends a riddle that names itself, asks another fact or reads as a plain question to needs_work with a fix rewriting it as a direct question; three_facts weight 1 → 2. Riddle ≈ 5 %, top clue ≈ 51–53 % (about as now)', NULL, '2026-10-17T15:29:58Z', '2026-10-17T15:32:24Z', 1574, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (352, 'Gallery reviews: a review set of the touched shots, linked as /gallery?set=<name>', 'answered', '[]', 'Developer, 2026-10-17 (task 1581): quick feedback cycles; no baseline, no comparison. Sets live in work/gallery/sets/<name>/ and <name>.json; plain /gallery stays the full gallery; a missing set is an error on the page.', 'When a change to the game''s screens needs the developer''s eyes, the screenshots to look at should be only the ones the change touched, ready in minutes, not the whole gallery of every screen in every language, which takes a quarter of an hour and buries the change. This rule says how such a review is prepared and handed over.', 'A task wanting gallery feedback runs trivia-gallery --set task-<its id> --only <the touched shots> (es, es-ES, en, de; --size 1920x1080,1280x800 where both sizes matter) and its review decision gives /gallery?set=task-<id>; never a full gallery run for a review; the same set name again overwrites', NULL, '2026-10-17T17:53:10Z', '2026-10-17T17:53:10Z', 1581, NULL, 'rule', 1581, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (353, 'Category splash on the question screen: approve the exits and sounds?', 'answered', '["Approve: the look and the sounds are fine", "Problems: list the exits, sounds or screens to change in the feedback"]', 'Look: /gallery?set=task-1590 (es, es-ES, en, de at 1920x1080 and 1280x800): shots question-splash, question-splash-long (a long category and subcategory name) and timed-splash, each frozen at the hold. Exits and sounds: /?efectos plays all 20 exits with their sound; also play a real game on the TV. Sounds: all 20 cues are recordings. Reused samples: whoosh (fly left, zoom at 1.3x), escoba (fly right, wind), susurro-papel (fade), swoosh-sube (spin), estallido (explode), cohete (rocket), golpe (drop), rebobinar (blind), silbato (drain), pop (shrink to a dot), vidrio (shatter), papel (paper plane). New Kenney CC0 recordings: disolver (dissolve), derretir (melt), agujero-negro (black hole), pajaros (letters scatter like birds; a chirpy sweep, the weakest fit), gelatina (jelly), maquina-escribir (typewriter). No cue is synth-only; the synth recipes remain as fallback.', 'Every new question now opens with its category shown big in the middle of the screen and its subcategory in small text below, which then leave with one of twenty playful exit animations and a matching sound. Before the feature is called finished, the developer should see how it looks in all four languages and at both screen sizes, and hear the sounds on the TV. The answer decides whether it ships as is or gets fixes first.', 'problems: swap the sizes on the splash: the subcategory big in the middle, the category small below it (all four languages, both sizes; also question-splash-long and timed-splash). Exits and sounds approved as they are.', NULL, '2026-10-17T18:18:50Z', '2026-10-17T18:59:13Z', 1590, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-17, task 1590: Splash sizes swapped: the subcategory is the big centred line (it carries the exits and per-letter splits), the category the small line below, alone big when there is no subcategory; Splash.svelte, splash.ts comment, plans/04-ui-tv-display.md updated; gallery set task-1590 reshot (question-splash, question-splash-long, timed-splash; es, es-ES, en, de; 1920x1080 and 1280x800). Exits and sounds unchanged.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (354, 'Mode and age screens reviewed in /gallery?', 'answered', '["approved  (recommended)", "changes (listed in the answer)"]', 'Shots (work/gallery/sets/task-1463/, es, es-ES, en, de at 1920x1080 and 1280x800): mode-multi only; the other mode and age shots are unchanged since the last answer.
Changes since decision 329 (flags 22–29 in ui-flags.json, now fixed):
- en: groups «Co-operative» / «Competitive»; «Taking turns» (Beat the game together, taking turns); «Compete simultaneously» (Whoever answers first gets the question); «Every player fights for themselves»; round-robin competitive keeps its name
- es, es-ES, de follow the same meaning: Cooperativo / Competitivo, «Por turnos», «Todos a la vez»; Kooperativ / Gegeneinander, «Reihum», «Gleichzeitig»
- shortcut keys moved with the names (en T / V / S, es U / T / V, de R / G / L), collision check passes', 'Choosing how to play is now split into separate screens, and the names of the multiplayer modes were reworded after your last review. Please look at the updated mode screen in all four languages at /gallery?set=task-1463 and say whether it is right or what should still change.', 'approved', NULL, '2026-10-17T18:35:18Z', '2026-10-17T18:46:13Z', 1463, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (355, 'Mode and age screens: design', 'answered', '[]', '- Screen 1 «¿Cómo se juega?»: «Solo o en grupo» / «Multijugador».
- Screen 2a (single): Estándar group: «Solo o en grupo», «Modo anfitrión».
- Screen 2b (multi): visually separated groups «Cooperativo» (rr-coop) and «Competitivo» (rr-competitive, timed); one pick.
- Age screen on its own: one per game; rr-competitive one per player, after the join screen. «Personalizar partida» lives on it. Choice has no mode or age rows.
- Selected state everywhere: existing tile look (outline + tint).
- Names (decision 354): es Por turnos / Por turnos, todos contra todos / Todos a la vez; en Taking turns / Round-robin competitive / Compete simultaneously; de Reihum / Reihum gegeneinander / Gleichzeitig; es-ES shares es.
- Walkers (gallery, smoke, screenshots, trailer) follow this flow.', 'The game''s mode choice used to share one screen with the age group. After several review rounds in the gallery, the developer approved a separate flow: first solo or multiplayer, then the mode, then the age group. This records the final design as a rule for later screens.', 'Player → Mode → (Join) → Age → Bundles → Level', NULL, '2026-10-17T18:46:47Z', '2026-10-17T18:46:47Z', 1463, NULL, 'rule', 1463, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (356, 'Telemetry: deploy the server change and update the store privacy text', 'pending', '["Done: every row ✓ (give date and which)", "Some rows ✗ (name them)"]', 'Plan 110 row set, written against the code as built (checked 2026-10-17). Answer with the date and ✓/✗ per row; a ✗ gets a follow-up task (server → plan 105, texts → plan 108).

Server is at `https://trivia-reports.trivia-question-reports.workers.dev` (`decision 147: Report server: deployed on Cloudflare? URL and date`; also `reportUrl` in `app/desktop/package.json`). No new secret: the telemetry pull uses the reports'' `PULL_TOKEN` (`decision 118: Telemetry server storage and pull token`).

1. Deploy
   - dev shell (`direnv allow` or `nix develop`), `git pull` (the telemetry commits must be in the checkout)
   - `trivia-report-server deploy` → applies `report-server/migrations/0002_telemetry.sql` to the remote D1, then deploys the Worker with the `TELEMETRY_*` / `RATE_TELEMETRY_*` vars from `report-server/wrangler.toml` (`TELEMETRY_KEEP_DAYS = "30"`, `TELEMETRY_OPEN = "1"`)
2. `curl https://trivia-reports.trivia-question-reports.workers.dev/health` → `{"ok":true,"api":1}`
3. Route live:
   - `curl -i -X POST https://trivia-reports.trivia-question-reports.workers.dev/telemetry -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' --data @report-server/fixtures/telemetry-session.json`
   - expected `401 {"error":"invalid_ticket"}` (the fixture''s `dev-fixture` ticket isn''t faked remotely)
   - while `STEAM_APP_ID` in `report-server/wrangler.toml` is still `""` (decision 147: still waiting for the App ID) or `STEAM_WEB_API_KEY` is unset, the Worker answers `502 steam_unavailable` instead: that also proves the route is live; mark ✓ and note "502, no App ID yet". Not 404, not 500, not 415/400.
4. Pull route: `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $(cat state/report-token)" https://trivia-reports.trivia-question-reports.workers.dev/telemetry` → `200 {"sessions":[],"more":false}` (`qgen telemetry --pull` reads the same token: `TRIVIA_REPORT_TOKEN` or `state/report-token`). Without the header: `401`.
5. Steamworks store text (field and steps: `plans/11-steam.md` "Privacy (ST-5)" → "Where it goes on Steam"):
   - Edit Store Page → Description → "About This Game", per language (English, Spanish – Latin America, Spanish – Spain, German): replace the Privacy paragraph with the "Store text" version there (it now has the opt-in telemetry paragraph; es-419 and es-ES share one text)
   - Preview; Publish only together with the first build that has telemetry. The text says "optional", so publishing now is also fine if the build with telemetry comes soon; say which: ✓ live, or ✓ scheduled with the release of `<tag>`
   - the `PRIVACY.md` URL if a privacy field exists: `https://github.com/rubenmoor/trivia/blob/main/PRIVACY.md`

After the answer, the worker writes the consequences (deploy date, store text live or scheduled) and the ST-5 note in `plans/11-steam.md`.', 'The game can now send anonymous play data, but only if a player agrees, and only once the online service that receives it has been updated. This asks you to update that service, check that it answers, and replace the privacy paragraph on the store page with the version that mentions the optional data. Your answer says which of these steps worked and whether the new store text is live or waits for the first release that sends data.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17T19:57:46Z', NULL, 894, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (357, 'Task 1579 left unstaged changes after `pm task done`: investigate', 'answered', '[]', 'Run 1623 of task 1579 closed the task but left 1 file unstaged. pm committed them on the branch `pm/task-1579-run-1623-left` and cleaned the tree.

     M authoring/reports/batches.md

Look: `git show pm/task-1579-run-1623-left`. Keep: `git merge pm/task-1579-run-1623-left`. Then `git branch -D pm/task-1579-run-1623-left`.', 'A piece of automated work finished but left changes behind that it didn''t hand in. They were set aside, nothing is lost. Decide whether to keep them or throw them away.', 'discarded: stale batches.md, main moved on', NULL, '2026-10-17T23:07:10Z', '2026-10-24T02:51:39Z', NULL, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (358, 'Spot check batch-11 done?', 'answered', '["done"]', 'Link: http://127.0.0.1:8001/review?batch=batch-11&sample=1 (start with `trivia-authoring`, :8001). Size: 30 (quality.spot_check_size). Read agreement apart from the es batches; compare with batch-9 (28/30, 93 %) and batch-10 (29/30, 97 %). Mark the problem kinds in the feedback box.', 'A sample of 30 newly written quiz questions has to be checked by a person, blind to what the automatic reviewer decided, so we can measure whether the reviewer judges like the developer. This is the quality check after the third English batch of questions. Once it is marked done, the automatic quality report can be produced.', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-17T23:50:03Z', '2026-10-22T02:14:20Z', 1580, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-24, task 639: No wait: batch-11''s spot check was done; tr-en-2 followed batch-15.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (359, 'batch-11: health stop, ack?', 'answered', '["Ack batch-11 (qgen health ack batch-11 \"<note>\"), then rerun", "Do not rerun; investigate the drop rate first"]', 'Output of `nix develop -c qgen batch --bundle colombia` (exit 2), nothing staged:

```
batch-11 fails the batch health thresholds: drop rate.
See `qgen report --batches` or authoring/reports/batches.md. The developer looks at it and clears the stop with: qgen health ack batch-11 "<note>"
```

No `claude:` line was printed (the command stopped before any call). Answer "Ack": run `qgen health ack batch-11 "<note>"`, then the task reruns the same command.', 'A batch of Colombian trivia questions was stopped before it started because the previous batch lost too many questions along the way. Someone has to look at the numbers and decide whether that is acceptable. If acknowledged, the next batch runs; otherwise it stays blocked.', 'Ack batch-11 (qgen health ack batch-11 "<note>"), then rerun', NULL, '2026-10-17T23:51:19Z', '2026-10-22T02:14:21Z', 1295, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (360, 'Joker sounds on the TV: approve Paso y fuera, Soplo and Hada madrina?', 'pending', '["approve", "changes: …"]', 'Listen via the sound list page (`/?efectos`, recorded vs synthesized) and in a real game (launch with `TRIVIA_SOUND=1`): play Paso y fuera, Soplo and Hada madrina.
- Paso y fuera: cue `broom`, `barrido.m4a` (first 1.6 s of Freesound 118975 «Straw Broom Sweeping Gentle», esperri, CC0); plays on the sweep, replaces `escoba` there
- Soplo: cue `bing`, `microondas.m4a` (first 0.75 s of Freesound 872984 «Bell_Microwave Oven Bell», CAT-FOX_ALEX, CC0); plays when the note lands, the rustle follows 300 ms later
- Hada madrina: cue `wand`, `varita.m4a` (first 1.8 s of Freesound 683323 «Magic Spell Fairy Dust», zazz.sound.design, CC0); replaces the swanee whistle in the card flip
- Doña Exigente and Tiro mágico unchanged; the category splash and Timed keep `escoba`, `silbato`, `susurro-papel`
From `task 1599: Joker sounds that say what the joker does: broom, microwave bing, fairy wand`; follows `decision 81: Recorded sound effects: approve on the TV?`.', 'Three jokers in the game now have new sounds that are meant to say what the joker does: a broom sweeping, a microwave bell and a fairy''s magic wand. They were chosen by looking at the shape and brightness of the recordings, not by listening, so they need to be heard on the TV. Either they are approved as they are, or you say what to change and the sounds are swapped or adjusted.', NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17T23:56:58Z', NULL, 146, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (361, 'Soundtracks: take the sets found, or look further?', 'answered', '["Take what sounds right: listen to the staged sets in work/soundtracks/ and say which of sin-prisa, reflejos go in with caja (changes: <set> → ... )", "Take caja only; keep three soundtracks (synth, variaciones, caja)", "Take caja plus sin-prisa and reflejos as they are, unheard", "Keep looking for more matched sets (name a style or source)"]', 'Installed already: `caja` (musica-caja-*.m4a, in the Esc menu): OpenGameArt «Happy/melancholic synth + bells song – Adaptive layers pack» by 3xBlast, CC BY 3.0 (credited). One 16-bar loop (24.5 s, ~157 bpm) in three layers: music box alone, music box + bass drum and synth, full synth; 0.9 MB for the three. Vibe from the file names and loudness/brightness only, not heard. The pack''s ''Higher Pitch'' variants were avoided for the last loop in case they are transposed (key clash at the cut); unverified.

Staged to listen to in work/soundtracks/ of the main checkout (converted like the others, not in the game):
- sin-prisa-{normal,pregunta,enviada}.m4a: Little Robot Sound Factory «Thoughtful Music Loops Library», CC BY 3.0 (https://opengameart.org/content/thoughtful-music-loops-library), song «No Need To Worry» loops 00, 08, 05, all 20.0 s; brightness rises 943 → 2161 → 3833 Hz, loudness before normalizing -19.3 → -12.9 → -13.6 LUFS. Guess: calm and soft to bright and busy.
- reflejos-{normal,pregunta,enviada}.m4a: same library, song «Reflections» loops 00, 04, 05 doubled to 22.6 s; brightness 791 → 1001 → 1910 Hz, loudness -11.8 → -9.9 → -8.2 LUFS. The three lengths differ by 20 ms, so the beat would drift slightly on the cut.
- caja-*.m4a: the installed set, for comparison.
Not tried: that library''s other 17 songs (variants are song sections, not intensity steps); Kenney has no music loops. Each set would take ids sin-prisa / reflejos, names «Sin prisa» / «Reflejos», CREDITS rows and a SOUNDTRACKS entry.', 'The game''s music is becoming a choice of soundtracks, each one a matching set of three loops: calm for the menu, tenser for a question, tensest once an answer is locked in. Only one set (a music box that builds up) was found with the same song at three clearly different intensities and a licence we can use; two more candidates exist, but the three-intensity matching is a guess from their loudness and brightness because the files could not be listened to. Which of these go in decides how many soundtracks the Esc menu offers and whether the search goes on.', 'add caja, sin-pria and reflejos to the existing tracks. make "synthesized" the default', NULL, '2026-10-18T00:04:37Z', '2026-10-22T03:10:51Z', 1604, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-22, task 1605: 2026-10-22, tasks 1604 and 1605: sin-prisa and reflejos installed next to caja (musica-<id>-normal|pregunta|enviada.m4a, SOUNDTRACKS entries, soundtrack.<id> names in es, en, de, CREDITS.md rows; audio folder 5.4 MB of 7 MB). Default stays sintetizada (DEFAULT_SOUNDTRACK in sound.svelte.ts), named in plans/04-ui-tv-display.md Music; no separate TV-listening decision was added, this answer settles it.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (362, 'Demo start screen and bundle tile reviewed in /gallery?', 'answered', '["approved", "problems: …"]', 'Review set: /gallery?demo&set=task-1555 on trivia-authoring (es, es-ES, en, de at 1920x1080 and 1280x800; shots language, start, start-resume, start-save-notice, menu-start, bundles, game-settings, level; 0 unmatched text). Full demo run: /gallery?demo. Look at: the demo line on Start (`task 1552: Demo line on the Start screen`), the lone demo tile on Bundles (`task 1553: Demo base tile: name and count`), no Mods entry in the Esc menu on Start and no consent screen (`task 1554: Demo hides mods and the features decision 337 turns off`).

PLACEHOLDER hits: none on the eight shots. In code, `PLACEHOLDER(1453)` (`task 1453`, `plan 164: Timed game screens, drama and sound`) is on the timed round screen (Level.svelte) and the timed question screen (Timed.svelte); the demo has timed mode, so those two screens would show it, but they are outside this shot set. Part 4''s `trivia-release-check --demo` is meant to fail on one.', 'The free demo version of the game changes a few screens: the start screen says it is the free demo, and the question-pack screen shows a single demo pack with its question count. Screenshots of these screens in all four languages and two window sizes are ready to look at. The choice is whether they look right as they are or need changes.', 'approved', NULL, '2026-10-18T00:27:57Z', '2026-10-18T01:44:35Z', 1555, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (363, 'Demo store material approved?', 'answered', '["approved", "changes (list)"]', 'Texts, in plans/17a-store-page.md ''Free demo'' (after the offline bullet, at launch only, decision 344):
- en: [*]Free demo to try before you buy
- es and es-ES: [*]Demostración gratuita para probar el juego antes de comprarlo
- de: [*]Kostenlose Demo zum Ausprobieren vor dem Kauf
Not rendered: demo capsules, screenshots, trailer (decision 343: no demo-specific store media). Open: the demo app''s Library assets (capsule 600x900, header 920x430, hero 3840x1240, logo) were not rendered because decision 343 says no demo-specific store media; if Steamworks requires them for the demo app, either reuse the full game''s art (authoring/store/out/capsules/) or answer ''changes'' and a demo-marked set gets rendered from capsules.mjs. A demo-specific size list was not checked (no web access).', 'The demo will be offered as a Download demo button on the full game''s store page, with no page of its own. The only store material left is one line in the full game''s description that names the free demo, in each store language. Please check the wording, and say whether the demo''s entry in the Steam library needs pictures of its own.', 'approved', NULL, '2026-10-18T01:19:24Z', '2026-10-18T01:40:36Z', 1566, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (364, 'Translation health stops tr-en-1, tr-es-ES-1, tr-de-1: ack so the demo list''s 74 translations can run?', 'answered', '["Ack the three stops (qgen health ack <run> \"<note>\"), then rerun qgen batch --translate en|es-ES|de; listed ids go first", "Review the three reports first, then ack", "Make missing translations a warning in qgen validate until they land"]', 'Task 1607 found: `qgen validate` fails on 79 `authoring/data/demo.json` ids with no translation, none rejected or untranslatable. Per locale: en, es-ES, de lack all 79 (74 es-sourced, 5 en-sourced); es lacked 5 (en-sourced), now translated and approved (`qgen batch --translate es`, 181 calls, opus 161 / sonnet 20, $7.75, 32m). `qgen batch --translate en|es-ES|de` exit 2: health thresholds (audit/review agreement) of `tr-en-1`, `tr-es-ES-1`, `tr-de-1` (reports `authoring/reports/tr-<locale>-1.md`); only the developer runs `qgen health ack`.
Also: after the es run `qgen demo --check` reports "solo / gamemaster / rr-coop, kids|young_teens (es): reserve 2 short" (es pool is now 125; difficulty mix of the 5 new ids may not help); may need `qgen demo --replace` once the other locales land.
After the acks, rerun `qgen batch --translate <locale>` per locale (about 74 ids each, ~12 min of calls per 50 for es), then `qgen demo --check`.', 'Three of the four translation runs were stopped by an automatic quality check and will not continue until the developer clears them. The demo''s question list needs 74 more translations in each of English, Spanish (Spain) and German, so the demo cannot be finished until the stops are cleared or handled another way. Spanish (Latin America) is done: its five missing translations were made and approved.', '1 — Ack the three stops, then rerun qgen batch --translate en|es-ES|de; listed ids go first. The audit/review gap is the false media-title findings (task 1492: audit ran without the media-candidates cache, every picked file was there); without them agreement is ≈96–100 %. Real finding: q-0708 (es-ES) answer «Col» gives itself away via «coleslaw»: back to «Repollo» (the developer fixes it in review).', NULL, '2026-10-18T01:24:58Z', '2026-10-18T01:33:10Z', 1607, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (365, 'Bundle tiles name the unit: look at the gallery sets', 'answered', '["approved", "needs changes (say what)"]', 'Gallery sets: /gallery?set=task-1610 and /gallery?demo&set=task-1610 (task 1610: Bundle tiles: «5000+ questions», not a bare number).', 'Each bundle tile on the bundle screen now says what the number counts, for example «5000+ questions» instead of just «5000+», in all four languages. Please look at the screens, including the longest language (German) and the demo, and say whether the tiles read and fit well. If something looks off, say which language or screen.', 'approved', NULL, '2026-10-18T01:49:59Z', '2026-10-18T02:03:00Z', 1610, NULL, 'once', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (366, 'Demo list: 6 listed questions can''t be translated cleanly: replace them, fix their sources, or warn?', 'answered', '["Fix the sources of q-0116, q-0872, q-1032, q-1412 with qgen rework (developer-only), retranslate; replace q-0110 and q-1248 by hand in demo.json, since qgen demo --replace finds no replacement", "Replace all six in demo.json by hand (developer picks), then reject the stale translations of q-0110 and q-1692", "Make pending ids a warning in qgen validate until fixed"]', 'State after task 1607 (translation runs tr-en-2, tr-es-ES-2, tr-de-2 finished and staged; 79 missing ids down to 4 in de plus the cases below):

- q-0110 and q-1248: confirmed not travelling (Spanish-only song / rhyme), source now `translatable: false`. `qgen demo --replace` reports "no replacement" for both.
- q-0116: en needs_work, source fun fact says Cervantes died April 23 (died April 22).
- q-0872, q-1032: de/en/es-ES needs_work, source uses the retired "what do these have in common?" style.
- q-1412: de/en needs_work, source hint 1 says Buddha was born in northern India (Lumbini, Nepal).
- `qgen validate` also errors on approved translations of untranslatable sources: q-0110 (en, es-ES), q-1692 (es-ES): "reject the translation".
- `qgen demo --check` reserve-short failures (several age groups per locale) remain until the list is repaired.', 'The free demo has a fixed list of questions that must exist in all four languages. After the translation runs, all but six of them do; those six have a flaw (a faulty source text, a retired question style, or a joke that doesn''t travel) that the translators correctly refused to carry over. Either the six are swapped for other questions, their sources are repaired and retranslated, or the check that blocks every commit is relaxed for now.', 'Own answer (developer, 2026-10-21):
- q-0110: translatable. Drop translatable:false; keep the approved en and es-ES; de gets translated (next tr-de run, or run it here).
- q-1248: regional, translatable:false stays. Remove it from demo.json; propose 3 replacement candidates in a decision (same age group/level), I pick.
- q-0116: fix the source now, by hand, no qgen rework. fun_fact: «El Día del Idioma, el 23 de abril, recuerda a Cervantes: murió el 22 y lo enterraron el 23.» Then retranslate en, es-ES, de (all three carry the old fact).
- q-1412: fix the source now, by hand. Hint 1: «Es un maestro espiritual nacido hace unos 2500 años en lo que hoy es Nepal.» Then retranslate en, es-ES, de.
- q-0872, q-1032: fine as they are. Their translations'' only finding was the ''in common'' style: set the en, es-ES, de translations to approved (reviewer human, this decision).
- qgen validate must pass afterwards.', NULL, '2026-10-21T20:17:31Z', '2026-10-21T22:05:47Z', 1607, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-21, task 1607: q-0110 translatable; q-1248 left demo.json; q-0116 and q-1412 sources fixed by hand and en/es-ES/de retranslated; q-0872, q-1032 en/es-ES/de approved (reviewer human). Done earlier; qgen validate passes.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (367, 'Topic bundle icons: an optional icon field in bundles.json, pin as fallback', 'answered', '[]', 'A field keeps the icon with the row it belongs to: no id-to-icon table in the client to keep in sync, a renamed or new bundle needs no code change, and mods'' theme bundles can pick one of our icons the same way (by id would leave mods with the fallback only). Fallback stays what players see today, so old mods and rows without the field are unchanged; mods warn rather than fail, as with other unknown keys (decision 133). Region rows keep the flag rule of decision 263. Plan for the five topic bundles in the game (milestone 19 part 4).', 'Each extra question set shows a small picture on its tile so players can tell them apart: regional sets show their country''s flag, the general set a book, the rest a generic pin. The coming topic sets (science, sports, history, movies, geography) each need their own picture. This settles where a set says which picture it uses, and what a player-made set shows when it names none or names one the game doesn''t have.', 'An optional `icon` field on non-region rows of bundles.json (ours and mods''), naming an `Icon.svelte` symbol from a fixed list of bundle icons; region rows keep their flag and reject `icon`; missing or unknown → today''s fallback (ours: pin, mods: puzzle), unknown also a warning in --check-mod and an error in qgen validate for our rows', NULL, '2026-10-21T20:22:06Z', '2026-10-21T20:22:06Z', 1618, NULL, 'rule', 1618, '2026-10-21, task 1618: written into plan 185: Topic bundles in the game (task 1); decision 368 raised for theme bundle achievements (task 5).');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (368, 'Achievements for the topic bundles: one per bundle like the regional ones?', 'answered', '["Yes: BUNDLE_<ID> per topic bundle, 50 correct answers, entered with its DLC", "No: no achievements of their own"]', 'Today: `BUNDLE_<ID>` (50 correct answers from the bundle, standard-rules games only, decision 73) exists only for `kind: region` (`achievements.ts`), entered in Steamworks with its DLC (`DLC_BUNDLES`); mods'' bundles never earn it (decision 146). Yes: same trigger and pattern for `kind: theme` (`BUNDLE_STEM`, `BUNDLE_SPORTS`, `BUNDLE_HISTORY`, `BUNDLE_MOVIES`, `BUNDLE_GEOGRAPHY`), icon SVGs in `app/desktop/achievements/`, texts per language drafted in a later review decision, entered in Steamworks with each DLC (milestone 19 part 5). No: theme bundles earn nothing of their own; a family that plays only topic questions still earns the general ones (wins, jokers, SPECIALIST).', 'Each regional question set has its own Steam achievement, earned by answering 50 of its questions right (for example «¡Qué chévere!» for Colombia). The five coming topic sets (science, sports, history, movies, geography) could get the same, or none. The answer decides whether the game counts them, whether five more icons and texts in four languages are made, and whether each topic set''s Steam entry carries an achievement.', 'Yes: BUNDLE_<ID> per topic bundle, 50 correct answers, entered with its DLC', NULL, '2026-10-21T20:22:15Z', '2026-10-21T21:53:02Z', 1618, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-21, task 1656: Task 1656: BUNDLE_STEM/SPORTS/HISTORY/MOVIES/GEOGRAPHY rows ''with its DLC'' in plans/18-steam-integration.md; tokens NEW_ACHIEVEMENT_1_25..29 in app/desktop/steam-achievements.vdf (renumber to Steamworks'' real ids when entered). DLC_BUNDLES unchanged until the record task.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (369, 'Topic bundles: names, descriptions and rules', 'answered', '["Recommended: «A fondo: …» / «In depth: …» / «Im Detail: …» names and descriptions as in the first table, the rules as listed, movies film only", "As recommended, but movies covers film + TV series («A fondo: Cine y series», «In depth: Film and TV», «Im Detail: Film und Serien»; its film + TV rule)", "«Paquete de …» / «… bundle» / «…paket» names (second table), descriptions and rules as listed, movies film only", "Your own wording (names, descriptions, rules or movies scope, in the answer)"]', 'Task 1 of `plan 186: The five topic bundles: rows and taxonomies`; the rows are written by `task 1644: Create the five topic bundles` from this answer.

## Read
- Style guides `es`, `es-ES`, `en`, `de`: «paquete de preguntas» / «question bundle» / «Fragenpaket» (`decision 50: Play-test of age groups and bundles`, never «Temas»); «tema» / «Thema» is the on-screen word for a category, so no «Tema: …» prefix either.
- `app/data/bundles.json`, `names.{en,de}.json`: regional rows are «Regional: X» with a «Para quien tiene relación con X: …» description; en/de names and descriptions live in `names.<locale>.json`, es-ES reads es.
- Base''s categories on these topics (approved, es pool): «Ciencia y matemáticas» 94, «Planeta Tierra» 95, «Espacio» 13, «Inventos y tecnología» 102, «Cuerpo humano» 24; «Deportes» 86, «Fútbol» 31; «Historia» 239; «Cine, series y superhéroes» 186; «Geografía del mundo» 96. A bundle called plainly «Deportes» or «Historia» would read like base''s category of the same name.
- Bundle letter keys (plan 29, `BundleSelector.svelte`): the first free letter after a «Prefix:»; a shared prefix keeps keys on the topic word (as «Regional:» does), a shared first word («Paquete de …») doesn''t: the five would get P, A, Q, U, E.

## Recommended names: prefix «A fondo:» / «In depth:» / «Im Detail:»
Same shape as «Regional: X»; says what the bundle adds (more, deeper), no clash with base''s categories. es-ES: no override (no glossary difference in these words).

| id | es name | es description | en name | en description | de name | de description |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `stem` | «A fondo: Ciencia y técnica» | «Más preguntas de ciencia, y más a fondo: naturaleza, espacio, inventos, técnica y matemáticas.» | «In depth: Science and tech» | «More and deeper questions on science: nature, space, inventions, engineering and maths.» | «Im Detail: Wissenschaft und Technik» | «Mehr und tiefere Fragen zur Wissenschaft: Natur, Weltall, Erfindungen, Technik und Mathe.» |
| `sports` | «A fondo: Deportes» | «Más preguntas de deporte, y más a fondo: fútbol y mucho más, clubes, leyendas, Juegos Olímpicos y Mundiales.» | «In depth: Sports» | «More and deeper questions on sport: football and much more, clubs, legends, the Olympics and World Cups.» | «Im Detail: Sport» | «Mehr und tiefere Fragen zum Sport: Fußball und vieles mehr, Vereine, Legenden, Olympische Spiele und Weltmeisterschaften.» |
| `history` | «A fondo: Historia» | «Más preguntas de historia, y más a fondo: épocas, imperios, personajes y sucesos de todo el mundo.» | «In depth: History» | «More and deeper questions on history: eras, empires, people and events from all over the world.» | «Im Detail: Geschichte» | «Mehr und tiefere Fragen zur Geschichte: Epochen, Reiche, Menschen und Ereignisse aus aller Welt.» |
| `movies` | «A fondo: Cine» | «Más preguntas de cine, y más a fondo: películas y animación de todas las épocas y países, estrellas y premios.» | «In depth: Film» | «More and deeper questions on film: live action and animation from every era and country, stars and awards.» | «Im Detail: Film» | «Mehr und tiefere Fragen zum Film: Real- und Animationsfilme aller Zeiten und Länder, Stars und Preise.» |
| `geography` | «A fondo: Geografía» | «Más preguntas de geografía, y más a fondo: países, ciudades, mapas, banderas, montañas, ríos y mares.» | «In depth: Geography» | «More and deeper questions on geography: countries, cities, maps, flags, mountains, rivers and seas.» | «Im Detail: Erdkunde» | «Mehr und tiefere Fragen zur Erdkunde: Länder, Städte, Karten, Flaggen, Berge, Flüsse und Meere.» |

Keys (es): C, D, H, I (Cine, C taken), G.

## Alternative names: «Paquete de …» / «… bundle» / «…paket»
Same family as «Paquete básico» / «Base bundle» / «Grundpaket»; descriptions as above. Downside: keys off the topic (es P, A, Q, U, E).

| id | es | en | de |
|---|---|---|---|
| `stem` | «Paquete de ciencias» | «Science bundle» | «Wissenschaftspaket» |
| `sports` | «Paquete de deportes» | «Sports bundle» | «Sportpaket» |
| `history` | «Paquete de historia» | «History bundle» | «Geschichtspaket» |
| `movies` | «Paquete de cine» | «Film bundle» | «Filmpaket» |
| `geography` | «Paquete de geografía» | «Geography bundle» | «Erdkundepaket» |

## Rules (English, for the pipeline; same in every option)
Every rule starts with the shared part, then its own topic and exclusions. Shared part: "More and deeper questions on <topic> at every difficulty, from kids to adults, answerable by families anywhere in the world whatever their language; fan-level detail is welcome, while the famous core base already asks stays in `base`, and things only one country''s players know stay in that country''s regional bundle (`usa`, `spain`, …)".

| id | topic and exclusions |
|---|---|
| `stem` | topic: natural sciences, technology, engineering and maths: living things, the human body, physics, chemistry, space, geology, weather and ecology, inventions and machines, numbers and shapes, and their history (scientists, inventions, the space race); exclusions: present-day places, maps and climate zones are `geography`''s, sport `sports`'', film `movies`'', history outside science `history`''s |
| `sports` | topic: sport: football and every other sport, clubs, leagues, competitions, legendary players, records and rules, the Olympics and World Cups, and the history of each sport; exclusions: films about sport are `movies`'', the science of the body `stem`''s |
| `history` | topic: history: eras, civilisations, empires, rulers, wars, revolutions, explorers and everyday life in the past, historical borders and old place names, with every region of the world in balance; exclusions: the history of science, inventions and the space race is `stem`''s, of a sport, the Olympics and World Cups `sports`'', of film `movies`'', present-day places `geography`''s |
| `movies` (film only) | topic: film: films of every era and country, live action and animation, genres, directors, actors, characters, quotes, soundtracks, awards and film history; exclusions: TV series, cartoons made for TV and reality TV stay in `base` |
| `movies` (film + TV) | topic: film and TV series: films and series of every era and country, live action and animation, genres, directors, actors, characters, quotes, soundtracks, awards and screen history; exclusions: reality TV and news stay in `base` |
| `geography` | topic: present-day geography: countries, regions, cities and capitals, flags, maps and borders, mountains, rivers, lakes, seas, islands, deserts, climate zones and populations; exclusions: geology, weather physics and ecology are `stem`''s, historical borders, empires and old place names `history`''s |

## `movies` scope (sub-question)
- Film only (recommended): animated films included; TV stays base''s, which has «Cine, series y superhéroes» with series, cartoons, reality TV and telenovelas; one clear topic for a 2000-question bundle; name «Cine» / «Film» / «Film».
- Film + TV series: wider pool to draw from, names «Cine y series» / «Film and TV» / «Film und Serien», more overlap with base''s TV subcategories.

## Not here
- `icon` per row: `plan 185: Topic bundles in the game` (decision 367); the category joker («Doña Exigente») showing a topic bundle next to base''s similar categories: same plan.
- Store names (Steam): `plan 187: Steam DLC and store for the topic bundles` starts from these names.', 'The game is getting five new optional question packs, on science and technology, sports, history, film and geography, each adding many more and deeper questions on its topic than the general pack has. This decision fixes what players see (each pack''s name and short description in Spanish, English and German) and the one-line rule that tells the question writers what belongs in each pack and where the borders between the packs run. It also settles whether the film pack covers TV series too. The answer becomes the packs'' entries in the game and the starting point for their store names.', 'almost:

the correct names in english are:

Science questions bundle
Sports questions bundle
History questions bundle
Movies & Series questions bundle
Geography questions bundle

i leave the translations to you.

the descriptions:

More questions nature, space, inventions, engineering and maths
More questions on sports: athletes, events, teams, records.
More questions on history: eras, empires, people and events from all over the world.
More questions on movies and series: your favorite shows, characters and stories.
