The qgen: line did not print (the run stops at validate).', 'A batch of Spanish translations of English questions finished its work but the final consistency check refuses it. The check complains about a few translations whose source question was withdrawn, and about the list of questions used in the demo, which is now out of date. A person has to say whether those inconsistencies get fixed first or the run is accepted as it is.', 'Own answer (developer, 2026-10-21): neither option. The causes are settled by decision 366 (applied by task 1607): q-0110 is translatable, keep its en and es-ES translations; the demo list gets repaired there. Wait until task 1607 is done, then rerun tr-es-1 unchanged. q-1692''s es-ES translation may be rejected for now (task 1607 or this task), since decision 385 decides its fate later. If validate still fails after task 1607 for another reason, raise a new decision with only that output.', NULL, '2026-10-21T21:44:14Z', '2026-10-21T22:16:15Z', 1223, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-23, task 1228: after task 1607 the tr-es chain ran unchanged; tr-es-2 validated and exported (2351 es questions); no further validate failure.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (375, 'Topic bundle achievement texts?', 'answered', '["approved as drafted", "changes: …"]', 'Drafted rows are in the achievement table of `plans/18-steam-integration.md` (`BUNDLE_STEM`, `BUNDLE_SPORTS`, `BUNDLE_HISTORY`, `BUNDLE_MOVIES`, `BUNDLE_GEOGRAPHY`). Bundle names in the descriptions are placeholders until `plan 186: The five topic bundles: rows and taxonomies` fixes the real names; adjust to match. Titles: STEM «Mente brillante» / Lab Rat / Forscherdrang; SPORTS «¡Gooool!» / Game On / Sportskanone; HISTORY «Cuestión de tiempo» / Time Traveller / Zeitreisender; MOVIES «¡Corten!» / That''s a Wrap / Cineast; GEOGRAPHY «Rumbo al mundo» / Globetrotter / Weltenbummler. Per `decision 368: Achievements for the topic bundles: one per bundle like the regional ones?`. Steamworks entries come with the DLCs (part 5).', 'Each of the five topic bundles (science and tech, sports, history, movies, geography) gets its own Steam achievement for answering 50 of its questions right, like the Colombia bundle already has. The names and descriptions are drafted in Latin American Spanish, English and German and need a quick read before they go into the Steam entries. The icons are done: the bundle''s own symbol on a night-blue tile.', 'approved as drafted', NULL, '2026-10-21T21:55:13Z', '2026-10-21T22:14:47Z', 1640, NULL, 'rule', NULL, '2026-10-21, task 1656: Task 1656: approved texts carried into steam-achievements.vdf (latam, spanish, english, german); plan 18 table rows unchanged.');
INSERT INTO decision (id, subject, status, options, body, intro, answer, reason, created_at, closed_at, created_by_task, signoff, kind, decided_by_task, consequences) VALUES (376, '''In common'' questions: no new drafts, existing ones never rejected', 'answered', '[]', 'Developer rule, 2026-10-21 (task 1672: ''In common'' style: no new drafts, existing questions not rejected). Replaces the full retirement from commit 7cef782c, which was never a developer decision. Context: decision 366: Demo list: 6 listed questions can''t be translated cleanly: replace them, fix their sources, or warn?. Move connection stays at weight 0; review rejects the style only in new drafts; translation review, audit, rework and tighten ignore it.', 'Quiz questions that ask what several things have in common made weak questions when written in bulk, so the writing step no longer produces them. Questions of that kind that are already approved are fine, and must not be rejected or sent back for rework for that reason in any language.', 'No new drafts in the ''in common'' style; existing approved questions are never rejected for it', NULL, '2026-10-21T22:07:00Z', '2026-10-21T22:07:00Z', 1672, NULL, 'rule', 1672, '');
