INSERT INTO summary (id, task_id, body, head_commit, created_at) VALUES (1, 1132, '# Trivia: executive summary

Trivia is a quiz game for families to play together in front of the living-room TV: the family works as one team through twelve questions of rising difficulty, with a few "jokers" to help out of a tight spot. It started as a game for one Spanish-speaking family and is now being turned into a product to sell on Steam, the largest store for PC games.

**Where it stands:** the game is complete and playable as a desktop program, and most of what a Steam launch needs is built, but it is not yet on Steam, and the questions exist only in Spanish so far.

## What exists today

- **A finished game.** Five ways to play, from a host who controls everything to players taking turns, with sound, music, jokers and a polished look. It works with a game controller as well as keyboard and mouse.
- **About 2,000 approved questions** in Spanish, each with a picture, sound or short video, for players of different ages. A small extra set about Colombia can be switched on.
- **A desktop version for Windows and Linux**, ready for Steam: saved progress across computers, Steam achievements, and an English and German version of every on-screen text.
- **Players can change the game themselves** ("mods") and share their changes through Steam, from new question sets to a whole new look.
- **Players can report a bad question** with one click, and can choose to share anonymous play data to help tune difficulty.

## What comes next

The family''s playtests in each language, a first test version on Steam, the store page, and more questions: the goal is 5,000 in Spanish, then translations into English and German. The main risk to the timing is content: the question count must more than double, and translating and checking questions for the other languages has barely started.', 'b058a5cec54717d02ee217106e3eaea4c9df30ad', '2026-10-15T18:47:41Z');
INSERT INTO summary (id, task_id, body, head_commit, created_at) VALUES (2, 1609, '# Trivia: executive summary

Trivia is a quiz game for families to play together in front of the living-room TV: the family works as one team through twelve questions of rising difficulty, with a few "jokers" to help out of a tight spot. It started as a game for one Spanish-speaking family and is now being turned into a product to sell on Steam, the largest store for PC games.

**Where it stands:** the full game is finished and playable, and the free demo that comes before the Steam launch is nearly ready, so the project is on track, though nothing is public yet.

## What''s new

- **A free demo.** It has every feature of the full game but only a small, fixed set of about 200 questions, enough to play once in each game mode and age group. The questions are chosen the same way every time, so every demo player sees the same game. Its start screen says plainly that this is the free version. The demo can be built, checked and prepared for upload to Steam, and its store page material is written. A demo lets people try the game at no risk, which should help sales.
- **Better sound.** Jokers now have sound effects that say what they do, such as a broom, a microwave bell or a fairy wand. Players can pick from several recorded music tracks in the menu.
- **More lively question screens.** Each question now opens with a short animated category introduction, and the screens for choosing a game mode and age group were reworked.
- **Better new questions.** The process that drafts new questions now repeats itself less and asks fewer "What am I?" riddles, so the question pool stays varied as it grows.

## What comes next

The demo still needs its Steam entry set up and a final playthrough by the developer. After that the focus returns to the full release: more questions (the goal is 5,000 in Spanish), then English and German versions, family playtests, the store page and a first test version on Steam. The main risk to the timing remains content: the question count must more than double, and the other languages have barely started.', 'accb09c697937eb7083a30d97edf197f7cfb1b66', '2026-10-18T01:24:28Z');

INSERT INTO resource_use_report (id, task_id, head_commit, created_at) VALUES (1, 1133, '4f4e71b7932d0ec5a389156a9cd990030391fe23', '2026-10-15T18:51:49Z');

INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (1, 1, 'Question authoring', 'Making the question pool: the qgen pipeline, its prompts, batch runs, quality control, difficulty and content targets, subcategories, regional bundle content, the authoring review/stats pages and media sourcing for questions.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (2, 1, 'Game rules and engine', 'How the game plays and the code that referees it: the TypeScript engine port and its fixtures, selection, jokers, game modes and settings, age groups and bundles logic, seen counters, save document and migration, the retired Python game server.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (3, 1, 'Game screens and input', 'What the family sees and presses on the TV: Svelte screens and dialogs, layout and animation polish, keyboard/focus/gamepad input and glyphs, Deck-size layout, media preload, image peek, icons.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (4, 1, 'Sound and music', 'Recorded sound effects and music loops in the game.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (5, 1, 'Translations and UI wording', 'Any language work: the i18n catalogs and helper, pseudo-locale, en/de/es-ES UI texts, language setting and pickers, question translation pipeline and its review tool, style guides, the screen gallery, joker names.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (6, 1, 'Licences and credits', 'Rights to ship: media licence data and audit, replacing problem files, code and content licence, Freesound terms, the credits screen and CREDITS.md.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (7, 1, 'Desktop app and Steam integration', 'The shipped Electron app and its path onto Steam: shell, file saves, builds and packaging, shipped media encoding, Steamworks binding, achievements, Cloud, overlay, Deck, version and patch safety, depots, release check and upload tooling.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (8, 1, 'Store page, publishing and launch', 'Selling the game on Steam: store texts, screenshots, capsules, trailer, price, partner account, name check, content survey, Coming soon, launch and content-update plans and announcements.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (9, 1, 'Player reports and telemetry', 'Data coming back from players: the question flag/report dialog, the report server, qgen flag pulls, opt-in telemetry recording, sending, consent, privacy texts and played-difficulty analysis.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (10, 1, 'Modding and Workshop', 'Letting players change the game: readable build, mod overlay, mod bundles, code add-ons, mods screen and safe start, Workshop source and publishing, the modding kit, guide and examples.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (11, 1, 'Code review and dev tooling', 'Code health and the developer''s own tools: the code-review milestone and its fixes, linters and type-checks, refactors that split files, the Node dev server, muted runs for agents, dev-only shortcuts.');
INSERT INTO resource_use_category (id, report_id, name, criteria) VALUES (12, 1, 'Project steering', 'Work about the project as a whole: masterplans and close-outs spanning several areas, post-milestone doc cleanups, executive summaries and project-wide doc sweeps.');

